e `_nexus/verify` section) and `docs/evidence/v1.3.0/VR2.md`: (a) the client chooses the directory a session works in, so a verification covers that directory; the operator's verifier command and deliverable list are fixed at start-up but are applied to the session's directory (check `cli/src/config.ts` ~529 and the worker for how deliverables resolve, and describe it exactly); the result and receipt name the workspace and base so a reader can see what was covered; (b) the base is pinned per workspace for the life of the process (after change 2), so commits made before the first session on that directory are the baseline, and restarting `nexus acp` re-pins; (c) the same-user limit already described in `docs/MCP_GUIDE.md` applies. In the evidence doc, replace any test-count claim you cannot reproduce with the counts from your own run at the current head, and keep its statement about hosted CI truthful (say CI results are on the PR rather than claiming none ran).\n\nThen run, one at a time with a throwaway HOME: `acp_stdio`, `acp_validate`, `acp_schema`, `acp_mapping`, `acp_review_fixes`, `acp_client_conformance`, `verify_service`; `tsc --noEmit`; `node cli/scripts/gen_acp_schema.mjs --check` (or whatever the check invocation is); `node scripts/check_invariants.mjs`; `node scripts/check_doc_versions.mjs`. Run `acp_stdio` three times in a row. Report file:line per change, tests added, pass/fail counts, the mutation result, and anything not done or untested."}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011ChLXAo92VfK3i97Tef4uM","requestRef":"34ab0f1e-a59a-4781-9bbb-b3bda007e9e9","requestedModel":"claude-fable-5-2","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"345de2d6-ced1-4bc3-8236-422a1ba1dfcf","timestamp":"2026-11-23T20:51:44.251Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb6