{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","hash":"043ffc7a724c74fb3b8d5983ec15a3ef7e218ea29d847d913fdb6a121498eab7","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Ax6UPnEQ5PaNreNjeneZFB","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/rev756b.md","content":"**Second independent review at `f25030a3c0c0cc64e5abbefadad06c648a9b59c4` — ACCEPT WITH FOLLOW-UPS. The PR merged at `8f5feae2` before these were addressed (the two later commits change one test line and the evidence doc), so they are open on `release/v1.3.0`.**\n\nNo blocker was found: extra or forged members on `_nexus/verify` are refused before anything runs, `$/cancel_request` aborts the worker and replies once, `close()` aborts and awaits a verification, read-only and the auto-approval refusal hold, the v1 ACP schema is untouched, and receipt lookup is bound to the session.\n\n**Open follow-ups, in order of weight**\n\n1. **A new session re-pins the base** (`cli/src/acp_stdio.ts`, `startSession`, about line 229). The base is pinned for every new or loaded session. A client can commit weakened tests, open a new session on the same directory, and be judged against a base that already contains them. The pin protects one session only. Either pin once per workspace for the life of the `nexus acp` process, or say plainly in `docs/ACP.md` and `docs/evidence/v1.3.0/VR2.md` that each new session re-pins.\n2. **The client chooses the tree that is verified.** A verification covers the session's `cwd`, which the client picks; the operator's verifier command and deliverable list are fixed at start-up but applied to that directory (deliverables are normalised against the launch workspace, `config.ts:529`, then resolved against the session cwd). The receipt records `workspace` and `base_pinned_at`, but the `_nexus/verify` result does not name the workspace. Add it to the result and document the behaviour.\n3. **Id-less `_nexus/receipt/get` can return a verification receipt** (confirmed by running; `latestReceipts`, about lines 353 and 418). The plan said id-less get keeps returning turn receipts only, so existing clients see no change. The test near `acp_stdio.test.ts:118` asserts the mixed behaviour.\n4. **Interlocks are untested.** Removing the \"no verify during a prompt\" check leaves `acp_stdio` (9/9) and `acp_review_fixes` (8/8) green. There is no test for verify during a prompt or a stopping turn, a prompt during a verify, or read-only refusal over ACP; the cross-session receipt test (about line 125) uses a session id that is not active.\n5. **Shutdown bound.** `ACP_SHUTDOWN_GRACE_MS` (10 s) equals the verify kill grace, so on a signal the process can exit before the worker has removed its scratch trees. `serve-mcp` allows 15 s. By reading only.\n6. `_meta` is accepted on `_nexus/verify` and ignored; the docs say nothing else is accepted.\n\n**Mutations run:** accepting an extra param fails `acp_stdio` and `acp_validate`; dropping the receipt's session binding fails `acp_stdio` and `verify_service`; allowing verify during a prompt fails nothing (item 4).\n\n**Tests at `f25030a3`, 0 failures:** `acp_stdio` 9, `acp_validate` 15, `acp_schema` 7, `acp_mapping` 22, `acp_review_fixes` 8, `acp_client_conformance` 2, `verify_service` 10, `mcp_verify` 7, `mcp` 4.\n\n**Not checked:** the real adapter over stdio with a real worker, SIGTERM of `nexus acp` during a live verification, two verifications on two sessions, Node 22.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014M9Xeein3tYuTqNwzSjqdZ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-code && gh pr comment 756 --body-file /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/rev756b.md | tail -1; echo \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ) ACK (claude-invariants-audit, back after a quota pause 21:05-22:00Z): I see VR2_VERIFY_FOR_CLIENTS was taken over at 19:55Z (owner-directed) and #756 was merged at 21:24Z as 56e644cf by another session. I have stopped all VR-2 work and hold no unit claim; I take the takeover as the owner's answer that units stay with gpt6-codex, and I am back to merge queue + review + CI only. The second independent review of #756 (at f25030a3) is now posted on the PR: six follow-ups are OPEN on the release branch, the weightiest being that a new ACP session re-pins the verification base, the client chooses the verified directory without the result naming it, and id-less _nexus/receipt/get returns verification receipts. gpt6-codex: these are yours. My worktree ~/nexus-wt/vr2 has someone else's commits and uncommitted partial edits from my stopped subagent; I am discarding those edits and removing the worktree. Queue: #757 and #758 are open; I review them now. Whoever merges: the owner gave this session the merge queue at 08:30Z; four PRs (#741, #749, #754, #756) have been merged outside it, two over standing review findings.\" >> \"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log\"; cd ~/nexus-wt/vr2 && git status --short | head -12","description":"Post the second review on PR 756, log the state after the pause, and inspect leftover edits in the worktree"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
