{"parentUuid":"294ef6e6-7b61-460a-87fb-0cbfa5994015","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011ChLdQkaLE8e7aQB2FCjCR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1366,"cache_read_input_tokens":471832,"output_tokens":2548,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":37},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1366,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2548,"cache_read_input_tokens":471832,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1366,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1366},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":552,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011ChLdQkPfYqpFpqVgxeb5X","requestRef":"48ff61bd-03af-4109-831a-93ae45ef0120","requestedModel":"claude-fable-5-2","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"77d54012-b314-419c-902f-4669628b30de","timestamp":"2026-11-23T22:13:07.276Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"main","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
{"parentUuid":"77d54012-b314-419c-902f-4669628b30de","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011ChLdQkaLE8e7aQB2FCjCR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LQf3MHyvJT7Y5HnnagAgbc","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-wt/readyfix && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='docs/releases/v1.3.0-READINESS.md'; s=open(p).read()\ndef rep(old,new):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(old)==1, old\n    s=s.replace(old,new)\nrep(\"| VR-2 | Landed | PR #756 |\",\n    \"| VR-2 | Landed, follow-ups open | PR #756. Six findings from its second review are open (listed on the PR): a new ACP session re-pins the verification base; the client chooses the verified directory and the result does not name it; id-less `_nexus/receipt/get` returns verification receipts; the verify/prompt interlocks are untested; the shutdown bound; `_meta` |\")\nrep(\"| GV-1 | Landed | Managed policy library + enforcement |\",\n    \"| GV-1 | Partial | Library (#717) and enforcement (#738) landed. Open per `docs/MANAGED_POLICY.md`: the `nexus policy` commands and doctor findings, `sandbox.*` reaching `nexus verify --sandbox`, and the TUI \\\"always\\\" answer under `approval.disable_auto` |\")\nrep(\"| GV-5 | Landed | `approval.strict` refuses `--yes` / `--mode auto` with source tag; MCP/plugin allowlists in schema |\",\n    \"| GV-5 | Partial | `approval.strict` refuses `--yes` / `--mode auto` with source tag. The MCP and plugin allowlists (`mcp.allow`, `mcp.disable_workspace`, `plugins.allow`, `plugins.disable_workspace`) are accepted by the schema and enforce nothing yet (`docs/MANAGED_POLICY.md`: \\\"not yet\\\") |\")\nrep(\"| PA-3 / HK-3 / BG-3 | Stretch (may roll) | Per plan Phase D |\",\n    \"| PA-3 | Partial | #706 landed the goal ledger; pause-on-restart is in review (#758, changes requested: a restart without a host reboot is not detected) |\\n| HK-3 / BG-3 | Stretch (may roll) | Per plan Phase D; BG-3 is deferred to v1.4 by the plan |\\n| SB-1 | Open | No named permission profiles |\\n| MT-1 | Not measured here | The `agent.ts` split landed in v1.2.1 (#591); the unit's acceptance test was not located |\\n| MT-2 | Open | No spec-plus-handler tool registry |\")\nrep(\"| G-3 | Hostile verify / managed-policy / ACP gate tests present; full hostile matrix not re-audited here |\",\n    \"| G-3 | Hostile verify / managed-policy / ACP gate tests present; full hostile matrix not re-audited here. As planned the gate also spans hooks, plugins and schedules, which do not exist yet, so it cannot be evaluated in full |\")\nrep(\"| G-1 | Tip CI green; local full-suite on tip not re-run in this inventory |\",\n    \"| G-1 | Tip CI green; local full-suite on tip not re-run in this inventory. The real-server LSP suite and the real-project smoke run on `main` only by schedule; dispatched by hand on the release branch on 2026-11-23 (LSP 14/14 after #751, which fixed a Pyright regression nothing else had caught; smoke passed) |\")\nold=\"ship PF-1/2, AC-1/2, VR-1/2/3, GV-1–5, LS-*, CI shards;\"\nassert old in s\ns=s.replace(old,\"ship PF-1/2, AC-1/2, VR-1/2/3, GV-1–5 as far as they have landed (GV-1 and GV-5 are partial: say so in the notes or finish them first), LS-*, CI shards;\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngit diff --stat | tail -1; node scripts/check_doc_versions.mjs 2>&1 | tail -1; git commit -qam \"docs(v1.3.0): correct the readiness inventory where it overstates the branch\n\nGV-1 and GV-5 were listed as landed. docs/MANAGED_POLICY.md on this branch\nsays the policy commands and doctor findings are not in and marks the MCP\nand plugin allowlists 'not yet': both are partial. VR-2 landed with six\nreview findings open. SB-1, MT-1 and MT-2 were missing, and PA-3 was filed\nas stretch while #758 is in review for it. G-1 and G-3 gain what was and\nwas not measured.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>\" && git push -q -u origin v1/readiness-corrections 2>&1 | tail -1; gh pr create --base release/v1.3.0 --head v1/readiness-corrections --title \"docs(v1.3.0): correct the readiness inventory where it overstates the branch\" --body \"#757 merged at \\`f40c2974\\` with the review's corrections unapplied (they are on that PR). This applies them, docs only, one file.\n\n- **GV-1: Landed → Partial.** \\`docs/MANAGED_POLICY.md\\` on this branch says the \\`nexus policy\\` commands and doctor findings are not in, \\`sandbox.*\\` does not reach \\`nexus verify --sandbox\\`, and the TUI \\\"always\\\" answer under \\`approval.disable_auto\\` is planned.\n- **GV-5: Landed → Partial.** The same document marks \\`mcp.allow\\`, \\`mcp.disable_workspace\\`, \\`plugins.allow\\` and \\`plugins.disable_workspace\\` \\\"not yet\\\": accepted, enforcing nothing.\n- **VR-2:** landed, with the six open findings from its second review named.\n- **Added rows:** SB-1 (open), MT-2 (open), MT-1 (not measured here). **PA-3** moved out of \\\"stretch\\\": #706 landed part, #758 is in review with changes requested.\n- **G-1, G-3:** what was and was not measured, including that the real-server LSP suite and the smoke run only on \\`main\\` by schedule and were dispatched by hand on this branch.\n- The thin-RC proposal now says GV-1 and GV-5 are partial, so the notes must say so or the units must be finished first.\n\nA release decision should not be read off rows that say more than the branch holds.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\" | tail -1; echo \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ) NOTE + PR (claude-invariants-audit): #757 was merged at 22:12Z by another session with my REQUEST CHANGES unapplied, so the readiness inventory on the release branch lists GV-1 and GV-5 as Landed although docs/MANAGED_POLICY.md says otherwise. Opened a docs-only correction PR from ~/nexus-wt/readyfix (v1/readiness-corrections). That is the fifth PR merged outside the queue today (#741, #749, #754, #756, #757), three of them over open review findings.\" >> \"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log\"","description":"Correct the inventory rows, commit, open the PR and log it"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1366,"cache_read_input_tokens":471832,"output_tokens":2548,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":37},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1366,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2548,"cache_read_input_tokens":471832,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1366,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1366},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":19361,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01LQf3MHyvJT7Y5HnnagAgbc":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-wt/readyfix && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='docs/releases/v1.3.0-READINESS.md'; s=open(p).read()\ndef rep(old,new):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(old)==1, old\n    s=s.replace(old,new)\nrep(\"| VR-2 | Landed | PR #756 |\",\n    \"| VR-2 | Landed, follow-ups open | PR #756. Six findings from its second review are open (listed on the PR): a new ACP session re-pins the verification base; the client chooses the verified directory and the result does not name it; id-less `_nexus/receipt/get` returns verification receipts; the verify/prompt interlocks are untested; the shutdown bound; `_meta` |\")\nrep(\"| GV-1 | Landed | Managed policy library + enforcement |\",\n    \"| GV-1 | Partial | Library (#717) and enforcement (#738) landed. Open per `docs/MANAGED_POLICY.md`: the `nexus policy` commands and doctor findings, `sandbox.*` reaching `nexus verify --sandbox`, and the TUI \\\"always\\\" answer under `approval.disable_auto` |\")\nrep(\"| GV-5 | Landed | `approval.strict` refuses `--yes` / `--mode auto` with source tag; MCP/plugin allowlists in schema |\",\n    \"| GV-5 | Partial | `approval.strict` refuses `--yes` / `--mode auto` with source tag. The MCP and plugin allowlists (`mcp.allow`, `mcp.disable_workspace`, `plugins.allow`, `plugins.disable_workspace`) are accepted by the schema and enforce nothing yet (`docs/MANAGED_POLICY.md`: \\\"not yet\\\") |\")\nrep(\"| PA-3 / HK-3 / BG-3 | Stretch (may roll) | Per plan Phase D |\",\n    \"| PA-3 | Partial | #706 landed the goal ledger; pause-on-restart is in review (#758, changes requested: a restart without a host reboot is not detected) |\\n| HK-3 / BG-3 | Stretch (may roll) | Per plan Phase D; BG-3 is deferred to v1.4 by the plan |\\n| SB-1 | Open | No named permission profiles |\\n| MT-1 | Not measured here | The `agent.ts` split landed in v1.2.1 (#591); the unit's acceptance test was not located |\\n| MT-2 | Open | No spec-plus-handler tool registry |\")\nrep(\"| G-3 | Hostile verify / managed-policy / ACP gate tests present; full hostile matrix not re-audited here |\",\n    \"| G-3 | Hostile verify / managed-policy / ACP gate tests present; full hostile matrix not re-audited here. As planned the gate also spans hooks, plugins and schedules, which do not exist yet, so it cannot be evaluated in full |\")\nrep(\"| G-1 | Tip CI green; local full-suite on tip not re-run in this inventory |\",\n    \"| G-1 | Tip CI green; local full-suite on tip not re-run in this inventory. The real-server LSP suite and the real-project smoke run on `main` only by schedule; dispatched by hand on the release branch on 2026-11-23 (LSP 14/14 after #751, which fixed a Pyright regression nothing else had caught; smoke passed) |\")\nold=\"ship PF-1/2, AC-1/2, VR-1/2/3, GV-1–5, LS-*, CI shards;\"\nassert old in s\ns=s.replace(old,\"ship PF-1/2, AC-1/2, VR-1/2/3, GV-1–5 as far as they have landed (GV-1 and GV-5 are partial: say so in the notes or finish them first), LS-*, CI shards;\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngit diff --stat | tail -1; node scripts/check_doc_versions.mjs 2>&1 | tail -1; git commit -qam \"docs(v1.3.0): correct the readiness inventory where it overstates the branch\n\nGV-1 and GV-5 were listed as landed. docs/MANAGED_POLICY.md on this branch\nsays the policy commands and doctor findings are not in and marks the MCP\nand plugin allowlists 'not yet': both are partial. VR-2 landed with six\nreview findings open. SB-1, MT-1 and MT-2 were missing, and PA-3 was filed\nas stretch while #758 is in review for it. G-1 and G-3 gain what was and\nwas not measured.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>\" && git push -q -u origin v1/readiness-corrections 2>&1 | tail -1; gh pr create --base release/v1.3.0 --head v1/readiness-corrections --title \"docs(v1.3.0): correct the readiness inventory where it overstates the branch\" --body \"#757 merged at \\`f40c2974\\` with the review's corrections unapplied (they are on that PR). This applies them, docs only, one file.\n\n- **GV-1: Landed → Partial.** \\`docs/MANAGED_POLICY.md\\` on this branch says the \\`nexus policy\\` commands and doctor findings are not in, \\`sandbox.*\\` does not reach \\`nexus verify --sandbox\\`, and the TUI \\\"always\\\" answer under \\`approval.disable_auto\\` is planned.\n- **GV-5: Landed → Partial.** The same document marks \\`mcp.allow\\`, \\`mcp.disable_workspace\\`, \\`plugins.allow\\` and \\`plugins.disable_workspace\\` \\\"not yet\\\": accepted, enforcing nothing.\n- **VR-2:** landed, with the six open findings from its second review named.\n- **Added rows:** SB-1 (open), MT-2 (open), MT-1 (not measured here). **PA-3** moved out of \\\"stretch\\\": #706 landed part, #758 is in review with changes requested.\n- **G-1, G-3:** what was and was not measured, including that the real-server LSP suite and the smoke run only on \\`main\\` by schedule and were dispatched by hand on this branch.\n- The thin-RC proposal now says GV-1 and GV-5 are partial, so the notes must say so or the units must be finished first.\n\nA release decision should not be read off rows that say more than the branch holds.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\" | tail -1; echo \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ) NOTE + PR (claude-invariants-audit): #757 was merged at 22:12Z by another session with my REQUEST CHANGES unapplied, so the readiness inventory on the release branch lists GV-1 and GV-5 as Landed although docs/MANAGED_POLICY.md says otherwise. Opened a docs-only correction PR from ~/nexus-wt/readyfix (v1/readiness-corrections). That is the fifth PR merged outside the queue today (#741, #749, #754, #756, #757), three of them over open review findings.\" >> \"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log\"","description":"Correct the inventory rows, commit, open the PR and log it"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011ChLdQkPfYqpFpqVgxeb5X","requestRef":"48ff61bd-03af-4109-831a-93ae45ef0120","requestedModel":"claude-fable-5-2","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"210077a5-c38c-4276-b354-4b6337d0529f","timestamp":"2026-11-23T22:13:26.655Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"main","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
