p10_inference_submission_budget.test.ts']`. The PR's new test builds an agent or gateway and has no guard or baseline entry.\n- Fix: add the leak guard to the test, or list it in `cli/test/leak_guard_baseline.json`.\n- I did not run this file on base. The failure names the PR's own new file, so it comes from this PR.\n\n**CI at `75a838be`** (run 45279103535, failed shards 22/24 × 1/2). The failing tests, by name:\n- \"checked-in ACP adapter schema equals a fresh generation\": fixed by `f4abea7a`. `acp_schema` passes 7/7.\n- \"gen_acp_schema.mjs --check passes on the checked-in schema and ledger\": fixed, same file.\n- \"checked-in schema samples equal a fresh generation\": still failing.\n- \"the leak ratchet holds\": still failing.\n- \"record shard execution\": fails on all 8 shard jobs. It appears to be a reporter step, not a test. I did not investigate it.\n- The current head's runs are still in progress, so I haven't seen their results.\n\n**Non-blocking items**\n- Docs now say retries count and availability probes don't. The counter persists with the objective, and the ceiling covers the primary turn only, not delegated inference.\n- The plan progress note says delegated paths remain outside the bound.\n- Still not stated: findings extraction and the compaction calls are not counted. Also missing: a project `.env` can set `NEXUS_MAX_INFERENCE_SUBMISSIONS`.\n\n**Earlier guarantees:** I only reran the tests; I did not re-read the code. `p10_inference_submission_budget` passes 4/4. The delta is schema and version metadata only, so nothing in `src/` that enforces the budget changed.\n\n**Mutation:** I replaced the `admitted` line in `execution_tracking.ts` so any request is admitted, then ran `p10_inference_submission_budget`. It failed 1 of 4. I restored the file with `git checkout`.\n\n**Test counts at head**\n\n| File | Pass | Fail |\n|---|---|---|\n| `p10_inference_submission_budget` | 4 | 0 |\n| `protocol_parity` | 4 | 1 |\n| `protocol_schema` | 8 | 0 |\n| `r