{"parentUuid":"4fe321bd-7b32-4fa6-a86a-fbe596aa7ad4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011ChLpsVpMM1C6WR1sh4VfG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RADtJ5h7AjNXxnHxwYUDnx","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Third review PR #758","subagent_type":"reviewer","prompt":"Third-round review of GitHub PR #758 in the repo at ~/nexus-code (`gh pr view 758 --comments`, `gh pr diff 758`), \"fix(goal): pause stale boot goals with visible reason (PA-3 slice)\", base `release/v1.3.0`. The previous review (the comment beginning \"Re-review at `725a4435…`\") requested changes. The author pushed a new head (short `9b637c48`; take the full SHA from `gh pr view 758 --json headRefOid`, review exactly that, and check at the end whether it moved). See `git diff 725a4435..<new> -- cli docs`.\n\nVerify by running:\n1. BLOCKER from last round: `cli/test/operation_entry_integrity.test.ts` (\"a stale snapshot … not written back over COMPLETE\") failed at 725a4435 (2 pass, 1 fail: PAUSED instead of COMPLETE) and passed on `origin/release/v1.3.0`. Cause: `cli/src/core/operation.ts` (~570) plans operations as RUNNING with no owner identity, and `driveOperation` in `cli/src/core/operation_runner.ts` (~735-745) treated any existing RUNNING operation without identity as stale, so a freshly planned operation resumed via `operation_cli.ts:391`, `loop.ts:471` or `batch.ts:223` could be paused before it ever ran. Run that test file now. Then check the fix's logic: which operations does `driveOperation` now treat as stale, and can a freshly planned, never-run operation still be paused? Conversely, did the fix reopen the original hole: a goal left RUNNING / WAITING / BLOCKED by a dead process, or with no identity at all (state written before this PR), must still come back PAUSED through `goalStatus` (probe the real functions with seeded state in a throwaway HOME, as `cli/test/goal_lifecycle.test.ts` does); a goal whose owner process is alive must not be paused or stolen; PAUSED / COMPLETE / CANCELLED must be left alone.\n2. Is there now a test on the `driveOperation` stale path (search the tests for `pauseForStaleDriver` / `stale_driver` / \"Paused on resume\")? Mutate: remove the goal-level stale check and, separately, the driveOperation-level one; `cli/test/goal_lifecycle.test.ts` and whichever operation test covers it must fail; restore with `git checkout`.\n3. Status of earlier non-blocking items: the doc `docs/v1.3.0/PA3_GOAL_LIFECYCLE.md` states the limits (a reused pid reads as alive; a state from another host, or with a pid and no host, stays RUNNING; boot id only); `pauseReason ?? stale` precedence; the reason text wording; the early `return` without `/proc` in the host-boot test; the `(state as any)` casts.\n4. Nothing in the delta lets model text, a tool call or workspace content change a goal's lifecycle, and nothing loosens approval, budget or managed-policy checks (`cli/src/core/policy_runtime.ts`).\n5. Run at head, one file at a time: every `cli/test/goal*.test.ts` and `cli/test/operation*.test.ts`, plus `cli/test/leak_guard.test.ts` (new test files must register the leak guard) and any test file the delta adds. For any failure, check the same file on `origin/release/v1.3.0`.\n\nMandatory rules:\n- Do NOT edit ~/nexus-code or existing worktrees. `git -C ~/nexus-code fetch origin && git -C ~/nexus-code worktree add --detach ~/nexus-wt/rev758c <full sha>`; `cp -a ~/nexus-code/cli/node_modules ~/nexus-wt/rev758c/cli/`; copy `~/nexus-wt/ls1b/core/target/release/{harness-core,nexus-tui}` into `~/nexus-wt/rev758c/core/target/release/`. Remove the worktree at the end (`git -C ~/nexus-code worktree remove --force ~/nexus-wt/rev758c`). No commits, pushes or GitHub comments.\n- Every run uses a throwaway HOME: `cd cli && HOME=$(mktemp -d) node --import tsx --test test/<name>.test.ts 2>&1 | tail -20`, foreground, one file at a time, timeout at most 9 minutes (the runner prints `ℹ pass` / `ℹ fail`). Probe scripts live in a separate scratch directory. Never read the real ~/.nexus, /etc/nexus or ~/.config/nexus. No live inference, no network.\n- Stop every process you start by its own pid; never `pkill -f`. No background loops. Aim for about 30 minutes.\n- Shell is zsh (use `bash -c` for loops); output passes through `rtk` (use `rtk proxy <cmd>` if it looks filtered).\n\nReport under 450 words: verdict (ACCEPT / ACCEPT WITH FOLLOW-UPS / REQUEST CHANGES) at the exact full SHA; the blocker fixed or not and what you ran; whether the original restart protection still holds; status of non-blocking items; new findings ranked, blocking vs not; mutation results; test counts; what you did not check."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":534,"cache_read_input_tokens":546792,"output_tokens":1900,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":534,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1900,"cache_read_input_tokens":546792,"cache_creation_input_tokens":534,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":534},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.2.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"}],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":15250,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01RADtJ5h7AjNXxnHxwYUDnx":{"description":"Third review PR #758","subagent_type":"reviewer","prompt":"Third-round review of GitHub PR #758 in the repo at ~/nexus-code (`gh pr view 758 --comments`, `gh pr diff 758`), \"fix(goal): pause stale boot goals with visible reason (PA-3 slice)\", base `release/v1.3.0`. The previous rev