{"parentUuid":"b6109e7d-8359-41ce-a88c-cf914fdc895a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011ChLtvzY4HV4KCbSUzmRbz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016MJajbgRg51PvFy1prr1bB","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-code && gh pr comment 763 --body \"**Check at \\`a18ec4c9\\` — ACCEPT WITH FOLLOW-UPS, pending green required checks on this head.**\n\nThe blocker is resolved as \\\"intended\\\": \\`flight_sanitization.test.ts\\` now asserts that after a classifier failure the log holds only \\`recording_gap\\` rows, each with exactly \\`reason\\` and \\`recordingSkipped\\`, that the secret is absent, and that the log loads as \\`recordingSkipped: true\\`. Run at this head: \\`flight_sanitization\\` 3/3, \\`hash_chain\\` 28/28. The commit changes that test file only.\n\nOpen follow-ups from the review above, in order of weight:\n\n1. When the gap marker cannot be written either (the disk-failure case), a restart still reads as \\\"chain intact, closed\\\". \\`docs/AUDIT.md\\` does not state this limit; it should, or the flag needs a second home.\n2. A skip on the first record exports as \\`unchained\\` and \\`audit verify\\` returns exit 0 with only a note; the bundle carries nothing about the skip.\n3. One failed redaction still ends chaining for the rest of the session.\n4. \\`docs/AUDIT.md\\` should say the new verifier can turn an existing bundle's verdict from \\`intact_unsigned\\` to \\`tampered\\` when its exported log was already broken.\" | tail -1; bash -c 'for i in $(seq 1 17); do c=$(gh pr checks 763 2>&1 | grep -E \"^(test-matrix|linux-x86_64)\" | grep -c pass); f=$(gh pr checks 763 2>&1 | grep -E \"^test-|^linux\" | grep -c fail); [ \"$c\" = 3 ] && break; [ \"$f\" != 0 ] && break; sleep 30; done; gh pr checks 763 2>&1 | grep -E \"^test-matrix|^linux-x86_64|^test-.*(fail|pending)\" | cut -c1-55; gh pr view 763 --json headRefOid,state --jq \"[.state,.headRefOid]|@tsv\"; git fetc