{"parentUuid":"992f00f6-835a-4b54-9752-c34fda00aa05","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011ChLvNfRCXik3KDv1ctCcF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"#763 is merged and the release branch is green at `c2faaa89`. No PRs are open.\n\n**#763 (flight recording gaps), merged after review**\n- **What it adds:**\n  - a skipped record now leaves a durable marker, so a restart no longer hides it;\n  - the operator gets a one-time warning when recording degrades;\n  - `audit verify` fails a bundle whose exported log was already broken.\n- **Blocker, fixed before merge:** an existing test asserted that a sanitizer failure leaves no log file, and the new marker creates one. The author changed the test to assert that only gap markers are written and that none carries the payload. I ran it at the final head; it passes.\n- **Follow-ups on the PR, none blocking:**\n  - **Disk failure still hides a skip.** If the marker itself can't be written, a restart reads as an intact chain again, and the docs don't say so.\n  - **First-record skip passes verification.** It exports as \"unchained\", and `audit verify` exits 0 with only a note.\n  - **Chaining stays off.** One failed redaction still ends chaining for the rest of the session.\n\n**Merged by me after review since the quota pause:** #758, #759, #760, #761, #762, #763.\n\n**What still stands between here and landing v1.3.0, unchanged**\n- **Unbuilt:** PF-3, PF-4, SB-1, MT-2, BG-1, BG-2, HK-1 to HK-3, PA-2.\n- **Unfinished:** GV-1 slices 3–4, the GV-5 allowlists, the six VR-2 follow-ups.\n- **Yours:** which units roll to v1.4, then the go-ahead for the merge to `main` and the release-candidate tag."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":385,"cache_read_input_tokens":573755,"output_tokens":570,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_searc