{"parentUuid":"54b45096-0aa7-454f-9674-96d2e0602f63","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011ChLvo6zzV66cQG2rMaPRS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I reviewed follow-up PR #764 myself, confirmed its tests fail when the new check is disabled, and am posting my verdict now while its checks run.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1025,"cache_read_input_tokens":576635,"output_tokens":1174,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1025,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1174,"cache_read_input_tokens":576635,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1025,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1025},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":10,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011ChLvo6XiWM6mUEoWjnyEZ","requestRef":"7f9ac045-570e-4e43-b361-4e149b9d1730","requestedModel":"claude-fable-5-2","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"bc7659ef-6354-4669-8bd6-dac1335a4f9f","timestamp":"2026-11-24T02:01:07.310Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"main","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
{"parentUuid":"bc7659ef-6354-4669-8bd6-dac1335a4f9f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011ChLvo6zzV66cQG2rMaPRS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01B71JqfJHJaWWzH3GqNKDbT","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-code && gh pr comment 764 --body \"**Review at \\`5e5bb11f\\` (read and run by me; +52/−1) — ACCEPT, pending green required checks.**\n\nIt closes three of the follow-ups left on #763:\n\n- **A skip on the first record no longer verifies clean.** \\`audit verify\\` adds \\`log_recording_gap_at_export\\` whenever an exported flight log holds a \\`recording_gap\\` marker, including when no chained record precedes it. With that check disabled, \\`audit_bundle\\` fails 1 of 25 and \\`audit_command\\` 1 of 8.\n- **The unwritable-marker limit is now stated** in \\`docs/AUDIT.md\\`: if the recorder cannot persist the marker either, the log alone cannot show the skip; the operator warning is the only record.\n- **The verdict change on existing bundles and the closed-enum caveat are documented**, with a new ledger entry at \\`schema_version\\` 1.\n\nRun at this head: \\`audit_bundle\\` 25/25, \\`audit_command\\` 8/8, \\`audit_schema\\` 7/7, \\`audit_export\\` 18/18, \\`tsc\\` clean.\n\nStill open from #761/#763, unchanged here: one failed redaction ends chaining for the rest of the session, and a marker-less disk failure followed by a restart reads as intact (now documented rather than fixed).\n\nNot checked: Node 22 locally, a signed bundle.\" | tail -1; bash -c 'for i in $(seq 1 17); do c=$(gh pr checks 764 2>&1 | grep -E \"^(test-matrix|linux-x86_64)\" | grep -c pass); f=$(gh pr checks 764 2>&1 | grep -E \"^test-|^linux\" | grep -c fail); [ \"$c\" = 3 ] && break; [ \"$f\" != 0 ] && break; sleep 30; done; gh pr checks 764 2>&1 | grep -E \"^test-matrix|^linux-x86_64|^test-.*(fail|pending)\" | cut -c1-55; gh pr view 764 --json headRefOid,state --jq \"[.state,.headRefOid]|@tsv\"; git fetch -q origin; echo \"tip $(git rev-parse --short origin/release/v1.3.0)\"; m=$(gh api repos/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pulls/764 --jq .merge_commit_sha); git fetch -q origin $m 2>/dev/null; echo \"merge parents: $(git log -1 --format=%P $m | tr \" \" \"\\n\" | cut -c1-8 | tr \"\\n\" \" \")\"; gh run list --branch release/v1.3.0 --workflow ci.yml --limit 1 --json status,conclusion,headSha --jq \".[0]|[.status,.conclusion,.headSha[0:8]]|@tsv\"'","description":"Post the verdict on PR 764, wait for its checks, and re-read the release state","timeout":590000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1025,"cache_read_input_tokens":576635,"output_tokens":1174,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1025,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1174,"cache_read_input_tokens":576635,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1025,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1025},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":7489,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01B71JqfJHJaWWzH3GqNKDbT":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-code && gh pr comment 764 --body \"**Review at \\`5e5bb11f\\` (read and run by me; +52/−1) — ACCEPT, pending green required checks.**\n\nIt closes three of the follow-ups left on #763:\n\n- **A skip on the first record no longer verifies clean.** \\`audit verify\\` adds \\`log_recording_gap_at_export\\` whenever an exported flight log holds a \\`recording_gap\\` marker, including when no chained record precedes it. With that check disabled, \\`audit_bundle\\` fails 1 of 25 and \\`audit_command\\` 1 of 8.\n- **The unwritable-marker limit is now stated** in \\`docs/AUDIT.md\\`: if the recorder cannot persist the marker either, the log alone cannot show the skip; the operator warning is the only record.\n- **The verdict change on existing bundles and the closed-enum caveat are documented**, with a new ledger entry at \\`schema_version\\` 1.\n\nRun at this head: \\`audit_bundle\\` 25/25, \\`audit_command\\` 8/8, \\`audit_schema\\` 7/7, \\`audit_export\\` 18/18, \\`tsc\\` clean.\n\nStill open from #761/#763, unchanged here: one failed redaction ends chaining for the rest of the session, and a marker-less disk failure followed by a restart reads as intact (now documented rather than fixed).\n\nNot checked: Node 22 locally, a signed bundle.\" | tail -1; bash -c 'for i in $(seq 1 17); do c=$(gh pr checks 764 2>&1 | grep -E \"^(test-matrix|linux-x86_64)\" | grep -c pass); f=$(gh pr checks 764 2>&1 | grep -E \"^test-|^linux\" | grep -c fail); [ \"$c\" = 3 ] && break; [ \"$f\" != 0 ] && break; sleep 30; done; gh pr checks 764 2>&1 | grep -E \"^test-matrix|^linux-x86_64|^test-.*(fail|pending)\" | cut -c1-55; gh pr view 764 --json headRefOid,state --jq \"[.state,.headRefOid]|@tsv\"; git fetch -q origin; echo \"tip $(git rev-parse --short origin/release/v1.3.0)\"; m=$(gh api repos/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pulls/764 --jq .merge_commit_sha); git fetch -q origin $m 2>/dev/null; echo \"merge parents: $(git log -1 --format=%P $m | tr \" \" \"\\n\" | cut -c1-8 | tr \"\\n\" \" \")\"; gh run list --branch release/v1.3.0 --workflow ci.yml --limit 1 --json status,conclusion,headSha --jq \".[0]|[.status,.conclusion,.headSha[0:8]]|@tsv\"'","description":"Post the verdict on PR 764, wait for its checks, and re-read the release state","timeout":590000}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011ChLvo6XiWM6mUEoWjnyEZ","requestRef":"7f9ac045-570e-4e43-b361-4e149b9d1730","requestedModel":"claude-fable-5-2","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"c3aedbb8-06fd-4236-9b50-7a141d6df1ba","timestamp":"2026-11-