{"parentUuid":"999d93a0-9fd7-4ab5-a28f-3978933cdf4c","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"fe8cdc99-57c4-4dc1-a999-66e8e4b40dda","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NPvSfuDYosuPzonstjHo3h","type":"tool_result","content":"-`NEXUS_MAX_INFERENCE_SUBMISSIONS` sets a finite objective-wide provider request ceiling (default 1,000; hard maximum\n-10,000). Provider retries count before dispatch; availability probes do not. The consumed count and chosen ceiling persist\n-with the objective, so a later run cannot raise an exhausted budget. Older saved objectives report earlier request\n-history as unknown; only requests made after this counter was introduced are counted exactly. This ceiling currently\n-covers the primary objective turn; delegated inference and durable operation work units still need shared accounting.\n-Malformed persisted counters or ceilings stop before inference dispatch.\n+`NEXUS_MAX_INFERENCE_SUBMISSIONS` sets a provider request ceiling (default 1,000; hard maximum 10,000). It can be set\n+in a project `.env`, so a project may raise the default up to that hard maximum; on resume, the saved ceiling can only\n+stay the same or decrease. The ceiling currently counts requests made by the primary turn's provider-recovery loop,\n+including retries, before dispatch; availability probes do not count. It does **not** yet cap all provider use: context\n+findings extraction, LLM compaction summaries and their requirement probes, delegated `spawn_subagent` calls, and\n+durable operation work units do not share this counter. Without durable objective state, the counter is in-memory and\n+resets on each turn. With durable objective state, the primary-turn count and ceiling persist with the objective.\n+Older saved objectives report earlier request history as unknown; only requests made after this counter was introduced\n+are counted exactly. Malformed persisted counters or ceilings stop before a counted inference dispatch.\n-**Progress (2026-11-23, merged PR #760):** Primary objective turns reserve every inference request, including provider recovery retries, against a persisted objective ceiling (default 1,000; hard maximum 10,000). Persistence failure prevents dispatch; resume can lower but not raise the saved ceiling; legacy records expose earlier inference history as unknown. The feature test and all required exact-head checks passed at merge commit `51bf3db79fdadca26dbde6bbf752c9982c7793e3`; both post-merge CI runs also passed on\n+**Progress (2026-11-23, merged PR #760):** The primary turn's provider-recovery loop reserves each request, including retries, against a persisted objective ceiling (default 1,000; hard maximum 10,000). Persistence failure prevents dispatch; resume can lower but not raise the saved ceiling; legacy records expose earlier inference history as unknown. The feature test and all required exact-head checks passed at merge commit `51bf3db79fdadca26dbde6bbf752c9982c7793e3`; post-merge CI passed on that merge commit. This \n188:  \"NEXUS_MAX_INFERENCE_SUBMISSIONS\",\n829:  const raw = options.maxInferenceSubmissions ?? effectiveSetting(\"NEXUS_MAX_INFERENCE_SUBMISSIONS\");\n44:import { TurnResult, VerificationEvidence, TypecheckEvidence, InterruptionRecord, InferenceFailure, CapacityRecord, M\n2739:  private summarizeDiscardedHistory(messages: ChatMessage[], detailBudgetChars: number, unseen: ReadonlySet<ChatMes\n3166:    const summary = this.summarizeDiscardedHistory(messagesToSummarize.map(({ message }) => message), detailBudgetC\n3783:            content: \"You are an AI context summarizer. Distill the conversation into concise engineering bullet po\n4965:    return { completed: false, summary, reason: summarizeTurn(turn).line };","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"f709f61b-b821-4562-a51c-bc5b08ef1556","timestamp":"2026-11-24T02:23:53.604Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"-`NEXUS_MAX_INFERENCE_SUBMISSIONS` sets a finite objective-wide provider request ceiling (default 1,000; hard maximum\n-10,000). Provider retries count before dispatch; availability probes do not. The consumed count and chosen ceiling persist\n-with the objective, so a later run cannot raise an exhausted budget. Older saved objectives report earlier request\n-history as unknown; only requests made after this counter was introduced are counted exactly. This ceiling currently\n-covers the primary objective turn; delegated inference and durable operation work units still need shared accounting.\n-Malformed persisted counters or ceilings stop before inference dispatch.\n+`NEXUS_MAX_INFERENCE_SUBMISSIONS` sets a provider request ceiling (default 1,000; hard maximum 10,000). It can be set\n+in a project `.env`, so a project may raise the default up to that hard maximum; on resume, the saved ceiling can only\n+stay the same or decrease. The ceiling currently counts requests made by the primary turn's provider-recovery loop,\n+including retries, before dispatch; availability probes do not count. It does **not** yet cap all provider use: context\n+findings extraction, LLM compaction summaries and their requirement probes, delegated `spawn_subagent` calls, and\n+durable operation work units do not share this counter. Without durable objective state, the counter is in-memory and\n+resets on each turn. With durable objective state, the primary-turn count and ceiling persist with the objective.\n+Older saved objectives report earlier request history as unknown; only requests made after this counter was introduced\n+are counted exactly. Malformed persisted counters or ceilings stop before a counted inference dispatch.\n-**Progress (2026-11-23, merged PR #760):** Primary objective turns reserve every inference request, including provider recovery retries, against a persisted objective ceiling (default 1,000; hard maximum 10,000). Persistence failure prevents dispatch; resume can lower but not raise the saved ceiling; legacy records expose earlier inference history as unknown. The feature test and all required exact-head checks passed at merge commit `51bf3db79fdadca26dbde6bbf752c9982c7793e3`; both post-merge CI runs also passed on\n+**Progress (2026-11-23, merged PR #760):** The primary turn's provider-recovery loop reserves each request, including retries, against a persisted objective ceiling (default 1,000; hard maximum 10,000). Persistence failure prevents dispatch; resume can lower but not raise the saved ceiling; legacy records expose earlier inference history as unknown. The feature test and all required exact-head checks passed at merge commit `51bf3db79fdadca26dbde6bbf752c9982c7793e3`; post-merge CI passed on that merge commit. This \n188:  \"NEXUS_MAX_INFERENCE_SUBMISSIONS\",\n829:  const raw = options.maxInferenceSubmissions ?? effectiveSetting(\"NEXUS_MAX_INFERENCE_SUBMISSIONS\");\n44:import { TurnResult, VerificationEvidence, TypecheckEvidence, InterruptionRecord, InferenceFailure, CapacityRecord, M\n2739:  private summarizeDiscardedHistory(messages: ChatMessage[], detailBudgetChars: number, unseen: ReadonlySet<ChatMes\n3166:    const summary = this.summarizeDiscardedHistory(messagesToSummarize.map(({ message }) => message), detailBudgetC\n3783:            content: \"You are an AI context summarizer. Distill the conversation into concise engineering bullet po\n4965:    return { completed: false, summary, reason: summarizeTurn(turn).line };","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"999d93a0-9fd7-4ab5-a28f-3978933cdf4c","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"main","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
