{"parentUuid":"14135867-625e-4c44-a122-21e22c3c523f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011ChM1pbKTCxnA5SFaag4xL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"A new PR arrived, #766: a CI gate on function complexity. It touches the Makefile and adds a dependency, so I'm sending it for an independent review that includes the dependency change."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":965,"cache_read_input_tokens":593355,"output_tokens":2636,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":93},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":965,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2636,"cache_read_input_tokens":593355,"cache_creation_input_tokens":965,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":965},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011ChM1pajy8mJ9ibFuo4uJV","requestRef":"e6e7051d-c87c-4339-b65e-b417636414b6","requestedModel":"claude-fable-5-2","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"04eedd72-e439-4568-84f0-2111c842635a","timestamp":"2026-11-24T03:07:01.635Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"main","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
{"parentUuid":"04eedd72-e439-4568-84f0-2111c842635a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011ChM1pbKTCxnA5SFaag4xL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Am51M9bLBiyDWqzoNeX5iJ","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Review PR #766 complexity gate","subagent_type":"reviewer","prompt":"Independent pre-merge review of GitHub PR #766 in the repo at ~/nexus-code (`gh pr view 766`, `gh pr diff 766`), \"ci: gate critical function complexity against release baseline\", base `release/v1.3.0`. Take the full head SHA from `gh pr view 766 --json headRefOid`, review exactly that, and check at the end whether it moved. Files: `Makefile`, `cli/critical-complexity-baseline.json`, `cli/package.json`, `cli/package-lock.json`, `cli/scripts/check_critical_complexity.ts`, `cli/test/critical_complexity.test.ts`, `docs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md` (+326/−0).\n\nContext: work package WP-P10-05 of `docs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md` (static analysis / complexity gate: \"a changed critical function crossing an agreed, baseline-derived CC/nesting threshold fails a focused check\"). CI structure (`.github/workflows/ci.yml` on the base): `test-gates` (Node 22 and 24) runs `make lint` and other gates; `test-shard` legs run the CLI suite in four shards; `test-matrix (22|24)` aggregate; `linux-x86_64` packages. `cli/test/release_workflow_parity.test.ts` pins that structure.\n\nAnswer with file:line evidence, running things where practical:\n1. Dependency change: `cli/package.json` / `package-lock.json` — what was added (name, version, dev or runtime dependency, transitive packages)? Is it a devDependency only (it must not ship in the packaged CLI: check how `scripts/package-linux.sh` installs/prunes dependencies and whether the new package would be included in the release tarball)? Licence compatible with the repo's policy (see `deny.toml` for Rust and how npm licences are checked, e.g. `scripts/check_notices.mjs`, THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES generation in `scripts/package-linux.sh`)? Does the lockfile pass `node scripts/check_deprecated_lock.mjs cli/package-lock.json` and keep `engines`/lockfile metadata consistent (a past incident: a stale `engines.node` in the lockfile broke CI)? Any install scripts in the new packages? Do NOT run `npm install` against the network; inspect the lockfile diff and, if the package is already present in `~/nexus-code/cli/node_modules`, read it there (say if it is not present and what you therefore could not run).\n2. Where does the gate run? Does `make lint` (or whatever Makefile target changed) now run it, and therefore `test-gates` in CI on both Node versions? Does it also run where it should not (the packaging job, `release.yml`)? Time cost of the check (run it and time it). Does `release_workflow_parity.test.ts` still pass?\n3. The check itself (`cli/scripts/check_critical_complexity.ts`): what does it measure (cyclomatic complexity? nesting?), for which functions (how is \"critical\" defined: a hand list in the baseline, or derived?), and what fails: any increase over baseline, or crossing a threshold? Can it be bypassed trivially (renaming a function, moving code to a helper not on the list, a function missing from the baseline passing silently, a parse error being swallowed, deleting the baseline entry in the same PR)? Is the baseline updated only deliberately (is there an `--update` mode, and does CI ever run it)? Does a function that no longer exists fail or pass? Fail-closed on unreadable/malformed baseline?\n4. Baseline (`cli/critical-complexity-baseline.json`): which functions, what numbers; regenerate it with the script (if it has a mode for that, in the throwaway worktree) and confirm it matches the checked-in file at this head. Is `runTurnImpl` (named in the plan as \"a critical large function\") covered?\n5. Tests (`cli/test/critical_complexity.test.ts`): do they fail if the gate is made to always pass? Mutate (then `git checkout`). Does the test file itself run inside a CI shard without needing the network? Does it register in `cli/scripts/test_durations.json`/the shard assignment correctly (a file missing from the durations manifest is assigned how? see `cli/scripts/test_shards.mjs`)?\n6. Run at head, one file at a time: `critical_complexity`, `release_workflow_parity`, `leak_guard`, `check_requirements`, plus `make lint` semantics as far as possible without cargo if cargo/clippy is too slow (say what you skipped), `node scripts/check_deprecated_lock.mjs cli/package-lock.json`, `node scripts/check_invariants.mjs`, `cd cli && npx tsc --noEmit -p .`.\n7. Docs: does the plan text claim only what the code and tests show?\n\nMandatory rules:\n- Do NOT edit ~/nexus-code or existing worktrees. `git -C ~/nexus-code fetch origin && git -C ~/nexus-code worktree add --detach ~/nexus-wt/rev766 <full sha>`; `cp -a ~/nexus-code/cli/node_modules ~/nexus-wt/rev766/cli/` (this copy will NOT contain a newly added package unless it was already installed; do not run npm install/ci against the network — if the check cannot run without the new package, report exactly that and review by reading); copy `~/nexus-wt/ls1b/core/target/release/{harness-core,nexus-tui}` into `~/nexus-wt/rev766/core/target/release/`. Remove the worktree at the end (`git -C ~/nexus-code worktree remove --force ~/nexus-wt/rev766`). No commits, pushes or GitHub comments.\n- Every run uses a throwaway HOME: `cd cli && HOME=$(mktemp -d) node --import tsx --test test/<name>.test.ts 2>&1 | tail -20`, foreground, one file at a time, timeout at most 9 minutes (the runner prints `ℹ pass` / `ℹ fail`). Never read the real ~/.nexus, /etc/nexus or ~/.config/nexus. No live inference.\n- Stop every process you start by its own pid; never `pkill -f`. No background loops. Aim for about 30 minutes.\n- Shell is zsh (use `bash -c` for loops; `$PIPESTATUS` is empty in zsh); output passes through `rtk` (use `rtk proxy <cmd>` if it looks filtered).\n\nReport under 550 words: verdict (ACCEPT / ACCEPT WITH FOLLOW-UPS / REQUEST CHANGES) at the exact full SHA; the dependency facts; where the gate runs and its cost; bypasses found, ranked; other findings with file:line, each marked confirmed-by-running or by-reading, blocking vs non-blocking; mutation results; test counts; what you could not run and why."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":965,"cache_read_input_tokens":593355,"output_tokens":2636,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":93},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":965,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2636,"cache_read_input_tokens":593355,"cache_creation_input_tokens":965,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":965},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":22708,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Am51M9bLBiyDWqzoNeX5iJ":{"description":"Review PR #766 complexity gate","subagent_type":"reviewer","prompt":"Independent pre-merge review of GitHub PR #766 in the repo at ~/nexus-code (`gh pr view 766`, `gh pr diff 766`), \"ci: gate critical function complexity against release baseline\", base `release/v1.3.0`. Take the full head SHA from `gh pr view 766 --json headRefOid`, review exactly that, and check at the end whether it moved. Files: `Makefile`, `cli/critical-complexity-baseline.json`, `cli/package.json`, `cli/package-lock.json`, `cli/scripts/check_critical_complexity.ts`, `cli/test/critical_complexity.test.ts`, `docs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md` (+326/−0).\n\nContext: work package WP-P10-05 of `docs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION