{"parentUuid":"489609eb-25bd-4bbd-aef3-f2d02d73c5ec","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011ChM9B5cAgogKjypZWMLyC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":719,"cache_read_input_tokens":645026,"output_tokens":3045,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":122},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":719,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3045,"cache_read_input_tokens":645026,"cache_creation_input_tokens":719,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":719},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":1418,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011ChM9B5PXACxMAb4FviDBs","requestRef":"d20cec09-20bd-4009-9827-03e346f6ce96","requestedModel":"claude-fable-5-2","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"2247cb46-281c-4c17-8024-f9787d209640","timestamp":"2026-11-24T04:43:26.995Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"main","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
{"parentUuid":"2247cb46-281c-4c17-8024-f9787d209640","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011ChM9B5cAgogKjypZWMLyC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RYf9vt4wfBo1XpB2vQeekE","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Review PR #770 kill tree fix","subagent_type":"reviewer","prompt":"Independent review of GitHub PR #770 in the repo at ~/nexus-code (`gh pr view 770`, `gh pr diff 770`), \"fix(verify): stop the process tree before signalling it, and remember what was seen\", base `release/v1.3.0`. Take the full head SHA from `gh pr view 770 --json headRefOid`, review exactly that, and check at the end whether it moved or was merged. The change is confined to `forkRunner` / `signalTree` / `descendants` / a new `startedAt` in `cli/src/core/verify_service.ts` (+56/−15). Read the PR description first; it explains the two escape routes it closes (a fork after the single process listing; a sandbox handed to init when its parent dies of SIGTERM while it ignores the signal) and reports a cancel loop: 340 runs, 0 orphans, against about 1 in 70 before.\n\nThe mechanism: every signal stage (SIGTERM; after a grace SIGKILL of descendants with the worker spared; after another grace SIGKILL of everything; plus a new sweep in `finish` when a cancelled worker exits, plus `onProcessExit`) first sends SIGSTOP to the worker and, pass by pass (up to `KILL_LISTING_PASSES`), to every descendant found, until a listing adds nothing; then sends the stage's signal; then SIGCONT to what is not being killed. Every pid seen is remembered with its kernel start time from `/proc/<pid>/stat`; a remembered pid whose start time still matches is used as an extra root in later listings and signalled even when it is no longer below the worker.\n\nTry to find what is wrong with it. Answer with file:line, by running where practical:\n1. Can it signal a process that is NOT part of this verification? Consider: pid reuse between remembering and signalling (is the start-time comparison sufficient; what if `startedAt` returns undefined at record time — is the pid then never remembered, or remembered with undefined and matched against undefined later?); the parsing of `/proc/<pid>/stat` (field 22 after the last `)`; a process name containing `)` or spaces); `survivors()` used as roots, then `descendants(roots)`: if a remembered pid was reparented to init, are init's other children ever pulled in (they must not be: roots' descendants only)? What if a remembered pid IS reused by an unrelated process with (impossibly) the same start time? Could pid 1, the server itself, or the MCP/ACP client ever be in `seen`?\n2. Can it leave a process stopped forever (SIGSTOP sent, then neither killed nor continued)? Walk every path: SIGTERM stage (CONT to all stopped and to the worker); SIGKILL with `worker=false` (descendants killed; worker continued?); SIGKILL with worker (nothing continued, everything killed — is the worker always killed even if the pass loop hits its limit?); `KILL_LISTING_PASSES` exhausted with fresh pids still appearing (are those extra pids stopped-but-not-signalled, or never stopped?); an exception thrown mid-way (e.g. `spawnSync(\"ps\")` failing or timing out at 5 s — returns empty listing: then what is stopped/continued?); `child.pid` undefined.\n3. Does stopping the worker before SIGTERM break the graceful path the earlier design relied on (the worker handles SIGTERM, lets `verifyChange` unwind at its `checkpoint()`, removes its scratch trees, reports `interrupted`, exits)? Run `cli/test/verify_service.test.ts` and `cli/test/mcp_verify.test.ts` and specifically confirm scratch directories are removed after a cancellation and after the watchdog timeout (the tests assert it; say which).\n4. The new sweep in `finish` (`if (signal.aborted) signalTree(\"SIGKILL\", false)`): it runs on every settle after an abort, including the normal case where the worker exited cleanly. Cost (it runs `ps` at least once, synchronously, up to 5 s timeout, on the server's event loop): acceptable? Could it kill a process the worker legitimately left behind on purpose (there should be none)? Does it run when the abort came from the watchdog timeout as well?\n5. `onProcessExit` now does the stop/list passes synchronously inside a process `exit` handler: fine, or can it hang server exit (multiple `ps` calls × 5 s timeout × passes)? Give the worst-case bound.\n6. Reproduce the measurement: the loop script is at `/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/loop.mts` (env: `WT=<worktree>`, `N=<runs>`, `TRAP=1` for a SIGTERM-ignoring verifier; run from `<worktree>/cli` with a throwaway HOME: `HOME=$(mktemp -d) WT=... N=120 TRAP=1 timeout 520 node --import tsx <loop.mts>`). Run one batch of 120 with TRAP=1 at the PR head and report orphans; also run a batch of 60 with a stopped-forever check added by you (after each cancellation, list processes carrying the run's marker in state `T` via `ps -o pid=,stat=,args=`) to catch finding 2 empirically. Copy the script before modifying it. Run only ONE loop at a time.\n7. Anything else in the diff: readability of the comments (they should explain why), dead code, and whether a unit test could cover any part deterministically (e.g. `startedAt` parsing, `descendants` with several roots) — suggest, don't write.\n\nMandatory rules:\n- Do NOT edit ~/nexus-code or existing worktrees. `git -C ~/nexus-code fetch origin && git -C ~/nexus-code worktree add --detach ~/nexus-wt/rev770 <full sha>`; `cp -a ~/nexus-code/cli/node_modules ~/nexus-wt/rev770/cli/`; copy `~/nexus-wt/ls1b/core/target/release/{harness-core,nexus-tui}` into `~/nexus-wt/rev770/core/target/release/`. Remove the worktree at the end (`git -C ~/nexus-code worktree remove --force ~/nexus-wt/rev770`). No commits, pushes or GitHub comments.\n- Every run uses a throwaway HOME; tests: `cd cli && HOME=$(mktemp -d) node --import tsx --test test/<name>.test.ts 2>&1 | tail -20`, foreground (`mcp_verify` takes about 3 minutes; allow 9). Never read the real ~/.nexus, /etc/nexus or ~/.config/nexus. No live inference, no network.\n- Stop every process you start by its own pid; never `pkill -f`. At the end, list any process whose args contain your loop's `sleep 7<pid>.` marker and kill it by pid; also make sure none is left in state T. Hard timeouts on everything. Aim for about 35 minutes.\n- Shell is zsh (use `bash -c` for loops; `$PIPESTATUS` is empty in zsh); output passes through `rtk` (use `rtk proxy <cmd>` if it looks filtered).\n\nReport under 500 words: verdict (ACCEPT / ACCEPT WITH FOLLOW-UPS / REQUEST CHANGES) at the exact SHA; findings ranked with file:line, confirmed-by-running or by-reading, blocking vs not; loop results (runs, orphans, stopped-forever); test counts; worst-case exit delay; what you did not check."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":719,"cache_read_input_tokens":645026,"output_tokens":3045,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":122},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":719,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3045,"cache_read_input_tokens":645026,"cache_creation_input_tokens":719,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":719},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":26880,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01RYf9vt4wfBo1XpB2vQeekE":{"description":"Review PR #770 kill tree fix","subagent_type":"reviewer","prompt":"Independent review of GitHub PR #770 in the repo at ~/nexus-code (`gh pr view 770`, `gh pr diff 770`), \"fix(verify): stop the process tree before s