{"parentUuid":"84cc2598-c92a-421b-8dd4-3c8742a37003","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"bcce610b-ace2-415b-a3ed-3201cc442273","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018UbgRP2oTVHuanu5EUviRq","type":"tool_result","content":"release/v1.3.0\tcodex/p10-03-audit-candidate-binding\t160\t7\tfeat(audit): bind exported receipts to the current candidate\tcli/src/audit_export.ts,cli/test/audit_export.test.ts,docs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md\n## Summary\n\n- Add `receipts/candidate-binding.json` to audit exports. It compares each persisted validation receipt's candidate digest with a bounded computation of the recorded workspace's current candidate identity.\n- Report `matched`, `mismatch`, `partial`, `no_receipts`, or `unavailable`; the human-readable export prints the status and mismatches or unknowns appear as warnings. The artifact explicitly says the comparison is a separate, non-atomic sample and does not establish verifier success or task acceptance.\n- Reuse the existing candidate identity and checkout-trust routines. Bound the scan to 50,000 entries and 256 MiB and the report to 10,000 receipts. Unsupported or untrusted checkouts fail to an unavailable result.\n- Add matching, post-validation mutation, unavailable workspace, and receipt-cap tests; update the approved implementation plan with the slice and its remaining ga","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"88177ce4-2b80-4417-a9c4-6b0f8a97181c","timestamp":"2026-11-24T05:43:30.589Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"release/v1.3.0\tcodex/p10-03-audit-candidate-binding\t160\t7\tfeat(audit): bind exported receipts to the current candidate\tcli/src/audit_export.ts,cli/test/audit_export.test.ts,docs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md\n## Summary\n\n- Add `receipts/candidate-binding.json` to audit exports. It compares each persisted validation receipt's candidate digest with a bounded computation of the recorded workspace's current candidate identity.\n- Report `matched`, `mismatch`, `partial`, `no_receipts`, or `unavailable`; the human-readable export prints the status and mismatches or unknowns appear as warnings. The artifact explicitly says the comparison is a separate, non-atomic sample and does not establish verifier success or task acceptance.\n- Reuse the existing candidate identity and checkout-trust routines. Bound the scan to 50,000 entries and 256 MiB and the report to 10,000 receipts. Unsupported or untrusted checkouts fail to an unavailable result.\n- Add matching, post-validation mutation, unavailable workspace, and receipt-cap tests; update the approved implementation plan with the slice and its remaining ga","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"84cc2598-c92a-421b-8dd4-3c8742a37003","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"main","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
