es not stop clean filters.\n   - The routine is shared and the exposure already exists, so this is not new in kind. The new part is `audit_export.ts:646-647`, where an auditor's `audit export` reads whatever workspace the state records.\n   - Fix: for the export, refuse a workspace whose `.git/config` or `.gitattributes` sets `filter.*`. Otherwise run git with `GIT_CONFIG_*` overrides that neutralise filters and fail closed. If you decline, document the exposure.\n   - `git rev-parse` and `git config --get` also run without the hardening flags.\n\n**Non-blocking findings**\n3. **Possible false mismatch, by reading.** `spine_handlers.ts:452` computes receipt candidates on `activeWorktree.worktreePath`. The export uses the recorded `workspacePath`. If these differ, every receipt reports `mismatch`. Please confirm they are the same directory, or say which one is used.\n4. **Warning on every receipt-less export, by reading.** `audit_export.ts` adds a warning for `no_receipts` on every export without receipts. Other no-op cases are quiet, so this is noisy and changes the warnings of existing bundles.\n5. **Exit status, by reading.** Warnings are only warnings, so a mismatch exits 0. It is visible in the printed text and in `warnings`. The PR doesn't state the policy and `docs/AUDIT.md` doesn't document it.\n6. **Docs, by reading.** `docs/AUDIT.md` isn't updated. The file list (line 70) and \"the two `receipts/` files\" (line 115) are now wrong. The plan text says tests are \"not yet run\", which will be stale once the tests pass.\n\n**Checked and fine**\n- **Digest inputs:** it is the same routine with the same defaults. The only difference is the lower limits, and those make it throw rather than produce a different digest.\n- **Bound hit:** it reports `unavailable` (reason `candidate_scan_limit_exceeded`), never `matched`.\n- **Receipt cap:** truncation gives `partial`, and a test covers it.\n- **Bundle integrity:** the new file goes through `generated()`. That applies redaction and the sensitive-content check, and the file gets a manifest hash like every other file. The role `validation_receipts` already exists, and `audit_schema` passes (7/0).\n- **Privacy and determinism:** the report holds ids and statuses only. `checked_at` is the bundle's `createdAt`. I saw no absolute paths.\n- **Compatibility:** the verifier checks roles generically, so an older bundle without the file should still verify.\n\n**Mutations on `audit_export.test.ts`** (baseline at head is 2 failures)\n- **Mismatch always reported as match:** caught. The binding test fails (3 failures).\n- **All three bounds raised:** caught, but only by the 10,001-receipt cap. No test builds a workspace over 50,000 entries or 256 MiB, so those two bounds are unproven.\n- **Untrusted-checkout refusal line removed:** not caught (same 2 failures as baseline). The git path re-checks inside `computeCandidateIdentitySync`, so the line is redundant there. There is also no test with an untrusted checkout.\n\n**Other results at head**\n- `audit_bundle` 25/0\n- `audit_schema` 7/0\n- `leak_guard` 6/0\n- `verify_hostile` 46/0\n- `check_requirements` 28/0\n- `tsc --noEmit` clean\n- `check_invariants` passed\n\n**Not checked**\n- Whether the byte-flip tamper test fails the verify step. I judged this by reading only.\n- An older `audit verify` binary against a new bundle.\n- Whether `audit_export` is a listed function in the complexity gate. I did not run `make lint` or the gate.\n- Symlink and submodule digest behaviour.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>63178</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>23</tool_uses><duration_ms>877174</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"},"uuid":"fe8e1005-6790-40aa-a70f-0f99ce9fc395","timestamp":"2026-11-24T05:58:34.965Z","permissionMode":"bypassPermissions","origin":{"kind":"task-notification","producer":"session-task","runId":"0mwu9ro52-5bb36b24"},"promptSource":"system","turnOrigin":"task_notification","turnPromptId":"9f999a6e-36b6-4981-abc4-fe8c1c2486a6","tu