{"parentUuid":"a4a7ff20-4bf7-4b74-ad78-05802644404d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011ChMNswcMcTarvBYiJ5VZ3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The reviewer is still working (its worktree exists and it has a process running), so I'm leaving it to finish.\n\nSomething changed underneath it: **#771 was merged at 07:35Z by another session, without #772.** That was over three request-changes reviews and two do-not-merge notes in the claims log. The release branch (`3b15d89f`) therefore now contains the exposure: `audit export` runs filters that a repository configures for itself, with the exporter's rights. I measured four such configurations executing at that code.\n\nWhat I've done:\n\n- **#772 is the fix and is now aimed at the release branch.** GitHub retargeted it when #771 merged. It is up to date with the new tip, and its checks are running.\n- **I'll merge #772 as soon as its review and checks are both in.** If the review finds a bypass, I'll fix that first.\n- **Logged** as the eighth merge outside the queue and the fourth over open review findings.\n\nThis is the second time a known security defect has reached the release branch this way (the first was #741). Whichever session is merging is not reading the PR comments or the claims log. That is worth settling when you're back."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":471,"cache_read_input_tokens":740586,"output_tokens":360,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":471,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":360,"cache_read_input_tokens":740586,"cache_creation_input_tokens":471,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1