{"parentUuid":"8b4d1a05-7623-4d8b-b707-68f142d0e320","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011ChMTVmEzCRQs32Cd82yuj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here is where things stand. This session won't be woken again until you send a message.\n\n**Release branch:** `release/v1.3.0` is at `4ae25a10`, CI green, with no open PRs.\n\n**The audit-export exposure opened and closed while I was waiting on a review**\n- **#771 merged at 07:35Z** by another session, without the fix, over three request-changes reviews and two do-not-merge notes. That put the exposure on the release branch: `audit export` ran git filters that a repository configured for itself.\n- **#772 (my fix) merged at 07:50Z**, also by another session, before its independent review had reported. So the hole was open on the release branch for about fifteen minutes and is now closed to the extent of that check.\n- **The review of #772 is still outstanding.** The reviewer has been running for ninety minutes with no report, so I've asked it to stop and report what it has. If it found a way around the check, that becomes a follow-up PR; I can't say yet whether it did.\n- **Known gaps in #772, stated on the PR:**\n  - Its test exercises five of the nine vectors; `includeIf`, a redirected git directory, `core.worktree` and a process filter are covered by the key list but not by the test.\n  - A submodule's own configuration isn't checked.\n  - The same exposure remains for the other callers of the candidate-identity routine.\n\n**Merge queue:** nine PRs have now been merged outside it, four of them over open review findings. Whichever session is doing that is not reading PR comments or the claims log.\n\n**What still stands between here and landing v1.3.0, unchanged**\n- **Unbuilt:** PF-3, PF-4, SB-1, MT-2, BG-1, BG-2, HK-1 to HK-3, PA-2.\n- **Unfinished:** GV-1 slices 3–4, the GV-5 allowlists, the six VR-2 follow-ups.\n- **Yours:** which units roll to v1.4, the go-ahead for the merge to `main` and the release-candidate tag, and who holds the merge queue."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":643,"cache_read_input_tokens":743082,"output_tokens":673,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":643,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":673,"cache_read_input_tokens":743082,"cache_creation_input_tokens":643,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":643},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011ChMTVm2M3Rb4VM1yTRcDZ","requestRef":"295bdeb6-b814-473d-aa8e-a0ab2aaa6383","requestedModel":"claude-fable-5-2","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"9a77c204-4e2c-4146-b6b9-9f98dcaa43ae","timestamp":"2026-11-24T08:43:47.980Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"main","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
