{"parentUuid":"66cd2ead-1c23-4562-be10-a72f56fb28d3","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PreToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_012txQsxJxHgRSWvknozvwzV","hookEvent":"PreToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"hookSpecificOutput\":{\"hookEventName\":\"PreToolUse\",\"permissionDecisionReason\":\"RTK auto-rewrite\",\"updatedInput\":{\"command\":\"cd ~/nexus-code && rtk gh pr comment 776 --body \\\"**Independent review at \\\\`7ad1d864dd6601f255279558155e3466419df47e\\\\` — ACCEPT WITH FOLLOW-UPS**\\n\\n- \\\\`audit_export.test.ts\\\\` 21/21 at this head. With both submodule conditions disabled, the new test fails with \\\\\\\"the submodule's configured command ran\\\\\\\".\\n- Probes through the real export, filter planted last:\\n\\n| Workspace | Planted program ran? | Binding |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| a nested plain repository, not registered as a submodule | no | compared normally (\\\\`git status --untracked-files=all\\\\` does not descend into it) |\\n| a gitlink added with \\\\`update-index --cacheinfo 160000\\\\` | no | \\\\`unavailable\\\\`, \\\\`workspace_configures_git_programs\\\\` |\\n| a gitlink removed with \\\\`git rm --cached\\\\`, \\\\`.git/modules/sub\\\\` left behind | no | \\\\`unavailable\\\\`, \\\\`workspace_configures_git_programs\\\\` |\\n\\n- By reading: \\\\`git ls-files --stage\\\\` and \\\\`git rev-parse --absolute-git-dir\\\\` read no working-tree file, so no filter applies to them. A failed listing, a timeout, an overflowing buffer and an unreadable \\\\`modules/\\\\` all refuse. The only \\\\\\\"no\\\\\\\" left is a directory that is not a Git work tree, where no Git command runs.\\n\\nFollow-ups, none blocking:\\n- In a linked worktree, \\\\`--absolute-git-dir\\\\` is the worktree's own git directory, while stored modules live in the common one. The gitlink condition still catches a registered submodule there; the \\\\`modules/\\\\` condition alone would not. Worth a probe.\\n- A timeout on a very large index is reported with the same reason as a real hit; a distinct reason would read better.\\n- Not checked: sparse checkouts, a \\\\`.gitmodules\\\\` with no gitlink, Node 22 locally.\\\" | tail -1; bash -c 'for i in $(seq 1 17); do st=$(gh pr view 776 --json state --jq .state); c=$(gh pr checks 776 2>&1 | grep -E \\\"^(test-matrix|linux-x86_64)\\\" | grep -c pass); f=$(gh pr checks 776 2>&1 | grep -E \\\"^test-|^linux\\\" | grep -c fail); [ \\\"$st\\\" != OPEN ] && break; [ \\\"$c\\\" = 3 ] && break; [ \\\"$f\\\" != 0 ] && break; sleep 30; done; echo \\\"state $st pass $c fail $f\\\"; gh pr checks 776 2>&1 | grep -E \\\"^test-matrix|^linux-x86_64|^test-.*(fail|pending)\\\" | cut -c1-55; gh pr view 776 --json headRefOid,mergedAt --jq \\\"[.headRefOid,(.mergedAt//\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\")]|@tsv\\\"; git fetch -q origin; echo \\\"tip $(git rev-parse --short origin/release/v1.3.0)\\\"; gh run list --branch release/v1.3.0 --workflow ci.yml --limit 1 --json status,conclusion,headSha --jq \\\".[0]|[.status,.conclusion,.headSha[0:8]]|@tsv\\\"'\",\"timeout\":590000,\"description\":\"Post the review on PR 776, wait for its checks, and re-read the release state\"}}}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"rtk hook claude","durationMs":90},"type":"attachment","uuid":"bb993cd2-e803-4e8d-89fd-74be4f3ab1ec","timestamp":"2026-11-24T09:16:39.698Z","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"main","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
