{"type":"data-flow-records","v":1,"sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","records":[{"response_id":"msg_011ChMXJyrvy1NKiekqCe6ij","mark_sent_by":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","listed":["msg_011ChMXJeEECr9zJu2viBeKL"]},{"response_id":"msg_011ChMXJbuZsxBtUsBnv2c8w","mark_sent_by":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b"}]}
{"parentUuid":"e07c7e7c-ee68-4d56-8e90-5a0308664884","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011ChMXJbuZsxBtUsBnv2c8w","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The plans for background runs and hooks are written, and I've started building both: BG-1 (detached, resumable runs) and HK-1 (pre-tool and post-tool hooks), each in its own worktree under its own claim.\n\n**Design decisions the plans took, at the plan's defaults or the conservative option**\n- **Background runs:**\n  - A foreground `nexus runner serve` under a documented systemd user unit, with one worker process per job.\n  - Jobs are read-only by default; writes only happen in a fresh worktree.\n  - A job never runs in auto mode and never grants \"allow always\".\n  - After a worker crash, a job resumes at most three times.\n  - Live attach is left to PF-3; a job is followed through its log and state.\n- **Schedules (BG-2):** cron, interval and one-shot triggers only. Event triggers and SSH execution stay in v1.4, which is D21's default.\n- **Hooks:**\n  - Two events only, pre-tool and post-tool.\n  - A hook can deny or annotate. Its \"allow\" and any changed input are ignored.\n  - A failing or timed-out pre-tool hook denies.\n  - Project hooks run only after their exact file hash is approved.\n- **Plugins (HK-2, HK-3):** installed from a git URL pinned to a full commit, verified on load, contributing hooks, skills and MCP servers only. Workspace plugins need per-file approval.\n\nIf you disagree with any of these, say so before the later slices build on them.\n\n**Running now:** BG-1, HK-1, GV-1 slices 3–4 with GV-5, the plan for PF-3/PF-4/SB-1/MT-2/PA-2, and reviews of #777 (mine) and #774/#775 (the other session's)."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6610,"cache_read_input_tokens":811891,"output_tokens":576,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6610,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":576,"cache_read_input_tokens":811891,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6610,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6610},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011ChMXJbVmyPswKqibUS2a1","requestRef":"e63b0e7e-5fc1-4e1c-922e-416371bc8708","requestedModel":"claude-fable-5-2","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"a449975b-cd96-4eba-a1e1-df8d5fac389b","timestamp":"2026-11-24T09:33:43.198Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"main","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
