g to apply to. The acceptance wording only names the socket, the token and mode 0600, so it is still met. Only the same user can connect. The token is 256 bits, kept in a 0600 file and compared in constant time.\n- **PF-3 clients:** one controller and any number of read-only observers; only the controller answers approvals. On the socket, allow-always becomes allow-once, and `/mode auto`, `!`, `/cd` and `provider.*` are refused.\n- **PF-3 approvals:** a pending approval is re-sent when a controller reattaches. It is denied after 600 seconds with no controller.\n- **PF-3 startup:** `nexus serve` refuses auto approval and unconfined commands.\n- **SB-1:** three profiles, selected through `--sandbox [engine]:profile`. There is no new flag and no new managed-policy key. The doctor schema stays at version 2.\n- **MT-2:** `dispatchToolCallImpl` keeps its name and file. The complexity baseline moves forward only once, after the last slice, and only with your acknowledgement.\n- **PA-2:**\n  - After each merge, it re-runs every verifier already integrated plus the operator's verifier, capped at 16 distinct checks.\n  - A failing check is re-run on the pre-merge tree to decide whether the new unit caused it.\n  - A unit that edits another integrated unit's test files is refused.\n  - The operation schema goes to v5.\n  - \"Neither is integrated silently\" means the first unit lands with a verified record and the second is refused with a decision naming both units.\n\n**Main risks**\n- `dispatchToolCallImpl` has no complexity headroom: any added branch, including in SB-1 slice 3, fails CI.\n- Whether TypeScript 7 can emit the lib's type declarations is untested; the plan includes a hand-written fallback. `\"private\": true` might change the license notices output and break the byte-for-byte build check.\n- Contention with Codex claims on the hot files.\n- Allowing a socket client to reattach and answer a pending approval is new behaviour.\n- PA-2 adds verifier runs on every merge, and those checks run unsandboxed on the host.\n- `agent.ts` is at 4,967 lines, 33 under MT-1's 5,000-line limit.\n\n**Could not determine**\n- Whether TypeScript 7 supports declaration emit here.\n- Whether the PA-3/PA-4 lanes also plan an operation schema bump.\n- Which `security.ts` function PA-2 should reuse to classify verification files.\n- Whether any test depends on the full list of operation event types; probably not, because `WORK_INTEGRATED` only appears in `operation.ts` and the runner.\n- MT-1 is done (it brought `agent.ts` under 5,000 lines), but no acceptance test for it exists; MT-2 slice 1 adds one. Its BG-1 clause can't be checked until BG-1 exists.\n- Node can't read the connecting process's user ID, so file permissions are the only check on who connects.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>73454</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>120</tool_uses><duration_ms>2153919</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>\n</system-reminder>"}]}}
