{"parentUuid":"88238bcc-9f08-42ef-8fa2-cee701e736d6","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"7527f3f2-461b-49ec-b4c9-bee1af3d2d6e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a0eeab406c46b4559</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01BCGX6HR1QcJuwrW1YWFPza</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666/tasks/a0eeab406c46b4559.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Review PR #777 VR-2 follow-ups\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>**Verdict: ACCEPT WITH FOLLOW-UPS** at `d4117b8668715da096b10e107ce6293d546f75dc`. At the end of the review the PR was still open and the head had not moved. I found no blockers.\n\n**Findings**\n\n1. Non-blocking, confirmed by reading and running: `docs/evidence/v1.3.0/VR2.md` and the PR body say `acp_client_conformance` passed 2/2. On this host it fails 0/2 at head. Both the Zed and CodeCompanion replays time out waiting for the turn output, and the log shows \"Inference request aborted by operator\". It also fails 0/2 on `origin/release/v1.3.0` (bd0cd1c2b), so it comes from the host (no inference or network) and not from this PR. The adapter's `initialize` output in the failure log is correct: the extensions are listed, and `session/new` succeeds. The recorded fixtures were therefore not shown to replay here. Fix: word the evidence as host-conditional, or note that the test needs a working turn.\n2. Non-blocking, by reading: a client can permanently deny verification of any directory for the life of the process.\n   - It can pin a directory before it has a commit.\n   - It can open 16 throwaway directories, after which new workspaces are refused.\n   - A failed `session/load` also uses a pin slot (`workspaceBase`, `acp_stdio.ts:248-257`).\n   - The only person affected is the client's own, since stdio serves one client. This is a limit to document, not a fix. `docs/ACP.md` states most of it but not the denial angle.\n3. Non-blocking, by reading: the base is pinned per canonical directory, not per repository.\n   - A bind mount, a `mv`, or a new linked worktree gives a new key and a fresh pin.\n   - The same-user limit already covers this, since the client can clone the repository anyway.\n   - A subdirectory session is not a bypass, because `core/verify.ts:860-863` refuses a worktree that is not the top of the Git tree.\n4. Non-blocking: `receipt.workspace` is a fresh `realpathSync` at issue time (`verify_service.ts:363`). The result's `workspace` therefore comes from that receipt, not from `session.cwd`. If the directory is renamed mid-run, the field could differ from what was passed. This is very unlikely in practice.\n\n**Claim 1, the pin**\n- Canonical is `fs.realpathSync` through `canonicalCwd`. It handles symlinks, `..` and trailing slashes. Linux is case-sensitive. The map key is the same string later passed as `worktree`.\n- `session/new` and `session/load` both go through `startSession`, so they use the same pin.\n- Two `session/new` calls on one directory cannot race. `pinBase` is a synchronous `spawnSync` and the map get/set has no `await` between them.\n- A failed pin is stored and reused, so the refusal sticks until restart. Existing pins are kept at the cap; nothing is evicted or re-pinned.\n- `pinBase` runs `rev-parse --verify --quiet --end-of-options HEAD^{commit}` through the hardened `git()` wrapper. That wrapper has pinned flags, a checkout check, a scrubbed environment and a timeout. `rev-parse` runs no repository-configured program.\n\n**Claim 2, result fields**\n- `base_pinned_commit` and `base_pinned_at` come from the same `session.verifyBase` object that is passed to the service.\n- Refusals and service errors return a JSON-RPC error with no result, so no field can describe something that did not run.\n- `docs/protocol/acp-adapter-v1..v3.schema.json` are byte-identical to the base branch. `gen_acp_schema.mjs --check` reports v4 current, and the version constant is 4.\n\n**Claim 3, receipt separation**\n- Only an explicit id reaches `verifyService.receipt(id, sessionId)`, and it is bound to the session.\n- Verify no longer sets `latestReceipts`. I covered the three orderings and the forged-id case by reading the code and the tests. I did not run my own probes.\n\n**Claims 4 and 5, interlocks and shutdown**\n- The interlock code is as described in the PR.\n- `shutdownGraceMs()` is computed once, when the signal arrives. The longer deadline applies only while a verify is pending. With none running, the original bound is used.\n- I did not probe cancel, close or stopping during a verify.\n\n**Mutations** (source copied aside and restored; the worktree was clean afterwards)\n\n| Mutation | Test file that failed |\n|---|---|\n| Remove the verify-during-prompt check (`if (false)`) | `acp_verify_followups` failed 1 |\n| Remove the pin reuse | `acp_verify_followups` failed 1 |\n| Restore `latestReceipts.set` in verify, with the id gate removed | `acp_verify_followups` failed 1 |\n\nDropping the id gate alone leaves everything passing. That is an equivalent mutation, because verify no longer records its receipt, so the gate is redundant. Only the `latestReceipts.set` mutation is a real one.\n\n**Claim 6, test timing**\nBesides the wait going from 10 s to 45 s, one assertion changed. The \"latest receipt includes the verification receipt\" check became \"no turn receipt, so -32602\". The new assertions add `workspace` and the pinned fields. None is weakened.\n\n**Claim 7, docs**\nThe new `_nexus/verify` section in `docs/ACP.md`, `docs/evidence/v1.3.0/VR2.md` and `docs/MCP_GUIDE.md` match the code, except the conformance count in finding 1.\n\n**Test counts at head** (Node 24, one file at a time, throwaway `HOME`)\n\n| File | Pass | Fail |\n|---|---|---|\n| `acp_verify_followups` | 8 | 0 |\n| `acp_review_fixes` | 9 | 0 |\n| `acp_stdio` | 9 | 0 |\n| `acp_validate` | 15 | 0 |\n| `acp_schema` | 7 | 0 |\n| `acp_mapping` | 22 | 0 |\n| `acp_jsonrpc` | 11 | 0 |\n| `verify_service` | 10 | 0 |\n| `leak_guard` | 6 | 0 |\n| `acp_client_conformance` | 0 | 2 (host-dependent, same on base) |\n\n`tsc --noEmit` produced no output. The schema generator check and the complexity gate passed.\n\n**Not checked**\n- Node 22.\n- My own runtime probes for symlink, `session/load`, cap and pin-failure behaviour, and for `$/cancel_request`, `session/cancel` and connection close during a verify.\n- A real SIGTERM during a verification.\n\nI removed both worktrees (`rev777` and `rev777b`, the latter a base-branch checkout I added for the comparison) and wrote no probe files.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>58301</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>20</tool_uses><duration_ms>700560</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"},"uuid":"5d683a8e-5e44-4470-8db8-8631b0de6c97","timestamp":"2026-11-24T09:40:56.221Z","permissionMode":"bypassPermissions","origin":{"kind":"task-notification","producer":"session-task","runId":"0mwuhtela-d2947acd"},"promptSource":"system","turnOrigin":"task_notification","turnPromptId":"7527f3f2-461b-49ec-b4c9-bee1af3d2d6e","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":40,"turnIndex":261},"queueSkipAttachments":true,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"main","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
