ut of date. The new `TurnResult` fields make `protocol_schema` fail 1 of 8: \"checked-in protocol schema equals a fresh generation\". Running `node cli/scripts/gen_protocol_schema.mjs` adds 12 lines, and `--check` fails. I reverted the regeneration in my worktree. The fix is to regenerate it and record the version decision in `docs/protocol/VERSIONS.json`. I did not check that failure on the base; #775, on a nearby base, passes this test. (confirmed by running)\n\n**Non-blocking**\n- The admission mutation survived. I made `initialTaskTimeStopReason` return `undefined`, and all 6 tests still passed. The loop-top `Date.now() &gt; turnDeadline` check is a backstop, since the timer is not armed at a zero limit. That makes the admission check redundant, and the test at line 78 does not pin it. With a zero limit the backstop uses `&gt;` on the same millisecond, so a step could dispatch. Add a test with a stubbed or frozen clock. (confirmed by running)\n- The reset mutation was caught. Setting `taskElapsedMs = 0` on begin fails the \"can only be lowered on resume\" test (5 pass, 1 fail). (confirmed by running)\n- A backwards clock jump within a process exhausts the whole budget. `finishTaskElapsedBudget` sets elapsed to the maximum whenever now &lt; `taskActiveSinceMs`. This fails closed, but a small NTP step permanently kills a long objective. Consider a monotonic `process.hrtime` delta within one process, and wall clock only across processes. (by reading)\n- Legacy objectives with no counter are charged `now − startedAt`. Any objective older than 3 days (the 4320 min default) is exhausted on its first resume. This is deliberate and conservative, but it should be called out in the docs. (by reading)\n- Idle time between clean turns is not counted. Only running intervals and crash or kill downtime are counted. Any open interval is charged through downtime, so a kill followed by a resume a week later exhausts the budget. The code behaves this way, but I found no operator-facing doc stating it. (by reading)\n- `--no-continuation` leaves `budget` undefined, so there is no task limit. This matches the #762 turn deadline. (by reading)\n- Persisted elapsed time is written once at begin, as `taskActiveSinceMs`, which survives a kill. The reservation is saved before any dispatch, and a failed save blocks inference. (by reading plus a test)\n- The deadline timer is cleared on the catch path and on the normal path. The normal-path clear moved after the compaction drain. A timer firing during that drain is neutralised by `shouldOverrideStopAfterDeadline`. The unified `min(turn, task remaining)` timer avoids two timers. (by reading)\n- The limit is configured by `--max-task-minutes` or `NEXUS_MAX_TASK_MINUTES`. It sits in `PROJECT_ENV_KEYS`, so a project `.env` can set it, as with the submission budget. It can only lower the ceiling, because a resume keeps `min(saved, new)`. It defaults to 4320 and is capped at `MAX_CONTINUATION_MINUTES`. Invalid values throw in `assertValidContinuationBudget`. The docs touch only the plan progress note, and I did not check whether it names the project-`.env` behaviour. (by reading)\n\n**Gates**\n- Complexity: `runTurnImpl` CC 324→324, nesting 5→5. Lines went 1262→1290, and the gate did not complain about that.\n- Samples: `gen_protocol_samples --check` says current.\n- Run-result schema: additive, `schema_version` stays 1, and a ledger entry was appended.\n- Leak guard: imported by the new test file.\n- tsc: clean.\n\n**Tests**\n\n| File | Pass | Fail |\n|---|---|---|\n| p10_task_elapsed_budget | 6 | 0 |\n| leak_guard | 6 | 0 |\n| protocol_parity | 5 | 0 |\n| protocol_schema | 7 | 1 |\n| run_json_contract | 15 | 0 |\n| check_requirements | 28 | 0 |\n| p10_inference_submission_budget | 4 | 0 |\n| turn_deadline_abort | 3 | 0 |\n\n## PR #775: ACCEPT WITH FOLLOW-UPS, but the head moved\nI reviewed af6c50e046ba157d716313ebbe4ed8b62442a22a. The head is now 7945d57b46f4e2e4a27d9d43bc250cef6c60c914, so this verdict does not cover it. I did not review the new commit.\n\n**Non-blocking**\n- **Doc over-claims resume.** The doc says \"Resume continues after the operator raises the cap\". I found no operator path that raises `policy.maxTotalTokens` on a saved goal. `resume` only clears the pause, and the policy is fixed at creation. A resume would hit the cap again immediately. Either add the path or reword the doc. (by reading)\n- **Cap checks are before dispatch only.** One unit can overshoot by an unbounded amount, and the doc does not say so. (by reading)\n- **Failure to measure is silent.** `rolledUpTokens` swallows child-state load errors, and no store means no enforcement. That fails open. It is the same posture as the existing usage code, and the doc does state it. (by reading)\n- **Dead code.** `pauseForTokenBudget` has an empty `BLOCKED` branch. Remove it. (by reading)\n- **Test gaps.** The test sets `operation.policy` directly. Nothing covers the env or config → `team.plan` path, the no-cap case, or the resume-after-raise claim. (by reading)\n\n**Answers**\n- The cap counts rolled-up `stats.total` per goal across its sub-operations. Reported and estimated tokens are both included. The goal ends `PAUSED` with a visible reason, never `COMPLETE`.\n- Models, tools and workspace content cannot raise it. `NEXUS_OPERATION_MAX_TOTAL_TOKENS` and the config.json key are operator-controlled. The env key is not in `PROJECT_ENV_KEYS`, so a project `.env` cannot set it.\n- The cap is optional and the schema change is optional. Goals without it behave as before.\n\n**Gates and mutation**\n- Complexity: `driveOperation` CC 17→17, nesting 3→3, lines 47→47. The `runTurnImpl` line in the same run (CC 324→324) is from the #774 worktree.\n- Mutation: replacing the cap condition with `false` fails the new cap test in `goal_lifecycle` (7 pass, 1 fail). (confirmed by running)\n- tsc: clean.\n\n| File | Pass | Fail |\n|---|---|---|\n| goal_lifecycle | 8 | 0 |\n| leak_guard | 6 | 0 |\n| protocol_parity | 5 | 0 |\n| protocol_schema | 8 | 0 |\n| run_json_contract | 15 | 0 |\n| check_requirements | 28 | 0 |\n| goal_ledger_propagation | 2 | 0 |\n| operation_entry_integrity | 3 | 0 |\n| operation_schema | 18 | 0 |\n| operation_runner_restart | 1 | 0 |\n\n**Not checked**\n- Neither PR was run on Node 22 and 24.\n- I did not run the full suites.\n- For #774, I did not check the plan doc text beyond its first line, or the `taskActiveSinceMs` write ordering under real kills.\n- I did not run the failing #774 test on the base worktree.\n- I did not review #775's new head commit.\n\nI removed both worktrees at the end. They were first created at the wrong commit by a shell slip, and I re-checked them out to the exact SHAs before reviewing.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>71553</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>30</tool_uses><duration_ms>1044971</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"main","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
