{"parentUuid":"3c5cbdb3-7b92-4b5f-a964-4dd6c3fe52fa","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011ChMbrJCKwaNYvbG1Rcjwe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The GV-1/GV-5 branch merged cleanly with the release branch, type-checks, and its four new test files pass. It's pushed; opening the PR and sending it for independent review."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":980,"cache_read_input_tokens":864024,"output_tokens":2408,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":980,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2408,"cache_read_input_tokens":864024,"cache_creation_input_tokens":980,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":980},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011ChMbrHzvDpZN1vDDSheUS","requestRef":"91183c91-7244-4318-91d6-8c80f5f7ac73","requestedModel":"claude-fable-5-2","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"d2261e27-6471-4594-b517-e4d46b6414fe","timestamp":"2026-11-24T10:33:15.855Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"main","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
{"parentUuid":"d2261e27-6471-4594-b517-e4d46b6414fe","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011ChMbrJCKwaNYvbG1Rcjwe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012rZhSGGpWTNxfd4MLZLULU","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/pr_gv.md","content":"Finishes GV-1 (slices 3 and 4 of `GV1_PLAN.md`) and GV-5's allowlists. `docs/MANAGED_POLICY.md` marked these \"not yet\" or \"planned\"; it now says what is enforced.\n\n## GV-5: MCP and plugin allowlists\n\n`mcp.allow`, `mcp.disable_workspace`, `plugins.allow` and `plugins.disable_workspace` were accepted by the schema and enforced nothing.\n\n- **MCP** (`cli/src/mcp.ts`): every server is checked before it starts, on all three paths (`loadAndConnect`, `addServer`, `addConnection`). A refused `/mcp add` saves nothing.\n- **Plugins** (`cli/src/plugins.ts`): the real path and SHA-256 are checked before `import()`.\n- **`disable_workspace`** ignores a definition that belongs to the workspace by path or by symlink target.\n- A refusal names the policy source, is printed once on stderr and is available to callers. An unreadable policy admits nothing.\n\n## GV-1 slice 3\n\n- Under `approval.disable_auto` or `strict`, an \"always\" answer approves that one call and is not remembered (`cli/src/sidecar.ts`). No change to the Rust TUI: the enforcement is on the sidecar side.\n- The line-mode REPL had the same gap and the documentation said it did not: `/mode auto` and \"always\" set the REPL's own copy of the mode, and it stopped asking. Fixed (`cli/src/repl.ts`); `/mode auto` now answers with the refusal and its source.\n- `nexus verify` refuses `--yes`, `--sandbox none` and `--sandbox-network` when policy forbids them, exit 2.\n\n## GV-1 slice 4\n\n- `nexus policy show` and `nexus policy check [file]`, both with `--json`; exit 2 on an invalid policy. They run even when the installed policy is broken, which is when they are needed.\n- `nexus doctor`: findings `policy.system`, `policy.user`, `policy.project`, `policy.effective`. `doctor --fix` skips any `policy.toml`.\n\n## Behaviour changes for the release notes\n\n- A server or plugin outside the allowlists no longer starts or loads.\n- \"Always\" and `/mode auto` are refused under `approval.disable_auto` or `strict`, in the TUI and the REPL.\n- `nexus verify` refuses the three flags above under policy.\n- When the workspace is the home directory, `disable_workspace` also switches off the user's own MCP configuration and plugins, because they are then workspace files.\n\n## Decisions and limits\n\n- `nexus policy approve` is not implemented: it would be a second approval path that a model could run. `nexus trust` stays the only one.\n- A bare or unnormalised command never matches a `command:` allowlist entry; WebSocket servers match by name only.\n- A plugin is hashed and then imported by path, so a replacement between the two is not detected (documented).\n- Left \"not yet\": `egress.secret_destinations` (not in slices 3–4), and the sandbox consulting `sandbox.forbid_network` itself (slice 5 in the plan; the document says so).\n\n## Tests\n\nNew: `managed_policy_allowlists` (18, with the hostile cases: a workspace policy adding to an allowlist, name and case tricks, a symlinked workspace configuration, empty versus absent allowlist), `policy_cli` (23), `managed_policy_always` (6), `managed_policy_verify` (12). Updated to the new state: `managed_policy_enforcement`, `managed_policy_schema`.\n\nLocal, Node 24, after merging the release branch: the four new files pass, `leak_guard` 6/6, `tsc` clean, `check_invariants`, `check_requirements`, `check_doc_versions` and the complexity gate pass. Before the merge: the eight existing managed-policy files (465 tests), `approval_policy` 16/16, `mcp` 4/4, `mcp_verify` 7/7, `verify_command` 18/18, `verify_sandbox` 10/10, `check_requirements` 28/28, `release_workflow_parity` 6/6, `lsp_shape` 8/8.\n\n**Not clean locally, and why:** the host was at a load average of 10 to 20 from parallel work. `sidecar.test.ts` had 8 failures of 65, all 10-second waits and timing assertions; the approval tests among them pass when rerun alone, and one of the eight fails on the base branch too; two were not rerun. `context_convergence` was cut off after 15 minutes with 6 tests passed and none failed. `doctor.test.ts` fails the same 11 tests as the base branch. CI is the arbiter for these three.\n\nNo model-facing tool description changed.\n\n## Reference coding\n\nXERJ was not queried for this change. The design follows `GV1_PLAN.md`, whose reference-coding section covers the unit.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":980,"cache_read_input_tokens":864024,"output_tokens":2408,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":980,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2408,"cache_read_input_tokens":864024,"cache_creation_input_tokens":980,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":980},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":16185,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_012rZhSGGpWTNxfd4MLZLULU":{"file_path":"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/pr_gv.md","content":"Finishes GV-1 (slices 3 and 4 of `GV1_PLAN.md`) and GV-5's allowlists. `docs/MANAGED_POLICY.md` marked these \"not yet\" or \"planned\"; it now says what is enforced.\n\n## GV-5: MCP and plugin allowlists\n\n`mcp.allow`, `mcp.disable_workspace`, `plugins.allow` and `plugins.disable_workspace` were accepted by the schema and enforced nothing.\n\n- **MCP** (`cli/src/mcp.ts`): every server is checked before it starts, on all three paths (`loadAndConnect`, `addServer`, `addConnection`). A refused `/mcp add` saves nothing.\n- **Plugins** (`cli/src/plugins.ts`): the real path and SHA-256 are checked before `import()`.\n- **`disable_workspace`** ignores a definition that belongs to the workspace by path or by symlink target.\n- A refusal names the policy source, is printed once on stderr and is available to callers. An unreadable policy admits nothing.\n\n## GV-1 slice 3\n\n- Under `approval.disable_auto` or `strict`, an \"always\" answer approves that one call and is not remembered (`cli/src/sidecar.ts`). No change to the Rust TUI: the enforcement is on the sidecar side.\n- The line-mode REPL had the same gap and the documentation said it did not: `/mode auto` and \"always\" set the REPL's own copy of the mode, and it stopped asking. Fixed (`cli/src/repl.ts`); `/mode auto` now answers with the refusal and its source.\n- `nexus verify` refuses `--yes`, `--sandbox none` and `--sandbox-network` when policy forbids them, exit 2.\n\n## GV-1 slice 4\n\n- `nexus policy show` and `nexus policy check [file]`, both with `--json`; exit 2 on an invalid policy. They run even when the installed policy is broken, which is when they are needed.\n- `nexus doctor`: findings `policy.system`, `policy.user`, `policy.project`, `policy.effective`. `doctor --fix` skips any `policy.toml`.\n\n## Behaviour changes for the release notes\n\n- A server or plugin outside the allowlists no longer starts or loads.\n- \"Always\" and `/mode auto` are refused under `approval.disable_auto` or `strict`, in the TUI and the REPL.\n- `nexus verify` refuses the three flags above under policy.\n- When the workspace is the home directory, `disable_workspace` also switches off the user's own MCP configuration and plugins, because they are then workspace files.\n\n## Decisions and limits\n\n- `nexus policy approve` is not implemented: it would be a second approval path that a model could run. `nexus trust` stays the only one.\n- A bare or unnormalised command never matches a `command:` allowlist entry; WebSocket servers match by name only.\n- A plugin is hashed and then imported by path, so a replacement between the two is not detected (documented).\n- Left \"not yet\": `egress.secret_destinations` (not in slices 3–4), and the sandbox consulting `sandbox.forbid_network` itself (slice 5 in the plan; the document says so).\n\n## Tests\n\nNew: `managed_policy_allowlists` (18, with the hostile cases: a workspace policy adding to an allowlist, name and case tricks, a symlinked workspace configuration, empty versus absent allowlist), `policy_cli` (23), `managed_policy_always` (6), `managed_policy_verify` (12). Updated to the new state: `managed_policy_enforcement`, `managed_policy_schema`.\n\nLocal, Node 24, after merging the release branch: the four new files pass, `leak_guard` 6/6, `tsc` clean, `check_invariants`, `check_requirements`, `check_doc_versions` and the complexity gate pass. Before the merge: the eight existing managed-policy files (465 tests), `approval_policy` 16/16, `mcp` 4/4, `mcp_verify` 7/7, `verify_command` 18/18, `verify_sandbox` 10/10, `check_requirements` 28/28, `release_workflow_parity` 6/6, `lsp_shape` 8/8.\n\n**Not clean locally, and why:** the host was at a load average of 10 to 20 from parallel work. `sidecar.test.ts` had 8 failures of 65, all 10-second waits and timing assertions; the approval tests among them pass when rerun alone, and one of the eight fails on the base branch too; two were not rerun. `context_convergence` was cut off after 15 minutes with 6 tests passed and none failed. `doctor.test.ts` fails the same 11 tests as the base branch. CI is the arbiter for these three.\n\nNo model-facing tool description changed.\n\n## Reference coding\n\nXERJ was not queried for this change. The design follows `GV1_PLAN.md`, whose reference-coding section covers the unit.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011ChMbrHzvDpZN1vDDSheUS","requestRef":"91183c91-7244-4318-91d6-8c80f5f7ac73","requestedModel":"claude-fable-5-2","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"dbf49402-bcb9-4049-bb97-79be796ce3c8","timestamp":"2026-11-24T10:33:32.055Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"main","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
