file passed 3 runs in a row with 0 failures.\n- **Added:** `cli/src/core/{strict_json,process_identity,content_trust,hook_runner,hooks}.ts`, `cli/src/{hooks_cli,doctor_hooks}.ts`, `cli/scripts/gen_hooks_schema.mjs`, `docs/protocol/hooks-v1.schema.json`, `docs/protocol/HOOKS_VERSIONS.json`, `docs/HOOKS.md`, `examples/hooks/`, `cli/test/helpers/hooks_fixture.ts`.\n- **Changed:** `agent.ts` (one 16-line block plus an import), `spine.ts`, `flight.ts`, `verify_service.ts` (helpers moved out), `index.ts` (2 lines), `doctor.ts` (8 lines), plus small additions to the manual, changelog, state-compatibility, doctor and protocol docs.\n- **Untouched:** `dispatch_tool_call.ts`, `run_turn.ts`, `sidecar.ts`, `types.ts`, `config.ts`, `mcp.ts`, `plugins.ts`, Rust.\n- **Gates at the final state:** `tsc` clean, the required test list all green, the three `scripts/check_*.mjs`, the complexity gate (all five functions unchanged), and the hooks and sidecar schema `--check`.\n- **`doctor.test`:** 49 pass, 11 fail, the identical failing set with and without my `doctor.ts` edit.\n\n## Acceptance: \"a hook's allow has no effect\"\n\n`hooks_gate_bypass` runs each gate twice, without hooks and with an operator hook that answers approve in every dialect plus an `updatedInput` aimed at `Makefile`. The two receipts must be equal.\n\n- **Dispatcher gates:** headless approval, operator refusal, `VERIFICATION_CONFIG_PROTECTED`, CS-9 forbidden, managed forbid, managed `require_human`, delegation. The hook is never started for any of them.\n- **Read-only mode:** the hook runs, is recorded as `ignored_allow`, and the denial is word-for-word the same.\n- **`updatedInput`:** the approved file is written and `Makefile` is untouched.\n- **\"A changed project hook asks again\":** `hooks_project_trust`.\n- **\"Scripts of that shape transfer\":** `hooks_examples` feeds a Claude-Code-shaped payload from `docs/HOOKS.md` to the example script.\n\n## Security properties (test, then the mutation that fails it)\n\n- **Gate order:** making the authority stage skip after a hook allow fails the read-only test.\n- **Fail closed:** letting a hook error continue, or an invalid operator file pass, fails `hooks_deny`.\n- **`ask` denies:** covered in `hook_output_reduce`.\n- **Chain:** an allow that ends the chain fails `hooks_deny`.\n- **Project trust:** treating unapproved as active, skipping re-validation, dropping the read-only rule, keeping the approval after removal, and dropping the change time from the file stamp each fail `hooks_project_trust`.\n- **Secrets:** passing the full environment fails `hook_runner`; removing redaction fails `hooks_post_tool`.\n- **Process control:** removing the kill-by-pid of remembered descendants, the stdout cap, or the left-open-output failure each fail `hook_runner`.\n- **Visibility:** dropping `denialReason`, the receipt's `hooks`, or the flight record fails `hooks_deny`.\n- **CLI:** approval without a hash, a wrong hash, or an invalid file being approvable fails `hooks_cli`.\n\n## Plan premise that does not hold\n\nThe plan says the spine is reached only after every gate approved. Read-only mode, authority grants and the workspace boundary are enforced by the spine's authority stage, which runs after `contextAdmission`. A hook is therefore started for a read-only write. It still cannot allow it, but a hook that denies there replaces the gate's reason with `HOOK_DENIED`. I kept the plan's attachment, tested the real behaviour and documented it.\n\n## Deviations and choices\n\n- Project hooks are read without owner or mode checks (hash trust), because a default umask-002 clone would otherwise never run.\n- An unknown decision value denies (`HOOK_OUTPUT_INVALID`).\n- A hook that exits while a child holds its output open is `HOOK_FAILED`.\n- An approved file observed missing has its approval revoked.\n- The `post-tool` result is redacted; this is my addition.\n- Hooks are serialised per agent, because read-only calls are dispatched in parallel.\n- There is no session-start prompt for unapproved project hooks, only a notice on the first tool call.\n- The plan's in-process \"allow maps to admit\" mutation guard was done as manual mutations instead.\n- `tryEvent` (used by `nexus hooks test`) landed in the slice 2 commit; the change-time stamp fix landed in slice 3.\n- Tests were run with `TMPDIR` on `/dev/shm`, because fsync on the shared disk took seconds; the wiring tests also passed once on disk.\n- The slice 1 `context_convergence` run was cut by my own timeout. It passed 57/57 at the slice 2 and slice 3 states.\n\n## Left\n\nThe other seven events, HK-2 and HK-3. `docs/releases/v1.3.0-READINESS.md` still lists HK-1 as open. The branch is 8 commits behind `origin/release/v1.3.0`.\n\n## Release note\n\n- Two events only: `pre-tool` and `post-tool`.\n- Hooks are unsandboxed.\n- An invalid `~/.config/nexus/hooks.json` denies every tool call.\n- Non-zero exits other than 2 deny, unlike Claude Code.\n- The approval prompt comes before hooks.\n- `serve-mcp` runs no hooks.\n- Project hooks are not a control over the agent, which can edit the file and so stop them.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>451017</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>154</tool_uses><duration_ms>4865998</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>\n</system-reminder>"}]}}
