{"parentUuid":"6b8512b0-06de-4bc5-9928-04f39b6c0255","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011ChMdkFyvrPWM6Ma33DGzz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Your usage limit has been reached, so I'm stopping here. The build is partway through and nothing is lost.\n\n**Done and on the release branch**\n- **VR-2 follow-ups:** merged as #777, reviewed.\n- **GV-1 slices 3–4 and the GV-5 allowlists:** merged as #778, with green required checks. Another session merged it before its independent review had reported, so that review result is still to be read and posted; any bypass it found becomes a follow-up.\n- **#776:** the audit export refuses a workspace that has a submodule.\n\n**Built but not yet merged**\n- **HK-1 (hooks):** all three slices are committed and pushed as `origin/v1/hk1-hooks-lib`, with the release branch merged in. No PR is open yet. One thing for its review: the plan assumed hooks run only after every gate has approved, but read-only mode is enforced after the hook stage. A hook therefore runs for a read-only write and still can't allow it, but a hook that denies there replaces the gate's reason with its own.\n\n**In progress, on disk only**\n- **BG-1 (detached runs):** slice 1 committed locally; slice 2 is uncommitted in `~/nexus-wt/bg1`.\n- **PF-4 (library entry):** slice 1 written, uncommitted, in `~/nexus-wt/pf4`.\n- **SB-1 (permission profiles):** slice 1 in progress, uncommitted, in `~/nexus-wt/sb1`.\n\nThe agents on these three will be cut off by the same limit. Their work stays in the worktrees.\n\n**Not started:** PA-2, MT-2, BG-2, HK-2, HK-3, PF-3. The plans for all of them are written in `~/nexus-wt/_plans/`.\n\n**Loose ends**\n- The pause note for the other sessions did not get written to the claims log; that last command failed. My claims on BG-1, PF-4, SB-1, HK-1 and PA-2 are still in place, but another session could take those worktrees over while I'm stopped. It has done that 