{"parentUuid":"9ee76f71-ca93-40a5-a365-e181a672cb64","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011ChMvsmqDePFNeawgoqGNu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm back: Codex has taken over BG-1, PF-4 and SB-1, opening PRs for two and merging SB-1's first slice, so I'm reviewing those while HK-1 and PA-2 stay mine. The hooks branch is current with release and its tests pass, so I'm opening its PR now.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":971,"cache_read_input_tokens":891289,"output_tokens":2548,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":971,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2548,"cache_read_input_tokens":891289,"cache_creation_input_tokens":971,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":971},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":7,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011ChMvsmSASk4ioDU4f65is","requestRef":"c8686ba7-7a5f-4f91-920a-e35b513a9701","requestedModel":"claude-fable-5-2","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"522b2195-cd8a-4bd6-b798-cd16e0bbaca3","timestamp":"2026-11-24T14:42:47.085Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"main","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
{"parentUuid":"522b2195-cd8a-4bd6-b798-cd16e0bbaca3","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011ChMvsmqDePFNeawgoqGNu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01L1uhrJEuzVrAwrMCx4MLCp","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/pr_hk1.md","content":"Plan unit HK-1: command hooks. Acceptance from the plan: \"a hook's allow has no effect\". Design: `HK_PLAN.md` (written from this branch's base); three slices, one commit each, plus merges of the release branch.\n\n## What it adds\n\n- **Two events only**: `pre-tool` and `post-tool`. A hook is a program the operator names in `~/.config/nexus/hooks.json`, or one in a project hooks file whose exact content hash the operator has approved (`nexus hooks approve`). A changed project file asks again.\n- **What a hook can do**: deny, or annotate. Its \"allow\" in any dialect and any `updatedInput` are ignored; `ask` counts as deny; an unknown decision denies. A `pre-tool` hook that errors, times out or leaves its output open denies. An invalid operator hooks file denies every tool call.\n- **How it runs**: a subprocess with a hard timeout, stdin JSON, bounded output, a reduced environment (no gateway key, no tool secrets), its process tree killed by pid with start-time checks. The `post-tool` payload is redacted.\n- **Where it attaches**: the spine's `contextAdmission` stage (pre-tool) and `evidenceEmission` (post-tool), through one 16-line block in `agent.ts`. `dispatchToolCallImpl`, `run_turn.ts` and `sidecar.ts` are not edited; the complexity gate is unchanged for all five functions.\n- **Visible**: a denial carries `HOOK_DENIED` and the hook's name in the tool receipt and the flight log.\n- **Commands and docs**: `nexus hooks list|test|approve|revoke`, a doctor finding `hooks.config`, `docs/HOOKS.md` with a runnable example under `examples/hooks/` that a test executes, the hooks file schema `docs/protocol/hooks-v1.schema.json` with its ledger.\n\n## The acceptance, and where the plan was wrong\n\n`hooks_gate_bypass` runs each gate twice, without hooks and with an operator hook that answers \"approve\" in every dialect plus an `updatedInput` aimed at another file, and requires the two receipts to be equal. For the dispatcher's gates (headless approval, operator refusal, protected verification configuration, forbidden command rule, managed-policy forbid and require-human, delegation) the hook is never started.\n\n**The plan assumed the spine is reached only after every gate has approved. That is not so for read-only mode, authority grants and the workspace boundary:** the spine's authority stage enforces them, and it runs after `contextAdmission`. So for a write in read-only mode the hook does run. It still cannot allow the write: its allow is recorded as `ignored_allow` and the denial is word for word the same. But a hook that *denies* there replaces the gate's reason with `HOOK_DENIED`. The attachment follows the plan; the tests assert the real behaviour and `docs/HOOKS.md` states it.\n\n## What a release note must say\n\n- Hooks are unsandboxed programs running with the operator's rights.\n- An invalid `~/.config/nexus/hooks.json` denies every tool call until it is fixed.\n- A non-zero exit other than 2 denies (stricter than the Claude Code convention the payload shape follows).\n- The approval prompt comes before hooks.\n- `serve-mcp` runs no hooks.\n- Project hooks are not a control over the agent: the agent can edit the file, which stops them until the operator approves the new content.\n\n## Tests\n\nThirteen new test files, 101 tests: `strict_json` 9, `hooks_config` 6, `hook_output_reduce` 13, `hook_runner` 8, `content_trust` 7, `hooks_schema` 5, `hooks_gate_bypass` 11, `hooks_deny` 9, `hooks_post_tool` 5, `hooks_project_trust` 9, `hooks_cli` 8, `hooks_examples` 6, `doctor_hooks` 5. Each passed three runs in a row. For each guard a mutation was shown to fail a test (gate order, fail-closed, chain handling, project trust in five ways, environment and redaction, kill and output caps, visibility, the CLI's hash checks); the list is in the implementation report and can be repeated.\n\nAfter merging the release branch (Node 24): the seven hook files rerun pass, `leak_guard` 6/6, `tsc` clean, complexity gate unchanged. Before the merge: the required list of existing files, `context_convergence` 57/57, the three `scripts/check_*.mjs`. `doctor.test.ts` fails the same 11 tests with and without this change (host state).\n\n## Other changes to existing files\n\n`spine.ts` and `flight.ts` (the hook record), `verify_service.ts` (process-identity helpers moved out to `core/process_identity.ts` so hooks and the verify service share them; no behaviour change intended), `index.ts` (2 lines), `doctor.ts` (8 lines), the manual and protocol docs.\n\n## Not in this PR\n\nThe other hook events, HK-2 (commit-pinned plugins) and HK-3 (per-plugin trust). There is no session-start prompt for unapproved project hooks, only a notice at the first tool call.\n\n## Reference coding\n\n`HK_PLAN.md` records the peer comparison (payload and exit-code conventions follow Claude Code's hooks so existing scripts transfer; the \"deny or annotate only, never allow\" rule and fail-closed pre-tool are this repo's own).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":971,"cache_read_input_tokens":891289,"output_tokens":2548,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":971,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2548,"cache_read_input_tokens":891289,"cache_creation_input_tokens":971,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":971},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":17342,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01L1uhrJEuzVrAwrMCx4MLCp":{"file_path":"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/pr_hk1.md","content":"Plan unit HK-1: command hooks. Acceptance from the plan: \"a hook's allow has no effect\". Design: `HK_PLAN.md` (written from this branch's base); three slices, one commit each, plus merges of the release branch.\n\n## What it adds\n\n- **Two events only**: `pre-tool` and `post-tool`. A hook is a program the operator names in `~/.config/nexus/hooks.json`, or one in a project hooks file whose exact content hash the operator has approved (`nexus hooks approve`). A changed project file asks again.\n- **What a hook can do**: deny, or annotate. Its \"allow\" in any dialect and any `updatedInput` are ignored; `ask` counts as deny; an unknown decision denies. A `pre-tool` hook that errors, times out or leaves its output open denies. An invalid operator hooks file denies every tool call.\n- **How it runs**: a subprocess with a hard timeout, stdin JSON, bounded output, a reduced environment (no gateway key, no tool secrets), its process tree killed by pid with start-time checks. The `post-tool` payload is redacted.\n- **Where it attaches**: the spine's `contextAdmission` stage (pre-tool) and `evidenceEmission` (post-tool), through one 16-line block in `agent.ts`. `dispatchToolCallImpl`, `run_turn.ts` and `sidecar.ts` are not edited; the complexity gate is unchanged for all five functions.\n- **Visible**: a denial carries `HOOK_DENIED` and the hook's name in the tool receipt and the flight log.\n- **Commands and docs**: `nexus hooks list|test|approve|revoke`, a doctor finding `hooks.config`, `docs/HOOKS.md` with a runnable example under `examples/hooks/` that a test executes, the hooks file schema `docs/protocol/hooks-v1.schema.json` with its ledger.\n\n## The acceptance, and where the plan was wrong\n\n`hooks_gate_bypass` runs each gate twice, without hooks and with an operator hook that answers \"approve\" in every dialect plus an `updatedInput` aimed at another file, and requires the two receipts to be equal. For the dispatcher's gates (headless approval, operator refusal, protected verification configuration, forbidden command rule, managed-policy forbid and require-human, delegation) the hook is never started.\n\n**The plan assumed the spine is reached only after every gate has approved. That is not so for read-only mode, authority grants and the workspace boundary:** the spine's authority stage enforces them, and it runs after `contextAdmission`. So for a write in read-only mode the hook does run. It still cannot allow the write: its allow is recorded as `ignored_allow` and the denial is word for word the same. But a hook that *denies* there replaces the gate's reason with `HOOK_DENIED`. The attachment follows the plan; the tests assert the real behaviour and `docs/HOOKS.md` states it.\n\n## What a release note must say\n\n- Hooks are unsandboxed programs running with the operator's rights.\n- An invalid `~/.config/nexus/hooks.json` denies every tool call until it is fixed.\n- A non-zero exit other than 2 denies (stricter than the Claude Code convention the payload shape follows).\n- The approval prompt comes before hooks.\n- `serve-mcp` runs no hooks.\n- Project hooks are not a control over the agent: the agent can edit the file, which stops them until the operator approves the new content.\n\n## Tests\n\nThirteen new test files, 101 tests: `strict_json` 9, `hooks_config` 6, `hook_output_reduce` 13, `hook_runner` 8, `content_trust` 7, `hooks_schema` 5, `hooks_gate_bypass` 11, `hooks_deny` 9, `hooks_post_tool` 5, `hooks_project_trust` 9, `hooks_cli` 8, `hooks_examples` 6, `doctor_hooks` 5. Each passed three runs in a row. For each guard a mutation was shown to fail a test (gate order, fail-closed, chain handling, project trust in five ways, environment and redaction, kill and output caps, visibility, the CLI's hash checks); the list is in the implementation report and can be repeated.\n\nAfter merging the release branch (Node 24): the seven hook files rerun pass, `leak_guard` 6/6, `tsc` clean, complexity gate unchanged. Before the merge: the required list of existing files, `context_convergence` 57/57, the three `scripts/check_*.mjs`. `doctor.test.ts` fails the same 11 tests with and without this change (host state).\n\n## Other changes to existing files\n\n`spine.ts` and `flight.ts` (the hook record), `verify_service.ts` (process-identity helpers moved out to `core/process_identity.ts` so hooks and the verify service share them; no behaviour change intended), `index.ts` (2 lines), `doctor.ts` (8 lines), the manual and protocol docs.\n\n## Not in this PR\n\nThe other hook events, HK-2 (commit-pinned plugins) and HK-3 (per-plugin trust). There is no session-start prompt for unapproved project hooks, only a notice at the first tool call.\n\n## Reference coding\n\n`HK_PLAN.md` records the peer comparison (payload and exit-code conventions follow Claude Code's hooks so existing scripts transfer; the \"deny or annotate only, never allow\" rule and fail-closed pre-tool are this repo's own).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011ChMvsmSASk4ioDU4f65is","requestRef":"c8686ba7-7a5f-4f91-920a-e35b513a9701","requestedModel":"claude-fable-5-2","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"8a1a5d1c-f037-44cc-920d-525941d4dac0","timestamp":"2026-11-24T14:43:04.440Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionI