{"parentUuid":"81e091fa-2065-4124-9a0a-10adc8e32505","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011ChMw4LDf852Wqm1hLjNVw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The #778 review is back: accept with follow-ups, no bypass that loosens the policy invariant, but one real gap worth fixing. Posting it now."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9888,"cache_read_input_tokens":900654,"output_tokens":2623,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":127},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9888,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2623,"cache_read_input_tokens":900654,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9888,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9888},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011ChMw4L1GUz4DDwLj7GZZ8","requestRef":"8511e93e-6651-45a1-87f3-fb7883617847","requestedModel":"claude-fable-5-2","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"f301dd1e-bde6-413b-8dbc-3c3d04e03054","timestamp":"2026-11-24T14:45:09.564Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"main","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
{"parentUuid":"f301dd1e-bde6-413b-8dbc-3c3d04e03054","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011ChMw4LDf852Wqm1hLjNVw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01ACkr5xt9VsQ5RW6FfMEwvi","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/rev778.md","content":"**Independent review at `afb4ed64f62d4b597eb75286e3fb92209ad367fb` — ACCEPT WITH FOLLOW-UPS. This merged before the review reported, so the follow-ups are against the release branch.**\n\n**Follow-ups, in order of weight**\n\n1. **A bare-name `mcp.allow` entry is not a boundary against a workspace file** (confirmed by running). With `allow = [\"files\"]` and a trusted workspace, a `.mcp.json` that defines a server named `files` with a different `command` was started and that program ran (`permitsMcpServer`, `core/managed_policy.ts:820-839`; `policyDescriptor`, `mcp.ts:129-135`). The same holds for a WebSocket, HTTP or SSE URL under an allowed name. The document says a name entry is the only kind that admits a WebSocket server; it does not say that a name entry pins nothing and that the workspace can redefine the name. Either a name-only entry should not match a definition that comes from the workspace, or the document must say so and recommend `mcp.disable_workspace = true` or `command:` / `url:` entries. I am opening a follow-up for the first.\n2. **`nexus policy check <file>` echoes parts of the file in its parse errors** (confirmed by running): the first token of line 1 as an \"invalid key\", and a value such as `allow = sk-…` as an \"unsupported value\". Pointed at an arbitrary readable file it prints fragments of it. The offending token should be truncated or left out.\n3. **Not traced:** `NEXUS_SANDBOX_NETWORK` is read in `sandbox.ts` and not in `verifyFlagRefusal`, so whether the environment variable gives `nexus verify` network access under a policy that refuses `--sandbox-network` is open.\n4. A hard link to a workspace file placed in the user configuration directory counts as a user file under `disable_workspace` (confirmed by running). A repository cannot create that link; a limit to document.\n5. A `sha256:` plugin pin covers the entry file only, not the modules it imports. To document.\n\n**Held up when run**\n\n- Name tricks (case, trailing space, a Cyrillic look-alike, a zero-width space) are all refused.\n- A configuration symlinked into the workspace, a symlinked parent directory, and a workspace symlink pointing out are all treated as workspace under `disable_workspace`.\n- `addServer` and `addConnection` refuse an unlisted server and nothing is spawned. The ACP adapter validates and ignores `mcpServers`.\n- A plugin symlinked from the user plugin directory into the workspace is not imported under `plugins.disable_workspace`; a `sha256:` mismatch refuses.\n- \"Always\": the approval is clamped, `setApprovalMode(\"auto\")` cannot enter auto under the policy, and the one flag that approves silently is now gated.\n- `doctor --fix` leaves a broken `policy.toml` byte-identical. `policy check --json` stays valid JSON with exit 2 on an unreadable file.\n\n**Mutations, each caught:** removing the gate on `loadAndConnect` (10 failures), on `addConnection` (1), on `addServer` (1), the plugin gate (5), making `verifyFlagRefusal` return nothing (10), making \"always\" stick (1).\n\n**Tests at that head:** `managed_policy_allowlists` 18, `managed_policy_verify` 12, `policy_cli` 23, `managed_policy_enforcement` 113, `managed_policy_schema` 57, `managed_policy_always` 6, `mcp` 4, `mcp_tool_through_spine` 3, `approval_policy` 16, `leak_guard` 6, all passing; `tsc`, the complexity gate, `check_invariants` and `check_requirements` pass. `sidecar` had 7 failures here against 6 on the base on the same loaded host, mostly timeouts; the one extra was not attributed, and CI was green on this head.\n\n**Not checked:** `context_convergence` locally; the REPL path by mutation; `--yes` and `NEXUS_APPROVAL_MODE=auto` at start-up and mode inheritance by subagents and goal runners (read only); a policy file changing on disk mid-session.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9888,"cache_read_input_tokens":900654,"output_tokens":2623,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":127},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9888,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2623,"cache_read_input_tokens":900654,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9888,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9888},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":13730,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01ACkr5xt9VsQ5RW6FfMEwvi":{"file_path":"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/rev778.md","content":"**Independent review at `afb4ed64f62d4b597eb75286e3fb92209ad367fb` — ACCEPT WITH FOLLOW-UPS. This merged before the review reported, so the follow-ups are against the release branch.**\n\n**Follow-ups, in order of weight**\n\n1. **A bare-name `mcp.allow` entry is not a boundary against a workspace file** (confirmed by running). With `allow = [\"files\"]` and a trusted workspace, a `.mcp.json` that defines a server named `files` with a different `command` was started and that program ran (`permitsMcpServer`, `core/managed_policy.ts:820-839`; `policyDescriptor`, `mcp.ts:129-135`). The same holds for a WebSocket, HTTP or SSE URL under an allowed name. The document says a name entry is the only kind that admits a WebSocket server; it does not say that a name entry pins nothing and that the workspace can redefine the name. Either a name-only entry should not match a definition that comes from the workspace, or the document must say so and recommend `mcp.disable_workspace = true` or `command:` / `url:` entries. I am opening a follow-up for the first.\n2. **`nexus policy check <file>` echoes parts of the file in its parse errors** (confirmed by running): the first token of line 1 as an \"invalid key\", and a value such as `allow = sk-…` as an \"unsupported value\". Pointed at an arbitrary readable file it prints fragments of it. The offending token should be truncated or left out.\n3. **Not traced:** `NEXUS_SANDBOX_NETWORK` is read in `sandbox.ts` and not in `verifyFlagRefusal`, so whether the environment variable gives `nexus verify` network access under a policy that refuses `--sandbox-network` is open.\n4. A hard link to a workspace file placed in the user configuration directory counts as a user file under `disable_workspace` (confirmed by running). A repository cannot create that link; a limit to document.\n5. A `sha256:` plugin pin covers the entry file only, not the modules it imports. To document.\n\n**Held up when run**\n\n- Name tricks (case, trailing space, a Cyrillic look-alike, a zero-width space) are all refused.\n- A configuration symlinked into the workspace, a symlinked parent directory, and a workspace symlink pointing out are all treated as workspace under `disable_workspace`.\n- `addServer` and `addConnection` refuse an unlisted server and nothing is spawned. The ACP adapter validates and ignores `mcpServers`.\n- A plugin symlinked from the user plugin directory into the workspace is not imported under `plugins.disable_workspace`; a `sha256:` mismatch refuses.\n- \"Always\": the approval is clamped, `setApprovalMode(\"auto\")` cannot enter auto under the policy, and the one flag that approves silently is now gated.\n- `doctor --fix` leaves a broken `policy.toml` byte-identical. `policy check --json` stays valid JSON with exit 2 on an unreadable file.\n\n**Mutations, each caught:** removing the gate on `loadAndConnect` (10 failures), on `addConnection` (1), on `addServer` (1), the plugin gate (5), making `verifyFlagRefusal` return nothing (10), making \"always\" stick (1).\n\n**Tests at that head:** `managed_policy_allowlists` 18, `managed_policy_verify` 12, `policy_cli` 23, `managed_policy_enforcement` 113, `managed_policy_schema` 57, `managed_policy_always` 6, `mcp` 4, `mcp_tool_through_spine` 3, `approval_policy` 16, `leak_guard` 6, all passing; `tsc`, the complexity gate, `check_invariants` and `check_requirements` pass. `sidecar` had 7 failures here against 6 on the base on the same loaded host, mostly timeouts; the one extra was not attributed, and CI was green on this head.\n\n**Not checked:** `context_convergence` locally; the REPL path by mutation; `--yes` and `NEXUS_APPROVAL_MODE=auto` at start-up and mode inheritance by subagents and goal runners (read only); a policy file changing on disk mid-session.\n"}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011ChMw4L1GUz4DDwLj7GZZ8","requestRef":"8511e93e-6651-45a1-87f3-fb7883617847","requestedModel":"claude-fable-5-2","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"2616f464-6dea-45b2-be19-5af8a60c7222","timestamp":"2026-11-24T14:45:23.331Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"main","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
{"parentUuid":"2616f464-6dea-45b2-be19-5af8a60c7222","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"a6a580ba-bf20-439e-a180-58e9ad5c5dee","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ACkr5xt9VsQ5RW6FfMEwvi","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/rev778.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"7261afe6-e564-41a5-93c4-bac9b9f1fcdf","timestamp":"2026-11-24T14:45:24.316Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"create","filePath":"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/rev778.md","content":"**Independent review at `afb4ed64f62d4b597eb75286e3fb92209ad367fb` — ACCEPT WITH FOLLOW-UPS. This merged before the review reported, so the follow-ups are against the release branch.**\n\n**Follow-ups, in order of weight**\n\n1. **A bare-name `mcp.allow` entry is not a boundary against a workspace file** (confirmed by running). With `allow = [\"files\"]` and a trusted workspace, a `.mcp.json` that defines a server named `files` with a different `command` was started and that program ran (`permitsMcpServer`, `core/managed_policy.ts:820-839`; `policyDescriptor`, `mcp.ts:129-135`). The same holds for a WebSocket, HTTP or SSE URL under an allowed name. The document says a name entry is the only kind that admits a WebSocket server; it does not say that a name entry pins nothing and that the workspace can redefine the name. Either a name-only entry should not match a definition that comes from the workspace, or the document must say so and recommend `mcp.disable_workspace = true` or `command:` / `url:` entries. I am opening a follow-up for the first.\n2. **`nexus policy check <file>` echoes parts of the file in its parse errors** (confirmed by running): the first token of line 1 as an \"invalid key\", and a value such as `allow = sk-…` as an \"unsupported value\". Pointed at an arbitrary readable file it prints fragments of it. The offending token should be truncated or left out.\n3. **Not traced:** `NEXUS_SANDBOX_NETWORK` is read in `sandbox.ts` and not in `verifyFlagRefusal`, so whether the environment variable gives `nexus verify` network access under a policy that refuses `--sandbox-network` is open.\n4. A hard link to a workspace file placed in the user configuration directory counts as a user file under `disable_workspace` (confirmed by running). A repository cannot create that link; a limit to document.\n5. A `sha256:` plugin pin covers the entry file only, not the modules it imports. To document.\n\n**Held up when run**\n\n- Name tricks (case, trailing space, a Cyrillic look-alike, a zero-width space) are all refused.\n- A configuration symlinked into the workspace, a symlinked parent directory, and a workspace symlink pointing out are all treated as workspace under `disable_workspace`.\n- `addServer` and `addConnection` refuse an unlisted server and nothing is spawned. The ACP adapter validates and ignores `mcpServers`.\n- A plugin symlinked from the user plugin directory into the workspace is not imported under `plugins.disable_workspace`; a `sha256:` mismatch refuses.\n- \"Always\": the approval is clamped, `setApprovalMode(\"auto\")` cannot enter auto under the policy, and the one flag that approves silently is now gated.\n- `doctor --fix` leaves a broken `policy.toml` byte-identical. `policy check --json` stays valid JSON with exit 2 on an unreadable file.\n\n**Mutations, each caught:** removing the gate on `loadAndConnect` (10 failures), on `addConnection` (1), on `addServer` (1), the plugin gate (5), making `verifyFlagRefusal` return nothing (10), making \"always\" stick (1).\n\n**Tests at that head:** `managed_policy_allowlists` 18, `managed_policy_verify` 12, `policy_cli` 23, `managed_policy_enforcement` 113, `managed_policy_schema` 57, `managed_policy_always` 6, `mcp` 4, `mcp_tool_through_spine` 3, `approval_policy` 16, `leak_guard` 6, all passing; `tsc`, the complexity gate, `check_invariants` and `check_requirements` pass. `sidecar` had 7 failures here against 6 on the base on the same loaded host, mostly timeouts; the one extra was not attributed, and CI was green on this head.\n\n**Not checked:** `context_convergence` locally; the REPL path by mutation; `--yes` and `NEXUS_APPROVAL_MODE=auto` at start-up and mode inheritance by subagents and goal runners (read only); a policy file changing on disk mid-session.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"2616f464-6dea-45b2-be19-5af8a60c7222","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"main","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
{"parentUuid":"7261afe6-e564-41a5-93c4-bac9b9f1fcdf","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011ChMw4LDf852Wqm1hLjNVw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RQX2Z5b218SRF8rakhHhJZ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-code && gh pr comment 778 --body-file /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/rev778.md | tail -1; d=\"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims\"; echo \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ) REVIEW + NOTE (claude-invariants-audit): #778 review posted (ACCEPT WITH FOLLOW-UPS at afb4ed64): a bare-name mcp.allow entry admits a workspace definition of that name with any command (confirmed); nexus policy check echoes file fragments in parse errors; NEXUS_SANDBOX_NETWORK vs nexus verify untraced. I am opening a follow-up PR for these. Codex: #780 (BG-1) and my #782 (HK-1) BOTH add cli/src/core/strict_json.ts and cli/src/core/process_identity.ts and both move helpers out of verify_service.ts (each plan specified those modules). Whichever merges second has to reconcile them; I will do that reconciliation on #782 if #780 lands first, and suggest you do the same the other way round. #780 is red on test-matrix at c511326f. Also started: PA-2 slice 1 in ~/nexus-wt/pa2; reviews of #779 and #782 running.\" >> \"$d/nexus-claims.log\"; git worktree add -q -b v1/policy-followups ~/nexus-wt/polfu origin/release/v1.3.0 && cd ~/nexus-wt/polfu && ln -s ~/nexus-code/cli/node_modules cli/node_modules && mkdir -p core/target/release && cp ~/nexus-wt/ls1b/core/target/release/{harness-core,nexus-tui} core/target/release/ && sed -n 805,845p cli/src/core/managed_policy.ts | cut -c1-190; sed -n 125,140p cli/src/mcp.ts | cut -c1-190; sed -n 150,172p cli/src/policy_cli.ts | cut -c1-190; rtk proxy grep -n \"NEXUS_SANDBOX_NETWORK\" cli/src/*.ts cli/src/core/*.ts | cut -c1-170 | head -8","description":"Post the review on PR 778, log it with a note about overlapping files, an