{"parentUuid":"d5cc64a4-efc5-4557-9ead-ebda87cc64a7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011ChMwKFBiH8go5t7h3weXa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HhjcC2sy6VryM4wgGQBYDg","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-wt/polfu && git fetch -q origin && git add -A cli docs && git commit -q -m \"fix(policy): a name in mcp.allow no longer admits a workspace-defined server; policy check stops echoing file text\n\nFrom the review of the allowlist enforcement:\n\n- With a name-only entry in mcp.allow, a workspace .mcp.json could define a\n  server of that name with any program or URL, and it was started. A server\n  configured by a workspace file is now admitted only by a command: or url:\n  entry that matches what it would reach; the refusal says so.\n- nexus policy check <file> quoted the tokens it rejected, so pointing it at\n  an arbitrary file printed fragments of it. A rejected token that is not\n  shaped like a policy key is cut to eight characters.\n\nThe document also states what an entry does not pin (arguments, a plugin's\nimports, a hard link in the user's configuration directory).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>\" && git merge -q origin/release/v1.3.0 --no-edit 2>&1 | tail -1; cd cli && npx tsc --noEmit -p . >/dev/null; echo \"tsc $?\"; cd .. && git push -q -u origin v1/policy-followups 2>&1 | tail -1; echo \"remote: $(git ls-remote origin refs/heads/v1/policy-followups | cut -c1-8) local: $(git rev-parse --short=8 HEAD)\"; cd ~/nexus-code && u=$(gh pr create --base release/v1.3.0 --head v1/policy-followups --title \"fix(policy): a name in mcp.allow no longer admits a workspace-defined server; policy check stops echoing file text\" --body \"Follow-ups from the independent review of #778 (posted there; that PR merged before the review reported).\n\n## 1. A name entry did not hold against a workspace file\n\nWith \\`mcp.allow = [\\\"files\\\"]\\` and a trusted workspace, a \\`.mcp.json\\` that defines a server named \\`files\\` with its own \\`command\\` was started, and that program ran (confirmed by the reviewer by running it). The same held for a URL under an allowed name. A name is whatever the configuring file says it is.\n\nNow: a server configured by a file of the workspace is admitted only by a \\`command:\\` or \\`url:\\` entry that matches what it would reach. With only a name entry it is refused, and the message says to list its program or URL. A name entry still admits a server from the operator's own configuration. With no allowlist, nothing changes.\n\n**Behaviour change for the release notes:** an operator who allowed a workspace-defined server by name must switch that entry to \\`command:/absolute/path\\` or \\`url:https://origin\\`. A WebSocket server, which only a name entry can admit, can therefore only come from the operator's own configuration.\n\n## 2. \\`nexus policy check <file>\\` echoed file text\n\nIts parse errors quote the token they reject. Pointed at a file that is not a policy, it printed the first token of a line and rejected values. A quoted token that is not shaped like a policy key (lower-case words joined by dots and underscores) is now cut to eight characters. A mistyped key is still named in full.\n\n## 3. Checked and not a defect\n\nThe review asked whether \\`NEXUS_SANDBOX_NETWORK\\` gives \\`nexus verify\\` network access under a policy that refuses \\`--sandbox-network\\`. It does not: verify passes \\`network\\` explicitly from the flag (\\`index.ts:720-726\\`), and the sandbox consults the variable only when \\`network\\` is left undefined (\\`sandbox.ts:720, 892\\`).\n\n## Docs\n\n\\`docs/MANAGED_POLICY.md\\` states the new rule and what an entry does not pin: a \\`command:\\` entry's arguments, the modules a \\`sha256:\\`-pinned plugin imports, and a hard link in the user's configuration directory to a workspace file.\n\n## Tests\n\nNew test in \\`managed_policy_merge\\` (the operator's definition admitted; three workspace redefinitions refused with the message; \\`command:\\` and \\`url:\\` matches admitted; no allowlist unchanged) and in \\`policy_cli\\` (a credentials-shaped file is not readable through the errors; a mistyped key is still named). Each fails with its fix removed.\n\nLocal, Node 24: \\`managed_policy_merge\\` 47/47, \\`policy_cli\\` 24/24, \\`managed_policy_allowlists\\` 18/18, \\`managed_policy_enforcement\\` 113/113, \\`mcp\\` 4/4, \\`leak_guard\\` 6/6, \\`tsc\\` clean.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\" | tail -1); echo \"$u\"; echo \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ) PR (claude-invariants-audit): $u from ~/nexus-wt/polfu: follow-ups to the #778 review (name-only mcp.allow no longer admits a workspace-defined server; policy check errors no longer echo file text). Small; I will get a short independent review before merging. Do not merge before it is posted.\" >> \"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log\"","description":"Commit, merge the release tip, push, open the follow-up PR and log it","timeout":200000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1529,"cache_read_input_tokens":929251,"output_tokens":1871,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1529,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1871,"cache_read_input_tokens":929251,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1529,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1529},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":15043,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01HhjcC2sy6VryM4wgGQBYDg":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-wt/polfu && git fetch -q origin && git add -A cli docs && git commit -q -m \"fix(policy): a name in mcp.allow no longer admits a workspace-defined server; policy check stops echoing file text\n\nFrom the review of the allowlist enforcement:\n\n- With a name-only entry in mcp.allow, a workspace .mcp.json could define a\n  server of that name with any program or URL, and it was started. A server\n  configured by a workspace file is now admitted only by a command: or url:\n  entry that matches what it would reach; the refusal says so.\n- nexus policy check <file> quoted the tokens it rejected, so pointing it at\n  an arbitrary file printed fragments of it. A rejected token that is not\n  shaped like a policy key is cut to eight characters.\n\nThe document also states what an entry does not pin (arguments, a plugin's\nimports, a hard link in the user's configuration directory).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>\" && git merge -q origin/release/v1.3.0 --no-edit 2>&1 | tail -1; cd cli && npx tsc --noEmit -p . >/dev/null; echo \"tsc $?\"; cd .. && git push -q -u origin v1/policy-followups 2>&1 | tail -1; echo \"remote: $(git ls-remote origin refs/heads/v1/policy-followups | cut -c1-8) local: $(git rev-parse --short=8 HEAD)\"; cd ~/nexus-code && u=$(gh pr create --base release/v1.3.0 --head v1/policy-followups --title \"fix(policy): a name in mcp.allow no longer admits a workspace-defined server; policy check stops echoing file text\" --body \"Follow-ups from the independent review of #778 (posted there; that PR merged before the review reported).\n\n## 1. A name entry did not hold against a workspace file\n\nWith \\`mcp.allow = [\\\"files\\\"]\\` and a trusted workspace, a \\`.mcp.json\\` that defines a server named \\`files\\` with its own \\`command\\` was started, and that program ran (confirmed by the reviewer by running it). The same held for a URL under an allowed name. A name is whatever the configuring file says it is.\n\nNow: a server configured by a file of the workspace is admitted only by a \\`command:\\` or \\`url:\\` entry that matches what it would reach. With only a name entry it is refused, and the message says to list its program or URL. A name entry still admits a server from the operator's own configuration. With no allowlist, nothing changes.\n\n**Behaviour change for the release notes:** an operator who allowed a workspace-defined server by name must switch that entry to \\`command:/absolute/path\\` or \\`url:https://origin\\`. A WebSocket server, which only a name entry can admit, can therefore only come from the operator's own configuration.\n\n## 2. \\`nexus policy check <file>\\` echoed file text\n\nIts parse errors quote the token they reject. Pointed at a file that is not a policy, it printed the first token of a line and rejected values. A quoted token that is not shaped like a policy key (lower-case words joined by dots and underscores) is now cut to eight characters. A mistyped key is still named in full.\n\n## 3. Checked and not a defect\n\nThe review asked whether \\`NEXUS_SANDBOX_NETWORK\\` gives \\`nexus verify\\` network access under a policy that refuses \\`--sandbox-network\\`. It does not: verify passes \\`network\\` explicitly from the flag (\\`index.ts:720-726\\`), and the sandbox consults the variable only when \\`network\\` is left undefined (\\`sandbox.ts:720, 892\\`).\n\n## Docs\n\n\\`docs/MANAGED_POLICY.md\\` states the new rule and what an entry does not pin: a \\`command:\\` entry's arguments, the modules a \\`sha256:\\`-pinned plugin imports, and a hard link in the user's configuration directory to a workspace file.\n\n## Tests\n\nNew test in \\`managed_policy_merge\\` (the operator's definition admitted; three workspace redefinitions refused with the message; \\`command:\\` and \\`url:\\` matches admitted; no allowlist unchanged) and in \\`policy_cli\\` (a credentials-shaped file is not readable through the errors; a mistyped key is still named). Each fails with its fix removed.\n\nLocal, Node 24: \\`managed_policy_merge\\` 47/47, \\`policy_cli\\` 24/24, \\`managed_policy_allowlists\\` 18/18, \\`managed_policy_enforcement\\` 113/113, \\`mcp\\` 4/4, \\`leak_guard\\` 6/6, \\`tsc\\` clean.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\" | tail -1); echo \"$u\"; echo \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ) PR (claude-invariants-audit): $u from ~/nexus-wt/polfu: follow-ups to the #778 review (name-only mcp.allow no longer admits a workspace-defined server; policy check errors no longer echo file text). Small; I will get a short independent review before merging. Do not merge before it is posted.\" >> \"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log\"","description":"Commit, merge the release tip, push, open the follow-up PR and log it","timeout":200000}},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011ChMwKErdA2RujT5Sx8yZN","requestRef":"e1fd834f-d40f-4b5b-a2e6-2f7df6843e9a","requestedModel":"claude-fable-5-2","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"28cfa4c5-877d-4d8c-bc02-8efd67b8e24e","timestamp":"2026-11-24T14:48:45.706Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"main","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
