{"parentUuid":"0c2a6877-82c2-4c19-8a15-3dbdcd00714a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011ChMxYnCFRfZaonpT2Abc7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The review of Codex's #779 (library entry) is back as request changes, with one blocker in its example. Posting it now."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4001,"cache_read_input_tokens":958081,"output_tokens":2467,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4001,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2467,"cache_read_input_tokens":958081,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4001,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4001},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.2.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"}],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011ChMxYmVqDpUMvrSFngXyP","requestRef":"8322b66f-3e83-41a6-b710-62330807c865","requestedModel":"claude-fable-5-2","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"38c28dd6-d1b8-401e-a163-11fc1b11a4bb","timestamp":"2026-11-24T15:04:41.536Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"main","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
{"parentUuid":"38c28dd6-d1b8-401e-a163-11fc1b11a4bb","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011ChMxYnCFRfZaonpT2Abc7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013ABL9nJAHjRwRPv31fCWcq","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/rev779.md","content":"**Independent review at `a299f8093a827450b3a4a4d642a557e94a2bcd5b` — REQUEST CHANGES (one blocker, in the example and the docs snippet; the library itself is sound)**\n\n**Blocking**\n\n- **The example approves any request whose tool is `\"verifier\"`** (`examples/embed/embed.mjs:34-38`, the snippet in `docs/EMBEDDING.md`, `examples/embed/README.md`; added by this head commit). That tool name is used for the operator's configured verifier (seen here as `review: {command: \"node --test\", detail: \"configured\"}`), and also for a verifier the model declares for a requirement (`completion_oracle.ts:274-275`), for a discovered project verifier, and for the type-check oracle (`completion_oracle.ts:126`). The example approves all of them without looking at the command or where it came from. The library denies by default, so the fault is not in a default; but a copied example lets a project-supplied or model-declared verifier run with no human grant, where the CLI asks the operator (and auto-approves only with `-y`).\n  Fix: approve only when `request.tool === \"verifier\" && request.review?.command === \"node --test\" && request.review?.detail === \"configured\"`, deny the rest, change the docs snippet the same way, and add a test in which a model-declared verifier request is denied.\n\n**Not blocking**\n\n1. `extraArgs: [\"-y\"]` and `[\"--mode\", \"auto\"]` reach auto approval: both runs ended VERIFIED with no approval request, and the sidecar does not refuse them (run). `docs/EMBEDDING.md` says `extraArgs` is the embedder's own authority and the plan accepted it. A test should pin it; consider refusing those flags in `extraArgs`, or in the sidecar as `nexus acp` does.\n2. No timeout on `onApproval` (`sidecar_client.ts:315`): a handler that never answers holds the turn until the abort signal. An optional timeout that denies would bound it.\n3. The no-handler default is only pinned once the real decision path is mutated (changing the initial value alone is an equivalent mutant).\n4. `tsconfig.lib.json` emits about 60 declaration files into `dist/types`, and `package-linux.sh:64` copies all of `dist`, so the tarball grows. The output is deterministic, so the two-build comparison should hold; the package build was not run here.\n5. A managed policy that cannot be used ends the sidecar with exit 1 instead of 2 (it loads policy through `buildConfig`, not `requireManagedPolicyAtStartup`).\n\n**Held up**\n\n- **Exports:** `NEXUS_LIB_API_VERSION`, `spawnSidecar`, `SidecarClient`, `SidecarClientError`, and types. Nothing runs a turn in-process, skips managed policy or workspace trust, selects auto, or grants allow-always.\n- **Import side effects:** the import graph reaches `sidecar_client.ts`, `acp/jsonrpc.ts` and `acp/types.ts` only; nothing from `index.ts`. Importing `dist/lib.js` with a HOME that does not exist: exit 0, no output, nothing created.\n- **Approvals through the client**, with a fake child: no handler, `{approve: true}`, `{always: true}`, `true`, `\"Approve\"` and `\"approve-always\"` all become deny; only `\"approve\"` approves, always with `always: false`. Concurrent requests are answered separately; a stale id is ignored; a checkpoint choice cancels the turn.\n- **Robustness:** lines bounded at 16 MiB; a wrong protocol version dropped; a hello timeout that kills the child by pid; shutdown by SIGTERM then SIGKILL on the pid.\n- **Packaging:** no lockfile change, no new dependency; `bin`, `test` and `test:cli` unchanged (`release_workflow_parity` 6/6); `npm run build` succeeds.\n- **The acceptance:** the example spawns the real sidecar against the scripted gateway and ends `VERIFIED`; a false completion claim is not VERIFIED, and with the verifier denied the outcome is UNVERIFIED.\n- **Mutations:** approving on an undefined decision (2 failures), letting `{always: true}` through (1), any truthy decision allowing (1), `lib.ts` importing `index.js` (the test file aborts).\n\n**Tests at this head:** `lib_entry` 6/6, `sidecar_client` 19/19, `embed_example` 3/3, `sidecar` 65/65, `protocol_parity` 5/5, `leak_guard` 6/6, `release_workflow_parity` 6/6, `check_requirements` 28/28; `tsc`, `check_invariants`, `check_deprecated_lock` and the complexity gate pass.\n\n**Not checked:** the full package build twice with the byte comparison, the SBOM and notices, Node 22, the hang and huge-line paths against a real child.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4001,"cache_read_input_tokens":958081,"output_tokens":2467,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4001,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2467,"cache_read_input_tokens":958081,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4001,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4001},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.2.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"}],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":14448,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_013ABL9nJAHjRwRPv31fCWcq":{"file_path":"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/rev779.md","content":"**Independent review at `a299f8093a827450b3a4a4d642a557e94a2bcd5b` — REQUEST CHANGES (one blocker, in the example and the docs snippet; the library itself is sound)**\n\n**Blocking**\n\n- **The example approves any request whose tool is `\"verifier\"`** (`examples/embed/embed.mjs:34-38`, the snippet in `docs/EMBEDDING.md`, `examples/embed/README.md`; added by this head commit). That tool name is used for the operator's configured verifier (seen here as `review: {command: \"node --test\", detail: \"configured\"}`), and also for a verifier the model declares for a requirement (`completion_oracle.ts:274-275`), for a discovered project verifier, and for the type-check oracle (`completion_oracle.ts:126`). The example approves all of them without looking at the command or where it came from. The library denies by default, so the fault is not in a default; but a copied example lets a project-supplied or model-declared verifier run with no human grant, where the CLI asks the operator (and auto-approves only with `-y`).\n  Fix: approve only when `request.tool === \"verifier\" && request.review?.command === \"node --test\" && request.review?.detail === \"configured\"`, deny the rest, change the docs snippet the same way, and add a test in which a model-declared verifier request is denied.\n\n**Not blocking**\n\n1. `extraArgs: [\"-y\"]` and `[\"--mode\", \"auto\"]` reach auto approval: both runs ended VERIFIED with no approval request, and the sidecar does not refuse them (run). `docs/EMBEDDING.md` says `extraArgs` is the embedder's own authority and the plan accepted it. A test should pin it; consider refusing those flags in `extraArgs`, or in the sidecar as `nexus acp` does.\n2. No timeout on `onApproval` (`sidecar_client.ts:315`): a handler that never answers holds the turn until the abort signal. An optional timeout that denies would bound it.\n3. The no-handler default is only pinned once the real decision path is mutated (changing the initial value alone is an equivalent mutant).\n4. `tsconfig.lib.json` emits about 60 declaration files into `dist/types`, and `package-linux.sh:64` copies all of `dist`, so the tarball grows. The output is deterministic, so the two-build comparison should hold; the package build was not run here.\n5. A managed policy that cannot be used ends the sidecar with exit 1 instead of 2 (it loads policy through `buildConfig`, not `requireManagedPolicyAtStartup`).\n\n**Held up**\n\n- **Exports:** `NEXUS_LIB_API_VERSION`, `spawnSidecar`, `SidecarClient`, `SidecarClientError`, and types. Nothing runs a turn in-process, skips managed policy or workspace trust, selects auto, or grants allow-always.\n- **Import side effects:** the import graph reaches `sidecar_client.ts`, `acp/jsonrpc.ts` and `acp/types.ts` only; nothing from `index.ts`. Importing `dist/lib.js` with a HOME that does not exist: exit 0, no output, nothing created.\n- **Approvals through the client**, with a fake child: no handler, `{approve: true}`, `{always: true}`, `true`, `\"Approve\"` and `\"approve-always\"` all become deny; only `\"approve\"` approves, always with `always: false`. Concurrent requests are answered separately; a stale id is ignored; a checkpoint choice cancels the turn.\n- **Robustness:** lines bounded at 16 MiB; a wrong protocol version dropped; a hello timeout that kills the child by pid; shutdown by SIGTERM then SIGKILL on the pid.\n- **Packaging:** no lockfile change, no new dependency; `bin`, `test` and `test:cli` unchanged (`release_workflow_parity` 6/6); `npm run build` succeeds.\n- **The acceptance:** the example spawns the real sidecar against the scripted gateway and ends `VERIFIED`; a false completion claim is not VERIFIED, and with the verifier denied the outcome is UNVERIFIED.\n- **Mutations:** approving on an undefined decision (2 failures), letting `{always: true}` through (1), any truthy decision allowing (1), `lib.ts` importing `index.js` (the test file aborts).\n\n**Tests at this head:** `lib_entry` 6/6, `sidecar_client` 19/19, `embed_example` 3/3, `sidecar` 65/65, `protocol_parity` 5/5, `leak_guard` 6/6, `release_workflow_parity` 6/6, `check_requirements` 28/28; `tsc`, `check_invariants`, `check_deprecated_lock` and the complexity gate pass.\n\n**Not checked:** the full package build twice with the byte comparison, the SBOM and notices, Node 22, the hang and huge-line paths against a real child.\n"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011ChMxYmVqDpUMvrSFngXyP","requestRef":"8322b66f-3e83-41a6-b710-62330807c865","requestedModel":"claude-fable-5-2","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"66c9e271-d7d7-4d9c-888b-e7a498166b02","timestamp":"2026-11-24T15:04:56.005Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"main","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
