{"parentUuid":"b429a675-a3e8-45d9-86ec-6112d1cf310b","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"c3e4ded3-5447-4b5c-9048-d207d606abe7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<system-reminder>\n<tools-used-before-summary>Agent, AskUserQuestion, Bash, Edit, Monitor, Read, ReadMcpResourceTool, ScheduleWakeup, SendMessage, TaskStop, ToolSearch, WebFetch, Write, mcp__plugin_claude-mem_mcp-search__get_observations</tools-used-before-summary>\n</system-reminder>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   - **Active goal (Stop hook):** `/goal complete and land v1.3.0` — \"treat the condition itself as your directive and do not pause to ask the user what to do.\" Plan: `docs/v1.3.0/PLAN.md`; all work lands on `release/v1.3.0`; one merge to `main` at the end.\n   - **Latest and governing owner directive (2026-11-24 ~08:50Z, verbatim):** \"Required: completion of Unbuilt and Unfinished items as listed above. Once that has been satisfied, the merge to main and release process is yours to complete.\" The list it refers to: **Unbuilt** PF-3, PF-4, SB-1, MT-2, BG-1, BG-2, HK-1, HK-2, HK-3, PA-2; **Unfinished** GV-1 slices 3–4, the GV-5 allowlists, the six VR-2 follow-ups (on PR #756). This supersedes the earlier \"merge and CI only\" role for these units. The go-ahead for merge to `main`, RC tag and release is conditional on those items being complete (not a go-ahead to tag earlier). BG-3 stays deferred to v1.4 (plan defers it).\n   - **Earlier owner messages in this segment:** \"dependabot PRs were supposed to be retarted to v1.3.0\" (correction: retarget Dependabot PRs to the release branch and merge there; don't park them); \"proceed\".\n   - **Earlier role decisions (still relevant for queue behaviour):** owner gave this session the MERGE QUEUE and CI work (\"Merge and CI, as before\"); \"let codex focus on the release development work itself. you take the CI work.\"\n   - **Standing security/process constraints (remain in force, verbatim where from owner/AGENTS.md):**\n     - \"Push, tag and publish only on an explicit owner instruction; release authority is the owner's.\" (now delegated conditionally per the directive above)\n     - Gateway key \"comes from the environment (`~/.config/nexus/config.env`) and is never printed\"; take the `GATEWAY` claim for any inference run; the gateway (10.0.8.5) is the only live provider.\n     - \"A throwaway `HOME` is mandatory\" for tests; isolate HOME for every test or probe. Never read anything under the real `~/.nexus` or the real `/etc/nexus` (or `~/.config/nexus`, `~/.gitconfig`).\n     - \"stop a process by its own pid, never `pkill -f`\"; claim a slice or hot file under `$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/` before editing; one worktree and branch per slice under `~/nexus-wt/`, never `~/nexus-code` itself; check `git log` for foreign commits before each commit.\n     - Merge rules: required checks `test-matrix (22)`, `test-matrix (24)`, `linux-x86_64`; read each conclusion; `gh pr merge <n> --merge --match-head-commit <full-sha>`; one PR at a time then read the release-branch CI; confirm PR checks ran on the current merge commit (merge parents = current tip + head); bring branches up to date by MERGING the release branch in, never rebase/force-push. Version tags are immutable. Never rewrite history.\n     - Release-branch rule: nothing merges into `main` until the release is ready to tag; PRs opened against `main` (Dependabot, others) get retargeted to `release/v1.3.0`.\n     - Never include the user's name/email/project in requests to outside services; never print or commit secrets.\n     - Re-read claims (`owner.json`) and the claims log before every commit, push, PR and merge, and after any pause.\n     - Reviews are posted as PR COMMENTS with verdict + SHA; independent review before merging anything security-relevant, including my own PRs.\n     - Release mechanics follow AGENTS.md and `docs/RELEASE_PROCESS.md`: RC first; stable = version-only commit on the accepted RC, landed on `main` via merge-commit PR, then tag (`release.yml` requires tagged commit to be an ancestor of `main`); report gates as measured (\"ledger closed, qualification pending\").\n     - No deletion of `~/.nexus/backups` has been authorised.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Nexus Code: TypeScript CLI (`cli/src`), Rust core/TUI (`core/`), sidecar NDJSON protocol, eval harness.\n   - Multi-agent coordination via `.git/nexus-claims/<CLAIM>/owner.json` + `nexus-claims.log`. Agents: this session (`claude-invariants-audit`), Codex (`gpt6-codex`/`GPT-6 Codex`/`codex-gpt-6`), Cursor. All use the same GitHub account; another session repeatedly merges PRs outside the queue (including over open REQUEST CHANGES) and takes over my claims/worktrees during quota pauses.\n   - CI (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`): `test-gates` (22/24: lint incl. complexity gate, cargo test, gates), `test-shard` (Node × 4 shards, with push-written cargo cache), aggregator `test-matrix`, `linux-x86_64` (packaging only since #746, ~5–7 min), `diff-coverage`. `lsp-real-servers.yml` and `real-project-smoke.yml` only run on `main` by schedule → dispatch by hand on release (`gh workflow run <wf> --ref release/v1.3.0`).\n   - Complexity gate: `cli/critical-complexity-baseline.json`, `cli/scripts/check_critical_complexity.ts` (needs `@babel/parser`, installed `--no-save` into `~/nexus-code/cli/node_modules`): `runTurnImpl`, `dispatchToolCallImpl`, `runSubagent`, `compactNowImpl`, `driveOperation` must not grow in CC/nesting.\n   - Recurring CI pitfalls for new PRs: new test files must `import \"./helpers/leak_guard.js\"`; regenerate `docs/protocol/sidecar-v1.schema.json` (`gen_protocol_schema.mjs`) and `cli/test/fixtures/protocol_v1_schema_samples.jsonl` (`gen_protocol_samples.mjs`); ACP schema generator `gen_acp_schema.mjs --check`.\n   - Security patterns established: verify service kill logic (SIGSTOP tree before each signal stage, remember pid+start time, sweep survivors); audit export refuses repos whose own git config names programs or that have submodules; hooks deny/annotate only; managed policy can only tighten.\n   - Host notes: zsh (use `bash -c` for loops; `$PIPESTATUS` empty); `rtk` filters output (`rtk proxy`); a safety check blocks shell scripts containing `rm` (write scripts with Write tool, avoid rm); host 18 cores, load 13–20 from parallel agents makes timing tests flaky (`acp_client_conformance`, `turn_deadline_abort`, `sidecar` timing tests, `context_convergence` very slow; `doctor.test.ts` fails 11 tests on base too); use `TMPDIR=/dev/shm` for fsync-heavy tests; fresh worktree needs `ln -s ~/nexus-code/cli/node_modules cli/node_modules` and `cp ~/nexus-wt/ls1b/core/target/release/{harness-core,nexus-tui} core/target/release/`. Usage-limit pauses kill subagents (resume via SendMessage).\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **Memory** (`/home/mike/.claude/projects/-home-mike-nexus-code/memory/`): `v130-progress.md` (running log; last entries describe build phase and the 11:00Z usage stop), `v130-owner-directive-build-and-release-2026-11-24.md` (the directive verbatim + interpretation), `dependabot-retarget-to-release-branch.md`, `merge-and-review-role-2026-11-23.md`, `recheck-claims-after-pause.md`, `MEMORY.md` index.\n   - **Plans** (`/home/mike/nexus-wt/_plans/`): `BG_PLAN.md` (BG-1/BG-2: `nexus runner serve` under systemd user unit, one worker per job, jobs read-only by default, fresh worktree, no auto/allow-always, ≤3 auto-resumes, live attach left to PF-3; schedules = cron/every/once, D21 default), `HK_PLAN.md` (HK-1 two events; HK-2 commit-pinned plugins contributing hooks/skills/MCP only; HK-3 per-file approval for workspace JS plugins), `PF_SB_MT_PA_PLAN.md` (PF-4 unpublished lib driving sidecar as separate process; PF-3 unix socket only, token 0600, one controller + observers; SB-1 three profiles via `--sandbox [engine]:profile`; MT-2 characterization first, dispatch split last with baseline moved once with owner acknowledgement; PA-2 re-run integrated verifiers after each merge, cap 16, refuse edits to other units' tests, operation schema bump), plus `AC1_PLAN.md`, `GV1_PLAN.md`, `VR2_PLAN.md`, etc.\n   - **Merged to `release/v1.3.0` in this segment (by me unless noted):** #746, #747, #722, #725, #720, #719, #748, #745, #750, #751, #752, #753, #755, #758, #759, #760, #761, #762, #763, #764, #766, #769, #770, #776, #777; by other sessions: #741, #749, #754, #756, #757, #765, #767, #768, #771, #772, #773, #774, #775, #778, #781. Release tip at last check `83413dc8` (CI green).\n   - **`cli/src/audit_export.ts`** (`repositoryConfiguresPrograms`, `GIT_PROGRAM_KEYS`, reason `workspace_configures_git_programs`): lists repo-scope git config for `filter.*`, `core.fsmonitor|attributesfile|worktree|hookspath|sshcommand|gitproxy`, `diff.*.textconv|command`, `diff.external`; refuses if scope not system/global/command; also refuses gitlink (mode 160000 in `git ls-files --stage`) or non-empty `<gitdir>/modules/`; no early return after clean config (#772 + #776).\n   - **`cli/src/core/verify_service.ts`** `forkRunner`/`signalTree` (#767, #770): stop tree (SIGSTOP worker and descendants pass by pass, `KILL_LISTING_PASSES = 6`), signal, SIGCONT survivors; `seen` map pid→kernel start time (`startedAt` from `/proc/<pid>/stat`); sweep in `finish` when aborted; don't touch worker pid after exit; `onProcessExit` uses 1 pass.\n   - **`cli/src/lsp.ts`** (#751): after `initialized`, `this.sendNotification(\"workspace/didChangeConfiguration\", { settings: {} });` (Pyright waits for it when workspaceFolders offered).\n   - **`cli/test/sandbox_cancel.test.ts`** (#750): unique `NAP = 100_000 + process.pid` sleep and bwrap pids filtered by test root.\n   - **`cli/src/acp_stdio.ts`** (#752, #753, #777): `acpStartupRefusal`, signal exit, checkpoint choice → cancel, `dropPendingApproval`, `stopping` flag, shutdown grace; per-workspace base pin (`workspaceBase`, cap 16), result fields `workspace`/`base_pinned_commit`/`base_pinned_at` (schema v4), id-less receipt get returns turn receipts only.\n   - **Open PRs at last check:** #782 `v1/hk1-hooks-lib` head `034c278c` (mine, HK-1, three slices: `cli/src/core/{hooks,hook_runner,content_trust,strict_json,process_identity}.ts`, `cli/src/{hooks_cli,doctor_hooks}.ts`, block in `agent.ts`, `docs/HOOKS.md`, `examples/hooks/`, 13 test files/101 tests; known wrinkle: spine authority stage runs after hook stage so a deny hook replaces gate reason with `HOOK_DENIED` for read-only writes); #779 `v1/pf4-lib-entry` head `a299f809` (Codex, PF-4, checks green; last commit \"approve configured verifier in embedder\" needs scrutiny); #780 `v1/bg1-runner-lib` head `c511326f` (Codex, BG-1, +7182, test-matrix RED; also adds `strict_json.ts` and `process_identity.ts` → conflicts with #782).\n   - **Worktrees:** `~/nexus-wt/hk1` (v1/hk1-hooks-lib, mine), `~/nexus-wt/pa2` (v1/pa2-verified-merges, mine, implementer running), `~/nexus-wt/polfu` (v1/policy-followups, new, for #778 follow-ups, nothing edited yet), `~/nexus-wt/bg1`, `pf4`, `sb1` (now Codex's), `gv1c` (merged).\n   - **Claims:** mine: `HK1_HOOKS`, `PA2_VERIFIED_MERGES`, `V130_REMAINING_UNITS_PLANS`, `GV1_SLICES_3_4_GV5` (merged; can be released). Codex: `BG1_DETACHED_RUNS`, `PF4_LIBRARY_ENTRY`, `SB1_PERMISSION_PROFILES` (handoff 12:12Z).\n   - **Code read for the in-progress follow-up (polfu):**\n     - `cli/src/core/managed_policy.ts` `permitsMcpServer`: `const matches = (entry) => { if (entry.startsWith(\"command:\")) return server.command !== undefined && entry.slice(8) === server.command; if (entry.startsWith(\"url:\")) return serverOrigin !== undefined && entry.slice(4) === serverOrigin; return entry === server.name; };` — planned change: a bare-name entry must not match when `server.fromWorkspace` is true.\n     - `cli/src/policy_cli.ts` `checkPolicyFile`: error string `` `${line}: ${error.detail}` `` echoes file tokens — planned: truncate/omit quoted tokens.\n     - `cli/src/index.ts` ~720–730 (verify action): `network: Boolean(options.sandboxNetwork)`; `verifyFlagRefusal(managedPolicy(), { yes, sandboxNone, sandboxNetwork: Boolean(options.sandboxNetwork) })`; `cli/src/sandbox.ts:720,892`: `networkAllowed = options.network !== false && (options.network === true || sandboxNetworkEnabled())` — so with `network: false` passed explicitly the env `NEXUS_SANDBOX_NETWORK` is NOT consulted (line 722/726 pass a boolean); only if `network` were undefined would the env apply. `config.ts:511` already clamps the env for normal runs. Conclusion pending: verify path appears safe when a boolean is always passed; confirm the `sandbox === undefined` case.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - Parked Dependabot PRs because they targeted `main` → **user correction** (\"dependabot PRs were supposed to be retarted to v1.3.0\"): retargeted with `gh pr edit --base`, merged `main` into release via #747 to remove conflicts, merged each after merging release in; saved memory.\n   - Claimed in a PR comment and log that I had pushed a fix to #762 before reading the push result (rejected): posted corrections; rule: read every push/merge result before stating it. Later log template printed \"merge call: not issued\" for a successful merge (empty output): corrected in log; now use explicit `res=succeeded/failed`.\n   - `git checkout <file>` to undo a mutation wiped uncommitted changes twice: now copy the file aside and restore from the copy; commit before mutating.\n   - #767 diagnosis (worker starts next verifier) was only partly right; reviewer's cancel loop found the real window (fork after `ps` snapshot; sandbox reparented to init); three iterations of fix until 0 orphans in ~600 runs (#770). Lesson: measure before asserting a cause.\n   - #772's first hostile test was vacuous (changed file size so git never re-hashed; unquoted `;` cut the included filter command): fixed by `fs.utimesSync` same-size mtime bump and quoting; confirmed failing with guard removed. Then a probe found the submodule bypass; first fix had no effect because of an early `return false` in my function; fixed in #776.\n   - Shell quoting failures (apostrophe inside `bash -c '…'`, backticks in heredoc) → write bodies/scripts with the Write tool and use `--body-file`.\n   - Safety check blocked a script containing `rm` inside `bash -c` → rewrote as script file using `mktemp -d`, no rm.\n   - Started VR-2 myself when queue was empty; it was taken over \"owner-directed\" by Codex; later the owner explicitly directed me to build the remaining units.\n   - Usage-limit pauses killed subagents; Codex took BG-1/PF-4/SB-1 during the last pause; I acknowledged in the log and left those to Codex.\n   - The pause note to the claims log failed (cwd issue: `.git/nexus-claims` relative path) — later ACK written on resume.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Solved: Pyright regression on release (#751); sandbox_cancel flake (#750); CI long pole (#746, #748: required checks ~10 min); orphaned verifier on cancel (#770); audit-export git program execution incl. submodules (#772, #776); four ACP blockers after #741 was merged over review (#752/#753); readiness inventory overstatements (#759); VR-2 follow-ups (#777); GV-1 s3–4 + GV-5 (#778).\n   - Reviews posted with verdicts on #741, #745 (3 rounds), #757, #758 (3 rounds), #760 (2), #761, #762, #763, #764, #765, #766, #767, #769, #770, #771 (3), #772, #774, #775, #776, #777, #778.\n   - Open follow-ups recorded on PRs: #778 (bare-name `mcp.allow` admits workspace redefinition; `policy check` echoes file fragments; hard-link limit; sha256 pin covers entry file only), #770/#761/#763 (flight recorder: marker-unwritable restart; one failed redaction ends chaining), #766 (complexity gate ignores inline callbacks; wiring not pinned), #775 (doc over-claims resume after raising cap), #774 (admission check not pinned; clock step), #768 doc sentence wrong (lint not in linux-x86_64), candidate-identity git exposure for other callers, GV-1 \"slice 5\" items still \"not yet\" (`egress.secret_destinations`, sandbox consulting `sandbox.forbid_network`).\n   - Ongoing: flaky tests under host load (`acp_client_conformance`, `turn_deadline_abort`, sidecar timing); #780/#782 overlap on `strict_json.ts`/`process_identity.ts`; operation schema version reconciliation between PA-2 and #780.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - \"dependabot PRs were supposed to be retarted to v1.3.0\"\n   - \"proceed\"\n   - \"Required: completion of Unbuilt and Unfinished items as listed above. Once that has been satisfied, the merge to main and release process is yours to complete.\"\n   - (System-generated: Stop-hook feedback repeatedly stating v1.3.0 is not landed; goal check-ins; usage-limit notices; \"Your claude.ai usage limit has reset. Continue the task…\".)\n   - (Carried from earlier summary: \"saying so\"; \"Merge and review only (Recommended)\"; \"Review the OpenCode CI files…\"; \"let codex focus on the release development work itself. you take the CI work.\"; \"#737 had requested changes applied already\"; \"review the dependabot PRs too\"; \"Merge and CI, as before\"; Cursor handoff paste.)\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - **Units still to complete (owner directive):** HK-1 (#782: get review result, fix findings, reconcile with #780 if it lands first, merge), PA-2 (implementer running in `~/nexus-wt/pa2`; then push/PR/review/merge), MT-2 (slice 1 characterization, then registry, dispatch split last with freeze + baseline move), BG-2, HK-2, HK-3, PF-3 (claim each before starting; ask Codex in log first); BG-1 (#780, Codex, red), PF-4 (#779, Codex), SB-1 slices 2–3 (Codex) — review and merge via queue.\n   - Post review of #779 when its reviewer reports; review #780 when green.\n   - #778 follow-up PR from `~/nexus-wt/polfu` (branch `v1/policy-followups`): bare-name allow must not match workspace definitions; truncate tokens in `policy check` errors; settle/document `NEXUS_SANDBOX_NETWORK` vs `nexus verify`; docs for hard-link and sha256 limits.\n   - Release the stale `GV1_SLICES_3_4_GV5` claim; update `docs/releases/v1.3.0-READINESS.md` and CHANGELOG as units land.\n   - When all listed items are complete and gates G-1..G-7 can be evaluated: version bump + changelog + release notes (G-7 framing), single merge of `release/v1.3.0` to `main` via merge-commit PR, RC tag, measurement, stable (version-only commit, tag) per `docs/RELEASE_PROCESS.md`.\n   - Dispatch `lsp-real-servers.yml` and `real-project-smoke.yml` on the release tip after significant merges.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   Just resumed after the 11:00–14:40Z usage pause (2026-11-24). Release tip `83413dc8`, CI green. I logged an ACK that Codex now owns BG-1/PF-4/SB-1; merged release into `v1/hk1-hooks-lib`, pushed (`034c278c`), opened **#782** (HK-1) and launched its reviewer (agent `a113015cb5d57f7c1`); launched reviewer for **#779** (agent `a51e8a083eab51d80`) and the **PA-2 implementer** (agent `a2b26453fbd1df4f6`, worktree `~/nexus-wt/pa2`, commits locally per slice, no push); resumed and received the #778 review (ACCEPT WITH FOLLOW-UPS) and posted it on the PR; logged the #780/#782 file overlap for Codex. I then created `~/nexus-wt/polfu` (branch `v1/policy-followups` from `origin/release/v1.3.0`, node_modules symlink and Rust binaries in place) and was reading code for the three #778 follow-ups; the last command traced `sandboxNetworkEnabled()` uses in `cli/src/sandbox.ts` (lines 720 and 892: env is consulted only when `options.network` is neither `true` nor `false`). No edits have been made in `polfu` yet.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Continue the #778 follow-up in `~/nexus-wt/polfu` (stated on the PR: \"I am opening a follow-up for the first\"): change `permitsMcpServer` so a bare-name `mcp.allow` entry does not match a server with `fromWorkspace: true` (with a refusal message pointing to `command:`/`url:` entries), cap echoed tokens in `checkPolicyFile` errors, confirm whether `nexus verify` ever passes `network: undefined` (index.ts ~720–726) and document or clamp, update `docs/MANAGED_POLICY.md`, add tests to `managed_policy_allowlists.test.ts`/`policy_cli.test.ts`, run them plus `tsc` and gates, push, open the PR, get an independent review, merge when green. In parallel, act on the notifications from the #782 reviewer, the #779 reviewer and the PA-2 implementer as they arrive (post reviews; push PA-2 and open its PR), keeping to the owner directive: \"Required: completion of Unbuilt and Unfinished items as listed above. Once that has been satisfied, the merge to main and release process is yours to complete.\"\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /home/mike/.claude/projects/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\n\nThe messages after this summary are the most recent messages from before compaction, kept verbatim. The summary was written without seeing them, so something it says has not happened yet may already have happened in them."},"isVisibleInTranscriptOnly":true,"isCompactSummary":true,"uuid":"1d1a7fd5-4a24-4f09-878f-51489093419b","timestamp":"2026-11-24T14:47:46.599Z","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":40,"turnIndex":268},"turnPromptId":"c3e4ded3-5447-4b5c-9048-d207d606abe7","turnOrigin":"task_notification","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"main","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
{"parentUuid":"1d1a7fd5-4a24-4f09-878f-51489093419b","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/rev779.md","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/rev779.md","content":"**Independent review at `a299f8093a827450b3a4a4d642a557e94a2bcd5b` — REQUEST CHANGES (one blocker, in the example and the docs snippet; the library itself is sound)**\n\n**Blocking**\n\n- **The example approves any request whose tool is `\"verifier\"`** (`examples/embed/embed.mjs:34-38`, the snippet in `docs/EMBEDDING.md`, `examples/embed/README.md`; added by this head commit). That tool name is used for the operator's configured verifier (seen here as `review: {command: \"node --test\", detail: \"configured\"}`), and also for a verifier the model declares for a requirement (`completion_oracle.ts:274-275`), for a discovered project verifier, and for the type-check oracle (`completion_oracle.ts:126`). The example approves all of them without looking at the command or where it came from. The library denies by default, so the fault is not in a default; but a copied example lets a project-supplied or model-declared verifier run with no human grant, where the CLI asks the operator (and auto-approves only with `-y`).\n  Fix: approve only when `request.tool === \"verifier\" && request.review?.command === \"node --test\" && request.review?.detail === \"configured\"`, deny the rest, change the docs snippet the same way, and add a test in which a model-declared verifier request is denied.\n\n**Not blocking**\n\n1. `extraArgs: [\"-y\"]` and `[\"--mode\", \"auto\"]` reach auto approval: both runs ended VERIFIED with no approval request, and the sidecar does not refuse them (run). `docs/EMBEDDING.md` says `extraArgs` is the embedder's own authority and the plan accepted it. A test should pin it; consider refusing those flags in `extraArgs`, or in the sidecar as `nexus acp` does.\n2. No timeout on `onApproval` (`sidecar_client.ts:315`): a handler that never answers holds the turn until the abort signal. An optional timeout that denies would bound it.\n3. The no-handler default is only pinned once the real decision path is mutated (changing the initial value alone is an equivalent mutant).\n4. `tsconfig.lib.json` emits about 60 declaration files into `dist/types`, and `package-linux.sh:64` copies all of `dist`, so the tarball grows. The output is deterministic, so the two-build comparison should hold; the package build was not run here.\n5. A managed policy that cannot be used ends the sidecar with exit 1 instead of 2 (it loads policy through `buildConfig`, not `requireManagedPolicyAtStartup`).\n\n**Held up**\n\n- **Exports:** `NEXUS_LIB_API_VERSION`, `spawnSidecar`, `SidecarClient`, `SidecarClientError`, and types. Nothing runs a turn in-process, skips managed policy or workspace trust, selects auto, or grants allow-always.\n- **Import side effects:** the import graph reaches `sidecar_client.ts`, `acp/jsonrpc.ts` and `acp/types.ts` only; nothing from `index.ts`. Importing `dist/lib.js` with a HOME that does not exist: exit 0, no output, nothing created.\n- **Approvals through the client**, with a fake child: no handler, `{approve: true}`, `{always: true}`, `true`, `\"Approve\"` and `\"approve-always\"` all become deny; only `\"approve\"` approves, always with `always: false`. Concurrent requests are answered separately; a stale id is ignored; a checkpoint choice cancels the turn.\n- **Robustness:** lines bounded at 16 MiB; a wrong protocol version dropped; a hello timeout that kills the child by pid; shutdown by SIGTERM then SIGKILL on the pid.\n- **Packaging:** no lockfile change, no new dependency; `bin`, `test` and `test:cli` unchanged (`release_workflow_parity` 6/6); `npm run build` succeeds.\n- **The acceptance:** the example spawns the real sidecar against the scripted gateway and ends `VERIFIED`; a false completion claim is not VERIFIED, and with the verifier denied the outcome is UNVERIFIED.\n- **Mutations:** approving on an undefined decision (2 failures), letting `{always: true}` through (1), any truthy decision allowing (1), `lib.ts` importing `index.js` (the test file aborts).\n\n**Tests at this head:** `lib_entry` 6/6, `sidecar_client` 19/19, `embed_example` 3/3, `sidecar` 65/65, `protocol_parity` 5/5, `leak_guard` 6/6, `release_workflow_parity` 6/6, `check_requirements` 28/28; `tsc`, `check_invariants`, `check_deprecated_lock` and the complexity gate pass.\n\n**Not checked:** the full package build twice with the byte comparison, the SBOM and notices, Node 22, the hang and huge-line paths against a real child.\n","numLines":29,"startLine":1,"totalLines":29}},"displayPath":"../../../tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/rev779.md","savedCopyFraming":{"enveloped":false}},"type":"attachment","uuid":"fb944e08-abe3-4f5a-8932-ce96b10371c0","timestamp":"2026-11-24T15:06:17.307Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/rev779.md\"}\n</system-reminder>"},{"content":"<system-reminder>\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\t**Independent review at `a299f8093a827450b3a4a4d642a557e94a2bcd5b` — REQUEST CHANGES (one blocker, in the example and the docs snippet; the library itself is sound)**\n2\t\n3\t**Blocking**\n4\t\n5\t- **The example approves any request whose tool is `\"verifier\"`** (`examples/embed/embed.mjs:34-38`, the snippet in `docs/EMBEDDING.md`, `examples/embed/README.md`; added by this head commit). That tool name is used for the operator's configured verifier (seen here as `review: {command: \"node --test\", detail: \"configured\"}`), and also for a verifier the model declares for a requirement (`completion_oracle.ts:274-275`), for a discovered project verifier, and for the type-check oracle (`completion_oracle.ts:126`). The example approves all of them without looking at the command or where it came from. The library denies by default, so the fault is not in a default; but a copied example lets a project-supplied or model-declared verifier run with no human grant, where the CLI asks the operator (and auto-approves only with `-y`).\n6\t  Fix: approve only when `request.tool === \"verifier\" && request.review?.command === \"node --test\" && request.review?.detail === \"configured\"`, deny the rest, change the docs snippet the same way, and add a test in which a model-declared verifier request is denied.\n7\t\n8\t**Not blocking**\n9\t\n10\t1. `extraArgs: [\"-y\"]` and `[\"--mode\", \"auto\"]` reach auto approval: both runs ended VERIFIED with no approval request, and the sidecar does not refuse them (run). `docs/EMBEDDING.md` says `extraArgs` is the embedder's own authority and the plan accepted it. A test should pin it; consider refusing those flags in `extraArgs`, or in the sidecar as `nexus acp` does.\n11\t2. No timeout on `onApproval` (`sidecar_client.ts:315`): a handler that never answers holds the turn until the abort signal. An optional timeout that denies would bound it.\n12\t3. The no-handler default is only pinned once the real decision path is mutated (changing the initial value alone is an equivalent mutant).\n13\t4. `tsconfig.lib.json` emits about 60 declaration files into `dist/types`, and `package-linux.sh:64` copies all of `dist`, so the tarball grows. The output is deterministic, so the two-build comparison should hold; the package build was not run here.\n14\t5. A managed policy that cannot be used ends the sidecar with exit 1 instead of 2 (it loads policy through `buildConfig`, not `requireManagedPolicyAtStartup`).\n15\t\n16\t**Held up**\n17\t\n18\t- **Exports:** `NEXUS_LIB_API_VERSION`, `spawnSidecar`, `SidecarClient`, `SidecarClientError`, and types. Nothing runs a turn in-process, skips managed policy or workspace trust, selects auto, or grants allow-always.\n19\t- **Import side effects:** the import graph reaches `sidecar_client.ts`, `acp/jsonrpc.ts` and `acp/types.ts` only; nothing from `index.ts`. Importing `dist/lib.js` with a HOME that does not exist: exit 0, no output, nothing created.\n20\t- **Approvals through the client**, with a fake child: no handler, `{approve: true}`, `{always: true}`, `true`, `\"Approve\"` and `\"approve-always\"` all become deny; only `\"approve\"` approves, always with `always: false`. Concurrent requests are answered separately; a stale id is ignored; a checkpoint choice cancels the turn.\n21\t- **Robustness:** lines bounded at 16 MiB; a wrong protocol version dropped; a hello timeout that kills the child by pid; shutdown by SIGTERM then SIGKILL on the pid.\n22\t- **Packaging:** no lockfile change, no new dependency; `bin`, `test` and `test:cli` unchanged (`release_workflow_parity` 6/6); `npm run build` succeeds.\n23\t- **The acceptance:** the example spawns the real sidecar against the scripted gateway and ends `VERIFIED`; a false completion claim is not VERIFIED, and with the verifier denied the outcome is UNVERIFIED.\n24\t- **Mutations:** approving on an undefined decision (2 failures), letting `{always: true}` through (1), any truthy decision allowing (1), `lib.ts` importing `index.js` (the test file aborts).\n25\t\n26\t**Tests at this head:** `lib_entry` 6/6, `sidecar_client` 19/19, `embed_example` 3/3, `sidecar` 65/65, `protocol_parity` 5/5, `leak_guard` 6/6, `release_workflow_parity` 6/6, `check_requirements` 28/28; `tsc`, `check_invariants`, `check_deprecated_lock` and the complexity gate pass.\n27\t\n28\t**Not checked:** the full package build twice with the byte comparison, the SBOM and notices, Node 22, the hang and huge-line paths against a real child.\n29\t\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"user","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"main","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
{"parentUuid":"fb944e08-abe3-4f5a-8932-ce96b10371c0","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/rev782.md","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/rev782.md","content":"**Independent review at `034c278cad62e7e849c4b68037d2ef32b2801af5` — REQUEST CHANGES. The hook output handling and the gate ordering hold; all three blockers are about who can get a hook trusted. I am fixing them on this branch.**\n\n**Blocking, each confirmed by running**\n\n1. **The model can approve its own project hooks.** `nexus hooks approve --sha256 <hex>` works with no terminal (`hooks_cli.ts`, about line 118), and neither the trust store (`extension_trust.json`) nor `hooks.json` is in `DEFAULT_PROTECTED_PATHS` (`security.ts:163`), unlike `policy_trust.json` and `trusted_workspaces.json`. In auto mode: `write_file .nexus/hooks.json`, then `run_command \"nexus hooks approve --sha256 <hash> -w <repo>\"` exited 0, wrote the store, and the hook ran on the next call. (Unsandboxed `run_command` sees `~/.config/nexus`; with `--sandbox` the home directory is masked; in review mode the operator would see the command.)\n2. **With the workspace set to the home directory, the model can write an active operator hooks file.** `write_file .config/nexus/hooks.json` succeeded; at umask 022 the file is mode 644, which the mode check accepts, and the \"operator\" hook ran with no approval. At umask 002 the file is rejected and every call is denied instead.\n3. **Approval does not pin the script a hook names.** After approving `command: [\"./guard.sh\"]`, the model overwrote `guard.sh` and the next call ran the model's script with the operator's rights, outside the sandbox, with no new approval. `docs/HOOKS.md` says the approval is for \"the file's exact bytes\" and never says this.\n\n**Not blocking**\n\n- A hook's denial reason reaches the model as `[hook X (project)] <up to 1000 chars>`: one line, named and sourced, but not marked as untrusted text, so an instruction in it passes through. It should be quoted as hook-supplied text. (Plain stdout and the receipt's hook summaries do not reach the model.)\n- A running hook is not stopped by cancel or by the turn deadline, and time spent queued behind another hook is outside its 120 s budget. The document says the first.\n- `HOOKS.md` claims subagents and operation units are covered. Subagents are (same dispatch and spine). Operation units get their own agent on another workspace path, so project hooks do not run there; no test covers either.\n- The hooks stage also gates the operator's own `!cmd`; undocumented.\n- When a hook denies a call that a spine-stage gate (read-only, workspace boundary, grants) would have denied, the gate's reason and anything the later stages would have recorded (sandbox-denial events) are replaced by `HOOK_DENIED`. A hook-denied call is still charged to the tool-invocation budget.\n\n**Held up**\n\n- Nineteen output shapes fed to the reducer (duplicate keys, a BOM, `continue` as a string, null and array decisions, a deny mixed with an allow, exit codes 1, 3 and 126, stderr only): none admitted anything, and every unreadable or unknown shape denied.\n- A `post-tool` hook only reads the receipt. The move of helpers out of `verify_service.ts` is verbatim (`verify_service` 10/10, `mcp_verify` 7/7).\n- Mutations, each caught: an allow that skips the authority stage; a hook error that continues; skipping the project hash check (6 failures); passing the full environment.\n\n**Tests at this head, 0 failures:** the thirteen hook files (101 tests), `approval_policy` 16, `mcp_tool_through_spine` 3, `sandbox_denial_events` 6, `hash_chain` 28, `leak_guard` 6, `protocol_parity` 5, `protocol_schema` 8, `check_requirements` 28; `tsc`, the complexity gate and `check_invariants` pass.\n\n**Not checked:** the approve command under `--sandbox` in production form; a hook stalling a turn past its deadline (read only); the doctor output for an invalid operator file beyond its test; the schema and examples.\n","numLines":26,"startLine":1,"totalLines":26}},"displayPath":"../../../tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/rev782.md","savedCopyFraming":{"enveloped":false}},"type":"attachment","uuid":"48540a6f-e304-4a1a-b5e5-91c24af448d4","timestamp":"2026-11-24T15:06:17.307Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/rev782.md\"}\n</system-reminder>"},{"content":"<system-reminder>\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\t**Independent review at `034c278cad62e7e849c4b68037d2ef32b2801af5` — REQUEST CHANGES. The hook output handling and the gate ordering hold; all three blockers are about who can get a hook trusted. I am fixing them on this branch.**\n2\t\n3\t**Blocking, each confirmed by running**\n4\t\n5\t1. **The model can approve its own project hooks.** `nexus hooks approve --sha256 <hex>` works with no terminal (`hooks_cli.ts`, about line 118), and neither the trust store (`extension_trust.json`) nor `hooks.json` is in `DEFAULT_PROTECTED_PATHS` (`security.ts:163`), unlike `policy_trust.json` and `trusted_workspaces.json`. In auto mode: `write_file .nexus/hooks.json`, then `run_command \"nexus hooks approve --sha256 <hash> -w <repo>\"` exited 0, wrote the store, and the hook ran on the next call. (Unsandboxed `run_command` sees `~/.config/nexus`; with `--sandbox` the home directory is masked; in review mode the operator would see the command.)\n6\t2. **With the workspace set to the home directory, the model can write an active operator hooks file.** `write_file .config/nexus/hooks.json` succeeded; at umask 022 the file is mode 644, which the mode check accepts, and the \"operator\" hook ran with no approval. At umask 002 the file is rejected and every call is denied instead.\n7\t3. **Approval does not pin the script a hook names.** After approving `command: [\"./guard.sh\"]`, the model overwrote `guard.sh` and the next call ran the model's script with the operator's rights, outside the sandbox, with no new approval. `docs/HOOKS.md` says the approval is for \"the file's exact bytes\" and never says this.\n8\t\n9\t**Not blocking**\n10\t\n11\t- A hook's denial reason reaches the model as `[hook X (project)] <up to 1000 chars>`: one line, named and sourced, but not marked as untrusted text, so an instruction in it passes through. It should be quoted as hook-supplied text. (Plain stdout and the receipt's hook summaries do not reach the model.)\n12\t- A running hook is not stopped by cancel or by the turn deadline, and time spent queued behind another hook is outside its 120 s budget. The document says the first.\n13\t- `HOOKS.md` claims subagents and operation units are covered. Subagents are (same dispatch and spine). Operation units get their own agent on another workspace path, so project hooks do not run there; no test covers either.\n14\t- The hooks stage also gates the operator's own `!cmd`; undocumented.\n15\t- When a hook denies a call that a spine-stage gate (read-only, workspace boundary, grants) would have denied, the gate's reason and anything the later stages would have recorded (sandbox-denial events) are replaced by `HOOK_DENIED`. A hook-denied call is still charged to the tool-invocation budget.\n16\t\n17\t**Held up**\n18\t\n19\t- Nineteen output shapes fed to the reducer (duplicate keys, a BOM, `continue` as a string, null and array decisions, a deny mixed with an allow, exit codes 1, 3 and 126, stderr only): none admitted anything, and every unreadable or unknown shape denied.\n20\t- A `post-tool` hook only reads the receipt. The move of helpers out of `verify_service.ts` is verbatim (`verify_service` 10/10, `mcp_verify` 7/7).\n21\t- Mutations, each caught: an allow that skips the authority stage; a hook error that continues; skipping the project hash check (6 failures); passing the full environment.\n22\t\n23\t**Tests at this head, 0 failures:** the thirteen hook files (101 tests), `approval_policy` 16, `mcp_tool_through_spine` 3, `sandbox_denial_events` 6, `hash_chain` 28, `leak_guard` 6, `protocol_parity` 5, `protocol_schema` 8, `check_requirements` 28; `tsc`, the complexity gate and `check_invariants` pass.\n24\t\n25\t**Not checked:** the approve command under `--sandbox` in production form; a hook stalling a turn past its deadline (read only); the doctor output for an invalid operator file beyond its test; the schema and examples.\n26\t\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"user","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"main","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
{"parentUuid":"48540a6f-e304-4a1a-b5e5-91c24af448d4","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/rev778.md","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/rev778.md","content":"**Independent review at `afb4ed64f62d4b597eb75286e3fb92209ad367fb` — ACCEPT WITH FOLLOW-UPS. This merged before the review reported, so the follow-ups are against the release branch.**\n\n**Follow-ups, in order of weight**\n\n1. **A bare-name `mcp.allow` entry is not a boundary against a workspace file** (confirmed by running). With `allow = [\"files\"]` and a trusted workspace, a `.mcp.json` that defines a server named `files` with a different `command` was started and that program ran (`permitsMcpServer`, `core/managed_policy.ts:820-839`; `policyDescriptor`, `mcp.ts:129-135`). The same holds for a WebSocket, HTTP or SSE URL under an allowed name. The document says a name entry is the only kind that admits a WebSocket server; it does not say that a name entry pins nothing and that the workspace can redefine the name. Either a name-only entry should not match a definition that comes from the workspace, or the document must say so and recommend `mcp.disable_workspace = true` or `command:` / `url:` entries. I am opening a follow-up for the first.\n2. **`nexus policy check <file>` echoes parts of the file in its parse errors** (confirmed by running): the first token of line 1 as an \"invalid key\", and a value such as `allow = sk-…` as an \"unsupported value\". Pointed at an arbitrary readable file it prints fragments of it. The offending token should be truncated or left out.\n3. **Not traced:** `NEXUS_SANDBOX_NETWORK` is read in `sandbox.ts` and not in `verifyFlagRefusal`, so whether the environment variable gives `nexus verify` network access under a policy that refuses `--sandbox-network` is open.\n4. A hard link to a workspace file placed in the user configuration directory counts as a user file under `disable_workspace` (confirmed by running). A repository cannot create that link; a limit to document.\n5. A `sha256:` plugin pin covers the entry file only, not the modules it imports. To document.\n\n**Held up when run**\n\n- Name tricks (case, trailing space, a Cyrillic look-alike, a zero-width space) are all refused.\n- A configuration symlinked into the workspace, a symlinked parent directory, and a workspace symlink pointing out are all treated as workspace under `disable_workspace`.\n- `addServer` and `addConnection` refuse an unlisted server and nothing is spawned. The ACP adapter validates and ignores `mcpServers`.\n- A plugin symlinked from the user plugin directory into the workspace is not imported under `plugins.disable_workspace`; a `sha256:` mismatch refuses.\n- \"Always\": the approval is clamped, `setApprovalMode(\"auto\")` cannot enter auto under the policy, and the one flag that approves silently is now gated.\n- `doctor --fix` leaves a broken `policy.toml` byte-identical. `policy check --json` stays valid JSON with exit 2 on an unreadable file.\n\n**Mutations, each caught:** removing the gate on `loadAndConnect` (10 failures), on `addConnection` (1), on `addServer` (1), the plugin gate (5), making `verifyFlagRefusal` return nothing (10), making \"always\" stick (1).\n\n**Tests at that head:** `managed_policy_allowlists` 18, `managed_policy_verify` 12, `policy_cli` 23, `managed_policy_enforcement` 113, `managed_policy_schema` 57, `managed_policy_always` 6, `mcp` 4, `mcp_tool_through_spine` 3, `approval_policy` 16, `leak_guard` 6, all passing; `tsc`, the complexity gate, `check_invariants` and `check_requirements` pass. `sidecar` had 7 failures here against 6 on the base on the same loaded host, mostly timeouts; the one extra was not attributed, and CI was green on this head.\n\n**Not checked:** `context_convergence` locally; the REPL path by mutation; `--yes` and `NEXUS_APPROVAL_MODE=auto` at start-up and mode inheritance by subagents and goal runners (read only); a policy file changing on disk mid-session.\n","numLines":25,"startLine":1,"totalLines":25}},"displayPath":"../../../tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/rev778.md","savedCopyFraming":{"enveloped":false}},"type":"attachment","uuid":"88361e99-6f98-4e9e-87d2-1fddca953eba","timestamp":"2026-11-24T15:06:17.307Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/rev778.md\"}\n</system-reminder>"},{"content":"<system-reminder>\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\t**Independent review at `afb4ed64f62d4b597eb75286e3fb92209ad367fb` — ACCEPT WITH FOLLOW-UPS. This merged before the review reported, so the follow-ups are against the release branch.**\n2\t\n3\t**Follow-ups, in order of weight**\n4\t\n5\t1. **A bare-name `mcp.allow` entry is not a boundary against a workspace file** (confirmed by running). With `allow = [\"files\"]` and a trusted workspace, a `.mcp.json` that defines a server named `files` with a different `command` was started and that program ran (`permitsMcpServer`, `core/managed_policy.ts:820-839`; `policyDescriptor`, `mcp.ts:129-135`). The same holds for a WebSocket, HTTP or SSE URL under an allowed name. The document says a name entry is the only kind that admits a WebSocket server; it does not say that a name entry pins nothing and that the workspace can redefine the name. Either a name-only entry should not match a definition that comes from the workspace, or the document must say so and recommend `mcp.disable_workspace = true` or `command:` / `url:` entries. I am opening a follow-up for the first.\n6\t2. **`nexus policy check <file>` echoes parts of the file in its parse errors** (confirmed by running): the first token of line 1 as an \"invalid key\", and a value such as `allow = sk-…` as an \"unsupported value\". Pointed at an arbitrary readable file it prints fragments of it. The offending token should be truncated or left out.\n7\t3. **Not traced:** `NEXUS_SANDBOX_NETWORK` is read in `sandbox.ts` and not in `verifyFlagRefusal`, so whether the environment variable gives `nexus verify` network access under a policy that refuses `--sandbox-network` is open.\n8\t4. A hard link to a workspace file placed in the user configuration directory counts as a user file under `disable_workspace` (confirmed by running). A repository cannot create that link; a limit to document.\n9\t5. A `sha256:` plugin pin covers the entry file only, not the modules it imports. To document.\n10\t\n11\t**Held up when run**\n12\t\n13\t- Name tricks (case, trailing space, a Cyrillic look-alike, a zero-width space) are all refused.\n14\t- A configuration symlinked into the workspace, a symlinked parent directory, and a workspace symlink pointing out are all treated as workspace under `disable_workspace`.\n15\t- `addServer` and `addConnection` refuse an unlisted server and nothing is spawned. The ACP adapter validates and ignores `mcpServers`.\n16\t- A plugin symlinked from the user plugin directory into the workspace is not imported under `plugins.disable_workspace`; a `sha256:` mismatch refuses.\n17\t- \"Always\": the approval is clamped, `setApprovalMode(\"auto\")` cannot enter auto under the policy, and the one flag that approves silently is now gated.\n18\t- `doctor --fix` leaves a broken `policy.toml` byte-identical. `policy check --json` stays valid JSON with exit 2 on an unreadable file.\n19\t\n20\t**Mutations, each caught:** removing the gate on `loadAndConnect` (10 failures), on `addConnection` (1), on `addServer` (1), the plugin gate (5), making `verifyFlagRefusal` return nothing (10), making \"always\" stick (1).\n21\t\n22\t**Tests at that head:** `managed_policy_allowlists` 18, `managed_policy_verify` 12, `policy_cli` 23, `managed_policy_enforcement` 113, `managed_policy_schema` 57, `managed_policy_always` 6, `mcp` 4, `mcp_tool_through_spine` 3, `approval_policy` 16, `leak_guard` 6, all passing; `tsc`, the complexity gate, `check_invariants` and `check_requirements` pass. `sidecar` had 7 failures here against 6 on the base on the same loaded host, mostly timeouts; the one extra was not attributed, and CI was green on this head.\n23\t\n24\t**Not checked:** `context_convergence` locally; the REPL path by mutation; `--yes` and `NEXUS_APPROVAL_MODE=auto` at start-up and mode inheritance by subagents and goal runners (read only); a policy file changing on disk mid-session.\n25\t\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"user","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"main","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
{"parentUuid":"88361e99-6f98-4e9e-87d2-1fddca953eba","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/pr_hk1.md","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/pr_hk1.md","content":"Plan unit HK-1: command hooks. Acceptance from the plan: \"a hook's allow has no effect\". Design: `HK_PLAN.md` (written from this branch's base); three slices, one commit each, plus merges of the release branch.\n\n## What it adds\n\n- **Two events only**: `pre-tool` and `post-tool`. A hook is a program the operator names in `~/.config/nexus/hooks.json`, or one in a project hooks file whose exact content hash the operator has approved (`nexus hooks approve`). A changed project file asks again.\n- **What a hook can do**: deny, or annotate. Its \"allow\" in any dialect and any `updatedInput` are ignored; `ask` counts as deny; an unknown decision denies. A `pre-tool` hook that errors, times out or leaves its output open denies. An invalid operator hooks file denies every tool call.\n- **How it runs**: a subprocess with a hard timeout, stdin JSON, bounded output, a reduced environment (no gateway key, no tool secrets), its process tree killed by pid with start-time checks. The `post-tool` payload is redacted.\n- **Where it attaches**: the spine's `contextAdmission` stage (pre-tool) and `evidenceEmission` (post-tool), through one 16-line block in `agent.ts`. `dispatchToolCallImpl`, `run_turn.ts` and `sidecar.ts` are not edited; the complexity gate is unchanged for all five functions.\n- **Visible**: a denial carries `HOOK_DENIED` and the hook's name in the tool receipt and the flight log.\n- **Commands and docs**: `nexus hooks list|test|approve|revoke`, a doctor finding `hooks.config`, `docs/HOOKS.md` with a runnable example under `examples/hooks/` that a test executes, the hooks file schema `docs/protocol/hooks-v1.schema.json` with its ledger.\n\n## The acceptance, and where the plan was wrong\n\n`hooks_gate_bypass` runs each gate twice, without hooks and with an operator hook that answers \"approve\" in every dialect plus an `updatedInput` aimed at another file, and requires the two receipts to be equal. For the dispatcher's gates (headless approval, operator refusal, protected verification configuration, forbidden command rule, managed-policy forbid and require-human, delegation) the hook is never started.\n\n**The plan assumed the spine is reached only after every gate has approved. That is not so for read-only mode, authority grants and the workspace boundary:** the spine's authority stage enforces them, and it runs after `contextAdmission`. So for a write in read-only mode the hook does run. It still cannot allow the write: its allow is recorded as `ignored_allow` and the denial is word for word the same. But a hook that *denies* there replaces the gate's reason with `HOOK_DENIED`. The attachment follows the plan; the tests assert the real behaviour and `docs/HOOKS.md` states it.\n\n## What a release note must say\n\n- Hooks are unsandboxed programs running with the operator's rights.\n- An invalid `~/.config/nexus/hooks.json` denies every tool call until it is fixed.\n- A non-zero exit other than 2 denies (stricter than the Claude Code convention the payload shape follows).\n- The approval prompt comes before hooks.\n- `serve-mcp` runs no hooks.\n- Project hooks are not a control over the agent: the agent can edit the file, which stops them until the operator approves the new content.\n\n## Tests\n\nThirteen new test files, 101 tests: `strict_json` 9, `hooks_config` 6, `hook_output_reduce` 13, `hook_runner` 8, `content_trust` 7, `hooks_schema` 5, `hooks_gate_bypass` 11, `hooks_deny` 9, `hooks_post_tool` 5, `hooks_project_trust` 9, `hooks_cli` 8, `hooks_examples` 6, `doctor_hooks` 5. Each passed three runs in a row. For each guard a mutation was shown to fail a test (gate order, fail-closed, chain handling, project trust in five ways, environment and redaction, kill and output caps, visibility, the CLI's hash checks); the list is in the implementation report and can be repeated.\n\nAfter merging the release branch (Node 24): the seven hook files rerun pass, `leak_guard` 6/6, `tsc` clean, complexity gate unchanged. Before the merge: the required list of existing files, `context_convergence` 57/57, the three `scripts/check_*.mjs`. `doctor.test.ts` fails the same 11 tests with and without this change (host state).\n\n## Other changes to existing files\n\n`spine.ts` and `flight.ts` (the hook record), `verify_service.ts` (process-identity helpers moved out to `core/process_identity.ts` so hooks and the verify service share them; no behaviour change intended), `index.ts` (2 lines), `doctor.ts` (8 lines), the manual and protocol docs.\n\n## Not in this PR\n\nThe other hook events, HK-2 (commit-pinned plugins) and HK-3 (per-plugin trust). There is no session-start prompt for unapproved project hooks, only a notice at the first tool call.\n\n## Reference coding\n\n`HK_PLAN.md` records the peer comparison (payload and exit-code conventions follow Claude Code's hooks so existing scripts transfer; the \"deny or annotate only, never allow\" rule and fail-closed pre-tool are this repo's own).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n","numLines":46,"startLine":1,"totalLines":46}},"displayPath":"../../../tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/pr_hk1.md","savedCopyFraming":{"enveloped":false}},"type":"attachment","uuid":"d28269b0-4417-40b3-b59e-a7c270532bde","timestamp":"2026-11-24T15:06:17.307Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/pr_hk1.md\"}\n</system-reminder>"},{"content":"<system-reminder>\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\tPlan unit HK-1: command hooks. Acceptance from the plan: \"a hook's allow has no effect\". Design: `HK_PLAN.md` (written from this branch's base); three slices, one commit each, plus merges of the release branch.\n2\t\n3\t## What it adds\n4\t\n5\t- **Two events only**: `pre-tool` and `post-tool`. A hook is a program the operator names in `~/.config/nexus/hooks.json`, or one in a project hooks file whose exact content hash the operator has approved (`nexus hooks approve`). A changed project file asks again.\n6\t- **What a hook can do**: deny, or annotate. Its \"allow\" in any dialect and any `updatedInput` are ignored; `ask` counts as deny; an unknown decision denies. A `pre-tool` hook that errors, times out or leaves its output open denies. An invalid operator hooks file denies every tool call.\n7\t- **How it runs**: a subprocess with a hard timeout, stdin JSON, bounded output, a reduced environment (no gateway key, no tool secrets), its process tree killed by pid with start-time checks. The `post-tool` payload is redacted.\n8\t- **Where it attaches**: the spine's `contextAdmission` stage (pre-tool) and `evidenceEmission` (post-tool), through one 16-line block in `agent.ts`. `dispatchToolCallImpl`, `run_turn.ts` and `sidecar.ts` are not edited; the complexity gate is unchanged for all five functions.\n9\t- **Visible**: a denial carries `HOOK_DENIED` and the hook's name in the tool receipt and the flight log.\n10\t- **Commands and docs**: `nexus hooks list|test|approve|revoke`, a doctor finding `hooks.config`, `docs/HOOKS.md` with a runnable example under `examples/hooks/` that a test executes, the hooks file schema `docs/protocol/hooks-v1.schema.json` with its ledger.\n11\t\n12\t## The acceptance, and where the plan was wrong\n13\t\n14\t`hooks_gate_bypass` runs each gate twice, without hooks and with an operator hook that answers \"approve\" in every dialect plus an `updatedInput` aimed at another file, and requires the two receipts to be equal. For the dispatcher's gates (headless approval, operator refusal, protected verification configuration, forbidden command rule, managed-policy forbid and require-human, delegation) the hook is never started.\n15\t\n16\t**The plan assumed the spine is reached only after every gate has approved. That is not so for read-only mode, authority grants and the workspace boundary:** the spine's authority stage enforces them, and it runs after `contextAdmission`. So for a write in read-only mode the hook does run. It still cannot allow the write: its allow is recorded as `ignored_allow` and the denial is word for word the same. But a hook that *denies* there replaces the gate's reason with `HOOK_DENIED`. The attachment follows the plan; the tests assert the real behaviour and `docs/HOOKS.md` states it.\n17\t\n18\t## What a release note must say\n19\t\n20\t- Hooks are unsandboxed programs running with the operator's rights.\n21\t- An invalid `~/.config/nexus/hooks.json` denies every tool call until it is fixed.\n22\t- A non-zero exit other than 2 denies (stricter than the Claude Code convention the payload shape follows).\n23\t- The approval prompt comes before hooks.\n24\t- `serve-mcp` runs no hooks.\n25\t- Project hooks are not a control over the agent: the agent can edit the file, which stops them until the operator approves the new content.\n26\t\n27\t## Tests\n28\t\n29\tThirteen new test files, 101 tests: `strict_json` 9, `hooks_config` 6, `hook_output_reduce` 13, `hook_runner` 8, `content_trust` 7, `hooks_schema` 5, `hooks_gate_bypass` 11, `hooks_deny` 9, `hooks_post_tool` 5, `hooks_project_trust` 9, `hooks_cli` 8, `hooks_examples` 6, `doctor_hooks` 5. Each passed three runs in a row. For each guard a mutation was shown to fail a test (gate order, fail-closed, chain handling, project trust in five ways, environment and redaction, kill and output caps, visibility, the CLI's hash checks); the list is in the implementation report and can be repeated.\n30\t\n31\tAfter merging the release branch (Node 24): the seven hook files rerun pass, `leak_guard` 6/6, `tsc` clean, complexity gate unchanged. Before the merge: the required list of existing files, `context_convergence` 57/57, the three `scripts/check_*.mjs`. `doctor.test.ts` fails the same 11 tests with and without this change (host state).\n32\t\n33\t## Other changes to existing files\n34\t\n35\t`spine.ts` and `flight.ts` (the hook record), `verify_service.ts` (process-identity helpers moved out to `core/process_identity.ts` so hooks and the verify service share them; no behaviour change intended), `index.ts` (2 lines), `doctor.ts` (8 lines), the manual and protocol docs.\n36\t\n37\t## Not in this PR\n38\t\n39\tThe other hook events, HK-2 (commit-pinned plugins) and HK-3 (per-plugin trust). There is no session-start prompt for unapproved project hooks, only a notice at the first tool call.\n40\t\n41\t## Reference coding\n42\t\n43\t`HK_PLAN.md` records the peer comparison (payload and exit-code conventions follow Claude Code's hooks so existing scripts transfer; the \"deny or annotate only, never allow\" rule and fail-closed pre-tool are this repo's own).\n44\t\n45\t🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n46\t\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"user","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"main","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
{"parentUuid":"d28269b0-4417-40b3-b59e-a7c270532bde","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/pr_gv.md","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/pr_gv.md","content":"Finishes GV-1 (slices 3 and 4 of `GV1_PLAN.md`) and GV-5's allowlists. `docs/MANAGED_POLICY.md` marked these \"not yet\" or \"planned\"; it now says what is enforced.\n\n## GV-5: MCP and plugin allowlists\n\n`mcp.allow`, `mcp.disable_workspace`, `plugins.allow` and `plugins.disable_workspace` were accepted by the schema and enforced nothing.\n\n- **MCP** (`cli/src/mcp.ts`): every server is checked before it starts, on all three paths (`loadAndConnect`, `addServer`, `addConnection`). A refused `/mcp add` saves nothing.\n- **Plugins** (`cli/src/plugins.ts`): the real path and SHA-256 are checked before `import()`.\n- **`disable_workspace`** ignores a definition that belongs to the workspace by path or by symlink target.\n- A refusal names the policy source, is printed once on stderr and is available to callers. An unreadable policy admits nothing.\n\n## GV-1 slice 3\n\n- Under `approval.disable_auto` or `strict`, an \"always\" answer approves that one call and is not remembered (`cli/src/sidecar.ts`). No change to the Rust TUI: the enforcement is on the sidecar side.\n- The line-mode REPL had the same gap and the documentation said it did not: `/mode auto` and \"always\" set the REPL's own copy of the mode, and it stopped asking. Fixed (`cli/src/repl.ts`); `/mode auto` now answers with the refusal and its source.\n- `nexus verify` refuses `--yes`, `--sandbox none` and `--sandbox-network` when policy forbids them, exit 2.\n\n## GV-1 slice 4\n\n- `nexus policy show` and `nexus policy check [file]`, both with `--json`; exit 2 on an invalid policy. They run even when the installed policy is broken, which is when they are needed.\n- `nexus doctor`: findings `policy.system`, `policy.user`, `policy.project`, `policy.effective`. `doctor --fix` skips any `policy.toml`.\n\n## Behaviour changes for the release notes\n\n- A server or plugin outside the allowlists no longer starts or loads.\n- \"Always\" and `/mode auto` are refused under `approval.disable_auto` or `strict`, in the TUI and the REPL.\n- `nexus verify` refuses the three flags above under policy.\n- When the workspace is the home directory, `disable_workspace` also switches off the user's own MCP configuration and plugins, because they are then workspace files.\n\n## Decisions and limits\n\n- `nexus policy approve` is not implemented: it would be a second approval path that a model could run. `nexus trust` stays the only one.\n- A bare or unnormalised command never matches a `command:` allowlist entry; WebSocket servers match by name only.\n- A plugin is hashed and then imported by path, so a replacement between the two is not detected (documented).\n- Left \"not yet\": `egress.secret_destinations` (not in slices 3–4), and the sandbox consulting `sandbox.forbid_network` itself (slice 5 in the plan; the document says so).\n\n## Tests\n\nNew: `managed_policy_allowlists` (18, with the hostile cases: a workspace policy adding to an allowlist, name and case tricks, a symlinked workspace configuration, empty versus absent allowlist), `policy_cli` (23), `managed_policy_always` (6), `managed_policy_verify` (12). Updated to the new state: `managed_policy_enforcement`, `managed_policy_schema`.\n\nLocal, Node 24, after merging the release branch: the four new files pass, `leak_guard` 6/6, `tsc` clean, `check_invariants`, `check_requirements`, `check_doc_versions` and the complexity gate pass. Before the merge: the eight existing managed-policy files (465 tests), `approval_policy` 16/16, `mcp` 4/4, `mcp_verify` 7/7, `verify_command` 18/18, `verify_sandbox` 10/10, `check_requirements` 28/28, `release_workflow_parity` 6/6, `lsp_shape` 8/8.\n\n**Not clean locally, and why:** the host was at a load average of 10 to 20 from parallel work. `sidecar.test.ts` had 8 failures of 65, all 10-second waits and timing assertions; the approval tests among them pass when rerun alone, and one of the eight fails on the base branch too; two were not rerun. `context_convergence` was cut off after 15 minutes with 6 tests passed and none failed. `doctor.test.ts` fails the same 11 tests as the base branch. CI is the arbiter for these three.\n\nNo model-facing tool description changed.\n\n## Reference coding\n\nXERJ was not queried for this change. The design follows `GV1_PLAN.md`, whose reference-coding section covers the unit.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n","numLines":52,"startLine":1,"totalLines":52}},"displayPath":"../../../tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/pr_gv.md","savedCopyFraming":{"enveloped":false}},"type":"attachment","uuid":"d1afde5f-d19c-47f2-9d59-03c2dae20f12","timestamp":"2026-11-24T15:06:17.307Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/pr_gv.md\"}\n</system-reminder>"},{"content":"<system-reminder>\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\tFinishes GV-1 (slices 3 and 4 of `GV1_PLAN.md`) and GV-5's allowlists. `docs/MANAGED_POLICY.md` marked these \"not yet\" or \"planned\"; it now says what is enforced.\n2\t\n3\t## GV-5: MCP and plugin allowlists\n4\t\n5\t`mcp.allow`, `mcp.disable_workspace`, `plugins.allow` and `plugins.disable_workspace` were accepted by the schema and enforced nothing.\n6\t\n7\t- **MCP** (`cli/src/mcp.ts`): every server is checked before it starts, on all three paths (`loadAndConnect`, `addServer`, `addConnection`). A refused `/mcp add` saves nothing.\n8\t- **Plugins** (`cli/src/plugins.ts`): the real path and SHA-256 are checked before `import()`.\n9\t- **`disable_workspace`** ignores a definition that belongs to the workspace by path or by symlink target.\n10\t- A refusal names the policy source, is printed once on stderr and is available to callers. An unreadable policy admits nothing.\n11\t\n12\t## GV-1 slice 3\n13\t\n14\t- Under `approval.disable_auto` or `strict`, an \"always\" answer approves that one call and is not remembered (`cli/src/sidecar.ts`). No change to the Rust TUI: the enforcement is on the sidecar side.\n15\t- The line-mode REPL had the same gap and the documentation said it did not: `/mode auto` and \"always\" set the REPL's own copy of the mode, and it stopped asking. Fixed (`cli/src/repl.ts`); `/mode auto` now answers with the refusal and its source.\n16\t- `nexus verify` refuses `--yes`, `--sandbox none` and `--sandbox-network` when policy forbids them, exit 2.\n17\t\n18\t## GV-1 slice 4\n19\t\n20\t- `nexus policy show` and `nexus policy check [file]`, both with `--json`; exit 2 on an invalid policy. They run even when the installed policy is broken, which is when they are needed.\n21\t- `nexus doctor`: findings `policy.system`, `policy.user`, `policy.project`, `policy.effective`. `doctor --fix` skips any `policy.toml`.\n22\t\n23\t## Behaviour changes for the release notes\n24\t\n25\t- A server or plugin outside the allowlists no longer starts or loads.\n26\t- \"Always\" and `/mode auto` are refused under `approval.disable_auto` or `strict`, in the TUI and the REPL.\n27\t- `nexus verify` refuses the three flags above under policy.\n28\t- When the workspace is the home directory, `disable_workspace` also switches off the user's own MCP configuration and plugins, because they are then workspace files.\n29\t\n30\t## Decisions and limits\n31\t\n32\t- `nexus policy approve` is not implemented: it would be a second approval path that a model could run. `nexus trust` stays the only one.\n33\t- A bare or unnormalised command never matches a `command:` allowlist entry; WebSocket servers match by name only.\n34\t- A plugin is hashed and then imported by path, so a replacement between the two is not detected (documented).\n35\t- Left \"not yet\": `egress.secret_destinations` (not in slices 3–4), and the sandbox consulting `sandbox.forbid_network` itself (slice 5 in the plan; the document says so).\n36\t\n37\t## Tests\n38\t\n39\tNew: `managed_policy_allowlists` (18, with the hostile cases: a workspace policy adding to an allowlist, name and case tricks, a symlinked workspace configuration, empty versus absent allowlist), `policy_cli` (23), `managed_policy_always` (6), `managed_policy_verify` (12). Updated to the new state: `managed_policy_enforcement`, `managed_policy_schema`.\n40\t\n41\tLocal, Node 24, after merging the release branch: the four new files pass, `leak_guard` 6/6, `tsc` clean, `check_invariants`, `check_requirements`, `check_doc_versions` and the complexity gate pass. Before the merge: the eight existing managed-policy files (465 tests), `approval_policy` 16/16, `mcp` 4/4, `mcp_verify` 7/7, `verify_command` 18/18, `verify_sandbox` 10/10, `check_requirements` 28/28, `release_workflow_parity` 6/6, `lsp_shape` 8/8.\n42\t\n43\t**Not clean locally, and why:** the host was at a load average of 10 to 20 from parallel work. `sidecar.test.ts` had 8 failures of 65, all 10-second waits and timing assertions; the approval tests among them pass when rerun alone, and one of the eight fails on the base branch too; two were not rerun. `context_convergence` was cut off after 15 minutes with 6 tests passed and none failed. `doctor.test.ts` fails the same 11 tests as the base branch. CI is the arbiter for these three.\n44\t\n45\tNo model-facing tool description changed.\n46\t\n47\t## Reference coding\n48\t\n49\tXERJ was not queried for this change. The design follows `GV1_PLAN.md`, whose reference-coding section covers the unit.\n50\t\n51\t🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n52\t\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"user","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"main","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
