Adversarial Security Probe Launched for repositoryConfiguresPrograms() Guard\\nS2914 Complete all remaining unbuilt/unfinished v1.3.0 units then execute merge to main and release (Nov 24, 8:54 AM)\\n42589 8:55a ⚖ Owner Directive: Build All Remaining v1.3.0 Units and Execute Release\\n42590 \\\" ○ Release Queue State at Build Directive Start — PR #774 Open, Six Plans Exist\\n42591 8:56a ◆ Three Work Claims Filed and Two Worktrees Created for Remaining v1.3.0 Units\\n42593 8:57a ◆ VR-2 Follow-Up Subagent Launched — Six Security Hardening Items for ACP Verify\\n42599 10:01a ○ Release Queue State at ~10:00Z — PRs #776 and #777 Merged, Five Units Still Claimed by Same Agent\\n42669 10:23a ○ PR #774 New Head 02e1d755 — Schema Refresh Commits Pushed, CI Partially Pending\\n42679 10:27a ○ PR #774 Head 02e1d755 — turn_deadline_abort Has 2 Failures, All Other Tests Pass\\n42683 10:28a ○ turn_deadline_abort Tests Failing Under High Load — Not a Code Regression\\n42686 10:29a ✓ PR #774 Merged — PA-2 Turn Deadline / Budget Schema Lands in release/v1.3.0\\n42688 10:30a ◆ GV-1 (slices 3-4) and GV-5 Policy Enforcement Committed to gv1c Worktree\\n42696 10:33a ◆ GV-1 Slices 3-4 Branch Passes All Gates and Pushed to Origin\\n42697 \\\" ✓ GV-1 Slices 3-4 + GV-5 PR Description Drafted\\n42698 \\\" ◆ PR #778 Opened — GV-1 Slices 3-4 and GV-5 Policy Enforcement\\n42702 10:34a ◆ PR #778 Security Review Dispatched — 9-Vector Adversarial Probe of GV-1 Policy Enforcement\\nS2915 Goal check-in: background work still running — BG-1 job status schema and PF-4 pre-commit status at ~10:48Z (Nov 24, 10:34 AM)\\n42733 10:42a ○ Build Worktree Status at 10:42Z — HK-1 Ahead, SB-1/PF-4 Still Uncommitted\\n42742 2:41p ○ Release Queue State at 14:41Z — PR #781 Merged, Two PRs Open, SB-1 Claim Handed Off\\n42743 \\\" ⚖ Post-Pause Work Division Logged — Claude Resumes HK-1/PA-2, Defers BG-1/PF-4/SB-1 to Codex\\n42744 2:42p ◆ HK-1 Hooks Library Branch Passes All Gates — 56 Tests Green, Pushed to Origin\\n42745 2:43p ◆ HK-1 PR Description Written — Command Hooks Implementation Summary and Release Note Requirements\\n42746 \\\" ✓ PR #782 Opened — HK-1 Pre-Tool and Post-Tool Command Hooks\\n42747 \\\" ✓ PR #782 Security Review Dispatched — 9-Section Adversarial Probe of HK-1 Hooks\\n42748 \\\" ✓ PR #778 Review Agent Resumed — Findings Now Become Follow-Ups Against release/v1.3.0\\n42752 2:44p ○ Codex PR #779 (PF-4 Lib API) Passes CI — PR #780 (BG-1 Job Schema) Fails test-matrix\\n42758 \\\" ◆ PR #779 (PF-4) Security Review Dispatched — 9-Section Adversarial Probe of Sidecar Embedding API\\n42768 2:46p ◆ Name-Only Allowlist Entry Blocked for Workspace-Defined MCP Servers\\n42769 \\\" ● withoutFileText() Refined to Preserve Policy Key Tokens in Error Messages\\n42770 \\\" ◆ Test Added for Name-Only mcp.allow Entry Blocking Workspace-Configured Servers\\n42773 2:47p ✓ MANAGED_POLICY.md Expanded With Name-Entry Limits and What Entries Do Not Pin\\n42777 2:48p ◆ PF-4 Policy CLI — Credential-Leak and Guard-Removal Tests Added and Validated\\n42783 2:49p ◆ PR #783 Opened — PF-4 Policy Follow-Ups: Name-Only MCP Allow Fix and Policy Check Echo Fix\\nS2916 PA-2 verified-merge build started; SB-1 subagent stopped; parallel reviews of #782/#779/#783 running (Nov 24, 2:51 PM)\\n42795 2:53p ● withoutFileText() Refined — Quotes Processed in Order, Policy Key Names Exempted\\n42796 \\\" ○ withoutFileText() Truncation Behavior Verified Across Five Adversarial Cases\\n42802 2:54p ● withoutFileText() MESSAGE_EXAMPLES Allowlist Prevents Truncation of Policy Literals\\n42803 2:55p ● PR #783 PF-4 Error-Text Cut Fix Committed and Pushed — Head dd42ea30\\n42804 2:56p ⚠ PR #782 HK-1 Hooks — Three Blocking Security Vulnerabilities Found at 034c278c\\n42805 \\\" ⚠ PR #782 Do-Not-Merge Block Logged — extension_trust.json and hooks.json Missing from DEFAULT_PROTECTED_PATHS\\n42808 \\\" ⚖ HK-1 Three Security Blockers Assigned for Fix\"},\"systemMessage\":\"View Observations Live @ http://localhost:37