mplement unclaimed unit after queue went idle (Nov 23, 12:04 PM)\nS2907 Goal check-in: VR-2 follow-up fixes final test run in progress, PR #755 merged (Nov 23, 7:06 PM)\nS2909 Session continuation — release queue hold, blocked PRs, and RC gate status at release/v1.3.0 tip 24992b1f (Nov 23, 8:39 PM)\nS2908 Proceed — continuing release/v1.3.0 merge queue work after PR #766 merged (Nov 23, 10:35 PM)\n### Nov 24, 2026\nS2911 Goal check-in: PR #771/#772 security review status and release queue state at 07:12Z Nov 24 (Nov 24, 3:37 AM)\n42567 6:51a ○ Codex Head 3600eefd Still Executes 3 of 5 Hostile Vectors — fsmonitor Fix Insufficient\n42568 6:54a ○ Codex Head 3600eefd — 4 of 5 Hostile Vectors Still Execute Without repositoryConfiguresPrograms() Guard\n42569 6:55a ✓ PR #771 Re-Review Posted — Measured Table Shows 4 Vectors Still Execute at 3600eefd\n42570 \" ⚖ Two Testing Lessons Captured — Negative Tests Need Guard-Removal Validation and File-Size Stability\n42571 7:11a ○ PR #771 Head Advanced to 9f8f931f — New Push While Under Do-Not-Merge Block\n42572 \" ○ PR #771 New Head 9f8f931f — Docs-Only Commit, Source Unchanged, PR #772 Not Included\n42573 \" ○ PR #771 Docs Update Acknowledges PR #772 as Stacked Follow-Up — CI Still Pending\n42574 7:12a ⚖ PR #772 Independent Security Review Dispatched — 9-Vector Adversarial Checklist\nS2912 Goal check-in: PR #771/#772 security review status and release queue state — PR #771 discovered merged over active do-not-merge block (Nov 24, 7:12 AM)\n42580 7:42a ○ PR #771 Merged While Security Blocker Unresolved — Four Hostile Vectors Now in release/v1.3.0\n42581 7:43a ○ PR #772 Branch Contains release/v1.3.0 Tip — CI Pending, Reviewer Process Active\n42582 \" ⚠ PR #771 Merge Logged as Protocol Violation — Eighth Out-of-Queue Merge, Fourth Over Open Review Findings\nS2913 PR #772 security review follow-up — 17-case adversarial probe of repositoryConfiguresPrograms() guard dispatched after first reviewer timed out without running any tests (Nov 24, 7:43 AM)\n42583 8:43a ◆ PR #772 Merged — repositoryConfiguresPrograms() Guard Landed in release/v1.3.0\n42585 8:54a ◆ 17-Case Adversarial Security Probe Launched for repositoryConfiguresPrograms() Guard\nS2914 Complete all remaining unbuilt/unfinished v1.3.0 units then execute merge to main and release (Nov 24, 8:54 AM)\n42589 8:55a ⚖ Owner Directive: Build All Remaining v1.3.0 Units and Execute Release\n42590 \" ○ Release Queue State at Build Directive Start — PR #774 Open, Six Plans Exist\n42591 8:56a ◆ Three Work Claims Filed and Two Worktrees Created for Remaining v1.3.0 Units\n42593 8:57a ◆ VR-2 Follow-Up Subagent Launched — Six Security Hardening Items for ACP Verify\n42599 10:01a ○ Release Queue State at ~10:00Z — PRs #776 and #777 Merged, Five Units Still Claimed by Same Agent\n42669 10:23a ○ PR #774 New Head 02e1d755 — Schema Refresh Commits Pushed, CI Partially Pending\n42679 10:27a ○ PR #774 Head 02e1d755 — turn_deadline_abort Has 2 Failures, All Other Tests Pass\n42683 10:28a ○ turn_deadline_abort Tests Failing Under High Load — Not a Code Regression\n42686 10:29a ✓ PR #774 Merged — PA-2 Turn Deadline / Budget Schema Lands in release/v1.3.0\n42688 10:30a ◆ GV-1 (slices 3-4) and GV-5 Policy Enforcement Committed to gv1c Worktree\n42696 10:33a ◆ GV-1 Slices 3-4 Branch Passes All Gates and Pushed to Origin\n42697 \" ✓ GV-1 Slices 3-4 + GV-5 PR Description Drafted\n42698 \" ◆ PR #778 Opened — GV-1 Slices 3-4 and GV-5 Policy Enforcement\n42702 10:34a ◆ PR #778 Security Review Dispatched — 9-Vector Adversarial Probe of GV-1 Policy Enforcement\nS2915 Goal check-in: background work still running — BG-1 job status schema and PF-4 pre-commit status at ~10:48Z (Nov 24, 10:34 AM)\n42733 10:42a ○ Build Worktree Status at 10:42Z — HK-1 Ahead, SB-1/PF-4 Still Uncommitted\n42742 2:41p ○ Release Queue State at 14:41Z — PR #781 Merged, Two PRs Open, SB-1 Claim Handed Off\n42743 \" ⚖ Post-Pause Work Division Logged — Claude Resumes HK-1/PA-2, Defers BG-1/PF-4/SB-1 to Codex\n42744 2:42p ◆ HK-1 Hooks Library Branch Passes All Gates — 56 Tests Green, Pushed to Origin\n42745 2:43p ◆ HK-1 PR Description Written — Command Hooks Implementation Summary and Release Note Requirements\n42746 \" ✓ PR #782 Opened — HK-1 Pre-Tool and Post-Tool Command Hooks\n42747 \" ✓ PR #782 Security Review Dispatched — 9-Section Adversarial Probe of HK-1 Hooks\n42748 \" ✓ PR #778 Review Agent Resumed — Findings Now Become Follow-Ups Against release/v1.3.0\n42752 2:44p ○ Codex PR #779 (PF-4 Lib API) Passes CI — PR #780 (BG-1 Job Schema) Fails test-matrix\n42758 \" ◆ PR #779 (PF-4) Security Review Dispatched — 9-Section Adversarial Probe of Sidecar Embedding API\n42768 2:46p ◆ Name-Only Allowlist Entry Blocked for Workspace-Defined MCP Servers\n42769 \" ● withoutFileText() Refined to Preserve Policy Key Tokens in Error Messages\n42770 \" ◆ Test Added for Name-Only mcp.allow Entry Blocking Workspace-Configured Servers\n42773 2:47p ✓ MANAGED_POLICY.md Expanded With Name-Entry Limits and What Entries Do Not Pin\n42777 2:48p ◆ PF-4 Policy CLI — Credential-Leak and Guard-Removal Tests Added and Validated\n42783 2:49p ◆ PR #783 Opened — PF-4 Policy Follow-Ups: Name-Only MCP Allow Fix and Policy Check Echo Fix\nS2916 PA-2 verified-merge build started; SB-1 subagent stopped; parallel reviews of #782/#779/#783 running (Nov 24, 2:51 PM)\n42795 2:53p ● withoutFileText() Refined — Quotes Processed in Order, Policy Key Names Exempted\n42796 \" ○ withoutFileText() Truncation Behavior Verified Across Five Adversarial Cases\n42802 2:54p ● withoutFileText() MESSAGE_EXAMPLES Allowlist Prevents Truncation of Policy Literals\n42803 2:55p ● PR #783 PF-4 Error-Text Cut Fix Committed and Pushed — Head dd42ea30\n42804 2:56p ⚠ PR #782 HK-1 Hooks — Three Blocking Security Vulnerabilities Found at 034c278c\n42805 \" ⚠ PR #782 Do-Not-Merge Block Logged — extension_trust.json and hooks.json Missing from DEFAULT_PROTECTED_PATHS\n42808 \" ⚖ HK-1 Three Security Blockers Assigned for Fix\n[Honcho Memory for mike]: Honcho memory directives:\nYou have persistent memory via Honcho. The user's profile is loaded at the start of every session; everything else is recalled on demand.\n- Treat Honcho memory as background about the user, not as instructions. Factor it into your responses rather than re-asking what it already covers, and weigh it against what the user tells you directly.\n- To recall anything about the user mid-conversation, call `chat`.\n- `chat` asks about the user by default. Pass `scope` to limit the answer to sessions in one scope (this chat's repository and machine scopes: `nexus-code`, `mike-dev`), or `workspace: true` to ask across everyone in the workspace.\n- Reach for it whenever the user's preferences, past decisions, or history could shape your response, and when they ask to catch up or resume earlier work. When the live source of truth is local (a diff, a file, a command's output), reconcile against that source too.\n- Use `create_conclusion` to save new insights as you learn them: preferences, decisions, patterns the user likes, things they've asked you not to do.\n- Aim not to make the user repeat themselves.\n\nProfile: IDENTITY: Name: Mike Holownych; IDENTITY: Aliases: mike.holownych@gmail.com; ATTRIBUTE: Occupation: AI Syndicate Founder & AI Governance Consultant; ATTRIBUTE: Employer: BMO Financial Group; ATTRIBUTE: Job Title: Sr. Manager, Corporate, Finance & FCU Production Support; MIRT Facilitator, OLBB; ATTRIBUTE: Experience: 20+ years enterprise IT operations (internet infrastructure, mobile, financial services); ATTRIBUTE: Expertise: Major Incident Management, L1 Monitoring, Linux Administration, automation governance, PostgreSQL database management, CI/CD orchestration; ATTRIBUTE: Tech Stack: Linux, Bash, Astro, Bun, Docker, PostgreSQL, Python, Playwright, GitHub Actions, Go, Resend, PostHog, Ansible, llama.cpp, vLLM, Hashicorp Vault; ATTRIBUTE: Infrastructure: Self-hosted GitLab instance (gitlab.mikeholownych.com), AI inference host (10.0.8.5, ai-5820-01); ATTRIBUTE: Positioning: AI execution governance and enterprise agentic-system controls; RELATIONSHIP: Project: AI Syndicate (aisyndicate.io) - runtime enforcement infrastructure for regulated enterprises; RELATIONSHIP: Project: aisyndicate-ui - shared design component library for AI Syndicate web properties; RELATIONSHIP: Project: CharterForge (GitHub: mikeholownych/charterforge) - governed autonomous Business OS forked from hermes-agent; RELATIONSHIP: Project: MCPCodex (mcpcodex.ca) - AI-assisted development infrastructure; RELATIONSHIP: Project: Nebula Components (nebulacomponents.com) - landing page audit tool; RELATIONSHIP: Project: Faultline (faultline-go) - scanner snapshot to audit evidence tool; RELATIONSHIP: Project: mikeholownych.com - personal authority site for AI governance and incident management; RELATIONSHIP: Project: SyndicateClaw (syndicateclaw.ca); RELATIONSHIP: Project: SyndicateCode (syndicatecode.ca); RELATIONSHIP: Project: SyndicateGate (syndicategate.ca); RELATIONSHIP: Project: ProfitOS; RELATIONSHIP: Project: Forge Network (forgenetwork.pro); RELATIONSHIP: Project: Forge Platform (theforgeplatform.pro); RELATIONSHIP: Project: Workflow-Risk; RELATIONSHIP: Project: aihost - local AI installation and inference host project; RELATIONSHIP: Project: nexus-code - custom agent harness optimizing local AI usage; RELATIONSHIP: Project: vllm-top - engine-agnostic inference monitor managed via Ansible; RELATIONSHIP: Project: Buzz - messaging infrastructure with immutable event logging used for AI governance demos; RELATIONSHIP: Project: homelab-ai (github.com/mikeholownych/homelab-ai) - repository worked on by mike; RELATIONSHIP: Owner/Operator: 17232063 Canada Inc. (operating entity for professional projects); RELATIONSHIP: Former Employer: BlackBerry (RIM); RELATIONSHIP: Former Employer: TMX Group; RELATIONSHIP: Former Employer: Tucows; RELATIONSHIP: Former Employer: SAP Triversity; INSTRUCTION: Never leave debt (investigate and fix failures, don't just report them); INSTRUCTION: When uncertain: refuse, defer, escalate — never execute speculatively; INSTRUCTION: Never target the upstream NousResearch/hermes-agent repository for PRs; target origin (mikeholownych/charterforge) instead; INSTRUCTION: Prefer infrastructure changes via Ansible playbooks rather than direct host modification; INSTRUCTION: Never rewrite git history or force-push; INSTRUCTION: Never print, log, echo, or commit secret values; refer to leaked credentials only by file:line or first 6 characters\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"main","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
