780, Codex, red), PF-4 (#779, Codex), SB-1 slices 2–3 (Codex) — review and merge via queue.\n   - Post review of #779 when its reviewer reports; review #780 when green.\n   - #778 follow-up PR from `~/nexus-wt/polfu` (branch `v1/policy-followups`): bare-name allow must not match workspace definitions; truncate tokens in `policy check` errors; settle/document `NEXUS_SANDBOX_NETWORK` vs `nexus verify`; docs for hard-link and sha256 limits.\n   - Release the stale `GV1_SLICES_3_4_GV5` claim; update `docs/releases/v1.3.0-READINESS.md` and CHANGELOG as units land.\n   - When all listed items are complete and gates G-1..G-7 can be evaluated: version bump + changelog + release notes (G-7 framing), single merge of `release/v1.3.0` to `main` via merge-commit PR, RC tag, measurement, stable (version-only commit, tag) per `docs/RELEASE_PROCESS.md`.\n   - Dispatch `lsp-real-servers.yml` and `real-project-smoke.yml` on the release tip after significant merges.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   Just resumed after the 11:00–14:40Z usage pause (2026-11-24). Release tip `83413dc8`, CI green. I logged an ACK that Codex now owns BG-1/PF-4/SB-1; merged release into `v1/hk1-hooks-lib`, pushed (`034c278c`), opened **#782** (HK-1) and launched its reviewer (agent `a113015cb5d57f7c1`); launched reviewer for **#779** (agent `a51e8a083eab51d80`) and the **PA-2 implementer** (agent `a2b26453fbd1df4f6`, worktree `~/nexus-wt/pa2`, commits locally per slice, no push); resumed and received the #778 review (ACCEPT WITH FOLLOW-UPS) and posted it on the PR; logged the #780/#782 file overlap for Codex. I then created `~/nexus-wt/polfu` (branch `v1/policy-followups` from `origin/release/v1.3.0`, node_modules symlink and Rust binaries in place) and was reading code for the three #778 follow-ups; the last command traced `sandboxNetworkEnabled()` uses in `cli/src/sandbox.ts` (lines 720 and 892: env is consulted only when `options.network` is neither `true` nor `false`). No edits have been made in `polfu` yet.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Continue the #778 follow-up in `~/nexus-wt/polfu` (stated on the PR: \"I am opening a follow-up for the first\"): change `permitsMcpServer` so a bare-name `mcp.allow` entry does not match a server with `fromWorkspace: true` (with a refusal message pointing to `command:`/`url:` entries), cap echoed tokens in `checkPolicyFile` errors, confirm whether `nexus verify` ever passes `network: undefined` (index.ts ~720–726) and document or clamp, update `docs/MANAGED_POLICY.md`, add tests to `managed_policy_allowlists.test.ts`/`policy_cli.test.ts`, run them plus `tsc` and gates, push, open the PR, get an independent review, merge when green. In parallel, act on the notifications from the #782 reviewer, the #779 reviewer and the PA-2 implementer as they arrive (post reviews; push PA-2 and open its PR), keeping to the owner directive: \"Required: completion of Unbuilt and Unfinished items as listed above. Once that has been satisfied, the merge to main and release process is yours to complete.\"\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /home/mike/.claude/projects/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\n\nThe messages after this summary are the most recent messages from before compaction, kept verbatim. The summary was written without seeing them, so something it says has not happened yet may already have happened in them."}]}}
