{"parentUuid":"6baefa29-1b9a-4af9-b41c-6891dc199186","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011ChMxgGwqNkqGoeGCQSGSm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019D4UtWReAoNFvbA5Xhe2hN","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"MT-2 slice 1 characterization tests","subagent_type":"general-purpose","prompt":"Implement MT-2 slice 1 (characterization tests ONLY, no source changes) in the worktree /home/mike/nexus-wt/mt2 (branch `v1/mt2-characterization`, based on `origin/release/v1.3.0`; repo is the Nexus Code TypeScript CLI in `cli/`). Read first: `/home/mike/nexus-wt/_plans/PF_SB_MT_PA_PLAN.md` (the MT-2 section: it defines the slices; you do slice 1 only), `/home/mike/nexus-wt/mt2/AGENTS.md`, `docs/v1.3.0/PLAN.md` (the MT-2 unit), then the code the later slices will rewrite: `cli/src/core/dispatch_tool_call.ts`, the tool definitions and dispatch in `cli/src/agent.ts` / `cli/src/tools.ts`, `cli/src/core/spine_handlers.ts`, and `cli/critical-complexity-baseline.json`.\n\nGoal: pin today's behaviour so that the later registry refactor and the split of `dispatchToolCallImpl` can be proven behaviour-preserving. Tests must pass on the unmodified source. Cover, as the plan lists (follow the plan where it differs from this summary):\n1. What the model sees: the exact list of tool definitions (names, order, descriptions, JSON schemas) sent to the model for each relevant configuration (default, read-only mode, subagent, with/without MCP tools, LSP on/off, any feature flags that add or remove tools) as a golden snapshot, byte-exact, with a generator/`--check` style or an inline fixture following whatever convention the repo already uses for golden files (look at how `cli/test/fixtures/` and the protocol schema samples are regenerated).\n2. Dispatch: for every built-in tool name, an unknown tool name, malformed arguments, and an MCP tool, the sequence of gates/stages a call passes through and the shape of the result/receipt (which gate denies, the error codes, the order of approval vs. policy vs. hooks-free spine stages), using the existing test helpers for a scripted model/agent (find them under `cli/test/helpers/`; see `approval_policy.test.ts`, `mcp_tool_through_spine.test.ts`, `sandbox_denial_events.test.ts` for patterns).\n3. A table-driven test that every tool the model can be offered has a dispatch route and every dispatch route corresponds to an offered tool (no orphan either way), written so it will keep working once a registry exists.\n\nRules: do not edit any file under `cli/src` or `core/`; if you believe a source change is needed, stop and report it instead. Every new test file starts with `import \"./helpers/leak_guard.js\";`. Run a single test file with `cd /home/mike/nexus-wt/mt2/cli && TMPDIR=/dev/shm HOME=$(mktemp -d) node --import tsx --test test/<name>.test.ts 2>&1 | tail -30` (a throwaway HOME is mandatory; never read the real ~/.nexus, ~/.config/nexus, /etc/nexus). No network, no inference runs. Stop any process only by its own pid, never `pkill -f`. Shell is zsh: use `bash -c` for loops; shell output passes through `rtk` which can filter it — prefix with `rtk proxy` if output looks cut. `cli/node_modules` is a symlink and the Rust binaries are already in `core/target/release/`. The host is loaded by other agents; timing-sensitive existing tests may flake — do not chase those. Verify each new test actually pins something: for at least three representative assertions, temporarily mutate the source (copy the file aside first and restore it from the copy; never `git checkout` to undo) and confirm the test fails for the right reason, then restore and confirm `git status` shows only your new test/fixture files. Run each new file three times; run `npx tsc --noEmit -p .` in `cli/`; run `leak_guard.test.ts`. Check `git log origin/release/v1.3.0..HEAD` for foreign commits, then commit locally (do NOT push, do not open a PR) with message `test(tools): characterize the model-facing tool list and dispatch routes (MT-2 slice 1)` ending with the line `Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>`.\n\nReport under 400 words: files added with test counts; the configurations snapshotted; the mutations and which test caught each; anything in today's behaviour that looks like a defect or an inconsistency the refactor must decide about (do not fix it; pin it and flag it); what the plan asked for that you did not cover and why; commit hash."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":103616,"cache_read_input_tokens":32782,"output_tokens":2075,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":104},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":103616,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2075,"cache_read_input_tokens":32782,"cache_creation_input_tokens":103616,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":103616},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.2.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"},{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.5.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"},{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.8.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"},{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.8.content.1","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"},{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.21.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"},{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.30.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"},{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.37.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"},{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.42.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mism