{"parentUuid":"67aea54f-ef72-48fb-a114-d2ab963d0e7d","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"c3e4ded3-5447-4b5c-9048-d207d606abe7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019D4UtWReAoNFvbA5Xhe2hN","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Async agent launched successfully. (This tool result is internal metadata — never quote or paste any part of it, including the agentId below, into a user-facing reply.)\nagentId: a6eab58ec58e56906 (internal ID - do not mention to user. Use SendMessage with to: 'a6eab58ec58e56906', summary: '<5-10 word recap>' to continue this agent.)\nThe agent is working in the background. You will be notified automatically when it completes. You know nothing about its results until that notification arrives — do not report, assume, or predict them; continue other work or respond to the user in the meantime.\nDo not duplicate this agent's work — avoid working with the same files or topics it is using.\noutput_file: /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666/tasks/a6eab58ec58e56906.output\nDo NOT Read or tail this file via the shell tool — it is the full subagent JSONL transcript and reading it will overflow your context. If the user asks for progress, say the agent is still running; you'll get a completion notification."}]}]},"uuid":"f968f19c-65ed-412a-b769-34331296cba4","timestamp":"2026-11-24T15:06:43.618Z","toolUseResult":{"isAsync":true,"status":"async_launched","agentId":"a6eab58ec58e56906","description":"MT-2 slice 1 characterization tests","resolvedModel":"claude-fable-5-2","prompt":"Implement MT-2 slice 1 (characterization tests ONLY, no source changes) in the worktree /home/mike/nexus-wt/mt2 (branch `v1/mt2-characterization`, based on `origin/release/v1.3.0`; repo is the Nexus Code TypeScript CLI in `cli/`). Read first: `/home/mike/nexus-wt/_plans/PF_SB_MT_PA_PLAN.md` (the MT-2 section: it defines the slices; you do slice 1 only), `/home/mike/nexus-wt/mt2/AGENTS.md`, `docs/v1.3.0/PLAN.md` (the MT-2 unit), then the code the later slices will rewrite: `cli/src/core/dispatch_tool_call.ts`, the tool definitions and dispatch in `cli/src/agent.ts` / `cli/src/tools.ts`, `cli/src/core/spine_handlers.ts`, and `cli/critical-complexity-baseline.json`.\n\nGoal: pin today's behaviour so that the later registry refactor and the split of `dispatchToolCallImpl` can be proven behaviour-preserving. Tests must pass on the unmodified source. Cover, as the plan lists (follow the plan where it differs from this summary):\n1. What the model sees: the exact list of tool definitions (names, order, descriptions, JSON schemas) sent to the model for each relevant configuration (default, read-only mode, subagent, with/without MCP tools, LSP on/off, any feature flags that add or remove tools) as a golden snapshot, byte-exact, with a generator/`--check` style or an inline fixture following whatever convention the repo already uses for golden files (look at how `cli/test/fixtures/` and the protocol schema samples are regenerated).\n2. Dispatch: for every built-in tool name, an unknown tool name, malformed arguments, and an MCP tool, the sequence of gates/stages a call passes through and the shape of the result/receipt (which gate denies, the error codes, the order of approval vs. policy vs. hooks-free spine stages), using the existing test helpers for a scripted model/agent (find them under `cli/test/helpers/`; see `approval_policy.test.ts`, `mcp_tool_through_spine.test.ts`, `sandbox_denial_events.test.ts` for patterns).\n3. A table-driven test that every tool the model can be offered has a dispatch route and every dispatch route corresponds to an offered tool (no orphan either way), written so it will keep working once a registry exists.\n\nRules: do not edit any file under `cli/src` or `core/`; if you believe a source change is needed, stop and report it instead. Every new test file starts with `import \"./helpers/leak_guard.js\";`. Run a single test file with `cd /home/mike/nexus-wt/mt2/cli && TMPDIR=/dev/shm HOME=$(mktemp -d) node --import tsx --test test/<name>.test.ts 2>&1 | tail -30` (a throwaway HOME is mandatory; never read the real ~/.nexus, ~/.config/nexus, /etc/nexus). No network, no inference runs. Stop any process only by its own pid, never `pkill -f`. Shell is zsh: use `bash -c` for loops; shell output passes through `rtk` which can filter it — prefix with `rtk proxy` if output looks cut. `cli/node_modules` is a symlink and the Rust binaries are already in `core/target/release/`. The host is loaded by other agents; timing-sensitive existing tests may flake — do not chase those. Verify each new test actually pins something: for at least three representative assertions, temporarily mutate the source (copy the file aside first and restore it from the copy; never `git checkout` to undo) and confirm the test fails for the right reason, then restore and confirm `git status` shows only your new test/fixture files. Run each new file three times; run `npx tsc --noEmit -p .` in `cli/`; run `leak_guard.test.ts`. Check `git log origin/release/v1.3.0..HEAD` for foreign commits, then commit locally (do NOT push, do not open a PR) with message `test(tools): characterize the model-facing tool list and dispatch routes (MT-2 slice 1)` ending with the line `Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>`.\n\nReport under 400 words: files added with test counts; the configurations snapshotted; the mutations and which test caught each; anything in today's behaviour that looks like a defect or an inconsistency the refactor must decide about (do not fix it; pin it and flag it); what the plan asked for that you did not cover and why; commit hash.","outputFile":"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666/tasks/a6eab58ec58e56906.output","canReadOutputFile":true,"canContinueAgent":true},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"67aea54f-ef72-48fb-a114-d2ab963d0e7d","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"main","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
