 An operator file inside the workspace is invalid and every call is denied with guidance. I tried HOME, `~/.config`, `~/.config/nexus`, the parent of HOME, and symlinks to each. The operator hook never ran, and a repo workspace ran it normally.\n\n**Blocker 3, script pinning: partly closed (run).**\n- Overwriting the script through `write_file` stopped the hook, with a notice naming the file, for `[\"./guard.sh\"]`, `[\"bash\",\"./guard.sh\"]` and `[\"node\",\"scripts/guard.js\",\"--flag\"]`.\n- These were also refused or stopped:\n  - a symlink out of the workspace;\n  - a symlink to a changed in-workspace file;\n  - a swapped parent directory;\n  - a script created after approval;\n  - `../x.sh`;\n  - a shell-string command;\n  - a 2 MB script (bounded at 1 MiB).\n- **Blocking: four forms that name a workspace file are not pinned.** After `write_file` replaced the file, the hook ran the new content with no notice and no new approval:\n  - a directory argument (`[\"node\",\"hookdir\"]`);\n  - `[\"sh\",\"-c\",\"./guard.sh x\"]`;\n  - `[\"bash\",\"-c\",\"exec ./guard.sh\"]`;\n  - `[\"node\",\"--require=./pre.js\",…]`.\n- Cause: `coveredProjectFiles` (`core/hooks.ts`, the `for (const arg of args)` loop) pins only arguments that are themselves existing regular files.\n- Fix: refuse as `invalid` any argument that resolves inside the workspace to a directory. Also refuse arguments that contain a `/` path or `=path` naming a workspace file, and refuse `-c` shell strings, unless the file is pinned.\n- `HOOKS.md` 86-93 says \"every argument that is an existing file\" is covered, which implies more than is done.\n- **TOCTOU (read).** `resolve()` hashes the files once per call, and the spawn comes later. The window includes queue time behind another hook (`this.last`, up to its timeout). The script is re-read by the interpreter, not pinned by file descriptor. Reaching it needs a concurrent process, so only an unsandboxed shell can use it. Non-blocking.\n\n**Denial framing: closed (run).** Newlines, quotes, backslashes, control characters, and \"IGNORE PREVIOUS INSTRUCTIONS\" arrive as one JSON-quoted string in the fixed sentence, with no raw newline. A 5,000-character reason is capped to 1,147 characters in total.\n\n**Regression: closed.**\n- An old record without `files` for `./guard.sh` reads as `changed` (asks again). For `/bin/true` it reads as `active`, which is correct. A malformed `files` field makes the store unusable.\n- `gen_hooks_schema.mjs --check` passes.\n\n**Non-blocking.**\n- `projectHooksState` runs on every call and re-hashes up to 32 files of 1 MiB each. Cache it by file stamp.\n- Two mutations survived. Dropping the stdout-TTY check (`hooks_cli.ts` `interactive`) fails no test; add a stdin-only-TTY case. Dropping the \"approved file no longer named\" comparison also fails no test.\n\n**Tests at head: 0 failures.**\n- Hook suites: `hook_output_reduce` 13, `hook_runner` 8, `hooks_cli` 10, `hooks_config` 6, `hooks_deny` 9, `hooks_examples` 6, `hooks_gate_bypass` 11, `hooks_post_tool` 5, `hooks_project_trust` 9, `hooks_schema` 5, `hooks_self_approval` 6.\n- Other suites: `content_trust` 7, `strict_json` 9, `doctor_hooks` 5, `security` 14, `security_gates` 10, `workspace_trust` 5, `managed_policy_enforcement` 113, `approval_policy` 16, `leak_guard` 6, `check_requirements` 28.\n- `tsc`, the complexity gate and `check_invariants` pass.\n\n**Mutations.** Each protected name removed: caught, 1 and 2 failures (all in `hooks_self_approval`). Terminal check off: caught. Pinned-file comparison skipped: caught. Operator file accepted inside the workspace: caught. The two survivors are listed above.\n\n**Not checked.** `--sandbox` masking of the store, `nexus trust`, MCP tools as write routes, hardlinks to the operator file, and Node 22 versus 24.\n\nI removed the worktree and the probe files.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>120483</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>54</tool_uses><duration_ms>572096</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"},"uuid":"f79d781c-5d6c-4609-8bf6-85668d70b501","timestamp":"2026-11-24T15:22:06.366Z","permissionMode":"bypassPermissions","origin":{"kind":"task-notification","producer":"session-task","runId":"0mwuu2wkg-90414680"},"promptSource":"system","turnOrigin":"task_notification","turnPromptId":"19d02b09-5ec8-4b26-9f0e-2223bce93fdb","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":40,"turnIndex":271},"queueSkipAttachments":true,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"main","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
