{"parentUuid":"ca810bab-edda-4177-96ec-a365b535f564","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011ChMyt4g5vu7ppWhCyJ514","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01D4LJ7MK3DMf7upBPWxzeUx","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"a317b41792fa50650","summary":"Close remaining script-pinning gaps in hooks","message":"Re-review of your fix (now at 258f72ff in /home/mike/nexus-wt/hk1, release branch merged in on top of 3f769c90b; start with `git status` and `git log --oneline -4`; same rules; commit locally, do not push; message `fix(hooks): <what>` + the Co-Authored-By line). Blockers 1 and 2 are closed. Blocker 3 is closed only for plain file arguments. Still BLOCKING, each confirmed by running: after approval, the agent replaced a workspace file with `write_file` and the hook ran the new content with no notice, for these project-hook commands:\n - a directory argument: `[\"node\",\"hookdir\"]`\n - `[\"sh\",\"-c\",\"./guard.sh x\"]` and `[\"bash\",\"-c\",\"exec ./guard.sh\"]`\n - `[\"node\",\"--require=./pre.js\", ...]`\nCause: `coveredProjectFiles` (cli/src/core/hooks.ts, the `for (const arg of args)` loop) pins only arguments that are themselves existing regular files.\n\nFix by making the rule one that cannot be argued around: a project hook command is accepted only if every argument is either (a) pinned (an existing regular file inside the workspace, hashed) or (b) provably not a reference into the workspace. Concretely, refuse as invalid (unpinnable, with a message naming the argument and saying what to do: put the logic in one script file and name it directly):\n - any argument that resolves inside the workspace to a directory, or to anything that is not a regular file;\n - any argument of the form `--opt=VALUE` / `-oVALUE`-style where VALUE (after the `=`) resolves to an existing path inside the workspace: pin it if a regular file, else refuse (do pin the `=value` case rather than refuse, so `--require=./pre.js` is covered and named in `list`);\n - inline-code forms for project hooks: when command[0]'s basename is a known shell or interpreter (sh, bash, zsh, dash, ksh, fish, node, nodejs, bun, deno, python, python3, perl, ruby, php, pwsh, env, busybox, and versioned names like python3.12) refuse `-c`, `-e`, `--eval`, `-p`, `--print`, `-m`, `-r`/`--require`/`--import`/`--loader` given as a separate flag whose NEXT argument is not a pinned file (pin it if it is), and refuse `env` as command[0] altogether for project hooks (it hides the real program) — decide the exact list by what is simple and sound, and state the rule in the docs as: \"a project hook names a program and files; inline code is not accepted\";\n - any remaining argument that contains a `/` and resolves (relative to the workspace) to an existing path inside the workspace that is not pinned.\n Also consider the default-module resolution case the directory form stood for (`node hookdir` → index.js): the directory refusal covers it. And bare names with no slash that are existing workspace files (`[\"node\",\"guard.js\"]`) must already be pinned: confirm with a test.\nBe honest in docs/HOOKS.md about what remains: this is a refusal list for known interpreters, a program outside that list that takes inline code, files a pinned script itself loads, and the window between the hash check and the interpreter reading the file are not covered; correct the sentence at HOOKS.md ~86-93 that implies every reference is covered. Operator hooks are unaffected by these refusals.\n\nAlso fix the two surviving mutations: add a test with a terminal on stdin only (and one on stdout only) so that dropping the stdout check fails; add a test for the \"approved record names a file the hooks no longer name\" comparison (or remove that comparison if it protects nothing — say which and why). Cheap extra if simple: cache `projectHooksState` hashing by file stamp (dev, ino, size, mtimeNs) so each call does not re-hash up to 32 MiB; skip it if it adds risk, and say so.\n\nTests: one per refused form above (each of the four reviewer attacks end to end: approve is refused, or if the file was approved under the old code path the hooks are inactive), the `--require=./pre.js` pinned-and-overwritten case, and that ordinary forms still work (`[\"./guard.sh\"]`, `[\"bash\",\"./guard.sh\"]`, `[\"node\",\"scripts/guard.js\",\"--flag\"]`, `[\"/usr/bin/true\"]`, the shipped examples under examples/hooks — run `hooks_examples`). Mutation for each refusal. Then all hook test files, `leak_guard`, `security`, `managed_policy_enforcement`, `tsc --noEmit`, the complexity gate, `check_invariants`, `check_doc_versions`, the hooks schema `--check`. Report under 350 words: the final rule as implemented (file:line), tests and mutations, what is not covered, commit hash.","type":"message","recipient":"a317b41792fa50650","recipient_kind":"agent","content":"Re-review of your fix (now at 258f72ff in /home/m…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2747,"cache_read_input_tokens":147016,"output_tokens":2829,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2747,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":2829,"cache_read_input_tokens":147016,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2747,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2747},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.2.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"},{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.5.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"},{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.8.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_m