serve-mcp `tools/list`, ACP kinds.\n- **Dispatch:** all 44 registered tools in 10 approval postures, plus 55 special cases.\n\n**Mutations (each restored from a copy)**\n\n| Mutation | Caught by |\n|---|---|\n| One character in `read_file`'s description | definitions, configurations, derived |\n| Swap `read_findings` / `read_archive` order | configurations |\n| Unknown tool treated as a read instead of exec | cases, gate order |\n| `run_tests` dropped from bridge registration | bindings, four sweeps |\n| `read_archive` not registered | registered, sweeps, the no-orphan test |\n\n**Behaviour pinned that the refactor must decide about**\n- Arguments of JSON `null` make dispatch throw a `TypeError` (`dispatch_tool_call.ts:266`) instead of returning a receipt.\n- An unknown tool is put to the operator as `exec` and a baseline is captured before the spine answers FAIL-001. Argument validation (FAIL-002) also runs only after approval.\n- The plugin middleware pipeline (`executeToolPipeline`) is never reached: every registered tool resolves to a handler first.\n- Read-only mode offers the same list as default, write tools included. `run_command` reaches the bridge; egress and LSP tools run unasked; `update_plan` is refused (AUTH-009).\n- The checkpoint read-only fallback still lets `run_command` through.\n- Structural-repair, delegation and role denials emit no flight or observer events; the delete guard records a call with no result.\n- `denied: true` on `onToolEnd` is set for some denials only. A declined approval has no `denialReason`.\n- The fallback `capabilityId` for an unregistered tool varies by gate: `unknown`, `unregistered`, or the tool name.\n- The parser does not know `enable_tools`, `read_findings`, `read_archive`, `read_objective` or `read_tool_output`, and lists three names that are not tools.\n- `lsp_*` are effect `exec` but ACP kind `read`. `browser_click` counts as changing the workspace and `browser_type` does not.\n- The tester role is refused web tools but offered a remote MCP tool.\n- A wrong-typed argument passes spine validation.\n\n**Not covered**\n- Skill constraint and integrity gates, the injection ask, interrupted-call reissue, untrusted-skill activation, and the `run_tests` attempt recording after the spine.\n- The \"LSP on/off\" configuration you listed has no switch of its own; only the `lsp` tool group is snapshotted.\n- Neither Node 22 nor a full suite run was done (local Node is 24.11.1).\n- No XERJ query and no claim file were made.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>281111</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>48</tool_uses><duration_ms>1176636</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
