e workspace:** pinned (hashed, shown in `list` and `approve`).\n- **Nothing by that name, or outside the workspace:** accepted.\n- **Directory, dangling link, anything else in the workspace:** refused; the file is invalid and not run.\n\nFor known shells and interpreters (`:305`, version suffixes included):\n\n- **Inline code** (`:421`): any single-dash option containing `c e i m p r`, plus `--eval`, `--print`, `--command`, and `eval` for deno and bun, is refused.\n- **Loaders** (`:414`): `-r`, `--require`, `--import`, `--loader` need a pinned file as their value, so `--require=./pre.js` is accepted and pinned.\n- **Wrappers** (`:407`): `env` and `busybox` as the program are refused.\n\nThe single-dash rule is deliberately broad, so it also refuses harmless forms such as `bash -euo pipefail ./guard.sh`. Operator hooks are unaffected. The check re-runs before every call.\n\n## Tests (`hooks_cli` 13, `hooks_self_approval` 10, each 3 runs in a row)\n\n- **Refused forms:** 24 commands cannot be approved and list as `invalid`.\n- **Attacks end to end:** the four reviewer forms, with an old-style approval on record and the file overwritten by the agent's `write_file`: no hook runs and the notice says why.\n- **`--require=./pre.js`:** pinned, overwritten, hooks stop and name `pre.js`.\n- **Ordinary forms still work:** `[\"./guard.sh\"]`, `[\"bash\",\"./guard.sh\"]`, `[\"node\",\"guard.js\"]`, `[\"node\",\"scripts/guard.js\",\"--flag\"]`, `[\"/usr/bin/true\"]`, and `hooks_examples`.\n- **Terminal check:** now `isInteractiveTerminal` (`hooks_cli.ts:99`), tested with a terminal on stdin only and on stdout only.\n- **\"Approved record names a file no longer reached\":** kept and tested. It protects the case where a removed workspace program lets `PATH` fall through to a different one.\n- **Hash cache:** added, keyed by device, inode, size, mtime and ctime.\n\n## Mutations\n\nEach of these fails a test: accepting directories, inline options, unpinned loader values, or `env`; dropping the `=value` or `-ovalue` check; dropping either TTY side; dropping the removed-file comparison; a cache that ignores content identity.\n\n## Gates\n\nAll hook test files, `leak_guard`, `security`, `managed_policy_enforcement`, `tsc`, the complexity gate, `check_invariants`, `check_doc_versions` and the hooks schema `--check` pass. No schema change.\n\n## Not covered (stated in `docs/HOOKS.md`)\n\n- The interpreter list is a refusal list; other programs that take code or module names (`awk`, `make`, `sqlite3`) are not recognised.\n- Files a pinned script itself loads, and anything a program finds by its own rules (`node_modules`, config in the working directory), are not pinned.\n- The window between the hash check and the program reading the file is not closed.\n- The unsandboxed fake-terminal and direct-store-write limit from the previous round still stands.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>548848</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>7</tool_uses><duration_ms>423098</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}]}}
