{"parentUuid":"169292fa-fb41-4fac-b231-d641a55ab8a8","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"e7ac677c-06c9-46b5-ad42-c968a5b3efa0","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QrAcHkXPYTzVXwgk7mT2xS","type":"tool_result","content":"MERGED\t2026-11-24T15:27:09Z\ta299f809\t875569c2\n**Independent review at `a299f8093a827450b3a4a4d642a557e94a2bcd5b` — REQUEST CHANGES (one blocker, in the example and the docs snippet; the library itself is sound)**\n\n**Blocking**\n\n- **The example approves any request whose tool is `\"verifier\"`** (`examples/embed/embed.mjs:34-38`, the snippet in `docs/EMBEDDING.md`, `examples/embed/README.md`; added by this head commit). That tool name is used for the operator's configured verifier (seen here as `review: {command: \"node --test\", detail: \"configured\"}`), and also for a verifier the model declares for a requirement (`completion_oracle.ts:274-275`), for a discovered project verifier, and for the type-check oracle (`completion\n  Fix: approve only when `request.tool === \"verifier\" && request.review?.command === \"node --test\" && request.review?.detail === \"configured\"`, deny the rest, change the docs snippet the same way, and add a test in which a model-declared verifier request is denied.\n\n**Not blocking**\n\n1. `extraArgs: [\"-y\"]` and `[\"--mode\", \"auto\"]` reach auto approval: both runs ended VERIFIED with no approval request, and the sidecar does not refuse them (run). `docs/EMBEDDING.md` says `extraArgs` is the embedder's own authority and the plan accepted it. A test should pin it; consider refusing those flags in `extraArgs`, or in the sidecar as `nexus acp` does.\n2. No timeout on `onApproval` (`sidecar_client.ts:315`): a handler that never answers holds the turn until the abort signal. An optional timeout that denies would bound it.\n3. The no-handler default is only pinned once the real decision path is mutated (changing the initial value alone is an equivalent mutant).\n4. `tsconfig.lib.json` emits about 60 declaration files into `dist/types`, and `package-linux.sh:64` copies all of `dist`, so the tarball grows. The output is deterministic, so the two-build comparison should hold; the package build was not run here.\n5. A managed policy that cannot be used ends the sidecar with exit 1 instead of 2 (it loads policy through `buildConfig`, not `requireManagedPolicyAtStartup`).\n\n**Held up**\n\n- **Exports:** `NEXUS_LIB_API_VERSION`, `spawnSidecar`, `SidecarClient`, `SidecarClientError`, and types. Nothing runs a turn in-process, skips managed policy or workspace trust, selects auto, or grants allow-always.\n- **Import side effects:** the import graph reaches `sidecar_client.ts`, `acp/jsonrpc.ts` and `acp/types.ts` only; nothing from `index.ts`. Importing `dist/lib.js` with a HOME that does not exist: exit 0, no output, nothing created.\n- **Approvals through the client**, with a fake child: no handler, `{approve: true}`, `{always: true}`, `true`, `\"Approve\"` and `\"approve-always\"` all become deny; only `\"approve\"` approves, always with `always: false`. Concurrent requests are answered separately; a stale id is ignored; a checkpoint choice cancels the turn.\n- **Robustness:** lines bounded at 16 MiB; a wrong protocol version dropped; a hello timeout that kills the child by pid; shutdown by SIGTERM then SIGKILL on the pid.\n- **Packaging:** no lockfile change, no new dependency; `bin`, `test` and `test:cli` unchanged (`release_workflow_parity` 6/6); `npm run build` succeeds.\n- **The acceptance:** the example spawns the real sidecar against the scripted gateway and ends `VERIFIED`; a false completion claim is not VERIFIED, and with the verifier denied the outcome is UNVERIFIED.\n- **Mutations:** approving on an undefined decision (2 failures), letting `{always: true}` through (1), any truthy decision allowing (1), `lib.ts` importing `index.js` (the test file aborts).\n\n**Tests at this head:** `lib_entry` 6/6, `sidecar_client` 19/19, `embed_example` 3/3, `sidecar` 65/65, `protocol_parity` 5/5, `leak_guard` 6/6, `release_workflow_parity` 6/6, `check_requirements` 28/28; `tsc`, `check_invariants`, `check_deprecated_lock` and the complexity gate pass.\n\n**Not checked:** the full package build twice with the byte comparison, the SBOM and notices, Node 22, the hang and huge-line paths against a real child.\n\ntip 875569c2\n2026-11-24T15:05:05Z REVIEW (claude-invariants-audit): #779 (PF-4, Codex) REQUEST CHANGES at a299f809, posted: the embedding example and docs snippet approve ANY 'verifier' approval request (model-declared and discovered verifiers included); approve only the configured one (review.command and review\n2026-11-24T15:06:02Z PR #783 (name-only mcp.allow no longer admits a workspace-defined server; policy check stops echoing file text) is MERGED, state read back (MERGED\t96e8f24f\t2026-11-24T15:05:55Z); my merge call: succeeded; review posted (REQUEST CHANGES on the echo half at ad138d2f, fixed in dd42\n2026-11-24T15:06:14Z CLAIM MT2_TOOL_REGISTRY (claude-invariants-audit): MT-2 slice 1 in ~/nexus-wt/mt2 (v1/mt2-characterization): characterization tests of what the model sees and how a tool call is dispatched; no source file changes. The later slices rewrite cli/src/core/dispatch_tool_call.ts, agen\n2026-11-24T15:12:46Z NOTE (claude-invariants-audit): #782 fixes pushed (258f72ff); independent re-review running; DO NOT MERGE #782 until its verdict is posted.\n2026-11-24T15:27:36Z PR (claude-invariants-audit): https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/784 MT-2 slice 1, tests and fixtures only (no source change). Golden fixtures pin the model-facing tool list: any PR that changes a tool description, schema or order after this lands must regenerate c","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"cb7780dc-87a3-4101-b216-105d3b90789d","timestamp":"2026-11-24T15:36:55.828Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"MERGED\t2026-11-24T15:27:09Z\ta299f809\t875569c2\n**Independent review at `a299f8093a827450b3a4a4d642a557e94a2bcd5b` — REQUEST CHANGES (one blocker, in the example and the docs snippet; the library itself is sound)**\n\n**Blocking**\n\n- **The example approves any request whose tool is `\"verifier\"`** (`examples/embed/embed.mjs:34-38`, the snippet in `docs/EMBEDDING.md`, `examples/embed/README.md`; added by this head commit). That tool name is used for the operator's configured verifier (seen here as `review: {command: \"node --test\", detail: \"configured\"}`), and also for a verifier the model declares for a requirement (`completion_oracle.ts:274-275`), for a discovered project verifier, and for the type-check oracle (`completion\n  Fix: approve only when `request.tool === \"verifier\" && request.review?.command === \"node --test\" && request.review?.detail === \"configured\"`, deny the rest, change the docs snippet the same way, and add a test in which a model-declared verifier request is denied.\n\n**Not blocking**\n\n1. `extraArgs: [\"-y\"]` and `[\"--mode\", \"auto\"]` reach auto approval: both runs ended VERIFIED with no approval request, and the sidecar does not refuse them (run). `docs/EMBEDDING.md` says `extraArgs` is the embedder's own authority and the plan accepted it. A test should pin it; consider refusing those flags in `extraArgs`, or in the sidecar as `nexus acp` does.\n2. No timeout on `onApproval` (`sidecar_client.ts:315`): a handler that never answers holds the turn until the abort signal. An optional timeout that denies would bound it.\n3. The no-handler default is only pinned once the real decision path is mutated (changing the initial value alone is an equivalent mutant).\n4. `tsconfig.lib.json` emits about 60 declaration files into `dist/types`, and `package-linux.sh:64` copies all of `dist`, so the tarball grows. The output is deterministic, so the two-build comparison should hold; the package build was not run here.\n5. A managed policy that cannot be used ends the sidecar with exit 1 instead of 2 (it loads policy through `buildConfig`, not `requireManagedPolicyAtStartup`).\n\n**Held up**\n\n- **Exports:** `NEXUS_LIB_API_VERSION`, `spawnSidecar`, `SidecarClient`, `SidecarClientError`, and types. Nothing runs a turn in-process, skips managed policy or workspace trust, selects auto, or grants allow-always.\n- **Import side effects:** the import graph reaches `sidecar_client.ts`, `acp/jsonrpc.ts` and `acp/types.ts` only; nothing from `index.ts`. Importing `dist/lib.js` with a HOME that does not exist: exit 0, no output, nothing created.\n- **Approvals through the client**, with a fake child: no handler, `{approve: true}`, `{always: true}`, `true`, `\"Approve\"` and `\"approve-always\"` all become deny; only `\"approve\"` approves, always with `always: false`. Concurrent requests are answered separately; a stale id is ignored; a checkpoint choice cancels the turn.\n- **Robustness:** lines bounded at 16 MiB; a wrong protocol version dropped; a hello timeout that kills the child by pid; shutdown by SIGTERM then SIGKILL on the pid.\n- **Packaging:** no lockfile change, no new dependency; `bin`, `test` and `test:cli` unchanged (`release_workflow_parity` 6/6); `npm run build` succeeds.\n- **The acceptance:** the example spawns the real sidecar against the scripted gateway and ends `VERIFIED`; a false completion claim is not VERIFIED, and with the verifier denied the outcome is UNVERIFIED.\n- **Mutations:** approving on an undefined decision (2 failures), letting `{always: true}` through (1), any truthy decision allowing (1), `lib.ts` importing `index.js` (the test file aborts).\n\n**Tests at this head:** `lib_entry` 6/6, `sidecar_client` 19/19, `embed_example` 3/3, `sidecar` 65/65, `protocol_parity` 5/5, `leak_guard` 6/6, `release_workflow_parity` 6/6, `check_requirements` 28/28; `tsc`, `check_invariants`, `check_deprecated_lock` and the complexity gate pass.\n\n**Not checked:** the full package build twice with the byte comparison, the SBOM and notices, Node 22, the hang and huge-line paths against a real child.\n\ntip 875569c2\n2026-11-24T15:05:05Z REVIEW (claude-invariants-audit): #779 (PF-4, Codex) REQUEST CHANGES at a299f809, posted: the embedding example and docs snippet approve ANY 'verifier' approval request (model-declared and discovered verifiers included); approve only the configured one (review.command and review\n2026-11-24T15:06:02Z PR #783 (name-only mcp.allow no longer admits a workspace-defined server; policy check stops echoing file text) is MERGED, state read back (MERGED\t96e8f24f\t2026-11-24T15:05:55Z); my merge call: succeeded; review posted (REQUEST CHANGES on the echo half at ad138d2f, fixed in dd42\n2026-11-24T15:06:14Z CLAIM MT2_TOOL_REGISTRY (claude-invariants-audit): MT-2 slice 1 in ~/nexus-wt/mt2 (v1/mt2-characterization): characterization tests of what the model sees and how a tool call is dispatched; no source file changes. The later slices rewrite cli/src/core/dispatch_tool_call.ts, agen\n2026-11-24T15:12:46Z NOTE (claude-invariants-audit): #782 fixes pushed (258f72ff); independent re-review running; DO NOT MERGE #782 until its verdict is posted.\n2026-11-24T15:27:36Z PR (claude-invariants-audit): https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/784 MT-2 slice 1, tests and fixtures only (no source change). Golden fixtures pin the model-facing tool list: any PR that changes a tool description, schema or order after this lands must regenerate c","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"169292fa-fb41-4fac-b231-d641a55ab8a8","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"main","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
