{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","hash":"af4138903be561ba595e72efd7e528802a397925dc3bdf2362260ba8d100a216","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TDHpcFjZZfDystSmMHCY1c","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-wt/polfu/cli && cat > /dev/shm/wft.mts <<'EOF'\nimport fs from \"node:fs\"; import os from \"node:os\"; import path from \"node:path\";\nconst { checkPolicyFile } = await import(\"/home/mike/nexus-wt/polfu/cli/src/policy_cli.ts\");\nconst d = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), \"wft-\"));\nconst cases: Record<string, string> = {\n  bare_key: \"schema_version = 1\\ndbpassword_hunter2_abcdefghij\\n\",\n  value: \"schema_version = 1\\n[mcp]\\nallow = REDACTED\\n\",\n  quoted_value: 'schema_version = 1\\n[mcp]\\nallow = [\"has space secret phrase here\"]\\n',\n  lowercase_secret: \"schema_version = 1\\n[approval]\\nmysecretlowercasetoken = true\\n\",\n  typo: \"schema_version = 1\\n[approval]\\nstrictt = true\\n\",\n};\nfor (const [name, text] of Object.entries(cases)) { const f = path.join(d, name); fs.writeFileSync(f, text); console.log(name, \"=>\", (checkPolicyFile(f) as any).error); }\nEOF\nHOME=$(mktemp -d) node --import tsx /dev/shm/wft.mts 2>&1 | cut -c1-220","description":"Print the error text the check now produces for five crafted files"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","hash":"7366767638ae4e0bea491ac3b566d64ced0a852c19792e6a552795d7032a2792","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Tv3wNpLtLEHmHDVrouFNGj","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-wt/polfu && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='cli/src/policy_cli.ts'; s=open(p).read()\nold='''    text.length < 9 || policyName(text) ? all : `${quote}${text.slice(0, 8)}…${quote}`);'''\nnew='''    text.length < 9 || policyName(text) || MESSAGE_EXAMPLES.has(text) ? all : `${quote}${text.slice(0, 8)}…${quote}`);'''\nassert s.count(old)==1; s=s.replace(old,new)\nold='function withoutFileText(detail: string): string {'\ns=s.replace(old,'/** Quoted examples that the loader\\'s own messages contain; they are not text of the file. */\\nconst MESSAGE_EXAMPLES = new Set([\"command:/absolute/path\", \"url:https://origin\", \"sha256:<64 hex digits>\", \"file:/absolute/path\"]);\\n\\n'+old,1)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\nrtk proxy grep -rhn 'sha256:<\\|file:/absolute\\|\"command:/absolute/path\"' cli/src/core/managed_policy*.ts | cut -c1-200 | head -5; cd cli && npx tsc --noEmit -p . >/dev/null; echo \"tsc $?\"; HOME=$(mktemp -d) node --import tsx /dev/shm/wft.mts 2>&1 | sed -n 3p | cut -c1-230; bash -c 'for f in policy_cli managed_policy_merge managed_policy_toml managed_policy_load leak_guard; do TMPDIR=/dev/shm HOME=$(mktemp -d) timeout 280 node --import tsx --test test/$f.test.ts 2>&1 | grep -E \"^ℹ (pass|fail) \" | tr \"\\n\" \" \"; echo \"<- $f\"; done'","description":"Keep the loader's own quoted examples intact, then re-check the output and run the policy tests","timeout":400000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","hash":"e1b52702745677e65d6768806732ce8b5448cff2963459486626b26260eec3e7","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015UvEaLr1MaQGrE1fKEM4Uj","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-wt/polfu && git add -A cli && git commit -q -m \"fix(policy): cut rejected tokens by pairing quotes in order\n\nThe first version paired the second and third quote of a message such as\n\\\"expected '=' after the key 'x'\\\", cut the fixed text and left the file's\ntoken whole, so a line with no '=' was still read out in full. Quotes are now\ntaken pair by pair; a token is kept only when it is short, is a dotted name\nunder one of the policy's own tables, or is one of the loader's own examples.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>\" && git merge -q origin/release/v1.3.0 --no-edit 2>&1 | tail -1; git push -q origin v1/policy-followups 2>&1 | tail -1; echo \"remote: $(git ls-remote origin refs/heads/v1/policy-followups | cut -c1-8) local: $(git rev-parse --short=8 HEAD)\"; cd ~/nexus-code && gh pr comment 783 --body \"**Independent review at \\`ad138d2f\\` — REQUEST CHANGES on the error-text half; fixed in the commit now pushed.**\n\n- **The allowlist change is sound.** \\`fromWorkspace\\` is computed on the one path that reads files (\\`loadAndConnect\\`, through \\`isWorkspaceFile\\`, which also catches symlinks into the workspace). Configurations are not merged field by field: each name's whole entry comes from the first file that defines it, so there is no entry with a user's name and a workspace's command. A refused workspace entry falls through to the user's own entry of that name. \\`addServer\\` and \\`addConnection\\` pass \\`false\\`; their callers are the operator's \\`/mcp add\\` and the REPL wizard. A workspace server with a bare command such as \\`npx\\` has no pinnable path and is now refused with the new message, as the document says. Removing the rule fails the new test.\n- **The error-text cut did not work** (confirmed by running): the pattern paired the second and third quote of \\`expected '=' after the key '<key>'\\`, cut the fixed text and left the file's token whole. A line with no \\`=\\` was echoed in full, a 5,000-character line gave a 5,031-character error, and \\`--json\\` carried the same.\n\n**Fix:** quotes are now taken pair by pair, in order. A quoted token is kept only when it is shorter than nine characters, is a dotted lower-case name under one of the policy's own tables (what a mistyped key looks like), or is one of the loader's own examples (\\`command:/absolute/path\\` and the like). The test now includes the reviewer's two cases. What the check prints for five crafted files:\n\n\\`\\`\\`\nline 2: expected '=' after the key 'dbpasswo…'\nline 3: unsupported value 'sk-live-…': expected a \\\"string\\\", true, false, a whole number or an array of strings\nline 3: key 'mcp.allow', item 1 (\\\"has spac…\\\") must be a server name (…), \\\"command:/absolute/path\\\" or \\\"url:https://origin\\\"\nline 3: unknown key 'approval.mysecretlowercasetoken'\nline 3: unknown key 'approval.strictt'\n\\`\\`\\`\n\nThe fourth line is the remaining limit: a lower-case name under a real policy table is shown in full, because that is exactly what a mistyped key is.\n\nTests after the fix: \\`policy_cli\\` 24/24, \\`managed_policy_merge\\` 47/47, \\`managed_policy_toml\\` 111/111, \\`managed_policy_load\\` 97/97, \\`leak_guard\\` 6/6, \\`tsc\\` clean. Not checked by the reviewer: whether model-originated text can reach \\`/mcp add\\`.\" | tail -1","description":"Commit and push the corrected error-text cut and post the review and fix on PR 783"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","hash":"3c68604dff6f58437e3fcc4638b7f3031d3f1c9236df0b1447b13470c6f59100","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HzoTpGGCvxPdxpVMdJwggw","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/rev782.md","content":"**Independent review at `034c278cad62e7e849c4b68037d2ef32b2801af5` — REQUEST CHANGES. The hook output handling and the gate ordering hold; all three blockers are about who can get a hook trusted. I am fixing them on this branch.**\n\n**Blocking, each confirmed by running**\n\n1. **The model can approve its own project hooks.** `nexus hooks approve --sha256 <hex>` works with no terminal (`hooks_cli.ts`, about line 118), and neither the trust store (`extension_trust.json`) nor `hooks.json` is in `DEFAULT_PROTECTED_PATHS` (`security.ts:163`), unlike `policy_trust.json` and `trusted_workspaces.json`. In auto mode: `write_file .nexus/hooks.json`, then `run_command \"nexus hooks approve --sha256 <hash> -w <repo>\"` exited 0, wrote the store, and the hook ran on the next call. (Unsandboxed `run_command` sees `~/.config/nexus`; with `--sandbox` the home directory is masked; in review mode the operator would see the command.)\n2. **With the workspace set to the home directory, the model can write an active operator hooks file.** `write_file .config/nexus/hooks.json` succeeded; at umask 022 the file is mode 644, which the mode check accepts, and the \"operator\" hook ran with no approval. At umask 002 the file is rejected and every call is denied instead.\n3. **Approval does not pin the script a hook names.** After approving `command: [\"./guard.sh\"]`, the model overwrote `guard.sh` and the next call ran the model's script with the operator's rights, outside the sandbox, with no new approval. `docs/HOOKS.md` says the approval is for \"the file's exact bytes\" and never says this.\n\n**Not blocking**\n\n- A hook's denial reason reaches the model as `[hook X (project)] <up to 1000 chars>`: one line, named and sourced, but not marked as untrusted text, so an instruction in it passes through. It should be quoted as hook-supplied text. (Plain stdout and the receipt's hook summaries do not reach the model.)\n- A running hook is not stopped by cancel or by the turn deadline, and time spent queued behind another hook is outside its 120 s budget. The document says the first.\n- `HOOKS.md` claims subagents and operation units are covered. Subagents are (same dispatch and spine). Operation units get their own agent on another workspace path, so project hooks do not run there; no test covers either.\n- The hooks stage also gates the operator's own `!cmd`; undocumented.\n- When a hook denies a call that a spine-stage gate (read-only, workspace boundary, grants) would have denied, the gate's reason and anything the later stages would have recorded (sandbox-denial events) are replaced by `HOOK_DENIED`. A hook-denied call is still charged to the tool-invocation budget.\n\n**Held up**\n\n- Nineteen output shapes fed to the reducer (duplicate keys, a BOM, `continue` as a string, null and array decisions, a deny mixed with an allow, exit codes 1, 3 and 126, stderr only): none admitted anything, and every unreadable or unknown shape denied.\n- A `post-tool` hook only reads the receipt. The move of helpers out of `verify_service.ts` is verbatim (`verify_service` 10/10, `mcp_verify` 7/7).\n- Mutations, each caught: an allow that skips the authority stage; a hook error that continues; skipping the project hash check (6 failures); passing the full environment.\n\n**Tests at this head, 0 failures:** the thirteen hook files (101 tests), `approval_policy` 16, `mcp_tool_through_spine` 3, `sandbox_denial_events` 6, `hash_chain` 28, `leak_guard` 6, `protocol_parity` 5, `protocol_schema` 8, `check_requirements` 28; `tsc`, the complexity gate and `check_invariants` pass.\n\n**Not checked:** the approve command under `--sandbox` in production form; a hook stalling a turn past its deadline (read only); the doctor output for an invalid operator file beyond its test; the schema and examples.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01G66on1V3ZFUFM51sLsURJT","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-code && gh pr comment 782 --body-file /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/rev782.md | tail -1; echo \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ) REVIEW (claude-invariants-audit): #782 (my HK-1 hooks) REQUEST CHANGES at 034c278c, posted: the model can approve its own project hooks (nexus hooks approve --sha256 with no TTY; extension_trust.json and hooks.json not in DEFAULT_PROTECTED_PATHS); with workspace=HOME it can write an active operator hooks file; approval does not pin the script a hook names. DO NOT MERGE #782; I am fixing these on the branch. #783 fix pushed (dd42ea30) after its review.\" >> \"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log\"; cd ~/nexus-wt/hk1 && rtk proxy grep -n \"DEFAULT_PROTECTED_PATHS\" -A14 cli/src/security.ts | cut -c1-170 | head -24; rtk proxy grep -rn \"isatty\\|isTTY\" cli/src/index.ts cli/src/workspace_trust.ts cli/src/trust*.ts 2>/dev/null | cut -c1-170 | head -8","description":"Post the review on PR 782, log it, and read how protected paths and the trust command's terminal check work"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","hash":"05ce6a610cd9a375c604946982cca751eefcd23a3d4273971633832a245b7999","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both reviews are posted. I'm now sending the three trust fixes for hooks back to the agent that built HK-1, since it has the context."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013MXix3AgVYswvTvmWruZJj","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"a317b41792fa50650","summary":"Fix three trust blockers in HK-1 hooks","message":"Follow-up work on HK-1 in /home/mike/nexus-wt/hk1 (branch v1/hk1-hooks-lib; it now has the release branch merged in twice and is pushed as PR #782; start with `git status` and `git log --oneline -6`; do not push; commit locally at the end with message `fix(hooks): <what>` ending with the line `Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>`). An independent review of PR #782 found three blockers, all confirmed by running, plus smaller items. Same working rules as before (throwaway HOME, `TMPDIR=/dev/shm` for speed, leak guard, kill by pid, mutations restored from a copy and never with `git checkout`, complexity gate, no model-facing tool text changes). Fix these, each with a test that fails without the fix (read the failure message to check it fails for the right reason), and report under 450 words.\n\nBLOCKER 1: the model can approve its own project hooks. `nexus hooks approve --sha256 <hex>` works with no terminal (cli/src/hooks_cli.ts ~118), and the trust store `extension_trust.json` and `hooks.json` are not in `DEFAULT_PROTECTED_PATHS` (cli/src/security.ts:163), unlike `policy_trust.json` and `trusted_workspaces.json`. Repro in auto mode: `write_file .nexus/hooks.json`, then `run_command \"nexus hooks approve --sha256 <hash> -w <repo>\"` → exit 0, store written, hook runs on the next call.\n Fix, all three parts:\n (a) Add the trust store file name and the operator hooks file name to `DEFAULT_PROTECTED_PATHS` with a one-line reason each, exactly as GV-1 did for `policy_trust.json`; find GV-1's test for that (search the tests for `policy_trust.json` and `isPathProtected`) and add the equivalent for both names, including through the agent's write tools.\n (b) Approval must be an act of a person at a terminal: look at how `nexus trust` (workspace trust) and GV-1's project-policy approval decide that (search `isTTY`, `process.stdin.isTTY`, \"trust\" in cli/src/index.ts, cli/src/workspace_trust.ts, cli/src/core/policy_runtime.ts and their tests) and do the same for `nexus hooks approve`: refuse without an interactive terminal (stdin AND stdout a TTY), with a message that says why; the `--sha256` flag may stay only as a confirmation of WHICH content is being approved in an interactive run, never as a way to approve without a terminal. `nexus hooks revoke` may stay non-interactive (it only removes trust). Tests need a seam: inject the \"is interactive\" predicate the way the existing trust code's tests do (do not add an env var that a model could set to fake a terminal). Also check whether the model's shell tool could fake a TTY (`script -q -c ...`): if the existing `nexus trust` guard has an answer to that (e.g. a refusal when running under the agent, detected by an env marker the agent sets on its child processes — search for such a marker, e.g. `NEXUS_AGENT`/`NEXUS_INSIDE`/similar, in cli/src/tools.ts and the Rust bridge env), reuse it; if there is none, say so plainly in the report and in docs/HOOKS.md as a limit (an unsandboxed command run in auto mode acts with the operator's rights).\n (c) A test for the whole route: an agent in auto mode that writes a project hooks file and then tries to approve it by `run_command` must not end with an active hook.\n\nBLOCKER 2: with the workspace set to the home directory, `write_file .config/nexus/hooks.json` created an operator hooks file that was accepted (mode 644) and its hook ran. (a) above protects the name; in addition require the operator hooks file to be owned by the current user and not group- or world-writable AND refuse it when it lies inside the active workspace (the workspace is then the operator's home: say in the denial what to do); test the workspace=HOME case end to end.\n\nBLOCKER 3: approval does not pin the script a hook names. After approving `command: [\"./guard.sh\"]` the model overwrote `guard.sh` and the next call ran the model's script. Fix: the approved identity of a project hooks file must cover the bytes of every file its commands name that resolves inside the workspace (command[0] and any argument that is an existing file path inside the workspace; resolve symlinks; refuse a command[0] that is a relative path escaping the workspace or a symlink out of it), re-checked before each run exactly as the hooks file's own hash is; a change makes the hooks inactive and \"asks again\" like a changed hooks file. `nexus hooks list`/`approve` show which files are covered. For a command[0] that is a bare name found through PATH or an absolute path outside the workspace, nothing in the workspace can replace it: state in docs/HOOKS.md that such a program is trusted as installed. Test: approve, overwrite the script through the agent's write tool, next tool call: hook not run, denial/notice names the changed file, re-approval needed.\n\nSMALLER ITEMS (do them if cheap, otherwise list as open):\n - A hook's denial reason reaches the model as `[hook X (project)] <text>`; make it unmistakably quoted hook-supplied text (a fixed framing sentence that says the text comes from a hook program and is not an instruction, the reason JSON-string-quoted and still capped) and test that a reason containing \"IGNORE PREVIOUS INSTRUCTIONS\" arrives inside that quoting.\n - docs/HOOKS.md: correct the claim about operation units (project hooks do not run in a unit's own worktree agent unless that is changed; say what is true), say that the hooks stage also applies to the operator's own `!cmd`, that a running hook is not stopped by cancel or the turn deadline and queue time is outside its timeout, and that when a hook denies a call a spine-stage gate would also have denied, the gate's own reason and later-stage records are replaced by the hook denial.\n - Add a test that a subagent's tool call goes through the hooks (the review found none).\n\nThen run, one at a time: every hook test file, `leak_guard`, `approval_policy`, `check_requirements`, the GV-1 trust/protected-path tests you touched or copied from, `policy_cli`, `managed_policy_allowlists`, `tsc --noEmit`, the complexity gate, `node scripts/check_invariants.mjs`, `node scripts/check_doc_versions.mjs`, and the hooks schema generator's `--check` if the trust record format changed (bump/ledger per the repo's rule if it did). Report: per blocker, file:line of the fix, the test names, the mutation that fails each; what the TTY guard can and cannot stop; any schema/ledger change; test counts; the commit hash; what is left open."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","hash":"be7c7a7ff2b2fce301b0a84ebc97ca8a742770a5839b40cdc76e5b1d6b51a91a","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01T3ApyeYAP6JVdaCYR1FUq7","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-code && bash -c 'L=\"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log\"; h=$(gh pr view 783 --json headRefOid --jq .headRefOid); git fetch -q origin; tip=$(git rev-parse --short=8 origin/release/v1.3.0); m=$(gh api repos/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pulls/783 --jq .merge_commit_sha); git fetch -q origin $m 2>/dev/null; par=$(git log -1 --format=%P $m | tr \" \" \"\\n\" | cut -c1-8 | tr \"\\n\" \" \"); r=$(gh run list --branch release/v1.3.0 --workflow ci.yml --limit 1 --json status,conclusion,headSha --jq \".[0]|.status+\\\"/\\\"+(.conclusion//\\\"\\\")+\\\"/\\\"+.headSha[0:8]\"); echo \"head ${h:0:8} tip $tip parents $par release $r\"; res=\"not issued\"; case \"$par\" in \"$tip \"*) if [ \"$r\" = \"completed/success/$tip\" ] && [ \"${h:0:8}\" = dd42ea30 ]; then if gh pr merge 783 --merge --match-head-commit $h; then res=succeeded; else res=failed; fi; sleep 5; fi;; esac; s=$(gh pr view 783 --json state,mergeCommit,mergedAt --jq \"[.state,.mergeCommit.oid[0:8],.mergedAt]|@tsv\"); echo \"merge call: $res; state: $s\"; case \"$s\" in MERGED*) echo \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ) PR #783 (name-only mcp.allow no longer admits a workspace-defined server; policy check stops echoing file text) is MERGED, state read back ($s); my merge call: $res; review posted (REQUEST CHANGES on the echo half at ad138d2f, fixed in dd42ea30; the fix commit itself was not re-read by a second reviewer); required checks green on the merge with tip $tip; release CI green at $tip first.\" >> \"$L\";; esac'; git -C ~/nexus-code worktree remove --force ~/nexus-wt/polfu 2>&1 | tail -1","description":"Merge PR 783 after re-reading tip, tested merge and release CI; read the state back, log it, remove the worktree"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","hash":"048be7074383c07f5eebe64ce5027c66d268d8625d81d224c506669381dad9d3","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FoxEojQ2de4fQP8he6yaqs","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-code && git fetch -q origin && d=\"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims\" && now=$(date -u +%FT%TZ) && mkdir -p $d/MT2_TOOL_REGISTRY && printf '{\"agent\":\"claude-invariants-audit\",\"branch\":\"v1/mt2-characterization\",\"since\":\"%s\",\"worktree\":\"/home/mike/nexus-wt/mt2\",\"note\":\"Owner directive 2026-11-24: this session completes the unbuilt v1.3.0 units. Plan: ~/nexus-wt/_plans/PF_SB_MT_PA_PLAN.md (MT-2).\",\"scope\":\"MT-2 slice 1: characterization tests only, no source changes. Slices 2-4 (registry, dispatch split, baseline move) later, announced here before they start.\"}\\n' \"$now\" > $d/MT2_TOOL_REGISTRY/owner.json && echo \"$now CLAIM MT2_TOOL_REGISTRY (claude-invariants-audit): MT-2 slice 1 in ~/nexus-wt/mt2 (v1/mt2-characterization): characterization tests of what the model sees and how a tool call is dispatched; no source file changes. The later slices rewrite cli/src/core/dispatch_tool_call.ts, agent.ts and spine_handlers.ts and will be announced here first. Also: #783 merged by me as 96e8f24f.\" >> $d/nexus-claims.log; git worktree add -q -b v1/mt2-characterization ~/nexus-wt/mt2 origin/release/v1.3.0 && ln -s ~/nexus-code/cli/node_modules ~/nexus-wt/mt2/cli/node_modules && mkdir -p ~/nexus-wt/mt2/core/target/release && cp ~/nexus-wt/ls1b/core/target/release/{harness-core,nexus-tui} ~/nexus-wt/mt2/core/target/release/ && echo ready","description":"Claim MT-2, log it, and create its worktree"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","hash":"d08db40fb95e3398d960aab59878894b5b97d6381f4b47df7bba206e649ac367","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019D4UtWReAoNFvbA5Xhe2hN","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"MT-2 slice 1 characterization tests","subagent_type":"general-purpose","prompt":"Implement MT-2 slice 1 (characterization tests ONLY, no source changes) in the worktree /home/mike/nexus-wt/mt2 (branch `v1/mt2-characterization`, based on `origin/release/v1.3.0`; repo is the Nexus Code TypeScript CLI in `cli/`). Read first: `/home/mike/nexus-wt/_plans/PF_SB_MT_PA_PLAN.md` (the MT-2 section: it defines the slices; you do slice 1 only), `/home/mike/nexus-wt/mt2/AGENTS.md`, `docs/v1.3.0/PLAN.md` (the MT-2 unit), then the code the later slices will rewrite: `cli/src/core/dispatch_tool_call.ts`, the tool definitions and dispatch in `cli/src/agent.ts` / `cli/src/tools.ts`, `cli/src/core/spine_handlers.ts`, and `cli/critical-complexity-baseline.json`.\n\nGoal: pin today's behaviour so that the later registry refactor and the split of `dispatchToolCallImpl` can be proven behaviour-preserving. Tests must pass on the unmodified source. Cover, as the plan lists (follow the plan where it differs from this summary):\n1. What the model sees: the exact list of tool definitions (names, order, descriptions, JSON schemas) sent to the model for each relevant configuration (default, read-only mode, subagent, with/without MCP tools, LSP on/off, any feature flags that add or remove tools) as a golden snapshot, byte-exact, with a generator/`--check` style or an inline fixture following whatever convention the repo already uses for golden files (look at how `cli/test/fixtures/` and the protocol schema samples are regenerated).\n2. Dispatch: for every built-in tool name, an unknown tool name, malformed arguments, and an MCP tool, the sequence of gates/stages a call passes through and the shape of the result/receipt (which gate denies, the error codes, the order of approval vs. policy vs. hooks-free spine stages), using the existing test helpers for a scripted model/agent (find them under `cli/test/helpers/`; see `approval_policy.test.ts`, `mcp_tool_through_spine.test.ts`, `sandbox_denial_events.test.ts` for patterns).\n3. A table-driven test that every tool the model can be offered has a dispatch route and every dispatch route corresponds to an offered tool (no orphan either way), written so it will keep working once a registry exists.\n\nRules: do not edit any file under `cli/src` or `core/`; if you believe a source change is needed, stop and report it instead. Every new test file starts with `import \"./helpers/leak_guard.js\";`. Run a single test file with `cd /home/mike/nexus-wt/mt2/cli && TMPDIR=/dev/shm HOME=$(mktemp -d) node --import tsx --test test/<name>.test.ts 2>&1 | tail -30` (a throwaway HOME is mandatory; never read the real ~/.nexus, ~/.config/nexus, /etc/nexus). No network, no inference runs. Stop any process only by its own pid, never `pkill -f`. Shell is zsh: use `bash -c` for loops; shell output passes through `rtk` which can filter it — prefix with `rtk proxy` if output looks cut. `cli/node_modules` is a symlink and the Rust binaries are already in `core/target/release/`. The host is loaded by other agents; timing-sensitive existing tests may flake — do not chase those. Verify each new test actually pins something: for at least three representative assertions, temporarily mutate the source (copy the file aside first and restore it from the copy; never `git checkout` to undo) and confirm the test fails for the right reason, then restore and confirm `git status` shows only your new test/fixture files. Run each new file three times; run `npx tsc --noEmit -p .` in `cli/`; run `leak_guard.test.ts`. Check `git log origin/release/v1.3.0..HEAD` for foreign commits, then commit locally (do NOT push, do not open a PR) with message `test(tools): characterize the model-facing tool list and dispatch routes (MT-2 slice 1)` ending with the line `Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>`.\n\nReport under 400 words: files added with test counts; the configurations snapshotted; the mutations and which test caught each; anything in today's behaviour that looks like a defect or an inconsistency the refactor must decide about (do not fix it; pin it and flag it); what the plan asked for that you did not cover and why; commit hash."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01AgVzLsYwJWAbU71xenhK8o","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-code && gh run list --branch release/v1.3.0 --workflow ci.yml --limit 1 --json status,conclusion,headSha --jq '.[0]|[.status,.conclusion,.headSha[0:8]]|@tsv'; gh pr list --state open --json number,headRefOid,title --jq '.[]|[.number,.headRefOid[0:8],.title[0:60]]|@tsv'; tail -4 \"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log\" | cut -c1-260","description":"Read release CI after the merge, the open PRs and the latest claims log lines"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","hash":"8c8a52fc7acd4538412c4b4af4718acd8b1bf3c0fb8df5e363726b829e892f24","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013kWatKskpXciarzyEFjNNA","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-wt/hk1 && git status --short | head -5; git fetch -q origin && git log --oneline -3 | cut -c1-90; git merge -q origin/release/v1.3.0 --no-edit 2>&1 | tail -3; cd cli && npx tsc --noEmit -p . >/dev/null; echo \"tsc $?\"; bash -c 'for f in hooks_self_approval hooks_cli hooks_project_trust hooks_gate_bypass managed_policy_merge policy_cli leak_guard; do TMPDIR=/dev/shm HOME=$(mktemp -d) timeout 280 node --import tsx --test test/$f.test.ts 2>&1 | grep -E \"^ℹ (pass|fail) \" | tr \"\\n\" \" \"; echo \"<- $f\"; done'; cd .. && git push -q origin v1/hk1-hooks-lib 2>&1 | tail -1; echo \"remote: $(git ls-remote origin refs/heads/v1/hk1-hooks-lib | cut -c1-8) local: $(git rev-parse --short=8 HEAD)\"; cd ~/nexus-code && gh run list --branch release/v1.3.0 --workflow ci.yml --limit 1 --json status,conclusion,headSha --jq '.[0]|[.status,.conclusion,.headSha[0:8]]|@tsv'","description":"Merge the release tip into the hooks branch, re-run key tests, push, and read release CI","timeout":590000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
