{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","hash":"c1955716df1ee2fc5b8432bf4774a74caaf4cf68e68345c1e2408301b4541f06","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VxeXGTkjArCYhpLscv4Ukw","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/pr_mt2a.md","content":"Plan unit MT-2, slice 1 of 4: characterization tests only. No file under `cli/src` or `core/` changes. The later slices (tool registry, then the split of `dispatchToolCallImpl`) must leave these tests passing without editing their fixtures.\n\n## What is pinned\n\n- **What the model sees** (`tool_surface_characterization`, 6 tests, golden `fixtures/model_tools_v1.json`): the tool definitions, byte for byte (names, order, descriptions, schemas), in 42 configurations: the main agent in default, auto, auto with full access and read-only (by mode and by launch); each tool group alone and all together; an objective with and without requirements; skills; output masking; an MCP tool plus a plugin tool; delegated allow-lists; a subagent at depth 1; all ten roles at depth 0 and 1. Also the derived lists: `HARNESS_TOOLS`, the parser's known and write/exec names, the `serve-mcp` tool list, ACP kinds.\n- **How a call is dispatched** (`tool_dispatch_characterization`, 17 tests, golden `fixtures/tool_bindings_v1.json`): all 44 registered tools in ten approval postures, plus 55 special cases (unknown tool, malformed arguments, MCP tool, each gate's denial and its code and order).\n- **No orphans**: every offered tool has a route and every route an offered tool.\n- `mt1_core_import` (1 test): the plan's import check for the core.\n\nFixtures regenerate only with `NEXUS_TOOLS_RECORD=1`.\n\n## Mutations, each caught\n\nOne character in `read_file`'s description; two tools swapped in order; an unknown tool treated as a read; `run_tests` dropped from bridge registration; `read_archive` not registered.\n\n## Behaviour pinned as it is today, for the refactor to decide about\n\nThese are recorded, not fixed here. Several look like defects and I will raise them separately:\n\n- Arguments of JSON `null` make dispatch throw a `TypeError` (`dispatch_tool_call.ts:266`) instead of returning a receipt.\n- An unknown tool is put to the operator for approval as `exec` before the spine answers FAIL-001; argument validation (FAIL-002) also runs only after approval.\n- Read-only mode offers the same tool list as default, write tools included; `run_command` reaches the bridge, and the checkpoint read-only fallback also lets it through.\n- The plugin middleware pipeline is never reached: every registered tool resolves to a handler first.\n- Some denials (structural repair, delegation, role) emit no flight or observer events; `denied: true` is set for some denials only.\n- The parser's name lists are out of step with the registered tools (five tools unknown to it, three names that are not tools).\n- `lsp_*` are effect `exec` but ACP kind `read`; `browser_click` counts as changing the workspace and `browser_type` does not.\n- The tester role is refused web tools but offered a remote MCP tool.\n- A wrong-typed argument passes spine validation.\n\n## Not covered\n\nSkill constraint and integrity gates, the injection ask, interrupted-call reissue, untrusted-skill activation, `run_tests` attempt recording after the spine. Node 22 was not run locally (CI runs it).\n\n## Tests\n\nLocal, Node 24: the three files pass (6, 17, 1), three runs each; `leak_guard` passes; `tsc` clean.\n\n## Reference coding\n\nExempt: tests of this repo's existing behaviour, no new design.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RoSUGodBDurikWmqxk5AP8","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-code && u=$(gh pr create --base release/v1.3.0 --head v1/mt2-characterization --title \"test(tools): characterize the model-facing tool list and dispatch routes (MT-2 slice 1)\" --body-file /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/pr_mt2a.md | tail -1); echo \"$u\"; echo \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ) PR (claude-invariants-audit): $u MT-2 slice 1, tests and fixtures only (no source change). Golden fixtures pin the model-facing tool list: any PR that changes a tool description, schema or order after this lands must regenerate cli/test/fixtures/model_tools_v1.json and tool_bindings_v1.json with NEXUS_TOOLS_RECORD=1.\" >> \"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log\"","description":"Open the MT-2 slice 1 PR and log it with the fixture note for other agents"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
