{"parentUuid":"64f8003a-1391-47f6-bac9-d686827cab90","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"44e47e74-3f75-4bf4-a3a8-8bcf488638a3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MpvdGghrigUnoQ5GcsquEF","type":"tool_result","content":"# v1.3.0 readiness inventory\n\nMeasured against `origin/release/v1.3.0` tip **`56e644cf`** (2026-11-23). Version strings are still **1.2.2**; this is not an RC cut and not a tag. External qualification is pending. This is not a frontier-grade claim.\n\n## Merge queue\n\nEmpty against `release/v1.3.0` at inventory time. Required checks on tip: green (`linux-x86_64`, `test-matrix` 22/24).\n\n## Plan units (from `docs/v1.3.0/PLAN.md`)\n\n| Unit | Status on tip | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| PF-1 | Landed | `docs/PROTOCOL.md`, `docs/protocol/*.schema.json`, parity/conformance tests |\n| PF-2 | Landed | `cli/src/run_contract.ts`, `docs/protocol/RUN_RESULT_VERSIONS.json` |\n| PF-3 | Open | No UDS/multi-client transport beyond stdio |\n| PF-4 | Open | `cli/package.json` has no `exports` / `types` library entry |\n| AC-1 | Landed | ACP adapter + gate tests; PRs #740/#741 and follow-ups |\n| AC-2 | Landed | `docs/evidence/AC2_ACP_CONFORMANCE.md`; Zed + CodeCompanion fixtures |\n| VR-1 | Landed | `nexus verify` + hostile/fixture work (#732/#737) |\n| VR-2 | Landed, follow-ups open | PR #756. Six findings from its second review are open (listed on the PR): a new ACP session re-pins the verification base; the client chooses the verified directory and the result does \n| VR-3 | Landed | Sandbox denial records (PR #745) |\n| GV-1 | Partial | Library (#717) and enforcement (#738) landed. Open per `docs/MANAGED_POLICY.md`: the `nexus policy` commands and doctor findings, `sandbox.*` reaching `nexus verify --sandbox`, and the TUI \"always\" ans\n| GV-2 | Landed | `nexus audit export` / `verify` |\n| GV-3 | Landed | `cli/src/core/hash_chain.ts` + flight replay |\n| GV-4 | Landed | `docs/TELEMETRY.md` + no-network / off / retention tests |\n| GV-5 | Partial | `approval.strict` refuses `--yes` / `--mode auto` with source tag. The MCP and plugin allowlists (`mcp.allow`, `mcp.disable_workspace`, `plugins.allow`, `plugins.disable_workspace`) are accepted by the\n| LS-1 / LS-2 | Landed | Lifecycle, bounds, position encodings, project roots |\n| CI speedup | Landed | Shard fan-out PRs #742–#748 |\n| HK-1 / HK-2 | Open | No `docs/HOOKS.md`, no `nexus plugins install` |\n| BG-1 / BG-2 | Open | No detached runner / schedule CLI |\n| PA-1 | Partial | Resource admission documented; `operation watch` / owner receipts still open (`docs/v1.3.0/PA1_RESOURCE_ADMISSION.md`) |\n| PA-2 | Open | No verified merge arbitration |\n| PA-3 | Partial | #706 landed the goal ledger; pause-on-restart is in review (#758, changes requested: a restart without a host reboot is not detected) |\n| HK-3 / BG-3 | Stretch (may roll) | Per plan Phase D; BG-3 is deferred to v1.4 by the plan |\n| SB-1 | Open | No named permission profiles |\n| MT-1 | Not measured here | The `agent.ts` split landed in v1.2.1 (#591); the unit's acceptance test was not located |\n| MT-2 | Open | No spec-plus-handler tool registry |\n| PA-4 | Partial / staged | Provider-neutral workflow slices landed; WP-P10-02 and remaining lifecycle still in flight under Codex claims |\n\n## Active Codex lanes (do not steal)\n\n- `codex/context-maturity-v130` — full `make test` on `cabe335e` finished **failed** (2026-11-23 ~21:50Z): CLI suite `cloud_providers.test.ts` — `operator cancellation mid-stream aborts promptly as 'aborted'` hung ~3\n- `v1/p10-02-inference-submission-budget` — WP-P10-02 cumulative inference budget (live claim).\n\n## Release gates (G-1–G-7) — measured\n\n| Gate | Measured |\n|---|---|\n| G-1 | Tip CI green; local full-suite on tip not re-run in this inventory. The real-server LSP suite and the real-project smoke run on `main` only by schedule; dispatched by hand on the release branch on 2026-11-23 (LSP\n| G-2 | Protocol schemas + AC-2 fixtures present; AC-1 experimental wording still appropriate until notes say otherwise |\n| G-3 | Hostile verify / managed-policy / ACP gate tests present; full hostile matrix not re-audited here. As planned the gate also spans hooks, plugins and schedules, which do not exist yet, so it cannot be evaluated in\n| G-4 | Open until BG-1/BG-2 land |\n| G-5 | Audit export/verify tests present (GV-2) |\n| G-6 | Protocol, telemetry, managed policy, ACP docs present; hooks/plugins/schedules docs absent |\n| G-7 | Framing: ledger closed for landed units above, **qualification pending** |\n\n## RC / stable cut (owner-gated)\n\nDo **not** tag from this inventory. When scope for RC is agreed:\n\n1. Version bump + `CHANGELOG` replace Unreleased (see `docs/RELEASE_PROCESS.md`).\n2. Release notes under `docs/releases/v1.3.0-rc.N.md` with G-7 framing.\n3. Land via merge-commit PR to `main` / release branch; tag only on owner instruction after required checks and ancestor rules.\n\n## Deferred from a thin RC (candidate)\n\nIf the owner wants an early RC of the platform track that is already on tip: ship PF-1/2, AC-1/2, VR-1/2/3, GV-1–5 as far as they have landed (GV-1 and GV-5 are partial: say so in the notes or finish them first), LS-*,\n**Independent third re-review at `72cd08cce` — REQUEST CHANGES.**\n\nPrior blockers 1–4 are closed (self-approval, workspace≠home, the four unpinned forms, queue `hookStillCurrent` re-resolve).\n\n**New blocker: nested launchers.** `INTERPRETERS` / `WRAPPERS` / inline / loader rules apply only to `argv[0]`. Prefixes such as `nice` / `timeout` / `nohup` / `stdbuf` / `ionice` let `bash -c` / `python3 -c` / `node -e` approv\nNested-launcher blocker addressed at head after this push: WRAPPERS/INTERPRETERS apply at every argv index; WRAPPERS expanded (`nice`, `timeout`, `nohup`, `stdbuf`, `ionice`, `time`, `chrt`, `taskset`); hostile approve/runtime coverage added for the nested forms and for an unknown prefix over `bash -c`.\n\nReady for a fourth independent re-review of the new head when CI is green. Residual follow-up (not this fix): exec","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"fa90c51d-3a2d-4684-af06-2580090d8209","timestamp":"2026-11-24T19:41:14.488Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"# v1.3.0 readiness inventory\n\nMeasured against `origin/release/v1.3.0` tip **`56e644cf`** (2026-11-23). Version strings are still **1.2.2**; this is not an RC cut and not a tag. External qualification is pending. This is not a frontier-grade claim.\n\n## Merge queue\n\nEmpty against `release/v1.3.0` at inventory time. Required checks on tip: green (`linux-x86_64`, `test-matrix` 22/24).\n\n## Plan units (from `docs/v1.3.0/PLAN.md`)\n\n| Unit | Status on tip | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| PF-1 | Landed | `docs/PROTOCOL.md`, `docs/protocol/*.schema.json`, parity/conformance tests |\n| PF-2 | Landed | `cli/src/run_contract.ts`, `docs/protocol/RUN_RESULT_VERSIONS.json` |\n| PF-3 | Open | No UDS/multi-client transport beyond stdio |\n| PF-4 | Open | `cli/package.json` has no `exports` / `types` library entry |\n| AC-1 | Landed | ACP adapter + gate tests; PRs #740/#741 and follow-ups |\n| AC-2 | Landed | `docs/evidence/AC2_ACP_CONFORMANCE.md`; Zed + CodeCompanion fixtures |\n| VR-1 | Landed | `nexus verify` + hostile/fixture work (#732/#737) |\n| VR-2 | Landed, follow-ups open | PR #756. Six findings from its second review are open (listed on the PR): a new ACP session re-pins the verification base; the client chooses the verified directory and the result does \n| VR-3 | Landed | Sandbox denial records (PR #745) |\n| GV-1 | Partial | Library (#717) and enforcement (#738) landed. Open per `docs/MANAGED_POLICY.md`: the `nexus policy` commands and doctor findings, `sandbox.*` reaching `nexus verify --sandbox`, and the TUI \"always\" ans\n| GV-2 | Landed | `nexus audit export` / `verify` |\n| GV-3 | Landed | `cli/src/core/hash_chain.ts` + flight replay |\n| GV-4 | Landed | `docs/TELEMETRY.md` + no-network / off / retention tests |\n| GV-5 | Partial | `approval.stric