{"parentUuid":"c9a2ebb9-14f3-459e-8e43-879b68677a80","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"44e47e74-3f75-4bf4-a3a8-8bcf488638a3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0163KFvyiN54gwcY5FiN32VQ","type":"tool_result","content":"MT2_TOOL_REGISTRY.released-20261124-pr784-merged\nSB1_PERMISSION_PROFILES.handoff-20261124T121240Z-codex\nready\n1:# PF-3, PF-4, SB-1, MT-2, PA-2: implementation plans (read-only planning pass, 2026-11-24)\n2-\n3-Code read at `origin/release/v1.3.0` = `4ae25a10`, extracted with `git archive`. Nothing was run except the complexity checker's\n4-`measureFunction` against that snapshot and the baseline revision. Every `file:line` below was read at that commit; re-verify it\n5:before editing, because the branch moves. Unit text: `docs/v1.3.0/PLAN.md:46-47` (PF-3, PF-4), `:70` (SB-1), `:76-77` (MT-1, MT-2),\n6:`:110` (PA-2). Gates: `:125-135`. Decisions: D13 `:141`, D22 `:150`. Phases: PF-4, PA-2 and SB-1 are in B; PF-3 and MT-2 are in C (`:116-121`).\n7-\n8-Hard constraints common to all five (from the brief, not repeated per unit): gates G-3 and verification-path protection, managed policy\n9-and the VERIFIED ladder are never weakened. The five critical functions do not grow (`cli/critical-complexity-baseline.json`). Tests use\n10-a throwaway HOME, no network and no live inference (`cli/test/helpers/fixtures.ts:67` `startGateway`, `:179` `makeHome`). New test\n11-files `import \"./helpers/leak_guard.js\"`, and custom servers are registered with `trackResource` (`cli/test/helpers/leak_guard.ts:1-16`).\n12-Children are stopped by pid, and sockets and listeners are closed. Linux x86_64 only, on Node 22 and 24. Each new surface gets docs, a CI-run example\n13-(G-6, pattern `examples/README.md` + `cli/test/examples.test.ts:73` `runScript`), a ledger entry where one exists, and tests that fail when\n14-the guard is removed.\n15-\n16-Live claims seen on 2026-11-24 (`$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims`, re-check before every slice):\n17-`cli/src/index.ts`, `config.ts`, `doctor.ts` (Codex, `codex/p10-02-elapsed-budget`); `core/operation_runner.ts` (Codex,\n18-`codex/pa3-token-budget-accounting`); `agent.ts`, `types.ts`, `core/run_turn.ts`, `core/spine_handlers.ts`, `core/agent_support.ts`,\n19-`core/operation_runner_execution.ts`, `core/scheduler.ts`, `core/verify.ts`, `core/turn.ts`; tests `examples.test.ts`,\n20-`context_convergence.test.ts`, `operation_schema.test.ts`, `operation_concurrency.test.ts`, `harness.test.ts`; `examples/operation/isolate.json`;\n21-`core/src/bin/nexus_tui/live_view.rs`; `docs/v1.3.0/PLAN.md`; `CHANGELOG.md`. **Not claimed then:** `sidecar.ts`, `protocol.ts`, `sandbox.ts`,\n22-`sandbox_network.ts`, `tools.ts`, `repl.ts`, `core/dispatch_tool_call.ts`, `core/spine.ts`, `core/capabilities.ts`, `core/operation_git.ts`,\n23-`core/operation.ts`, `cli/package.json`, `scripts/*.sh`.\n24-\n25----\n26-\n27:## PF-3: transport beyond a parent's stdio (unix socket, token, attach and reattach)\n28-\n29-**Acceptance (verbatim):** \"a second client attaches to a running session; a wrong token is refused; the socket is mode 0600\".\n30-Unit text: \"a unix domain socket (default) with a token and origin check for any localhost HTTP/WebSocket listener (reference: goose\n31-`acp/transport/auth.rs`, constant-time compare); several clients may attach and reattach\".\n32-\n33-### What exists (read)\n34-- `SidecarServer` (`cli/src/sidecar.ts:106`) drives one `ApplicationCore` and writes every event through one `write` callback\n35-  (`SidecarOptions.write`, `:89-103`; `emit` → `formatSafeSidecarEvent` → `encodeEvent`, `:1362-1365`). Its state is per process, apart from\n36-  negotiation, which is per connection: `negotiated` (`:148`), and `initialize` (`:315-331`) refuses a second `initialize` with BAD_REQUEST.\n37-- Approvals: `requestApproval`/`openApproval` queue one at a time and emit `approval.request` with id `approval-N` (`:860-891`).\n38-  `resolveApproval` with `always: true` sets `alwaysApprove`, switches the mode to `auto` and re-emits `session.state` (`:893-908`, grant at\n39-  `:899-904`). So today any writer to the sidecar's stdin can grant allow-always.\n40-- `hello` and the first `session.state` are emitted once, in `start()` (`:170-196`). `emitSessionState` is private (`:1335-1360`).\n41-- Process entry `main` (`:1529-1625`): its own commander, the client lease, pending-restore recovery, `buildConfig`, and stdin through\n42-  `readline` with **no line cap** (`:1615-1618`, and `docs/PROTOCOL.md` ~`:42` \"sets no limit on the length of a line it reads\"). EOF\n43-  on stdin means shutdown (`:1619-1623`). Guarded by `isEntryPoint` (`:1628-1643`).\n44-- Protocol: `PROTOCOL_VERSION=1`, range `:13-22`, `SIDECAR_CAPABILITIES` `:34-55`, `EXPERIMENTAL_FEATURES=[]` `:62`, `ErrorCode` `:76`,\n45-  `SidecarCommand` `:257-288`, `parseCommand` `:305`. Schema `docs/protocol/sidecar-v1.schema.json` + ledger `docs/protocol/VERSIONS.json`\n46-  (additive changes keep protocol 1 with a note, `docs/protocol/README.md` \"Recording a version decision\"). `docs/PROTOCOL.md:9-15` states\n47:  \"No socket or network transport ... (planned as PF-3)\".\n48-- Reusable pieces: `BoundedLineReader` (`cli/src/acp/jsonrpc.ts:34-103`, cap and oversized reporting), `ACP_MAX_LINE_BYTES=4 MiB` and\n49-  `ACP_MAX_OVERSIZED_LINES=3` (`acp/types.ts:97-99`), `ACP_PERMISSION_TIMEOUT_SECS=600` (`acp/types.ts:120`), and the ACP refusal of auto\n50-  approval at startup (`index.ts:1526-1539`, `acpStartupRefusal`). The private-dir and `lstat` pattern is in `core/client_lease.ts`\n51-  (`clientLeasePath`: `/tmp/nexus-client-leases-<uid>`, 0700, lstat-checked), and `writePrivateFile` is in `core/durable_file.ts:120`.\n52-- Sandbox already hides `/run/user/<uid>` from write-mode bwrap commands (`--tmpfs`, `cli/src/sandbox.ts:804-806`), and `/tmp` is a\n53-  fresh tmpfs in both bwrap branches. The read-only branch starts from `--tmpfs /` (`:741-770`). Docker mounts only the workspace.\n54-- XERJ (goose, lexical): `crates/goose/src/acp/transport/mod.rs:184-223` uses an `x-secret-key` header with an `AcpOriginPolicy`,\n55-  but its aux routes use `CorsLayer::allow_origin(Any)`. We take the shared-secret idea and reject any HTTP listener.\n56-\n57-### Design\n58-**Scope decision (D-PF3-1):** v1.3.0 ships **a unix domain socket only, with no TCP, HTTP or WebSocket listener**. The unit asks for an origin check\n59-only \"for any localhost HTTP/WebSocket listener\", so with no such listener there is nothing to check. The acceptance names only the\n60-socket, the token and mode 0600, so it is met in full. A browser cannot open an `AF_UNIX` connection, so DNS rebinding and CSRF have no","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"13d516ed-1373-4e52-aa4e-7757ea885666","timestamp":"2026-11-24T19:42:35.206Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"MT2_TOOL_REGISTRY.released-20261124-pr784-merged\nSB1_PERMISSION_PROFILES.handoff-20261124T121240Z-codex\nready\n1:# PF-3, PF-4, SB-1, MT-2, PA-2: implementation plans (read-only planning pass, 2026-11-24)\n2-\n3-Code read at `origin/release/v1.3.0` = `4ae25a10`, extracted with `git archive`. Nothing was run except the complexity checker's\n4-`measureFunction` against that snapshot and the baseline revision. Every `file:line` below was read at that commit; re-verify it\n5:before editing, because the branch moves. Unit text: `docs/v1.3.0/PLAN.md:46-47` (PF-3, PF-4), `:70` (SB-1), `:76-77` (MT-1, MT-2),\n6:`:110` (PA-2). Gates: `:125-135`. Decisions: D13 `:141`, D22 `:150`. Phases: PF-4, PA-2 and SB-1 are in B; PF-3 and MT-2 are in C (`:116-121`).\n7-\n8-Hard constraints common to all five (from the brief, not repeated per unit): gates G-3 and verification-path protection, managed policy\n9-and the VERIFIED ladder are never weakened. The five critical functions do not grow (`cli/critical-complexity-baseline.json`). Tests use\n10-a throwaway HOME, no network and no live inference (`cli/test/helpers/fixtures.ts:67` `startGateway`, `:179` `makeHome`). New test\n11-files `import \"./helpers/leak_guard.js\"`, and custom servers are registered with `trackResource` (`cli/test/helpers/leak_guard.ts:1-16`).\n12-Children are stopped by pid, and sockets and listeners are closed. Linux x86_64 only, on Node 22 and 24. Each new surface gets docs, a CI-run example\n13-(G-6, pattern `examples/README.md` + `cli/test/examples.test.ts:73` `runScript`), a ledger entry where one exists, and tests that fail when\n14-the guard is removed.\n15-\n16-Live claims seen on 2026-11-24 (`$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims`, re-check before every slice):\n17-`cli/src/index.ts`, `config.ts`, `doctor.ts` (Codex, `codex/p10-02-elapsed-budget`); `core/operation_runner.ts` (Codex,\n18-`codex/pa3-token-budget-accounting`); `agent.ts`, `types.ts`, `core/run_turn.ts`, `core/spine_handlers.ts`, `core/agent_support.ts`,\n19-`core/operation_runner_execution.ts`, `core/scheduler.ts`, `core/verify.ts`, `core/turn.ts`; tests `examples.test.ts`,\n20-`context_convergence.test.ts`, `operation_schema.test.ts`, `operation_concurrency.test.ts`, `harness.test.ts`; `examples/operation/isolate.json`;\n21-`core/src/bin/nexus_tui/live_view.rs`; `docs/v1.3.0/PLAN.md`; `CHANGELOG.md`. **Not claimed then:** `sidecar.ts`, `protocol.ts`, `sandbox.ts`,\n22-`sandbox_network.ts`, `tools.ts`, `repl.ts`, `core/dispatch_tool_call.ts`, `core/spine.ts`, `core/capabilities.ts`, `core/operation_git.ts`,\n23-`core/operation.ts`, `cli/package.json`, `scripts/*.sh`.\n24-\n25----\n26-\n27:## PF-3: transport beyond a parent's stdio (unix socket, token, attach and reattach)\n28-\n29-**Acceptance (verbatim):** \"a second client attaches to a running session; a wrong token is refused; the socket is mode 0600\".\n30-Unit text: \"a unix domain socket (default) with a token and origin check for any localhost HTTP/WebSocket listener (reference: goose\n31-`acp/transport/auth.rs`, constant-time compare); several clients may attach and reattach\".\n32-\n33-### What exists (read)\n34-- `SidecarServer` (`cli/src/sidecar.ts:106`) drives one `ApplicationCore` and writes every event through one `write` callback\n35-  (`SidecarOptions.write`, `:89-103`; `emit` → `formatSafeSidecarEvent` → `encodeEvent`, `:1362-1365`). Its state is per process, apart from\n36-  negotiation, which is per connection: `negotiated` (`:148`), and `initialize` (`:315-331`) refuses a second `initialize` with BAD_REQUEST.\n37-- Approvals: `requestApproval`/`openApproval` queue one at a time and emit `approval.request` with id `approval-N` (`:860-891`).\n38-  `resolveApproval` with `always: true` sets `alwaysApprove`, switches the mode to `auto` and re-emits `session.state` (`:893-908`, grant at\n39-  `:899-904`). So today any writer to the sidecar's stdin can grant allow-always.\n40-- `hello` and the first `session.state` are emitted once, in `start()` (`:170-196`). `emitSessionState` is private (`:1335-1360`).\n41-- Process entry `main` (`:1529-1625`): its own commander, the client lease, pending-restore recovery, `buildConfig`, and stdin through\n42-  `readline` with **no line cap** (`:1615-1618`, and `docs/PROTOCOL.md` ~`:42` \"sets no limit on the length of a line it reads\"). EOF\n43-  on stdin means shutdown (`:1619-1623`). Guarded by `isEntryPoint` (`:1628-1643`).\n44-- Protocol: `PROTOCOL_VERSION=1`, range `:13-22`, `SIDECAR_CAPABILITIES` `:34-55`, `EXPERIMENTAL_FEATURES=[]` `:62`, `ErrorCode` `:76`,\n45-  `SidecarCommand` `:257-288`, `parseCommand` `:305`. Schema `docs/protocol/sidecar-v1.schema.json` + ledger `docs/protocol/VERSIONS.json`\n46-  (additive changes keep protocol 1 with a note, `docs/protocol/README.md` \"Recording a version decision\"). `docs/PROTOCOL.md:9-15` states\n47:  \"No socket or network transport ... (planned as PF-3)\".\n48-- Reusable pieces: `BoundedLineReader` (`cli/src/acp/jsonrpc.ts:34-103`, cap and oversized reporting), `ACP_MAX_LINE_BYTES=4 MiB` and\n49-  `ACP_MAX_OVERSIZED_LINES=3` (`acp/types.ts:97-99`), `ACP_PERMISSION_TIMEOUT_SECS=600` (`acp/types.ts:120`), and the ACP refusal of auto\n50-  approval at startup (`index.ts:1526-1539`, `acpStartupRefusal`). The private-dir and `lstat` pattern is in `core/client_lease.ts`\n51-  (`clientLeasePath`: `/tmp/nexus-client-leases-<uid>`, 0700, lstat-checked), and `writePrivateFile` is in `core/durable_file.ts:120`.\n52-- Sandbox already hides `/run/user/<uid>` from write-mode bwrap commands (`--tmpfs`, `cli/src/sandbox.ts:804-806`), and `/tmp` is a\n53-  fresh tmpfs in both bwrap branches. The read-only branch starts from `--tmpfs /` (`:741-770`). Docker mounts only the workspace.\n54-- XERJ (goose, lexical): `crates/goose/src/acp/transport/mod.rs:184-223` uses an `x-secret-key` header with an `AcpOriginPolicy`,\n55-  but its aux routes use `CorsLayer::allow_origin(Any)`. We take the shared-secret idea and reject any HTTP listener.\n56-\n57-### Design\n58-**Scope decision (D-PF3-1):** v1.3.0 ships **a unix domain socket only, with no TCP, HTTP or WebSocket listener**. The unit asks for an origin check\n59-only \"for any localhost HTTP/WebSocket listener\", so with no such listener there is nothing to check. The acceptance names only the\n60-socket, the token and mode 0600, so it is met in full. A browser cannot open an `AF_UNIX` connection, so DNS rebinding and CSRF have no","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c9a2ebb9-14f3-459e-8e43-879b68677a80","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"main","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
