e, a pre-existing symlink or regular file at the socket path, another uid's directory (simulate by mode/ownership checks you can do without root, or document), cleanup after shutdown, stdio mode unchanged.\n\nRules: new test files start with `import \"./helpers/leak_guard.js\";`. Run one test file at a time: `cd /home/mike/nexus-wt/pf3/cli && TMPDIR=/dev/shm HOME=$(mktemp -d) node --import tsx --test test/<name>.test.ts 2>&1 | tail -30` (throwaway HOME is mandatory; never read the real ~/.nexus, ~/.config/nexus, /etc/nexus). No network and no inference runs. Stop processes only by their own pid, never `pkill -f`. Shell is zsh (`bash -c` for loops), output passes through `rtk` (prefix `rtk proxy` if it looks cut); a safety check blocks scripts containing `rm`. `cli/node_modules` is a symlink; Rust binaries are in `core/target/release/`. Before each commit: `git fetch origin` and `git log origin/release/v1.3.0..HEAD` for foreign commits; merge origin/release/v1.3.0 in (never rebase). At the end run: `npx tsc --noEmit -p .` in `cli/`, the complexity gate, `node scripts/check_invariants.mjs`, `node scripts/check_doc_versions.mjs`, `leak_guard`, `sidecar`, `protocol_parity`, `protocol_schema`, `examples`, your new files three times each. The host is loaded; timing-sensitive existing tests may flake, rerun alone before concluding.\n\nReport under 450 words: files and commits (hashes), design decisions beyond the plan, tests with counts and the mutation that fails each, what the socket cannot protect against (same-uid processes, an unsandboxed model command that reads the token file: say so plainly), protocol/ledger changes, anything left open."}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011ChNKk1sH8zhRGGyvPuwB5","requestRef":"647e284a-ace9-4597-b69f-94d9ffbeac54","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"b2f8f20b-0238-4138-9b71-0039f9e600d1","timestamp":"2026-11-24T19:42:51.121Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"mediu