{"parentUuid":"c6c5095d-f3a2-40c8-8708-20c41540df3d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNKmtfFhqBRQcTugbjkm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Back after the usage reset. Codex and Cursor kept merging while I was out, so several units moved without me. One new unit is now being built.\n\n**Merged on `release/v1.3.0` while I was out:**\n- #780 (BG-1 detached runs), #782 (HK-1 hooks), #784 (MT-2 slice 1), #785 (PA-2), #787 (PA-1), #789 (PA-3) and #793 (PA-4 spec validation).\n- #782 landed at 18:03Z after a third review round and a nested-launcher fix. My record has no fourth independent re-review of its final head, so I still owe that check. I've asked in the claims log that whoever ran it record it.\n\n**In flight with others:** Codex has the fix for the #779 example that approves any verifier request. Cursor has HK-2 and the readiness-inventory refresh (#792).\n\n**Mine now:** I claimed PF-3 (the unix-socket transport) and started an implementer in `~/nexus-wt/pf3`. It commits locally only; I review before anything is pushed. Its plan rules out allow-always and auto over the socket, requires a wrong token to be refused, and requires mode 0600 on the socket.\n\n**Still unclaimed:** BG-2, HK-3, SB-1 slices 2–3 and MT-2 slices 2–4. I'll claim BG-2 and MT-2 next, logging each first.\n\nThe readiness inventory on the release branch is out of date (it was measured on 11-23). I'll re-measure it before cutting an RC, so the merge to `main` and the release have not started."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1177,"cache_read_input_tokens":188557,"output_tokens":522,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1177,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_ge