{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-11-24T19:57:38.551Z","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>af7235dbcad738773</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01BG4YgcKkZGXohcbasKDqsm</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666/tasks/af7235dbcad738773.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Implement PF-3 control socket\" is waiting on its own background work</summary>\n<note>This agent stopped with background work of its own still running. It may resume on its own when that work completes or reports, and the same task-id notifies again if it does; the result below may be interim.</note>\n<result>The mutation run is still going, and the unit isn't finished. Here is where it stands.\n\n**Done and committed**\n- Commit 1 is `b12eb255f`. It has the transport core:\n  - `cli/src/session_socket.ts` holds the hub: attach handshake, roles, caps, and the `listeningLine` helper.\n  - `cli/src/core/socket_files.ts` holds the private directory, token, stale-socket and descriptor code.\n  - The three new error codes (`UNAUTHORIZED`, `NOT_CONTROLLER`, `NOT_PERMITTED`) are in `protocol.ts`, `acp/mapping.ts`, the regenerated schema, a new `VERSIONS.json` entry and the `PROTOCOL.md` error table.\n  - `cli/test/session_socket.test.ts` has 28 tests, which pass in three consecutive runs. The 19 mutations I ran against `session_socket.ts` and `socket_files.ts` were all caught by a test except two.\n  - The two uncaught mutations were redundant guards. One was the symlink `isDirectory` check, already implied by `lstat`. The other was the hex pattern, since `timingSafeEqual` already rejects those values.\n  - I added a prefix-token test after a first mutation survived.\n\n**Written but not yet committed (commit 2 and part of 3)**\n- `sidecar.ts`: new `--listen` option, `attachSnapshot()`, and `pendingApproval.event`. It prints a `listening` line on stdout, refuses auto approval, and cleans up on exit, SIGTERM and SIGINT.\n- `cli/test/sidecar_socket.test.ts`: 8 tests, which pass in three consecutive runs.\n- `docs/PROTOCOL.md` \"Socket transport\" section, `examples/attach/`, a test appended to `cli/test/examples.test.ts`, and the CHANGELOG entry.\n\n**Still to do**\n- Wait for the sidecar mutation run (`run2.py`) to finish and confirm `sidecar.ts` was restored.\n- Run the `examples` test, which I deliberately held back because it uses `sidecar.ts` while the mutations are rewriting it.\n- Fetch origin, check for foreign commits, and make commits 2 and 3 as separate commits.\n- Run the full gate list: `tsc`, complexity gate, invariants, doc versions, `leak_guard`, `sidecar`, `protocol_parity`, `protocol_schema`, `examples`, and each new file three times.\n\n**Design decisions beyond the plan**\n- The flag is `--listen` on the existing sidecar, not a new `nexus serve` command.\n- Stdio remains the owner of the process. Socket clients are additional, and EOF on stdin still shuts the sidecar down.\n- `attach`, `attached` and `listening` are not in the `SidecarCommand`/`SidecarEvent` unions. The Rust parity test requires a hand-written Rust variant for each union member, so putting them there would force a Rust change. They are documented as transport lines instead, and only the error codes are in the schema.\n- `approve` with `always` is refused with `NOT_PERMITTED` rather than downgraded to once, and the approval stays open.\n- Every `slash` command is refused, as are `shutdown`, `model.select`, `models.list` and `provider.*`.\n- Per-connection `initialize` is answered by the hub, so `sidecar.ts` has no `negotiate()` change.\n- The 600-second approval timeout is dropped, because the stdio owner always exists.\n- A stale-socket sweep runs at start and removes only dead `s-*.sock` sockets owned by this uid.\n\n**What the socket cannot protect against**\n- A same-uid process, or unconfined model-driven code, that can read the 0600 descriptor can attach.\n- Root can always attach.\n- Node cannot read `SO_PEERCRED`, so the 0700 directory is the boundary.\n- libuv unlinks the bound path when the server closes, even if someone replaced the file there.\n\n**Open**\n- The bwrap mask of the socket directory is not done, and the claim in `PROTOCOL.md` that `/run/user/&lt;uid&gt;` is hidden from sandboxed commands is not yet verified against `sandbox.ts`.\n- Slow-observer drop has no test.\n- The other-uid directory check can only be tested with a stand-in uid, since I can't chown without root.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>207990</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>52</tool_uses><duration_ms>885164</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
