{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-11-24T19:58:26.752Z","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>af7235dbcad738773</task-id>\n<output-file>/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666/tasks/af7235dbcad738773.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Implement PF-3 control socket\" is waiting on its own background work</summary>\n<note>This agent stopped with background work of its own still running. It may resume on its own when that work completes or reports, and the same task-id notifies again if it does; the result below may be interim.</note>\n<result>The sidecar mutation rerun is in the background, and I'm waiting for it to finish. I can't run the `examples` test or commit until it does, because both depend on `sidecar.ts` being unmutated.\n\nThe unit is not finished. Commit 1 is in (`b12eb255f`). The sidecar wiring, protocol docs, example and CHANGELOG entry are written but uncommitted.\n\n**Verified so far**\n- `session_socket.test.ts`: 28 tests, passing across three consecutive runs.\n- `sidecar_socket.test.ts`: 8 tests, passing across three consecutive runs.\n- `cli/src/sidecar.ts` is intact: `tsc` is clean and the `--listen` auto-approval refusal is still there.\n\n**One finding from the first mutation run**\nWhen I removed the `--listen` auto-approval refusal, the test hung until its 300-second timeout instead of failing. The mutated sidecar kept running and the test waited on its exit forever. I killed the leftover process by pid. The guard is still caught, as a hang rather than a failure. The rerun now treats a timeout as a catch and cleans up by pid.\n\n**Still to do**\n- Read the rerun results and confirm which sidecar mutations are caught.\n- Run `examples.test.ts` for the new `attach` example.\n- Check for foreign commits on `origin/release/v1.3.0`, then make commits 2 and 3 separately.\n- Run the full gate list, with each new test file three times.\n\n**Still open**\n- The bubblewrap mask of the socket directory is not done. The `PROTOCOL.md` claim that `/run/user/&lt;uid&gt;` is hidden from sandboxed commands is not yet checked against `sandbox.ts`.\n- There is no test for dropping a slow observer.\n- The other-uid directory check uses a stand-in uid, since I can't chown without root.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>214394</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>56</tool_uses><duration_ms>933321</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
