{"parentUuid":"e55c4b73-668a-45b7-b7c3-394ce62fe8fc","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNNPw2cTYSiA4aR67WDX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PM7BAFDFcDQuPS3E6d5z6a","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-wt/pf3 && git fetch -q origin && git merge -q origin/release/v1.3.0 --no-edit 2>&1 | tail -2; git push -q -u origin v1/pf3-control-socket 2>&1 | tail -1; git log --oneline -1 | cut -c1-70; echo \"remote $(git ls-remote origin refs/heads/v1/pf3-control-socket | cut -c1-8) local $(git rev-parse --short=8 HEAD)\"; cat > /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/pr_pf3.md <<'EOF'\nPlan unit PF-3: a second client can attach to a running sidecar over a unix domain socket. Acceptance: \"a second client attaches to a running session; a wrong token is refused; the socket is mode 0600\".\n\n## What it adds\n\n- `nexus` sidecar option `--listen`: off by default, and with it absent the stdio behaviour is unchanged. With it, the sidecar prints one machine-readable `listening` line and accepts further clients on a socket in a private directory (0700, lstat-checked) with a random token in a 0600 descriptor file.\n- **Roles:** one controller (may prompt, answer approvals, interrupt) and any number of observers (read-only). A second controller is refused while one is attached; a controller may reattach after disconnecting. An open approval is replayed to a client that attaches.\n- **What a socket client can never do:** grant allow-always, switch to auto, run slash commands, shut down, select models or providers. `--listen` refuses auto approval at startup. Managed policy is unchanged.\n- **Guards:** token compared in constant time and checked before any command is parsed; line and connection caps (`BoundedLineReader`); stale-socket sweep removes only dead sockets of this uid; cleanup on exit, SIGTERM and SIGINT.\n- Three error codes (`UNAUTHORIZED`, `NOT_CONTROLLER`, `NOT_PERMITTED`) in the protocol schema and ledger. `attach`/`attached`/`listening` are documented transport lines, not members of the command/event unions (the Rust parity test requires a Rust variant for each union member).\n- Docs (`docs/PROTOCOL.md` \"Socket transport\"), a runnable example `examples/attach/` run by `examples.test.ts`, CHANGELOG entry.\n\n## What it cannot protect against (stated in the docs)\n\nA same-uid process, or unconfined model-driven code, that can read the 0600 descriptor can attach; root can. Node cannot read `SO_PEERCRED`, so the 0700 directory is the boundary. Not done: bubblewrap masking of the socket directory; a test for dropping a slow observer; a real other-uid check (no root here).\n\n## Tests\n\n`session_socket` 28, `sidecar_socket` 8, plus the attach example in `examples`. 19 mutations of the transport and 4 of the sidecar wiring were each caught (two redundant guards excepted; one wiring mutation is caught as a timeout rather than a failure). Locally, Node 24: those two files, `protocol_parity` 5, `protocol_schema` 8, `leak_guard` 6, `tsc` clean. An independent review is requested before merge.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\nEOF\ncd ~/nexus-code && u=$(gh pr create --base release/v1.3.0 --head v1/pf3-control-socket --title \"feat(sidecar): unix-socket transport with token, controller and observers (PF-3)\" --body-file /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/pr_pf3.md | tail -1); echo \"$u\"; echo \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ) PR (claude-invariants-audit): $u PF-3 opened; independent security review running; DO NOT MERGE until it is posted.\" >> \"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log\"","description":"Push PF-3, open its PR and log that it awaits review"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":667,"cache_read_input_tokens":197715,"output_tokens":1611,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":101},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":667,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1611,"cache_read_input_tokens":197715,"cache_creation_input_tokens":667,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":667},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":9343,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01PM7BAFDFcDQuPS3E6d5z6a":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-wt/pf3 && git fetch -q origin && git merge -q origin/release/v1.3.0 --no-edit 2>&1 | tail -2; git push -q -u origin v1/pf3-control-socket 2>&1 | tail -1; git log --oneline -1 | cut -c1-70; echo \"remote $(git ls-remote origin refs/heads/v1/pf3-control-socket | cut -c1-8) local $(git rev-parse --short=8 HEAD)\"; cat > /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/pr_pf3.md <<'EOF'\nPlan unit PF-3: a second client can attach to a running sidecar over a unix domain socket. Acceptance: \"a second client attaches to a running session; a wrong token is refused; the socket is mode 0600\".\n\n## What it adds\n\n- `nexus` sidecar option `--listen`: off by default, and with it absent the stdio behaviour is unchanged. With it, the sidecar prints one machine-readable `listening` line and accepts further clients on a socket in a private directory (0700, lstat-checked) with a random token in a 0600 descriptor file.\n- **Roles:** one controller (may prompt, answer approvals, interrupt) and any number of observers (read-only). A second controller is refused while one is attached; a controller may reattach after disconnecting. An open approval is replayed to a client that attaches.\n- **What a socket client can never do:** grant allow-always, switch to auto, run slash commands, shut down, select models or providers. `--listen` refuses auto approval at startup. Managed policy is unchanged.\n- **Guards:** token compared in constant time and checked before any command is parsed; line and connection caps (`BoundedLineReader`); stale-socket sweep removes only dead sockets of this uid; cleanup on exit, SIGTERM and SIGINT.\n- Three error codes (`UNAUTHORIZED`, `NOT_CONTROLLER`, `NOT_PERMITTED`) in the protocol schema and ledger. `attach`/`attached`/`listening` are documented transport lines, not members of the command/event unions (the Rust parity test requires a Rust variant for each union member).\n- Docs (`docs/PROTOCOL.md` \"Socket transport\"), a runnable example `examples/attach/` run by `examples.test.ts`, CHANGELOG entry.\n\n## What it cannot protect against (stated in the docs)\n\nA same-uid process, or unconfined model-driven code, that can read the 0600 descriptor can attach; root can. Node cannot read `SO_PEERCRED`, so the 0700 directory is the boundary. Not done: bubblewrap masking of the socket directory; a test for dropping a slow observer; a real other-uid check (no root here).\n\n## Tests\n\n`session_socket` 28, `sidecar_socket` 8, plus the attach example in `examples`. 19 mutations of the transport and 4 of the sidecar wiring were each caught (two redundant guards excepted; one wiring mutation is caught as a timeout rather than a failure). Locally, Node 24: those two files, `protocol_parity` 5, `protocol_schema` 8, `leak_guard` 6, `tsc` clean. An independent review is requested before merge.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\nEOF\ncd ~/nexus-code && u=$(gh pr create --base release/v1.3.0 --head v1/pf3-control-socket --title \"feat(sidecar): unix-socket transport with token, controller and observers (PF-3)\" --body-file /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/pr_pf3.md | tail -1); echo \"$u\"; echo \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ) PR (claude-invariants-audit): $u PF-3 opened; independent security review running; DO NOT MERGE until it is posted.\" >> \"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log\"","description":"Push PF-3, open its PR and log that it awaits review"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011ChNNPvrCBQUR5motXoZ2y","requestRef":"4d618628-bee1-4fb8-8d86-f1b73d3ea7a0","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"4895ea48-6a68-4343-8dc0-0e3d99713878","timestamp":"2026-11-24T20:17:34.518Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"main","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
