{"parentUuid":"3249abb9-1e14-4d91-a88d-8264d99901e3","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"73d4db91-5979-4604-9d87-ffa0509a3208","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011URXaqpzGXkJEERGMuCXRT","type":"tool_result","content":"797 v1/pf3-control-socket feat(sidecar): unix-socket transport with token, controller \n796 v1/hk2-plugin-manifest feat(plugins): HK-2 local-path install, verify, and manifest\n795 v1/sb1-profiles feat(sandbox): wire SB-1 named profiles into config, doctor,\n22e9145f2 docs(mq4): record passing scheduled conformance run\n84fba37bd docs(evidence): MQ-4 first scheduled run, not conformant (lead-reasoning edit_file 5/50 reproduces)\n3a9fdebb9 feat(eval): scheduled gateway conformance job with claim protocol and alert path (MQ-4)\n1:# BG-1 + BG-2 plan: detached runner and unattended schedules (read-only planning pass)\n2-\n3-Status: PLAN, 2026-11-24, written read-only against `origin/release/v1.3.0` at `4ae25a10` (snapshot extracted with `git archive`; nothing in the repo was edited). Unit rows: `docs/v1.3.0/PLAN.md:83-85`; principle 4 (\"Unattended \n4-\n5-Acceptance (verbatim):\n6-- **BG-1:** \"kill the CLI, the run continues and resumes cleanly; the SI-7 kill test passes against the runner\"\n7:- **BG-2:** \"a scheduled run on a seeded failing verifier ends BLOCKED and says so; an unattended run asking for approval is denied, not blocked forever; missed runs are reported, not silently skipped\"\n8-- **G-4:** \"Unattended runs: tests show no allow-always, a fresh worktree, the unattended flag in receipts, and a kill-and-resume pass\"\n9-\n10:Defaults taken (owner authorised autonomous decisions; recorded below): **D15** = documented `systemd --user` unit only, no self-daemonizing mode. **D19** = `read-only` by default, `worktree-write` per schedule (and per job) on\n11-\n12-## 0. What exists (read, with citations)\n13-\n14-- **Durable operations are the unit a runner should own.** `nexus operation run|resume|decide|status|watch` (`cli/src/operation_cli.ts:299-581`). `run` validates the spec (`validateOperationSpec`, `:107`; unknown keys rejected,\n15-- **Fresh worktrees exist.** `planOperationGit(workspace, operationId, baseRef)` (`cli/src/core/operation_git.ts:62-86`) puts every isolated operation under `<repo>/.nexus/worktrees/op-<key>/` with an integration branch `nexus/\n16-- **Driver lock and stale-driver detection.** `OperationStore.acquire` (`cli/src/core/operation_runner_persistence.ts:202-242`) writes `{pid, host, at}` with `wx`; `judgeLock` (`:244-264`) calls a lock stale when the host match\n17-- **Pid + start time precedent.** `startedAt(pid)` reads field 22 of `/proc/<pid>/stat` (`cli/src/core/verify_service.ts:157-165`); `descendants()` walks `ps -A -o pid=,ppid=` (`:139-154`); the fork runner signals every remembe\n18-- **Kernel-owned locks.** `acquireFileGuard` (`cli/src/core/file_guard.ts`, header `:1`, contract comment above the export): `flock(1)` on an O_NOFOLLOW/O_EXCL 0600 file, owner and mode validated (`:16-24`), returns null on con\n19-- **SI-7 kill test.** `cli/test/fault_kill_mid_tool_call.test.ts:1-187`: a driver child runs a one-unit operation whose tool appends to a counter and sleeps; SIGKILL; a fresh driver recovers the unit as BLOCKED/`INTERRUPTED` wi\n20-- **Headless approvals already fail closed.** With no `onConfirm`, a call that needs a decision is DENIED with `DECISION_REQUIRED_NO_OPERATOR` and the turn ends BLOCKED/`NEEDS_INPUT` with one recorded question (`cli/src/core/di\n21-- **\"Always\" exists only in front ends.** Sidecar `alwaysApprove` (`cli/src/sidecar.ts:111,741,861,869,900`), REPL `a`/`always` (`cli/src/repl.ts:622`), managed clamp `clampAlwaysApproval` (`cli/src/core/managed_policy.ts:723-7\n22-- **Operator verifier needs no approval; a discovered one does.** Configured `authoritativeVerifierCommand` baseline (`cli/src/core/completion_oracle.ts:199-212`); a discovered verifier goes through `ensureVerifierApprovedImpl`\n23-- **P10 budgets.** `ContinuationBudget` (`cli/src/types.ts:170-193`): `maxTotalSteps`, `maxToolInvocations`, `maxInferenceSubmissions` are objective-wide across resumes; `maxTurnMinutes` bounds one invocation. Hard caps `MAX_*`\n24-- **Trust is exact-path.** `isWorkspaceTrusted` = env `NEXUS_TRUST_WORKSPACE=1` (unless managed policy disables it) or the real path listed in `~/.config/nexus/trusted_workspaces.json` (`cli/src/workspace_trust.ts:41-81`). A fr\n25-- **Managed policy.** `managedPolicy()` frozen per process (`cli/src/core/policy_runtime.ts:99-109`), `requireManagedPolicyAtStartup` (`:115-123`, called at `index.ts:1555`), `clampApprovalSettings` (`:167-171`), `humanRequirem\n26-- **Private files.** `ensurePrivateDir` (0700, `cli/src/core/durable_file.ts:86`), `writePrivateFile` (atomic, 0600, `:120`). Task state root: `NEXUS_STATE_DIR` or `~/.nexus` (`cli/src/core/state.ts:350-355`).\n27-- **Run contract.** `RUN_RESULT_SCHEMA_VERSION = 1` (`cli/src/run_contract.ts:17`), ledger `docs/protocol/RUN_RESULT_VERSIONS.json`; schema generators share `cli/scripts/result_schema.mjs` (e.g. `gen_policy_schema.mjs`).\n28:- **Nothing background exists.** `docs/releases/v1.3.0-READINESS.md`: \"BG-1 / BG-2 | Open | No detached runner / schedule CLI\"; G-4 \"Open until BG-1/BG-2 land\". No sidecar/daemon fits: the sidecar is bound to its parent's stdin\n29-\n30-## 1. Shared design (designed once; the slice that introduces each part is named)\n31-\n32-### 1.1 Process model (answers \"what owns a detached run\")\n33-\n34-Three processes, all plain `nexus` invocations so every one gets the real startup sequence (state-restore recovery, client lease, `loadEnvironment`, managed policy: `index.ts:83-131,1555`):\n35-\n36:1. **Runner** `nexus runner serve` (foreground, never forks itself away). D15: it is meant to run as the `systemd --user` unit `nexus-runner.service`; outside systemd the operator may run it under any supervisor. One runner per\n37-2. **Worker** `nexus job __worker <job-id>` (hidden subcommand), one per running job, spawned by the runner with `detached: true` (own session/process group), stdout → `/dev/null`, stderr → the job's `stderr.log`. It holds \n38-3. **Client** `nexus job …` / `nexus schedule …`: writes requests, reads records, tails logs. Killing it has no effect on any job (the acceptance case).\n39-\n40-Rejected: re-parenting the sidecar (stdin-bound, one client); a self-daemonizing double fork (D15 default says no; the supervisor is systemd's job); running jobs in the runner's own process (one job's process-global state, cons\n41-\n42-**Systemd unit** (written by `nexus runner install-unit`, never auto-enabled):\n43-\n44-```\n45-[Unit]\n46-Description=Nexus Code detached job runner\n47-[Service]\n48-Type=simple\n49-ExecStart=<absolute path of the resolved nexus launcher> runner serve\n50-Restart=on-failure\n51-RestartSec=5\n52-UMask=0077\n53-NoNewPrivileges=yes\n54-TimeoutStopSec=60\n55-[Install]\n56-WantedBy=default.target\n57-```\n58-\n--\n78-| `R/jobs/<job-id>/receipt.json` | runner | 0600 | the job receipt (§1.7) |","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"6a4259d5-b5c7-46fa-8dc5-1829bf918e68","timestamp":"2026-11-24T20:18:24.110Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"797 v1/pf3-control-socket feat(sidecar): unix-socket transport with token, controller \n796 v1/hk2-plugin-manifest feat(plugins): HK-2 local-path install, verify, and manifest\n795 v1/sb1-profiles feat(sandbox): wire SB-1 named profiles into config, doctor,\n22e9145f2 docs(mq4): record passing scheduled conformance run\n84fba37bd docs(evidence): MQ-4 first scheduled run, not conformant (lead-reasoning edit_file 5/50 reproduces)\n3a9fdebb9 feat(eval): scheduled gateway conformance job with claim protocol and alert path (MQ-4)\n1:# BG-1 + BG-2 plan: detached runner and unattended schedules (read-only planning pass)\n2-\n3-Status: PLAN, 2026-11-24, written read-only against `origin/release/v1.3.0` at `4ae25a10` (snapshot extracted with `git archive`; nothing in the repo was edite