{"parentUuid":"dd51ecc8-c0fe-48fa-9d2d-8948c8182a59","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNNV3E4YfW3cvo6p8r6L","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KH8auHoAoyAkpRwLuCW2Va","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Implement BG-2 schedules","subagent_type":"general-purpose","prompt":"Implement unit BG-2 (unattended schedules on top of the merged BG-1 detached runner) in the worktree /home/mike/nexus-wt/bg2 (branch `v1/bg2-schedules`, based on `origin/release/v1.3.0`; Nexus Code, TypeScript CLI in `cli/`). Read first: `/home/mike/nexus-wt/_plans/BG_PLAN.md` (BG-2 sections and the shared design; written BEFORE BG-1 was merged, so re-verify against what BG-1 actually built: `docs/RUNNER.md`, `cli/src/core/job_runner.ts`, `job_worker.ts`, `job_receipt.ts`, `runner_store.ts`, and the `nexus job`/`nexus runner` commands in `cli/src/index.ts`), `/home/mike/nexus-wt/bg2/AGENTS.md`, `docs/v1.3.0/PLAN.md` (BG-2, gates G-3, G-4, G-6). Acceptance verbatim: \"a scheduled run on a seeded failing verifier ends BLOCKED and says so; an unattended run asking for approval is denied, not blocked forever; missed runs are reported, not silently skipped\". G-4: \"tests show no allow-always, a fresh worktree, the unattended flag in receipts, and a kill-and-resume pass\".\n\nDesign per the plan: schedules are cron / every / once (decision D21 default in the plan), stored privately (0700/0600, the runner's existing store conventions), fire jobs through the SAME path as `nexus job` (so every unattended rule BG-1 enforces applies: read-only by default, a fresh worktree, no auto, no allow-always, bounded auto-resumes), never a second execution path. A schedule cannot widen what a job may do: its permission level is fixed at creation by the operator and is subject to managed policy; a schedule created inside an untrusted workspace is refused; an agent/model-driven command must not be able to create or edit a schedule that grants write access (check how BG-1 protects its store paths from the agent's file tools: use the same mechanism and add the schedules file to the protected paths if BG-1 did that for its files; add a test that the agent's own write tools cannot create/modify a schedule). Missed runs (runner was down, host asleep, previous run still active, clock jump) are recorded and reported by `nexus schedule list/status` and in the next run's receipt, never silently skipped and never replayed as a burst: define the catch-up policy (default: report all missed, run at most one catch-up, configurable to skip-with-report), overlap policy (default: skip with a recorded 'overlap' miss), and clock-step handling, and document them. A scheduled run on a seeded failing verifier ends BLOCKED and the receipt/status says so; an unattended approval request is denied (not left waiting): prove both end to end against the scripted gateway helper (`cli/test/helpers/fixtures.ts` `startGateway`, `makeHome`), no live inference, no network.\n\nCommands: `nexus schedule add|list|status|remove|pause|resume` (plus `run-now` for tests if the plan has it), JSON output option consistent with `nexus job`. Keep `cli/src/index.ts` changes to command registration only; put the logic in new files (`cli/src/core/schedule_*.ts`, `cli/src/schedule_cli.ts`). The five critical functions in `cli/critical-complexity-baseline.json` must not grow. Receipts: add the schedule id/occurrence/missed info to the job receipt additively following the run-contract ledger rules (`docs/protocol/RUN_RESULT_VERSIONS.json`, `cli/scripts/result_schema.mjs`; read how BG-1 versioned its receipt and follow it). Docs: extend `docs/RUNNER.md` (or a new `docs/SCHEDULES.md`), a runnable example under `examples/` run in CI by `cli/test/examples.test.ts` (read how it runs scripts), `docs/USER_MANUAL.md` section, CHANGELOG Unreleased entry. systemd: BG-1 owns `nexus runner install-unit`; do not add a second supervisor path.\n\nDeliver as separate local commits, NOT pushed, no PR: (1) schedule store + parser (cron subset, every, once; strict validation; time zone = UTC unless the plan says otherwise; DST/leap handling documented) + due-time computation with unit tests, (2) runner integration (fire, overlap, missed runs, catch-up, kill-and-resume of a scheduled run) + CLI, (3) acceptance tests (the three acceptance cases + G-4 bullets) + docs/example/CHANGELOG/schema. Hostile tests, each failing when its guard is removed (mutate a copy of the file and restore from the copy; never `git checkout` to undo): schedule file tampering/other-uid ownership/symlink at the store path, an agent write tool creating a schedule, a schedule requesting write in an untrusted workspace, allow-always never reachable, a missed-run burst not replayed, overlap, clock step backwards, invalid cron strings, huge schedule counts (cap), a schedule pointing at a path outside the workspace.\n\nRules: new test files start with `import \"./helpers/leak_guard.js\";`. Run one test file at a time: `cd /home/mike/nexus-wt/bg2/cli && TMPDIR=/dev/shm HOME=$(mktemp -d) node --import tsx --test test/<name>.test.ts 2>&1 | tail -30` (throwaway HOME mandatory; never read the real ~/.nexus, ~/.config/nexus, /etc/nexus; no network, no live inference). Stop processes only by their own pid, never `pkill -f`; leave no runner or worker processes behind (the leak guard and your own cleanup). Shell is zsh (`bash -c` for loops); output passes through `rtk` (prefix `rtk proxy` if it looks cut); a safety check blocks scripts containing `rm`. `cli/node_modules` is a symlink; Rust binaries are in `core/target/release/`. Before each commit: `git fetch origin`, `git log origin/release/v1.3.0..HEAD` for foreign commits, merge origin/release/v1.3.0 in (never rebase). Note other agents are active in `cli/src/index.ts`, `docs/PROTOCOL.md`, CHANGELOG: merge often to avoid conflicts. At the end run `npx tsc --noEmit -p .` in `cli/`, the complexity gate, `node scripts/check_invariants.mjs`, `node scripts/check_doc_versions.mjs`, `leak_guard`, the BG-1 test files (find them: `ls cli/test | grep -iE \"runner|job\"`), `fault_kill_mid_tool_call`, `examples`, `protocol_schema`, and every new file three times. The host is loaded; timing-sensitive tests may flake: rerun alone before concluding.\n\nReport under 450 words: commits (hashes), the policies you chose (catch-up, overlap, time zone, caps), tests with counts and the mutation that fails each, what a schedule cannot protect against, schema/ledger changes, anything left open or any BG-1 defect you found (do not fix BG-1 in this branch: report it)."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1129,"cache_read_input_tokens":206181,"output_tokens":2578,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1129,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2578,"cache_read_input_tokens":206181,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1129,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1129},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":17373,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01KH8auHoAoyAkpRwLuCW2Va":{"description":"Implement BG-2 schedules","subagent_type":"general-purpose","prompt":"Implement unit BG-2 (unattended schedules on top of the merged BG-1 detached runner) in the worktree /home/mike/nexus-wt/bg2 (branch `v1/bg2-schedules`, based on `origin/release/v1.3.0`; Nexus Code, TypeScript CLI in `cli/`). Read first: `/home/mike/nexus-wt/_plans/BG_PLAN.md` (BG-2 sections and the shared design; written BEFORE BG-1 was merged, so re-verify against what BG-1 actually built: `docs/RUNNER.md`, `cli/src/core/job_runner.ts`, `job_worker.ts`, `job_receipt.ts`, `runner_store.ts`, and the `nexus job`/`nexus runner` commands in `cli/src/index.ts`), `/home/mike/nexus-wt/bg2/AGENTS.md`, `docs/v1.3.0/PLAN.md` (BG-2, gates G-3, G-4, G-6). Acceptance verbatim: \"a scheduled run on a seeded failing verifier ends BLOCKED and says so; an unattended run asking for approval is denied, not blocked forever; missed runs are reported, not silently skipped\". G-4: \"tests show no allow-always, a fresh worktree, the unattended flag in receipts, and a kill-and-resume pass\".\n\nDesign per the plan: schedules are cron / every / once (decision D21 default in the plan), stored privately (0700/0600, the runner's existing store conventions), fire jobs through the SAME path as `nexus job` (so every unattended rule BG-1 enforces applies: read-only by default, a fresh worktree, no auto, no allow-always, bounded auto-resumes), never a second execution path. A schedule cannot widen what a job may do: its permission level is fixed at creation by the operator and is subject to managed policy; a schedule created inside an untrusted workspace is refused; an agent/model-driven command must not be able to create or edit a schedule that grants write access (check how BG-1 protects its store paths from the agent's file tools: use the same mechanism and add the schedules file to the protected paths if BG-1 did that for its files; add a test that the agent's own write tools cannot create/modify a schedule). Missed runs (runner was down, host asleep, previous run still active, clock jump) are recorded and reported by `nexus schedule list/status` and in the next run's receipt, never silently skipped and never replayed as a burst: define the catch-up policy (default: report all missed, run at most one catch-up, configurable to skip-with-report), overlap policy (default: skip with a recorded 'overlap' miss), and clock-step handling, and document them. A scheduled run on a seeded failing verifier ends BLOCKED and the receipt/status says so; an unattended approval request is denied (not left waiting): prove both end to end against the scripted gateway helper (`cli/test/helpers/fixtures.ts` `startGateway`, `makeHome`), no live inference, no network.\n\nCommands: `nexus schedule add|list|status|remove|pause|resume` (plus `run-now` for tests if the plan has it), JSON output option consistent with `nexus job`. Keep `cli/src/index.ts` changes to command registration only; put the logic in new files (`cli/src/core/schedule_*.ts`, `cli/src/schedule_cli.ts`). The five critical functions in `cli/critical-complexity-baseline.json` must not grow. Receipts: add the schedule id/occurrence/missed info to the job receipt additively following the run-contract ledger rules (`docs/protocol/RUN_RESULT_VERSIONS.json`, `cli/scripts/result_schema.mjs`; read how BG-1 versioned its receipt and follow it). Docs: extend `docs/RUNNER.md` (or a new `docs/SCHEDULES.md`), a runnable example under `examples/` run in CI by `cli/test/examples.test.ts` (read how it runs scripts), `docs/USER_MANUAL.md` section, CHANGELOG Unreleased entry. systemd: BG-1 owns `nexus runner install-unit`; do not add a second supervisor path.\n\nDeliver as separate local commits, NOT pushed, no PR: (1) schedule store + parser (cron subset, every, once; strict validation; time zone = UTC unless the plan says otherwise; DST/leap handling documented) + due-time computation with unit tests, (2) runner integration (fire, overlap, missed runs, catch-up, kill-and-resume of a scheduled run) + CLI, (3) acceptance tests (the three acceptance cases + G-4 bullets) + docs/example/CHANGELOG/schema. Hostile tests, each failing when its guard is removed (mutate a copy of the file and restore from the copy; never `git checkout` to undo): schedule file tampering/other-uid ownership/symlink at the store path, an agent write tool creating a schedule, a schedule requesting write in an untrusted workspace, allow-always never reachable, a missed-run burst not replayed, overlap, clock step backwards, invalid cron strings, huge schedule counts (cap), a schedule pointing at a path outside the workspace.\n\nRules: new test files start with `import \"./helpers/leak_guard.js\";`. Run one test file at a time: `cd /home/mike/nexus-wt/bg2/cli && TMPDIR=/dev/shm HOME=$(mktemp -d) node --import tsx --test test/<name>.test.ts 2>&1 | tail -30` (throwaway HOME mandatory; never read the real ~/.nexus, ~/.config/nexus, /etc/nexus; no network, no live inference). Stop processes only by their own pid, never `pkill -f`; leave no runner or worker processes behind (the leak guard and your own cleanup). Shell is zsh (`bash -c` for loops); output passes through `rtk` (prefix `rtk proxy` if it looks cut); a safety check blocks scripts containing `rm`. `cli/node_modules` is a symlink; Rust binaries are in `core/target/release/`. Before each commit: `git fetch origin`, `git log origin/release/v1.3.0..HEAD` for foreign commits, merge origin/release/v1.3.0 in (never rebase). Note other agents are active in `cli/src/index.ts`, `docs/PROTOCOL.md`, CHANGELOG: merge often to avoid conflicts. At the end run `npx tsc --noEmit -p .` in `cli/`, the complexity gate, `node scripts/check_invariants.mjs`, `node scripts/check_doc_versions.mjs`, `leak_guard`, the BG-1 test files (find them: `ls cli/test | grep -iE \"runner|job\"`), `fault_kill_mid_tool_call`, `examples`, `protocol_schema`, and every new file three times. The host is loaded; timing-sensitive tests may flake: rerun alone before concluding.\n\nReport under 450 words: commits (hashes), the policies you chose (catch-up, overlap, time zone, caps), tests with counts and the mutation that fails each, what a schedule cannot protect against, schema/ledger changes, anything left open or any BG-1 defect you found (do not fix BG-1 in this branch: report it)."}},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011ChNNV339jFSbYmuJtkXQG","requestRef":"a30f737d-93fe-4d96-8a01-1