{"parentUuid":"33e6aeeb-cc71-486b-8684-667566d98024","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNNX8hH11E5XoY1PbN13","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"PF-3 (the unix-socket transport) is open as #797, and BG-2 (schedules) is claimed and being built. v1.3.0 is still not landed: nothing in this session has been merged, and the merge to `main` and the release have not started.\n\n- **PF-3, #797:** the builder's tests pass when I re-ran them, 28 for the transport and 8 for the sidecar wiring. The type check is clean. An independent security review is running, and #797 stays unmerged until its verdict is posted. The attached-client rules from the plan are in:\n  - a wrong token is refused;\n  - the socket is mode 0600;\n  - one controller plus observers;\n  - no allow-always, auto mode, slash commands or shutdown over the socket.\n- **Open on PF-3:** the claim in the docs that sandboxed commands can't reach `/run/user/<uid>` is not yet checked against `sandbox.ts`. I've asked the reviewer to settle that, because it decides whether a sandboxed or unsandboxed model command could attach as controller.\n- **BG-2:** claimed in the claims log, with an implementer building it in `~/nexus-wt/bg2` on top of the merged BG-1. It commits locally only, and I review before anything is pushed. It must show that:\n  - a scheduled run on a failing verifier ends BLOCKED;\n  - an unattended approval request is denied rather than left waiting;\n  - missed runs are reported, not replayed.\n- **Others:** Codex has SB-1 open as #795 and Cursor has HK-2 open as #796.\n\nStill to do:\n- **Unclaimed:** HK-3 and MT-2 slices 2–4.\n- **HK-1:** I still need to run my own check of the merged HK-1 head, since I have no record of a review of its final version.\n- **Readiness inventory:** it is out of date and needs re-measuring before an RC."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1022,"cache_read_input_tokens":210255,"output_tokens":622,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1022,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":622,"cache_read_input_tokens":210255,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1022,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1022},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011ChNNX8VspoQFS3k3JtZUq","requestRef":"19b24b42-18f0-4e63-8c05-067114d9861f","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"4767d961-c60d-4941-86ce-01b61245ce5e","timestamp":"2026-11-24T20:19:05.992Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"main","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
