{"parentUuid":"dc3ce655-d50b-4d2e-bc0a-a087e5eb96d1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNQWEo6jg3AE48YdZve1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The independent security review of #797 (PF-3) came back request changes at `512d0f9d`. The review is posted on the PR and the fixes are being made on the branch.\n\n**The blocker:** a model command can read the socket token and attach as controller in two cases.\n- **No sandbox**, which is the default.\n- **`--sandbox` with the socket directory outside the two paths the sandbox hides** (`/run/user/<uid>`, `/tmp`), for example under `/var/tmp` or inside the workspace.\n\nA controller can answer approvals, so an approved command could approve later approvals of its own turn. The doc's claim that sandboxed commands can't reach the directory is true only for those two locations.\n\n**Fixes I've sent to the builder:**\n- Mask the real socket directory in the sandbox wherever it is.\n- Refuse `--listen` when the directory is inside the workspace.\n- Say plainly in the docs that without a sandbox a model command can attach.\n- Refuse socket prompts while the session is in auto mode, since the stdio parent can switch to it after startup.\n- Drop or document the extra controller commands.\n- Shorten the idle pre-authentication window.\n\n**What held up in the review, all by running attacks:** token handling, file modes, the second-controller refusal, observer read-only, and refusal of allow-always, slash commands and shutdown over the socket. 28/28 transport tests and the rest of the suites passed. Two mutations survived, both unreachable without root.\n\nSomeone else (the repo owner's account) pushed a one-line doc-test change to the branch after the review, which the reviewer did not cover. Merging stays blocked until the fixes are in and re-reviewed. BG-2 is still building."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3272,"cache_read_input_tokens":214566,"output_tokens":558,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3272,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":558,"cache_read_input_tokens":214566,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3272,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3272},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011ChNQWEdfqAJGMZa7oNzke","requestRef":"ef37ade7-3aad-49b6-b579-cbaad873d10f","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"3b0008c7-6927-4882-ac07-e915f175da21","timestamp":"2026-11-24T20:45:07.539Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"main","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
