{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-11-24T20:55:58.802Z","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>af7235dbcad738773</task-id>\n<output-file>/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666/tasks/af7235dbcad738773.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Implement PF-3 control socket\" is waiting on its own background work</summary>\n<note>This agent stopped with background work of its own still running. It may resume on its own when that work completes or reports, and the same task-id notifies again if it does; the result below may be interim.</note>\n<result>The four review fixes are written, and all nine mutations I ran against them are caught (the workspace-refusal one as a hang). I'm waiting on the full gate run before committing and pushing, so nothing is committed yet. This run replaces the one I stopped earlier.\n\n**What changed**\n- **Sandbox mask (`cli/src/sandbox.ts`):**\n  - New `hideDirectoryFromSandbox` registry and a `hideDirectories` option.\n  - Both bwrap branches mask the directory, and the worker launch inherits the mask. The read-only branch masks it only where its synthetic root could show it (under `$HOME` or inside the workspace). Elsewhere the directory is already absent from that root.\n  - A mask whose directory no longer exists is skipped, because bwrap cannot mount over it.\n- **Sidecar (`cli/src/sidecar.ts`):**\n  - `--listen` registers the socket directory with the sandbox.\n  - It refuses to start when that directory is inside the workspace.\n  - New `socketMayDriveTurns()` is false in auto mode or after allow-always.\n- **Hub (`cli/src/session_socket.ts`):**\n  - While the session approves everything, `prompt.submit` and `steer` get `NOT_PERMITTED`.\n  - `answer` and `checkpoint.choice` are dropped from the controller list. The final list is `prompt.submit`, `steer`, `cancel`, `approve` (once only), `deny`, `receipt`, `tool.detail`.\n  - The attach deadline is now 2 seconds, and at most 4 connections may wait to attach.\n- **Docs (`docs/PROTOCOL.md`):**\n  - The false sandbox claim is replaced: masked under `--sandbox`, not hidden by default, and an unsandboxed command can read the descriptor and attach.\n  - The error table and controller list are updated.\n\n**Tests and mutations**\n- `session_socket.test.ts`: 31 tests.\n- `sidecar_socket.test.ts`: 12 tests. They include a real bwrap run with `XDG_RUNTIME_DIR` under `/var/tmp`, where a model command cannot read the token.\n- `sandbox_confine.test.ts`: 18 tests. They include a control that shows the file is readable without the mask.\n\nThese suites each passed three consecutive runs earlier in this session. The mutations covered removing each sandbox mask, the sidecar's sandbox registration, the workspace refusal, `socketMayDriveTurns`, the hub's work guard, the controller-list change, the pre-auth cap, and the 5-second timeout. I removed the hung leftover sidecar by pid.\n\n**Pending**\n- The full gate list, with each changed file run three times, is running now.\n- Then I commit as `fix(pf3): ...` with the Fable co-author line and push with a plain `git push origin v1/pf3-control-socket`.\n\nI merged the pushed `aa365cf3e` (the one `protocol_doc.test.ts` commit) in without a rebase.\n\n**Open**\n- The bwrap mask only applies while a sidecar process with `--listen` is the one running commands.\n- The slow-observer drop still has no test.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>270328</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>21</tool_uses><duration_ms>656657</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
