{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-11-24T21:02:28.605Z","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>af7235dbcad738773</task-id>\n<output-file>/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666/tasks/af7235dbcad738773.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Implement PF-3 control socket\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>All four review fixes are in commit `03d8ea1b5` and pushed to `v1/pf3-control-socket` with a plain push. I merged the one commit pushed after mine (`aa365cf3e`, `protocol_doc.test.ts`) without a rebase.\n\n**What changed**\n1. **Sandbox blocker:**\n   - `cli/src/sandbox.ts`: new `hideDirectoryFromSandbox` registry and a `hideDirectories` option. The general bwrap profile masks every hidden directory with `--tmpfs`, and the sandboxed worker inherits the mask. The read-only profile masks a directory only when it sits under `$HOME` or inside the workspace. Elsewhere that profile's synthetic root never contains it. A mask whose directory has been deleted is skipped, since bwrap can't mount over a missing path.\n   - `cli/src/sidecar.ts`: `--listen` registers the socket directory and refuses to start when it is inside the workspace.\n   - `docs/PROTOCOL.md`: masked under `--sandbox` wherever it resolves. Not hidden in the default no-sandbox case, where a command run in auto mode or approved in review mode can read the descriptor and attach. It recommends `--sandbox` for untrusted work.\n2. **Auto mode after start:** `socketMayDriveTurns()` in `sidecar.ts` is false in auto mode or after allow-always. In that state the hub answers socket `prompt.submit` and `steer` with `NOT_PERMITTED`. `cancel`, `deny`, `receipt` and `tool.detail` still work.\n3. **Controller list:** `answer` and `checkpoint.choice` are dropped. The controller may send `prompt.submit`, `steer`, `cancel`, `approve` (once only), `deny`, `receipt` and `tool.detail`, and that list is in `PROTOCOL.md`.\n4. **Pre-auth:** the attach deadline is 2 seconds, and at most 4 connections may be waiting to attach. A fifth gets `BUSY`.\n\n**Tests**\n- `session_socket.test.ts`: 31 tests.\n- `sidecar_socket.test.ts`: 12 tests. They include a real-bwrap run with `XDG_RUNTIME_DIR` under `/var/tmp`, where a model command cannot read the token.\n- `sandbox_confine.test.ts`: 18 tests. They include a control showing the descriptor is readable without the mask.\n- The sidecar, protocol, examples and other sandbox files also passed. Each new or changed file passed three consecutive runs.\n- `tsc`, the complexity gate, invariants and doc versions are clean.\n\n**Mutations**\nAll nine are caught:\n- general mask removed;\n- read-only mask removed;\n- sidecar's sandbox registration removed;\n- workspace refusal removed (caught as a hang);\n- `socketMayDriveTurns` forced true;\n- hub work guard off;\n- `answer`/`checkpoint.choice` allowed;\n- pre-auth cap off;\n- 5-second timeout restored.\n\n**Open**\n- The mask only applies inside the `--listen` sidecar process.\n- The slow-observer drop still has no test.\n- A real other-uid directory can't be tested without root, so that check uses a stand-in uid.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>273438</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>23</tool_uses><duration_ms>1046458</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
