ers the socket directory and refuses to start when it is inside the workspace.\n   - `docs/PROTOCOL.md`: masked under `--sandbox` wherever it resolves. Not hidden in the default no-sandbox case, where a command run in auto mode or approved in review mode can read the descriptor and attach. It recommends `--sandbox` for untrusted work.\n2. **Auto mode after start:** `socketMayDriveTurns()` in `sidecar.ts` is false in auto mode or after allow-always. In that state the hub answers socket `prompt.submit` and `steer` with `NOT_PERMITTED`. `cancel`, `deny`, `receipt` and `tool.detail` still work.\n3. **Controller list:** `answer` and `checkpoint.choice` are dropped. The controller may send `prompt.submit`, `steer`, `cancel`, `approve` (once only), `deny`, `receipt` and `tool.detail`, and that list is in `PROTOCOL.md`.\n4. **Pre-auth:** the attach deadline is 2 seconds, and at most 4 connections may be waiting to attach. A fifth gets `BUSY`.\n\n**Tests**\n- `session_socket.test.ts`: 31 tests.\n- `sidecar_socket.test.ts`: 12 tests. They include a real-bwrap run with `XDG_RUNTIME_DIR` under `/var/tmp`, where a model command cannot read the token.\n- `sandbox_confine.test.ts`: 18 tests. They include a control showing the descriptor is readable without the mask.\n- The sidecar, protocol, examples and other sandbox files also passed. Each new or changed file passed three consecutive runs.\n- `tsc`, the complexity gate, invariants and doc versions are clean.\n\n**Mutations**\nAll nine are caught:\n- general mask removed;\n- read-only mask removed;\n- sidecar's sandbox registration removed;\n- workspace refusal removed (caught as a hang);\n- `socketMayDriveTurns` forced true;\n- hub work guard off;\n- `answer`/`checkpoint.choice` allowed;\n- pre-auth cap off;\n- 5-second timeout restored.\n\n**Open**\n- The mask only applies inside the `--listen` sidecar process.\n- The slow-observer drop still has no test.\n- A real other-uid directory can't be tested without root, so that check