{"parentUuid":"67380b50-a42c-4b11-9d11-54b94a68cead","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNRqX8kaeyZjS3adxYNi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0157MNqsCpZbijZ95G4BfUSG","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Re-review PR #797 PF-3 fixes","subagent_type":"reviewer","prompt":"Independent RE-review of GitHub PR #797 (PF-3 unix-socket transport for the Nexus sidecar) in ~/nexus-code, base `release/v1.3.0`. Take the full head SHA from `gh pr view 797 --json headRefOid` (expected to start `03d8ea1b`), review exactly that, and check at the end whether it moved/merged. The first review (PR comment \"Independent security review at `512d0f9d…` — REQUEST CHANGES\", see `gh pr view 797 --comments`) found one blocker: a model command could read the socket token descriptor and attach as controller (no sandbox = default; `--sandbox` with the socket directory outside `/run/user/<uid>` and `/tmp`), plus suggestions. The fix commit is `03d8ea1b5` (`git show --stat`, then diff): sandbox mask `hideDirectoryFromSandbox`/`hideDirectories` in `cli/src/sandbox.ts` (both bwrap branches), `--listen` registers the directory and refuses a directory inside the workspace, `socketMayDriveTurns()` refusing socket `prompt.submit`/`steer` while auto/allow-always, controller list trimmed (`answer` and `checkpoint.choice` dropped), pre-auth deadline 2 s and cap 4, docs rewritten.\n\nTry to break it by RUNNING things (throwaway HOME, temp dirs, no network, no inference): (1) With `--sandbox` (real bwrap if available; check `bwrap --version`) and the socket directory at: default (`/run/user/<uid>`-style and the `/tmp` fallback), `XDG_RUNTIME_DIR` under `/var/tmp`, under a home path, under `/dev/shm`, a path reached through a symlink, a path with unusual characters, a bind-mounted-like path: can a sandboxed command list the directory, read the descriptor, or connect to the socket (`nc -U`/node `net.connect`)? Test BOTH bwrap branches (general; read-only/`--tmpfs /` branch) and the worker launch path (sandboxed worker inherits the mask), and the docker sandbox mode if it exists (does it mount the socket dir? say). Is the mask applied for commands run BEFORE the socket exists or after a sidecar restart? What happens when the mask directory vanishes or is replaced (skip logic: can the skip be abused to leave it unmasked)? Is the registry process-global in a way a second sidecar/session in the same process could miss? (2) Without a sandbox: confirm the doc states plainly the limit and that review-mode `run_command` needing approval shows the path. (3) `--listen` with the directory inside the workspace (incl. via symlink, relative path, `..`, workspace = parent of the socket dir) must refuse to start. (4) `socketMayDriveTurns`: start in review mode, have the stdio parent switch to auto (`/mode auto`) or approve with `always` AFTER the socket client attached: socket `prompt.submit`/`steer` refused with NOT_PERMITTED; `cancel` still works; after switching back, allowed again? Race: a prompt already in flight. (5) Controller list exactly as documented; `answer`, `checkpoint.choice`, `approve` with `always`, slash, shutdown, model/provider all refused. (6) Pre-auth: 5 idle connections → the fifth BUSY; a legitimate attach still works within 2 s after idles time out; a legitimate client that sends the attach line slowly (1.5 s) still works. (7) No regression: stdio behaviour unchanged without `--listen`; token/mode/role guards from the first review still hold (spot-check wrong token, second controller, socket 0600, dir 0700).\n\nThen run at head, one at a time: `session_socket`, `sidecar_socket`, `sandbox_confine` and every other `cli/test/sandbox*.test.ts`, `sidecar`, `protocol_parity`, `protocol_schema`, `protocol_doc`, `examples`, `leak_guard`, `check_requirements`; `cd cli && npx tsc --noEmit -p .`; the complexity gate; `node scripts/check_invariants.mjs`; `node scripts/check_doc_versions.mjs`. Mutations (copy aside, restore from the copy, never `git checkout`): remove the general-branch mask; remove the read-only-branch mask; remove the sidecar registration; remove the inside-workspace refusal; force `socketMayDriveTurns` true. Each must fail a test (a hang counts as caught; note it).\n\nRules: do NOT edit ~/nexus-code or existing worktrees. `git -C ~/nexus-code fetch origin && git -C ~/nexus-code worktree add --detach ~/nexus-wt/rev797b <full sha>`; `cp -a ~/nexus-code/cli/node_modules ~/nexus-wt/rev797b/cli/`; `mkdir -p ~/nexus-wt/rev797b/core/target/release && cp ~/nexus-wt/ls1b/core/target/release/{harness-core,nexus-tui} ~/nexus-wt/rev797b/core/target/release/`. Tests: `cd ~/nexus-wt/rev797b/cli && TMPDIR=/dev/shm HOME=$(mktemp -d) node --import tsx --test test/<name>.test.ts 2>&1 | tail -20`. Never read/write the real ~/.nexus, ~/.config/nexus, /etc/nexus. Stop processes by their own pid, never `pkill -f`; leave no listeners. No commits, pushes or GitHub comments. At the end remove probe files and `git -C ~/nexus-code worktree remove --force ~/nexus-wt/rev797b`. Shell is zsh (`bash -c` for loops); output passes through `rtk` (prefix `rtk proxy` if filtered); a safety check blocks scripts containing `rm`.\n\nReport under 450 words: verdict (ACCEPT / ACCEPT WITH FOLLOW-UPS / REQUEST CHANGES) at the exact SHA; the blocker closed or not, with the attack that shows it; new findings with file:line, run-or-read, blocking or not (any route by which a SANDBOXED model command or a non-operator client gains controller rights, allow-always, auto, or reads the token is blocking; the documented unsandboxed limit is not); test counts; mutation results; what you did not check."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1836,"cache_read_input_tokens":221578,"output_tokens":2298,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool