{"parentUuid":"f709a4b4-68c0-43d4-9ce4-37db62d915da","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNSKVDC3C25dits7z8Nt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DsJmZfZxxPGnBybTGqwXZi","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-wt/bg2 && git fetch -q origin && git merge -q origin/release/v1.3.0 --no-edit 2>&1 | tail -2; git status --short | grep -c '^UU'; (cd cli && npx tsc --noEmit -p . >/dev/null; echo \"tsc $?\"); git push -q -u origin v1/bg2-schedules 2>&1 | tail -1; echo \"remote $(git ls-remote origin refs/heads/v1/bg2-schedules | cut -c1-8) local $(git rev-parse --short=8 HEAD)\"; cat > /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/pr_bg2.md <<'EOF'\nPlan unit BG-2: unattended schedules on the BG-1 detached runner. Acceptance: \"a scheduled run on a seeded failing verifier ends BLOCKED and says so; an unattended run asking for approval is denied, not blocked forever; missed runs are reported, not silently skipped\". G-4: no allow-always, a fresh worktree, the unattended flag in receipts, a kill-and-resume pass.\n\n## What it adds\n\n- `nexus schedule add|list|status|remove|pause|resume|run-now` (`--json`), schedules as cron / every / once, stored privately (0700/0600, owner and symlink checks). A schedule fires a job through the same submission path as `nexus job` (`core/job_submission.ts`), so every unattended rule of BG-1 applies: read-only by default, fresh worktree, no auto, no allow-always.\n- **Policies** (in `docs/SCHEDULES.md`): UTC only; missed runs are all counted and reported as one gap and never replayed, with one catch-up job by default (`--on-missed report` runs none); a slot due while the previous job runs starts nothing and is recorded as an `overlap` gap; a clock stepped back by more than 2 minutes is counted and the next slot recomputed, and a slot that already has a job never starts twice; caps: 64 schedules, last 50 gaps, 20 missed receipts, 200,000 slots per scan.\n- **Authority:** `add` and every fire need a workspace in the operator's trust list; a schedule names one of two job levels and cannot widen them; the schedule files are protected paths for the agent's file tools.\n- Receipt fields `missed` (was reserved null) and `schedule_occurrence`, additively, ledgers appended and kept at version 1 (nothing shipped carried the old shape); `schedule-v1.schema.json` + `SCHEDULE_VERSIONS.json`.\n- Docs, a runnable example (`examples/schedules`, run by `schedule_examples.test.ts`), manual, CHANGELOG.\n\n## Tests\n\nEleven new files, 57 tests (`schedule` 14, `schedule_store` 10, `schedule_schema` 2, `schedule_engine` 13, `schedule_hostile` 7, `schedule_cli` 6, `schedule_failing_verifier`, `schedule_approval_denied`, `schedule_missed`, `schedule_examples` 1 each, `schedule_unattended` 2); each passed three runs. 18 mutations each fail a test (protected path, file mode/symlink/owner/directory checks, cap, trust list, overlap, burst advance, clock step, slot dedupe, cron validation, workspace link, missed info in receipt, the unattended approval policy letting exec and egress through).\n\n## Known limits and findings carried by this PR\n\n- Another program running as the user, including an agent's `run_command` with full access, can write a schedule record; the file tools refuse, shell commands are only advisory-checked. A planted record is bounded: two job levels, the workspace must be trusted at each run, unattended rules apply.\n- **BG-1 finding, affects the first acceptance sentence:** an unattended job's `--verifier` goes through the approval policy for exec and is denied, so a verifier like `node --test` is never run and `task_completed` always fails. The job ends BLOCKED by stagnation with reason `EXECUTION_FAILED`; the receipt does not name the verifier. So a seeded failing verifier does end BLOCKED, but not through the verifier's own failure. Being decided in review; if fixed it will be in a later commit on this PR.\n- Not done: an `unattended` stamp on the tool `ExecutionReceipt` (the job receipt and the operation origin carry it), `doctor` `schedules.*` findings, a `maxRounds` option, the readiness inventory.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\nEOF\ncd ~/nexus-code && u=$(gh pr create --base release/v1.3.0 --head v1/bg2-schedules --title \"feat(schedules): unattended cron/every/once schedules on the detached runner (BG-2)\" --body-file /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/pr_bg2.md | tail -1); echo \"$u\"; echo \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ) PR (claude-invariants-audit): $u BG-2 opened; independent review next; DO NOT MERGE until posted. Finding for BG-1's owner: unattended job --verifier is denied by the approval policy for exec, so the verifier never runs (details in the PR body).\" >> \"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log\"","description":"Merge release into the BG-2 branch, push, open its PR and log it","timeout":200000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2544,"cache_read_input_tokens":226093,"output_tokens":2216,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":207},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2544,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":2216,"cache_read_input_tokens":226093,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2544,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2544},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":11296,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01DsJmZfZxxPGnBybTGqwXZi":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-wt/bg2 && git fetch -q origin && 