{"parentUuid":"c0bd40b8-7a61-4ada-8de1-65ed03966223","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNSN59fx2oWrYbDok6MF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Dvv1sEjNhs8c9QSuMu573H","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Review PR #799 BG-2 schedules","subagent_type":"reviewer","prompt":"Independent security and acceptance review of GitHub PR #799 (BG-2: unattended schedules on the BG-1 detached runner) in ~/nexus-code, base `release/v1.3.0`. Take the full head SHA from `gh pr view 799 --json headRefOid` (expected to start `68bc626f`), review exactly that, and check at the end whether it moved or merged. Read the PR body, `docs/SCHEDULES.md`, `docs/RUNNER.md`, and the plan `/home/mike/nexus-wt/_plans/BG_PLAN.md`. Acceptance verbatim: \"a scheduled run on a seeded failing verifier ends BLOCKED and says so; an unattended run asking for approval is denied, not blocked forever; missed runs are reported, not silently skipped\". G-4: \"tests show no allow-always, a fresh worktree, the unattended flag in receipts, and a kill-and-resume pass\". Files: `cli/src/core/schedule_*.ts`, `cli/src/schedule_cli.ts`, `cli/src/core/job_submission.ts`, runner integration (`job_runner.ts`), receipt/schema changes (`job_receipt.ts`, `docs/protocol/*schedule*`, ledgers), `cli/src/security.ts` protected paths, `index.ts` registration, tests `cli/test/schedule*.test.ts`, `examples/schedules`. The branch history contains a second author's scaffold merged over the first implementation: check no dead, duplicated or conflicting schedule code (two stores, two parsers, two CLI registrations) remains and that `nexus schedule` registers once.\n\nKnown and to be judged by you: the builder reports a BG-1 defect that bears on acceptance sentence 1: an unattended job's `--verifier` goes through the approval policy for exec and is denied, so a verifier such as `node --test` is never run and `task_completed` always fails; the job ends BLOCKED by stagnation with reason `EXECUTION_FAILED` and the receipt never names the verifier. Reproduce it with the test helpers (`cli/test/schedule_failing_verifier.test.ts`, scripted gateway from `cli/test/helpers/fixtures.ts`, throwaway HOME): with a verifier that FAILS and one that PASSES, what does a scheduled/unattended job end as, what does the receipt/status say, and does a PASSING verifier ever run (i.e. can an unattended job ever reach VERIFIED)? Decide whether acceptance sentence 1 (\"ends BLOCKED and says so\") is truly met or only coincidentally, and what the minimal correct fix is (e.g. the operator-configured verifier set at job creation runs without approval like the operator's `authoritativeVerifierCommand` does in the interactive path, `cli/src/core/completion_oracle.ts` ~199-212; or the job says why it could not run it). Also check the builder's second note: are the runner's `inbox`/`jobs` and the schedules directory protected from the agent's file tools?\n\nAttack by RUNNING (throwaway HOME, temp dirs, no network, no live inference): schedule file tampering (other-uid owner can be simulated by checks only; symlinks at the store path or directory; mode 0644/0666; unknown keys; huge counts; duplicate ids; ids with path separators or `..`); cron/every/once parsing hostile strings (empty, 10k chars, unicode, negative, zero interval, huge interval, step 0, impossible dates like Feb 30, ranges reversed); `every` with tiny intervals (flooding: is there a minimum?); a schedule naming a workspace that is not trusted, that is a symlink to elsewhere, that vanishes; level escalation (`worktree-write` vs `read-only`: can a schedule record or an edit widen it; does managed policy still clamp; are `--yes`/auto/allow-always reachable in any scheduled job in any form); missed-run logic (runner down for days: burst replay impossible? one catch-up only; `--on-missed report` runs none; overlap; clock stepped back and forward; a record whose `last_seen` is in the future); kill-and-resume of a scheduled job (kill -9 the worker by its own pid: resumes cleanly, no double fire of the same slot); pause/resume/remove while a job runs; a runner restart during a fire (idempotent: the slot already has a job); `run-now` authority (can the agent run it? it is a CLI command run via `run_command`: what can a model command do with `nexus schedule add` in auto mode or when approved: it needs the workspace in the trust list; note what an unsandboxed command can do and whether the docs say so).\n\nThen run at head, one at a time: every `cli/test/schedule*.test.ts`, the BG-1 files (`ls cli/test | grep -iE \"runner|job\"`), `fault_kill_mid_tool_call`, `protocol_schema`, `examples`, `leak_guard`, `check_requirements`, `security`; `cd cli && npx tsc --noEmit -p .`; the complexity gate; `node scripts/check_invariants.mjs`; `node scripts/check_doc_versions.mjs`. `schedule_examples` needs a fresh `cli/dist` (`npm --prefix cli run build` inside the review worktree). Mutations (copy aside, restore from the copy, never `git checkout`): the protected path, the trust check, the overlap check, the burst guard, the unattended approval policy; each must fail a test.\n\nRules: do NOT edit ~/nexus-code or existing worktrees. `git -C ~/nexus-code fetch origin && git -C ~/nexus-code worktree add --detach ~/nexus-wt/rev799 <full sha>`; `cp -a ~/nexus-code/cli/node_modules ~/nexus-wt/rev799/cli/`; `mkdir -p ~/nexus-wt/rev799/core/target/release && cp ~/nexus-wt/ls1b/core/target/release/{harness-core,nexus-tui} ~/nexus-wt/rev799/core/target/release/`. Tests: `cd ~/nexus-wt/rev799/cli && TMPDIR=/dev/shm HOME=$(mktemp -d) node --import tsx --test test/<name>.test.ts 2>&1 | tail -20`. Never read/write the real ~/.nexus, ~/.config/nexus, /etc/nexus. Stop processes by their own pid, never `pkill -f`; leave no runner or worker processes. No commits, pushes or GitHub comments. At the end remove probe files and `git -C ~/nexus-code worktree remove --force ~/nexus-wt/rev799`. Shell is zsh (`bash -c` for loops); output passes through `rtk` (prefix `rtk proxy` if filtered); a safety check blocks scripts containing `rm`.\n\nReport under 500 words: verdict (ACCEPT / ACCEPT WITH FOLLOW-UPS / REQUEST CHANGES) at the exact SHA; the acceptance sentences each met or not, with the run that shows it; findings with file:line, run-or-read, blocking or not (any route by which a scheduled or unattended job gets allow-always, auto, write access beyond its level, an untrusted workspace, or a burst replay is blocking); test counts; mutation results; what you did not check."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":950,"cache_read_input_tokens":232323,"output_tokens":2769,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":178},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":950,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2769,"cache_read_input_tokens":232323,"cache_creation_input_tokens":950,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":950},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":15706,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Dvv1sEjNhs8c9QSuMu573H":{"description":"Review PR #799 BG-2 schedules","subagent_type":"reviewer","prompt":"Independent security and acceptance review of GitHub PR #799 (BG-2: unattended schedules on the BG-1 detached runner) in ~/nexus-code, base `release/v1.3.0`. Take the full head SHA from `gh pr view 799 --json headRefOid` (expected to start `68bc626f`), review exactly that, and check at the end whether it moved or merged. Read the PR body, `docs/SCHEDULES.md`, `docs/RUNNER.md`, and the plan `/home/mike/nexus-wt/_plans/BG_PLAN.md`. 