{"parentUuid":"9f098f4a-db00-4d0d-9bee-8eaab517fc13","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNSPdZ7DQv34FmWdUxWo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"BG-2 is built, but I did not open its PR. #799 already existed, opened by Codex, and its branch already contained my three commits plus Codex's own scaffold and one fix. My push was rejected as non-fast-forward, so nothing was overwritten. I corrected my claims-log entry and will review #799 as it stands.\n\nCodex's scaffold was merged over my implementation. The branch differs from my last commit by a four-line change, so I don't expect two competing schedule implementations. I've told the reviewer to confirm that.\n\nAn independent review of #799 is now running. It covers:\n- The three acceptance sentences.\n- Schedule tampering, permission escalation, missed-run replay and kill-and-resume of a scheduled job.\n- Whether the agent's file tools can reach the schedule and runner directories.\n\nI'll act on its verdict, and I won't push to that branch without saying so in the claims log first.\n\n**One finding bears on acceptance.** The BG-2 builder found that an unattended job's verifier is denied by the approval policy for command execution, so it never runs. A job on a failing verifier does end BLOCKED, but through stagnation (`EXECUTION_FAILED`), not through the verifier failing. The receipt never names the verifier. It also seems that an unattended job could never reach VERIFIED. The reviewer will reproduce this and judge whether the \"ends BLOCKED and says so\" sentence is truly met. It is a BG-1 defect, so the fix likely belongs there.\n\n**Other open work:**\n- **PF-3 (#797):** waiting on the re-review of the sandbox fixes.\n- **SB-1 and HK-2:** Codex's #795 and Cursor's #796 are still open.\n- **Unclaimed:** HK-3 and MT-2 slices 2–4.\n- **Still owed:** my own check of the merged HK-1 head, and the readiness re-measure.\n\nv1.3.0 is not landed. The merge to `main` and the release haven't started."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3139,"cache_read_input_tokens":233273,"output_tokens":652,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3139,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":652,"cache_read_input_tokens":233273,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3139,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3139},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011ChNSPdPRhUVNPpshEoRgC","requestRef":"2d0200fd-06aa-41f4-8901-c29a16181cd0","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"186c8756-9bb1-459d-9e8a-a8999edd7872","timestamp":"2026-11-24T21:09:51.219Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"main","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
