{"parentUuid":"b7bde718-f818-427b-9941-f90dab33d660","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"36d20a6c-5893-4e1b-badb-578d8502a085","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>adcdf77bcc6a2faa3</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_0157MNqsCpZbijZ95G4BfUSG</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666/tasks/adcdf77bcc6a2faa3.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Re-review PR #797 PF-3 fixes\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>**Verdict: REQUEST CHANGES at `03d8ea1b5d17c235253f050dec6a77615f9bf7d0`.** The original blocker is closed. One new narrow route is still open, and your rule makes it blocking. At the end the PR was still OPEN at that SHA and not merged.\n\n**Original blocker: closed.**\n- I ran real bwrap 0.13.1 against both profiles: the general one and the read-only one (`readOnlyHost`, fd 3).\n- Directories tested: `/run/user/&lt;uid&gt;`, the `/tmp` fallback, `/var/tmp`, under a throwaway `$HOME`, `/dev/shm`, through a symlinked parent, and a name containing quotes, spaces and `$(id)`.\n- Without the mask, the general profile showed the descriptor for `/var/tmp`, the symlinked path and the odd name. With the directory registered, a sandboxed `ls`, `cat` and node `net.connect` all failed (ENOENT) in both profiles.\n- The sandboxed worker (`wrapSandboxedWorker`) also read ENOENT for both the file and the socket.\n- Registration happens before the hub binds, so no command runs unmasked. A restarted sidecar re-registers.\n- If the directory is moved and replaced, vanishes, or becomes a symlink, it stays hidden or ENOENT. I found no way to abuse the skip.\n- The registry is process-global, so a second sidecar in the same process registers its own directory. I did not run that case.\n- Docker mounts only the workspace, so it exposes nothing, and `--listen` refuses a directory inside the workspace.\n\n**New finding (blocking by your rule; needs an unusual operator setup).**\n- `cli/src/sandbox.ts:275` (`isPathWithin`) and `cli/src/sidecar.ts:1688` (`isPathInside`) both test `relative.startsWith(\"..\")`. A first path segment that merely starts with `..` (such as `..hid`) is treated as outside the workspace.\n- I ran `XDG_RUNTIME_DIR=&lt;ws&gt;/..hid` through the sidecar. `--listen` was not refused: the process stayed running and printed `listening`.\n- With the socket directory at `&lt;ws&gt;/..hid/nexus`, the read-only profile printed `SENTINEL-DOTDOT`, so a sandboxed command read the descriptor. The general profile hid it, because its mask is unconditional.\n- Fix: replace the check with `relative === \"..\" || relative.startsWith(\"..\" + path.sep) || path.isAbsolute(relative)` in both places. Add a test with a `..x` directory.\n- This needs the operator to set `XDG_RUNTIME_DIR` to a path inside the workspace with a segment starting `..`. I rate it low likelihood.\n\n**Non-blocking.**\n- The socket directory is created before the inside-workspace refusal (`sidecar.ts:1663`), so the refused directory is left behind.\n\n**Other checks (all run).**\n- **Refusal cases:** these refused to start with exit 1 and no listener: directory inside the workspace, a `..` path inside it, a symlinked workspace, a symlinked XDG parent, and workspace equal to XDG. A relative `XDG_RUNTIME_DIR` falls back to `/tmp` and started normally.\n- **Mode switching:** `/mode auto` from stdio makes socket `prompt.submit` and `steer` return NOT_PERMITTED while `cancel` and `receipt` still work. Switching back to review allows `prompt.submit` again. After `approve always` on stdio, a mid-turn `steer` and `prompt.submit` were refused.\n- **Controller list:** `answer`, `checkpoint.choice`, `slash`, `shutdown`, `model.select`, `provider.connect`, `models.list` and `approve always` all returned NOT_PERMITTED. An observer got NOT_CONTROLLER.\n- **Pre-auth:** with 5 idle connections the fifth got BUSY, and the other four ended UNAUTHORIZED at 2 s. A slow attach at 1.5 s worked.\n- **Spot checks:** a wrong token got UNAUTHORIZED, a second controller got BUSY, the socket is 0600, the directory 0700 and the descriptor 0600.\n- **Docs:** `docs/PROTOCOL.md` states the unsandboxed limit plainly. I read it but did not run a review-mode approval to see the path displayed.\n\n**Tests (all green).**\n\n| Test | Pass |\n|---|---|\n| `session_socket` | 31 |\n| `sidecar_socket` | 12 |\n| `sandbox_confine` | 18 |\n| `sandbox_cancel` | 2 |\n| `sandbox_denial_events` | 6 |\n| `sandbox_docker` | 12 |\n| `sandbox_profiles` | 14 |\n| `sandbox_quoting` | 2 |\n| `sidecar` | 65 |\n| `protocol_parity` | 5 |\n| `protocol_schema` | 8 |\n| `protocol_doc` | 6 |\n| `examples` | 7 |\n| `leak_guard` | 6 |\n| `check_requirements` | 28 |\n\n`tsc --noEmit`, the complexity gate, `check_invariants` and `check_doc_versions` all exited 0.\n\n**Mutations (restored from the copy, tree clean).**\n\n| Mutation | Result |\n|---|---|\n| General-branch mask removed | caught: `sandbox_confine` 4 failures |\n| Read-only-branch mask removed | caught: 1 failure |\n| Sidecar registration removed | caught by `sidecar_socket` (1 failure); `sandbox_confine` stayed green, as expected |\n| Inside-workspace refusal removed | caught only as a hang: `sidecar_socket` timed out at 240 s, with 9 passed and 0 failed |\n| `socketMayDriveTurns` forced true | caught: `sidecar_socket` 2 failures; `session_socket` stayed green because it does not exercise that gate |\n\n**Not checked.**\n- Real bind mounts and a real Docker run.\n- A second sidecar in the same process.\n- Other auto-approval sources, such as managed-policy allow rules.\n- Node 22.\n- The core's own `bwrap` use: grep found none in the Rust source.\n\nProbe scripts are in `/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad`. I removed my temp directories and the `rev797b` worktree.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>108043</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>46</tool_uses><duration_ms>1184949</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"},"uuid":"6e73fcfe-99c0-4804-bde2-4f43227e695c","timestamp":"2026-11-24T21:22:33.331Z","permissionMode":"bypassPermissions","origin":{"kind":"task-notification","producer":"session-task","runId":"0mwv6lb6l-393467e6"},"promptSource":"system","turnOrigin":"task_notification","turnPromptId":"36d20a6c-5893-4e1b-badb-578d8502a085","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":40,"turnIndex":283},"queueSkipAttachments":true,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"main","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
