{"parentUuid":"14f82b70-a2e3-460e-9793-aa6774584275","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNTNKgezHNrtvk34h9iq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014BLpNuHPjch3V2y9qDKxAh","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-code && cat > /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/rev797b.md <<'EOF'\n**Independent re-review at `03d8ea1b5d17c235253f050dec6a77615f9bf7d0` — REQUEST CHANGES. The original blocker is closed; one narrow new route remains, fix in progress.**\n\n**Original blocker: closed (run, real bwrap 0.13.1, both profiles).** Without the mask the general profile showed the descriptor for a socket directory under `/var/tmp`, behind a symlinked parent, and with quotes, spaces and `$(id)` in the name. With the directory registered, a sandboxed `ls`, `cat` and node `net.connect` all failed with ENOENT in both profiles, and the sandboxed worker too. Registration happens before the hub binds; a restarted sidecar re-registers; a moved, vanished or symlinked directory stays hidden. Docker mounts only the workspace. `--listen` refused a directory inside the workspace, a `..` path into it, a symlinked workspace or XDG parent, and workspace = XDG.\n\n**New, blocking by the rule that a sandboxed command must not read the token:** `cli/src/sandbox.ts:275` (`isPathWithin`) and `cli/src/sidecar.ts:1688` (`isPathInside`) test `relative.startsWith(\"..\")`, so a first segment that merely starts with `..` (such as `..hid`) counts as outside the workspace. With `XDG_RUNTIME_DIR=<ws>/..hid`, `--listen` was not refused and printed `listening`; in the read-only profile a sandboxed command printed the descriptor's contents (the general profile hides it, its mask is unconditional). Needs an operator to point `XDG_RUNTIME_DIR` into the workspace at a `..`-prefixed segment: low likelihood. Fix: `relative === \"..\" || relative.startsWith(\"..\" + path.sep) || path.isAbsolute(relative)` in both places, with a test using a `..x` directory.\n**Not blocking:** the socket directory is created before the inside-workspace refusal (`sidecar.ts:1663`), so a refused directory is left behind; the test for the inside-workspace refusal fails only as a 240 s hang rather than an assertion.\n\n**Also checked (run):** `/mode auto` from stdio makes socket `prompt.submit` and `steer` return `NOT_PERMITTED` while `cancel` and `receipt` still work, and switching back allows them; after `approve always` on stdio the same; `answer`, `checkpoint.choice`, `slash`, `shutdown`, `model.select`, `provider.connect`, `models.list` and approve-with-`always` all refused; five idle connections gave `BUSY` on the fifth and a 1.5 s slow attach worked; wrong token, second controller, and the 0600/0700/0600 modes still hold.\n\n**Tests at that head, Node 24:** `session_socket` 31, `sidecar_socket` 12, `sandbox_confine` 18, `sandbox_cancel` 2, `sandbox_denial_events` 6, `sandbox_docker` 12, `sandbox_profiles` 14, `sandbox_quoting` 2, `sidecar` 65, `protocol_parity` 5, `protocol_schema` 8, `protocol_doc` 6, `examples` 7, `leak_guard` 6, `check_requirements` 28; `tsc`, the complexity gate, `check_invariants`, `check_doc_versions` pass. **Mutations:** general mask, read-only mask, sidecar registration, `socketMayDriveTurns` forced true: caught; the inside-workspace refusal: caught only as a hang.\n**Not checked:** real bind mounts, a real Docker run, a second sidecar in one process, managed-policy auto sources, Node 22.\nEOF\ngh pr comment 797 --body-file /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/rev797b.md | tail -1","description":"Post the re-review verdict on PR 797"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3396,"cache_read_input_tokens":236412,"output_tokens":2489,"output_tokens_details":{"thi