relative.startsWith(\"..\" + path.sep) || path.isAbsolute(relative)` in both places, with a test using a `..x` directory.\n**Not blocking:** the socket directory is created before the inside-workspace refusal (`sidecar.ts:1663`), so a refused directory is left behind; the test for the inside-workspace refusal fails only as a 240 s hang rather than an assertion.\n\n**Also checked (run):** `/mode auto` from stdio makes socket `prompt.submit` and `steer` return `NOT_PERMITTED` while `cancel` and `receipt` still work, and switching back allows them; after `approve always` on stdio the same; `answer`, `checkpoint.choice`, `slash`, `shutdown`, `model.select`, `provider.connect`, `models.list` and approve-with-`always` all refused; five idle connections gave `BUSY` on the fifth and a 1.5 s slow attach worked; wrong token, second controller, and the 0600/0700/0600 modes still hold.\n\n**Tests at that head, Node 24:** `session_socket` 31, `sidecar_socket` 12, `sandbox_confine` 18, `sandbox_cancel` 2, `sandbox_denial_events` 6, `sandbox_docker` 12, `sandbox_profiles` 14, `sandbox_quoting` 2, `sidecar` 65, `protocol_parity` 5, `protocol_schema` 8, `protocol_doc` 6, `examples` 7, `leak_guard` 6, `check_requirements` 28; `tsc`, the complexity gate, `check_invariants`, `check_doc_versions` pass. **Mutations:** general mask, read-only mask, sidecar registration, `socketMayDriveTurns` forced true: caught; the inside-workspace refusal: caught only as a hang.\n**Not checked:** real bind mounts, a real Docker run, a second sidecar in one process, managed-policy auto sources, Node 22.\nEOF\ngh pr comment 797 --body-file /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/rev797b.md | tail -1","description":"Post the re-review verdict on PR 797"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WGbgxcUfnirKJvzXP6mkye","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"af7235dbcad738773","summary":"Fix the dotdot containment check in PF-3","message":"Re-review of PF-3 (head 03d8ea1b5; worktree /home/mike/nexus-wt/pf3; `git fetch origin && git status` first, merge origin/release/v1.3.0 and origin/v1/pf3-control-socket if either moved, never rebase; plain `git push origin v1/pf3-control-socket` at the end, never force). The original blocker is closed. One narrow route remains: `cli/src/sandbox.ts:275` (`isPathWithin`) and `cli/src/sidecar.ts:1688` (`isPathInside`) use `relative.startsWith(\"..\")`, so a first segment that merely starts with `..` (e.g. `..hid`) counts as outside the workspace. With `XDG_RUNTIME_DIR=<ws>/..hid`, `--listen` was not refused and the read-only bwrap profile exposed the descriptor. Fix: in BOTH places use `relative === \"..\" || relative.startsWith(\"..\" + path.sep) || path.isAbsolute(relative)` as the \"outside\" test (grep the repo for other `startsWith(\"..\")` containment checks, list them in your report, and fix any that guard a security boundary in files this PR touches; others: report only). Test with a `..x` directory for both functions and end to end (`--listen` with `XDG_RUNTIME_DIR=<ws>/..hid` must refuse to start, exit 1, nothing bound); mutation: restore the old test, tests fail. Also: (a) do the inside-workspace refusal BEFORE creating the socket directory (sidecar.ts ~:1663) and test that a refused directory is not left behind; (b) make the inside-workspace-refusal test fail with an assertion rather than a 240 s hang (add a short timeout/race with a clear message), keep the mutation caught. Re-run: tsc, complexity gate, check_invariants, check_doc_versions, session_socket, sidecar_socket, sandbox_confine, sandbox_profiles, sidecar, protocol_parity, protocol_schema, protocol_doc, examples, leak_guard; changed files three times. Commit `fix(pf3): <what>` + `Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>`; push. Report under 200 words: file:line changes, other `startsWith(\"..\")` sites found, tests, mutation, commit hash."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
