{"parentUuid":"36436d00-ac4f-4658-a923-db237f59f30a","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"97e723e0-26a8-4d06-8ea7-1e22c950bac9","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>af7235dbcad738773</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01WGbgxcUfnirKJvzXP6mkye</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666/tasks/af7235dbcad738773.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Implement PF-3 control socket\" is waiting on its own background work</summary>\n<note>This agent stopped with background work of its own still running. It may resume on its own when that work completes or reports, and the same task-id notifies again if it does; the result below may be interim.</note>\n<result>The `..hid` fix is written (sandbox.ts, sidecar.ts and socket_files.ts), and the mutation run is going in the background. I've held off on the final gate run, the commit and the push until it finishes.\n\n**What changed**\n- `isPathWithin` in `cli/src/sandbox.ts` now counts a path as outside only when the relative path is exactly `..`, starts with `../`, or is absolute. It is now exported, and `sidecar.ts` uses it in place of its own `isPathInside`, so the check lives in one place.\n- The inside-workspace refusal in `sidecar.ts` now runs before the socket directory is created, using new helpers in `cli/src/core/socket_files.ts`: `socketRuntimeDirPath()` computes the path without touching the file system, and `realpathAllowingMissing()` resolves it.\n\n**New tests**\n- `sandbox_confine.test.ts` (19 tests): `isPathWithin` on `..hid`, `..`, sibling prefixes, and both bwrap profiles masking `&lt;ws&gt;/..hid`.\n- `sidecar_socket.test.ts` (13 tests): end-to-end for `XDG_RUNTIME_DIR` of `&lt;ws&gt;/run` and `&lt;ws&gt;/..hid`. Each must exit 1 and print no `listening` line, and the `nexus` directory must not exist afterwards. It races the exit against a 20-second timer and fails with a clear message instead of hanging for 240 seconds. The timer is cleared after the race; otherwise it tripped `leak_guard`.\n- Both files pass on their own; `sidecar_socket` passed three consecutive runs.\n\n**Other `startsWith(\"..\")` sites (reported only, not changed)**\n\n| File | Lines |\n|---|---|\n| `browser.ts` | 100, 120, 265 |\n| `core/authority.ts` | 637, 657, 692 |\n| `core/candidate.ts` | 1089 |\n| `core/observation_identity.ts` | 70, 93 |\n| `lsp.ts` | 406 |\n| `safe_fs.ts` | 39 |\n| `security.ts` | 797, 821, 1012 |\n| `skills.ts` | 332 |\n| `tester.ts` | 446 |\n| `workspace_trust.ts` | 39 |\n| `worktrunk/copy.ts` | 58 |\n| `worktrunk/paths.ts` | 122 |\n\nNone are in files this PR touches.\n\n**Still to do**\n- Read the mutation results. The planned mutations are the old `startsWith` check (unit and end-to-end), creating the directory before the check, and removing the refusal.\n- Run the full gate list, with changed files three times each.\n- Commit as `fix(pf3): ...` with the Fable co-author line, then push with a plain `git push origin v1/pf3-control-socket`.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>282910</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>5</tool_uses><duration_ms>191907</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"},"uuid":"cb8a79a6-4600-4086-b5b3-29cd03d01f1a","timestamp":"2026-11-24T21:26:03.538Z","permissionMode":"bypassPermissions","origin":{"kind":"task-notification","producer":"session-task","runId":"0mwv7b3sd-202b2bf2"},"promptSource":"system","turnOrigin":"task_notification","turnPromptId":"97e723e0-26a8-4d06-8ea7-1e22c950bac9","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":40,"turnIndex":284},"queueSkipAttachments":true,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"main","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
