{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-11-24T21:31:05.783Z","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a6f130bfd7646f382</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01Dvv1sEjNhs8c9QSuMu573H</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666/tasks/a6f130bfd7646f382.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Review PR #799 BG-2 schedules\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>**Verdict: REQUEST CHANGES at 68bc626f43e42bf8c6a7bd3958649bc1e0396583.** The PR head has since moved to `ce242d020`, still open and unmerged. That commit only edits `cli/test/schedule_missed.test.ts`. It looks like the B2 fix below, but I did not run it. The A1 blocker is not touched.\n\n**Acceptance**\n1. **\"Failing verifier ends BLOCKED and says so\": met only coincidentally.** I probed with throwaway HOME and a scripted gateway.\n   - A failing `node --test` ends BLOCKED/`EXECUTION_FAILED`, summary \"STAGNATION_DETECTED\".\n   - A passing `node --test`, `npm test`, `true` and `git status --short` end identically. Each `task_completed` fails with \"Verifier '…' requires operator approval (exec) … Run with --yes or --mode auto\". No verifier ever runs, so an unattended job can never reach VERIFIED.\n   - The receipt names the verifier but never says it was not run. The reason shown is stagnation, not the failing test.\n   - `schedule_failing_verifier.test.ts` passes, but it would pass the same way with a passing repo.\n2. **Approval denied, not blocked forever: met.** `schedule_approval_denied` passes, and mutating `UnattendedApprovalPolicy` makes it fail.\n3. **Missed runs reported, not skipped: met in code** (`schedule_engine`, `schedule_hostile`, mutations), **but `schedule_missed` fails at this SHA** (B2).\n4. **G-4 (no allow-always, fresh worktree, unattended flag, kill-and-resume): met.** `schedule_unattended` (2 tests) passes.\n\n**Blockers**\n- **B1: `cli/src/core/completion_oracle.ts:19-30` (via `spine_handlers.ts:216`), run.** The unattended verifier goes through `requiresDecision(\"exec\")` and is always denied.\n  - **Fix:** one line after the `requiresDecision` check. For `surface === \"unattended\"` and a command equal to the trimmed `authoritativeVerifierCommand`, return true. Managed `require_human` must still apply, and the command still runs in the sandbox.\n  - **Tried in a scratch edit, restored afterwards:** the verifier then ran. A failing one gave \"did not pass … CANDIDATE_FAILED\". A passing one gave `task_completed` ok.\n  - **Not shown:** I did not reach VERIFIED. A model edit to an imported source file hit \"verifier definition changed after its baseline\". That may be my probe or a separate oracle behaviour. The fix also needs a test with a passing verifier.\n  - **Two more things to change:** the denial text (\"Run with --yes or --mode auto\") is wrong for unattended runs, and the receipt should say \"verifier not run\".\n- **B1 (docs):** `docs/SCHEDULES.md:34` says \"`git status --short` run\". It is denied, so the doc is false.\n- **B2: `cli/test/schedule_missed.test.ts`, run.** `catches` omits `--on-missed run-once` after the default became `report`, so no catch-up fires. It failed twice (125 s timeout). `ce242d020` appears to fix it. The stale \"run-once (the default)\" text remains in `schedule_engine.ts:11`, `:15` and the test comment.\n\n**Non-blocking suggestions**\n- **`schedule.ts`:** cron `* * * * *` is accepted, so it fires every minute. `every` has a 5-minute floor. Reject crons whose next two slots are under 5 minutes apart. Overlap, the 32-job queue and budgets bound the flood.\n- **`schedule.ts` `scanSlots`:** a 200k-slot cron scan blocks the runner tick for about 2.6 s, and `fireDue` scans two or three times. Use a closed form or a lower cap.\n- **`schedule_cli.ts` `run-now`:** it checks for a running job without the schedule lock. A race with the runner could give two concurrent jobs of one schedule. Not reproduced.\n- **`security.ts`:** `inbox` and `jobs` are not protected paths (`isPathProtected` returned open). BG-1 relies on workspace confinement and denial of unapproved commands, which I did not exercise. Add an absolute-path pattern for the runner root.\n- **Schedule tampering:** after B1, a tampered `verifier` field becomes an unapproved sandboxed command. It is the same trust boundary the docs state; add a sentence.\n\n**Structure:** one store, one parser, one `registerScheduleCommands` call at `index.ts:1555`. No dead or duplicate code.\n\n**Test counts at head (run one at a time):**\n\n| Group | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `schedule*` | 54 pass, 1 fail (`schedule_missed`) |\n| BG-1 runner/job files | all pass |\n| `fault_kill_mid_tool_call` | 1 pass |\n| `protocol_schema` | 8 pass |\n| `examples` | 6 pass |\n| `leak_guard` | 6 pass |\n| `check_requirements` | 28 pass |\n| `security` | 14 pass |\n| `security_gates` | 10 pass |\n\n`tsc --noEmit`, the complexity gate, `check_invariants` and `check_doc_versions` are all clean.\n\n**Mutations (all killed):**\n- Protected path removed: `schedule_hostile` fails.\n- Trust check removed: `schedule_hostile` fails.\n- Overlap check removed: `schedule_engine` fails.\n- Burst guard (advance slot by slot): 3 tests fail.\n- Duplicate-slot guard removed: 1 test fails.\n- Unattended policy returns false: `schedule_approval_denied` fails.\n\nParser probes: all hostile cron/every/at inputs were rejected except the 1-minute cron above.\n\n**Not checked:** symlinked store paths and 0644/0666 modes by hand (relied on `schedule_store`/`schedule_hostile`), other-uid owner, an actual `kill -9` by me (relied on `schedule_unattended`), pause/remove during a run, clock-forward live runs, `nexus schedule add` through `run_command` in auto mode, managed-policy clamping, and Node 22 versus 24.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>133330</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>52</tool_uses><duration_ms>1279746</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
