{"parentUuid":"51c9700c-ab02-4207-b46b-ba2e059adc75","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"d651d684-5ccb-4198-a393-80c48adf3247","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JreruCqsjCiP8SGVXi7DUu","type":"tool_result","content":"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/799#issuecomment-7145041966","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"97fca8e0-9e16-44c5-a570-7090aa35f0d0","timestamp":"2026-11-24T21:31:25.185Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/799#issuecomment-7145041966","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"gitOperation":{"pr":{"number":799,"url":"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/799","action":"commented"}}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"51c9700c-ab02-4207-b46b-ba2e059adc75","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"main","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
{"parentUuid":"97fca8e0-9e16-44c5-a570-7090aa35f0d0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNU28qrAswx7qiNce95Q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MB6svzJXwoWjCwcruFM9UR","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"a497a5c16f766f926","summary":"Fix BG-2 review blockers on shared branch","message":"BG-2 review came back REQUEST CHANGES. Your commits are in PR #799 (Codex opened it from branch v1/bg2-schedules and added its own commits; the remote head is now ce242d020, ahead of your local 9f4cf34e). In /home/mike/nexus-wt/bg2 first `git fetch origin && git status && git merge origin/v1/bg2-schedules` (merge, never rebase; resolve conflicts keeping BOTH sides' intent; Codex's ce242d020 only fixes cli/test/schedule_missed.test.ts), then fix:\nB1 (blocking, reproduced): the unattended job's operator verifier is denied by the exec approval policy (cli/src/core/completion_oracle.ts:19-30 via spine_handlers.ts:216 `requiresDecision(\"exec\")`), so NO verifier ever runs and an unattended job can never reach VERIFIED; a seeded failing verifier ends BLOCKED only through stagnation (EXECUTION_FAILED) and the receipt never says the verifier was not run. Fix: when surface === \"unattended\" and the command equals the trimmed operator-configured `authoritativeVerifierCommand` (the one set at job creation), it is allowed without approval, exactly as the interactive path treats the operator's baseline (completion_oracle.ts ~199-212); managed `require_human` still applies; it still runs in the sandbox; any OTHER command (model-declared, discovered) stays denied. Then: (1) acceptance test rewrite: a seeded FAILING verifier must end BLOCKED with a reason that names the verifier failing (CANDIDATE_FAILED/verifier did not pass), and a seeded PASSING verifier must be able to end VERIFIED (use the scripted gateway; the reviewer saw 'verifier definition changed after its baseline' when a model edit touched an imported source: find out whether that is expected oracle behaviour and design the passing case so the edit is to the deliverable the oracle expects; if it is a real defect in the unattended path, report it); (2) a test that a model-declared or discovered verifier is still denied unattended, and that a schedule-record `verifier` is treated as the operator's own (document the trust boundary: a tampered schedule record can name a verifier command that then runs in the sandbox without approval: so the verifier string must be validated at `schedule add` time and again at fire time: bounded length, no newline/NUL, run through the same command rules as interactive; add a hostile test); (3) the denial text for unattended must not say 'Run with --yes or --mode auto' (say that unattended runs never approve and name the operator verifier mechanism); (4) when no verifier ran, the receipt/status says 'verifier not run' with the reason; (5) docs/SCHEDULES.md:34 (and any docs/RUNNER.md, manual text) corrected to what is true (`git status --short` etc. are not run unless it is the operator verifier or an allowed read-only command: check what actually runs); (6) stale 'run-once (the default)' text in cli/src/core/schedule_engine.ts:11,:15 and test comments now that the default is `report`; (7) non-blocking but cheap: reject cron expressions whose next two slots are under 5 minutes apart (matching the `every` floor), with a test; and make `scanSlots` cheaper (cap lower or closed form) so a 200k scan does not block the runner tick ~2.6 s; (8) `schedule run-now` must take the schedule lock for its running-job check (test the race by two concurrent run-now); (9) add the runner root (inbox, jobs, schedules) to the file tools' protected paths by absolute-path pattern if BG-1's existing mechanism allows (look at how security.ts DEFAULT_PROTECTED_PATHS handled `nexus/hooks.json`: HK-1 used a `nexus/...` suffix pattern), with a test.\nThen run, one at a time: every cli/test/schedule*.test.ts, the BG-1 files (ls cli/test | grep -iE 'runner|job'), fault_kill_mid_tool_call, completion_oracle-related tests (grep -l completion_oracle cli/test), approval_policy, security, protocol_schema, examples, leak_guard, check_requirements, tsc --noEmit, the complexity gate, check_invariants, check_doc_versions; changed files three times; mutate (copy aside, restore from the copy) the new guards. Commit `fix(schedule): <what>` + `Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>`; `git fetch origin` again, merge if it moved, plain `git push origin v1/bg2-schedules` (never force). Report under 300 words: changes with file:line, tests/mutations, commit hash, anything that surprised you.","type":"message","recipient":"a497a5c16f766f926","recipient_kind":"agent","content":"BG-2 review came back REQUEST CHANGES. Your commi…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2773,"cache_read_input_tokens":247238,"output_tokens":3973,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":195},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2773,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":3973,"cache_read_input_tokens":247238,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2773,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2773},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":11187,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01MB6svzJXwoWjCwcruFM9UR":{"to":"a497a5c16f766f926","summary":"Fix BG-2 review blockers on shared branch","message":"BG-2 review came back REQUEST CHANGES. Your commits are in PR #799 (Codex opened it from branch v1/bg2-schedules and added its own commits; the remote head is now ce242d020, ahead of your l