n at fire time: bounded length, no newline/NUL, run through the same command rules as interactive; add a hostile test); (3) the denial text for unattended must not say 'Run with --yes or --mode auto' (say that unattended runs never approve and name the operator verifier mechanism); (4) when no verifier ran, the receipt/status says 'verifier not run' with the reason; (5) docs/SCHEDULES.md:34 (and any docs/RUNNER.md, manual text) corrected to what is true (`git status --short` etc. are not run unless it is the operator verifier or an allowed read-only command: check what actually runs); (6) stale 'run-once (the default)' text in cli/src/core/schedule_engine.ts:11,:15 and test comments now that the default is `report`; (7) non-blocking but cheap: reject cron expressions whose next two slots are under 5 minutes apart (matching the `every` floor), with a test; and make `scanSlots` cheaper (cap lower or closed form) so a 200k scan does not block the runner tick ~2.6 s; (8) `schedule run-now` must take the schedule lock for its running-job check (test the race by two concurrent run-now); (9) add the runner root (inbox, jobs, schedules) to the file tools' protected paths by absolute-path pattern if BG-1's existing mechanism allows (look at how security.ts DEFAULT_PROTECTED_PATHS handled `nexus/hooks.json`: HK-1 used a `nexus/...` suffix pattern), with a test.\nThen run, one at a time: every cli/test/schedule*.test.ts, the BG-1 files (ls cli/test | grep -iE 'runner|job'), fault_kill_mid_tool_call, completion_oracle-related tests (grep -l completion_oracle cli/test), approval_policy, security, protocol_schema, examples, leak_guard, check_requirements, tsc --noEmit, the complexity gate, check_invariants, check_doc_versions; changed files three times; mutate (copy aside, restore from the copy) the new guards. Commit `fix(schedule): <what>` + `Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>`; `git fetch origin` again, merge if it moved, plain `git push origin v1/bg2-schedules` (never force). Report under 300 words: changes with file:line, tests/mutations, commit hash, anything that surprised you."}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011ChNU28ewCgXo3EvTGJBBp","requestRef":"c7ab13d9-575d-48d1-8852-acf63ee7dd64","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"6dc8d465-a7ff-4c88-8780-080cdb01cd0b","timestamp":"2026-11-24T21:31:34.459Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"main","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
