{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","hash":"1e1c63cf50c0b283e9109018f82ff6fcd318f3c821efac837248e4c2834ce164","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JreruCqsjCiP8SGVXi7DUu","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-code && cat > /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/rev799.md <<'EOF'\n**Independent review at `68bc626f43e42bf8c6a7bd3958649bc1e0396583` — REQUEST CHANGES. The head has since moved to `ce242d020` (only `cli/test/schedule_missed.test.ts`; it looks like the B2 fix, not run by the reviewer). B1 is untouched.**\n\n**Acceptance**\n1. **\"A scheduled run on a seeded failing verifier ends BLOCKED and says so\": met only coincidentally (run).** A failing `node --test` ends BLOCKED/`EXECUTION_FAILED` with \"STAGNATION_DETECTED\". A *passing* `node --test`, `npm test`, `true` and `git status --short` end identically: every `task_completed` fails with \"Verifier '…' requires operator approval (exec) … Run with --yes or --mode auto\". No verifier ever runs, so an unattended job can never reach VERIFIED. The receipt names the verifier and never says it was not run; the reason shown is stagnation, not the failing test. `schedule_failing_verifier` would pass the same way on a passing repo.\n2. **Approval denied, not blocked forever: met** (`schedule_approval_denied`; mutating `UnattendedApprovalPolicy` fails it).\n3. **Missed runs reported, not skipped: met in code**, but `schedule_missed` fails at this SHA (B2).\n4. **G-4 (no allow-always, fresh worktree, unattended flag, kill-and-resume): met** (`schedule_unattended`).\n\n**Blockers**\n- **B1, `cli/src/core/completion_oracle.ts:19-30` (via `spine_handlers.ts:216`):** the unattended verifier goes through `requiresDecision(\"exec\")` and is always denied. Fix: for `surface === \"unattended\"` and a command equal to the trimmed `authoritativeVerifierCommand`, allow it (managed `require_human` still applies; it still runs in the sandbox). Tried in a scratch edit by the reviewer: the verifier then ran; a failing one gave \"did not pass … CANDIDATE_FAILED\". VERIFIED was not reached (a model edit to an imported source file hit \"verifier definition changed after its baseline\", which may be the probe). Needs a test with a passing verifier, a denial text that is right for unattended runs (not \"Run with --yes or --mode auto\"), and a receipt that says \"verifier not run\" when it was not. `docs/SCHEDULES.md:34` says `git status --short` runs; it is denied, so that line is false.\n- **B2, `cli/test/schedule_missed.test.ts`:** `catches` omits `--on-missed run-once` after the default became `report`. Stale \"run-once (the default)\" text remains in `schedule_engine.ts:11`, `:15` and the test comment.\n\n**Non-blocking:** cron `* * * * *` is accepted (every minute; `every` has a 5-minute floor): reject slots under 5 minutes apart. A 200k-slot cron scan blocks the runner tick about 2.6 s and `fireDue` scans two or three times: use a closed form or a lower cap. `run-now` checks for a running job without the schedule lock (race not reproduced). `inbox` and `jobs` of the runner are not protected paths for the file tools: add an absolute-path pattern. State that a tampered schedule `verifier` becomes an unapproved sandboxed command, the same boundary the docs already state.\n\n**Structure:** one store, one parser, one `registerScheduleCommands` (`index.ts:1555`); no dead or duplicate code from the merged scaffold.\n**Tests at that head:** `schedule*` 54 pass and 1 fail (`schedule_missed`); BG-1 runner/job files, `fault_kill_mid_tool_call`, `protocol_schema` 8, `examples` 6, `leak_guard` 6, `check_requirements` 28, `security` 14, `security_gates` 10 pass; `tsc`, the complexity gate, `check_invariants`, `check_doc_versions` clean. **Mutations, all killed:** protected path, trust check, overlap check, burst guard, duplicate-slot guard, unattended policy.\n**Not checked:** symlinked store paths and 0644/0666 modes by hand, other-uid owner, a `kill -9` of my own, pause/remove during a run, live clock-forward runs, `nexus schedule add` through `run_command` in auto mode, managed-policy clamping, Node 22.\nEOF\ngh pr comment 799 --body-file /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/rev799.md | tail -1; echo \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ) REVIEW (claude-invariants-audit): #799 BG-2 REQUEST CHANGES at 68bc626f (head now ce242d020): B1 the unattended job's operator verifier is denied by the exec approval policy so no verifier ever runs and acceptance sentence 1 is met only through stagnation; fix in completion_oracle.ts; B2 test fixed by ce242d020. I am taking B1 (+ docs line, denial text, receipt wording, stale 'run-once default' comments) on branch v1/bg2-schedules from ~/nexus-wt/bg2: GPT-6 Codex, please do not push to that branch until I log the push here. DO NOT MERGE #799 meanwhile.\" >> \"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log\"","description":"Post the BG-2 review and log that I am taking the B1 fix"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MB6svzJXwoWjCwcruFM9UR","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"a497a5c16f766f926","summary":"Fix BG-2 review blockers on shared branch","message":"BG-2 review came back REQUEST CHANGES. Your commits are in PR #799 (Codex opened it from branch v1/bg2-schedules and added its own commits; the remote head is now ce242d020, ahead of your local 9f4cf34e). In /home/mike/nexus-wt/bg2 first `git fetch origin && git status && git merge origin/v1/bg2-schedules` (merge, never rebase; resolve conflicts keeping BOTH sides' intent; Codex's ce242d020 only fixes cli/test/schedule_missed.test.ts), then fix:\nB1 (blocking, reproduced): the unattended job's operator verifier is denied by the exec approval policy (cli/src/core/completion_oracle.ts:19-30 via spine_handlers.ts:216 `requiresDecision(\"exec\")`), so NO verifier ever runs and an unattended job can never reach VERIFIED; a seeded failing verifier ends BLOCKED only through stagnation (EXECUTION_FAILED) and the receipt never says the verifier was not run. Fix: when surface === \"unattended\" and the command equals the trimmed operator-configured `authoritativeVerifierCommand` (the one set at job creation), it is allowed without approval, exactly as the interactive path treats the operator's baseline (completion_oracle.ts ~199-212); managed `require_human` still applies; it still runs in the sandbox; any OTHER command (model-declared, discovered) stays denied. Then: (1) acceptance test rewrite: a seeded FAILING verifier must end BLOCKED with a reason that names the verifier failing (CANDIDATE_FAILED/verifier did not pass), and a seeded PASSING verifier must be able to end VERIFIED (use the scripted gateway; the reviewer saw 'verifier definition changed after its baseline' when a model edit touched an imported source: find out whether that is expected oracle behaviour and design the passing case so the edit is to the deliverable the oracle expects; if it is a real defect in the unattended path, report it); (2) a test that a model-declared or discovered verifier is still denied unattended, and that a schedule-record `verifier` is treated as the operator's own (document the trust boundary: a tampered schedule record can name a verifier command that then runs in the sandbox without approval: so the verifier string must be validated at `schedule add` time and again at fire time: bounded length, no newline/NUL, run through the same command rules as interactive; add a hostile test); (3) the denial text for unattended must not say 'Run with --yes or --mode auto' (say that unattended runs never approve and name the operator verifier mechanism); (4) when no verifier ran, the receipt/status says 'verifier not run' with the reason; (5) docs/SCHEDULES.md:34 (and any docs/RUNNER.md, manual text) corrected to what is true (`git status --short` etc. are not run unless it is the operator verifier or an allowed read-only command: check what actually runs); (6) stale 'run-once (the default)' text in cli/src/core/schedule_engine.ts:11,:15 and test comments now that the default is `report`; (7) non-blocking but cheap: reject cron expressions whose next two slots are under 5 minutes apart (matching the `every` floor), with a test; and make `scanSlots` cheaper (cap lower or closed form) so a 200k scan does not block the runner tick ~2.6 s; (8) `schedule run-now` must take the schedule lock for its running-job check (test the race by two concurrent run-now); (9) add the runner root (inbox, jobs, schedules) to the file tools' protected paths by absolute-path pattern if BG-1's existing mechanism allows (look at how security.ts DEFAULT_PROTECTED_PATHS handled `nexus/hooks.json`: HK-1 used a `nexus/...` suffix pattern), with a test.\nThen run, one at a time: every cli/test/schedule*.test.ts, the BG-1 files (ls cli/test | grep -iE 'runner|job'), fault_kill_mid_tool_call, completion_oracle-related tests (grep -l completion_oracle cli/test), approval_policy, security, protocol_schema, examples, leak_guard, check_requirements, tsc --noEmit, the complexity gate, check_invariants, check_doc_versions; changed files three times; mutate (copy aside, restore from the copy) the new guards. Commit `fix(schedule): <what>` + `Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>`; `git fetch origin` again, merge if it moved, plain `git push origin v1/bg2-schedules` (never force). Report under 300 words: changes with file:line, tests/mutations, commit hash, anything that surprised you."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
