{"parentUuid":"690ed662-8b74-4563-a730-c63d12efc62c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNU46hRPku2hazEUwwJu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The independent review of #799 (BG-2) came back request changes. The review is posted on the PR and the fix is now being made on the branch.\n\n**The blocker:** an unattended job's verifier is always denied by the command-approval policy, so no verifier ever runs.\n- A failing verifier ends BLOCKED, but only through stagnation (`EXECUTION_FAILED`), not through the failure.\n- A passing verifier ends the same way, so an unattended job can never reach VERIFIED.\n- The receipt never says the verifier was not run.\n- The docs wrongly say `git status --short` runs.\n- So the first acceptance sentence (\"a failing verifier ends BLOCKED and says so\") is met only by accident.\n\n**What I sent the builder:**\n- Let the operator-configured verifier run without approval when unattended; managed policy still applies and it still runs in the sandbox. Model-declared and discovered verifiers stay denied.\n- Rewrite the acceptance test so a failing verifier ends BLOCKED with the verifier named, and a passing one can reach VERIFIED.\n- Validate the verifier string when a schedule is created and again when it fires.\n- Fix the denial text, the receipt wording and the docs.\n- Smaller items: reject cron expressions that fire more than once every 5 minutes, make `run-now` take the schedule lock, and protect the runner directories from the agent's file tools.\n\n**Other findings in the review:**\n- One test, `schedule_missed`, failed at the reviewed commit. Codex's newer commit on the PR looks like it fixes that, but the reviewer didn't run it.\n- A 200,000-slot cron scan blocks the runner tick for about 2.6 seconds.\n\nThe acceptance sentences on denied approvals, missed runs and the unattended safeguards (G-4) are met. All six mutations the reviewer ran were caught.\n\nBecause Codex opened this PR, I logged that I'm taking the fix and asked it not to push to that branch meanwhile. #799 stays unmerged. The PF-3 fix to #797 is still waiting on its gate run. v1.3.0 is not landed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4151,"cache_read_input_tokens":250011,"output_tokens":700,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4151,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":700,"cache_read_input_tokens":250011,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4151,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4151},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011ChNU46VGsNb2o2uAnbkfF","requestRef":"02fdd43e-a670-4f26-a39b-5e7066e12757","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"cb0bef46-82f0-4227-b190-fceb70d913bd","timestamp":"2026-11-24T21:31:40.675Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"main","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
