{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-11-24T21:35:07.515Z","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>af7235dbcad738773</task-id>\n<output-file>/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666/tasks/af7235dbcad738773.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Implement PF-3 control socket\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>The `..hid` route is closed, and the fix is pushed as `a2f4376de` with a plain push, no force. `origin/v1/pf3-control-socket` matches that head. Neither `origin/release/v1.3.0` nor the PR branch had moved, so no merge was needed.\n\n**Changes**\n- `cli/src/sandbox.ts:275`: `isPathWithin` now treats a path as outside only when the relative path is `..`, starts with `../`, or is absolute. It is exported.\n- `cli/src/sidecar.ts`: the duplicate `isPathInside` is gone and the sidecar uses `isPathWithin`. The inside-workspace refusal now runs before the socket directory is created.\n- `cli/src/core/socket_files.ts`: new `socketRuntimeDirPath()` computes the planned path without touching the file system, and `realpathAllowingMissing()` resolves it.\n\n**Other `startsWith(\"..\")` sites (reported only, none in files this PR touches)**\n- `browser.ts`: 100, 120, 265\n- `core/authority.ts`: 637, 657, 692\n- `core/candidate.ts`: 1089\n- `core/observation_identity.ts`: 70, 93\n- `lsp.ts`: 406\n- `safe_fs.ts`: 39\n- `security.ts`: 797, 821, 1012\n- `skills.ts`: 332\n- `tester.ts`: 446\n- `workspace_trust.ts`: 39\n- `worktrunk/copy.ts`: 58\n- `worktrunk/paths.ts`: 122\n\n**Tests**\n- `sandbox_confine.test.ts` (19 tests): `isPathWithin` on `..hid`, `..`, and sibling-prefix paths, plus both bwrap profiles masking `&lt;ws&gt;/..hid`.\n- `sidecar_socket.test.ts` (13 tests): end to end for `XDG_RUNTIME_DIR` of `&lt;ws&gt;/run` and `&lt;ws&gt;/..hid`. Each must exit 1, print no `listening` line, and leave no `nexus` directory behind. It races a 20 s timer and fails with a clear message rather than hanging.\n- Both files passed three consecutive runs. `sidecar`, `protocol_parity`, `protocol_schema`, `protocol_doc`, `examples`, `leak_guard`, `sandbox_profiles` and `session_socket` pass. `tsc`, the complexity gate, invariants and doc versions are clean.\n\n**Mutations, all caught**\n- The old `startsWith` check, at both the unit and end-to-end levels.\n- Creating the directory before the check.\n- Removing the refusal.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>287651</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>10</tool_uses><duration_ms>735746</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
