{"parentUuid":"ddc9bc23-2cc4-4130-9e06-9e9ed65e1b74","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNUL2apokbAFmuAEumCB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Pg1Thh3jBzodZsYb9jYGMD","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Delta re-review PR #797 dotdot fix","subagent_type":"reviewer","prompt":"Short, time-boxed (about 15 minutes) independent delta review of GitHub PR #797 (PF-3 socket transport) in ~/nexus-code. Take the full head SHA from `gh pr view 797 --json headRefOid` (expected `a2f4376de…`), review exactly that, and say if it moved or merged. The previous independent review (PR comments; last: \"re-review at `03d8ea1b5` — REQUEST CHANGES\") found that `relative.startsWith(\"..\")` containment tests treated a segment such as `..hid` as outside the workspace, so `--listen` with `XDG_RUNTIME_DIR=<ws>/..hid` was not refused and the read-only bwrap profile exposed the token. The fix commit is `a2f4376de` (`git show --stat`, then the diff): `isPathWithin` in `cli/src/sandbox.ts:~275` (now exported), `cli/src/sidecar.ts` (uses it; the inside-workspace refusal runs BEFORE the socket directory is created), `cli/src/core/socket_files.ts` (`socketRuntimeDirPath`, `realpathAllowingMissing`), tests in `sandbox_confine.test.ts` and `sidecar_socket.test.ts`.\n\nBy RUNNING (throwaway HOME, temp dirs, no network, no inference): (1) `isPathWithin` on a table of hostile inputs: `..`, `../x`, `..x`, `..x/y`, `.../x`, `a/../..`, trailing slashes, absolute, a path equal to the base, the base's prefix sibling (`/ws2` vs `/ws`), symlinked components (is the check done on realpaths in the sidecar?), a not-yet-existing socket directory under a symlinked parent (`realpathAllowingMissing`: does it resolve the existing prefix and re-append the missing part correctly; can a symlink created later redirect it; race between check and mkdir). (2) end to end: `--listen` with `XDG_RUNTIME_DIR` = `<ws>/..hid`, `<ws>/run`, `<ws>` itself, a symlink inside the workspace pointing out, a symlink outside pointing into the workspace, the workspace's parent, `/tmp` fallback with workspace under /tmp: each refused (exit 1, no `listening`, no directory left behind) or accepted correctly (a directory genuinely outside). (3) with a legit outside directory and `--sandbox` real bwrap (check `bwrap --version`): both profiles still mask it (spot-check one `ls`/`cat`/`net.connect`). (4) Regression: spot-check wrong token → UNAUTHORIZED, second controller BUSY, modes 0600/0700/0600.\nRun at head, one at a time: `sandbox_confine`, `sidecar_socket`, `session_socket`, `sandbox_profiles`, `sidecar`, `protocol_doc`, `leak_guard`; `cd cli && npx tsc --noEmit -p .`. Mutate (copy aside, restore from the copy, never `git checkout`): revert `isPathWithin` to `startsWith(\"..\")`; create the directory before the check: tests must fail.\nRules: do NOT edit ~/nexus-code or existing worktrees. `git -C ~/nexus-code fetch origin && git -C ~/nexus-code worktree add --detach ~/nexus-wt/rev797c <full sha>`; `cp -a ~/nexus-code/cli/node_modules ~/nexus-wt/rev797c/cli/`; `mkdir -p ~/nexus-wt/rev797c/core/target/release && cp ~/nexus-wt/ls1b/core/target/release/{harness-core,nexus-tui} ~/nexus-wt/rev797c/core/target/release/`. Tests: `cd ~/nexus-wt/rev797c/cli && TMPDIR=/dev/shm HOME=$(mktemp -d) node --import tsx --test test/<name>.test.ts 2>&1 | tail -20`. Never touch the real ~/.nexus, ~/.config/nexus, /etc/nexus. Stop processes by their own pid, never `pkill -f`. No commits, pushes or GitHub comments. Remove probes and the worktree at the end. Shell is zsh (`bash -c` for loops); prefix `rtk proxy` if output looks filtered.\nReport under 300 words: verdict (ACCEPT / ACCEPT WITH FOLLOW-UPS / REQUEST CHANGES) at the exact SHA; whether the `..hid` route is closed (attack run); new findings with file:line, blocking or not; test counts; mutation results; what you did not check."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"sto