{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-11-24T21:44:41.951Z","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a0bff749f3ab5e366</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01Pg1Thh3jBzodZsYb9jYGMD</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666/tasks/a0bff749f3ab5e366.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Delta re-review PR #797 dotdot fix\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>**Verdict: ACCEPT WITH FOLLOW-UPS at `a2f4376de38e42a475974e0fb2e75e1a19ad22d5`.** The PR is still open and the head has not moved.\n\n**`..hid` route: closed.** I ran the real sidecar with `XDG_RUNTIME_DIR=&lt;ws&gt;/..hid`. It exited 1 with \"inside the workspace\", printed no `listening` line, and created no directory.\n\n**1. `isPathWithin` table (14 hostile inputs, all correct)**\n- `..`, `../x`, `a/../..`, `/ws2` against `/ws`, `/` and a relative path return false.\n- `..x`, `..x/y`, `.../x`, trailing slashes, the base itself and `a/../b` return true.\n- `realpathAllowingMissing` resolves the existing prefix and re-appends the missing part correctly under a symlink pointing out and one pointing in.\n- A dangling symlink or a regular file in the path is passed through unresolved. This is fail-safe, because creation then fails at the later private-directory check.\n- Check and use agree. `planned` is the same string `socketRuntimeDir` creates, and it is checked on realpaths. `ws/lnk/..` is normalised lexically both times, so it is refused.\n\n**2. End to end (a throwaway gateway served the model requests)**\n- Refused with exit 1, no `listening` line and nothing created: `&lt;ws&gt;/..hid`, `&lt;ws&gt;/run`, `&lt;ws&gt;` itself, a symlink outside pointing into the workspace, `outside/nexus` as a symlink into the workspace (dangling and existing), `ws/lnk2/..`, and workspace=`/tmp` with the `/tmp/nexus-sockets-&lt;uid&gt;` fallback.\n- A symlink inside the workspace pointing out is also exit 1, from the private-directory (`lstat`) check, and nothing is created.\n- The workspace's parent was refused only because `/dev/shm` is not mode 0700. A private parent would be accepted. That is correct, since the socket directory is then outside the workspace.\n- A genuinely outside directory, and a workspace under `/tmp` using the fallback, were accepted and listened.\n\n**3. bwrap 0.13.1:** the existing `sidecar_socket` test for the descriptor mask ran unskipped and passed. It only exercises the default profile with a `cat`/`ls` model command. I did not test `net.connect`, the read-only profile or a manual `ls`/`cat`.\n\n**4. Regression:** I did not spot-check wrong token → UNAUTHORIZED, second controller BUSY, or modes 0600/0700/0600 by hand. The `sidecar_socket` and `session_socket` suites pass.\n\n**Tests and tsc:** `sandbox_confine` 19/19, `sidecar_socket` 13/13, `session_socket` 33/33, `sandbox_profiles` 14/14, `sidecar` 65/65, `protocol_doc` 6/6 and `leak_guard` 6/6. `tsc --noEmit` is clean.\n\n**Mutations (both restored from copies, clean tree):**\n- `isPathWithin` reverted to `startsWith(\"..\")`: `sandbox_confine` failed 1, `sidecar_socket` failed 1.\n- Directory created before the check: `sidecar_socket` failed 2.\n\n**Findings:** none blocking. Non-blocking: `socket_files.ts` still uses `catch (error: any)` and `realpathAllowingMissing` has no direct unit test. Its behaviour is only covered through the sidecar tests.\n\n**Not checked:** a concurrent symlink swap racing the check and the `mkdir`, Docker, Node 22, and `net.connect` under the sandbox.\n\nI removed the worktree and the probe directories. The real `/tmp/nexus-sockets-1000` was left empty.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>50513</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>20</tool_uses><duration_ms>555820</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
