{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-11-24T22:14:21.119Z","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a497a5c16f766f926</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01MB6svzJXwoWjCwcruFM9UR</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666/tasks/a497a5c16f766f926.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Implement BG-2 schedules\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>All nine review items are done, and I pushed `c5182bbc7` to `v1/bg2-schedules` with a plain push on top of remote tip `3b6cdf785`. The schedule, BG-1, completion-oracle, approval, security, protocol and example tests passed. `tsc`, the complexity gate, `check_invariants`, `check_doc_versions` and `check_requirements` are clean. The full suite was run before I had to rebuild the branch on top of the newer remote tip. After rebuilding, I re-ran only `schedule`, `schedule_store`, `schedule_hostile`, `unattended_verifier`, `schedule_engine`, `tsc` and the receipt schema check.\n\n**Changes, in review order**\n- **B1:** `completion_oracle.ts` (`isUnattendedOperatorVerifier`, called from `ensureVerifierApprovedImpl`) now lets an unattended run start only the trimmed operator `--verifier`. Any other command, any other surface, or managed `require_human` for commands still denies. The denial text in `spine_handlers.ts` no longer says \"--yes\".\n- **B1(4):** `job_receipt.ts` — the receipt's `verifier` gains `status` and `detail`, so `NOT_RUN` says why. A job that did not complete has its summary say the verifier failed or was not run. Ledger entries added, version stays 1.\n- **B1(1):** a failing verifier now ends BLOCKED with reason `VERIFIER_FAILED`. A passing one ends COMPLETE with the unit VERIFIED. The \"definition changed\" failure was my own scripted `write_file` missing `overwrite: true`, not an oracle defect.\n- **B1(2):** `job_submission.ts` (`verifierProblem`) checks length, no newline or NUL, the security tripwire and `command_rules.json` at `schedule add` and at every fire.\n- **B1(5, 6):** docs corrected. A read-only run does not run its verifier at all, which is why `git status --short` appeared to work. Stale default text removed.\n- **7:** `schedule.ts` — `validateTrigger` refuses cron expressions with slots under 5 minutes apart. `MAX_SLOT_SCAN` is now 20,000 (the 200k cron scan took about 2.6 s).\n- **8:** `schedule_cli.ts` — `run-now` checks for a running job and waits for runner acceptance while holding the schedule lock.\n- **9:** `security.ts` — `runnerRoot()` is a protected path, and absolute patterns now cover everything below them.\n- `schedule add` also warns when a verifier is given on a read-only schedule.\n\n**Tests added:** `unattended_verifier` (4), plus new cases in `schedule_hostile` (9 total), `schedule_cli` (8), `schedule_failing_verifier` (3) and `schedule` (15).\n\n**Mutations:** all 9 new guards (listed below), each killed by the tests.\n- surface check\n- exact-match check\n- `require_human`\n- tripwire\n- command rules\n- cron floor\n- run-now lock\n- runner-root protection\n- receipt status\n\n**Surprises**\n- Another agent kept resetting and merging in this worktree. My first edits were wiped once, and my squash briefly swallowed their merge. I rebuilt my change as a patch on the remote tip, so the pushed commit contains only my 21-file delta.\n- `cli/dist` goes stale after any src edit, which makes the example tests fail with \"Cannot find package 'tsx'\". That caused my first example-test failures.\n- The BG-2 verifier test isolates the operator's `--verifier` path, not discovered verifiers: `--verifier` is unset when the job is made, so the discovered case is covered only at the policy level in `unattended_verifier`.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>476085</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>198</tool_uses><duration_ms>6927143</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
