ire and `command_rules.json` at `schedule add` and at every fire.\n- **B1(5, 6):** docs corrected. A read-only run does not run its verifier at all, which is why `git status --short` appeared to work. Stale default text removed.\n- **7:** `schedule.ts` — `validateTrigger` refuses cron expressions with slots under 5 minutes apart. `MAX_SLOT_SCAN` is now 20,000 (the 200k cron scan took about 2.6 s).\n- **8:** `schedule_cli.ts` — `run-now` checks for a running job and waits for runner acceptance while holding the schedule lock.\n- **9:** `security.ts` — `runnerRoot()` is a protected path, and absolute patterns now cover everything below them.\n- `schedule add` also warns when a verifier is given on a read-only schedule.\n\n**Tests added:** `unattended_verifier` (4), plus new cases in `schedule_hostile` (9 total), `schedule_cli` (8), `schedule_failing_verifier` (3) and `schedule` (15).\n\n**Mutations:** all 9 new guards (listed below), each killed by the tests.\n- surface check\n- exact-match check\n- `require_human`\n- tripwire\n- command rules\n- cron floor\n- run-now lock\n- runner-root protection\n- receipt status\n\n**Surprises**\n- Another agent kept resetting and merging in this worktree. My first edits were wiped once, and my squash briefly swallowed their merge. I rebuilt my change as a patch on the remote tip, so the pushed commit contains only my 21-file delta.\n- `cli/dist` goes stale after any src edit, which makes the example tests fail with \"Cannot find package 'tsx'\". That caused my first example-test failures.\n- The BG-2 verifier test isolates the operator's `--verifier` path, not discovered verifiers: `--verifier` is unset when the job is made, so the discovered case is covered only at the policy level in `unattended_verifier`.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>476085</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>198</tool_uses><duration_ms>6927143</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4