{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","hash":"9678faea554494653e42502d1c6f176de29d587e9b3678ff1020e484fd45b268","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SGmW3UsqYJ4jAH8zgUwTgn","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-code && cat > /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/rev799b.md <<'EOF'\n**Independent re-review at `c5182bbc70b65dd1f3f9d2522ba324a9c5144eee` — ACCEPT WITH FOLLOW-UPS.** The head has since moved to `1c840a53e`, a test-only commit that fixes the one red test the reviewer found (`job_receipt_schema`, 2 of 6 failed at `c5182bbc7`); the reviewer did not run at it, so acceptance depends on that commit being green.\n\n**Prior blockers: B1 closed, B2 closed (run).** `unattended_verifier` 4/4. A seeded passing verifier reaches COMPLETE/VERIFIED; a failing one ends BLOCKED with reason `VERIFIER_FAILED` and the receipt names the verifier with status FAILED; a read-only job does not run its verifier and the receipt says `NOT_RUN`; the denial text is unattended-specific; `docs/SCHEDULES.md:34` is corrected; `schedule_missed` passes.\n\n**Authority of the new allow (run).** Exact match of the trimmed operator `--verifier` only: doubled space, tab, case change, trailing `;`, `&&` chains, a `FOO=1` prefix, zero-width and Cyrillic look-alikes, quotes, `# x` and `--` were all denied. Only the `unattended` surface can reach it (set at `unattended.ts:90`); repl, headless, tui, acp and mcp never do. Managed `require_human` still denies. `verifierProblem` runs at `nexus job` submission, at `schedule add` and at every fire.\n**What a hostile repository or model can do through the operator verifier:** edits to `./verify.sh` or `package.json` are refused (`VERIFICATION_CONFIG_PROTECTED`), but a model can still write a new test file that the unattended `node --test` then runs without approval. The reviewer did this: it ran as the operator's uid inside the sandbox; the network connect failed (ENETUNREACH), HOME was an empty fake directory, `~/.ssh` and `~/.config` were absent, and writes to `../` and `/dev/shm` stayed inside the sandbox. The job ended BLOCKED `REGRESSION_FREE`. No route for another command, allow-always, auto, a widened level, an untrusted workspace or a burst replay was found. The docs do not yet say that repository-controlled or model-written code runs unapproved under the operator verifier.\n\n**Follow-ups (non-blocking, being fixed on the branch):** (1) `job_receipt.ts` `verifierState` says `NOT_RUN` / \"Verifier not run\" when the verifier ran and passed but the job ended `REGRESSION_FREE`. (2) `schedule.ts:113-119`: the cron floor skips the midnight wrap when day-of-month or day-of-week is restricted: `59,0 23,0 1,2 * *` is accepted and fires one minute apart. (3) `job_runner.ts:99` `submissionProblem` does not call `verifierProblem`, so a hand-written inbox request skips it (own-account boundary, but cheap to close). (4) `0 0 31 2 *` is accepted and never fires: reject at `add`. (5) add the missing documentation sentence.\n\n**Also run:** the cron floor rejects `* * * * *`, `*/2`, `0,3` and accepts `*/5` and hourly; leap-day, yearly and a 2031 once compute; `runnerRoot()` protection held for absolute inbox/jobs paths, a symlink, a relative path from a workspace that is HOME, `..`, uppercase and a double slash; the PR is nine commits on the remote tip with none dropped and no duplicate schedule code; ledger entries keep version 1; the schema `--check`, `tsc`, the complexity gate, `check_invariants`, `check_doc_versions` are clean. **Tests at that head:** `schedule*` 64, `unattended*` 21, `protocol_schema` 8, `run_json_contract` 15, `examples` 7, `leak_guard` 6, `check_requirements` 28, `approval_policy` 16, `security` 14, `security_gates` 10, `fault_kill_mid_tool_call` 1; one failure (`job_receipt_schema`, since fixed). **Mutations, all killed:** surface check, exact-match check, `require_human`, fire-time `verifierProblem`, `runnerRoot()`, cron floor.\n**Not checked by hand:** the concurrent `run-now` race, a `kill -9` of the reviewer's own, a tampered record with an enormous verifier, `command_rules.json` changed between fires, Node 22.\nEOF\ngh pr comment 799 --body-file /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/rev799b.md | tail -1; echo \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ) REVIEW (claude-invariants-audit): #799 BG-2 ACCEPT WITH FOLLOW-UPS at c5182bbc7 (head moved to 1c840a53e, test-only). Follow-ups (receipt wording when the verifier ran, cron floor midnight wrap, inbox verifierProblem, Feb-31 reject, doc sentence on repo-written tests under the operator verifier) are being pushed by me to v1/bg2-schedules; please do not push there; I will merge after green.\" >> \"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log\"","description":"Post the BG-2 re-review and log the follow-up work"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Y2JL6sxr4NbuA1XgzhKuwR","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"a497a5c16f766f926","summary":"Close BG-2 follow-ups from re-review","message":"BG-2 re-review: ACCEPT WITH FOLLOW-UPS at c5182bbc7. Please finish these five small items on v1/bg2-schedules (worktree /home/mike/nexus-wt/bg2: `git fetch origin && git status`; the remote head is now 1c840a53e (test-only fix of job_receipt_schema.test.ts by another author); merge origin/v1/bg2-schedules and origin/release/v1.3.0, never rebase, never `git reset` over others' commits; if the worktree has been disturbed, rebuild as a patch on the remote tip as you did before). (1) cli/src/core/job_receipt.ts `verifierState`: it says NOT_RUN / \"Verifier not run\" when the verifier DID run and passed but the job ended REGRESSION_FREE (\"Passing test run did not cover the modified deliverables\"). Record that the verifier ran (status PASSED with the detail) or reword; test with a model