{"parentUuid":"8543bc90-0a07-4508-8c63-9640aa357de6","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNYh31vLQeq9zoiwJufP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The re-review of #799 (BG-2 schedules) came back accept with follow-ups, and the review is posted on the PR. The first two blockers are closed: the unattended verifier now runs and a failing one ends BLOCKED with the verifier named, and `schedule_missed` passes. The reviewer also tried to widen the new \"operator verifier runs without approval\" rule and found no route for another command, allow-always, auto, a higher permission level, an untrusted workspace or a missed-run replay.\n\n**What a hostile repository or model can do through the operator verifier:** it can't edit the verifier's own definition files, but a model can write a new test file and the unattended `node --test` then runs it without approval. The reviewer did this. It ran sandboxed with no network, an empty home directory and no host writes, and the job still ended BLOCKED. The docs don't say this yet.\n\nFive follow-ups, none blocking, are being pushed by the BG-2 builder:\n- A receipt can say \"Verifier not run\" when the verifier actually ran and passed.\n- The cron frequency check misses some midnight and month wraps, for example `59,0 23,0 1,2 * *`, which fires one minute apart.\n- A hand-written inbox request skips the verifier check.\n- `0 0 31 2 *` (Feb 31) is accepted but never fires.\n- The missing docs sentence about repository-written tests above.\n\nThe branch head also moved to a test-only commit that fixes the one red test the reviewer found; the reviewer did not run at it, so I'll confirm it's green before merging. I told Codex in the log not to push to that branch meanwhile.\n\nv1.3.0 is not landed. Release CI on the PF-3 merge is still being watched, and HK-3 (#798) and SB-1 (#795) are open from other agents."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3618,"cache_read_input_tokens":275199,"output_tokens":589,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3618,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":589,"cache_read_input_tokens":275199,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3618,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3618},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011ChNYh2qF6it82wP7FKsa6","requestRef":"3f1d1edf-ed1f-4246-abc0-196f179945ff","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"2b77fb95-b092-42cd-8bdb-6430c129dba1","timestamp":"2026-11-24T22:32:28.429Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"v1/bg3-trust-abuse-model","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
