{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-11-24T23:00:14.342Z","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a497a5c16f766f926</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01Y2JL6sxr4NbuA1XgzhKuwR</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666/tasks/a497a5c16f766f926.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Implement BG-2 schedules\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>All five follow-ups are done and pushed as `0fe359008` on `v1/bg2-schedules` (plain push, no force). The remote head `1c840a53e` was already merged, and `origin/release/v1.3.0` had nothing new.\n\n**Changes**\n1. **Verifier status:** `job_receipt.ts` `verifierState` now reads a blocked REGRESSION_FREE unit as `PASSED` with that detail. NO_TESTS_EXECUTED reads as `PASSED` with its own detail. VERIFIER_FAILED reads as `FAILED` and a timeout as `TIMED_OUT`. The summary says the verifier passed without establishing the change, not \"not run\".\n2. **Cron floor:** `schedule.ts` `cronMinGapMinutes` now checks consecutive matching days over 2024–2027, so month ends, leap day and year end are covered. `59,0 23,0 1,2 * *` and `0,4 * * * *` are refused; `0 0 31 * *` is accepted.\n3. **Request verifiers:** `verifierProblem` moved to the new `verifier_check.ts`. `submissionProblem` in `job_runner.ts` now calls it, so a hand-written inbox request with a refused verifier is rejected.\n4. **Never-matching cron:** `validateTrigger` refuses it with \"never matches a date\", so `schedule add` and hand-edited records both reject `0 0 31 2 *`.\n5. **Docs:** `docs/SCHEDULES.md` and the manual state plainly that the operator verifier runs repository and model-written code without approval, inside the sandbox, with the advice to use a narrow verifier for untrusted repositories.\n\n**Tests added**\n- A scripted run that ends REGRESSION_FREE and must show `PASSED`, never NOT_RUN.\n- Cron floor and never-matches tables in `schedule.test.ts`, and a 31 February row in `schedule_cli.test.ts`.\n- A runner test refusing a request that carries `rm -rf /` as its verifier.\n\n**Mutations:** 4 guards (the REGRESSION_FREE branch, the cross-day gap check, the never-matches check, the request-verifier check), each caught by its tests.\n\n**Runs:** every `schedule*` file and `unattended_verifier` passed three times. The BG-1 files, `fault_kill_mid_tool_call`, `protocol_schema`, `run_json_contract`, `leak_guard` and `security` passed once, and the example tests passed after a rebuild. `tsc`, the complexity gate, `check_invariants`, `check_doc_versions`, `check_requirements` and the three schema `--check` generators are clean.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>497970</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>26</tool_uses><duration_ms>1671448</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
