{"parentUuid":"9f325d10-4390-455c-a8f4-d6648aa43418","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNaqx6EHKSbiXd23zv5S","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0153eG5JQNi6HTDcWCdtErES","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-code && echo \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ) NOTE (claude-invariants-audit): #799 was MERGED (ab5eb011) at 1c840a53e, BEFORE my follow-up commit 0fe359008 (receipt wording when the verifier ran, cron floor midnight wrap, runner inbox verifier check, Feb-31 reject, docs sentence) reached it: it was announced here as pending and the PR was merged anyway. I am opening a follow-up PR from v1/bg2-schedules (0fe359008 on top of the merged head) now.\" >> \"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log\"; git diff --stat origin/release/v1.3.0...origin/v1/bg2-schedules | tail -3; cat > /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/pr_bg2f.md <<'EOF'\nFollow-ups from the independent re-review of #799 (ACCEPT WITH FOLLOW-UPS at `c5182bbc7`). #799 merged at `1c840a53e` before this commit reached it.\n\n1. **Receipt wording.** A job that ended `REGRESSION_FREE` (the verifier ran and passed but did not cover the change) said \"Verifier not run\". It now reads `PASSED` with that detail; `NO_TESTS_EXECUTED` reads `PASSED` with its own detail; `VERIFIER_FAILED` reads `FAILED`; a timeout `TIMED_OUT`.\n2. **Cron floor.** The 5-minute floor skipped the midnight wrap when day-of-month or day-of-week is restricted: `59,0 23,0 1,2 * *` fired one minute apart. The gap is now checked over consecutive matching days across 2024–2027 (month ends, leap day, year end). `0,4 * * * *` is refused; `0 0 31 * *` is accepted.\n3. **Runner request check.** `submissionProblem` now applies the same verifier check as `nexus job` and `schedule add` (`verifier_check.ts`, moved out of `job_submission.ts`), so a hand-written inbox request cannot carry a verifier those commands would refuse.\n4. **Never-matching cron** (`0 0 31 2 *`) is refused at `schedule add` and in hand-edited records.\n5. **Docs** (`SCHEDULES.md`, manual): the operator verifier runs repository-controlled and model-written code without approval, inside the sandbox (no network, empty fake home, writes do not reach the host); use a narrow verifier for untrusted repositories.\n\nTests: a scripted run ending REGRESSION_FREE must show `PASSED`; cron floor and never-matches tables; a 31 February row; a runner test refusing a request whose verifier is `rm -rf /`. Four guards mutated, each caught. Every `schedule*` file and `unattended_verifier` passed three runs; BG-1 files, `fault_kill_mid_tool_call`, `protocol_schema`, `run_json_contract`, `leak_guard`, `security` once; `tsc`, the complexity gate, invariants, doc versions, `check_requirements` and the three schema `--check` generators are clean.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\nEOF\ngit fetch -q origin && git -C ~/nexus-wt/bg2 merge -q origin/release/v1.3.0 --no-edit 2>&1 | tail -2; git -C ~/nexus-wt/bg2 push -q origin v1/bg2-schedules 2>&1 | tail -1; u=$(gh pr create --base release/v1.3.0 --head v1/bg2-schedules --title \"fix(schedule): BG-2 review follow-ups (receipt wording, cron floor, request verifier check, docs)\" --body-file /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/pr_bg2f.md | tail -1); echo \"$u\"","description":"Log the out-of-order merge and open a follow-up PR with the commit that missed it","timeout":120000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":655,"cache_read_input_tokens":283497,"output_tokens":1741,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":198},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":655,"ephem