w applies the same verifier check as `nexus job` and `schedule add` (`verifier_check.ts`, moved out of `job_submission.ts`), so a hand-written inbox request cannot carry a verifier those commands would refuse.\n4. **Never-matching cron** (`0 0 31 2 *`) is refused at `schedule add` and in hand-edited records.\n5. **Docs** (`SCHEDULES.md`, manual): the operator verifier runs repository-controlled and model-written code without approval, inside the sandbox (no network, empty fake home, writes do not reach the host); use a narrow verifier for untrusted repositories.\n\nTests: a scripted run ending REGRESSION_FREE must show `PASSED`; cron floor and never-matches tables; a 31 February row; a runner test refusing a request whose verifier is `rm -rf /`. Four guards mutated, each caught. Every `schedule*` file and `unattended_verifier` passed three runs; BG-1 files, `fault_kill_mid_tool_call`, `protocol_schema`, `run_json_contract`, `leak_guard`, `security` once; `tsc`, the complexity gate, invariants, doc versions, `check_requirements` and the three schema `--check` generators are clean.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\nEOF\ngit fetch -q origin && git -C ~/nexus-wt/bg2 merge -q origin/release/v1.3.0 --no-edit 2>&1 | tail -2; git -C ~/nexus-wt/bg2 push -q origin v1/bg2-schedules 2>&1 | tail -1; u=$(gh pr create --base release/v1.3.0 --head v1/bg2-schedules --title \"fix(schedule): BG-2 review follow-ups (receipt wording, cron floor, request verifier check, docs)\" --body-file /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/pr_bg2f.md | tail -1); echo \"$u\"","description":"Log the out-of-order merge and open a follow-up PR with the commit that missed it","timeout":120000}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011ChNaqwupZPxk1EpGWg2ae","requestRef":"b79accb9-b34a-4d43-b70a-aa8e270b1498","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"1a23d9c4-a248-4650-b739-c428a