{"parentUuid":"e9250cce-ac64-4b19-bba1-cb96f8bd4cac","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNbdwq8fWZkpdkFw788Z","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The BG-2 review follow-ups are now merged into `release/v1.3.0` as `d9b0f5a6` (#802). The required checks were green at the exact head, and release CI was green at the tip first. I read the merged state back after the merge call.\n\n#799 had already been merged by another session at `1c840a53e`, before my follow-up commit (`0fe359008`) reached it, even though the log said that commit was pending. The follow-up PR carried it in. It covers:\n- the receipt wording when the verifier ran;\n- the cron minimum-gap check across month and year wraps;\n- the runner's check of a hand-written request's verifier;\n- rejecting a cron that never matches a date, such as Feb 31;\n- the docs sentence that the operator verifier runs repository-written code without approval.\n\nThe independent reviewer accepted #799 with these as follow-ups, and I read the follow-up diff against that review; no second reviewer saw it. Four mutations of the new guards were each caught.\n\nWith PF-3 and BG-2 now merged, what's left for the release is:\n- **Open from others:** SB-1 (#795, Codex) and HK-3 (#798).\n- **Still unclaimed:** MT-2 slices 2–4.\n- **Owed by me:** my own check of the merged HK-1 head and the readiness re-measure.\n- **Then:** the RC, the merge to `main`, and the release.\n\nv1.3.0 is not landed yet."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":312,"cache_read_input_tokens":286583,"output_tokens":471,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":312,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"