{"parentUuid":"96af74fd-d518-48ae-aa6b-ec07b827e28e","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PreToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_01SsuCNN6BcZ8oSHhEgFCvgM","hookEvent":"PreToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"claude-mem hook claude-code file-context","durationMs":399},"type":"attachment","uuid":"945de9c8-5db3-4401-80ed-3af737a81c33","timestamp":"2026-11-24T23:11:29.854Z","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"v1/bg3-trust-abuse-model","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
{"parentUuid":"96af74fd-d518-48ae-aa6b-ec07b827e28e","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"aac5bc77-7cbb-4a24-9dad-12eb33149bbd","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SsuCNN6BcZ8oSHhEgFCvgM","type":"tool_result","content":"ready\n- **Handlers come from five places:**\n  1. `spine.registerHandler` in `setupSpineHandlers` (`core/spine_handlers.ts:61,502,729-969`, ts-native tools);\n  2. `registry.setHandler` in `registerBridgeCapabilities` (`tools.ts:1827-1853`, rust_rpc plus six listed tools);\n  3. `capability.handler`;\n  4. `context.defaultHandler` built in dispatch for MCP, plugin and pipeline (`dispatch_tool_call.ts:672-692`);\n  5. `context.bridge.executeTool`.\n\n  The resolution order is in `ExecutionSpine.execute` (`core/spine.ts:562-584`).\n- The **model-visible list** is built separately in `AutonomousAgent.effectiveTools` (`agent.ts:1335-1365`): `HARNESS_TOOLS` filtered by\n  group and skills, plus agent-local specs, MCP and plugin definitions, then role allow/deny and delegated allow-list filters.\n  `parser.ts:6` builds `KNOWN_TOOLS` from `HARNESS_TOOLS`; serve-mcp lists `HARNESS_TOOLS` minus two (`mcp.ts:1062`); the ACP kind table\n  covers `HARNESS_TOOLS` (`acp/mapping.ts:103`).\n- **Dispatch** `dispatchToolCallImpl` (`core/dispatch_tool_call.ts:37-935`, one 900-line function bound to the agent with `this: any`).\n  Phases in order:\n  1. args parse and repair (`:45-87`);\n  2. delegated allow-list (`:97`), role allow/deny (`:124-151`), skill constraints and integrity (`:154-221`), flight (`:234`), deletion\n     guard (`:239`);\n  3. effect from the registry (`:269-271`), checkpoint read-only fallback (`:275`);\n  4. managed policy and context clamp (`:317-357`), forbidden (`:358`), egress allowlist (`:363`), verification-edit decision\n     (`:391-440`), CS-9 rules (`:441-496`), ask decision (`:497-512`), skill confirm (`:513`);\n  5. needs-input / confirm (`:540-668`);\n  6. plugin notify and execution context (`:670-692`), journal and baseline capture (`:693-743`), `spine.execute` (`:744-768`);\n  7. after: eval receipts, journal end, `notifyToolResult`, `run_tests` attempts (`:807`), file and diff tracking (`:851-872`), VR-3 events\n     (`:873-876`), flight (`:889`), return (`:934-935`).\n\n  The sandbox is applied inside the bridge (`tools.ts:1680-1745`), not in dispatch.\n- **Complexity gate:** `cli/critical-complexity-baseline.json` (revision `4d9996d4…`) with `cli/scripts/check_critical_complexity.ts`.\n  Measured today, equal to the baseline (**zero headroom**): `dispatchToolCallImpl` CC 288 / nesting 6 / 900 lines; `runTurnImpl` 324/5;\n  `runSubagent` 70/4; `compactNowImpl` 17/3; `driveOperation` 17/3. The checker reads the function **by file and name at the baseline\n  revision and at HEAD** (`:175-196`, `findTargetFunction` throws unless exactly one match), so renaming or moving it fails closed (exit 2).\n  `cli/test/critical_complexity.test.ts:37-42` pins the revision and `rows.length === 5`.\n- **Characterization coverage today:**\n  - `capabilities.test.ts` (36 tools, registration);\n  - `lsp_shape.test.ts:67` (description sizes);\n  - `tool_groups.test.ts`, `role_deny_lists.test.ts`, `acp_mapping.test.ts`, `tool_grammar*.test.ts`, `context_convergence.test.ts`\n    (claimed);\n  - dispatch: `command_rules_dispatch`, `managed_policy_dispatch`, `vllm_nullable_dispatch`, `approval_policy`, `injection_gate`,\n    `security_gates`, `sandbox_denial_events`, `subagent_delegation_authority` (claimed), `agt111_subagent_parity`;\n  - G-3 spread across `acp_stdio.test.ts:182,221`, `sidecar.test.ts:232-351`, `verify_hostile.test.ts` (claimed),\n    `managed_policy_*`, `repl_approval_e2e`.\n  - **No test snapshots the full model-visible list per context, and none snapshots the handler resolution per tool.** Those come first.\n\n### Design\n- **`cli/src/core/tool_registry.ts` (new):**\n  ```ts\n  export type ToolBinding =\n    | { kind: \"native\"; handler: CapabilityHandler }   // today's spine.registerHandler tools\n    | { kind: \"bridge\" }                                // RustCoreBridge.executeTool (today's registerBridgeCapabilities set)\n    | { kind: \"extension\" };                            // MCP / plugin via the plugin pipeline (today's defaultHandler)\n  export type OfferRule = \"always\" | \"group\" | \"skills\" | \"objective\" | \"requirements\" | \"mask\" | \"until-all-groups\";\n  export interface RegisteredTool { spec: CanonicalCapability; binding: ToolBinding; offer: OfferRule }\n  export class ToolRegistry {\n    register(t: RegisteredTool): void;      // throws: duplicate name; spec.handler set (one source only); extension effect not exec|egress; non-extension without binding\n    resolve(name: string): RegisteredTool | undefined;\n    modelTools(ctx: OfferContext): ToolDefinition[];  // exactly today's effectiveTools order and filters\n    capabilities(): CapabilityRegistry;     // adapter: existing getByToolName callers keep working\n  }\n  ```\n  The order is the insertion order of today's `effectiveTools` array: `HARNESS_TOOLS` order, then `ENABLE_TOOLS`, `READ_OBJECTIVE`,\n  `REQUIREMENTS`, `READ_FINDINGS`, `READ_ARCHIVE`, `READ_TOOL_OUTPUT`, MCP, plugins. `HARNESS_TOOLS`, `KNOWN_TOOLS` and the serve-mcp list\n  are derived from the registry's baseline set, so they are identical.\n- **One execution path:** `ExecutionSpine.execute` resolves the handler only through `registry.resolve(name).binding`. The fallback chain at\n  `spine.ts:566-569` and the `context.defaultHandler` and bridge fallbacks are removed **only after** the slice-1 table proves equivalence.\n  Pipeline stages named as the unit asks: **approve** (dispatch decide/confirm), **sandbox** (unchanged, inside `bridge.executeTool` for\n  `bridge` bindings), **run** (`spine.execute`), **hooks** (`pluginManager.notifyToolCall` before execution,\n  `notifyToolResult`/`executeToolPipeline` after; HK-1 attaches here later).\n- **Dispatch decomposition** (behaviour-preserving, side-effect order preserved), in new `cli/src/core/tool_pipeline.ts`:\n  - `parseToolArguments(call)` → `{args, structurallyRepaired}`;\n  - `admitToolCall(agent, name, args, ...)` → `{refuse: receipt} | {ok}` for phases 2-3;\n  - `decideToolCall(agent, ...)` → `{refuse} | {ask: question} | {run}` for phase 4;\n  - `confirmToolCall(...)` for phase 5;\n  - `executeToolCall(...)` for phase 6;\n  - `afterToolCall(...)` for phase 7.\n\n  **`dispatchToolCallImpl` stays in `core/dispatch_tool_call.ts` under the same name and signature** as a straight-line orchestrator\n  (target CC ≤ 20, nesting ≤ 2). The baseline then measures a much smaller function against 288/6 and passes.\n- **Baseline handling (D-MT2-2):** do not edit `critical-complexity-baseline.json` during slices 2-3. The extracted functions are new and\n  untracked. Slice 4 is one small PR, made after the last extraction merges. It:\n  - moves `baselineRevision` to that merge commit (an ancestor of HEAD);\n  - adds `decideToolCall`, `admitToolCall`, `confirmToolCall`, `executeToolCall` and `afterToolCall` (`file: cli/src/core/tool_pipeline.ts`)\n    to `functions`;\n  - updates `critical_complexity.test.ts` (revision; `rows.length` 5 → 10);\n  - pastes the checker's before/after table into the PR.\n\n  This is tighten-only: the gate had already proved every tracked function ≤ the old baseline, so advancing can only lower the\n  references. It changes the gate's reference commit, so it lands only with the owner's acknowledgement (merge role per memory). If\n  declined, the extracted functions stay untracked and `dispatchToolCallImpl` keeps its new low numbers against the old reference.\n- **No new grant path:**\n  - the registry has no API that lowers an effect, marks a tool approval-free or overrides `requiresDecision`;\n  - an extension cannot register `read_workspace` or `internal`;\n  - `decideToolCall` is the only function returning `{run}` for an asking effect, and only after `confirm` or an operator rule exactly as\n    today;\n  - allow-always remains the sidecar's or REPL's concern, untouched.\n\n### Security analysis\nThe risk is a silent behaviour change in a gate during the move. Mitigations:\n- characterization tables land first and stay byte-identical;\n- each extraction PR moves one phase group;\n- no phase changes order;\n- refusal receipts keep their exact text and `status`;\n- the G-3 focused set (below) runs on every slice at head and at base (`review-run-existing-suites` lesson);\n- registry construction **fails closed** at startup (a spec without a binding throws), which differs from opencode's skip-and-log\n  (`packages/core/src/tool.ts:246`), rejected.\n\n### Files\nAdd: `cli/src/core/tool_registry.ts`, `cli/src/core/tool_pipeline.ts`, `cli/test/tool_surface_characterization.test.ts`,\n`cli/test/tool_dispatch_characterization.test.ts`, `cli/test/mt1_core_import.test.ts`, `cli/test/tool_registry.test.ts`,\n`cli/test/fixtures/model_tools_v1.json`, `cli/test/fixtures/tool_bindings_v1.json`, `docs/TOOL_REGISTRY.md` (how to add a tool).\nChange: `cli/src/core/capabilities.ts`, `cli/src/core/spine.ts`, `cli/src/core/spine_handlers.ts`, `cli/src/tools.ts`\n(`registerBridgeCapabilities`), `cli/src/agent.ts` (`effectiveTools`, registration), `cli/src/core/dispatch_tool_call.ts`,\n`cli/src/parser.ts`, `cli/src/mcp.ts` (derived lists), and in slice 4 `cli/critical-complexity-baseline.json` and\n`cli/test/critical_complexity.test.ts`.\n\n### Tests\n**Characterization, before any refactor (slice 1); green before and after every later slice; fixtures regenerate only with","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"570917d9-5a29-475c-bb0b-4f96e17d9d10","timestamp":"2026-11-24T23:11:31.458Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"ready\n- **Handlers come from five places:**\n  1. `spine.registerHandler` in `setupSpineHandlers` (`core/spine_handlers.ts:61,502,729-969`, ts-native tools);\n  2. `registry.setHandler` in `registerBridgeCapabilities` (`tools.ts:1827-1853`, rust_rpc plus six listed tools);\n  3. `capability.handler`;\n  4. `context.defaultHandler` built in dispatch for MCP, plugin and pipeline (`dispatch_tool_call.ts:672-692`);\n  5. `context.bridge.executeTool`.\n\n  The resolution order is in `ExecutionSpine.execute` (`core/spine.ts:562-584`).\n- The **model-visible list** is built separately in `AutonomousAgent.effectiveTools` (`agent.ts:1335-1365`): `HARNESS_TOOLS` filtered by\n  group and skills, plus agent-local specs, MCP and plugin definitions, then role allow/deny and delegated allow-list filters.\n  `parser.ts:6` builds `KNOWN_TOOLS` from `HARNESS_TOOLS`; serve-mcp lists `HARNESS_TOOLS` minus two (`mcp.ts:1062`); the ACP kind table\n  covers `HARNESS_TOOLS` (`acp/mapping.ts:103`).\n- **Dispatch** `dispatchToolCallImpl` (`core/dispatch_tool_call.ts:37-935`, one 900-line function bound to the agent with `this: any`).\n  Phases in order:\n  1. args parse and repair (`:45-87`);\n  2. delegated allow-list (`:97`), role allow/deny (`:124-151`), skill constraints and integrity (`:154-221`), flight (`:234`), deletion\n     guard (`:239`);\n  3. effect from the registry (`:269-271`), checkpoint read-only fallback (`:275`);\n  4. managed policy and context clamp (`:317-357`), forbidden (`:358`), egress allowlist (`:363`), verification-edit decision\n     (`:391-440`), CS-9 rules (`:441-496`), ask decision (`:497-512`), skill confirm (`:513`);\n  5. needs-input / confirm (`:540-668`);\n  6. plugin notify and execution context (`:670-692`), journal and baseline capture (`:693-743`), `spine.execute` (`:744-768`);\n  7. after: eval receipts, journal end, `notifyToolResult`, `run_tests` attempts (`:807`), file and diff tracking (`:851-872`), VR-3 events\n     (`:873-876`), flight (`:889`), return (`:934-935`).\n\n  The sandbox is applied inside the bridge (`tools.ts:1680-1745`), not in dispatch.\n- **Complexity gate:** `cli/critical-complexity-baseline.json` (revision `4d9996d4…`) with `cli/scripts/check_critical_complexity.ts`.\n  Measured today, equal to the baseline (**zero headroom**): `dispatchToolCallImpl` CC 288 / nesting 6 / 900 lines; `runTurnImpl` 324/5;\n  `runSubagent` 70/4; `compactNowImpl` 17/3; `driveOperation` 17/3. The checker reads the function **by file and name at the baseline\n  revision and at HEAD** (`:175-196`, `findTargetFunction` throws unless exactly one match), so renaming or moving it fails closed (exit 2).\n  `cli/test/critical_complexity.test.ts:37-42` pins the revision and `rows.length === 5`.\n- **Characterization coverage today:**\n  - `capabilities.test.ts` (36 tools, registration);\n  - `lsp_shape.test.ts:67` (description sizes);\n  - `tool_groups.test.ts`, `role_deny_lists.test.ts`, `acp_mapping.test.ts`, `tool_grammar*.test.ts`, `context_convergence.test.ts`\n    (claimed);\n  - dispatch: `command_rules_dispatch`, `managed_policy_dispatch`, `vllm_nullable_dispatch`, `approval_policy`, `injection_gate`,\n    `security_gates`, `sandbox_denial_events`, `subagent_delegation_authority` (claimed), `agt111_subagent_parity`;\n  - G-3 spread across `acp_stdio.test.ts:182,221`, `sidecar.test.ts:232-351`, `verify_hostile.test.ts` (claimed),\n    `managed_policy_*`, `repl_approval_e2e`.\n  - **No test snapshots the full model-visible list per context, and none snapshots the handler resolution per tool.** Those come first.\n\n### Design\n- **`cli/src/core/tool_registry.ts` (new):**\n  ```ts\n  export type ToolBinding =\n    | { kind: \"native\"; handler: CapabilityHandler }   // today's spine.registerHandler tools\n    | { kind: \"bridge\" }                                // RustCoreBridge.executeTool (today's registerBridgeCapabilities set)\n    | { kind: \"extension\" };                            // MCP / plugin via the plugin pipeline (today's defaultHandler)\n  export type OfferRule = \"always\" | \"group\" | \"skills\" | \"objective\" | \"requirements\" | \"mask\" | \"until-all-groups\";\n  export interface RegisteredTool { spec: CanonicalCapability; binding: ToolBinding; offer: OfferRule }\n  export class ToolRegistry {\n    register(t: RegisteredTool): void;      // throws: duplicate name; spec.handler set (one source only); extension effect not exec|egress; non-extension without binding\n    resolve(name: string): RegisteredTool | undefined;\n    modelTools(ctx: OfferContext): ToolDefinition[];  // exactly today's effectiveTools order and filters\n    capabilities(): CapabilityRegistry;     // adapter: existing getByToolName callers keep working\n  }\n  ```\n  The order is the insertion order of today's `effectiveTools` array: `HARNESS_TOOLS` order, then `ENABLE_TOOLS`, `READ_OBJECTIVE`,\n  `REQUIREMENTS`, `READ_FINDINGS`, `READ_ARCHIVE`, `READ_TOOL_OUTPUT`, MCP, plugins. `HARNESS_TOOLS`, `KNOWN_TOOLS` and the serve-mcp list\n  are derived from the registry's baseline set, so they are identical.\n- **One execution path:** `ExecutionSpine.execute` resolves the handler only through `registry.resolve(name).binding`. The fallback chain at\n  `spine.ts:566-569` and the `context.defaultHandler` and bridge fallbacks are removed **only after** the slice-1 table proves equivalence.\n  Pipeline stages named as the unit asks: **approve** (dispatch decide/confirm), **sandbox** (unchanged, inside `bridge.executeTool` for\n  `bridge` bindings), **run** (`spine.execute`), **hooks** (`pluginManager.notifyToolCall` before execution,\n  `notifyToolResult`/`executeToolPipeline` after; HK-1 attaches here later).\n- **Dispatch decomposition** (behaviour-preserving, side-effect order preserved), in new `cli/src/core/tool_pipeline.ts`:\n  - `parseToolArguments(call)` → `{args, structurallyRepaired}`;\n  - `admitToolCall(agent, name, args, ...)` → `{refuse: receipt} | {ok}` for phases 2-3;\n  - `decideToolCall(agent, ...)` → `{refuse} | {ask: question} | {run}` for phase 4;\n  - `confirmToolCall(...)` for phase 5;\n  - `executeToolCall(...)` for phase 6;\n  - `afterToolCall(...)` for phase 7.\n\n  **`dispatchToolCallImpl` stays in `core/dispatch_tool_call.ts` under the same name and signature** as a straight-line orchestrator\n  (target CC ≤ 20, nesting ≤ 2). The baseline then measures a much smaller function against 288/6 and passes.\n- **Baseline handling (D-MT2-2):** do not edit `critical-complexity-baseline.json` during slices 2-3. The extracted functions are new and\n  untracked. Slice 4 is one small PR, made after the last extraction merges. It:\n  - moves `baselineRevision` to that merge commit (an ancestor of HEAD);\n  - adds `decideToolCall`, `admitToolCall`, `confirmToolCall`, `executeToolCall` and `afterToolCall` (`file: cli/src/core/tool_pipeline.ts`)\n    to `functions`;\n  - updates `critical_complexity.test.ts` (revision; `rows.length` 5 → 10);\n  - pastes the checker's before/after table into the PR.\n\n  This is tighten-only: the gate had already proved every tracked function ≤ the old baseline, so advancing can only lower the\n  references. It changes the gate's reference commit, so it lands only with the owner's acknowledgement (merge role per memory). If\n  declined, the extracted functions stay untracked and `dispatchToolCallImpl` keeps its new low numbers against the old reference.\n- **No new grant path:**\n  - the registry has no API that lowers an effect, marks a tool approval-free or overrides `requiresDecision`;\n  - an extension cannot register `read_workspace` or `internal`;\n  - `decideToolCall` is the only function returning `{run}` for an asking effect, and only after `confirm` or an operator rule exactly as\n    today;\n  - allow-always remains the sidecar's or REPL's concern, untouched.\n\n### Security analysis\nThe risk is a silent behaviour change in a gate during the move. Mitigations:\n- characterization tables land first and stay byte-identical;\n- each extraction PR moves one phase group;\n- no phase changes order;\n- refusal receipts keep their exact text and `status`;\n- the G-3 focused set (below) runs on every slice at head and at base (`review-run-existing-suites` lesson);\n- registry construction **fails closed** at startup (a spec without a binding throws), which differs from opencode's skip-and-log\n  (`packages/core/src/tool.ts:246`), rejected.\n\n### Files\nAdd: `cli/src/core/tool_registry.ts`, `cli/src/core/tool_pipeline.ts`, `cli/test/tool_surface_characterization.test.ts`,\n`cli/test/tool_dispatch_characterization.test.ts`, `cli/test/mt1_core_import.test.ts`, `cli/test/tool_registry.test.ts`,\n`cli/test/fixtures/model_tools_v1.json`, `cli/test/fixtures/tool_bindings_v1.json`, `docs/TOOL_REGISTRY.md` (how to add a tool).\nChange: `cli/src/core/capabilities.ts`, `cli/src/core/spine.ts`, `cli/src/core/spine_handlers.ts`, `cli/src/tools.ts`\n(`registerBridgeCapabilities`), `cli/src/agent.ts` (`effectiveTools`, registration), `cli/src/core/dispatch_tool_call.ts`,\n`cli/src/parser.ts`, `cli/src/mcp.ts` (derived lists), and in slice 4 `cli/critical-complexity-baseline.json` and\n`cli/test/critical_complexity.test.ts`.\n\n### Tests\n**Characterization, before any refactor (slice 1); green before and after every later slice; fixtures regenerate only with","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"96af74fd-d518-48ae-aa6b-ec07b827e28e","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"v1/bg3-trust-abuse-model","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
