{"parentUuid":"d33d5474-fc08-4c9d-9e68-a3c5adfd9487","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNbjfmfhmN1x7CND7jsb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Dwt938pUdMxK5mPm8nHPik","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Review PR #798 HK-3 plugin trust","subagent_type":"reviewer","prompt":"Independent security review of GitHub PR #798 (HK-3: per-plugin workspace trust, marked \"partial\") in ~/nexus-code, base `release/v1.3.0`. Take the full head SHA from `gh pr view 798 --json headRefOid`, review exactly that, and say at the end whether it moved or merged. Read the PR body and `gh pr diff 798`, the plan `/home/mike/nexus-wt/_plans/HK_PLAN.md` (HK-3 section: \"per-file approval for workspace JS plugins\"), `docs/v1.3.0/PLAN.md` HK-3 row and gates G-3/G-6, `cli/src/plugins.ts`, `cli/src/workspace_trust.ts`, `cli/src/core/extension_trust.ts` (or wherever trust records live), `docs/SKILLS_AND_PLUGINS.md`, and how managed policy `plugins.allow` / `plugins.disable_workspace` (GV-5, `cli/src/core/managed_policy.ts`) interact (policy can only tighten).\n\nAcceptance to judge (from the plan; state the exact wording you find): a workspace JavaScript plugin does not run until the operator approves THAT file's exact bytes; a changed file asks again; approval cannot be given by the agent itself; trust of the workspace alone no longer imports workspace plugin code. Say what \"partial\" leaves out and whether that is acceptable for an RC.\n\nAttack by RUNNING things (throwaway HOME, temp workspaces, no network, no inference):\n1. Does any workspace plugin import execute before approval, including on workspace trust alone, via `NEXUS_TRUST_WORKSPACE=1`, via a symlinked plugin directory/file, via a plugin file imported by another plugin or by a package `main`/`exports` field, via `import()` of a path outside the approved file (the approved file imports a sibling that the model can edit: is the sibling covered? the PR may only hash the entry file: say so plainly), via TypeScript/ESM/CJS variants, a file replaced between hash and import (TOCTOU window: hash then `import()` by path: how wide), a file with the same hash in another workspace?\n2. Self-approval: agent file tools writing the trust record/store or approving through `run_command` (compare with the HK-1 fixes: protected paths for the store file, terminal-only approval; check the same classes here: `write_file` to the store, workspace=HOME, symlinks, `..`). Is the approval command usable with no TTY? Is there a `--yes` or env bypass?\n3. Managed policy: `plugins.disable_workspace` still disables; `plugins.allow` sha256/file entries still apply on top; a managed policy can only tighten (an approval cannot override a policy refusal).\n4. Revocation/removal, changed bytes → asks again with a clear notice, listing; large files; invalid UTF-8; a plugin that registers tools (effects exec/egress only: confirm no new grant path); `/mcp`-like add flows; no secrets in the trust record; trust records mode 0600, private directory.\n5. Docs: the doc claims match the code (list each claim and verify).\n\nRun at head, one at a time: every plugin/trust test touched or added (`git diff --stat origin/release/v1.3.0...HEAD -- cli/test`), `plugins*`, `workspace_trust`, `managed_policy_allowlists`, `extension_trust*`, `security`, `leak_guard`, `check_requirements`; `cd cli && npx tsc --noEmit -p .`; complexity gate; `node scripts/check_invariants.mjs`; `node scripts/check_doc_versions.mjs`. Mutations (copy aside, restore from the copy, never `git checkout`): skip the hash comparison; import before the approval check; drop the protected path for the store; drop the terminal check: each must fail a test.\n\nRules: do NOT edit ~/nexus-code or existing worktrees. `git -C ~/nexus-code fetch origin && git -C ~/nexus-code worktree add --detach ~/nexus-wt/rev798 <full sha>`; `cp -a ~/nexus-code/cli/node_modules ~/nexus-wt/rev798/cli/`; `mkdir -p ~/nexus-wt/rev798/core/target/release && cp ~/nexus-wt/ls1b/core/target/release/{harness-core,nexus-tui} ~/nexus-wt/rev798/core/target/release/`. Tests: `cd ~/nexus-wt/rev798/cli && TMPDIR=/dev/shm HOME=$(mktemp -d) node --import tsx --test test/<name>.test.ts 2>&1 | tail -20`. Never touch the real ~/.nexus, ~/.config/nexus, /etc/nexus. Stop processes by their own pid; never `pkill -f`. No commits, pushes or GitHub comments. Remove probes and the worktree at the end. Shell is zsh (`bash -c` for loops); prefix `rtk proxy` if output looks filtered; a safety check blocks scripts containing `rm`.\n\nReport under 450 words: verdict (ACCEPT / ACCEPT WITH FOLLOW-UPS / REQUEST CHANGES) at the exact SHA; each acceptance clause met or not with the run that shows it; findings with file:line, run-or-read, blocking or not (any route by which workspace plugin code runs without that file's approval, or by which the agent approves for itself, is blocking); what \"partial\" omits; test counts; mutation results; what you did not check."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":817,"cache_read_input_tokens":303406,"output_tokens":2107,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":113},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":817,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2107,"cache_read_input_tokens":303406,"cache_creation_input_tokens":817,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":817},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":12828,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Dwt938pUdMxK5mPm8nHPik":{"description":"Review PR #798 HK-3 plugin trust","subagent_type":"reviewer",