{"parentUuid":"a8d8eed8-b8d5-43ee-b3f3-1fad64c4bf62","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNcNicMD3p7HtEZoJWLn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3669,"cache_read_input_tokens":306731,"output_tokens":5070,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":489},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3669,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":5070,"cache_read_input_tokens":306731,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3669,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3669},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":4012,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011ChNcNiNDMgafjFo8F3CWF","requestRef":"ab906705-091d-4ec8-8f5a-69ef21323822","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"1fe092de-daa3-4728-985a-61a3c3401630","timestamp":"2026-11-24T23:20:47.462Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"v1/bg3-trust-abuse-model","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
{"parentUuid":"1fe092de-daa3-4728-985a-61a3c3401630","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNcNicMD3p7HtEZoJWLn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Qr8UxnkmqE5g9MZ439KS7S","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-code && cat > /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/hk1final.md <<'EOF'\n**Independent hostile check of the merged HK-1 code at release tip `d9b0f5a63` — DEFECTS FOUND (project-hook pinning). The approval store and the operator hooks file hold up. Fix in progress on `v1/hk1-pinning-allowlist`; v1.3.0 must not be cut before it lands.**\n\nBlocking (each run):\n1. **Pinning is a blocklist** (`cli/src/core/hooks.ts:342-449`, `INTERPRETERS`/`WRAPPERS` at 305 and 310). A repository that ships `[\"script\",\"-qec\",\"sh g.sh\",\"/dev/null\"]`, `[\"awk\",\"BEGIN{system(\\\"sh g.sh\\\")}\"]`, `[\"node\",\"--run\",\"x\"]` or `npm run x` is approved with no covered files listed; the agent then edits `g.sh` or the `package.json` script and the next tool call runs the edited code with no notice and no re-approval (a marker file appeared outside the workspace). Accepted but not executed in the probe: `ash`, `csh`, `tcsh`, `mksh`, `rbash`, `lua5.4`, `Rscript`, `su -c`, `runuser -c`. `setsid`, `flock`, `sudo`, `unshare`, `xargs`, `sh -- -c`, `-ec`, `--command=`, `nice`/`timeout`/`env`/`busybox` before `bash -c` are refused.\n2. **TOCTOU between the hash check and the spawn is winnable from the sandbox** (`hookStillCurrent` + `runHookProcess`, `hooks.ts:645-683`, `hook_runner.ts:102`). A background `run_command` looping copy-and-rename over the pinned `g.sh`: 150 tool calls gave 80 hook runs and 27 executions of the evil copy (about 34% per run; the others dropped the hook). Each call is a free retry. The docs call this limit \"not detected\"; it needs only workspace writes, which the sandbox allows.\n3. **Sibling files a pinned script sources or imports are not pinned** (documented): `. ./lib.sh` edited after approval ran without notice.\n\nNon-blocking: when the workspace is `~/.config/nexus` the hooks file and trust store are not protected paths by absolute pattern; `delete_file` with `recursive` on a directory that contains a protected path succeeded at bridge level (the real agent denies every call there, because the in-workspace hooks file is invalid); on `output_left_open` the runner denies but does not kill the process group (an orphaned child survived); docs should name `script`, `su`, `node --run`, `npm run` as unrecognised.\n\nSound: with `--sandbox` the store and `hooks.json` are unreachable (workspace = repo, `~`, `~/.config/nexus`); file tools hold across `..`, `//`, case, symlinked parents; an operator file inside the workspace, group-writable or symlinked, denies every call; fail-closed on exit 1, timeout, 64 KiB output, bad JSON, duplicate keys; denial text framed and capped; no provider key in the hook environment. The unsandboxed fake-terminal limit stands as documented. Tests: 18 files, 181/181; `tsc` clean; six mutations killed. Not checked: read-only-mode `run_command`, MCP/plugin tool routes, post-tool redaction beyond reading the test, relative PATH entries, cancel while a hook runs.\n\n**Fix plan:** an allowlist (argv[0] a pinned workspace file, or a known shell/interpreter whose first non-option argument is a pinned file with options from a short list; everything else is operator-file only), execution from the hashed bytes (verified private copy), self-contained scripts stated in the docs, the three non-blocking code items.\nEOF\ngh pr comment 782 --body-file /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/hk1final.md | tail -1; echo \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ) SECURITY (claude-invariants-audit): hostile check of merged HK-1 at d9b0f5a6 found project-hook pinning defects (blocklist gaps, TOCTOU winnable from the sandbox): details on #782. I am fixing on v1/hk1-pinning-allowlist from ~/nexus-wt/hk1b (claim HK1_PINNING_ALLOWLIST). Please do not edit cli/src/core/hooks.ts or hook_runner.ts meanwhile, and do not cut an RC before it merges.\" >> \"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log\"; d=\"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims\"; mkdir -p $d/HK1_PINNING_ALLOWLIST && printf '{\"agent\":\"claude-invariants-audit\",\"branch\":\"v1/hk1-pinning-allowlist\",\"since\":\"%s\",\"worktree\":\"/home/mike/nexus-wt/hk1b\",\"scope\":\"cli/src/core/hooks.ts, hook_runner.ts, hooks_cli.ts, security.ts protected paths, docs/HOOKS.md, hooks tests\"}\\n' \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ)\" > $d/HK1_PINNING_ALLOWLIST/owner.json; git fetch -q origin; git worktree add -q -b v1/hk1-pinning-allowlist ~/nexus-wt/hk1b origin/release/v1.3.0 && ln -s ~/nexus-code/cli/node_modules ~/nexus-wt/hk1b/cli/node_modules && mkdir -p ~/nexus-wt/hk1b/core/target/release && cp ~/nexus-wt/ls1b/core/target/release/{harness-core,nexus-tui} ~/nexus-wt/hk1b/core/target/release/ && echo ready","description":"Post the hostile-check findings on the merged HK-1 PR, log and claim the fix, and create its worktree"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3669,"cache_read_input_tokens":306731,"output_tokens":5070,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":489},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3669,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":5070,"cache_read_input_tokens":306731,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3669,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3669},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":13014,"