{"type":"data-flow-records","v":1,"sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","records":[{"response_id":"msg_011ChNcRWg5UjKAMgkTszzHo","mark_sent_by":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","listed":["msg_011ChNcRnu9Rv1nuws77kcao"]},{"response_id":"msg_011ChNcRrRyWaLe3owyFAMSf","mark_sent_by":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b"}]}
{"parentUuid":"bf7f7c5f-d395-4b91-a124-516bc8347dc8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNcRWg5UjKAMgkTszzHo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The hostile re-check of the merged HK-1 hooks found defects in project-hook pinning. A repository can get unpinned code run with the operator's rights, so I'm holding the release until it is fixed.\n\n**Blockers, each confirmed by running at release tip `d9b0f5a63`:**\n- **Pinning is a blocklist.** A project hook such as `[\"script\",\"-qec\",\"sh g.sh\",…]`, `awk` with `system()`, `node --run` or `npm run x` is approved with no covered files listed. The agent can then edit the script it runs, and the next tool call executes the edit with no notice or re-approval.\n- **The hash-then-spawn race is winnable from the sandbox.** A background command swapping the pinned script won 27 of 80 hook runs.\n- **Files a pinned script sources are not pinned.** This one is documented.\n\n**What held up:** the trust store and the operator hooks file are unreachable under `--sandbox`. File tools resist every path trick tried. Hook failures deny the call. The environment contains no gateway key. All 181 tests passed and all six mutations were caught.\n\nI posted the findings on #782 and logged them. I claimed the fix and sent it to the HK-1 builder in a new worktree off the release tip. The fix:\n- replaces the blocklist with an allowlist, so everything outside it moves to the operator's own hooks file;\n- runs hooks from a private copy of the exact bytes that were hashed;\n- documents that scripts must be self-contained;\n- adds the smaller items: protected paths when the workspace is `~/.config/nexus`, refusing deletion of a directory containing a protected path, killing orphaned hook children, and doc updates.\n\nI've asked the builder to push the fix branch; I'll open the PR and get an independent review before merging.\n\nThe reviews of HK-3 (#798) and the MT-2 registry build are still running. Not yet reviewed: #801 and #803. v1.3.0 is not landed. The merge to `main` and the release haven't started."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5249,"cache_read_input_tokens":310400,"output_tokens":659,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5249,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":659,"cache_read_input_tokens":310400,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5249,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5249},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011ChNcRWRwvWUKAJwbEWXRG","requestRef":"9453a1f8-a1fa-4a6d-b8e6-a9cb66818d6c","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"34ebbd8e-3b77-46b8-b3c5-f60e52516e14","timestamp":"2026-11-24T23:21:25.660Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"v1/bg3-trust-abuse-model","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
