{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"remove","timestamp":"2026-11-24T23:28:24.030Z","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a558e367ba3840735</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01RHUhvUYEonVEQJfzxwVorY</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666/tasks/a558e367ba3840735.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Implement MT-2 slice 2 registry\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Slice 2 is done and behaviour-preserving. The slice-1 tests and fixtures pass unedited, and the failing sets match base. Nothing is pushed and there is no PR.\n\n**Commits** (local, on `v1/mt2-registry`; no foreign commits on the release branch):\n- `2bf28af61` feat(tools): register every tool as a spec and binding pair\n- `4f4f38188` docs(tools): `docs/TOOL_REGISTRY.md`\n- `8b540fb94` test(tools): pin each shipped tool's binding to the routing characterization\n\n**Resolves through the registry now**\n- `AutonomousAgent.effectiveTools` is now a call to `ToolRegistry.modelTools(ctx)`. The agent computes the context and the role/delegation predicate. Offer rules rank as group/skills, until-all-groups, objective, requirements, always, mask, then MCP and plugin tools, which reproduces today's order exactly.\n- The agent's six local specs and the extension sync register through `register`. `ExecutionSpine.execute` calls `resolveHandler`: spine handler, then the `native` binding's handler, then the capability's handler.\n- `HARNESS_TOOLS` stays defined in `capabilities.ts` and is checked equal to the registry's baseline. Parser `KNOWN_TOOLS`, the serve-mcp list and `registerBridgeCapabilities` come from the registry; the last through `isBridgeBound`, the same predicate that gives the `bridge` binding.\n\n**Not derived: the ACP kind table.** The fixture pins its key order, which groups by kind and puts `verifier` between tools, so it can't be built from registry order. It stays hand-written, and a tool missing from it falls back to `other`.\n\n**Fallbacks**\n- Removed: `|| capability.handler`. It is the same object `registry.getHandler` already returns.\n- Kept: the context `defaultHandler` and `context.bridge` fallbacks, and `registry.getHandler`. The bridge tools' handlers still come from `registerBridgeCapabilities`, because `routeProbe` and the golden pin them as \"registry-handler\". The extension route needs the plugin pipeline.\n- The `bridge` binding is therefore classification and validation for now, pinned to the fixture by the new test.\n\n**Head vs base** (35 files, 371 passing at both; the set is the slice-1 files, the focused dispatch/policy/G-3 list, `spine*`, `parser`, `tool_grammar*`, `hooks_*`). Failing set is empty at both. `context_convergence` at HEAD: 57/57 pass, 162 s.\n\n**Gates**\n- `tsc`: clean.\n- `check_invariants` and `check_doc_versions`: pass.\n- Complexity gate, baseline unedited:\n  - `runTurnImpl`: CC 324→324, nesting 5→5.\n  - `dispatchToolCallImpl`: CC 288→288, nesting 6→6.\n  - `runSubagent`: CC 70→70, nesting 4→4.\n  - `compactNowImpl`: CC 17→17, nesting 3→3.\n  - `driveOperation`: CC 17→17, nesting 3→3.\n  - None grew. `runTurnImpl` lines went 1262→1290 from other merges, not from this slice.\n- `agent.ts` is 4,974 lines, up from 4,967 in the plan. The `effectiveTools` shrink is offset by imports and constructor registrations.\n\n**Tests:** `tool_registry.test.ts`, 17 passing, each with a mutation that fails it:\n\n| Mutation | Test that fails |\n|---|---|\n| Duplicate accepted | \"a duplicate name is refused\" |\n| Extension accepted with `read_workspace` or `internal` | the extension-effect test |\n| Spec without a binding accepted | \"a non-extension spec without a binding is refused\" |\n| `modelTools` order swapped | the order test, and the surface characterization (matrix) |\n| Shipped binding kinds inverted | the shipped-binding pin |\n| Spine resolves the wrong kind | the \"adding a tool\" test and the binding-route test |\n\nThe no-grant test asserts the exact exported members and rejects names matching effect/approve/grant/override/setHandler. Mutations 1 and 3 are also caught by the underlying `CapabilityRegistry` guard, so those two failures have a second guard behind them.\n\n**Characterization flags:** none made worse or better. The registry is additive, so the per-tool effect, mutating and changesWorkspace facts are unchanged.\n\n**Needed by slices 3 and 4**\n- `capabilities()` returns the real `CapabilityRegistry`, so `register`, `unregister` and `setHandler` there still bypass the registry's checks. Closing that means moving the remaining direct callers onto `ToolRegistry`; I found no live bypass other than the spine tests.\n- If `registerBridgeCapabilities` is retired in favour of binding-based bridge resolution, `routeProbe` in `helpers/tool_characterization.ts` and the golden both change, so the owner has to approve that.\n- Slice 3 still has to decompose `dispatchToolCallImpl`, and slice 4 move the baseline. I touched neither.\n\nTemporary worktrees are removed; `/home/mike/nexus-wt/mt2r` is clean.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>150601</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>46</tool_uses><duration_ms>968943</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>","reason":"absorbed_mid_turn","commandUuid":"65220a82-be23-4708-9656-bef17c8718c9","deliveryId":"ec7102ca-dcc1-409e-aaa1-4d4bb284f797"}
