{"parentUuid":"904dd37f-1e7f-498e-b312-ff6eefbefa18","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNcxkBJjHuT3vTtdVhrx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LGVj1BD2AkUDUFHT7fToPE","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-wt/mt2r && git fetch -q origin && git merge -q origin/release/v1.3.0 --no-edit 2>&1 | tail -2; git status --short | grep -c '^UU'; (cd cli && npx tsc --noEmit -p . >/dev/null; echo \"tsc $?\"); git push -q -u origin v1/mt2-registry 2>&1 | tail -1; echo \"remote $(git ls-remote origin refs/heads/v1/mt2-registry | cut -c1-8) local $(git rev-parse --short=8 HEAD)\"; cat > /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/pr_mt2b.md <<'EOF'\nPlan unit MT-2, slice 2 of 4: the tool registry. Behaviour-preserving: the slice-1 characterization tests and fixtures (#784) pass **unedited**.\n\n## What changes\n\n- New `cli/src/core/tool_registry.ts`: `ToolRegistry` of `RegisteredTool { spec, binding, offer }`, `binding` one of `native` (a handler), `bridge`, `extension`. `register` fails closed: duplicate name; a spec that already carries a handler and a binding; an extension whose effect is not `exec`/`egress`; a non-extension spec without a binding. The registry has **no** API that lowers an effect, marks a tool approval-free or overrides `requiresDecision` (a test asserts the exported members).\n- `AutonomousAgent.effectiveTools` is now `ToolRegistry.modelTools(ctx)`, reproducing today's order and filters exactly; the agent's six local specs and the extension sync register through `register`.\n- `ExecutionSpine.execute` resolves handlers through `resolveHandler` (spine handler, then the `native` binding's handler, then the capability's handler). `HARNESS_TOOLS` is checked equal to the registry's baseline; parser `KNOWN_TOOLS`, the serve-mcp list and `registerBridgeCapabilities` derive from the registry (the last through `isBridgeBound`).\n- `docs/TOOL_REGISTRY.md`: how to add a tool as a registered spec+handler pair; a test shows a test-only registry instance gaining a tool in the model list, the dispatch route and the derived lists with no other edit.\n\n## What does not change, and why\n\n- The ACP kind table stays hand-written (the fixture pins its key order, which groups by kind); a tool missing from it falls back to `other`.\n- Fallbacks removed: `|| capability.handler` (the same object `registry.getHandler` returns). Kept: the context `defaultHandler` and `context.bridge` fallbacks and the bridge handlers from `registerBridgeCapabilities`, because the characterization pins them; the `bridge` binding is classification and validation for now.\n- `capabilities()` still returns the real `CapabilityRegistry`, so `register`/`unregister`/`setHandler` there bypass the new checks; I found no live bypass besides spine tests. Slice 3/4 should move the remaining callers.\n- The five critical functions are unchanged against the baseline (CC 324/288/70/17/17, nesting 5/6/4/3/3), baseline file unedited. `dispatchToolCallImpl` is not decomposed here (slice 3), nor is the baseline moved (slice 4, needs your acknowledgement).\n\n## Tests\n\n`tool_registry` 17 (six mutations, each fails its test: duplicate, extension effect, no binding, order swap, binding kinds, wrong-kind resolution). Head vs base, 35 files (slice-1 files, the focused dispatch/policy/G-3 list, `spine*`, `parser`, `tool_grammar*`, `hooks_*`): 371 passing at both, failing sets empty at both; `context_convergence` 57/57 at head. `tsc`, `check_invariants`, `check_doc_versions` pass.\n\n## Reference coding\n\n`MT2_PLAN` in `/home/mike/nexus-wt/_plans/PF_SB_MT_PA_PLAN.md` compares peers (opencode's tool registry skips-and-logs a spec without a handler; rejected here in favour of failing closed).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\nEOF\ncd ~/nexus-code && u=$(gh pr create --base release/v1.3.0 --head v1/mt2-registry --title \"f