{"type":"data-flow-records","v":1,"sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","records":[{"response_id":"msg_011ChNd1xACrwVL91fEs3zuZ","mark_sent_by":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b"}]}
{"parentUuid":"3cbd83f3-931c-457c-95cd-2d2b14dacd49","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNd1xACrwVL91fEs3zuZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The #798 (HK-3) review came back request changes, and the MT-2 registry slice is now open as #804. Both reviews are posted or running, and nothing new has been merged since #802. v1.3.0 is not landed.\n\n**HK-3 (#798):** two blockers, both run.\n- **Siblings not covered:** only the entry file is hashed, so a file it imports runs unchecked, and the approval record's `files` field exists but is unused.\n- **Hash-then-import race:** the swapper won in 92 of the 216 attempts that passed the hash check.\n\nThe fix is the same technique as the HK-1 pinning fix: hash and load the same bytes, for example from a `data:` URL, which also makes relative imports fail. I logged that I'll take it after the HK-1 fix lands, unless its owner says otherwise.\n\nApproval from a faked terminal (`script -qec`) is the documented unsandboxed limit, shared with `hooks approve`, so I did not count it as a blocker. The plugin docs still need to say so. #798 stays unmerged.\n\n**MT-2 registry (#804):** the builder says behaviour is unchanged.\n- The slice-1 characterization tests pass unedited.\n- Failing test sets are empty at head and base across 35 files (371 passing).\n- None of the five critical functions grew.\n\nAn independent review is now running. It compares handler resolution and the model-visible tool list against base across many configurations, and checks that no tool can avoid the approval path or shadow a built-in.\n\nThe HK-1 pinning fix is still being built by the HK-1 builder. #801 and #803 are not yet reviewed. After those: the readiness re-measure, version bump, changelog and the release steps."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3100,"cache_read_input_tokens":325586,"output_tokens":557,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3100,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":557,"cache_read_input_tokens":325586,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3100,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3100},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011ChNd1wz3KP9UfgwqQ3DNo","requestRef":"f7170cdc-a8de-46e1-93a8-d37ac1308df2","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"57fe52f7-faee-4cf8-8d85-1c04a3b434b9","timestamp":"2026-11-24T23:29:12.834Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"v1/bg3-trust-abuse-model","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
