{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-11-24T23:42:09.570Z","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a317b41792fa50650</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01JXhnQiUb9pjiz6ZVvdKJFe</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666/tasks/a317b41792fa50650.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Implement HK-1 hooks\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Both blockers are fixed and pushed on `v1/hk1-pinning-allowlist` (commits `4c9beed80` and `5408fab84`, plain push, release branch already up to date). The trust record format did not change.\n\n## Allowlist (`cli/src/core/hooks.ts:337`, `planProjectCommand`; table at `:309`)\n\nA project hook command is accepted in two forms only:\n\n- **A workspace script run directly:** argv[0] is a regular file inside the workspace (symlinks out refused), pinned.\n- **A listed interpreter, then a workspace script:** `sh`, `dash`, `bash`, `zsh`, `node`/`nodejs`, `python`/`python3`/`python3.N`, `perl`, `ruby`, installed outside the workspace. Only these options may precede the script:\n  - shells: `-e`, `-u`, `-x` and combinations; `bash` and `zsh` also `--posix`, `--norc`, `--noprofile`\n  - node: `--no-warnings`, `--no-deprecation`\n  - python: `-B -E -I -s -S -u`\n  - perl: `-w -T`; ruby: `-w`\n\nArguments after the script that name an existing workspace path must be regular files and are pinned (including `--opt=value` and `-ovalue`). Everything else is refused with the rule and \"belongs in your own hooks file\". I chose to refuse `[\"/usr/bin/true\"]` and every other installed program too: letting a project file pick arbitrary programs is the blocklist again. Operator hooks are unaffected.\n\n## Verified-copy execution (`hooks.ts:462`, used at `:745`)\n\n- Each pinned file is read once and its bytes are checked against the approved SHA-256.\n- The same bytes are written to `~/.nexus/hook-runs/run-XXXX/&lt;n&gt;/&lt;basename&gt;` (directory 0700, files 0500); the temp directory is used when the workspace is `$HOME`.\n- The command is started with the copies in place of the workspace paths, and the directory is removed afterwards. The working directory stays the workspace.\n- **Limits:** files the script sources or reads by workspace path are not covered; the interpreter is trusted as installed; an unsandboxed same-user process can still reach the private directory and the store.\n\n## Non-blocking items\n\n- **Absolute protected paths:** `security.ts:186`.\n- **Directory deletion:** `protectedBelow`, `tools.ts:76`, enforced in the bridge. It also refuses directories with more than 5000 entries.\n- **Left-open output:** the hook's process group is killed, `hook_runner.ts:205`.\n- **Docs:** `docs/HOOKS.md` rewritten for the allowlist, verified copies and the self-contained-file rule.\n\n## Tests and mutations\n\n- **Allowlist:** every attack in the finding, plus about 80 relatives, is refused at approve and lists as invalid; the ordinary forms and `hooks_examples` pass.\n- **Old approvals:** eleven attack commands with an old-style approval on record do not run.\n- **TOCTOU:** a deterministic swap at the spawn seam runs the original bytes; a 20-iteration stress with a concurrent copy-and-rename writer never ran the swapped bytes (15 extra runs clean).\n- **Mutations:** thirteen, each failing a test. Spawning the workspace path again fails the seam test and failed the stress test 5 of 5 times.\n- **Counts:** `hooks_self_approval` 16, `hooks_cli` 14, `hook_runner` 8, `deletion_guard` 2, `hooks_project_trust` 10, `doctor_hooks` 5.\n- **Repeats:** the changed files passed three runs each, except `hook_runner`, which failed once on a race in my new assertion. That is fixed in the second commit and passed five runs after.\n- **Gates:** the full requested list, `tsc`, the complexity gate, `check_invariants`, `check_doc_versions` and the schema `--check` pass.\n\n## What breaks for existing project hooks\n\n- Any non-listed program (including absolute paths outside the workspace), `--require`/`--import` preloads, and `ksh`/`fish`/`php`/`deno`/`bun` are now invalid.\n- Scripts that load siblings relative to their own location break (`require(\"./lib\")`, a `.js` ES module relying on the workspace `package.json`).</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>630276</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>31</tool_uses><duration_ms>1253097</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
