{"parentUuid":"3f397738-7144-4b81-b22f-b1a7c90930c7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNe1p3RFBwDUKXVH1SiZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2520,"cache_read_input_tokens":328686,"output_tokens":1901,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":36},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2520},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":1901,"cache_read_input_tokens":328686,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2520,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2520,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":302,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011ChNe1odcyr5nCEhdtEkjT","requestRef":"e5fbb62f-4a97-40b7-bbf9-2b0107cd16b5","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"5m","type":"assistant","uuid":"aea5389d-e988-4794-82d1-05a1a637f521","timestamp":"2026-11-24T23:42:13.769Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"v1/bg3-trust-abuse-model","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
{"parentUuid":"aea5389d-e988-4794-82d1-05a1a637f521","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNe1p3RFBwDUKXVH1SiZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014iT2Ae5ttKFzDKQf38yKah","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-code && git fetch -q origin && cat > /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/pr_hk1b.md <<'EOF'\nFixes the defects found by the independent hostile check of the merged HK-1 code (findings posted on #782, \"Independent hostile check of the merged HK-1 code at release tip d9b0f5a63\").\n\n## Blockers fixed\n\n1. **Allowlist instead of blocklist for project hooks** (`cli/src/core/hooks.ts` `planProjectCommand`). A project hook is accepted only as (a) a regular workspace file run directly, or (b) one of `sh dash bash zsh node nodejs python python3 python3.N perl ruby`, installed outside the workspace, followed by a workspace script, with only a short list of harmless options before the script (shells `-e -u -x`, bash/zsh `--posix --norc --noprofile`, node `--no-warnings --no-deprecation`, python `-B -E -I -s -S -u`, perl `-w -T`, ruby `-w`). Later arguments that name an existing workspace path must be regular files and are pinned (including `--opt=value`, `-ovalue`). Everything else (`script`, `awk`, `node --run`, `npm run`, `ash`/`csh`/`tcsh`/`mksh`/`rbash`, `lua`, `Rscript`, `su -c`, `runuser -c`, `env`, wrappers, preloads, absolute programs such as `/usr/bin/true`) is refused with the rule and \"belongs in your own hooks file\". Operator hooks are unaffected.\n2. **Execution from the verified bytes** (`hooks.ts`, used at spawn). Each pinned file is read once, its bytes are checked against the approved SHA-256, the same bytes are written to a private per-run directory (0700, files 0500, removed afterwards; the temp directory is used when the workspace is `$HOME`) and the command is started with the copies in place of the workspace paths; the working directory stays the workspace. A later change of the workspace file cannot affect a running hook. Limits (documented): files the script sources or reads by workspace path are not covered; the interpreter is trusted as installed; an unsandboxed same-user process can still reach the private directory and the store.\n\n## Non-blocking items from the same check\n\n- `security.ts`: absolute protected paths for `~/.config/nexus/hooks.json` and `extension_trust.json` (a workspace of `~/.config/nexus` is covered).\n- `tools.ts` `protectedBelow`: `delete_file` with `recursive` refuses a directory that contains a protected path (and one with more than 5,000 entries).\n- `hook_runner.ts`: on `output_left_open` the hook's process group is killed.\n- `docs/HOOKS.md` rewritten for the allowlist, verified copies and the self-contained-file rule.\n\n## What this breaks for existing project hooks (release-note material)\n\nAny program not on the list (including absolute paths outside the workspace), `--require`/`--import` preloads, and `ksh`/`fish`/`php`/`deno`/`bun` are now invalid in a PROJECT hooks file (put them in your own `~/.config/nexus/hooks.json`). Scripts that load siblings relative to their own location break (`require(\"./lib\")`, a `.js` ES module relying on the workspace `package.json`). The trust record format did not change.\n\n## Tests\n\nEvery attack in the finding, and about 80 relatives, is refused at approve and lists as invalid; ordinary forms and the shipped `examples/hooks` pass; eleven attack commands with an old-style approval on record do not run; a deterministic swap at the spawn seam runs the original bytes; a 20-iteration stress with a concurrent copy-and-rename writer never ran swapped bytes (15 extra runs clean). Thirteen mutations each fail a test (spawning the workspace path again fails the seam test and failed the stress test 5 of 5). `hooks_self_approval` 16, `hooks_cli` 14, `hook_runner` 8, `deletion_guard` 2, `hooks_project_trust` 10, `doctor_hooks` 5; changed files three runs each; `tsc`, complexity gate, invariants, doc versions, schema `--check` pass. Independent re-review requested before merge.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\nEOF\nu=$(gh pr create --base release/v1.3.0 --head v1/hk1-pinning-allowlist --title \"fix(hooks): allowlist project hook commands and run the verified bytes\" --body-file /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/pr_hk1b.md | tail -1); echo \"$u\"; echo \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ) PR (claude-invariants-audit): $u HK-1 pinning allowlist + verified-bytes execution; independent re-review next; DO NOT MERGE until posted.\" >> \"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log\"","description":"Open the PR for the HK-1 pinning fix and log it"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2520,"cache_read_input_tokens":328686,"output_tokens":1901,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":36},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2520},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":1901,"cache_read_input_tokens":328686,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2520,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2520,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":10287,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_014iT2Ae5ttKFzDKQf38yKah":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-code && git fetch -q origin && cat > /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/pr_hk1b.md <<'EOF'\nFixes the defects found by the independent hostile check of the merged HK-1 code (findings posted on #782, \"Independent hostile check of the merged HK-1 code at release tip d9b0f5a63\").\n\n## Blockers fixed\n\n1. **Allowlist instead of blocklist for project hooks** (`cli/src/core/hooks.ts` `planProjectCommand`). A project hook is accepted only as (a) a regular workspace file run directly, or (b) one of `sh dash bash zsh node nodejs python python3 python3.N perl ruby`, installed outside the workspace, followed by a workspace script, with only a short list of harmless options before the script (shells `-e -u -x`, bash/zsh `--posix --norc --noprofile`, node `--no-warnings --no-deprecation`, python `-B -E -I -s -S -u`, perl `-w -T`, ruby `-w`). Later arguments that name an existing workspace path must be regular files and are pinned (including `--opt=value`, `-ovalue`). Everything else (`script`, `awk`, `node --run`, `npm run`, `ash`/`csh`/`tcsh`/`mksh`/`rbash`, `lua`, `Rscript`, `su -c`, `runuser -c`, `env`, wrappers, preloads, absolute programs such as `/usr/bin/true`) is refused with the rule and \"belongs in your own hooks file\". Operator hooks are unaffected.\n2. **Execution from the verified bytes** (`hooks.ts`, used at spawn). Each pinned file is read once, its bytes are checked against the approved SHA-256, the same bytes are written to a private per-run directory (0700, files 0500, removed afterwards; the temp directory is used when the workspace is `$HOME`) and the command is started with the copies in place of the workspace paths; the working directory stays the workspace. A later change of the workspace file cannot affect a running hook. Limits (documented): files the script sources or reads by workspace path are not covered; the interpreter is trusted as installed; an unsandboxed same-user process can still reach the private directory and the store.\n\n## Non-blocking items from the same check\n\n- `security.ts`: absolute protected paths for `~/.config/nexus/hooks.json` and `extension_trust.json` (a workspace of `~/.config/nexus` is covered).\n- `tools.ts` `protectedBelow`: `delete_file` with `recursive` refuses a directory that contains a protected path (and one with more than 5,000 entries).\n- `hook_runner.ts`: on `output_left_open` the hook's process group is killed.\n- `docs/HOOKS.md` rewritten for the allowlist, verified copies and the self-contained-file rule.\n\n## What this breaks for existing project hooks (release-note material)\n\nAny program not on the list (including absolute paths outside the workspace), `--require`/`--import` preloads, and `ksh`/`fish`/`php`/`deno`/`bun` are now invalid in a PROJECT hooks file (put them in your own `~/.config/nexus/hooks.json`). Scripts that load siblings relative to their own location break (`require(\"./lib\")`, a `.js` ES module relying on the workspace `package.json`). The trust record format did not change.\n\n## Tests\n\nEvery attack in the finding, and about 80 relatives, is refused at approve and lists as invalid; ordinary forms and the shipped `examples/hooks` pass; eleven attack commands with an old-style approval on record do not run; a deterministic swap at the spawn seam runs the original bytes; a 20-iteration stress with a concurrent copy-and-rename writer never ran swapped bytes (15 extra runs clean). Thirteen mutations each fail a test (spawning the workspace path again fails the seam test and failed the stress test 5 of 5). `hooks_self_approval` 16, `hooks_cli` 14, `hook_runner` 8, `deletion_guard` 2, `hooks_project_trust` 10, `doctor_hooks` 5; changed files three runs each; `tsc`, complexity gate, invariants, doc versions, schema `--check` pass. Independent re-review requested before merge.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\nEOF\nu=$(gh pr create --base release/v1.3.0 --head v1/hk1-pinning-allowlist --title \"fix(hooks): allowlist project hook commands and run the verified bytes\" --body-file /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/pr_hk1b.md | tail -1); echo \"$u\"; echo \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ) PR (claude-invariants-audit): $u HK-1 pinning allowlist + verified-bytes execution; independent re-review next; DO NOT MERGE until posted.\" >> \"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log\"","description":"Open the PR for the HK-1 pinning fix and log it"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011ChNe1odcyr5nCEhdtEkjT","requestRef":"e5fbb62f-4a97-40b7-bbf9-2b0107cd16b5","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"5m","type":"assistant","uuid":"f7705793-5789-4e8b-b177-4e4762af409c","timestamp":"2026-11-24T23:42:24.077Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"v1/bg3-trust-abuse-model","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
