{"parentUuid":"3fe80221-6048-4f38-83dd-bec701b6bfcf","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNe2wWfBkqWBTE4iCowS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UUrmuwABRrBpYkSY2aUW4c","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Hostile review PR #805 hooks allowlist","subagent_type":"reviewer","prompt":"Independent hostile review of GitHub PR #805 (HK-1 project-hook allowlist and verified-bytes execution) in ~/nexus-code, base `release/v1.3.0`. Take the full head SHA from `gh pr view 805 --json headRefOid`, review exactly that, and say whether it moved or merged. Read the PR body, `docs/HOOKS.md`, and the two prior security comments on #782 (`gh pr view 782 --comments`: the review rounds and the last \"Independent hostile check of the merged HK-1 code\"). The fix: `cli/src/core/hooks.ts` (`planProjectCommand` allowlist; verified-copy execution), `cli/src/core/hook_runner.ts`, `cli/src/security.ts` (absolute protected paths), `cli/src/tools.ts` (`protectedBelow`), tests, docs. Your job is to find a way past it. By RUNNING (throwaway HOME, temp workspaces, no network, no live inference):\n1. Allowlist bypass: build the strangest accepted commands and see whether any makes an interpreter run unpinned code or a workspace file that is not hashed: interpreter options in the allowed list that change behaviour (`bash -x`/`-e` harmless, but `node --no-warnings` plus `NODE_OPTIONS`? env is scrubbed: confirm), combined flags (`-eu`, `-ex`, `-eC`), `--` handling, option arguments that consume the next token as code (`perl -w -T` fine; `python -I -S -u`; `python -B`; `ruby -w`; `sh -e -u -x`; try `sh -c` smuggled as `-ec`, `-xc`, `-uc`, `-ceu`: must be refused), a script whose shebang or first line runs another interpreter, a script argument that is a directory/FIFO/device/symlink to outside/proc path/`/dev/fd/N`, `argv[0]` workspace file with a shebang to a workspace interpreter, an argument after the script that is an existing workspace regular file under a symlinked dir, names with spaces/newlines/leading dashes (`-x.sh`: is it an option?), non-UTF-8 names, case-insensitive aliasing, hard links to files outside the workspace, a pinned file that is later replaced by a directory, `node` resolving to a workspace-controlled binary through PATH (is PATH scrubbed or is argv[0] resolved to an absolute path outside the workspace before pinning? what if PATH contains `.` or a workspace dir, or the workspace contains a file named `node`/`sh`/`bash`: the interpreter must be resolved from trusted dirs only), interpreter installed INSIDE the workspace (a file named bash in the repo: refused?).\n2. Verified-copy execution: confirm the process really runs the copies, not the workspace paths (strace-free proof: the hook prints `$0`/`__filename`/`/proc/self/cmdline`), that swapping the workspace file between hash and spawn (concurrent writer) never runs the swapped bytes (run the stress yourself, more iterations), the private directory's location/permissions (`~/.nexus/hook-runs/run-XXXX`: is it reachable/writable by the sandboxed model command? (bwrap masks?); can a sandboxed command replace the copy between write and exec (directory 0700, files 0500: can the same uid chmod/replace them? yes for an unsandboxed command (documented); under `--sandbox` check reachability), cleanup on kill/timeout/crash (leftover directories and their cleanup at next start), concurrent hook runs (name collisions), hooks run with cwd = workspace, a script that reads its own path or sibling files (documented break).\n3. Non-blocking items: the absolute protected paths for `~/.config/nexus/hooks.json` and `extension_trust.json` with workspace = `~/.config/nexus`, `~`, `~/.config` (write/edit/delete via the file tools and the bridge); `delete_file recursive` of a directory containing a protected path (and the 5000-entry rule: a legitimate large directory delete still works below that? what does a model get told; is refusing >5000 entries a regression for normal deletes of `node_modules`: check what base did and judge); the hook runner kills the process group on output left open (orphan test).\n4. Regression: operator hooks unaffected (any program allowed, no verified copy needed); existing trust records with old approvals: files that now violate the allowlist must be inactive and say why; `nexus hooks list/approve/test` output; `hooks_examples` and the shipped `examples/hooks` pass; the gate-ordering tests (`hooks_gate_bypass`) still pass.\nRun at head, one at a time: every `cli/test/hook*.test.ts` and `hooks_*.test.ts`, `content_trust`, `strict_json`, `doctor_hooks`, `security`, `security_gates`, `deletion_guard`, `approval_policy`, `managed_policy_enforcement`, `leak_guard`, `check_requirements`, `sandbox_confine`; `cd cli && npx tsc --noEmit -p .`; the complexity gate; `node scripts/check_invariants.mjs`; `node scripts/check_doc_versions.mjs`. Mutations (copy aside, restore from the copy, never `git checkout`): spawn the workspace path instead of the copy; accept one extra option; drop the interpreter-installed-outside-workspace check; drop the absolute protected path; drop `protectedBelow`: each must fail a test.\nRules: do NOT edit ~/nexus-code or existing worktrees. `git -C ~/nexus-code fetch origin && git -C ~/nexus-code worktree add --detach ~/nexus-wt/rev805 <full sha>`; `cp -a ~/nexus-code/cli/node_modules ~/nexus-wt/rev805/cli/`; `mkdir -p ~/nexus-wt/rev805/core/target/release && cp ~/nexus-wt/ls1b/core/target/release/{harness-core,nexus-tui} ~/nexus-wt/rev805/core/target/release/`. Tests: `cd ~/nexus-wt/rev805/cli && TMPDIR=/dev/shm HOME=$(mktemp -d) node --import tsx --test test/<name>.test.ts 2>&1 | tail -20`. Never touch the real ~/.nexus, ~/.config/nexus, /etc/nexus (a throwaway HOME means `~/.nexus/hook-runs` is under it). Stop processes by their own pid; never `pkill -f`. No commits, pushes or GitHub comments. Remove probes and the worktree at the end. Shell is zsh (`bash -c` for loops); prefix `rtk proxy` if output looks filtered; a safety check blocks scripts containing `rm`.\nReport under 500 words: verdict (ACCEPT / ACCEPT WITH FOLLOW-UPS / REQUEST CHANGES) at the exact SHA; the three earlier blockers closed or not, each with the attack tried; new findings with file:line, run-or-read, blocking or not (any way for a hostile repository or the agent's sandboxed tools to run unpinned or swapped code with the operator's rights, or to get a hook in force without approval, is blocking; the documented unsandboxed-shell limits are not); test counts; mutation results; what you did not check."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2047,"cache_read_input_tokens":331206,"output_tokens":2614,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2047},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2614,"cache_read_input_tokens":331206,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2047,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2047,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":17591,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01UUrmuwABRrBpYkSY2aUW4c":{"description":"Hostile review PR #805 hooks allowlist","subagent_type":"reviewer","prompt":"Independent hostile review of GitHub PR #805 (HK-1 project-hook allowlist and verified-bytes execution) in ~/nexus-code, base `release/v1.3.0`. Take the full head SHA from `gh pr view 805 --json headRefOid`, review exactly that, and say whether it moved or merged. Read the PR body, `docs/HOOKS.md`, and the two prior security comments on #782 (`gh pr view 782 --comments`: th