{"parentUuid":"d54f352c-d19b-487f-88ca-23c8c93d1f4d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNe9jrsRw5RsgzAmvaGG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"#803 is groundwork for BG-3, which the plan defers to v1.4 (\"needs a trust and abuse model first\"), and my recommendation is not to merge it into v1.3.0.\n\n**What it is:** 1,912 added lines across 10 files, all new. They are:\n- a trigger spec format for file-change and webhook events;\n- a content-hash trust store;\n- per-trigger rate limiting with quarantine after three strikes;\n- a `nexus triggers list|approve|revoke|status` command;\n- `docs/TRIGGERS.md`.\n\nThe PR states that the firing itself is deferred to v1.4. Its author reports 59 tests passing. Required checks on its head (`4dd93530`) are green, but nobody has independently reviewed it.\n\n**Why I'd hold it back:**\n- **No consumer.** It ships a new approval command and trust store that nothing uses yet. That adds attack surface and documentation to a release candidate for no user benefit.\n- **Approval-path risk.** It is a third place where terminal-only approval is enforced (alongside `hooks approve` and `plugins trust`). Review of the other two found that a faked terminal defeats this check when the shell is unsandboxed. Merging it would add the same weakness to a third command.\n- **Timing.** The hostile reviews have been finding real defects in similar trust code (HK-1, HK-3). I'd rather not add 1,900 unreviewed lines of the same kind right before an RC.\n\n**What I'd do:** retarget it to a v1.4 branch or leave it open, and record in the release notes that BG-3 is deferred. It's one of the other agents' PRs, so I'd log this in the claims log and wait for the author's response before closing or retargeting anything. If you want it in v1.3.0, I'd run the same independent security review first.\n\nStill running: the #804 and #805 reviews. Still pending: #798 and #801."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":728,"cache_read_input_tokens":338062,"output_tokens":623,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":728},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":623,"cache_read_input_tokens":338062,"cache_creation_input_tokens":728,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":728,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011ChNe9jgD48WKVoJ5XAfbz","requestRef":"e4e0791e-f6e5-4e5e-a978-aec44cd5f699","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"5m","type":"assistant","uuid":"a9261070-cae6-4b47-bd2c-286bfc010a85","timestamp":"2026-11-24T23:44:09.023Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"v1/bg3-trust-abuse-model","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
