{"parentUuid":"6fc1be90-42b4-4db3-b949-2f3ff0c42a8a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNeBgdDQUev6HS22uXLL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TWDHiJCdE2pWuNbxpjFcXD","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/mike/.claude/projects/-home-mike-nexus-code/memory && cat > v130-bg3-no-longer-deferred.md <<'EOF'\n---\nname: v130-bg3-no-longer-deferred\ndescription: Owner reversed the deferral of BG-3 (event triggers) on 2026-11-25: it is in scope for v1.3.0 and must be built, not rolled to v1.4\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\nOwner, 2026-11-25 (verbatim): \"BG-3 no longer defered.\"\n\nThe plan (`docs/v1.3.0/PLAN.md:85`) deferred BG-3 (event triggers: file change, webhook) to v1.4 pending a trust and abuse model. The owner reversed that. It joins the unbuilt units that must be complete before the merge to main and release. [[v130-owner-directive-build-and-release-2026-11-24]]'s list of units to complete now includes BG-3.\n\n**Why:** the owner wants event triggers shipped in v1.3.0.\n**How to apply:** PR #803 (Codex) holds the trust surface only (spec, trust store, rate limit, `nexus triggers` CLI; firing not built). The trigger FIRER (watchers, webhook listener, firing jobs through the BG-1/BG-2 unattended path) is still to build and needs its own independent security review. Update PLAN.md, readiness inventory and release notes (no longer \"deferred\"). Do not merge #803 or the firer without an independent hostile review: the terminal-only approval check is the same bypassable-by-pty limit as hooks/plugins.\nEOF\npython3 - <<'EOF'\np='MEMORY.md'; s=open(p).read()\ns=s.rstrip('\\n')+\"\\n- [BG-3 no longer deferred](v130-bg3-no-longer-deferred.md) — owner 2026-11-25: event triggers are in v1.3.0; #803 = trust surface only, firer still to build\\n\"\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ncd ~/nexus-code && echo \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ) OWNER (relayed by claude-invariants-audit): 'BG-3 no longer defered.' (2026-11-25). BG-3 is in scope for v1.3.0: PR #803 (trust surface) is NOT held back any more, and the trigger firer (file-change watcher, webhook listener, fire through the BG-1/BG-2 unattended path) still has to be built. Who owns the firer? Codex holds BG3_TRUST_ABUSE_MODEL: say here if you are building it; otherwise I claim BG3_TRIGGER_FIRER after an independent review of #803. I am starting the independent security review of #803 now; do not merge #803 before it is posted.\" >> \"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log\"; ls \"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims\" | grep -i BG3","description":"Save the owner's BG-3 reversal to memory and announce it in the claims log"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":636,"cache_read_input_tokens":338790,"output_tokens":3761,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":275},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":636},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":3761,"cache_read_input_tokens":338790,"cache_creation_input_tokens":636,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":636,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":6863,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01TWDHiJCdE2pWuNbxpjFcXD":{"command":"cd /home/mike/.claude/projects/-home-mike-nexus-code/memory && cat > v130-bg3-no-longer-deferred.md <<'EOF'\n---\nname: v130-bg3-no-longer-deferred\ndescription: Owner reversed the deferral of BG-3 (event triggers) on 2026-11-25: it is in scope for v1.3.0 and must be built, not rolled to v1.4\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\nOwner, 2026-11-25 (verbatim): \"BG-3 no longer defered.\"\n\nThe plan (`docs/v1.3.0/PLAN.md:85`) deferred BG-3 (event triggers: file change, webhook) to v1.4 pending a trust and abuse model. The owner reversed that. It joins the unbuilt units that must be complete before the merge to main and release. [[v130-owner-directive-build-and-release-2026-11-24]]'s list of units to complete now includes BG-3.\n\n**Why:** the owner wants event triggers shipped in v1.3.0.\n**How to apply:** PR #803 (Codex) holds the trust surface only (spec, trust store, rate limit, `nexus triggers` CLI; firing not built). The trigger FIRER (watchers, webhook listener, firing jobs through the BG-1/BG-2 unattended path) is still to build and needs its own independent security review. Update PLAN.md, readiness inventory and release notes (no longer \"deferred\"). Do not merge #803 or the firer without an independent hostile review: the terminal-only approval check is the same bypassable-by-pty limit as hooks/plugins.\nEOF\npython3 - <<'EOF'\np='MEMORY.md'; s=open(p).read()\ns=s.rstrip('\\n')+\"\\n- [BG-3 no longer deferred](v130-bg3-no-longer-deferred.md) — owner 2026-11-25: event triggers are in v1.3.0; #803 = trust surface only, firer still to build\\n\"\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ncd ~/nexus-code && echo \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ) OWNER (relayed by claude-invariants-audit): 'BG-3 no longer defered.' (2026-11-25). BG-3 is in scope for v1.3.0: PR #803 (trust surface) is NOT held back any more, and the trigger firer (file-change watcher, webhook listener, fire through the BG-1/BG-2 unattended path) still has to be built. Who owns the firer? Codex holds BG3_TRUST_ABUSE_MODEL: say here if you are building it; otherwise I claim BG3_TRIGGER_FIRER after an independent review of #803. I am starting the independent security review of #803 now; do not merge #803 before it is posted.\" >> \"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log\"; ls \"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims\" | grep -i BG3","description":"Save the owner's BG-3 reversal to memory and announce it in the claims log"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011ChNeBgTHcgK9ZvDT5h3Dn","requestRef":"7050e2ec-1edc-4533-ae6f-47b05d06113b","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"5m","type":"assistant","uuid":"0356d69c-f2c0-4b97-9e46-fba2f89d5087","timestamp":"2026-11-24T23:44:36.590Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"v1/bg3-trust-abuse-model","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
