{"parentUuid":"40c6efbb-9b53-4da3-83f0-32bc3658fc99","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNeDpxZsNAT6EANbkaZT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Understood: BG-3 is back in scope for v1.3.0, so my earlier advice to hold #803 back no longer applies. I recorded your reversal in memory and in the claims log.\n\nWhat this changes:\n- **#803 is the trust groundwork only.** It has the trigger spec, trust store, rate limiting and `nexus triggers` command. Nothing fires yet, so BG-3 still needs the part that watches for file changes, listens for webhooks, and starts jobs through the unattended path.\n- **#803 gets the same review as the other trust code.** The hostile reviews of the hooks and plugin code found real defects, and this code will be the authority boundary for the firer. An independent security review of #803 is now running. It also has to produce a concrete list of what the firer must add to be safe, including webhook authentication and replay protection.\n- **Who builds the firer.** Codex already holds the BG-3 claim. I asked in the claims log who is building the firer and said I'll claim it myself after #803 is reviewed if Codex isn't.\n\nI'll also update the plan, the readiness inventory and the release notes to drop the \"deferred\" wording. #803 stays unmerged until the review is posted.\n\nStill running: the #804 and #805 reviews. Still pending: #798 (two blockers) and #801. v1.3.0 is not landed. The merge to `main` and the release haven't started."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4313,"cache_read_input_tokens":339426,"output_tokens":449,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4313},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":449,"cache_read_input_tokens":339426,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4313,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4313,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011ChNeDpnAB4aAkTcQUxiao","requestRef":"c64411ee-f006-4496-bc64-cc0f6ab0e5d8","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"5m","type":"assistant","uuid":"a271e2a5-78ad-47ba-ae80-f099c1ef75c4","timestamp":"2026-11-24T23:45:00.157Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"v1/bg3-trust-abuse-model","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
