{"parentUuid":"b4ccfe57-7c5c-44db-9dac-47e4c906d7cd","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNeHuFQZKCLsdJTd43Nw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The MT-2 registry (#804, slice 2) is merged into `release/v1.3.0` as `f9754def`. The reviewer found no blockers, and required checks were green at the exact head. Release CI was green at the tip first, and I read the merged state back after the merge call.\n\nI haven't yet confirmed release CI on the new merge commit.\n\n**What the reviewer measured against the previous tip, all by running:**\n- Handler resolution was byte-identical for every tool, including an unknown tool and plugin tools named like built-ins.\n- The model-visible tool list was identical across 500 random configurations.\n- The serve-mcp list was unchanged.\n- The failing-test sets matched at 53 files (0 failures on both sides).\n- The complexity gate was unchanged for the five critical functions.\n\n**Follow-ups, none blocking, recorded on the PR:**\n- The baseline tool registry is an exported mutable object. A future registration there would expose a tool over serve-mcp with no approval path, and no code does that today. It should be frozen or exported read-only.\n- A handler bound in a registration now outranks one added later; no production tool uses it, but the precedence should be documented or tested.\n- Plugin tools named `read_tool_output` or `update_requirements` register as ordinary extensions when the built-in is absent. This predates the registry.\n\nMT-2 now has slice 1 and slice 2 merged. Slice 3 (decomposing `dispatchToolCallImpl`) and slice 4 (moving the complexity baseline, which needs your acknowledgement) are not started. The registry builder's report said `capabilities()` still exposes the unchecked registration calls, which slices 3–4 should close.\n\nThe hostile review of the HK-1 pinning fix (#805) and the security review of #803 are still running. Pending: #798 (two blockers), #801, the BG-3 firer, the readiness re-measure and the release steps. v1.3.0 is not landed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2258,"cache_read_input_tokens":346673,"output_tokens":638,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2258},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":638,"cache_read_input_tokens":346673,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2258,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2258,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011ChNeHu4VmXbk46KcBenGV","requestRef":"ad24d218-843b-4ad9-b2a8-11aea285cf93","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"5m","type":"assistant","uuid":"f7c572f0-7fd6-4dcc-98ec-e1fb6be4883c","timestamp":"2026-11-24T23:45:56.016Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"v1/bg3-trust-abuse-model","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
