{"parentUuid":"b1c12bb9-3e3e-4a30-8081-eaaa9b6f7a97","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNejWjHf6fGiBb4ZG7oh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Uty2BQrNLdLi1mHuxJFcE6","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-code && cat > /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/rev805.md <<'EOF'\n**Independent hostile review at `5408fab84cec54887e5c6b5c8106cde004106ee5` — REQUEST CHANGES (two new bypasses of the allowlist, both run). The three earlier blockers are closed at the argv level. I am fixing the rest on this branch.**\n\n**Closed (run):** about 60 commands through `planProjectCommand`: `-ec`, `-xc`, `-uc`, `-ceu`, `-eC`, `--`, `-`, `-x.sh` as an option, `-Bx`, `-m`, `-Mstrict`, `-rfoo`, `--require=`, `--rcfile` and wrappers are refused; a directory, a symlink out of the workspace and `/dev/fd` or `/proc` script arguments are refused; names with spaces or newlines are fine and `./-x.sh` is pinned. **Verified-copy execution:** the hook prints `$0`/`__filename`/`/proc/self/cmdline` and all name the copy `…/run-XXXX/0/g.sh`; a concurrent copy-and-rename and overwrite writer against 150 spawns gave 70 runs that all printed GOOD, 80 refusals, 0 swapped runs, no leftover directories; the private directory is 0700, files 0500, a symlinked or group-writable root is refused, and under `--sandbox` it is unreachable. **Non-blocking items:** absolute protected paths held for workspaces `~/.config/nexus`, `~`, `~/.config` and the parent of `~` across write/edit/delete spellings; the orphan-process test passes.\n\n**Blocking**\n- **B1: a shebang runs an unpinned workspace file.** `./shebang.sh` containing `#!./evil` (or `#!/proc/self/cwd/evil`) is approved with only `shebang.sh` pinned; the copy runs with cwd = workspace and executed the workspace's `evil`. After approval the agent can edit `evil` and the next call runs it with no re-approval. `planProjectCommand` never reads the first line. Fix: refuse any pinned script whose `#!` line is not an absolute path to an allowlisted interpreter outside the workspace, or run the copy through an explicit interpreter.\n- **B2: an interpreter that resolves into the workspace is accepted.** `[\"/proc/self/cwd/bash\",\"g.sh\"]` passes and runs the workspace's `bash`; and with PATH containing `.`, a relative entry or an empty entry (`/usr/bin::/bin`, `.:/usr/bin`, `/usr/bin:.`) an interpreter such as `python3.99` not found earlier ran the workspace file (`hooks.ts:371-384`: `onPath` skips empty entries and `real === undefined` is accepted). Fix: resolve `argv[0]` to an absolute path from absolute trusted PATH entries only, refuse `/proc` and `/dev`, spawn that absolute path, and refuse when not found.\n\n**Non-blocking:** S1 — refusing directories over 5,000 entries is a regression (`protectedBelow`, `tools.ts`): base had no limit; a 5,200-file `node_modules` is refused (\"delete it in parts\"), and the synchronous walk blocks the event loop: raise the limit well above normal dependency trees or walk without a cap. S2 — `/tmp/bash` or `/dev/shm/bash` as argv[0] is accepted (any absolute path outside the workspace, whatever its owner or writability): fix with B2 by using trusted directories. S3 (read) — `openSync` on the pin target can block on a FIFO swapped in after the plan (`hooks.ts` ~478): open with `O_NONBLOCK` and `fstat`. S4 (read) — no sweep of stale `run-*` directories after SIGKILL or `process.exit`.\n**Tests at that head, 0 failures:** the eleven hook files, `content_trust` 7, `strict_json` 9, `doctor_hooks` 5, `security` 14, `security_gates` 10, `deletion_guard` 2, `approval_policy` 16, `leak_guard` 6, `check_requirements` 28, `sandbox_confine` 19, `managed_policy_enforcement` 113; `tsc`, invariants, doc versions pass. **Mutations caught:** spawning the workspace path, one extra option, the interpreter-in-workspace check (1, `hooks_cli` only), the absolute protected path, `protectedBelow`. No test covers B1 or B2. Not checked: a real `--sandbox` run, winning the FIFO race, kill/crash cleanup beyond reading.\nEOF\ngh pr comment 805 --body-file /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/rev805.md | tail -1; echo \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ) REVIEW (claude-invariants-audit): #805 HK-1 pinning REQUEST CHANGES at 5408fab8: shebang runs an unpinned workspace interpreter; interpreter resolving into the workspace (PATH with ., empty, /proc/self/cwd). I am fixing both on v1/hk1-pinning-allowlist. DO NOT MERGE #805. #804 MT-2 slice 2 merged (f9754def).\" >> \"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log\"","description":"Post the #805 review and log it"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":319509,"cache_read_input_tokens":32782,"output_tokens":3802,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":149},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":319509},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":3802,"cache_read_input_tokens":32782,"cache_creation_input_tokens":319509,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":319509,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":10820,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Uty2BQrNLdLi1mHuxJFcE6":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-code && cat > /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/rev805.md <<'EOF'\n**Independent hostile review at `5408fab84cec54887e5c6b5c8106cde004106ee5` — REQUEST CHANGES (two new bypasses of the allowlist, both run). The three earlier blockers are closed at the argv level. I am fixing th