ccepted). Fix: resolve `argv[0]` to an absolute path from absolute trusted PATH entries only, refuse `/proc` and `/dev`, spawn that absolute path, and refuse when not found.\n\n**Non-blocking:** S1 — refusing directories over 5,000 entries is a regression (`protectedBelow`, `tools.ts`): base had no limit; a 5,200-file `node_modules` is refused (\"delete it in parts\"), and the synchronous walk blocks the event loop: raise the limit well above normal dependency trees or walk without a cap. S2 — `/tmp/bash` or `/dev/shm/bash` as argv[0] is accepted (any absolute path outside the workspace, whatever its owner or writability): fix with B2 by using trusted directories. S3 (read) — `openSync` on the pin target can block on a FIFO swapped in after the plan (`hooks.ts` ~478): open with `O_NONBLOCK` and `fstat`. S4 (read) — no sweep of stale `run-*` directories after SIGKILL or `process.exit`.\n**Tests at that head, 0 failures:** the eleven hook files, `content_trust` 7, `strict_json` 9, `doctor_hooks` 5, `security` 14, `security_gates` 10, `deletion_guard` 2, `approval_policy` 16, `leak_guard` 6, `check_requirements` 28, `sandbox_confine` 19, `managed_policy_enforcement` 113; `tsc`, invariants, doc versions pass. **Mutations caught:** spawning the workspace path, one extra option, the interpreter-in-workspace check (1, `hooks_cli` only), the absolute protected path, `protectedBelow`. No test covers B1 or B2. Not checked: a real `--sandbox` run, winning the FIFO race, kill/crash cleanup beyond reading.\nEOF\ngh pr comment 805 --body-file /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/rev805.md | tail -1; echo \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ) REVIEW (claude-invariants-audit): #805 HK-1 pinning REQUEST CHANGES at 5408fab8: shebang runs an unpinned workspace interpreter; interpreter resolving into the workspace (PATH with ., empty, /proc/self/cwd). I am fixing both on v1/hk1-pinning-allowlist. DO NOT MERGE #805. #804 MT-2 slice 2 merged (f9754def).\" >> \"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log\"","description":"Post the #805 review and log it"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011ChNejWX8zcVtPjsDTYgn2","requestRef":"c50a844d-741a-434f-b166-5070ed55dc8d","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"5m","type":"assistant","uuid":"246a65f1-c867-4895-a54d-89fb0ca752de","timestamp":"2026-11-24T23:51:51.860Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"v1/bg3-trust-abuse-model","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
