{"parentUuid":"246a65f1-c867-4895-a54d-89fb0ca752de","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"8b93c1e0-3613-4d11-8413-99cd8a6b86e5","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Uty2BQrNLdLi1mHuxJFcE6","type":"tool_result","content":"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/805#issuecomment-7147879779","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"d6583495-81ee-4eea-9c28-1d5668bce7f0","timestamp":"2026-11-24T23:51:54.845Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/805#issuecomment-7147879779","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"gitOperation":{"pr":{"number":805,"url":"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/805","action":"commented"}}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"246a65f1-c867-4895-a54d-89fb0ca752de","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"v1/bg3-trust-abuse-model","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
{"parentUuid":"d6583495-81ee-4eea-9c28-1d5668bce7f0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNejWjHf6fGiBb4ZG7oh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01EoXn9y2m2CdT1bzbzyx13F","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"a317b41792fa50650","summary":"Fix shebang and interpreter-resolution bypasses in hooks","message":"Review of your hooks allowlist PR #805 (worktree /home/mike/nexus-wt/hk1b, branch v1/hk1-pinning-allowlist, head 5408fab84): REQUEST CHANGES; read the full review: `gh pr view 805 --comments` (last comment). `git fetch origin && git status` first; merge origin/release/v1.3.0 (it moved: MT-2 registry #804 merged), never rebase; plain `git push origin v1/hk1-pinning-allowlist` at the end, never force. Fix:\nB1: a pinned script whose shebang points to an unpinned workspace file runs it (`#!./evil`, `#!/proc/self/cwd/evil`). planProjectCommand must read the pinned script's first line (from the VERIFIED bytes you already read) and refuse unless it is absent or `#!` + an absolute path to a trusted interpreter location (see B2), optionally one arg; for the direct-run form (argv[0] a workspace file) a shebang is REQUIRED to be of that kind or the file refused; for the interpreter form the shebang is ignored by the kernel (the interpreter is explicit) but still must not be an ambiguous case: decide and say. Remember that exec of the private copy with a shebang `#!/usr/bin/env bash` goes through env's PATH lookup: refuse `env` shebangs (or resolve safely): choose, test, document.\nB2: an interpreter that resolves into the workspace is accepted (`/proc/self/cwd/bash`, PATH entries `.`/relative/empty with an interpreter not found earlier). Fix: resolve argv[0] to an ABSOLUTE path from an explicit trusted directory list (e.g. /usr/bin, /bin, /usr/local/bin, /usr/sbin, /sbin, /opt/homebrew-free: Linux only) and/or PATH entries that are absolute, not under the workspace, not under /proc or /dev, not world/group-writable, realpath'd, owned by root or the current user; refuse `/tmp`, `/dev/shm`, `/var/tmp` and any directory writable by group/other; spawn the resolved absolute path; refuse when not found or the realpath lands in the workspace. Also S2: argv[0] given as an absolute path (`/tmp/bash`) must satisfy the same trusted-directory test. Document the list.\nS1 (regression): `protectedBelow` (tools.ts) refuses directories with more than 5000 entries; base had no limit and a 5200-file node_modules was refused (\"delete it in parts\"). Remove the cap: walk asynchronously/iteratively without a numeric refusal (bound only by time or by early exit once a protected path is found: a directory containing a protected path is refused as soon as one is found; the walk must not follow symlinks), and make sure a 20k-file tree deletes fine and does not block the event loop for long (test with a generated tree of ~6000 files, keep it fast).\nS3: open pin targets with O_NONBLOCK + fstat (regular file only) so a FIFO swapped in cannot block nexus; test with a FIFO.\nS4: sweep stale `run-*` directories (older than a few minutes, owned by us, 0700) at hook-runner start; test.\nTests for each (B1: `#!./evil`, `#!/proc/self/cwd/evil`, `#!/usr/bin/env bash`, valid `#!/bin/sh`; B2: `/proc/self/cwd/bash`, PATH variants `/usr/bin::/bin`, `.:/usr/bin`, `/usr/bin:.`, relative entry, a workspace file named bash/python3.99, `/tmp/bash`, `/dev/shm/bash`, group-writable trusted dir simulated if possible), and mutations for each guard (copy aside, restore from the copy). Run, one at a time: every cli/test/hook*.test.ts and hooks_*.test.ts, content_trust, strict_json, doctor_hooks, security, security_gates, deletion_guard, approval_policy, managed_policy_enforcement, leak_guard, check_requirements, sandbox_confine; tsc --noEmit; the complexity gate (check the exit code); check_invariants; check_doc_versions. Changed/new test files three times. Commit `fix(hooks): <what>` + `Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>`; push. Report under 250 words: file:line of each fix, the trusted-directory list, tests/mutations, commit hash.","type":"message","recipient":"a317b41792fa50650","recipient_kind":"agent","content":"Review of your hooks allowlist PR #805 (worktree …"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":319509,"cache_read_input_tokens":32782,"output_tokens":3802,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":149},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":319509},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":3802,"cache_read_input_tokens":32782,"cache_creation_input_tokens":319509,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":319509,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":11104,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01EoXn9y2m2CdT1bzbzyx13F":{"to":"a317b41792fa50650","summary":"Fix shebang and interpreter-resolution bypasses in hooks","message":"Review of your hooks allowlist PR #805 (worktree /home/mike/nexus-wt/hk1b, branch v1/hk1-pinning-allowlist, head 5408fab84): REQUEST CHANGES; read the full review: `gh pr view 805 --comments` (last comment). `git fetch origin && git status` first; merge origin/release/v1.3.0 (it moved: MT-2 registry #804 merged), never rebase; plain `git push origin v1/hk1-pinning-allowlist` at the end, never force. Fix:\nB1: a pinned script whose shebang points to an unpinned workspace file runs it (`#!./evil`, `#!/proc/self/cwd/evil`). planProjectCommand must read the pinned script's first line (from the VERIFIED bytes you already read) and refuse unless it is absent or `#!` + an absolute path to a trusted interpreter location (see B2), optionally one arg; for the direct-run form (argv[0] a workspace file) a shebang is REQUIRED to be of that kind or the file refused; for the interpreter form the shebang is ignored by the kernel (the interpreter is explicit) but still must not be an ambiguous case: decide and say. Remember that exec of the private copy with a shebang `#!/usr/bin/env bash` goes through env's PATH lookup: refuse `env` shebangs (or resolve safely): choose, test, document.\nB2: an interpreter that resolves into the workspace is accepted (`/proc/self/cwd/bash`, PATH entries `.`/relative/empty with an interpreter not found earlier). Fix: resolve argv[0] to an ABSOLUTE path from an explicit trusted directory list (e.g. /usr/bin, /bin, /usr/local/bin, /usr/sbin, /sbin, /opt/homebrew-free: Linux only) and/or PATH entries that are absolute, not under the workspace, not under /proc or /dev, not world/group-writable, realpath'd, owned by root or the current user; refuse `/tmp`, `/dev/shm`, `/var/tmp` and any directory writable by group/other; spawn the resolved absolute path; refuse when not found or the realpath lands in the workspace. Also S2: argv[0] given as an absolute path (`/tmp/bash`) must satisfy the same trusted-directory test. Document the list.\nS1 (regression): `protectedBelow` (tools.ts) refuses directories with more than 5000 entries; base had no limit and a 5200-file node_modules was refused (\"delete it in parts\"). Remove the cap: walk asynchronously/iteratively without a numeric refusal (bound only by time or by early exit once a protected path is found: a directory containing a protected path is refused as soon as one is found; the walk must not follow symlinks), and make sure a 20k-file tree deletes fine and does not block the event loop for long (test with a generated tree of ~6000 files, keep it fast).\nS3: open pin targets with O_NONBLOCK + fstat (regular file only) so a FIFO swapped in cannot block nexus; test with a FIFO.\nS4: sweep stale `run-*` directories (older than a few minutes, owned by us, 0700) at hook-runner start; test.\nTests for each (B1: `#!./evil`, `#!/proc/self/cwd/evil`, `#!/usr/bin/env bash`, valid `#!/bin/sh`; B2: `/proc/self/cwd/bash`, PATH variants `/usr/bin::/bin`, `.:/usr/bin`, `/usr/bin:.`, relative entry, a workspace file named bash/python3.99, `/tmp/bash`, `/dev/shm/bash`, group-writable trusted dir simulated if possible), and mutations for each guard (copy aside, restore from the copy). Run, one at a time: every cli/test/hook*.test.ts and hooks_*.test.ts, content_trust, strict_json, doctor_hooks, security, security_gates, deletion_guard, approval_policy, managed_policy_enforcement, leak_guard, check_requirements, sandbox_confine; tsc --noEmit; the complexity gate (check the exit code); check_invariants; check_doc_versions. Changed/new test files three times. Commit `fix(hooks): <what>` + `Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>`; push. Report under 250 words: file:line of each fix, the trusted-directory list, tests/mutations, commit hash."}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011ChNejWX8zcVtPjsDTYgn2","requestRef":"c50a844d-741a-434f-b166-5070ed55dc8d","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"5m","type":"assistant","uuid":"0637a866-9976-4335-8626-6c79924e50c8","timestamp":"2026-11-24T23:52:02.994Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"v1/bg3-trust-abuse-model","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
