{"parentUuid":"0637a866-9976-4335-8626-6c79924e50c8","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"8b93c1e0-3613-4d11-8413-99cd8a6b86e5","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EoXn9y2m2CdT1bzbzyx13F","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"success\":true,\"message\":\"Resuming agent a317b41\",\"resumedAgentId\":\"a317b41792fa50650\",\"pin\":{\"id\":\"a317b41792fa50650\",\"name\":\"a317b41792fa50650\",\"ref\":\"5636b0\"}}"}]}]},"uuid":"2ccac73f-2d07-43b0-ae32-09654a1336c5","timestamp":"2026-11-24T23:52:03.756Z","toolUseResult":{"success":true,"message":"Resuming agent a317b41","resumedAgentId":"a317b41792fa50650","revivedAgentId":"a317b41792fa50650","pin":{"id":"a317b41792fa50650","name":"a317b41792fa50650","ref":"5636b0"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0637a866-9976-4335-8626-6c79924e50c8","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"v1/bg3-trust-abuse-model","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","hash":"93f45adaba0274cab15d9e648cf36887492628bac497e1423ce821a7d4617bff","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Uty2BQrNLdLi1mHuxJFcE6","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-code && cat > /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/rev805.md <<'EOF'\n**Independent hostile review at `5408fab84cec54887e5c6b5c8106cde004106ee5` — REQUEST CHANGES (two new bypasses of the allowlist, both run). The three earlier blockers are closed at the argv level. I am fixing the rest on this branch.**\n\n**Closed (run):** about 60 commands through `planProjectCommand`: `-ec`, `-xc`, `-uc`, `-ceu`, `-eC`, `--`, `-`, `-x.sh` as an option, `-Bx`, `-m`, `-Mstrict`, `-rfoo`, `--require=`, `--rcfile` and wrappers are refused; a directory, a symlink out of the workspace and `/dev/fd` or `/proc` script arguments are refused; names with spaces or newlines are fine and `./-x.sh` is pinned. **Verified-copy execution:** the hook prints `$0`/`__filename`/`/proc/self/cmdline` and all name the copy `…/run-XXXX/0/g.sh`; a concurrent copy-and-rename and overwrite writer against 150 spawns gave 70 runs that all printed GOOD, 80 refusals, 0 swapped runs, no leftover directories; the private directory is 0700, files 0500, a symlinked or group-writable root is refused, and under `--sandbox` it is unreachable. **Non-blocking items:** absolute protected paths held for workspaces `~/.config/nexus`, `~`, `~/.config` and the parent of `~` across write/edit/delete spellings; the orphan-process test passes.\n\n**Blocking**\n- **B1: a shebang runs an unpinned workspace file.** `./shebang.sh` containing `#!./evil` (or `#!/proc/self/cwd/evil`) is approved with only `shebang.sh` pinned; the copy runs with cwd = workspace and executed the workspace's `evil`. After approval the agent can edit `evil` and the next call runs it with no re-approval. `planProjectCommand` never reads the first line. Fix: refuse any pinned script whose `#!` line is not an absolute path to an allowlisted interpreter outside the workspace, or run the copy through an explicit interpreter.\n- **B2: an interpreter that resolves into the workspace is accepted.** `[\"/proc/self/cwd/bash\",\"g.sh\"]` passes and runs the workspace's `bash`; and with PATH containing `.`, a relative entry or an empty entry (`/usr/bin::/bin`, `.:/usr/bin`, `/usr/bin:.`) an interpreter such as `python3.99` not found earlier ran the workspace file (`hooks.ts:371-384`: `onPath` skips empty entries and `real === undefined` is accepted). Fix: resolve `argv[0]` to an absolute path from absolute trusted PATH entries only, refuse `/proc` and `/dev`, spawn that absolute path, and refuse when not found.\n\n**Non-blocking:** S1 — refusing directories over 5,000 entries is a regression (`protectedBelow`, `tools.ts`): base had no limit; a 5,200-file `node_modules` is refused (\"delete it in parts\"), and the synchronous walk blocks the event loop: raise the limit well above normal dependency trees or walk without a cap. S2 — `/tmp/bash` or `/dev/shm/bash` as argv[0] is accepted (any absolute path outside the workspace, whatever its owner or writability): fix with B2 by using trusted directories. S3 (read) — `openSync` on the pin target can block on a FIFO swapped in after the plan (`hooks.ts` ~478): open with `O_NONBLOCK` and `fstat`. S4 (read) — no sweep of stale `run-*` directories after SIGKILL or `process.exit`.\n**Tests at that head, 0 failures:** the eleven hook files, `content_trust` 7, `strict_json` 9, `doctor_hooks` 5, `security` 14, `security_gates` 10, `deletion_guard` 2, `approval_policy` 16, `leak_guard` 6, `check_requirements` 28, `sandbox_confine` 19, `managed_policy_enforcement` 113; `tsc`, invariants, doc versions pass. **Mutations caught:** spawning the workspace path, one extra option, the interpreter-in-workspace check (1, `hooks_cli` only), the absolute protected path, `protectedBelow`. No test covers B1 or B2. Not checked: a real `--sandbox` run, winning the FIFO race, kill/crash cleanup beyond reading.\nEOF\ngh pr comment 805 --body-file /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/rev805.md | tail -1; echo \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ) REVIEW (claude-invariants-audit): #805 HK-1 pinning REQUEST CHANGES at 5408fab8: shebang runs an unpinned workspace interpreter; interpreter resolving into the workspace (PATH with ., empty, /proc/self/cwd). I am fixing both on v1/hk1-pinning-allowlist. DO NOT MERGE #805. #804 MT-2 slice 2 merged (f9754def).\" >> \"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log\"","description":"Post the #805 review and log it"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01EoXn9y2m2CdT1bzbzyx13F","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"a317b41792fa50650","summary":"Fix shebang and interpreter-resolution bypasses in hooks","message":"Review of your hooks allowlist PR #805 (worktree /home/mike/nexus-wt/hk1b, branch v1/hk1-pinning-allowlist, head 5408fab84): REQUEST CHANGES; read the full review: `gh pr view 805 --comments` (last comment). `git fetch origin && git status` first; merge origin/release/v1.3.0 (it moved: MT-2 registry #804 merged), never rebase; plain `git push origin v1/hk1-pinning-allowlist` at the end, never force. Fix:\nB1: a pinned script whose shebang points to an unpinned workspace file runs it (`#!./evil`, `#!/proc/self/cwd/evil`). planProjectCommand must read the pinned script's first line (from the VERIFIED bytes you already read) and refuse unless it is absent or `#!` + an absolute path to a trusted interpreter location (see B2), optionally one arg; for the direct-run form (argv[0] a workspace file) a shebang is REQUIRED to be of that kind or the file refused; for the interpreter form the shebang is ignored by the kernel (the interpreter is explicit) but still must not be an ambiguous case: decide and say. Remember that exec of the private copy with a shebang `#!/usr/bin/env bash` goes through env's PATH lookup: refuse `env` shebangs (or resolve safely): choose, test, document.\nB2: an interpreter that resolves into the workspace is accepted (`/proc/self/cwd/bash`, PATH entries `.`/relative/empty with an interpreter not found earlier). Fix: resolve argv[0] to an ABSOLUTE path from an explicit trusted directory list (e.g. /usr/bin, /bin, /usr/local/bin, /usr/sbin, /sbin, /opt/homebrew-free: Linux only) and/or PATH entries that are absolute, not under the workspace, not under /proc or /dev, not world/group-writable, realpath'd, owned by root or the current user; refuse `/tmp`, `/dev/shm`, `/var/tmp` and any directory writable by group/other; spawn the resolved absolute path; refuse when not found or the realpath lands in the workspace. Also S2: argv[0] given as an absolute path (`/tmp/bash`) must satisfy the same trusted-directory test. Document the list.\nS1 (regression): `protectedBelow` (tools.ts) refuses directories with more than 5000 entries; base had no limit and a 5200-file node_modules was refused (\"delete it in parts\"). Remove the cap: walk asynchronously/iteratively without a numeric refusal (bound only by time or by early exit once a protected path is found: a directory containing a protected path is refused as soon as one is found; the walk must not follow symlinks), and make sure a 20k-file tree deletes fine and does not block the event loop for long (test with a generated tree of ~6000 files, keep it fast).\nS3: open pin targets with O_NONBLOCK + fstat (regular file only) so a FIFO swapped in cannot block nexus; test with a FIFO.\nS4: sweep stale `run-*` directories (older than a few minutes, owned by us, 0700) at hook-runner start; test.\nTests for each (B1: `#!./evil`, `#!/proc/self/cwd/evil`, `#!/usr/bin/env bash`, valid `#!/bin/sh`; B2: `/proc/self/cwd/bash`, PATH variants `/usr/bin::/bin`, `.:/usr/bin`, `/usr/bin:.`, relative entry, a workspace file named bash/python3.99, `/tmp/bash`, `/dev/shm/bash`, group-writable trusted dir simulated if possible), and mutations for each guard (copy aside, restore from the copy). Run, one at a time: every cli/test/hook*.test.ts and hooks_*.test.ts, content_trust, strict_json, doctor_hooks, security, security_gates, deletion_guard, approval_policy, managed_policy_enforcement, leak_guard, check_requirements, sandbox_confine; tsc --noEmit; the complexity gate (check the exit code); check_invariants; check_doc_versions. Changed/new test files three times. Commit `fix(hooks): <what>` + `Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>`; push. Report under 250 words: file:line of each fix, the trusted-directory list, tests/mutations, commit hash."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
