{"parentUuid":"2ccac73f-2d07-43b0-ae32-09654a1336c5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNemR42mV1ihPheyYNJm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The hostile review of the HK-1 pinning fix (#805) came back request changes: it still has two bypasses, found by running them. The review is posted and the fixes are being made on the branch.\n\n**Blockers:**\n- **Shebang:** a pinned script whose first line is `#!./evil` runs the unpinned workspace file `evil`. Only the script itself is pinned, so editing `evil` after approval runs the edit with no re-approval.\n- **Interpreter resolution:** an interpreter can resolve into the workspace. `/proc/self/cwd/bash` is accepted, and so is a `PATH` containing `.`, a relative entry or an empty entry. In each case the workspace file ran.\n\n**Confirmed fixed:**\n- The argument-level attacks, about 60 commands.\n- The race: 150 spawns against a swapping writer gave 0 swapped runs.\n- The private copy directory is unreachable under `--sandbox`.\n- The protected paths for `~/.config/nexus`.\n\n**Smaller items I've sent with the fix:**\n- Only trusted interpreter directories are accepted, so `/tmp/bash` is refused.\n- The new refusal of directories over 5,000 entries is a regression, since base had no limit and a 5,200-file `node_modules` was refused. I've asked for it to be removed, with the walk made non-blocking.\n- A FIFO swapped in after approval could freeze nexus.\n- Stale run directories need a sweep.\n\n**MT-2 registry (#804):** merged as `f9754def`, no blockers (reported earlier).\n\nStill running: the security review of #803. Pending: #798 (two blockers), #801, the BG-3 firer, the readiness re-measure and the release steps. v1.3.0 is not landed. The merge to `main` and the release haven't started."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3978,"cache_read_input_tokens":352291,"output_tokens":596,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3978},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":596,"cache_read_input_tokens":352291,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3978,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3978,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011ChNemQt7WQqr9S4PHQs21","requestRef":"b9fcea4c-ef34-4392-8c96-0a3ff2d0be7d","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"5m","type":"assistant","uuid":"86760af0-1ef5-4ba5-b03a-adccc6224c37","timestamp":"2026-11-24T23:52:08.776Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"v1/bg3-trust-abuse-model","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
