{"parentUuid":"f05419f5-64d7-4ca3-b03c-6374d4f4040a","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_additional_context","content":["graphify: knowledge graph at graphify-out/. For focused questions, run `graphify query \"<question>\"` (scoped subgraph, usually much smaller than GRAPH_REPORT.md) instead of grepping raw files. Read GRAPH_REPORT.md only for broad architecture context."],"hookName":"PreToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_01E2ZNFE8x6jmhSAQwQqG76d","hookEvent":"PreToolUse","hookKinds":["SettingsHookText"]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"fa68bbcd-b56a-4e1a-8b90-5ba2cec55036","timestamp":"2026-11-24T23:54:03.279Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nPreToolUse:Bash hook additional context: graphify: knowledge graph at graphify-out/. For focused questions, run `graphify query \"<question>\"` (scoped subgraph, usually much smaller than GRAPH_REPORT.md) instead of grepping raw files. Read GRAPH_REPORT.md only for broad architecture context.\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"v1/bg3-trust-abuse-model","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
{"parentUuid":"30b2d93f-6bac-4fcc-9439-d92fc3c1001c","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"096ed6db-0e75-494a-b6d4-a23fe5a00ab4","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01E2ZNFE8x6jmhSAQwQqG76d","type":"tool_result","content":"# PA-3 goal semantics acceptance (v1.3.0 qualification record)\n\n## Scope (plan PA-3)\n\n- Stale goal (earlier process/boot) resumes **paused** with visible reason.\n- Stall counting by failure fingerprint, not turn count.\n- Completion decided only by a verifier receipt; a model \"I am done\" does not complete a goal.\n- Optional token budget rolling up from sub-operations.\n- `/team` leaves experimental only after PA-1 and PA-2.\n\n## Measured on release-branch head\n\nBase: `origin/release/v1.3.0` @ `2a28fca89` (includes merged #787 PA-1, #788/#790 PA-2, #789 fingerprint stalls).\n\nCommands (isolated HOME):\n\n- `npm --prefix cli run build` — **pass** (prior slice verification; tip includes schema v7)\n- `HOME=$(mktemp -d) node --import tsx --test test/goal_lifecycle.test.ts` (cli) — **10 pass / 0 fail** (includes fingerprint-stall case)\n\nObserved coverage from deterministic tests in `cli/test/goal_lifecycle.test.ts`:\n\n- stale goal from earlier boot/process resumes paused with visible reason — **pass**\n- goal pauses at a safe boundary when token budget cap is exhausted — **pass**\n- goal pauses before dispatch when prior child token accounting is unavailable — **pass**\n- PA-3: repeated same-fingerprint unit failures block as `NOT_CONVERGING` (fingerprint stall, not turn count) — **pass**\n- goal lifecycle/verifier-receipt completion gates — **pass** as part of the suite\n\nSupporting unit docs: `docs/v1.3.0/PA3_GOAL_LIFECYCLE.md` (retry preserves fingerprint counts; revise/replace/assign/set_inputs/lift clear them; schema v7).\n\n## PA-1 / PA-2 gate for `/team`\n\n- PA-1 owner receipts and operation visibility: landed (#787).\n- PA-2 verified merge arbitration + semantic-conflict qualification: landed (#785/#788/#790).\n- `/team` may leave the experimental catalogue label once this acceptance record is on tip (see slash catalogue change in the same PR if present).\n\n## Gaps / not claimed\n\n- Restart-specific interrupted-effect reconciliation beyond stale-driver pause still requires separate qualification.\n- Provider-neutral end-to-end / live-gateway qualification remains separate.\n- No merge/tag/publish performed solely from this record; tag remains owner-gated.\n\n## Reference coding\n\nXERJ unavailable for this refresh pass on the acceptance doc itself; prior PA-3 slices recorded opencode goal boot-id patterns. `git grep` used as fallback. No XERJ feedback submitted for this docs-only refresh.\nMERGED\t2026-11-24T00:52:31Z","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"27057f83-e6e9-4648-97af-3e80bace7684","timestamp":"2026-11-24T23:54:04.046Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"# PA-3 goal semantics acceptance (v1.3.0 qualification record)\n\n## Scope (plan PA-3)\n\n- Stale goal (earlier process/boot) resumes **paused** with visible reason.\n- Stall counting by failure fingerprint, not turn count.\n- Completion decided only by a verifier receipt; a model \"I am done\" does not complete a goal.\n- Optional token budget rolling up from sub-operations.\n- `/team` leaves experimental only after PA-1 and PA-2.\n\n## Measured on release-branch head\n\nBase: `origin/release/v1.3.0` @ `2a28fca89` (includes merged #787 PA-1, #788/#790 PA-2, #789 fingerprint stalls).\n\nCommands (isolated HOME):\n\n- `npm --prefix cli run build` — **pass** (prior slice verification; tip includes schema v7)\n- `HOME=$(mktemp -d) node --import tsx --test test/goal_lifecycle.test.ts` (cli) — **10 pass / 0 fail** (includes fingerprint-stall case)\n\nObserved coverage from deterministic tests in `cli/test/goal_lifecycle.test.ts`:\n\n- stale goal from earlier boot/process resumes paused with visible reason — **pass**\n- goal pauses at a safe boundary when token budget cap is exhausted — **pass**\n- goal pauses before dispatch when prior child token accounting is unavailable — **pass**\n- PA-3: repeated same-fingerprint unit failures block as `NOT_CONVERGING` (fingerprint stall, not turn count) — **pass**\n- goal lifecycle/verifier-receipt completion gates — **pass** as part of the suite\n\nSupporting unit docs: `docs/v1.3.0/PA3_GOAL_LIFECYCLE.md` (retry preserves fingerprint counts; revise/replace/assign/set_inputs/lift clear them; schema v7).\n\n## PA-1 / PA-2 gate for `/team`\n\n- PA-1 owner receipts and operation visibility: landed (#787).\n- PA-2 verified merge arbitration + semantic-conflict qualification: landed (#785/#788/#790).\n- `/team` may leave the experimental catalogue label once this acceptance record is on tip (see slash catalogue change in the same PR if present).\n\n## Gaps / not claimed\n\n- Restart-specific interrupted-effect reconciliation beyond stale-driver pause still requires separate qualification.\n- Provider-neutral end-to-end / live-gateway qualification remains separate.\n- No merge/tag/publish performed solely from this record; tag remains owner-gated.\n\n## Reference coding\n\nXERJ unavailable for this refresh pass on the acceptance doc itself; prior PA-3 slices recorded opencode goal boot-id patterns. `git grep` used as fallback. No XERJ feedback submitted for this docs-only refresh.\nMERGED\t2026-11-24T00:52:31Z","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"30b2d93f-6bac-4fcc-9439-d92fc3c1001c","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"v1/bg3-trust-abuse-model","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
