{"parentUuid":"c2e8891f-f9b2-4055-8c58-3d1d6e87a2e2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNex8yxZaaeeF4Td6Do1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Understood: PA-3 is back in scope for v1.3.0. I recorded the reversal in memory and in the claims log, and started an independent check of PA-3 against its acceptance.\n\n**Where PA-3 stands on the release branch:** most of it is already merged by Codex.\n- Pause on restart (#758), the failure-fingerprint stall counting (#789) and an acceptance record (#791) are merged.\n- That record's own \"not claimed\" section says restart-specific interrupted-effect reconciliation beyond the stale-driver pause still needs separate qualification.\n- I reviewed #758 earlier and requested changes because a restart without a host reboot wasn't detected. I don't yet know whether that was fixed.\n- The `/team` experimental label is meant to lift now that PA-1 and PA-2 have landed, and I haven't seen that done.\n\n**What the independent check will run, with no claims taken on trust:**\n- A goal active when the process is killed and restarted without a reboot, plus a reboot and a live second driver.\n- A tampered ledger.\n- Whether the model can lift a pause.\n- A model saying \"I am done\", or forging a receipt, must not complete a goal.\n- Stalls, budget and resets.\n- Where the `/team` label lives.\n\nIt will also produce a concrete list of what is still needed to call PA-3 done.\n\nStill running: the security review of #803, and the HK-1 pinning fixes (#805) being made by the builder. Pending: #798 (two blockers), #801 and the BG-3 firer. After these: the readiness re-measure and the release steps. v1.3.0 is not landed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3553,"cache_read_input_tokens":360868,"output_tokens":529,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3553},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":529,"cache_read_input_tokens":360868,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3553,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3553,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011ChNex8kZpoTAQJaP68gXZ","requestRef":"d713091d-df64-4b1d-9f19-345a11ed1260","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"5m","type":"assistant","uuid":"2c39494f-b094-47d7-8ae1-8e8697a597c6","timestamp":"2026-11-24T23:54:33.791Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"v1/bg3-trust-abuse-model","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
