{"parentUuid":"6f1794cd-8008-4bda-9d76-52db403a1e99","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNfv8YyLJP9kLJr9aeo3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The BG-3 trust fixes are pushed to the #803 branch (`3e5ab8e95`), and two pieces of work are now running in parallel. Nothing new is merged yet.\n\n- **Independent re-review of #803:** it will re-run each of the five original attacks against the pushed fixes. #803 stays unmerged until the review is posted.\n- **BG-3 trigger firer:** being built on top of the #803 branch, local commits only. I review before anything is pushed. It must:\n  - fire jobs through the same unattended submission path as `nexus job` and schedules;\n  - re-read and re-check the approved spec at every fire;\n  - keep loopback-only, signed, replay-protected, size-capped webhooks that open no listener unless a webhook trigger is approved and enabled;\n  - protect the file-change watcher against flooding and against a triggered job re-triggering itself.\n\nThe BG-3 builder reports all five blockers fixed. The rate limiter now handles 6,000 attempts in about 7 ms. A trigger whose spec has a bad entry or a duplicate id approves nothing. The `triggers release` command was dropped from the docs and gets built with the firer.\n\nStill running:\n- PA-3 verification.\n- The HK-1 pinning fixes (#805), which the HK-1 builder is working on.\n- #798 (HK-3), where Codex is working on the review blockers.\n\nI haven't looked at #801 beyond noting that it merged. v1.3.0 is not landed. The merge to `main` and the release haven't started."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6824,"cache_read_input_tokens":379321,"output_tokens":504,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemera