{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-11-25T00:08:04.820Z","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a317b41792fa50650</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01EoXn9y2m2CdT1bzbzyx13F</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666/tasks/a317b41792fa50650.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Implement HK-1 hooks\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>All of B1, B2 and S1–S4 are fixed and pushed as `bdc6ad036` on `v1/hk1-pinning-allowlist` (plain push, release branch merged first, no foreign commits on the branch).\n\n## Fixes (`cli/src/core/hooks.ts` unless noted)\n\n- **B1, `#!` line** (`shebangProblem`, `:415`; re-checked on the verified bytes at `:622`): a script run directly must start with `#!` plus the absolute path of a listed interpreter in a trusted directory, with at most one harmless option. `env` and relative paths are refused. After an explicit shell, `node` or `python` the line is a comment and is not checked; after `perl` or `ruby`, which act on it themselves, it is.\n- **B2 and S2, interpreter location** (`trustedProgram`, `:306`): Nexus resolves the name to an absolute path and starts that path (`:610`). An absolute `argv[0]` is held to the same test.\n- **S1** (`protectedBelow`, `cli/src/tools.ts:75`): no size cap, async, yields every 256 entries, stops at the first protected path, follows no links.\n- **S3** (`readRegularFile`, `:351`): `O_NONBLOCK` open plus `fstat`, regular files only.\n- **S4** (`sweepHookRuns`, `:567`): own `run-*` directories older than ten minutes are removed before a run.\n\n## Trusted directories (`:288`, `:290`)\n\nAbsolute `PATH` entries, then `/usr/local/bin`, `/usr/bin`, `/bin`, `/usr/sbin`, `/sbin`. Each must be owned by root or the user, not group- or world-writable, and outside the workspace, `/tmp`, `/var/tmp`, `/dev`, `/proc`, `/run`, `/sys`. The program file must meet the same conditions. Empty and relative entries are never used.\n\nOne consequence: an interpreter in a group-writable directory is not found. On this host `~/.local/bin` is mode 775, so `node` is taken from a later entry.\n\n## Tests and mutations\n\n- `hooks_cli` 16, `hooks_self_approval` 19, `deletion_guard` 3, three runs each, 0 failures.\n- Every listed case is covered, including the PATH variants, `/tmp/bash`, `/dev/shm/bash`, a simulated group-writable directory, a FIFO, and a 6,000-file tree.\n- 18 mutations, each failing a test. One (relative PATH entries) survived at first; I added a test and it now fails.\n- The full requested gate list, `tsc`, the complexity gate (exit 0), `check_invariants` and `check_doc_versions` pass.\n\n`docs/HOOKS.md` documents the directory list and the `#!` rule.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>683295</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>17</tool_uses><duration_ms>961576</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
