Nexus resolves the name to an absolute path and starts that path (`:610`). An absolute `argv[0]` is held to the same test.\n- **S1** (`protectedBelow`, `cli/src/tools.ts:75`): no size cap, async, yields every 256 entries, stops at the first protected path, follows no links.\n- **S3** (`readRegularFile`, `:351`): `O_NONBLOCK` open plus `fstat`, regular files only.\n- **S4** (`sweepHookRuns`, `:567`): own `run-*` directories older than ten minutes are removed before a run.\n\n## Trusted directories (`:288`, `:290`)\n\nAbsolute `PATH` entries, then `/usr/local/bin`, `/usr/bin`, `/bin`, `/usr/sbin`, `/sbin`. Each must be owned by root or the user, not group- or world-writable, and outside the workspace, `/tmp`, `/var/tmp`, `/dev`, `/proc`, `/run`, `/sys`. The program file must meet the same conditions. Empty and relative entries are never used.\n\nOne consequence: an interpreter in a group-writable directory is not found. On this host `~/.local/bin` is mode 775, so `node` is taken from a later entry.\n\n## Tests and mutations\n\n- `hooks_cli` 16, `hooks_self_approval` 19, `deletion_guard` 3, three runs each, 0 failures.\n- Every listed case is covered, including the PATH variants, `/tmp/bash`, `/dev/shm/bash`, a simulated group-writable directory, a FIFO, and a 6,000-file tree.\n- 18 mutations, each failing a test. One (relative PATH entries) survived at first; I added a test and it now fails.\n- The full requested gate list, `tsc`, the complexity gate (exit 0), `check_invariants` and `check_doc_versions` pass.\n\n`docs/HOOKS.md` documents the directory list and the `#!` rule.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>683295</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>17</tool_uses><duration_ms>961576</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>\n</system-reminder>"}]}}
