{"parentUuid":"da3b5c5a-a335-4752-986a-942aed14b977","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNfzUUto7s6ky77fWcYG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JzuTvXM27RVswoCuLS7C7R","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Re-review PR #805 hooks fixes","subagent_type":"reviewer","prompt":"Independent RE-review of GitHub PR #805 (HK-1 project-hook allowlist and verified-bytes execution) in ~/nexus-code, base `release/v1.3.0`. Take the full head SHA from `gh pr view 805 --json headRefOid` (expected to start `bdc6ad03`), review exactly that, and say whether it moved or merged. The previous review is the PR comment \"Independent hostile review at `5408fab8…` — REQUEST CHANGES\" (`gh pr view 805 --comments`): B1 a shebang (`#!./evil`, `#!/proc/self/cwd/evil`) ran an unpinned workspace file; B2 an interpreter resolving into the workspace (`/proc/self/cwd/bash`, PATH with `.`, relative or empty entries) ran workspace code; S1 refusing directories over 5000 entries was a regression; S2 `/tmp/bash` accepted; S3 FIFO could block; S4 no sweep of stale `run-*` dirs. Fix commit `bdc6ad036` (`git show --stat`, diff): `shebangProblem`, `trustedProgram`, trusted-directory list, `readRegularFile` (O_NONBLOCK+fstat), `sweepHookRuns`, async `protectedBelow` in `cli/src/tools.ts`, docs. Re-run the ORIGINAL attacks by RUNNING (throwaway HOME, temp workspaces, no network, no inference) and find new ones:\n1. Shebang: direct-run pinned script with `#!./evil`, `#!/proc/self/cwd/evil`, `#!/usr/bin/env bash`, `#!env -S ...`, `#!/bin/sh` (ok), `#!/usr/bin/bash -x`, `#!/bin/bash -c`, two options, a long line, CRLF (`#!/bin/sh\\r`), BOM before `#!`, NUL bytes, no shebang at all (kernel runs it as sh via ENOEXEC? the copy is exec'd directly: what happens: refused?), `#!/usr/bin/python3 -c ...`, `#! /bin/sh` with a space, interpreter listed but located in a group-writable dir, a shebang pointing to a symlink in /usr/bin that points into the workspace. After an explicit interpreter the shebang is a comment: check `perl`/`ruby` (which act on `#!` options such as `-x`, `-i`, `-e`? e.g. `#!/usr/bin/perl -e ...`, `#!perl -T -x`), and python/node/sh variants (sh with `#!` ignored: ok). Is the shebang checked on the VERIFIED bytes that run (not a re-read)?\n2. Interpreter location: `/proc/self/cwd/bash`, `/proc/self/root/...`, `/dev/shm/bash`, `/tmp/bash`, `/var/tmp/bash`, PATH variants `.`, `:`, `/usr/bin::/bin`, `~/bin`, relative `bin`, a PATH entry that is a symlink into the workspace (resolve with realpath, and the program file itself being a symlink into the workspace), a trusted directory that is a bind-like path, `python3.99` not found (refused?), the interpreter ELF itself replaced between resolution and spawn in a directory owned by the user (the user is the trust base; document), hard links, a workspace that is itself inside a trusted directory (e.g. workspace under /usr/local/bin?). Does the hook actually spawn the resolved ABSOLUTE path, and with a scrubbed environment (no PATH-dependent re-resolution inside `sh` for later commands is not our problem, but `env`/`LD_*`/`BASH_ENV`/`NODE_OPTIONS`/`PYTHONPATH`/`PERL5LIB`/`RUBYLIB`/`PYTHONSTARTUP`/`NODE_PATH` must not leak from the parent environment or be settable by the workspace: check each).\n3. Interpreter-specific implicit code loading with the verified copy: python adds the script's directory (the private run dir: empty/controlled) to sys.path: a workspace `python3` package of the same name as stdlib? cwd is the workspace: `python -I` isolates, but without `-I` python puts the SCRIPT dir not cwd on sys.path (ok), node resolves `node_modules` from the script directory (private dir: none) but `NODE_PATH`... ; perl `@INC` has no `.`; ruby; bash sources `BASH_ENV` (scrubbed); report what a script that does `require('./x')`/`import x`/`source ./x` gets (refused/fails: documented break), and whether any allowed interpreter loads code from the workspace implicitly (cwd) at startup (e.g. python `sitecustomize`/`usercustomize` from the cwd? no; node `.noderc`? ; perl `PERL5OPT`; ruby `RUBYOPT`): verify with a marker file test per interpreter available on the host.\n4. S1: delete a 20k-file generated tree works and does not block the event loop for long; a directory containing a protected path (`.git`? check what is protected: `hooks.json` inside a nested dir) is refused; symlink loops; a directory with a symlink to outside is not followed. S3: FIFO swapped in at the pin target does not hang (run with a timeout). S4: stale `run-*` older than 10 minutes swept, younger ones and other users' / non-matching names left alone; a symlink named `run-x` is not followed.\n5. Regression: operator hooks unaffected (any program, no allowlist, no verified copy); gate ordering (`hooks_gate_bypass`); `hooks_examples` and the shipped `examples/hooks`; docs claims vs code (`docs/HOOKS.md`: every claim about the allowlist, shebang rule, trusted directories, verified copy, the self-contained-file rule, unsandboxed limits).\nRun at head, one at a time: every `cli/test/hook*.test.ts` and `hooks_*.test.ts`, `content_trust`, `strict_json`, `doctor_hooks`, `security`, `security_gates`, `deletion_guard`, `approval_policy`, `managed_policy_enforcement`, `leak_guard`, `check_requirements`, `sandbox_confine`; `cd cli && npx tsc --noEmit -p .`; the complexity gate (check the exit code); `node scripts/check_invariants.mjs`; `node scripts/check_doc_versions.mjs`. Mutations (copy aside, restore from the copy, never `git checkout`): drop the shebang check; resolve interpreters through PATH including relative entries; accept `/tmp` as a trusted directory; spawn the workspace path; drop O_NONBLOCK; each must fail a test.\nRules: do NOT edit ~/nexus-code or existing worktrees. `git -C ~/nexus-code fetch origin && git -C ~/nexus-code worktree add --detach ~/nexus-wt/rev805b <full sha>`; `cp -a ~/nexus-code/cli/node_modules ~/nexus-wt/rev805b/cli/`; `mkdir -p ~/nexus-wt/rev805b/core/target/release && cp ~/nexus-wt/ls1b/core/target/release/{harness-core,nexus-tui} ~/nexus-wt/rev805b/core/target/release/`. Tests: `cd ~/nexus-wt/rev805b/cli && TMPDIR=/dev/shm HOME=$(mktemp -d) node --import tsx --test test/<name>.test.ts 2>&1 | tail -20`. Never touch the real ~/.nexus, ~/.config/nexus, /etc/nexus. Stop processes by their own pid; never `pkill -f`. No commits, pushes or GitHub comments. Remove probes and the worktree at the end. Shell is zsh (`bash -c` for loops); prefix `rtk proxy` if output looks filtered; a safety check blocks scripts containing `rm`.\nReport under 450 words: verdict (ACCEPT / ACCEPT WITH FOLLOW-UPS / REQUEST CHANGES) at the exact SHA; B1/B2/S1-S4 each closed or not with the attack run; new findings with file:line, run-or-read, blocking or not (any way for a hostile repository or the agent's sandboxed tools to run unpinned/swapped/workspace code with the operator's rights, or load workspace code implicitly through an allowed interpreter, is blocking; the documented unsandboxed limits are not); test counts; mutation results; what you did not check."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1922,"cache_read_input_tokens":386145,"output_tokens":3093,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":45},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1922},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":3093,"cache_read_input_tokens":386145,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1922,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1922,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":19244,"wireToolInputs