s explicit action.\n\n**`/team` label:** `slash/catalog.ts:138` has no `[experimental]` tag, and I found no git history that ever added one. The remaining labels are `docs/EXECUTION_CONVERGENCE.md:6` and `operation_cli.ts:300` (`nexus operation`). `docs/USER_MANUAL.md` has no `/goal` section, and the `/team` row at line 617 has no label. The lift is therefore effectively done in the catalogue; the doc and CLI label remain.\n\n**Docs vs code**\n- `PA3_GOAL_LIFECYCLE.md` says a live lock holder is never treated as stale. That is true only on the drive path, not the read path.\n- It says same-host process death is detected, which is true only when the pid is not recycled and `activeHost` is set.\n- It says the operator raises the cap, which has no mechanism (finding 5).\n- `PA3_ACCEPTANCE.md` says \"prior slice verification\" for the build, and it repeats the `/team` lift as pending.\n\n**Tests at the tip, one file at a time, all passing, no failures:**\n- `goal_lifecycle` 10, `goal_ledger_propagation` 2, `check_requirements` 28, `durable_continuity` 42, `fault_kill_mid_tool_call` 1, `leak_guard` 6.\n- All 19 `operation_*` files pass, including `operation_git` 44 and `operation_view` 34.\n- `tsc --noEmit` exit 0, complexity gate exit 0, `check_invariants` 0, `check_doc_versions` 0.\n\n**Mutations (restored from copies):**\n- Disabling the stale pause fails 2 tests.\n- Disabling the fingerprint stall fails 1.\n- Disabling the budget pause fails 1.\n- Disabling the reviewer gate fails 1.\n- Removing the verifier-receipt gate in `goalStatus` fails nothing (10 of 10 pass). That is a coverage gap.\n\n**Not checked:** Node 22, a host without `/proc`, two processes starting at once, a truncated state file, unknown-key tamper, the TUI and sidecar event stream, and a full end-to-end goal reaching COMPLETE.\n\n**Still needed to call PA-3 done**\n1. Fix finding 1: add start-time identity and make partial identity fail closed. Add tests for a recycled pid, another host, pid withou