{"parentUuid":"4d340cb2-c738-4fba-9cb8-63c38cdf4472","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNg2RMRyNBBhtJHDGM3n","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019qHkSAJUNrjwc2Yex7ESzR","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Complete PA-3 goal semantics","subagent_type":"general-purpose","prompt":"Complete unit PA-3 (goal semantics) in the worktree /home/mike/nexus-wt/pa3f (branch `v1/pa3-completion`, based on `origin/release/v1.3.0` tip; Nexus Code, TypeScript CLI in `cli/`). The owner revoked PA-3's deferral: it must meet its acceptance. Acceptance: \"stale goal resumes paused with a visible reason; a model 'I am done' does not complete a goal\". An independent verification at tip b6cb12d7 found the second clause MET and the first only PARTLY MET. Read first: `docs/v1.3.0/PA3_ACCEPTANCE.md`, `PA3_GOAL_LIFECYCLE.md`, `PA4_GOAL_LEDGER_PROPAGATION.md`, `cli/src/core/goal.ts` (~68-80 stale logic), `cli/src/core/operation_runner.ts` (~859-890 driver identity `activePid`/`activeHost`), `cli/src/core/process_identity.ts` (start-time identity helpers used by verify service and hooks), `cli/src/operation_cli.ts`, the `/goal` slash code, `cli/test/goal_lifecycle.test.ts`, `/home/mike/nexus-wt/pa3f/AGENTS.md`, `docs/v1.3.0/PLAN.md` PA-3 row. The verification findings you must fix (reproduce each first with a failing test):\n1. BLOCKING (run): the stale check FAILS OPEN and a plain `driveOperation` then executes the unit with no operator action in these seeded states: a recycled pid (pid alive but a different process), a state from another host, a pid with no host recorded, and a state with only the current boot id. The lock records `startTicks` but the goal identity does not (`goal.ts:72`, `operation_runner.ts:874`). Fix: record the driver's identity as {pid, host, start ticks (kernel start time from /proc/<pid>/stat via process_identity.ts), boot id}; a goal is considered actively driven ONLY if every identity field is present and matches a live process of this host whose start time equals; ANY missing/partial/mismatching identity = stale = resumes PAUSED with a specific visible reason (distinguish: process gone; pid recycled; other host; identity unknown); fail closed everywhere including the read path (`nexus operation status`, `--dag`, `/goal status`, `/goal list`) and the drive path; the read path must show PAUSED (derived) consistently with what drive would do (today `nexus operation status` shows RUNNING for a killed goal: derive the same state or say \"will pause on next drive: reason\"). Backward compatibility: state files written by the previous version (no start ticks) are treated as unknown identity = stale (pause) — document. Tests (each fails without the guard): recycled pid, other host, pid without host, boot-id only, hand-edited ledger (future timestamps, unknown keys, missing keys, type confusion), a live driver stays RUNNING and a second process cannot double-drive, kill -9 then restart pauses, reboot (other boot id) pauses, `/goal status` while another process drives must not throw `OperationLockedError` to the user (read path should report \"driven by pid N\").\n2. State tamper: `~/.nexus/tasks/<id>.json` (goal state, caps, stall counts) can be rewritten by an UNSANDBOXED `run_command`; file tools are jailed to the workspace and bwrap blocks shell writes under --sandbox. Do what is right and simple: (a) add the task-state directory (resolve the real state dir with the same function core/state.ts uses: `NEXUS_STATE_DIR` or `~/.nexus`, tasks subdirectory) to the protected paths with an absolute pattern the way `security.ts` DEFAULT_PROTECTED_PATHS handles `~/.config/nexus` entries (look for how HK-1's #805 did absolute patterns if landed on your base; `git fetch origin` and look; otherwise add a minimal absolute-path mechanism consistent with `isPathProtected`) so the advisory command check and the file tools refuse it; (b) state plainly in docs/v1.3.0/PA3_GOAL_LIFECYCLE.md and docs/USER_MANUAL.md that an unsandboxed command runs with the operator's rights and can rewrite goal state (use --sandbox for untrusted work), that integrity is by file mode 0600 and not by signature; do NOT add a signature scheme. Test the protected-path behaviour (tools refuse; `isPathProtected` true).\n3. Coverage gap: removing the verifier-receipt gate in `goalStatus` fails no test. Add a test that fails when that gate is removed (a goal with a unit marked done by the model but no verifier receipt must not report COMPLETE) and mutate to prove it.\n4. Fingerprint mismatch: a failure reason containing a secret-shaped string never stalls because the persisted fingerprint is redacted but the fresh one is not (count restarts at 1). Compute and compare fingerprints over the same redacted form; test with a secret-shaped reason repeated 3 times → NOT_CONVERGING; plain reasons still accumulate across reloads; different reasons do not trip.\n5. Token cap: the doc says the operator raises or removes the cap but no mechanism exists (the cap is read from `NEXUS_OPERATION_MAX_TOTAL_TOKENS` at plan time only). Add an operator command (terminal-or-not: it only tightens or loosens a numeric cap; decide: loosening needs the same operator-intent as resume; make it `nexus operation budget <id> --max-total-tokens N|none` that is refused when invoked from inside an agent-spawned process tree if such a marker exists, otherwise documented as an operator command; keep it simple) that updates the goal's cap, records an audit entry (who/when/old/new) in the operation journal, and takes effect on the next dispatch; also check the cap per dispatch so concurrent units cannot overshoot by more than one batch: document the bound honestly if not exact. Test.\n6. Docs and labels: fix the false claims in `PA3_GOAL_LIFECYCLE.md` (live lock holder never stale only on drive path; same-host death detection and recycled pids; cap mechanism) and `PA3_ACCEPTANCE.md` (\"prior slice verification\", `/team` lift pending); remove the `experimental` wording for `/team` in `docs/EXECUTION_CONVERGENCE.md:6` and `cli/src/operation_cli.ts:300` ONLY IF PA-1 and PA-2 gates are recorded as landed in `PA3_ACCEPTANCE.md` (they are: #787, #785/#788/#790): apply the lift and add a short `/team` and `/goal` section to docs/USER_MANUAL.md; fix the ungrammatical stale reason text; make `pauseReason ?? stale` not hide the stale reason (show both).\nRun, one at a time: `goal_lifecycle`, `goal_ledger_propagation`, `durable_continuity`, `fault_kill_mid_tool_call`, every `operation_*` test (`ls cli/test | grep operation`), `security`, `slash*`, `leak_guard`, `check_requirements`, `protocol_schema` and any schema `--check` generator whose output changes (operation state schema version bumps follow `docs/protocol` ledger rules and `STATE_COMPATIBILITY`: read how PA-3's earlier slice bumped it to v7: if the state shape gains fields, add them additively with a version note; do not break loading old states: they load as unknown identity = stale); `cd cli && npx tsc --noEmit -p .`; the complexity gate (check the exit code; `driveOperation` must not grow: if the stale check lives in it, extract a helper); `node scripts/check_invariants.mjs`; `node scripts/check_doc_versions.mjs`. Mutations (copy aside, restore from the copy, never `git checkout`): each new guard (identity partial → stale, pid recycled, other host, receipt gate, redacted fingerprint, protected path, cap audit): each must fail a test. Changed/new test files three times.\nRules: new test files start with `import \"./helpers/leak_guard.js\";`. One test file at a time: `cd /home/mike/nexus-wt/pa3f/cli && TMPDIR=/dev/shm HOME=$(mktemp -d) node --import tsx --test test/<name>.test.ts 2>&1 | tail -30` (throwaway HOME mandatory; never read the real ~/.nexus, ~/.config/nexus, /etc/nexus; no network, no live inference; scripted gateway `cli/test/helpers/fixtures.ts`). Stop processes only by their own pid, never `pkill -f`. Shell is zsh (`bash -c` for loops); output passes through `rtk` (prefix `rtk proxy` if cut); a safety check blocks scripts containing `rm`. Several agents edit `operation_runner.ts`, `index.ts`, CHANGELOG: `git fetch origin` and merge origin/release/v1.3.0 often, never rebase, check `git log origin/release/v1.3.0..HEAD` for foreign commits before each commit. Commit locally in 3-4 commits `fix(goal): …` / `docs(goal): …` each ending with `Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>`; do NOT push, no PR. Report under 450 words: commits (hashes), per finding the fix location and the test+mutation, state-schema changes, what an unsandboxed command can still do, anything left open."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6343,"cache_read_input_tokens":388067,"output_tokens":4335,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":141},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6343},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4335,"cache_read_input_tokens":388067,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6343,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6343,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":22544,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_019qHkSAJUNrjwc2Yex7ESzR":{"description":"Complete PA-3 goal semantics","subagent_type":"general-purpose","prompt":"Complete unit PA-3 (goal semantics) in the worktree /home/mike/nexus-wt/pa3f (branch `v1/pa3-completion`, based on `origin/release/v1.3.0` tip; Nexus Code, TypeScript CLI in `cli/`). The owner revoked PA-3's deferral: it must meet its acceptance. Acceptance: \"stale goal resumes paused with a visible reaso