{"parentUuid":"2d8b2c85-3af8-47cb-a50c-6484a2d62a4a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNg4sw9PB6P2vUJfeQtN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The PA-3 verification came back: only part of the acceptance is met, so PA-3 is not done. I've claimed the completion work and started a builder, which commits locally only.\n\n**What was verified (run, at release tip `b6cb12d7a`):**\n- **\"A model 'I am done' does not complete a goal\": met.** A model that only calls `task_completed`, marks its own requirement verified, or writes forged receipt files never completed a goal.\n- **\"A stale goal resumes paused with a visible reason\": only partly met.**\n  - The case from my earlier #758 review (restart without a host reboot) is fixed. A driver killed with `kill -9` and restarted reads PAUSED with a clear reason, and a live driver is never double-driven.\n  - The check still fails open in four seeded states: a recycled pid, another host, a pid with no host, and only a boot id. In those, a plain drive ran the unit with no operator action. The goal doesn't record the driver's process start time, which the lock does.\n\n**What the builder will fix:**\n- **Driver identity.** Record the driver's pid, host, start time and boot id. Any missing or partial identity counts as stale and pauses. The read path (`nexus operation status`, `/goal status`) must agree with the drive path. At present `operation status` shows RUNNING for a killed goal.\n- **Goal state protection.** Goal state under `~/.nexus/tasks` can be rewritten by an unsandboxed command. I'm adding a protected path for it and stating the limit in the docs, with no signature scheme.\n- **Test gap.** Removing the verifier-receipt gate currently fails no test, so I'm adding one.\n- **Fingerprint mismatch.** Failure reasons with a secret-shaped string never trigger a stall, and the redacted and fresh fingerprints will be compared consistently.\n- **Token cap.** The docs say the operator can raise or remove the cap, but there is no mechanism for that. I'm adding one with an audit entry.\n- **Docs and labels.** False claims in the PA-3 docs get corrected. The `/team` experimental label remains in two places (the CLI and one doc), and that lift gets applied now that PA-1 and PA-2 have landed.\n\n**Other work running:**\n- The re-review of the HK-1 hooks fixes (#805) at `bdc6ad036`.\n- The re-review of the BG-3 trust fixes (#803).\n- The BG-3 firer build.\n\nPending: #798 (HK-3) and #801. v1.3.0 is not landed. The merge to `main` and the release haven't started."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4758,"cache_read_input_tokens":394410,"output_tokens":849,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4758},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":849,"cache_read_input_tokens":394410,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4758,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4758,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011ChNg4smEMB6LbR5W2E93g","requestRef":"372b97d6-1196-4739-b61b-10bb3af7be0b","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"5m","type":"assistant","uuid":"c56aae94-8067-4af7-91a7-c7606cb53d32","timestamp":"2026-11-25T00:09:14.404Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"v1/bg3-trust-abuse-