mit.ts:344-348`: `recordFailure` skips the quarantine cap. 1,000 distinct ids gave 1,000 quarantines against a cap of 3, so the \"at most 4,096\" claim is false. Run. Fix: apply the same full-map guard.\n- `trigger_rate_limit.ts:443,474`: LRU eviction resets the evicted trigger's or workspace's window, so the rate cap resets. Run. Per-trigger it is bounded by the workspace cap; evicting a workspace window clears that workspace's own cap, which needs 256 other workspaces firing. The header says this fails closed, which is true only for quarantines. Also `limiterFor` creates limiters for denied and unknown ids. Fix: create limiters only for approved ids, or keep entries with a live window.\n- `limiterKey` checks only that the path is absolute. A symlinked workspace path does not share a limit with its real path; the caller must pass the real path. Fix: `realpath` inside.\n- A rate-limit-triggered quarantine (3 denials, 15 minutes) can be re-forced by whoever can fire the trigger. The design accepts this.\n- The terminal prompt crashes with an unhandled `AbortError` on EOF. It fails closed, but the stack trace is ugly.\n- Docs: `worktree-write` is described as opt-in, but the CLI has no flag, so such specs are refused. The field cap counts JSON quotes and escapes.\n- The path printed on the first line of `approve` is unescaped.\n- A sparse `admittedAt` array is accepted, but JSON cannot produce one.\n\n**Other checks**\n- A 0644 spec is accepted. 0664 and 0666 are refused with a `chmod go-w` hint, and a symlinked spec is refused. A file owned by another non-root uid is refused in code; I could not test it.\n- Duplicate ids and a bad third spec approve nothing.\n- `NEXUS_TRUST_WORKSPACE=1` does not count for `approve`, `list` or `status`.\n- `secretEnv` works. A 1-character inline secret is refused and a 16-character one is accepted.\n- The docs example parses.\n\n**Tests at head**\nAll pass: rate_limit 55, self_approval 2, spec 24, trust 18, triggers_cli 21, security 14, workspace_trust 5, hooks_self_approval 10, leak_guard 6, check_requirements 28, protocol_schema 8. `tsc`, the complexity gate (exit 0), `check_invariants` and `check_doc_versions` are clean.\n\n**Mutations**\nAll six failed tests, restored from copies with a clean tree afterwards:\n- Dropping the protected path: 2 failures.\n- Truncating the verifier in the display: 1 failure.\n- Skipping the terminal check: 1 failure.\n- Skipping the workspace cap: 2 failures.\n- Skipping validation in `restore`: 31 failures.\n- Recording denials: 2 failures.\n\n**Not checked**\n- Node 22.\n- `--sandbox` reachability.\n- A root-owned or other-uid store or spec.\n- The firer, which does not exist.\n\nI removed the probes and the worktree, and I did not touch the real HOME.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>97913</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>31</tool_uses><duration_ms>536543</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>\n</system-reminder>"}]}}
