{"parentUuid":"2e404f6d-28d0-41f6-b85d-73b0ccabc09c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNggtfoNKmZqBeAGM8Ho","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018dgEdzfd1VfV48cLLuvy3o","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"a88f34e8c89df42f5","summary":"Trust model merged; add review follow-ups to firer","message":"Update for the BG-3 firer: PR #803 (the trust model) was MERGED into release/v1.3.0 as 2aef3052 at head 3e5ab8e95 (re-review ACCEPT WITH FOLLOW-UPS). `git fetch origin` and merge `origin/release/v1.3.0` into `v1/bg3-firer` now (never rebase); that makes your base the release branch. In your firer branch ALSO fix the re-review's follow-ups (read the comment: `gh pr view 803 --comments`, last one), each with a test that fails without it (mutate a copy and restore from it): (1) triggers_cli.ts:~55 the confirmation must be the LITERAL `yes` (no /i, no trim: ` yes ` and `YES` refuse); (2) trigger_rate_limit.ts:~344-348 `recordFailure` must apply the same full-quarantine-map guard (1,000 distinct ids must not produce more than the cap); (3) trigger_rate_limit.ts:~443,474 LRU eviction must not reset a live window: create limiters only for approved ids (unknown/denied ids never create state) or keep entries that still have a live window; (4) `limiterKey` must realpath the workspace itself; (5) the terminal prompt must handle EOF/AbortError without a stack trace (print a clear refusal, exit 2); (6) docs: `worktree-write` triggers: either support it (it must then require the same explicit operator approval line as schedules' write level and show it in the approve display) or state it is refused in v1.3.0; escape the first path line in `approve` output. Then continue the firer as specified. Report as before when done (commits, design choices, tests/mutations, open items).","type":"message","recipient":"a88f34e8c89df42f5","recipient_kind":"agent","content":"Update for the BG-3 firer: PR #803 (the trust m