{"parentUuid":"eadbe61c-5c24-4a81-9c9d-2ad32e80e737","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNghLpQvPEG5zhDuCMAw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The BG-3 trust model (#803) is merged into `release/v1.3.0` as `2aef3052`. The re-review accepted it with follow-ups: all five earlier blockers were closed by re-running the original attacks, and there are no new blockers. Required checks were green at the exact head and release CI was green at the tip first. I read the merged state back, but I haven't yet confirmed release CI on the new merge commit.\n\nThe follow-ups, none blocking, are going into the firer branch:\n- Approval must require the literal `yes`; the current check accepts `YES` and ` yes `.\n- The failure path skips the quarantine cap, so 1,000 ids gave 1,000 quarantines against a cap of 3.\n- Evicting a limiter resets its rate window.\n- The workspace path should be resolved to its real path inside the limiter key.\n- The approval prompt crashes with a stack trace on end-of-input.\n- `worktree-write` triggers are documented as opt-in but refused.\n\nI told the firer's builder to merge the release branch and add these.\n\n**Still running:**\n- **BG-3 firer:** being built, commits local only.\n- **PA-3 completion:** builder working on the stale-identity and other fixes.\n- **HK-1 hooks (#805):** re-review of the shebang and interpreter-resolution fixes.\n\nPending: #798 (HK-3, with Codex on the review blockers). v1.3.0 is not landed. The merge to `main` and the release haven't started."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":847,"cache_read_input_tokens":405096,"output_tokens":486,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_token