{"parentUuid":"bfcb7445-b86f-4b6f-86b1-eb1d8d3d1878","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNgtduNnZLsmF6yLFiuD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DXx3u7ZpQGiHxURv2bubjF","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"a317b41792fa50650","summary":"Fix shebang whitespace bypass","message":"#805 re-review (head bdc6ad036): one blocker left, confirmed by running. In /home/mike/nexus-wt/hk1b (branch v1/hk1-pinning-allowlist): `git fetch origin && git status`, merge origin/release/v1.3.0 (never rebase; plain push at the end, never force). `shebangProblem` (hooks.ts ~415) uses `.trim()`, which strips form feed, CR, VT and NBSP, but the kernel skips only space and tab: `#!\\f/bin/sh`, `#!\\r/bin/sh`, `#!\\v/bin/sh` are accepted yet the kernel treats `\\f/bin/sh` as a path relative to the cwd (the workspace), where a hostile repo ships a directory named `\\f` containing `bin/sh`; it ran a workspace file. Fix: parse like the kernel: after `#!` skip only spaces and tabs, take the interpreter up to the next space or tab, one optional argument after further spaces/tabs; REFUSE the line if it contains any control character (<0x20 except the single trailing newline, and 0x7f) or any byte above 0x7f anywhere in the first line; the interpreter path must be absolute and pass `trustedProgram`. Tests: `#!\\f/bin/sh`, `#!\\r/bin/sh`, `#!\\v/bin/sh`, `#!\\xa0/bin/sh` (as bytes), `#!/bin/sh\\r`, tab variants, `#!\\t/bin/sh` (accepted: kernel skips tab), plus the existing cases; end-to-end spawn test with a planted directory named `\\f` in the workspace proving nothing runs; mutation: restore `.trim()` → test fails. Also drop `NODE_PATH` from the hook environment allowlist (`hook_runner.ts` hookEnvironment) with a test that it is absent when set in the parent. Rerun: every cli/test/hook*.test.ts and hooks_*.test.ts, content_trust, strict_json, doctor_hooks, security, security_gates, deletion_guard, approval_policy, mana