{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","hash":"20e090ae83f0d795fa12443bf5d463b9b6e43325ce58468dd442cc45cba48c43","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UfDqnA9u244cASPHnPfbER","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-code && gh pr comment 805 --body \"**Independent re-review at \\`bdc6ad0361245555052fbae468a8839b40a20476\\` — REQUEST CHANGES. B2 and S1–S4 are closed (run); B1 is closed except one whitespace bypass, fix in progress.**\n\n**B1 bypass (run):** \\`#!\\\\f/bin/sh\\`, \\`#!\\\\r/bin/sh\\` and \\`#!\\\\v/bin/sh\\` ran a workspace file (\\`EVILSH\\`). \\`shebangProblem\\` calls \\`.trim()\\`, which strips form feed, CR, VT and NBSP; the kernel skips only space and tab, so it reads \\`\\\\f/bin/sh\\` as a path relative to the cwd (the workspace), where a hostile repository ships a directory named \\`\\\\f\\` containing \\`bin/sh\\`. Fix: take the interpreter with the kernel's rule (skip spaces and tabs only, split on space/tab only) and refuse any control character or byte above 0x7f in the line; tests for \\`\\\\f\\`, \\`\\\\r\\`, \\`\\\\v\\`, \\`\\\\xa0\\`. A CRLF shebang fails ENOENT (safe). Refused as intended: \\`#!./evil\\`, \\`#!/proc/self/cwd/evil\\`, \\`env\\`, \\`-c\\`, two options, a BOM, no shebang, NUL; accepted: \\`#!/bin/sh\\`, \\`#! /bin/sh\\`, \\`#!/usr/bin/bash -x\\`.\n**Closed (run):** B2: \\`/proc/self/cwd/bash\\`, \\`/proc/self/root/…\\`, \\`/dev/shm\\`, \\`/tmp\\`, \\`/var/tmp\\`, a symlink into the workspace and \\`python3.99\\` refused; PATH entries \\`.\\`, \\`:\\`, \\`/usr/bin::/bin\\`, relative \\`bin\\` and a workspace symlink fall through to \\`/usr/bin/bash\\`; the spawned argv[0] is absolute. S1: deleting a 20,000-file tree took 97 ms with a longest event-loop gap of 13 ms; a nested \\`hooks.json\\` is refused; symlink loops and links out are not followed. S2: \\`/tmp/bash\\` refused. S3: a FIFO and \\`/dev/zero\\` refused in 1 ms. S4: old \\`run-*\\` swept; a young one, other names, a \\`run-file\\` file and a \\`run-x\\` symlink left alone.\n**Non-blocking:** \\`hook_runner.ts\\` \\`hookEnvironment\\` passes the parent's \\`NODE_PATH\\` through (the workspace cannot set it): drop it. The interpreter file is checked and then spawned later (covered by the documented trust-base rule). \\`source ./x\\` in a pinned script loads an unpinned file: documented self-contained-file rule. No allowed interpreter loaded workspace code at startup (python \\`sitecustomize\\`/stdlib shadowing/\\`import\\`, node \\`require\\`/\\`node_modules\\`/\\`.noderc\\`, perl \\`use\\`, bash \\`.bashrc\\`, sh \\`.profile\\`: all ignored the marker files); the hook environment is an allowlist without \\`BASH_ENV\\`, \\`ENV\\`, \\`PYTHONPATH\\`, \\`PERL5LIB\\`, \\`RUBYLIB\\`, \\`PYTHONSTARTUP\\`, \\`PERL5OPT\\`, \\`RUBYOPT\\`, \\`LD_*\\`.\n**Tests:** 23 files, 0 failures (\\`managed_policy_enforcement\\` 113, \\`hooks_self_approval\\` 19); \\`tsc\\`, the complexity gate, invariants, doc versions pass. Mutations that broke a test: dropping the shebang check (2), relative PATH entries (3), \\`/tmp\\` trusted (1), spawning the workspace path (2), dropping \\`O_NONBLOCK\\` (1). No test covers the whitespace bypass. Not checked: ruby (not installed), a workspace under \\`/usr/local/bin\\`, hard links, \\`#!perl -T -x\\` live.\" | tail -1; echo \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ) REVIEW (claude-invariants-audit): #805 REQUEST CHANGES at bdc6ad03: shebang whitespace bypass (\\\\f \\\\r \\\\v after #!, trim() vs kernel rule). Fixing on v1/hk1-pinning-allowlist. #803 BG-3 trust model MERGED (2aef3052). DO NOT MERGE #805.\" >> \"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log\"","description":"Post the #805 third review and log it"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DXx3u7ZpQGiHxURv2bubjF","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"a317b41792fa50650","summary":"Fix shebang whitespace bypass","message":"#805 re-review (head bdc6ad036): one blocker left, confirmed by running. In /home/mike/nexus-wt/hk1b (branch v1/hk1-pinning-allowlist): `git fetch origin && git status`, merge origin/release/v1.3.0 (never rebase; plain push at the end, never force). `shebangProblem` (hooks.ts ~415) uses `.trim()`, which strips form feed, CR, VT and NBSP, but the kernel skips only space and tab: `#!\\f/bin/sh`, `#!\\r/bin/sh`, `#!\\v/bin/sh` are accepted yet the kernel treats `\\f/bin/sh` as a path relative to the cwd (the workspace), where a hostile repo ships a directory named `\\f` containing `bin/sh`; it ran a workspace file. Fix: parse like the kernel: after `#!` skip only spaces and tabs, take the interpreter up to the next space or tab, one optional argument after further spaces/tabs; REFUSE the line if it contains any control character (<0x20 except the single trailing newline, and 0x7f) or any byte above 0x7f anywhere in the first line; the interpreter path must be absolute and pass `trustedProgram`. Tests: `#!\\f/bin/sh`, `#!\\r/bin/sh`, `#!\\v/bin/sh`, `#!\\xa0/bin/sh` (as bytes), `#!/bin/sh\\r`, tab variants, `#!\\t/bin/sh` (accepted: kernel skips tab), plus the existing cases; end-to-end spawn test with a planted directory named `\\f` in the workspace proving nothing runs; mutation: restore `.trim()` → test fails. Also drop `NODE_PATH` from the hook environment allowlist (`hook_runner.ts` hookEnvironment) with a test that it is absent when set in the parent. Rerun: every cli/test/hook*.test.ts and hooks_*.test.ts, content_trust, strict_json, doctor_hooks, security, security_gates, deletion_guard, approval_policy, managed_policy_enforcement, leak_guard, check_requirements, sandbox_confine; tsc; the complexity gate (exit code); check_invariants; check_doc_versions; changed files three times. Commit `fix(hooks): <what>` + `Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>`; push. Report under 150 words with the commit hash."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
