{"type":"data-flow-records","v":1,"sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","records":[{"response_id":"msg_011ChNgusdfG4qsmv24JJK4p","mark_sent_by":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b"}]}
{"parentUuid":"bbdec563-b3e8-4ce2-8c9d-ee9aa3b6b636","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNgusdfG4qsmv24JJK4p","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The third re-review of the HK-1 hooks fix (#805) came back request changes, with one blocker left. The review is posted on the PR, and the hooks builder is fixing it on the branch. #805 stays unmerged.\n\n**What's closed (run):**\n- The interpreter-location bypass, including `/proc/self/cwd/bash` and `PATH` entries that are `.`, empty or relative.\n- The 5,000-entry deletion cap; deleting a 20,000-file tree now takes 97 ms.\n- `/tmp/bash`.\n- A FIFO swapped in at the pin target.\n- The stale-directory sweep.\n- No allowed interpreter loaded workspace code at startup.\n\n**The remaining blocker:**\n- A script whose first line is `#!` followed by a form feed, carriage return or vertical tab, then `/bin/sh`, still runs an unpinned workspace file.\n- The check strips those characters, but the kernel treats them as part of the path, which resolves relative to the workspace. A hostile repository can ship a directory with that name.\n- The fix is to parse the shebang the way the kernel does, skipping only spaces and tabs, and to refuse any control character or non-ASCII byte in the line. A test will plant the hostile directory and confirm nothing runs.\n- The builder will also drop `NODE_PATH` from the hook environment.\n\nPA-3 completion and the BG-3 firer are still being built, and the BG-3 trust model (#803) is merged. Pending: #798 (HK-3). v1.3.0 is not landed. The merge to `main` and the release haven't started."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2819,"cache_read_input_tokens":408836,"output_tokens":528,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2819},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":528,"cache_read_input_tokens":408836,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2819,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2819,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011ChNgusRzZ6SeQWeZWwfXD","requestRef":"f0bb703b-7b35-4846-a095-52bca8e71c3a","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"5m","type":"assistant","uuid":"0b37b2a3-2069-49dc-b197-d49f9a92471c","timestamp":"2026-11-25T00:20:16.698Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"v1/bg3-trust-abuse-model","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
