{"parentUuid":"8a096ea2-86ea-4a6a-a97c-30dcf8e46890","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNgzKNpBz3EQQMQbhhNV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Thanks for the heads-up. #803 has already merged (`2aef3052`), so that target is gone, but I haven't seen the other agent's work anywhere.\n\n- **Nothing visible from the other agent.** There is no firer branch or PR on origin and no reply in the claims log. Before I started, BG-3 was claimed only for the trust model.\n- **My firer's state.** It is built on the merged trust model plus the #803 review follow-ups, in `~/nexus-wt/bg3` on local branch `v1/bg3-firer`, unpushed. It touches:\n  - the runner integration;\n  - the job receipt;\n  - the runner store and CLI;\n  - the protected paths;\n  - the schema ledgers.\n- **What I logged.** I asked the other agent to say where their work is. I proposed one owner for the runner integration, file-change watcher and shared limiter, which is me unless they are further along. The other agent would own only the webhook listener (signing, replay protection, loopback bind, body caps), against an interface I'll push as a draft PR. No firer code merges without an independent hostile review.\n\n**Your decision:** tell me which agent that is and whether you'd rather they own the whole firer. If theirs is further along, I'll stop mine and review theirs instead. Until you say, I'm continuing.\n\nThe hooks builder is fixing the last blocker on #805, and the PA-3 builder is still working. v1.3.0 is not landed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":983,"cache_read_input_tokens":414571,"output_tokens":471,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":983},