{"parentUuid":"834b7526-d623-4aa1-9538-34fa41d5f495","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNh3eT7t1soh8mKNo2m8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I looked at `~/nexus-wt/bg3-trust-abuse-model` read-only and changed nothing there. I'm continuing my firer, and I logged the reasoning in the claims log.\n\n**What the other agent has:**\n- **Base.** The worktree is on a detached head at `4dd93530c`, from before the trust-model fixes merged.\n- **Firer.** An uncommitted `trigger_firer.ts` (468 lines in one file) and `trigger_firer.test.ts` (272 lines). Together they cover the file watcher, the webhook listener and admission.\n- **Overlap.** It also edits `trigger_rate_limit.ts` and `triggers_cli.ts`, which duplicates the five review fixes already merged (`2aef3052`, then `26b6c1237`).\n\n**Why I'm keeping mine:**\n- **Execution path.** That firer starts \"a guarded autonomous turn\" through the application core in the calling process. The review, and your requirement that a fired trigger go through the same unattended job path as `nexus job` and schedules, call for the runner path. That means a fresh worktree, receipts that carry the trigger fields, and kill-and-resume.\n- **Mine.** It is split into watcher, webhook, state, paths and run modules. It integrates with the runner and updates the job and receipt schemas.\n- **Their webhook design.** I saw a hard-coded default port 8765 and a per-trigger secret read from an environment variable. Whether it signs with a timestamp and replay cache like the review requires, I didn't verify.\n\n**What I asked the other agent to do:**\n- Stop editing the rate-limiter and CLI files.\n- Move off the old base.\n- Review my firer when its draft PR appears, or take the webhook-listener hostile tests.\n\nIf you'd rather their firer be the base, say so and I'll stop mine and review theirs.\n\nStill running: my firer build, the PA-3 completion, and the HK-1 hooks fix for #805. v1.3.0 is not landed. The merge to `main` and the release haven't started."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":917,"cache_read_input_tokens":419727,"output_tokens":677,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":917},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":677,"cache_read_input_tokens":419727,"cache_creation_input_tokens":917,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":917,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011ChNh3eEyFuwSQwDJGTosS","requestRef":"ab60d6c8-209a-4f23-9d3e-fa955c865cec","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"5m","type":"assistant","uuid":"d09b188c-5c54-42a1-be01-bc8832d751de","timestamp":"2026-11-25T00:22:03.137Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"v1/bg3-trust-abuse-model","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
