mjs` that imports `./lib/h.mjs`, an approved `.js`/`.cjs` that `require`s a sibling, dynamic `import()`, `import.meta`-relative reads, `createRequire`, a bare package import resolving from workspace `node_modules` (when running from a private temp copy, what does module resolution find? could it now find workspace `node_modules` through a parent path or NODE_PATH? could the temp copy's location make `./x` resolve to something unexpected, e.g. the temp dir shared across plugins or writable by the workspace), and whether the CLAIM in the docs is honest: \"single self-contained file; imports of other workspace files fail\" vs \"absolute/dynamic loads are process-authority code the operator is approving\" (an approved plugin can `import(\"/abs/path/evil.mjs\")` or `fs`-read and `eval`: that is arbitrary code with the operator's rights by definition; the approval is of that plugin: judge the doc wording). Is the private temp copy directory 0700, outside the workspace, unreachable under `--sandbox`, cleaned up after, unique per load, and is a symlinked/swapped temp root refused? (c) the trust prompt: terminal-only, re-hash after the prompt, `--sha256`/`--yes`/env bypasses; the faked-terminal limit documented; protected-path coverage of the trust store (`extension_trust.json`, absolute `~/.config/nexus` patterns if present on your base) with workspace = HOME / `~/.config/nexus`; plugin file paths: symlinks, `..`, hard links, files > size caps, invalid UTF-8, BOM, `.ts`/`.mjs`/`.cjs`/`.js` variants, a plugin directory that is a symlink into the workspace; `NEXUS_TRUST_WORKSPACE=1` and workspace trust alone must not load workspace plugins; global/user plugins unaffected; managed policy (`plugins.allow`, `plugins.disable_workspace`) still refuses before any approval is read and an approval can never override a policy refusal. (d) A changed file asks again with a clear notice listing the reason; removal/revoke; two workspaces with the same bytes; the same plugin approved at one path and copied to another.\nAlso state what HK-3 still lacks to be called DONE against the plan (`docs/v1.3.0/PLAN.md` HK-3 row: \"decision D18; migration note for existing plugins\"; HK_PLAN §4.1: subprocess execution HK-3.2? doctor finding, migration notice for existing workspace plugins that now need approval, CLI tests, docs): list concretely which exist and which do not, run the migration scenario (an existing workspace plugin that used to load on workspace trust: what does the user see on first run after upgrade; is it silent breakage?).\nRun at head, one at a time: every plugin/trust test touched or added (`git diff --stat origin/release/v1.3.0...HEAD -- cli/test`), `plugin_trust`, `plugins*`, `workspace_trust`, `managed_policy_allowlists`, `content_trust`, `security`, `hooks_self_approval`, `leak_guard`, `check_requirements`, `doctor`; `cd cli && npx tsc --noEmit -p .`; the complexity gate (check the exit code); `node scripts/check_invariants.mjs`; `node scripts/check_doc_versions.mjs`. Mutations (copy aside, restore from the copy, never `git checkout`): import the workspace path instead of the verified copy; skip the hash comparison; import before the approval check; drop the terminal check; skip the re-hash after the prompt; each must fail a test.\nRules: do NOT edit ~/nexus-code or existing worktrees. `git -C ~/nexus-code fetch origin && git -C ~/nexus-code worktree add --detach ~/nexus-wt/rev798b <full sha>`; `cp -a ~/nexus-code/cli/node_modules ~/nexus-wt/rev798b/cli/`; `mkdir -p ~/nexus-wt/rev798b/core/target/release && cp ~/nexus-wt/ls1b/core/target/release/{harness-core,nexus-tui} ~/nexus-wt/rev798b/core/target/release/`. Tests: `cd ~/nexus-wt/rev798b/cli && TMPDIR=/dev/shm HOME=$(mktemp -d) node --import tsx --test test/<name>.test.ts 2>&1 | tail -20`. Never touch the real ~/.nexus, ~/.config/nexus, /etc/nexus. Stop processes by their own pid; never `pkill -f`. No commits, pushes or GitHub comments. Remove probes and the worktree at the end. Shell is zsh (`bash -c` for loops); prefix `rtk proxy` if output looks filtered; a safety check blocks scripts containing `rm`.\nReport under 500 words: verdict (ACCEPT / ACCEPT WITH FOLLOW-UPS / REQUEST CHANGES) at the exact SHA; my two blockers closed or not with the attack run; new findings with file:line, run-or-read, blocking or not (workspace plugin code running without that exact file's approval, the race still winnable, the agent approving for itself without the documented unsandboxed shell, or silent loss of existing plugins without a notice are blocking); the list of what HK-3 still needs to be DONE; test counts; mutation results; what you did not check."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2227,"cache_read_input_tokens":421341,"output_tokens":2813,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":165},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2227},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2813,"cache_read_input_tokens":421341,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2227,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2227,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":16848,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01HewaMLyLSoay5pz2jX8GMk":{"description":"Hostile re-review PR #798 HK-3","subagent_type":"reviewer","prompt":"Independent hostile RE-review of GitHub PR #798 (HK-3: per-plugin workspace trust) in ~/nexus-code, base `release/v1.3.0`. The owner has just put HK-3 FULLY in v1.3.0 (it was \"partial\"). Take the full head SHA from `gh pr view 798 --json headRefOid` (expected `605e3d5c…`), review exactly that, and say whether it moved or merged. My first review is th