{"parentUuid":"2b8ac678-5386-4b68-9ae5-470652aa0ed2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNhU7dAKj9XYN97Qdi7g","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015aUCwipC7KWFQuGqpLTtjJ","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Delta review PR #805 shebang parsing","subagent_type":"reviewer","prompt":"Short, time-boxed (about 20 minutes) independent delta review of GitHub PR #805 (HK-1 project-hook allowlist) in ~/nexus-code, base `release/v1.3.0`. Take the full head SHA from `gh pr view 805 --json headRefOid` (expected `1222ef16…`), review exactly that, and say whether it moved or merged. The previous review (PR comments, \"Independent re-review at `bdc6ad03…` — REQUEST CHANGES\") found a shebang bypass: `shebangProblem` used `.trim()`, which strips form feed, CR, VT and NBSP, but the Linux kernel skips only space and tab after `#!`, so `#!\\f/bin/sh` ran the workspace-relative path `\\f/bin/sh`. Fix commit `1222ef167` (`git show --stat`, diff): `shebangProblem` in `cli/src/core/hooks.ts` now parses like the kernel (only space/tab separate; one argument = rest of the line; any other control byte, 0x7f or byte above 0x7f refuses), `NODE_PATH` dropped from `hookEnvironment`.\nBy RUNNING (throwaway HOME, temp workspaces, no network, no inference): (1) Differential test of `shebangProblem` against the REAL kernel: generate files with first lines `#!` + every single byte 0x00-0xff in each position (before the interpreter, between interpreter and argument, inside the interpreter path, after the argument, trailing) plus combinations (tab/space mixes, two args, long lines up to 300 bytes (kernel BINPRM_BUF_SIZE is 256 on older kernels, 256 bytes: lines longer are truncated: what does the check do about a path that the kernel truncates into a DIFFERENT path: e.g. a 300-byte line whose first 255 bytes form a workspace-relative or other path), `#!/bin/sh` followed by newline vs EOF vs CRLF vs NUL; for each, put a decoy in the workspace (a directory named like the byte(s) containing `bin/sh` that prints MARK) and EXEC the private-copy-style file directly with cwd = the workspace (the way the hook runner does: read `cli/src/core/hooks.ts` for how it spawns) and compare: whenever the kernel would run anything outside the trusted-directory interpreter, `shebangProblem` must refuse. Report any accepted line where the kernel executes a path other than the absolute trusted interpreter named. (2) The interpreter in the shebang must satisfy `trustedProgram` (not /tmp, not a symlink into the workspace, not group-writable dir): try `#!/tmp/sh`, `#!/usr/bin/../../tmp/sh`, `#!//usr/bin/sh`, `#!/usr/bin/./sh`, `#!/usr//bin/sh` (kernel accepts these: does the check canonicalise and agree?), a trusted-dir symlink to elsewhere. (3) After an explicit interpreter (`[\"bash\",\"g.sh\"]`, `[\"perl\",\"g.pl\"]`, `[\"ruby\",\"g.rb\"]`) with a hostile `#!` line: kernel ignores it, but perl/ruby act on `#!` options (`-x`, `-i`, `-e`?): are they checked? run perl with `#!/usr/bin/perl -e ...`-like lines if perl is present. (4) `NODE_PATH` absent in the hook env (set it in the parent). (5) Regression: `hooks_examples` and the shipped `examples/hooks` still pass; ordinary shebangs `#!/bin/sh`, `#!/usr/bin/env`-less bash/python3/node/perl scripts approved.\nRun at head, one at a time: `hooks_cli`, `hooks_self_approval`, `hook_runner`, `hooks_examples`, `hooks_project_trust`, `hooks_gate_bypass`, `deletion_guard`, `leak_guard`, `check_requirements`, `security`, `sandbox_confine`; `cd cli && npx tsc --noEmit -p .`; the complexity gate (check the exit code). Mutations (copy aside, restore from the copy, never `git checkout`): restore `.trim()`; drop the non-ASCII refusal; drop the control-byte refusal; pass `NODE_PATH`: each must fail a test.\nRules: do NOT edit ~/nexus-code or existing worktrees. `git -C ~/nexus-code fetch origin && git -C ~/nexus-code worktree add --detach ~/nexus-wt/rev805c <full sha>`; `cp -a ~/nexus-code/cli/node_modules ~/nexus-wt/rev805c/cli/`; `mkdir -p ~/nexus-wt/rev805c/core/target/release && cp ~/nexus-wt/ls1b/core/target/release/{harness-core,nexus-tui} ~/nexus-wt/rev805c/core/target/release/`. Tests: `cd ~/nexus-wt/rev805c/cli && TMPDIR=/dev/shm HOME=$(mktemp -d) node --import tsx --test test/<name>.test.ts 2>&1 | tail -20`. Never touch the real ~/.nexus, ~/.config/nexus, /etc/nexus. Stop processes by their own pid; never `pkill -f`. No commits, pushes or GitHub comments. Remove probes and the worktree at the end. Shell is zsh (`bash -c` for loops); prefix `rtk proxy` if output looks filtered; a safety check blocks scripts containing `rm`.\nReport under 300 words: verdict (ACCEPT / ACCEPT WITH FOLLOW-UPS / REQUEST CHANGES) at the exact SHA; the bypass closed or not, with the differential result (number of lines tested, any accepted line where the kernel runs something else); findings with file:line, blocking or not; test counts; mutation results; what you did not check."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1432,"cache_read_input_tokens":426760,"output_tokens":2228,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":93},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1432},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":2228,"cache_read_input_tokens":426760,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1432,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1432,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":13244,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_015aUCwipC7KWFQuGqpLTtjJ":{"description":"Delta review PR #805 shebang parsing","subagent_type":"reviewer","prompt":"Shor