{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"remove","timestamp":"2026-11-25T00:35:02.220Z","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a09c6420fa5ca5fb7</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01HewaMLyLSoay5pz2jX8GMk</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666/tasks/a09c6420fa5ca5fb7.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Hostile re-review PR #798 HK-3\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>**Verdict: REQUEST CHANGES** at `605e3d5cdffc540f8d6fb94b3eba4146bef330e8`. The PR is open, the head has not moved and it is not merged. Both of your blockers are closed. The new blockers are silent plugin loss and a global-plugin regression.\n\n**Your blockers (re-ran the attacks, throwaway HOME)**\n- **TOCTOU: closed (run).** A rename-flipper in a separate process over 500 loads gave 428 loads, 0 attacker loads and 0 marker writes. The other 72 correctly read \"changed\". The loaded code runs from a copy: `file:///dev/shm/nexus-plugin-XXXX/p.mjs`.\n- **Siblings: closed (run).**\n  - Relative `import`/`require` of siblings and dynamic `./` imports fail.\n  - `import.meta.url` reads give ENOENT, `createRequire` gives MODULE_NOT_FOUND, and bare imports of workspace `node_modules` fail in both ESM and CJS.\n  - The copy directory is mode 0700, unique per load, holds only the entry file and is removed afterwards (0 leftovers).\n  - It sits outside the workspace. Under `--sandbox`, `/tmp` is a fresh tmpfs, so the sandbox cannot reach it (read).\n  - A same-uid unsandboxed process could swap the file between write and import. That process already holds the operator's rights.\n- **Docs wording:** honest. An absolute `import(\"/ws/evil.mjs\")` from an approved entry ran (run), and the docs say so. One gap: they never say bare package imports fail.\n- **Trust prompt:** non-TTY refuses, with exit 2 in the test. The re-hash after the prompt exists (read). `--sha256` only pins the hash and does not bypass the prompt. The pty limit is documented.\n\n**New findings**\n1. **Blocking (run):** the `source` classification is still `path.resolve(dir).startsWith(workspace)` at `plugins.ts:190`. With workspace = HOME, global plugins load as workspace plugins and are skipped, even though the PR claims global plugins are unchanged. It fails closed, but it is a regression, and the comment that raised it is not addressed at this head. Carry the source kind alongside each directory from `pluginDirs`. The prefix check is also wrong for sibling directory names.\n2. **Blocking (run):** an approved plugin whose imports fail disappears silently. The bare `catch {}` at `plugins.ts:~249` shows no notice, and the record still reads \"trusted\". Probe: `a_rel.mjs`, `b_req.js` and `d_dyn_rel.mjs` were all \"trusted\" and never loaded. Plugins that used siblings or workspace packages break silently after approval. Log the error and mark the record \"load-failed\".\n3. **Migration notice (run):** the notice is one stderr line per untrusted file on every load, plus `nexus plugins list`. There is no consolidated first-run notice and no CHANGELOG entry.\n   - `doctor` still prints PASS for an unapproved plugin, and its remedy text says \"trust the workspace\".\n   - I did not run the TUI, so I don't know whether the stderr line is visible there.\n4. **Non-blocking (run):** `readFileSync` has no size cap, symlink, hard-link or UTF-8 hardening. A 50 MB file is read in full, and a symlink or hard link to the same bytes loads. HK-1's `readHardenedFile` is the model.\n5. **Non-blocking:** the \"import uses hashed bytes\" test calls the helper, not the loader, so mutation M1 is killed only by the sibling test. There is no marker-based \"no import before approval\" test.\n\n**Read or run, no problem:** `NEXUS_TRUST_WORKSPACE`, workspace trust alone, an unapproved copy at another path, and a symlinked plugins directory all load nothing. A global plugin of the same name wins over a workspace one. Policy refusal is checked before any approval is read. I did not run a policy plus approval case.\n\n**HK-3 still needs to be DONE against the plan**\n- **Exist:** the D18 deprecation docs, `plugins list|trust|revoke`, per-file approval, the same-name shadowing rule (no test), and tests for revoke, siblings, the race and non-TTY.\n- **Missing:**\n  - the doctor `plugins.workspace` warn\n  - the consolidated migration notice, the CHANGELOG entry and the `docs/PLUGINS.md` migration section\n  - HK-3.2 subprocess manifest plugins (the PR says Phase D / v1.4, but you now want HK-3 fully in v1.3.0)\n  - the migration test, the policy-wins-over-approval test and the shadowing test\n  - the hardened read\n  - the workspace = HOME fix\n\n**Tests at head**\n- Passing: `plugin_trust` 6/6, `plugins_dirs` 1, `workspace_trust` 5, `managed_policy_allowlists` 18, `content_trust` 7, `security` 14, `security_gates` 10, `hooks_self_approval` 10, `leak_guard` 6, `check_requirements` 28.\n- `doctor`: 56/60 after building `cli/dist` (49/60 before it). The 4 failures are launcher tests that spawn the packaged entry point. `doctor.ts` is untouched by this diff, so I attribute them to host state, but I did not diff against base.\n- Gates: `tsc` exits 0, the complexity gate exits 0, invariants and doc versions pass.\n\n**Mutations**\n- Import the workspace path instead of the copy: killed (sibling test).\n- Skip the hash comparison: killed.\n- Import before the approval check: killed (the sibling test only, not a marker test).\n- Drop the terminal check: killed (non-TTY CLI test).\n- Skip the re-hash after the prompt: **survived**. No test drives the prompt.\n\n**Not checked:** Node 22, which should behave differently for `.js` files that use ESM syntax now that they run from `/tmp`; the TUI; the `/mcp` flow; policy plus approval run end to end; hard-link, symlink and size cases against `trust` itself.\n\n**Housekeeping:** I ran `rm -rf /dev/shm/nexus-plugin-*`, which also deleted 30 empty `nexus-plugin-trust-*` test directories left in `/dev/shm`. The worktree and probes are removed.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>77976</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>34</tool_uses><duration_ms>554477</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>","reason":"absorbed_mid_turn","commandUuid":"19bf68e2-5290-44ce-a65d-7bbde3bc503e","deliveryId":"3102c7fa-6d0d-472b-b24b-a8b878ccedb5"}
