 is also wrong for sibling directory names. Carry the source kind alongside each directory from `pluginDirs`.\n2. **An approved plugin whose imports fail disappears silently.** The bare `catch {}` at `plugins.ts:~249` shows no notice and the record still reads \"trusted\": `a_rel.mjs`, `b_req.js` and `d_dyn_rel.mjs` were \"trusted\" and never loaded. Plugins that used siblings or workspace packages break silently after approval. Log the error and mark the record \"load-failed\".\n3. **Migration:** the notice is one stderr line per untrusted file on every load plus `nexus plugins list`; there is no consolidated first-run notice and no CHANGELOG entry; `doctor` still prints PASS for an unapproved plugin and its remedy text says \"trust the workspace\". (TUI visibility not checked.)\n\n**Non-blocking:** `readFileSync` has no size cap, symlink, hard-link or UTF-8 hardening (50 MB read in full; a symlink or hard link to the same bytes loads): HK-1's `readHardenedFile` is the model. The \"import uses hashed bytes\" test calls the helper, not the loader, and there is no marker-based \"no import before approval\" test. Policy refusal is checked before any approval is read (a policy-plus-approval run end to end was not done).\n**What HK-3 still needs to be DONE** (the owner has put it fully in v1.3.0): the doctor `plugins.workspace` warning; a consolidated migration notice, a CHANGELOG entry and a `docs/PLUGINS.md` migration section; HK-3.2 subprocess manifest plugins (the PR defers them to v1.4); the migration test, the policy-wins-over-approval test and the same-name shadowing test; the hardened read; the workspace = HOME fix; the load-failed record.\n**Tests at that head:** `plugin_trust` 6, `plugins_dirs` 1, `workspace_trust` 5, `managed_policy_allowlists` 18, `content_trust` 7, `security` 14, `security_gates` 10, `hooks_self_approval` 10, `leak_guard` 6, `check_requirements` 28; `doctor` 56/60 after building `dist` (4 launcher failures, not attributed: `doctor.ts` untouched); `tsc`, complexity gate, invariants, doc versions pass. **Mutations:** workspace path instead of copy, skip hash comparison, import before approval, drop the terminal check: killed; skip the re-hash after the prompt: survived (no test drives the prompt). Not checked: Node 22 (`.js` files that use ESM syntax now run from `/tmp`), the TUI, `/mcp`.\nEOF\ngh pr comment 798 --body-file /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/rev798b.md | tail -1; d=\"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims\"; echo \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ) NOTE (claude-invariants-audit): #798 HK-3 was MERGED (06c003a6) while my hostile re-review at 605e3d5c (REQUEST CHANGES: global plugins skipped when workspace=HOME, approved plugin with failing imports disappears silently, no consolidated migration notice/doctor/CHANGELOG) was running; posted on the PR. HK-3 is fully in scope (owner): I am building the follow-up (those fixes + hardened read + doctor + migration docs + tests; HK-3.2 subprocess manifest plugins next) on v1/hk3-followups from ~/nexus-wt/hk3f, claim HK3_FOLLOWUPS. Please stop merging over unposted reviews: wait for the verdict.\" >> $d/nexus-claims.log; mkdir -p $d/HK3_FOLLOWUPS && printf '{\"agent\":\"claude-invariants-audit\",\"branch\":\"v1/hk3-followups\",\"since\":\"%s\",\"worktree\":\"/home/mike/nexus-wt/hk3f\",\"scope\":\"cli/src/plugins.ts, doctor plugin finding, plugin trust code, docs/PLUGINS.md, SKILLS_AND_PLUGINS.md, CHANGELOG, plugin tests\"}\\n' \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ)\" > $d/HK3_FOLLOWUPS/owner.json; git fetch -q origin; git worktree add -q -b v1/hk3-followups ~/nexus-wt/hk3f origin/release/v1.3.0 && ln -s ~/nexus-code/cli/node_modules ~/nexus-wt/hk3f/cli/node_modules && mkdir -p ~/nexus-wt/hk3f/core/target/release && cp ~/nexus-wt/ls1b/core/target/release/{harness-core,nexus-tui} ~/nexus-wt/hk3f/core/target/release/ && echo ready; sed -n '/HK-3/,/^## /p' ~/nexus-wt/_plans/HK_PLAN.md | head -70 | cut -c1-240","description":"Post the HK-3 review, log the out-of-order merge, claim the follow-up and create its worktree; read the HK-3 plan section"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3755,"cache_read_input_tokens":433334,"output_tokens":2895,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":327},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3755},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2895,"cache_read_input_tokens":433334,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3755,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3755,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":14281,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_0135dx2qeGL3vJATahrmSXAy":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-code && cat > /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/rev798b.md <<'EOF'\n**Independent hostile re-review at `605e3d5cdffc540f8d6fb94b3eba4146bef330e8` — REQUEST CHANGES. #798 merged (`06c003a6b`) while this review was running, so the blockers below are now on the release branch; the follow-up PR is being built.**\n\n**My two original blockers: closed (run).** TOCTOU: a rename-flipper in a separate process over 500 loads gave 428 loads, 0 attacker loads, 0 marker writes (the other 72 read \"changed\"); the loaded code runs from a copy (`file:///dev/shm/nexus-plugin-XXXX/p.mjs`). Siblings: relative `import`/`require`, dynamic `./` imports, `import.meta.url` reads, `createRequire` and bare imports of workspace `node_modules` all fail in ESM and CJS; the copy directory is 0700, unique per load, holds only the entry file, removed afterwards (0 leftovers); under `--sandbox` `/tmp` is a fresh tmpfs (read). A same-uid unsandboxed process could swap the file between write and import: it already has the operator's rights. Docs wording is honest (an absolute `import(\"/ws/evil.mjs\")` from an approved entry ran, and the docs say so); they should also say bare package imports fail. Trust prompt: non-TTY refuses (exit 2), `--sha256` only pins; the pty limit is documented.\n\n**New blocking findings (run)**\n1. **Global plugins regress when the workspace is HOME.** `plugins.ts:190` still classifies `source` by `path.resolve(dir).startsWith(workspace)`: with workspace = HOME, global plugins load as workspace plugins and are skipped, although the PR says global plugins are unchanged. It fails closed but it is a regression, and the prefix check is also wrong for sibling directory names. Carry the source kind alongside each directory from `pluginDirs`.\n2. **An approved plugin whose imports fail disappears silently.** The bare `catch {}` at `plugins.ts:~249` shows no notice and the record still reads \"trusted\": `a_rel.mjs`, `b_req.js` and `d_dyn_rel.mjs` were \"trusted\" and never loaded. Plugins that used siblings or workspace packages break silently after approval. Log the error and mark the record \"load-failed\".\n3. **Migration:** the notice is one stderr line per untrusted file on every load plus `nexus plugins list`; there is no consolidated first-run notice and no CHANGELOG entry; `doctor` still prints PASS for an unapproved plugin and its remedy text says \"trust the workspace\". (TUI visibility not checked.)\n\n**Non-blocking:** `readFileSync` has no size cap, symlink, hard-link or UTF-8 hardening (50 MB read in full; a symlink or hard link to the same bytes loads): HK-1's `readHardenedFile` is the model. The \"import uses hashed bytes\" test calls the helper, not the loader, and there is no marker-based \"no import before approval\" test. Policy refusal is checked before any approval is read (a policy-plus-approval run end to end was not done).\n**What HK-3 still needs to be DONE** (the owner has put it fully in v1.3.0): the doctor `plugins.workspace` warning; a consolidated migration notice, a CHANGELOG entry and a `docs/PLUGINS.md` migration section; HK-3.2 subprocess manifest plugins (the PR defers them to v1.4); the migration test, the policy-wins-over-approval test and the same-name shadowing test; the hardened read; the workspace = HOME fix; the load-failed record.\n**Tests at that head:** `plugin_trust` 6, `plugins_dirs` 1, `workspace_trust` 5, `managed_policy_allowlists` 18, `content_trust` 7, `security` 14, `security_gates` 10, `hooks_self_approval` 10, `leak_guard` 6, `check_requirements` 28; `doctor` 56/60 after building `dist` (4 launcher failures, not attributed: `doctor.ts` untouched); `tsc`, complexity gate, invariants, doc versions pass. **Mutations:** workspace path instead of copy, skip hash comparison, import before approval, drop the terminal check: killed; skip the re-hash after the prompt: survived (no test drives the prompt). Not checked: Node 22 (`.js` files that use ESM syntax now run from `/tmp`), the TUI, `/mcp`.\nEOF\ngh pr comment 798 --body-file /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/rev798b.md | tail -1; d=\"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims\"; echo \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ) NOTE (claude-invariants-audit): #798 HK-3 was MERGED (06c003a6) while my hostile re-review at 605e3d5c (REQUEST CHANGES: global plugins skipped when workspace=HOME, approved plugin with failing imports disappears silently, no consolidated migration notice/doctor/CHANGELOG) was running; posted on the PR. HK-3 is fully in scope (owner): I am building the follow-up (those fixes + hardened read + doctor + migration docs + tests; HK-3.2 subprocess manifest plugins next) on v1/hk3-followups from ~/nexus-wt/hk3f, claim HK3_FOLLOWUPS. Please stop merging over unposted reviews: wait for the verdict.\" >> $d/nexus-claims.log; mkdir -p $d/HK3_FOLLOWUPS && printf '{\"agent\":\"claude-invariants-audit\",\"branch\":\"v1/hk3-followups\",\"since\":\"%s\",\"worktree\":\"/home/mike/nexus-wt/hk3f\",\"scope\":\"cli/src/plugins.ts, doctor plugin finding, plugin trust code, docs/PLUGINS.md, SKILLS_AND_PLUGINS.md, CHANGELOG, plugin tests\"}\\n' \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ)\" > $d/HK3_FOLLOWUPS/owner.json; git fetch -q origin; git worktree add -q -b v1/hk3-followups ~/nexus-wt/hk3f origin/release/v1.3.0 && ln -s ~/nexus-code/cli/node_modules ~/nexus-wt/hk3f/cli/node_modules && mkdir -p ~/nexus-wt/hk3f/core/target/release && cp ~/nexus-wt/ls1b/core/target/release/{harness-core,nexus-tui} ~/nexus-wt/hk3f/core/target/release/ && echo ready; sed -n '/HK-3/,/^## /p' ~/nexus-wt/_plans/HK_PLAN.md | head -70 | cut -c1-240","description":"Post the HK-3 review, log the out-of-order merge, claim the follow-up and create its worktree; read the HK-3 plan section"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011ChNi3U9cjLQxBD2s8k6mg","requestRef":"8e3c28eb-0ade-4514-849a-b78a915973db","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"5m","type":"assistant","uuid":"2f65c294-2aa3-4412-9e2e-c13eedb5b647","timestamp":"2026-11-25T00:35:20.543Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"v1/bg3-trust-abuse-model","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
{"type":"pr-link","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","prNumber":798,"prUrl":"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/798","prRepository":"mikeholownych/nexus-code","timestamp":"2026-11-25T00:35:24.615Z"}
{"parentUuid":"2f65c294-2aa3-4412-9e2e-c13eedb5b647","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PreToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_0135dx2qeGL3vJATahrmSXAy","hookEvent":"PreToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"claude-mem hook claude-code file-context","durationMs":493},"type":"attachment","uuid":"98670db8-5090-4edc-9fdb-b99938186313","timestamp":"2026-11-25T00:35:21.097Z","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"v1/bg3-trust-abuse-model","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
{"parentUuid":"2f65c294-2aa3-4412-9e2e-c13eedb5b647","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6a32d5e1-7e35-4288-9eb0-1efa74e07e42","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0135dx2qeGL3vJATahrmSXAy","type":"tool_result","content":"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/798#issuecomment-7148669147\nready\n# HK-1 + HK-2 + HK-3 plan: command hooks, commit-pinned plugins, per-plugin trust (read-only planning pass)\n\nStatus: PLAN, 2026-11-24, written read-only against `origin/release/v1.3.0` at `4ae25a10` (snapshot extracted with `git archive`; nothing in the repo was edited), plus a read-only look at the uncommitted GV-5 work in `/home/mike/nexus-wt/gv\n\nAcceptance (verbatim):\n- **HK-1:** \"a hook that returns `allow` for a denied action has no effect; a changed project hook asks again; the contract is documented so existing hook scripts of that shape transfer\"\n- **HK-2:** \"installing a plugin whose declared permissions exceed the system policy is refused; `verify` detects a modified install; a skill whose trigger did not fire adds nothing to the request (request-shape snapshot)\"\n- **HK-3:** \"decision D18; migration note for existing plugins\"\n- **G-3 (hook and plugin rows):** \"a hostile … hook, plugin … cannot approve a denied action, raise a verdict, widen a policy tier, or remove a verification-file protection\"\n\nD18 default taken: **keep in-process workspace JS plugins, but move them to per-plugin trust with a deprecation note.**\n\n## 0. What exists (read, with citations)\n- **Managed policy for plugins and MCP** (GV-1 library): `PluginsPolicy {allow?: (\"sha256:<hex>\"|\"file:/abs\")[], disable_workspace?}` (`cli/src/core/managed_policy.ts:101-107`); `permitsPlugin(policy, {path, sha256, fromWorkspace})` (`:851-\n- **Trust.** Workspace trust = exact real path in `~/.config/nexus/trusted_workspaces.json` or `NEXUS_TRUST_WORKSPACE=1` (`workspace_trust.ts:41-81`); never in read-only mode. GV-1 has a hash-keyed approval store for the project policy (`re\n- **Skills.** Every discovered trusted skill is in the catalog of every request (`cli/src/skills.ts:498-503`) and may be named in a per-prompt note (`findSkills`, `:439`; `skillNoteFor`, `agent.ts:3933-3942`). `request_shape.test.ts` exists\n- **Flight recorder** has typed records, e.g. `recordMiddlewareRewrite` (`cli/src/flight.ts:318-330`); GV-3 hash-chains it.\n- **Doctor** plugin check `pluginCheck` (`cli/src/doctor.ts:1218-1241`), checks table (`:1254-1268`).\n- **No strict JSON reader.** `JSON.parse` keeps the last duplicate key; GV-1 avoided JSON for that reason (`managed_policy_toml.ts:16,289`).\n- **Readiness:** \"HK-1 / HK-2 | Open | No `docs/HOOKS.md`, no `nexus plugins install`\" (`docs/releases/v1.3.0-READINESS.md`).\n\n## 1. Shared machinery (designed once; the introducing slice is named)\n| Strict bounded JSON reader (duplicate keys, depth ≤ 8, size cap, unknown keys rejected by callers) + hardened file open (lstat, no symlink, O_NOFOLLOW, fstat recheck, owner = euid, no 0o022 bits), copied from `readOperatorConfigDocument\n| Process identity + tree kill by pid with start ticks (moved from `verify_service.ts:139-165`) | `cli/src/core/process_identity.ts` | HK-1.1 (or BG-1.1, whichever first) | hook runner, BG runner |\n| Content-hash approval store (`{version:1, entries:[{kind, scope, key, sha256, approvedAt, summary}]}`, `writePrivateFile` 0600, ≤ 256 KiB, unreadable or invalid store = **no approvals** plus a notice, never fail open) | `cli/src/core/co\n| Command hook runner (spawn, stdin JSON, timeout, scrubbed env, output caps, decision reduction where `allow` is ignored) | `cli/src/core/hook_runner.ts` | HK-1.1 | operator, project and plugin hooks (HK-2, HK-3) |\n| Hook registry and spine attachment (contextAdmission = pre-tool, evidenceEmission = post-tool) | `cli/src/core/hooks.ts` + `agent.ts` spine block | HK-1.2 | plugin hooks are just another source of declarations |\n| Verified installed-plugin store (manifest, tree digest, install receipts, memoised verification per process) | `cli/src/core/plugin_manifest.ts`, `cli/src/core/plugin_store.ts` | HK-2.1 | hooks, skills, MCP (HK-2.2/2.3), workspace manifes\n\n## 2. HK-1: declarative command hooks\n- **Plugin** declarations (HK-2) and **workspace manifest plugins** (HK-3.2) add sources later. Order of execution: operator → installed plugins → workspace manifest plugins → project. No source can remove or disable another's hooks (\n\n```jsonc\n{\n  \"version\": 1,\n  \"hooks\": {\n    \"pre-tool\": [\n      { \"name\": \"no-force-push\", \"tools\": [\"run_command\"], \"command\": \"~/bin/nexus-guard.sh\", \"timeout_secs\": 10 }\n    ],\n    \"post-tool\": [\n      { \"name\": \"audit\", \"tools\": [\"*\"], \"command\": [\"/usr/bin/logger\", \"-t\", \"nexus-hook\"], \"timeout_secs\": 5 }\n    ]\n  }\n}\n```\n\nRules: `name` `[A-Za-z0-9._-]{1,64}`, unique per file; `tools` = exact Nexus tool names or `[\"*\"]` (no regex: no ReDoS, no surprises), ≤ 64; `command` = string (run with `/bin/sh -c`, as peers do for configured hooks; `~/` expanded once) \n\n### 2.3 Wire contract (stdin / stdout / exit), Claude-Code-shaped so scripts transfer\n\nstdin, one JSON object, then EOF:\n\n```jsonc\n{\n  \"session_id\": \"<task id>\", \"cwd\": \"/abs/workspace\",\n  \"hook_event_name\": \"PreToolUse\" | \"PostToolUse\",   // peer names, so existing scripts match\n  \"nexus_event\": \"pre-tool\" | \"post-tool\",\n  \"permission_mode\": \"review\" | \"auto\" | \"read-only\",\n  \"tool_name\": \"run_command\",                       // Nexus names; docs map Bash→run_command, Write→write_file, Edit→edit_file, Read→read_file, …\n  \"tool_input\": { … arguments as the tool will receive them … },\n  \"tool_response\": { \"success\": true, \"output\": \"<≤ 32 KiB>\", \"error\": null }   // post-tool only\n}\n```\n\nstdout ≤ 64 KiB, stderr ≤ 8 KiB (excess → treated as a hook failure). Interpretation (`reduceHookOutput`, pure):\n\n| Hook result | pre-tool | post-tool |\n|---|---|---|\n| exit 0, empty stdout | no opinion | recorded |\n| exit 0, JSON with `decision: \"block\"\\|\"deny\"`, or `hookSpecificOutput.permissionDecision: \"deny\"`, or `continue: false` | **DENY** (`reason` / `permissionDecisionReason` / `stopReason`) | recorded, no effect |","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"4d6dcffd-8811-40dc-975a-cc690feb232e","timestamp":"2026-11-25T00:35:24.900Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/798#issuecomment-7148669147\nready\n# HK-1 + HK-2 + HK-3 plan: command hooks, commit-pinned plugins, per-plugin trust (read-only planning pass)\n\nStatus: PLAN, 2026-11-24, written read-only against `origin/release/v1.3.0` at `4ae25a10` (snapshot extracted with `git archive`; nothing in the repo was edited), plus a read-only look at the uncommitted GV-5 work in `/home/mike/nexus-wt/gv\n\nAcceptance (verbatim):\n- **HK-1:** \"a hook that returns `allow` for a denied action has no effect; a changed project hook asks again; the contract is documented so existing hook scripts of that shape transfer\"\n- **HK-2:** \"installing a plugin whose declared permissions exceed the system policy is refused; `verify` detects a modified install; a skill whose trigger did not fire adds nothing to the request (request-shape snapshot)\"\n- **HK-3:** \"decision D18; migration note for existing plugins\"\n- **G-3 (hook and plugin rows):** \"a hostile … hook, plugin … cannot approve a denied action, raise a verdict, widen a policy tier, or remove a verification-file protection\"\n\nD18 default taken: **keep in-process workspace JS plugins, but move them to per-plugin trust with a deprecation note.**\n\n## 0. What exists (read, with citations)\n- **Managed policy for plugins and MCP** (GV-1 library): `PluginsPolicy {allow?: (\"sha256:<hex>\"|\"file:/abs\")[], disable_workspace?}` (`cli/src/core/managed_policy.ts:101-107`); `permitsPlugin(policy, {path, sha256, fromWorkspace})` (`:851-\n- **Trust.** Workspace trust = exact real path in `~/.config/nexus/trusted_workspaces.json` or `NEXUS_TRUST_WORKSPACE=1` (`workspace_trust.ts:41-81`); never in read-only mode. GV-1 has a hash-keyed approval store for the project policy (`re\n- **Skills.** Every discovered trusted skill is in the catalog of every request (`cli/src/skills.ts:498-503`) and may be named in a per-prompt note (`findSkills`, `:439`; `skillNoteFor`, `agent.ts:3933-3942`). `request_shape.test.ts` exists\n- **Flight recorder** has typed records, e.g. `recordMiddlewareRewrite` (`cli/src/flight.ts:318-330`); GV-3 hash-chains it.\n- **Doctor** plugin check `pluginCheck` (`cli/src/doctor.ts:1218-1241`), checks table (`:1254-1268`).\n- **No strict JSON reader.** `JSON.parse` keeps the last duplicate key; GV-1 avoided JSON for that reason (`managed_policy_toml.ts:16,289`).\n- **Readiness:** \"HK-1 / HK-2 | Open | No `docs/HOOKS.md`, no `nexus plugins install`\" (`docs/releases/v1.3.0-READINESS.md`).\n\n## 1. Shared machinery (designed once; the introducing slice is named)\n| Strict bounded JSON reader (duplicate keys, depth ≤ 8, size cap, unknown keys rejected by callers) + hardened file open (lstat, no symlink, O_NOFOLLOW, fstat recheck, owner = euid, no 0o022 bits), copied from `readOperatorConfigDocument\n| Process identity + tree kill by pid with start ticks (moved from `verify_service.ts:139-165`) | `cli/src/core/process_identity.ts` | HK-1.1 (or BG-1.1, whichever first) | hook runner, BG runner |\n| Content-hash approval store (`{version:1, entries:[{kind, scope, key, sha256, approvedAt, summary}]}`, `writePrivateFile` 0600, ≤ 256 KiB, unreadable or invalid store = **no approvals** plus a notice, never fail open) | `cli/src/core/co\n| Command hook runner (spawn, stdin JSON, timeout, scrubbed env, output caps, decision reduction where `allow` is ignored) | `cli/src/core/hook_runner.ts` | HK-1.1 | operator, project and plugin hooks (HK-2, HK-3) |\n| Hook registry and spine attachment (contextAdmission = pre-tool, evidenceEmission = post-tool) | `cli/src/core/hooks.ts` + `agent.ts` spine block | HK-1.2 | plugin hooks are just another source of declarations |\n| Verified installed-plugin store (manifest, tree digest, install receipts, memoised verification per process) | `cli/src/core/plugin_manifest.ts`, `cli/src/core/plugin_store.ts` | HK-2.1 | hooks, skills, MCP (HK-2.2/2.3), workspace manifes\n\n## 2. HK-1: declarative command hooks\n- **Plugin** declarations (HK-2) and **workspace manifest plugins** (HK-3.2) add sources later. Order of execution: operator → installed plugins → workspace manifest plugins → project. No source can remove or disable another's hooks (\n\n```jsonc\n{\n  \"version\": 1,\n  \"hooks\": {\n    \"pre-tool\": [\n      { \"name\": \"no-force-push\", \"tools\": [\"run_command\"], \"command\": \"~/bin/nexus-guard.sh\", \"timeout_secs\": 10 }\n    ],\n    \"post-tool\": [\n      { \"name\": \"audit\", \"tools\": [\"*\"], \"command\": [\"/usr/bin/logger\", \"-t\", \"nexus-hook\"], \"timeout_secs\": 5 }\n    ]\n  }\n}\n```\n\nRules: `name` `[A-Za-z0-9._-]{1,64}`, unique per file; `tools` = exact Nexus tool names or `[\"*\"]` (no regex: no ReDoS, no surprises), ≤ 64; `command` = string (run with `/bin/sh -c`, as peers do for configured hooks; `~/` expanded once) \n\n### 2.3 Wire contract (stdin / stdout / exit), Claude-Code-shaped so scripts transfer\n\nstdin, one JSON object, then EOF:\n\n```jsonc\n{\n  \"session_id\": \"<task id>\", \"cwd\": \"/abs/workspace\",\n  \"hook_event_name\": \"PreToolUse\" | \"PostToolUse\",   // peer names, so existing scripts match\n  \"nexus_event\": \"pre-tool\" | \"post-tool\",\n  \"permission_mode\": \"review\" | \"auto\" | \"read-only\",\n  \"tool_name\": \"run_command\",                       // Nexus names; docs map Bash→run_command, Write→write_file, Edit→edit_file, Read→read_file, …\n  \"tool_input\": { … arguments as the tool will receive them … },\n  \"tool_response\": { \"success\": true, \"output\": \"<≤ 32 KiB>\", \"error\": null }   // post-tool only\n}\n```\n\nstdout ≤ 64 KiB, stderr ≤ 8 KiB (excess → treated as a hook failure). Interpretation (`reduceHookOutput`, pure):\n\n| Hook result | pre-tool | post-tool |\n|---|---|---|\n| exit 0, empty stdout | no opinion | recorded |\n| exit 0, JSON with `decision: \"block\"\\|\"deny\"`, or `hookSpecificOutput.permissionDecision: \"deny\"`, or `continue: false` | **DENY** (`reason` / `permissionDecisionReason` / `stopReason`) | recorded, no effect |","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"gitOperation":{"pr":{"number":798,"url":"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/798","action":"commented"}}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"2f65c294-2aa3-4412-9e2e-c13eedb5b647","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"v1/bg3-trust-abuse-model","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
