{"parentUuid":"4d6dcffd-8811-40dc-975a-cc690feb232e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNi59ymum91SpBtg5Jut","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Fcqx7DecSuRA5dSSL55R1d","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"sed -n '/^## 4/,/^## 5/p' ~/nexus-wt/_plans/HK_PLAN.md | head -60 | cut -c1-300","description":"Read the HK-3 section of the plan for the follow-up scope"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5531,"cache_read_input_tokens":437089,"output_tokens":143,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5531},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":143,"cache_read_input_tokens":437089,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5531,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5531,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":606,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Fcqx7DecSuRA5dSSL55R1d":{"command":"sed -n '/^## 4/,/^## 5/p' ~/nexus-wt/_plans/HK_PLAN.md | head -60 | cut -c1-300","description":"Read the HK-3 section of the plan for the follow-up scope"}},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011ChNi59mdDDTywJmZ7zRb7","requestRef":"d5159ff8-7e08-49ca-bcc0-5a127faebf63","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"5m","type":"assistant","uuid":"d754fdaf-220a-4f84-b2ec-716e2bae4b4e","timestamp":"2026-11-25T00:35:26.997Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"v1/bg3-trust-abuse-model","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
{"parentUuid":"d754fdaf-220a-4f84-b2ec-716e2bae4b4e","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PreToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_01Fcqx7DecSuRA5dSSL55R1d","hookEvent":"PreToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"claude-mem hook claude-code file-context","durationMs":396},"type":"attachment","uuid":"986a1eac-7e6d-44d7-8234-427edeabfbcd","timestamp":"2026-11-25T00:35:27.438Z","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"v1/bg3-trust-abuse-model","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
{"parentUuid":"d754fdaf-220a-4f84-b2ec-716e2bae4b4e","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6a32d5e1-7e35-4288-9eb0-1efa74e07e42","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Fcqx7DecSuRA5dSSL55R1d","type":"tool_result","content":"## 4. HK-3: per-plugin trust (D18: keep in-process JS, per-plugin trust, deprecation note)\n\n### 4.1 Design\n\n- **Workspace JS plugins** (`<ws>/.nexus/plugins/*.js|mjs`, `<ws>/plugins/*.js|mjs`): loaded only when **that file's** bytes are approved in `extension_trust.json` (kind `workspace-js`, scope = workspace real path, key = relative path, sha256). Workspace trust (`nexus trust`) alone no longer loads t\n- **User-level JS plugins** (`~/.nexus/plugins`, `~/.config/nexus/plugins`): operator-placed, unchanged apart from GV-5's allowlist and HK-2's error reporting.\n- **Commands** in `plugins_cli.ts`: `nexus plugins trust <file|dir> [-w] [--sha256 <hex>]` (TTY asks after showing path + hash + size; non-TTY needs `--sha256`), `nexus plugins untrust <file|dir> [-w]`; `nexus plugins list` shows `approved | not_approved | changed` per workspace plugin.\n- **Workspace manifest plugins (HK-3.2, the subprocess path):** `<ws>/.nexus/plugins/<name>/nexus-plugin.json` with **hooks and skills only** (no MCP: `.mcp.json` already covers workspace servers), approved per plugin by its tree digest (kind `workspace-manifest`); hooks run as subprocesses through \n- **Migration (no automatic approval):** after upgrading, a trusted workspace's JS plugins stop loading until approved; the first session prints one notice listing them with the exact `nexus plugins trust` commands; doctor shows a warn finding. `docs/PLUGINS.md` \"Migrating workspace plugins\" maps `p\n\n### 4.2 Security analysis (HK-3)\n\nA cloned repository can no longer get code executed in-process merely because the operator once trusted the directory for MCP or skills; each file needs its own approval and a change asks again. The hostile cases: a repo that adds a new `.js` to an already trusted workspace (not loaded), modifies an\n\n### 4.3 Files, tests, slices (HK-3)\n\nFiles: `cli/src/plugins.ts`, `cli/src/plugins_cli.ts`, `cli/src/core/content_trust.ts` (kinds), `cli/src/core/plugin_store.ts` (workspace manifest variant), `cli/src/core/hooks.ts` (workspace manifest source), **`cli/src/doctor.ts`** (`plugins.workspace` finding), `docs/PLUGINS.md`, `CHANGELOG.md`.\n\nTests: `plugin_trust_workspace.test.ts` (unapproved not imported in a trusted workspace; approved imported; one byte changed → not imported + notice; untrust; read-only; `plugins.disable_workspace` wins over an approval; repo-shipped trust file ignored; name shadowing), `plugin_trust_migration.tes\n\nSlices:\n1. **HK-3.1 Per-file trust for workspace JS (M).** `plugins.ts`, `plugins_cli.ts` trust/untrust, migration notice, doctor (**hot: `doctor.ts`**), docs + deprecation note.\n2. **HK-3.2 Workspace manifest plugins as subprocess hooks (S/M, may roll to v1.4 with Phase D).** `plugin_store.ts` + `hooks.ts` sources, tests.\n\n## Decisions taken (defaults; no user questions asked)\n\n- Hook events in v1.3.0: `pre-tool` and `post-tool` only. Attachment through the spine's unused `contextAdmission` and `evidenceEmission` stages: zero edits to complexity-baselined functions.\n- Hook outputs: deny or annotate only. `allow`/`approve` ignored and recorded; `ask` = deny; `updatedInput` ignored (argument tightening deferred).\n- Fail closed for pre-tool: any failure, timeout, oversize or malformed JSON denies. Invalid operator hooks file denies every call (no startup refusal); invalid or unapproved project file is not run.\n- Claude-Code event names in `hook_event_name` (plus `nexus_event`) so existing scripts transfer; Nexus tool names in `tool_name` with a mapping table in the docs; `CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR` set alongside `NEXUS_PROJECT_DIR`.\n- Project hooks and workspace plugins approved per file/tree by SHA-256 in one store `~/.config/nexus/extension_trust.json`; approval is independent of workspace trust; non-TTY approvals pin the hash with `--sha256`, never `--yes`.\n- Hooks run unsandboxed with the MCP environment scrubber; sequential; default timeout 10 s, max 60 s.\n- Manifest plugins contribute hooks, triggered skills and MCP servers only; no in-process code, custom tools or verifiers. Contributions are the declared permissions.\n- Git installs require a full commit id; no checkout (ls-tree + cat-file); own tree-digest format; `plugins.allow = [\"sha256:<tree digest>\"]` admits an install.\n- Skill triggers: `prompt_keywords` only (no file globs) in v1.3.0.\n- D18: keep in-process JS plugins; workspace ones need per-file approval; deprecation note; no automatic migration approval.\n- `strict_json.ts`, `process_identity.ts` and `content_trust.ts` are introduced by HK-1.1 and shared with BG/HK-2/HK-3.\n\n## Out of scope for v1.3.0\n\nEvents `pre-verify`, `post-verify`, `permission-request`, `session-start`, `session-end`, `stop`, `pre-compact`; http/prompt/subagent hook handlers; argument rewriting by hooks; managed-policy keys for hooks (`hooks.disable_project`, system-tier hooks); hooks for `serve-mcp`; plugin verifiers, custo\n\n## Reference coding\n\nXERJ node active but holds only `opencode` (flagged \"not verified complete\"), `awesome-ai-system-prompts`, `serverless-workflow-spec`; Gemini CLI, goose, Cline and Codex are not indexed, so their parts come from the source reading recorded in `docs/v1.3.0/PLAN.md:19-21` (2026-11-13/14/23). Query run\n\n## Risks\n\n- **Approval-then-deny UX** (hooks run after the interactive prompt) may surprise; documented, revisited with MT-2's router.\n- **Fail-closed hooks can stop work** (a slow or broken operator hook denies everything); doctor and `nexus hooks test` make it diagnosable; operator-chosen.\n- **`agent.ts`, `index.ts`, `doctor.ts`, `plugins.ts`, `mcp.ts` are claimed or being edited** (agent.ts/index.ts/doctor.ts live claims; plugins.ts/mcp.ts by GV-5): HK-1.2, HK-1.3, HK-2.1/2.2/2.3 must rebase on those PRs; the HK-1.2 `agent.ts` change is two lines in the spine block.\n- **Migration friction** for workspace JS plugins (they stop loading until approved); deliberate, one clear notice.\n- **Git fetch-by-id** support varies by host; the fallback fetches all refs (slower, still verified by id and digest).\n- **Unsandboxed hooks** run with user authority; mitigated only by trust and the scrubbed env.\n- **TOCTOU** between hashing a workspace JS file and importing it; documented residual.\n\n## Open questions that could not be settled from the code\n\n- Whether `ExecutionReceipt` reaches any published schema through a path not checked here (it is absent from every `docs/protocol/*.schema.json` today); if a later unit publishes it, the new `hooks` member needs a ledger note.\n- GV-5's final API for `PluginManager` and `mcp.ts` (read from an uncommitted worktree); HK-2/HK-3 follow whatever merges.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"7e02951f-fad8-4d2b-8df6-e9da5eb5a18f","timestamp":"2026-11-25T00:35:27.679Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"## 4. HK-3: per-plugin trust (D18: keep in-process JS, per-plugin trust, deprecation note)\n\n### 4.1 Design\n\n- **Workspace JS plugins** (`<ws>/.nexus/plugins/*.js|mjs`, `<ws>/plugins/*.js|mjs`): loaded only when **that file's** bytes are approved in `extension_trust.json` (kind `workspace-js`, scope = workspace real path, key = relative path, sha256). Workspace trust (`nexus trust`) alone no longer loads t\n- **User-level JS plugins** (`~/.nexus/plugins`, `~/.config/nexus/plugins`): operator-placed, unchanged apart from GV-5's allowlist and HK-2's error reporting.\n- **Commands** in `plugins_cli.ts`: `nexus plugins trust <file|dir> [-w] [--sha256 <hex>]` (TTY asks after showing path + hash + size; non-TTY needs `--sha256`), `nexus plugins untrust <file|dir> [-w]`; `nexus plugins list` shows `approved | not_approved | changed` per workspace plugin.\n- **Workspace manifest plugins (HK-3.2, the subprocess path):** `<ws>/.nexus/plugins/<name>/nexus-plugin.json` with **hooks and skills only** (no MCP: `.mcp.json` already covers workspace servers), approved per plugin by its tree digest (kind `workspace-manifest`); hooks run as subprocesses through \n- **Migration (no automatic approval):** after upgrading, a trusted workspace's JS plugins stop loading until approved; the first session prints one notice listing them with the exact `nexus plugins trust` commands; doctor shows a warn finding. `docs/PLUGINS.md` \"Migrating workspace plugins\" maps `p\n\n### 4.2 Security analysis (HK-3)\n\nA cloned repository can no longer get code executed in-process merely because the operator once trusted the directory for MCP or skills; each file needs its own approval and a change asks again. The hostile cases: a repo that adds a new `.js` to an already trusted workspace (not loaded), modifies an\n\n### 4.3 Files, tests, slices (HK-3)\n\nFiles: `cli/src/plugins.ts`, `cli/src/plugins_cli.ts`, `cli/src/core/content_trust.ts` (kinds), `cli/src/core/plugin_store.ts` (workspace manifest variant), `cli/src/core/hooks.ts` (workspace manifest source), **`cli/src/doctor.ts`** (`plugins.workspace` finding), `docs/PLUGINS.md`, `CHANGELOG.md`.\n\nTests: `plugin_trust_workspace.test.ts` (unapproved not imported in a trusted workspace; approved imported; one byte changed → not imported + notice; untrust; read-only; `plugins.disable_workspace` wins over an approval; repo-shipped trust file ignored; name shadowing), `plugin_trust_migration.tes\n\nSlices:\n1. **HK-3.1 Per-file trust for workspace JS (M).** `plugins.ts`, `plugins_cli.ts` trust/untrust, migration notice, doctor (**hot: `doctor.ts`**), docs + deprecation note.\n2. **HK-3.2 Workspace manifest plugins as subprocess hooks (S/M, may roll to v1.4 with Phase D).** `plugin_store.ts` + `hooks.ts` sources, tests.\n\n## Decisions taken (defaults; no user questions asked)\n\n- Hook events in v1.3.0: `pre-tool` and `post-tool` only. Attachment through the spine's unused