{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","hash":"2a5956e3adc39613d6c7fdfb62518f3fd3c208fa8e1172c7498ea8c1ffb3df2e","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CPQdCgh1sCipKLPizxE4eS","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"a317b41792fa50650","summary":"Build HK-3 follow-ups: fixes, migration, manifest plugins","message":"New task, after your #805 work: HK-3 completion. Worktree /home/mike/nexus-wt/hk3f (branch `v1/hk3-followups`, from origin/release/v1.3.0 tip 06c003a6, which contains merged PR #798 = HK-3 slice 1 \"partial\" by another author). The owner has put HK-3 FULLY into v1.3.0. My hostile re-review of #798 (it merged while I reviewed) is the last comment on `gh pr view 798 --comments` (\"Independent hostile re-review at 605e3d5c…\"); read it and `/home/mike/nexus-wt/_plans/HK_PLAN.md` section 4 (HK-3.1 and HK-3.2), `docs/SKILLS_AND_PLUGINS.md`, `cli/src/plugins.ts`, `plugins_cli.ts`, `core/content_trust.ts`, `core/plugin_store.ts`/`plugin_manifest.ts` (HK-2, merged #796), `core/hooks.ts` (your HK-1 final code: hook sources, verified-copy execution, trusted-program logic, `readHardenedFile`), `doctor.ts`, `docs/v1.3.0/PLAN.md` HK-3 row, AGENTS.md. Same working rules as before (throwaway HOME, TMPDIR=/dev/shm, leak guard, kill by pid, mutations from a copy restored from it, never `git checkout`, complexity gate untouched, `git fetch origin` and merge origin/release/v1.3.0 often, never rebase). Local commits, then push with a plain `git push origin v1/hk3-followups` (never force) when green; I open the PR. Do these in order, each as its own commit(s):\nA (blocking findings from my review): (1) `plugins.ts:~190` classify plugin `source` (workspace vs global/user) by carrying the source kind alongside each directory from `pluginDirs`, NOT by `startsWith(workspace)`; with workspace = HOME the global plugin dirs must still load as global; sibling-prefix directory names must not misclassify; tests incl. workspace = HOME and `/ws` vs `/ws2`. (2) an approved plugin whose import FAILS must not vanish silently: catch, record the error (message, redacted, capped), print one clear notice per plugin on stderr/TUI notice path used by other plugin notices, mark the trust record/list status `load-failed` (distinct from `trusted`), show the reason in `nexus plugins list` and doctor; test with plugins that import siblings, `require` a workspace package, use `import.meta.url` file reads, throw at top level. (3) hardened read: reuse `readHardenedFile`/strict reader from HK-1 for the plugin file (size cap e.g. 1 MiB, regular file only, no symlink/hardlink trick, UTF-8 valid, no BOM issues), also used by `plugins trust` hashing; tests for 50 MB file, symlink, hard link, FIFO, invalid UTF-8. (4) the test that the loader imports the VERIFIED copy and not the workspace path must drive the real loader (marker-based: the plugin writes its own `import.meta.url`/stack to a marker file proving it ran from the private copy), plus a marker-based \"no import before approval\" test, plus a test that drives the trust prompt so skipping the re-hash after the prompt fails a test (inject the prompt answer function; bytes change during the question → refused).\nB (migration, per plan 4.1): a consolidated first-session notice listing the workspace JS plugins that are not approved (once per session, with the exact `nexus plugins trust <file>` commands, capped list), doctor finding `plugins.workspace` (warn for unapproved/changed/load-failed workspace plugins; remedy text must say per-file `nexus plugins trust`, NOT \"trust the workspace\"; PASS only when none pending), CHANGELOG Unreleased entry with the behaviour change for the release notes, `docs/PLUGINS.md` \"Migrating workspace plugins\" (create it if absent: how the old behaviour mapped, what silently stops loading, how to approve, that sibling imports and workspace `node_modules` imports no longer work, that bare package imports fail, that absolute/dynamic loads inside an approved entry are the operator's responsibility), tests: migration (plugin that loaded before upgrade = not loaded, notice, doctor warn), policy wins over approval end to end (`plugins.disable_workspace` and `plugins.allow` with an approval present: refused), same-name shadowing (a workspace plugin named like a global one: global wins, notice), repo-shipped trust file ignored.\nC (HK-3.2, workspace manifest plugins): implement per plan 4.1: `<ws>/.nexus/plugins/<name>/nexus-plugin.json` contributing HOOKS and SKILLS only (no MCP, no in-process code, no custom tools/verifiers), approved per plugin by TREE DIGEST (kind `workspace-manifest`, reuse the HK-2 manifest/tree-digest code and the extension trust store), hooks from such plugins run as subprocesses through the SAME hook runner and the SAME project-hook allowlist rules (planProjectCommand: pinned workspace file or listed interpreter + pinned script, verified-copy execution, shebang rules) because they are workspace-controlled; a change of any file in the tree asks again (hash all files of the tree listed in the manifest; refuse unlisted files or symlinks inside the tree); terminal-only approval via `nexus plugins trust <dir>` (same approval path and same documented unsandboxed limit); order of hook sources per plan (operator → installed plugins → workspace manifest plugins → project); no source can remove or disable another source's hooks; workspace-trust gate and managed policy (`plugins.disable_workspace` disables them too; a policy refusal beats an approval). Skills contributed only through the triggered-skill rules of HK-2 (a skill whose trigger did not fire adds nothing to the request: the request-shape snapshot test must still pass). Docs in `docs/PLUGINS.md`, CHANGELOG, doctor finding extended. Tests: unapproved not run; approved runs; one byte changed anywhere in the tree → not run + notice; unlisted file in tree; symlink in tree; hook command outside allowlist refused with the rule; policy beats approval; read-only mode; `nexus plugins list` shows state; hostile: manifest naming a hook `command` that points outside the tree, plugin hooks cannot allow a denied action (reuse `hooks_gate_bypass` shape for a manifest source). Mutations for each guard.\nRun, one at a time: every plugin/trust/hook test (`ls cli/test | grep -iE 'plugin|hook|trust|doctor|request_shape|skill'`), `security`, `managed_policy_allowlists`, `leak_guard`, `check_requirements`; `tsc --noEmit`; the complexity gate (check the exit code); `check_invariants`; `check_doc_versions`; schema `--check` generators if you touch a schema (extension trust record additions are additive with a ledger note). Changed/new test files three times. Commit `feat(plugins): …`/`fix(plugins): …` + `Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>`. Report under 400 words per milestone: after A+B (push, I will start the review), then after C."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
