{"parentUuid":"8d02ca36-061e-4dfd-b733-62624332fbce","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNi7CPwFwuYGNs56kZT8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2729,"cache_read_input_tokens":445557,"output_tokens":1952,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":74},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2729},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1952,"cache_read_input_tokens":445557,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2729,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2729,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":576,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011ChNi7CDXEwkktw3W7dFUa","requestRef":"46682e5f-fe42-40a3-9d4e-e47ecd17baae","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"5m","type":"assistant","uuid":"49e33dc8-c69b-4ed0-afa1-235131668a8e","timestamp":"2026-11-25T00:35:54.462Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"v1/bg3-trust-abuse-model","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
{"parentUuid":"49e33dc8-c69b-4ed0-afa1-235131668a8e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNi7CPwFwuYGNs56kZT8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012RieBPGsa44G3CUsUQn2Cq","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-code && cat > /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/pr_pa3.md <<'EOF'\nCompletes PA-3 (goal semantics), whose deferral the owner revoked. An independent verification at tip `b6cb12d7` found \"a model 'I am done' does not complete a goal\" met and \"a stale goal resumes paused with a visible reason\" only partly met: the stale check failed OPEN for a recycled pid, another host, a pid with no host, and a state with only the current boot id (a plain drive then executed the unit with no operator action).\n\n## What changes\n\n- **Driver identity fails closed** (`core/driver_identity.ts`, `goal.ts`, `operation_runner.ts`). The goal records {pid, host, start ticks, boot id}. A goal counts as driven only when all four are present and match a live process of this host; otherwise it pauses with one of: process gone, pid recycled, other host, other boot, identity unknown. Drive, `/goal` status and list, `nexus operation status` and `--dag` share one verdict (`operation status` no longer shows RUNNING for a killed goal); `/goal status` while another process drives reports \"Driven by pid N\" instead of throwing `OperationLockedError`. `activeStartTicks` is an optional additive field (state schema v7 unchanged, note in `operation_schema.ts`); records from the previous build read as unknown identity and pause once.\n- **Goal state is a protected path** (`security.ts`, absolute `defaultTaskStateDir()`): the file tools and the advisory command check refuse it. Docs state plainly that an unsandboxed command runs with the operator's rights and can rewrite goal state, caps, stall counts and driver identity; integrity is file mode 0600, there is no signature.\n- **Receipt gate test**: a goal with a model-marked-done unit and no verifier receipt cannot report COMPLETE; deleting the gate now fails a test.\n- **Fingerprints** are computed over the redacted reason on both sides, so a secret-shaped failure repeated 3 times stalls as `NOT_CONVERGING`.\n- **Token cap**: `nexus operation budget <id> --max-total-tokens N|none` (`core/operation_budget.ts`) takes the driver lock, journals `OPERATION_BUDGET_CHANGED` (who, when, old, new), applies from the next dispatch, does not resume a paused goal. Overshoot bound is one dispatched batch, not exact (documented). No marker exists for an agent-spawned process, so the command cannot refuse an agent that shells out; it is an operator command.\n- **Docs and labels**: `PA3_GOAL_LIFECYCLE.md`, `PA3_ACCEPTANCE.md`, `PLAN.md`, CHANGELOG corrected; \"[experimental]\" removed from `/team` and `nexus operation` now that PA-1/PA-2 are recorded landed; `/team` and `/goal` section in the manual; the stale reason text fixed and both pause and stale reasons are shown.\n\n## Behaviour changes for the release notes\n\nA fresh plan with no identity and no started units may still start (`loop.ts` relies on it); a goal at an operator decision (BLOCKED) stays BLOCKED (before, `/goal` showed PAUSED while drive never paused it); off Linux an interrupted goal always pauses (identity comes from `/proc`).\n\n## Tests\n\n`goal_driver_identity` (recycled pid, other host, pid without host, boot-id-only, hand-edited ledger, live driver stays RUNNING and cannot be double-driven, kill -9 then restart pauses, reboot pauses), `goal_pa3_completion` (receipt gate, fingerprint, protected path, budget audit). Mutations each fail a test (host, ticks, boot requirements, recycled-pid check, other-host/boot checks, derived read view, lock-error surfacing, unsupported platform accepted, receipt gate, redacted fingerprint, protected path, cap journal). `goal_lifecycle`, `goal_ledger_propagation`, `durable_continuity`, `fault_kill_mid_tool_call`, all `operation_*`, `security`, `leak_guard`, `check_requirements`, `tsc`, complexity gate, invariants and doc versions pass locally on Node 24 (not Node 22; CI runs both). Independent review requested before merge.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\nEOF\nu=$(gh pr create --base release/v1.3.0 --head v1/pa3-completion --title \"fix(goal): PA-3 fail-closed driver identity, audited token cap, protected goal state\" --body-file /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/pr_pa3.md | tail -1); echo \"$u\"; echo \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ) PR (claude-invariants-audit): $u PA-3 completion; independent review next; DO NOT MERGE until posted.\" >> \"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log\"","description":"Open the PA-3 completion PR and log it"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2729,"cache_read_input_tokens":445557,"output_tokens":1952,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":74},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2729},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1952,"cache_read_input_tokens":445557,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2729,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2729,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":11094,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_012RieBPGsa44G3CUsUQn2Cq":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-code && cat > /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/pr_pa3.md <<'EOF'\nCompletes PA-3 (goal semantics), whose deferral the owner revoked. An independent verification at tip `b6cb12d7` found \"a model 'I am done' does not complete a goal\" met and \"a stale goal resumes paused with a visible reason\" only partly met: the stale check failed OPEN for a recycled pid, another host, a pid with no host, and a state with only the current boot id (a plain drive then executed the unit with no operator action).\n\n## What changes\n\n- **Driver identity fails closed** (`core/driver_identity.ts`, `goal.ts`, `operation_runner.ts`). The goal records {pid, host, start ticks, boot id}. A goal counts as driven only when all four are present and match a live process of this host; otherwise it pauses with one of: process gone, pid recycled, other host, other boot, identity unknown. Drive, `/goal` status and list, `nexus operation status` and `--dag` share one verdict (`operation status` no longer shows RUNNING for a killed goal); `/goal status` while another process drives reports \"Driven by pid N\" instead of throwing `OperationLockedError`. `activeStartTicks` is an optional additive field (state schema v7 unchanged, note in `operation_schema.ts`); records from the previous build read as unknown identity and pause once.\n- **Goal state is a protected path** (`security.ts`, absolute `defaultTaskStateDir()`): the file tools and the advisory command check refuse it. Docs state plainly that an unsandboxed command runs with the operator's rights and can rewrite goal state, caps, stall counts and driver identity; integrity is file mode 0600, there is no signature.\n- **Receipt gate test**: a goal with a model-marked-done unit and no verifier receipt cannot report COMPLETE; deleting the gate now fails a test.\n- **Fingerprints** are computed over the redacted reason on both sides, so a secret-shaped failure repeated 3 times stalls as `NOT_CONVERGING`.\n- **Token cap**: `nexus operation budget <id> --max-total-tokens N|none` (`core/operation_budget.ts`) takes the driver lock, journals `OPERATION_BUDGET_CHANGED` (who, when, old, new), applies from the next dispatch, does not resume a paused goal. Overshoot bound is one dispatched batch, not exact (documented). No marker exists for an agent-spawned process, so the command cannot refuse an agent that shells out; it is an operator command.\n- **Docs and labels**: `PA3_GOAL_LIFECYCLE.md`, `PA3_ACCEPTANCE.md`, `PLAN.md`, CHANGELOG corrected; \"[experimental]\" removed from `/team` and `nexus operation` now that PA-1/PA-2 are recorded landed; `/team` and `/goal` section in the manual; the stale reason text fixed and both pause and stale reasons are shown.\n\n## Behaviour changes for the release notes\n\nA fresh plan with no identity and no started units may still start (`loop.ts` relies on it); a goal at an operator decision (BLOCKED) stays BLOCKED (before, `/goal` showed PAUSED while drive never paused it); off Linux an interrupted goal always pauses (identity comes from `/proc`).\n\n## Tests\n\n`goal_driver_identity` (recycled pid, other host, pid without host, boot-id-only, hand-edited ledger, live driver stays RUNNING and cannot be double-driven, kill -9 then restart pauses, reboot pauses), `goal_pa3_completion` (receipt gate, fingerprint, protected path, budget audit). Mutations each fail a test (host, ticks, boot requirements, recycled-pid check, other-host/boot checks, derived read view, lock-error surfacing, unsupported platform accepted, receipt gate, redacted fingerprint, protected path, cap journal). `goal_lifecycle`, `goal_ledger_propagation`, `durable_continuity`, `fault_kill_mid_tool_call`, all `operation_*`, `security`, `leak_guard`, `check_requirements`, `tsc`, complexity gate, invariants and doc versions pass locally on Node 24 (not Node 22; CI runs both). Independent review requested before merge.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\nEOF\nu=$(gh pr create --base release/v1.3.0 --head v1/pa3-completion --title \"fix(goal): PA-3 fail-closed driver identity, audited token cap, protected goal state\" --body-file /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/pr_pa3.md | tail -1); echo \"$u\"; echo \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ) PR (claude-invariants-audit): $u PA-3 completion; independent review next; DO NOT MERGE until posted.\" >> \"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log\"","description":"Open the PA-3 completion PR and log it"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011ChNi7CDXEwkktw3W7dFUa","requestRef":"46682e5f-fe42-40a3-9d4e-e47ecd17baae","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"5m","type":"assistant","uuid":"121ecea6-aac5-44ff-91ba-fc5cbaf78e9c","timestamp":"2026-11-25T00:36:05.580Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"v1/bg3-trust-abuse-model","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
