{"parentUuid":"ad8cfa30-f14f-4a6f-ace8-7c7548b7fa51","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNi8RFsNGt9MCApwf8dp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XATo7WZNeK9uuUL6todrtv","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Hostile review PR #806 PA-3","subagent_type":"reviewer","prompt":"Independent hostile review of GitHub PR #806 (PA-3 goal semantics completion) in ~/nexus-code, base `release/v1.3.0`. Take the full head SHA from `gh pr view 806 --json headRefOid` (expected `a8a8c64e…` or later), review exactly that, and say whether it moved or merged. Background: an independent verification at tip `b6cb12d7` (agent report, summarised in the PR body) found the stale-goal clause only partly met: the stale check failed open for a recycled pid, another host, a pid with no host, and boot-id-only state, so a plain `driveOperation` executed the unit with no operator action; goal state under `~/.nexus/tasks` was tamperable by an unsandboxed command; the verifier-receipt completion gate had no test; a secret-shaped failure reason never stalled (redacted vs fresh fingerprint mismatch); the docs promised a cap-raising mechanism that did not exist; `nexus operation status` showed RUNNING for a killed goal. This PR fixes these (read the PR body; commits `34fdb604a`, `2da38b8fa`, `1f756a54e`, merge `a8a8c64ed`; `cli/src/core/driver_identity.ts`, `goal.ts`, `operation_runner.ts`, `operation_cli.ts`, `core/operation_budget.ts`, `scheduler.ts`, `security.ts`, docs `docs/v1.3.0/PA3_*.md`). Acceptance: \"stale goal resumes paused with a visible reason; a model 'I am done' does not complete a goal\".\nTry to break it by RUNNING (throwaway HOME, temp workspaces, scripted gateway `cli/test/helpers/fixtures.ts`, no network, no live inference):\n1. Stale detection, every seeded state through BOTH the read path (`nexus operation status`, `--dag`, `/goal status`, `/goal list`) and a plain `driveOperation`/`nexus operation resume`: recycled pid (pid alive with a different start time: spawn a process, record its pid with wrong ticks), same pid and ticks (live driver: must stay RUNNING and a second driver must be refused), other host, pid missing, host missing, ticks missing, boot id missing/other/current-only, malformed values (strings for numbers, negative, huge, NaN, floats, `__proto__`, arrays), future timestamps, a pid of a zombie or of a thread id, pid 0/1/-1, a state written by the previous build (no ticks), identity fields present but the process on a different PID namespace (containers: /proc/<pid> exists but is another process: document), a driver that exits between the identity check and the dispatch (race: can a unit execute for a goal whose identity check failed? try with the test seams), two operators resuming concurrently. The model's reach: can model text/tool calls change identity fields, un-pause, or resume (file tools on `defaultTaskStateDir()` incl. `..`/symlinks/case/hard links, workspace = HOME/`~/.nexus`; slash commands typed by the model; `run_command` unsandboxed vs `--sandbox`: state plainly what an unsandboxed command can do; the new `nexus operation budget` command: can it be run through `run_command` in review mode (needs approval) and sandboxed (state dir masked?)).\n2. \"I am done\" never completes: scripted models that claim completion in prose, call `task_completed`, mark requirements verified, write forged receipts into every plausible location (workspace, `.nexus`, task state dir), replay a receipt from another goal/unit, edit the ledger through file tools. Confirm the receipt gate mutation now fails a test.\n3. Budget: `nexus operation budget <id> --max-total-tokens N|none`: lock taken, journal event (who/when/old/new), applies next dispatch, does not resume a paused goal, rejects junk (negative, NaN, 1e30, strings, float), a running driver in another process (lock contention: clear error), concurrent units overshoot bound documented honestly. Can the cap be raised by anything model-controlled (env var read at plan time; `NEXUS_OPERATION_MAX_TOTAL_TOKENS` in a workspace `.env`/config.env loaded by workspace trust?).\n4. Fingerprints: secret-shaped reasons stall after 3; different reasons do not; fingerprints persisted and compared on the same redacted form; do fingerprints or the pause reason leak secrets into status/receipts/flight; reset actions (revise/replace/assign/set_inputs/lift) cannot be triggered by model input.\n5. Labels and docs: `/team` and `nexus operation` no longer say experimental; verify every claim in `PA3_GOAL_LIFECYCLE.md`, `PA3_ACCEPTANCE.md`, the manual `/team` and `/goal` section, and CHANGELOG against the code (false claims = findings). Behaviour changes listed in the PR body (fresh plan with no identity may start; BLOCKED stays BLOCKED; off-Linux always pauses): verify, and say whether \"fresh plan with no identity may start\" can be abused (a state file with all identity fields deleted and no started units: does that start work? is that a bypass of a pause?).\nRun at head, one at a time: `goal_driver_identity`, `goal_pa3_completion`, `goal_lifecycle`, `goal_ledger_propagation`, `durable_continuity`, `fault_kill_mid_tool_call`, every `operation_*` test (`ls cli/test | grep operation`), `security`, slash tests, `leak_guard`, `check_requirements`, `protocol_schema`; `cd cli && npx tsc --noEmit -p .`; the complexity gate (check the exit code; `driveOperation` must not have grown); `node scripts/check_invariants.mjs`; `node scripts/check_doc_versions.mjs`. Mutations (copy aside, restore from the copy, never `git checkout`): drop the host requirement; drop the ticks requirement; drop the recycled-pid check; make read path ignore identity; drop the protected path; drop the receipt gate; revert the redacted fingerprint; drop the budget journal write: each must fail a test.\nRules: do NOT edit ~/nexus-code or existing worktrees. `git -C ~/nexus-code fetch origin && git -C ~/nexus-code worktree add --detach ~/nexus-wt/rev806 <full sha>`; `cp -a ~/nexus-code/cli/node_modules ~/nexus-wt/rev806/cli/`; `mkdir -p ~/nexus-wt/rev806/core/target/release && cp ~/nexus-wt/ls1b/core/target/release/{harness-core,nexus-tui} ~/nexus-wt/rev806/core/target/release/`. Tests: `cd ~/nexus-wt/rev806/cli && TMPDIR=/dev/shm HOME=$(mktemp -d) node --import tsx --test test/<name>.test.ts 2>&1 | tail -20`. Never touch the real ~/.nexus, ~/.config/nexus, /etc/nexus. Stop processes by their own pid; never `pkill -f`; do not delete files outside your own temp dirs. No commits, pushes or GitHub comments. Remove probes and the worktree at the end. Shell is zsh (`bash -c` for loops); prefix `rtk proxy` if output looks filtered; a safety check blocks scripts containing `rm`.\nReport under 500 words: verdict (ACCEPT / ACCEPT WITH FOLLOW-UPS / REQUEST CHANGES) at the exact SHA; each acceptance clause MET/NOT MET with the run that shows it; each earlier finding closed or not; new findings with file:line, run-or-read, blocking or not (a goal that resumes running or executes a unit when its driver identity is unproven, completes without a verifier receipt, or can be un-paused, reset or budget-raised by model-controlled input without the documented unsandboxed shell, is blocking); test counts; mutation results; what you did not check."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2011,"cache_read_input_tokens":448286,"output_tokens":2848,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2011},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2848,"cache_read_input_tokens":448286,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2011,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2011,"ephemeral_1h_input_tok