{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-11-25T00:36:34.922Z","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a0287b52f3a6989b3</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_015aUCwipC7KWFQuGqpLTtjJ</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666/tasks/a0287b52f3a6989b3.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Delta review PR #805 shebang parsing\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>**Verdict: ACCEPT** at `1222ef167b47a6c3fbbb5da693db3ada235fb121`. The PR is open and the head has not moved. I did not check whether `release/v1.3.0` moved after I fetched it.\n\n**Bypass closed: yes.**\n- **Differential, kernel 6.8:** I tested 6611 first-line variants by executing each file directly with cwd set to the workspace.\n  - The variants put every byte 0x00–0xff in each of 21 positions, plus 144 two-byte combinations of space-like bytes (0x00, 0x09, 0x0b, 0x0c, 0x0d, 0x1c–0x1f, 0x20, 0x85, 0xa0), and lines of 240–300 bytes, including ones near the 256-byte truncation point.\n  - They also cover CRLF, NUL, EOF and bare-newline endings, and decoy `&lt;bytes&gt;/bin/sh` directories that print MARK.\n  - `shebangProblem` accepted 677. MARK never printed, and I found no accepted line where the kernel ran anything other than the named absolute interpreter.\n  - Seven accepted lines produced no \"OK\" output. All are harmless: a script body error, an empty body, the interpreters' own behaviour with my test body, and `#!/bin/sh/` (ENOTDIR).\n  - The check refuses 430 lines the kernel would run fine. That is the safe direction.\n  - The 256-byte case is handled: any line with its newline past index 256 is refused.\n- **Interpreter path:**\n  - `/tmp/sh`, `/usr/bin/../../tmp/sh`, a symlink into the workspace, and a symlink in a non-trusted directory are refused.\n  - `//usr/bin/sh`, `/usr/bin/./sh` and `/usr//bin/sh` are accepted, and the kernel runs them the same way.\n- **Perl:**\n  - With an explicit `perl g.pl`, the lines `#!/usr/bin/perl -e …`, `-x`, `-i.bak` and `-Mstrict` are refused. Perl itself rejects `-e`, `-x` and `-M` (\"Can't emulate\" / \"Too late\"), and `-i` is refused by the check.\n  - `-w` and `-T` are accepted, which is intended.\n  - Ruby is not installed, so I did not run it.\n- **`NODE_PATH`:** `hook_runner.ts:59` deletes it from the hook environment. Mutation M4 below covers it.\n\n**Findings (all non-blocking):**\n- `hooks.ts:~430`: `path.basename` ignores a trailing slash, so `#!/bin/sh/` is accepted. The kernel fails it with ENOTDIR, so nothing runs. Optionally refuse any program path that ends in `/`.\n- I did not run the hook runner's own spawn path in the differential. I used a direct exec with cwd set to the workspace, as the runner does.\n\n**Tests:** all pass at head.\n\n| Test | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `hooks_cli` | 16/16 |\n| `hooks_self_approval` | 19/19 |\n| `hook_runner` | 8/8 |\n| `hooks_examples` | 6/6 |\n| `hooks_project_trust` | 10/10 |\n| `hooks_gate_bypass` | 11/11 |\n| `deletion_guard` | 3/3 |\n| `leak_guard` | 6/6 |\n| `check_requirements` | 28/28 |\n| `security` | 14/14 |\n| `sandbox_confine` | 19/19 |\n\n`tsc --noEmit` is clean and the complexity gate exited 0.\n\n**Mutations:** each failed at least one test.\n\n| Mutation | Tests that failed |\n|---|---|\n| M1: restore `.trim()` | `hooks_cli`, `hooks_self_approval` |\n| M2: drop the non-ASCII refusal | `hooks_cli` |\n| M3: drop the control-byte refusal | `hooks_cli`, `hooks_self_approval` |\n| M4: pass `NODE_PATH` | `hook_runner` |\n\nFiles were restored from copies and the worktree is clean.\n\n**Not checked:** ruby, kernels other than 6.8, and a differential through the hook runner itself.\n\n**Cleanup:** I removed the worktree. I left probe files in `/dev/shm` (`dw-TgkrCg`, `t2-SzEc8g`, `t2lnk`, `o-*.txt`, `hooks.orig*`, `hr.orig`, `cx.*`) because the safety check blocks `rm`.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>42261</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>11</tool_uses><duration_ms>528025</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
