{"parentUuid":"a5fd14dd-2644-4d61-898f-af00dda8e9f1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNiA4Mpqpdcd5rw6TGNf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"PA-3's completion is open as #806 and an independent hostile review is running. #806 stays unmerged until the verdict is posted. HK-3 (#798) merged while my review of it was in flight, so its defects are now on the release branch and I'm building a follow-up.\n\n**HK-3 (#798, merged as `06c003a6b` before my review finished):**\n- **Closed:** both of my original blockers. The race over 500 loads never ran attacker bytes, and sibling and workspace-package imports fail by construction.\n- **Blocking, now on the release branch:**\n  - With the workspace set to home, global plugins are skipped as if they were workspace plugins.\n  - An approved plugin whose imports fail disappears silently, and its record still says \"trusted\".\n  - There is no consolidated migration notice, and `doctor` still passes with unapproved plugins and tells the user to trust the whole workspace.\n- **Still missing:** the doctor warning, the changelog and migration docs, the hardened file read, and the subprocess-manifest part (HK-3.2). Since you put HK-3 fully in scope, that part comes now.\n- I posted the review on #798 and logged the out-of-order merge. The HK-1 builder is doing the follow-up in two stages: the fixes and migration first, then HK-3.2. The first stage gets its own review before merge.\n\n**#805 (HK-1 hooks):** release moved on; a narrow review of the final shebang fix, tested against the real kernel, is still running.\n\n**PA-3 builder's report** (#806): both acceptance clauses now met locally. Driver identity fails closed on a recycled pid, another host or a missing field. The read path agrees with the drive path. Goal state is a protected path. The token cap can be changed through an audited `nexus operation budget` command. The `/team` experimental label is lifted.\n\n**BG-3 firer:** my build is still running. v1.3.0 is not landed. The merge to `main` and the release haven't started."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3229,"cache_read_input_tokens":450297,"output_tokens":645,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3229},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":645,"cache_read_input_tokens":450297,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3229,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3229,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011ChNiA48S7c9JSew7hhKT3","requestRef":"adf6b462-8873-43d6-9fad-8099b586f503","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"5m","type":"assistant","uuid":"9bf9bab9-806d-4fda-b384-e18ca6eba909","timestamp":"2026-11-25T00:36:36.981Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"v1/bg3-trust-abuse-model","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
