er path:**\n  - `/tmp/sh`, `/usr/bin/../../tmp/sh`, a symlink into the workspace, and a symlink in a non-trusted directory are refused.\n  - `//usr/bin/sh`, `/usr/bin/./sh` and `/usr//bin/sh` are accepted, and the kernel runs them the same way.\n- **Perl:**\n  - With an explicit `perl g.pl`, the lines `#!/usr/bin/perl -e …`, `-x`, `-i.bak` and `-Mstrict` are refused. Perl itself rejects `-e`, `-x` and `-M` (\"Can't emulate\" / \"Too late\"), and `-i` is refused by the check.\n  - `-w` and `-T` are accepted, which is intended.\n  - Ruby is not installed, so I did not run it.\n- **`NODE_PATH`:** `hook_runner.ts:59` deletes it from the hook environment. Mutation M4 below covers it.\n\n**Findings (all non-blocking):**\n- `hooks.ts:~430`: `path.basename` ignores a trailing slash, so `#!/bin/sh/` is accepted. The kernel fails it with ENOTDIR, so nothing runs. Optionally refuse any program path that ends in `/`.\n- I did not run the hook runner's own spawn path in the differential. I used a direct exec with cwd set to the workspace, as the runner does.\n\n**Tests:** all pass at head.\n\n| Test | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `hooks_cli` | 16/16 |\n| `hooks_self_approval` | 19/19 |\n| `hook_runner` | 8/8 |\n| `hooks_examples` | 6/6 |\n| `hooks_project_trust` | 10/10 |\n| `hooks_gate_bypass` | 11/11 |\n| `deletion_guard` | 3/3 |\n| `leak_guard` | 6/6 |\n| `check_requirements` | 28/28 |\n| `security` | 14/14 |\n| `sandbox_confine` | 19/19 |\n\n`tsc --noEmit` is clean and the complexity gate exited 0.\n\n**Mutations:** each failed at least one test.\n\n| Mutation | Tests that failed |\n|---|---|\n| M1: restore `.trim()` | `hooks_cli`, `hooks_self_approval` |\n| M2: drop the non-ASCII refusal | `hooks_cli` |\n| M3: drop the control-byte refusal | `hooks_cli`, `hooks_self_approval` |\n| M4: pass `NODE_PATH` | `hook_runner` |\n\nFiles were restored from copies and the worktree is clean.\n\n**Not checked:** ruby, kernels other than 6.8, and a differential through the hook runner itself.\n\n**Cleanup:** I removed the worktree. I left probe files in `/dev/shm` (`dw-TgkrCg`, `t2-SzEc8g`, `t2lnk`, `o-*.txt`, `hooks.orig*`, `hr.orig`, `cx.*`) because the safety check blocks `rm`.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>42261</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>11</tool_uses><duration_ms>528025</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"},"uuid":"3d2811d4-8986-484f-ac7b-f286fd8477bc","timestamp":"2026-11-25T00:36:46.816Z","permissionMode":"bypassPermissions","origin":{"kind":"task-notification","producer":"session-task","runId":"0mwvdwwuv-4a7a2308"},"promptSource":"system","turnOrigin":"task_notification","turnPromptId":"134fa427-871a-49ef-b5ad-6bb85ad668de","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":46,"turnIndex":309},"queueSkipAttachments":true,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"v1/bg3-trust-abuse-model","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
