{"parentUuid":"72530909-de64-433b-b57f-cbd21439e70d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNiaoDCwmZWc3yxpkJrT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The HK-1 pinning fix (#805) is merged into `release/v1.3.0` as `758116aa`. The fourth review accepted it. Required checks were green at the exact head, release CI was green at the tip first, and I read the merged state back. I haven't yet confirmed release CI on the new merge commit.\n\nThe reviewer ran 6,611 first-line variants against the real kernel (every byte value in each position, plus truncation near 256 bytes). No accepted line made the kernel run anything but the named trusted interpreter. The earlier bypasses are closed: the allowlist, the verified-copy execution, the interpreter location and the shebang whitespace trick. One non-blocking item remains: `#!/bin/sh/` is accepted, but the kernel fails it. The HK-1 pinning review chain took four rounds and each found a real bypass.\n\n**Still running:**\n- **BG-3 firer:** the builder is in its mutation matrix and hasn't pushed.\n- **PA-3 (#806):** the hostile review.\n- **HK-3 follow-up:** the first stage covers the plugin fixes and migration. The subprocess-manifest part comes after.\n\nv1.3.0 is not landed. The merge to `main` and the release haven't started. After these, the readiness re-measure, version bump, changelog, release notes and the smoke workflows on the final tip are still to do."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":425743,"cache_read_input_tokens":32782,"output_tokens":451,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":425743,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":451,"cache_read_input_tokens":32782,"cache_creation_input_tokens":425743,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":425743},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011ChNianghoCLPLdykBzGXw","requestRef":"5e80faf6-aabc-4301-a6ef-6ecc7b92d045","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"2e0ca725-f422-4cb1-b217-f6b1721c84a8","timestamp":"2026-11-25T00:42:11.199Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"v1/bg3-trust-abuse-model","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
