{"parentUuid":"e95444fb-2800-45f8-b0a3-7e0f5055bbf4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNjKZ9ZPyRrvy3J6btL8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018ttZkAaT5yVe3x5B3mYMMs","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"a6379c334af41ccf9","summary":"Fix PA-3 review findings B1 and S1-S6","message":"PA-3 review of #806 (your branch v1/pa3-completion, worktree /home/mike/nexus-wt/pa3f, head a8a8c64e) is REQUEST CHANGES: read the PR comment `gh pr view 806 --comments` (last one). `git fetch origin && git status`, merge origin/release/v1.3.0 (moved: HK-1 and others merged), never rebase; plain `git push origin v1/pa3-completion` at the end (the PR already exists), never force. Fix, each with a test that fails without it (mutate a copy and restore from it; never `git checkout`):\nB1 (blocking, confirmed by running): with the workspace = $HOME (or containing it) `--sandbox` (bwrap) does not hide `~/.nexus/tasks`: `wrapSandboxedCommand(..., {mode:\"bwrap\"})` rewrote `$HOME/.nexus/tasks/g.json` on the host because `.nexus` is not in `HOME_DENIED` in cli/src/sandbox.ts. Mask the REAL task-state directory (`defaultTaskStateDir()` resolved with realpath; honour NEXUS_STATE_DIR) in both bwrap branches the way PF-3's `hideDirectoryFromSandbox`/`hideDirectories` does for the socket directory (it is on the release branch: reuse it, do not duplicate), also for the sandboxed worker launch; test with workspace = HOME and workspace elsewhere (a sandboxed command must neither read nor write the task dir; if bwrap is unavailable follow how `sandbox_confine.test.ts` skips); update the docs (PA3_GOAL_LIFECYCLE.md Integrity, manual) to say exactly what holds.\nS1: `nexus operation watch` (operation_cli.ts ~613) and `--replay` show RUNNING for a killed driver: apply the same derived-pause view as status/`--dag`. Test.\nS2: a zombie driver (state Z in /proc/<pid>/stat) reads ALIVE in both `processStartTicks` and the lock's `processAlive`: treat Z (and X) as gone. Test with a real zombie (spawn a child whose parent does not reap).\nS3: a state naming a live pid that holds no lock runs the whole plan under a second driver (baseline probe executed 5 units): refuse to drive when the recorded driver identity is ALIVE and is not this process (clear error naming pid), even when the lock file is absent. Test.\nS4: protected path must also cover `realpathSync(defaultTaskStateDir())` (symlinked HOME: the real-path spelling was allowed) and the file tools' hard-link case: a hard link inside the workspace to a state file must be refused for write/edit/delete (check nlink > 1 on protected targets' siblings? Simplest: refuse writes through any path whose realpath/inode equals a protected file's: compare dev+ino of the target with the protected files in the state dir; implement in the shared protected-path check without a heavy scan; if too invasive, document and test only the symlinked-HOME part and say so). Test.\nS5: fix the PR description claim: the advisory command check does NOT refuse the state dir (only the file tools do; `--sandbox` blocks shell writes). Edit the PR body with `gh pr edit 806 --body-file` after reading the current body (`gh pr view 806 --json body`) and correcting only that sentence + adding the HOME-workspace sandbox fix; also make sure docs/CHANGELOG say the same.\nS6: correct the job_worker.ts:~154 comment (the stale pause is overridden by `prepare` for unattended resumes; say so) and look at loop.ts:~469: does an unattended resume of a PAUSED goal still require the operator's explicit action? If the pause is overridden unattended for a goal whose driver identity is unproven, make the unattended path respect the stale pause for goals (fail closed) unless it is the operator-submitted job itself; if that is a larger change, document the exact behaviour and open a GitHub issue (`gh issue create`) describing it, and say which you did.\nRe-run: goal_driver_identity, goal_pa3_completion, goal_lifecycle, goal_ledger_propagation, durable_continuity, fault_kill_mid_tool_call, every operation_* test, sandbox_confine, sandbox_profiles, security, slash_router, slash_resume_other, leak_guard, check_requirements, protocol_schema, the runner/job tests (`ls cli/test | grep -iE 'runner|job|schedule|trigger'` since a job-worker comment/behaviour may change); tsc; complexity gate (exit code); check_invariants; check_doc_versions. Changed/new test files three times. Commit `fix(goal): <what>` + `Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>`; push. Report under 250 words with commit hash, and what you chose for S4 and S6.","type":"message","recipient":"a6379c334af41ccf9","recipient_kind":"agent","content":"PA-3 review of #806 (your branch v1/pa3-completio…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3251,"cache_read_input_tokens":461541,"output_tokens":4102,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":112},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3251,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":4102,"cache_read_input_tokens":461541,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3251,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3251},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":12056,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_018ttZkAaT5yVe3x5B3mYMMs":{"to":"a6379c334af41ccf9","summary":"Fix PA-3 review findings B1 and S1-S6","message":"PA-3 review of #806 (your branch v1/pa3-completion, worktree /home/mike/nexus-wt/pa3f, head a8a8c64e) is REQUEST CHANGES: read the PR comment `gh pr view 806 --comments` (last one). `git fetch origin && git status`, merge origin/