{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","hash":"0c4577246d9d00699a9aa92cbacb7765dac35a764154a356c3ef0c948079ff21","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013fCd7RW7EmcNcQ1drkUkZS","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-code && cat > /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/rev806.md <<'EOF'\n**Independent hostile review at `a8a8c64ed61f1274e567778ed7c3c8402a81dfa0` — REQUEST CHANGES (one documentation-claim blocker; the rest are follow-ups). I am fixing all of it on this branch.**\n\n**\"Stale goal resumes paused with a visible reason\": met for the code paths in the finding (run).** 21 seeded identity states through the read path and a plain `driveOperation`: recycled pid, other host, other boot, missing host, missing ticks, missing boot, empty host all read PAUSED and drive executed 0 units; malformed records (string, negative, 0, float, array or null pid; numeric or array ticks, host or boot) are refused at load; `__proto__` injection reads as unknown identity; three drivers raced on one stale goal: one drove, two were refused by the lock, each unit ran once. **Not met on `nexus operation watch`** (S1). **\"I am done\" does not complete a goal: met** (`goal_pa3_completion` fails when the receipt gate is dropped; the model has no slash-command path: `executeGoalCommand` is called only from `repl.ts` and the sidecar). Earlier findings: fail-open stale check, receipt-gate test, redacted fingerprint, `operation status` RUNNING, cap-raising mechanism: **closed** (`nexus operation budget` rejects -5, NaN, 1e30, `abc`, 1.5, 0, empty, 20 digits, `0x10`; it took the lock, journalled by/pid/from/to, left the goal PAUSED, and failed clearly while another process held the lock; the cap env vars are operator-only, so a workspace `.env` cannot set them). **Tamperable state: not closed** (B1, S4).\n\n**Blocking**\n- **B1: `--sandbox` does not block goal-state writes when the workspace is `$HOME` or contains it (run).** `wrapSandboxedCommand(..., {mode:\"bwrap\"})` with the workspace set to HOME rewrote `$HOME/.nexus/tasks/g.json` on the host: `.nexus` is not in `HOME_DENIED` in `cli/src/sandbox.ts`, so the workspace overlay does not hide it. This breaks the PR's own claim that shell writes are blocked under `--sandbox` (`PA3_GOAL_LIFECYCLE.md` \"Integrity\", the manual). With the workspace elsewhere the write was blocked. Fix: mask the real task-state directory in the sandbox (wherever it resolves) and/or state the exception in both docs.\n\n**Follow-ups:** S1 `nexus operation watch` (`operation_cli.ts:613`) shows RUNNING for a killed driver; `--replay` also reads raw state: apply `withDerivedPause`. S2 a zombie driver reads ALIVE (`processStartTicks` and the lock's `processAlive` count state `Z` as live): treat `Z` as gone. S3 a state naming a live pid that holds no lock runs the whole plan under a second driver (5 units executed in the baseline probe; needs a lock-file loss): refuse when the recorded driver is alive and is not this process. S4 the protected-path pattern is not realpath'd: with a symlinked HOME the real-path spelling is allowed; a workspace hard link to a state file is allowed (creating one needs a shell): add `realpathSync(defaultTaskStateDir())`. S5 the PR body says the advisory command check refuses the state dir: it does not (`isCommandBlocked` allowed `sed -i`, `echo >`, `python -c`, `nexus operation budget`); only the file tools refuse; the docs are correct, the PR body was wrong. S6 `loop.ts:469` and `job_worker.ts:154` resume a PAUSED operation unattended through `prepare`, overriding the stale pause: pre-existing and outside goals, but the `job_worker` comment says the stale pause applies \"unchanged\", which is not true.\n**Behaviour changes verified:** a fresh plan with no identity needs no identity field at all and cannot unpause anything; BLOCKED stays BLOCKED (read); off Linux an interrupted goal always pauses (read). **Tests at that head, 0 failures:** `goal_driver_identity` 12, `goal_pa3_completion` 6, `goal_lifecycle` 10, `goal_ledger_propagation` 2, `durable_continuity` 42, `fault_kill_mid_tool_call` 1, 22 `operation_*` files, `security` 14, `slash_router` 39, `slash_resume_other` 9, `leak_guard` 6, `check_requirements` 28, `protocol_schema` 8; `tsc`, invariants, doc versions, the complexity gate pass (`driveOperation` shrank: CC 17 → 15, lines 47 → 33). **Mutations, all 9 caught:** host, ticks, recycled pid, derived read view, goal-status read path, protected path, receipt gate, redacted fingerprint, budget journal write. Not checked: Node 22, containers and PID namespaces, live `run_command` approval gating, forged receipts through the file tools, concurrent overshoot of the cap, secret leakage into flight and receipts, `--dag` beyond one run.\nEOF\ngh pr comment 806 --body-file /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/rev806.md | tail -1; echo \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ) REVIEW (claude-invariants-audit): #806 PA-3 REQUEST CHANGES at a8a8c64e: --sandbox does not protect ~/.nexus/tasks when the workspace is HOME; watch/replay show RUNNING; zombie driver reads alive; follow-ups. Fixing on v1/pa3-completion. DO NOT MERGE #806.\" >> \"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log\"","description":"Post the PA-3 review and log it"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018ttZkAaT5yVe3x5B3mYMMs","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"a6379c334af41ccf9","summary":"Fix PA-3 review findings B1 and S1-S6","message":"PA-3 review of #806 (your branch v1/pa3-completion, worktree /home/mike/nexus-wt/pa3f, head a8a8c64e) is REQUEST CHANGES: read the PR comment `gh pr view 806 --comments` (last one). `git fetch origin && git status`, merge origin/release/v1.3.0 (moved: HK-1 and others merged), never rebase; plain `git push origin v1/pa3-completion` at the end (the PR already exists), never force. Fix, each with a test that fails without it (mutate a copy and restore from it; never `git checkout`):\nB1 (blocking, confirmed by running): with the workspace = $HOME (or containing it) `--sandbox` (bwrap) does not hide `~/.nexus/tasks`: `wrapSandboxedCommand(..., {mode:\"bwrap\"})` rewrote `$HOME/.nexus/tasks/g.json` on the host because `.nexus` is not in `HOME_DENIED` in cli/src/sandbox.ts. Mask the REAL task-state directory (`defaultTaskStateDir()` resolved with realpath; honour NEXUS_STATE_DIR) in both bwrap branches the way PF-3's `hideDirectoryFromSandbox`/`hideDirectories` does for the socket directory (it is on the release branch: reuse it, do not duplicate), also for the sandboxed worker launch; test with workspace = HOME and workspace elsewhere (a sandboxed command must neither read nor write the task dir; if bwrap is unavailable follow how `sandbox_confine.test.ts` skips); update the docs (PA3_GOAL_LIFECYCLE.md Integrity, manual) to say exactly what holds.\nS1: `nexus operation watch` (operation_cli.ts ~613) and `--replay` show RUNNING for a killed driver: apply the same derived-pause view as status/`--dag`. Test.\nS2: a zombie driver (state Z in /proc/<pid>/stat) reads ALIVE in both `processStartTicks` and the lock's `processAlive`: treat Z (and X) as gone. Test with a real zombie (spawn a child whose parent does not reap).\nS3: a state naming a live pid that holds no lock runs the whole plan under a second driver (baseline probe executed 5 units): refuse to drive when the recorded driver identity is ALIVE and is not this process (clear error naming pid), even when the lock file is absent. Test.\nS4: protected path must also cover `realpathSync(defaultTaskStateDir())` (symlinked HOME: the real-path spelling was allowed) and the file tools' hard-link case: a hard link inside the workspace to a state file must be refused for write/edit/delete (check nlink > 1 on protected targets' siblings? Simplest: refuse writes through any path whose realpath/inode equals a protected file's: compare dev+ino of the target with the protected files in the state dir; implement in the shared protected-path check without a heavy scan; if too invasive, document and test only the symlinked-HOME part and say so). Test.\nS5: fix the PR description claim: the advisory command check does NOT refuse the state dir (only the file tools do; `--sandbox` blocks shell writes). Edit the PR body with `gh pr edit 806 --body-file` after reading the current body (`gh pr view 806 --json body`) and correcting only that sentence + adding the HOME-workspace sandbox fix; also make sure docs/CHANGELOG say the same.\nS6: correct the job_worker.ts:~154 comment (the stale pause is overridden by `prepare` for unattended resumes; say so) and look at loop.ts:~469: does an unattended resume of a PAUSED goal still require the operator's explicit action? If the pause is overridden unattended for a goal whose driver identity is unproven, make the unattended path respect the stale pause for goals (fail closed) unless it is the operator-submitted job itself; if that is a larger change, document the exact behaviour and open a GitHub issue (`gh issue create`) describing it, and say which you did.\nRe-run: goal_driver_identity, goal_pa3_completion, goal_lifecycle, goal_ledger_propagation, durable_continuity, fault_kill_mid_tool_call, every operation_* test, sandbox_confine, sandbox_profiles, security, slash_router, slash_resume_other, leak_guard, check_requirements, protocol_schema, the runner/job tests (`ls cli/test | grep -iE 'runner|job|schedule|trigger'` since a job-worker comment/behaviour may change); tsc; complexity gate (exit code); check_invariants; check_doc_versions. Changed/new test files three times. Commit `fix(goal): <what>` + `Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>`; push. Report under 250 words with commit hash, and what you chose for S4 and S6."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
