{"parentUuid":"c9cb357a-80cf-4e22-8b3d-76c0587364ab","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNjMdu7Mj4fCTmzoJ73U","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The hostile review of PA-3 (#806) came back request changes with one blocker and several follow-ups. The review is posted on the PR, and the PA-3 builder is fixing everything on the branch. #806 stays unmerged.\n\n**The clause results:**\n- **A stale goal resumes paused:** met for the paths I named. 21 seeded states (recycled pid, other host, missing identity fields and so on) each read PAUSED, and none executed a unit when driven. Three drivers racing on one stale goal gave one winner and no double runs.\n- **A model's \"I am done\" does not complete a goal:** met.\n- **Token cap command:** works and rejects junk input. It does not resume a paused goal.\n\n**The blocker:** with the workspace set to the home directory, `--sandbox` does not hide `~/.nexus/tasks`, so a sandboxed command rewrote goal state on the host. That contradicts the docs' claim that sandboxing blocks shell writes. The fix reuses the directory-masking mechanism added for the socket work.\n\n**Follow-ups I sent with it:**\n- `nexus operation watch` and `--replay` still show RUNNING for a killed driver.\n- A zombie driver reads as alive.\n- A state naming a live pid with no lock runs the plan under a second driver.\n- The protected path misses the real-path spelling under a symlinked home.\n- The PR body wrongly says the advisory command check refuses the state directory. Only the file tools do.\n- Unattended job paths can resume a paused operation. That was already the case before this PR, but the worker comment is wrong and the builder should fix it or document it.\n\nAll nine mutations the reviewer tried were caught, and `driveOperation` got smaller (complexity 17 to 15).\n\nStill running: the BG-3 firer (in its mutation run) and the HK-3 follow-up. v1.3.0 is not landed. The merge to `main` and the release haven't started."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4284,"cache_read_input_tokens":464792,"output_tokens":631,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4284,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":631,"cache_read_input_tokens":464792,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4284,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4284},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011ChNjMdgiwUCfsVkDrJ2RE","requestRef":"2b854a96-f5ea-4d57-a026-c3ca6c74b958","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"a414bf59-8fe6-45d2-960c-3a96ac4ab9ce","timestamp":"2026-11-25T00:52:20.707Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"v1/bg3-trust-abuse-model","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
