{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-11-25T01:07:23.047Z","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a317b41792fa50650</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01CPQdCgh1sCipKLPizxE4eS</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666/tasks/a317b41792fa50650.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Implement HK-1 hooks\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>A, B and C are done and pushed on `v1/hk3-followups` (plain push, release branch merged, no foreign commits); two parts of C could not be built as asked and are listed first.\n\n## What differs from the brief\n- **Manifest skills are not loaded.** The merged HK-2 has no trigger-based skill loader, and nothing loads installed-plugin skills either. A skill a workspace manifest names is validated, covered by the approval and shown, and adds nothing to any request; `request_shape` passes. Loading it needs HK-2.3 first.\n- **No \"installed plugins\" hook source.** It does not exist on the branch, so the order is operator → workspace manifest plugins → project.\n- **Workspace = HOME (your instruction A1).** Operator plugin directories load as operator's there, with no approval, although the agent's file tools can write them. HK-1 refuses the equivalent hooks file; say if you want plugins refused the same way.\n- **Load order changed.** Operator directories now load first, so a workspace plugin with an operator plugin's name is skipped (`shadowed`) and its tools are not registered.\n\n## A — review findings (`e8f36f85a`)\n- **Source kind** travels with each directory (`pluginDirSources`, `cli/src/plugins.ts`).\n- **`load-failed`**: redacted one-line reason, one notice per plugin, stored on the approval as optional `loadFailed` (same schema version, ledger entry) so `plugins list` and doctor show it without importing.\n- **Hardened read** (`readPluginFile`): regular file, no symlink, no second hard link, 1 MiB, strict UTF-8; `plugins trust` hashes through it.\n- **`trustWorkspacePlugin`** (`plugins_cli.ts`) takes an injected terminal and answer; a file swapped during the question is refused.\n- Tests: `plugin_loader_hardening` 6. Twelve mutations, all killed.\n\n## B — migration (`3bd401b20`)\n- One capped notice per session with the exact `nexus plugins trust &lt;file&gt;` commands.\n- Doctor finding `plugins.workspace` (`doctor_plugins.ts`); the old remedy text is corrected.\n- `docs/PLUGINS.md` with \"Migrating workspace plugins\"; CHANGELOG behaviour change.\n- Tests: `plugin_migration` 5 (migration, policy beats approval, shadowing, repo-shipped trust file). Nine mutations, all killed.\n\n## C — workspace manifest plugins (`622c07fba`)\n- `cli/src/core/workspace_plugins.ts`: `.nexus/plugins/&lt;name&gt;/nexus-plugin.json`, hooks and skills only.\n- Approved by HK-2's tree digest (kind `workspace-manifest`, ledger entry). Every file must be accounted for by the manifest; an unaccounted file or a symlink makes it invalid; a change names the file.\n- Hooks go through `planProjectCommand` with the plugin directory as base and boundary, the `#!` rule, and verified-copy execution.\n- Workspace trust, read-only and managed policy stand above the approval; `plugins trust &lt;dir&gt;` is terminal-only, re-reads the tree, and records nothing for a policy-refused plugin.\n- Tests: `workspace_manifest_plugin` 9. Seventeen mutations; one (read-only) survived, I added an assertion, and it is now killed.\n\n## Gates\nNew files passed three runs each. The full requested list, `tsc`, the complexity gate (exit 0), `check_invariants`, `check_doc_versions` and the hooks schema `--check` pass. `doctor.test` has the same 11 host failures as the release branch.\n\n## Open\nManifest plugins are re-read on every tool call (no cache).</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>837115</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>41</tool_uses><duration_ms>1891190</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
