{"parentUuid":"c4c89223-13c5-41c4-8c03-455d8cc584b7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNkWnCYaKFkUX5YEGAx4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Peb9x3PqzJbNsVHgBdL26d","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-wt/hk3f && git fetch -q origin && git merge -q origin/release/v1.3.0 --no-edit 2>&1 | tail -2; git status --short | grep -c '^UU'; (cd cli && npx tsc --noEmit -p . >/dev/null; echo \"tsc $?\"); git push -q origin v1/hk3-followups 2>&1 | tail -1; echo \"remote $(git ls-remote origin refs/heads/v1/hk3-followups | cut -c1-8) local $(git rev-parse --short=8 HEAD)\"; git log --oneline origin/release/v1.3.0..HEAD | cut -c1-90; cd ~/nexus-code && cat > /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/pr_hk3f.md <<'EOF'\nCompletes HK-3 (workspace plugin trust), which the owner put fully into v1.3.0. #798 (slice 1) merged while my hostile re-review of it was still running; its findings are here (\"Independent hostile re-review at `605e3d5c…`\" on #798).\n\n## A. Review findings fixed (`e8f36f85a`)\n- **Source kind** travels with each plugin directory (`pluginDirSources`, `plugins.ts`) instead of a `startsWith(workspace)` guess: global plugins load as global when the workspace is HOME; sibling-prefix names no longer misclassify.\n- **`load-failed`**: an approved plugin whose imports fail no longer disappears silently: a redacted one-line reason, one notice per plugin, stored on the approval as optional `loadFailed` (same schema version, ledger entry) so `plugins list` and doctor show it without importing.\n- **Hardened read** (`readPluginFile`): regular file, no symlink, no second hard link, 1 MiB, strict UTF-8; `plugins trust` hashes through it.\n- `trustWorkspacePlugin` takes an injected terminal and answer; a file swapped during the question is refused (the re-hash after the prompt is now tested).\n- Operator plugin directories load first, so a workspace plugin with an operator plugin's name is skipped (`shadowed`) and its tools are not registered.\n\n## B. Migration (`3bd401b20`)\nOne capped notice per session with the exact `nexus plugins trust <file>` commands; doctor finding `plugins.workspace` (`doctor_plugins.ts`; the old \"trust the workspace\" remedy text is corrected); `docs/PLUGINS.md` \"Migrating workspace plugins\"; CHANGELOG behaviour change.\n\n## C. Workspace manifest plugins, HK-3.2 (`622c07fba`)\n`.nexus/plugins/<name>/nexus-plugin.json` contributes hooks (and skills, see below), approved per plugin by HK-2's tree digest (kind `workspace-manifest`, ledger entry); every file must be accounted for by the manifest, an unaccounted file or a symlink makes it invalid, a change names the file. Hooks run through the same `planProjectCommand` allowlist (plugin directory as base and boundary), the `#!` rule and verified-copy execution as project hooks. Workspace trust, read-only and managed policy stand above an approval; `plugins trust <dir>` is terminal-only, re-reads the tree and records nothing for a policy-refused plugin.\n\n## What differs from the plan (said plainly)\n- **Manifest skills are validated, covered by the approval and shown, but add nothing to any request**: the merged HK-2 has no trigger-based skill loader and nothing loads installed-plugin skills. `request_shape` passes. Loading them needs the HK-2.3 loader.\n- There is no \"installed plugins\" hook source on this base, so the order is operator → workspace manifest plugins → project.\n- Workspace = HOME: operator plugin directories load as the operator's, with no approval, although the agent's file tools can write them (HK-1 refuses the equivalent hooks file). To be decided in review.\n- Manifest plugins are re-read on every tool call (no cache).\n\n## Tests\n`plugin_loader_hardening` 6, `plugin_migration` 5, `workspace_manifest_plugin` 9; 38 mutations in total (12, 9, 17), all killed after one added assertion. New files three runs each; the full requested list, `tsc`, the complexity gate, `check_invariants`, `check_doc_versions` and the hooks schema `--check` pass locally on Node 24; `doctor.test` has the same 11 host failures as the release branch. Independent hostile review requested before merge.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\nEOF\nu=$(gh pr create --base release/v1.3.0 --head v1/hk3-followups --title \"feat(plugins): complete HK-3: loader fixes, migration notice and doctor, workspace manifest plugins\" --body-file /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/pr_hk3f.md | tail -1); echo \"$u\"; echo \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ) PR (claude-invariants-audit): $u HK-3 completion; independent hostile review next; DO NOT MERGE until posted.\" >> \"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log\"","description":"Merge release into the HK-3 follow-up branch, push, open its PR and log it","timeout":200000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1863,"cache_read_input_tokens":470743,"output_tokens":2052,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":65},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1863,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":2052,"cache_read_input_tokens":470743,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1863,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1863},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":11021,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Peb9x3PqzJbNsVHgBdL26d":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-wt/hk3f && git fetch -q origin && git merge -q origin/release/v1.3.0 --no-edit 2>&1 | tail -2; git status --