aviour change.\n\n## C. Workspace manifest plugins, HK-3.2 (`622c07fba`)\n`.nexus/plugins/<name>/nexus-plugin.json` contributes hooks (and skills, see below), approved per plugin by HK-2's tree digest (kind `workspace-manifest`, ledger entry); every file must be accounted for by the manifest, an unaccounted file or a symlink makes it invalid, a change names the file. Hooks run through the same `planProjectCommand` allowlist (plugin directory as base and boundary), the `#!` rule and verified-copy execution as project hooks. Workspace trust, read-only and managed policy stand above an approval; `plugins trust <dir>` is terminal-only, re-reads the tree and records nothing for a policy-refused plugin.\n\n## What differs from the plan (said plainly)\n- **Manifest skills are validated, covered by the approval and shown, but add nothing to any request**: the merged HK-2 has no trigger-based skill loader and nothing loads installed-plugin skills. `request_shape` passes. Loading them needs the HK-2.3 loader.\n- There is no \"installed plugins\" hook source on this base, so the order is operator → workspace manifest plugins → project.\n- Workspace = HOME: operator plugin directories load as the operator's, with no approval, although the agent's file tools can write them (HK-1 refuses the equivalent hooks file). To be decided in review.\n- Manifest plugins are re-read on every tool call (no cache).\n\n## Tests\n`plugin_loader_hardening` 6, `plugin_migration` 5, `workspace_manifest_plugin` 9; 38 mutations in total (12, 9, 17), all killed after one added assertion. New files three runs each; the full requested list, `tsc`, the complexity gate, `check_invariants`, `check_doc_versions` and the hooks schema `--check` pass locally on Node 24; `doctor.test` has the same 11 host failures as the release branch. Independent hostile review requested before merge.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\nEOF\nu=$(gh pr create --base release/v1.3.0 --head v1/hk3-f