{"parentUuid":"c4c51766-a84f-4540-8b7d-61eba9bd353f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNkaGt3Xyhy17iQMHXfx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The HK-3 completion is open as #808, and an independent hostile review is running. #808 stays unmerged until the verdict is posted.\n\n**What the HK-1 builder reports in the PR:**\n- **Loader fixes:**\n  - Global plugins now load as global when the workspace is home.\n  - An approved plugin whose imports fail is recorded as `load-failed` with one notice, instead of vanishing.\n  - Plugin files are read with a hardened reader.\n  - A file swapped during the trust question is refused.\n- **Migration:** one capped notice per session with the exact `nexus plugins trust` commands, a doctor finding that no longer says \"trust the workspace\", a migration section in `docs/PLUGINS.md`, and a changelog entry.\n- **Workspace manifest plugins (HK-3.2):** hook-only plugins, approved by tree digest. They use the same allowlist and verified-copy execution as project hooks.\n- All 38 mutations are reported caught, after one assertion was added for the one that survived.\n\n**Where the builder deviated from the plan, stated in the PR:**\n- Manifest plugins can name skills, but those are validated and shown only. They add nothing to any request, because the merged plugin store has no trigger-based skill loader.\n- There is no \"installed plugins\" hook source on this base.\n- With the workspace set to home, operator plugin directories load without approval, even though the agent's file tools can write them. The hooks code refuses the equivalent case. I told the reviewer to judge this and I expect it to be blocking.\n- Manifest plugins are re-read on every tool call.\n\nStill running: the BG-3 firer (mutation checks) and the PA-3 fixes for #806. v1.3.0 is not landed. The merge to `main` and the release haven't started."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_