e `plugins trust <dir>` file list prints `file.path` raw (`plugins_cli.ts` ~75): a skill file named `z\\x1b[5A\\x1b[2K…` reached the approval prompt with its ESC intact, so a repository can overwrite the hook lines the operator is shown; doctor evidence and action text carry the same raw names. Fix: `printableRefusal` or the existing strip from `loadFailureText` on every printed name. (3) `treeFiles` (`workspace_plugins.ts:54`) caps files at 64 but not directories, depth or total bytes, and the tree is re-read and re-hashed several times per tool call, even for unapproved or invalid plugins: 50,000 empty directories cost 3.4 s per inspect; 60 files of 1 MiB cost 545 ms per inspect (32 such plugins ≈ 17 s of hashing per call). Fix: cap directories, depth and total bytes, and cache by stat stamp within a call. (4) Any write to a plugin's tree makes the plugin inactive, so an agent can neutralise a repository guard with one `write_file` (same as HK-1 project hooks; the notice is told once): consider protecting `.nexus/plugins/**`. `noteExtensionLoad` rewrites the trust store without a lock, so it can race with `plugins trust` in another process. A malformed `loadFailed` value drops the whole trust store (fails closed; the store is a protected path).\n\n**Earlier findings:** workspace = HOME blocker above; `/ws` vs `/ws2` and symlinked plugin directories classify correctly; a workspace directory that resolves to an operator directory is deduplicated to global. A failing approved plugin gives a `load-failed` record (reason redacted and capped at 300 characters; a secret-shaped string became `[REDACTED:…]`; ESC and newline stripped), shown in `plugins list` and doctor; a forged or cleared `loadFailed` only causes a retry, never an unapproved load. Hardened read (1 MiB cap, symlink, hard link, FIFO, invalid UTF-8) and the injected-answer re-hash tests passed. The earlier race blockers stay closed (400 verified-copy runs against a concurrent writer: 99 copies, all bytes matching the approved hash, 301 refused). **Manifest plugins:** `./guard.sh` and `bash guard.sh` accepted; `node --run`, `npm run`, `env`, `sh -c`, an absolute `/usr/bin/true`, a script outside the plugin directory, a string command and a script symlinked into the workspace refused; a changed byte → `changed`; an unlisted file, a symlink, a FIFO, a directory swapped for a script, a renamed script → `invalid`; a BOM, duplicate keys, an oversize or deep file, an unknown key, `..` or absolute hook paths refused; hook ordering, deny-only (`ignored_allow`), policy above approval, read-only and untrusted gates, and \"skills add nothing to a request\" are covered by tests. **Tests at that head, 0 failures:** `plugin_loader_hardening` 6, `plugin_migration` 5, `workspace_manifest_plugin` 9, `plugin_trust` 6, `hooks_gate_bypass` 11, `managed_policy_enforcement` 113, `check_requirements` 28 and the rest of the list; `doctor` 60/60 with `dist` built; `tsc`, the complexity gate, invariants, doc versions and the hooks schema `--check` exit 0. **Mutations killed:** digest comparison, unlisted file, `planProjectCommand` skipped (9 failures; a narrower version 1), workspace path instead of the verified copy, terminal check, policy above approval, `load-failed` write; the `sha256` half of the digest comparison alone survived (redundant with the per-file comparison). Not checked: the new head, Node 22, a live end-to-end CLI run, case-variant names, hard-link swap to a file outside the tree, concurrent trust-store writes.\nEOF\ngh pr comment 808 --body-file /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/rev808.md | tail -1; echo \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ) REVIEW (claude-invariants-audit): #808 HK-3 completion REQUEST CHANGES at 622c07fb: with workspace=HOME an agent-written ~/.nexus/plugins/x.mjs loads as operator code (executed in a probe); escape injection in notices/approval list; tree-walk caps. Fixing on v1/hk3-followups. DO NOT MERGE #808.\" >> \"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log\"","description":"Post the HK-3 completion review and log it"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3979,"cache_read_input_tokens":478497,"output_tokens":4331,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":86},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3979,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":4331,"cache_read_input_tokens":478497,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3979,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3979},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":12699,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01UMojTjPDtaiZ5wsp45AE6b":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-code && cat > /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/rev808.md <<'EOF'\n**Independent hostile review at `622c07fba25807b03cba4e976aae4724f8c1f90a` — REQUEST CHANGES (one blocker). The head has since moved to `d3f8ef038`, a merge commit; the plugin files and `hooks.ts` are unchanged, but `security.ts` gained 36 lines from a merge of other work that this review did not cover, and nothing was re-run at the new head. I am fixing the findings on this branch.**\n\n**Blocking (run) — `cli/src/plugins.ts:62-76` (`pluginDirSources`):** with the workspace equal to HOME, `~/.nexus/plugins/x.mjs` and `~/.config/nexus/plugins/` load as `global` with no approval, and `SecurityManager.isPathProtected` returns `false` for both. A `write_file` of an agent-written `x.mjs` loaded on the next start and executed its code (it created `$HOME/PWNED`): an agent-written file loads as operator code. HK-1 refuses the equivalent hooks file (`operatorFileInWorkspace`) and protects `nexus/hooks.json` (`security.ts:173`); plugin directories got neither. Fix: when an operator plugin directory lies inside the workspace, skip it with a notice (as HK-1 does) and/or protect both directories. `docs/PLUGINS.md` says the operator's directories \"cannot be changed by the repository\", which is false in this case.\n\n**Non-blocking (run):** (2) terminal-escape injection: plugin file names with ESC, newline or bidi characters reach stderr unsanitised in the pending-plugins notice (`plugins.ts` `announcePending`), the load-failed and shadowed notices and the manifest-plugin notices (`hooks.ts` ~890-897): a name containing `\\nnexus: APPROVED ALL` forges a notice line; the `plugins trust <dir>` file list prints `file.path` raw (`plugins_cli.ts` ~75): a skill file named `z\\x1b[5A\\x1b[2K…` reached the approval prompt with its ESC intact, so a repository can overwrite the hook lines the operator is shown; doctor evidence and action text carry the same raw names. Fix: `printableRefusal` or the existing strip from `loadFailureText` on every printed name. (3) `treeFiles` (`workspace_plugins.ts:54`) caps files at 64 but not directories, depth or total bytes, and the tree is re-read and re-hashed several times per tool call, even for unapproved or invalid plugins: 50,000 empty directories cost 3.4 s per inspect; 60 files of 1 MiB cost 545 ms per inspect (32 such plugins ≈ 17 s of hashing per call). Fix: cap directories, depth and total bytes, and cache by stat stamp within a call. (4) Any write to a plugin's tree makes the plugin inactive, so an agent can neutralise a repository guard with one `write_file` (same as HK-1 project hooks; the notice is told once): consider protecting `.nexus/plugins/**`. `noteExtensionLoad` rewrites the trust store without a lock, so it can race with `plugins trust` in another process. A malformed `loadFailed` value drops the whole trust store (fails closed; the store is a protected path).\n\n**Earlier findings:** workspace = HOME blocker above; `/ws` vs `/ws2` and symlinked plugin directories classify correctly; a workspace directory that resolves to an operator directory is deduplicated to global. A failing approved plugin gives a `load-failed` record (reason redacted and capped at 300 characters; a secret-shaped string became `[REDACTED:…]`; ESC and newline stripped), shown in `plugins list` and doctor; a forged or cleared `loadFailed` only causes a retry, never an unapproved load. Hardened read (1 MiB cap, symlink, hard link, FIFO, invalid UTF-8) and the injected-answer re-hash tests passed. The earlier race blockers stay closed (400 verified-copy runs against a concurrent writer: 99 copies, all bytes matching the approved hash, 301 refused). **Manifest plugins:** `./guard.sh` and `bash guard.sh` accepted; `node --run`, `npm run`, `env`, `sh -c`, an absolute `/usr/bin/true`, a script outside the plugin directory, a string command and a script symlinked into the workspace refused; a changed byte → `changed`; an unlisted file, a symlink, a FIFO, a directory swapped for a script, a renamed script → `invalid`; a BOM, duplicate keys, an oversize or deep file, an unknown key, `..` or absolute hook paths refused; hook ordering, deny-only (`ignored_allow`), policy above approval, read-only and untrusted gates, and \"skills add nothing to a request\" are covered by tests. **Tests at that head, 0 failures:** `plugin_loader_hardening` 6, `plugin_migration` 5, `workspace_manifest_plugin` 9, `plugin_trust` 6, `hooks_gate_bypass` 11, `managed_policy_enforcement` 113, `check_requirements` 28 and the rest of the list; `doctor` 60/60 with `dist` built; `tsc`, the complexity gate, invariants, doc versions and the hooks schema `--check` exit 0. **Mutations killed:** digest comparison, unlisted file, `planProjectCommand` skipped (9 failures; a narrower version 1), workspace path instead of the verified copy, terminal check, policy above approval, `load-failed` write; the `sha256` half of the digest comparison alone survived (redundant with the per-file comparison). Not checked: the new head, Node 22, a live end-to-end CLI run, case-variant names, hard-link swap to a file outside the tree, concurrent trust-store writes.\nEOF\ngh pr comment 808 --body-file /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/rev808.md | tail -1; echo \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ) REVIEW (claude-invariants-audit): #808 HK-3 completion REQUEST CHANGES at 622c07fb: with workspace=HOME an agent-written ~/.nexus/plugins/x.mjs loads as operator code (executed in a probe); escape injection in notices/approval list; tree-walk caps. Fixing on v1/hk3-followups. DO NOT MERGE #808.\" >> \"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log\"","description":"Post the HK-3 completion review and log it"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011ChNmDURN6rKLpG4umLjeK","requestRef":"e20bccf0-3908-46bc-86d1-3853c5a76dd2","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"94776f49-a203-4615-b780-79a04c2f044b","timestamp":"2026-11-25T01:16:53.019Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"v1/bg3-trust-abuse-model","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
