{"parentUuid":"94776f49-a203-4615-b780-79a04c2f044b","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"148d442a-40b5-4f4b-bf12-cdb9ac1659c9","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UMojTjPDtaiZ5wsp45AE6b","type":"tool_result","content":"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/808#issuecomment-7149388027","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"7cd5a739-8f91-4426-bea2-628e855ebbc7","timestamp":"2026-11-25T01:16:56.745Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/808#issuecomment-7149388027","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"gitOperation":{"pr":{"number":808,"url":"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/808","action":"commented"}}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"94776f49-a203-4615-b780-79a04c2f044b","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"v1/bg3-trust-abuse-model","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
{"parentUuid":"7cd5a739-8f91-4426-bea2-628e855ebbc7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNmDUfkTVaYNfXKcFDeX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NAZABESR1qMcBa1AkLduN8","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"a317b41792fa50650","summary":"Fix HK-3 completion review findings","message":"Review of #808 (your branch v1/hk3-followups, worktree /home/mike/nexus-wt/hk3f, head was 622c07fb, now d3f8ef038 after someone merged release into it) is REQUEST CHANGES: read the PR comment `gh pr view 808 --comments` (last). `git fetch origin && git status`, merge origin/release/v1.3.0 and origin/v1/hk3-followups (never rebase), plain push at the end, never force. Fix, each with a test that fails without it (mutate a copy, restore from it):\n1. BLOCKING (reproduced: an agent-written ~/.nexus/plugins/x.mjs executed with workspace = HOME): operator plugin dirs (`~/.nexus/plugins`, `~/.config/nexus/plugins`) inside the workspace must NOT load as operator code. Follow what HK-1 does for the hooks file (`operatorFileInWorkspace`): when an operator plugin directory lies inside the workspace (realpath containment, correct `..`/prefix handling, symlinks), SKIP it with a clear one-time notice (\"start Nexus in a project directory; operator plugins in the workspace are not loaded\"), and ALSO add absolute protected-path patterns for both operator plugin dirs (real config/state dir resolution as `security.ts` does for hooks.json/extension_trust.json) so the file tools refuse them in any workspace. Fix the false sentence in docs/PLUGINS.md (\"cannot be changed by the repository\") to state exactly what holds incl. the unsandboxed limit. Tests: workspace = HOME with agent-written plugin in both dirs (not loaded, no PWNED marker), workspace elsewhere (loads), protected-path tests (write/edit/delete refused), `/ws` vs `/ws2`.\n2. Escape injection: every printed plugin/file/skill name must be sanitised (control chars, ESC, newline, bidi controls, DEL escaped to \\uXXXX or stripped, length-capped) in: announcePending, load-failed, shadowed notices, manifest-plugin notices (hooks.ts ~890-897), the `plugins trust <dir>` approval file list (plugins_cli.ts ~75), `plugins list`, doctor evidence and action text. One shared helper; tests with names containing `\\nnexus: APPROVED ALL`, `\\x1b[5A\\x1b[2K`, bidi overrides: output contains no raw control characters (assert on the exact bytes written to the stream).\n3. Tree walk DoS (`treeFiles`, workspace_plugins.ts:54): cap directories (e.g. 256), depth (e.g. 8), total bytes (e.g. 8 MiB) in addition to 64 files; over any cap = invalid with the reason; and cache the digest per plugin by a stat stamp (dev, ino, size, mtimeNs, ctimeNs of every file + directory listing signature) so repeated reads within one tool call and across calls do not re-hash unchanged trees: the cache must never serve stale content (any stamp change re-hashes; test by changing a byte with mtime preserved via utimes and same size: ctime changes: still detected). Tests: 50,000 empty directories refused fast (<200 ms), 60x1 MiB refused or cached, a hot path benchmark that 100 repeated inspections of an unchanged 64-file tree stays well under 100 ms total.\n4. Protect `.nexus/plugins/**` for the AGENT'S file tools? Decide: workspace plugins' trees live in the workspace and the repo/agent can edit them (change = inactive + notice, same as project hooks). Keep as is, but make the notice for a plugin made inactive by a change louder (once per session, names the changed file) and document the \"agent can neutralise a repo guard by editing it\" limit in docs/PLUGINS.md and HOOKS.md. No protected path for them.\n5. `noteExtensionLoad` must take the same lock/atomic-rename discipline as `plugins trust` for the trust store (a lock file with O_EXCL + pid/start-time staleness like the other stores, or write-temp + rename with a read-modify-write under a lock): test two concurrent writers (child processes) never lose an entry or corrupt the file.\nThen re-run, one at a time: plugin_loader_hardening, plugin_migration, workspace_manifest_plugin, plugin_trust, plugins_dirs, workspace_trust, every hook test (`ls cli/test | grep -iE 'hook'`), content_trust, strict_json, doctor_hooks, doctor (build cli/dist first), request_shape, skills*, managed_policy_allowlists, managed_policy_enforcement, security, security_gates, leak_guard, check_requirements; tsc; the complexity gate (exit code); check_invariants; check_doc_versions; the schema --check generators. Changed/new test files three times. Commit `fix(plugins): <what>` + `Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>`; push. Report under 250 words with the commit hash.","type":"message","recipient":"a317b41792fa50650","recipient_kind":"agent","content":"Review of #808 (your branch v1/hk3-followups, wor…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3979,"cache_read_input_tokens":478497,"output_tokens":4331,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":86},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3979,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":4331,"cache_read_input_tokens":478497,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3979,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3979},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":12376,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01NAZABESR1qMcBa1AkLduN8":{"to":"a317b41792fa50650","summary":"Fix HK-3 completion review findings","message":"Review of #808 (your branch v1/hk3-followups, worktree /home/mike/nexus-wt/hk3f, head was 622c07fb, now d3f8ef038 after someone merged release into it) is REQUEST CHANGES: read the PR comment `gh pr view 808 --comments` (last). `git fetch origin && git status`, merge origin/release/v1.3.0 and origin/v1/hk3-followups (never rebase), plain push at the end, never force. Fix, each with a test that fails without it (mutate a copy, restore from it):\n1. BLOCKING (reproduced: an agent-written ~/.nexus/plugins/x.mjs executed with workspace = HOME): operator plugin dirs (`~/.nexus/plugins`, `~/.config/nexus/plugins`) inside the workspace must NOT load as operator code. Follow what HK-1 does for the hooks file (`operatorFileInWorkspace`): when an operator plugin directory lies inside the workspace (realpath containment, correct `..`/prefix handling, symlinks), SKIP it with a clear one-time notice (\"start Nexus in a project directory; operator plugins in the workspace are not loaded\"), and ALSO add absolute protected-path patterns for both operator plugin dirs (real config/state dir resolution as `security.ts` does for hooks.json/extension_trust.json) so the file tools refuse them in any workspace. Fix the false sentence in docs/PLUGINS.md (\"cannot be changed by the repository\") to state exactly what holds incl. the unsandboxed limit. Tests: workspace = HOME with agent-written plugin in both dirs (not loaded, no PWNED marker), workspace elsewhere (loads), protected-path tests (write/edit/delete refused), `/ws` vs `/ws2`.\n2. Escape injection: every printed plugin/file/skill name must be sanitised (control chars, ESC, newline, bidi controls, DEL escaped to \\uXXXX or stripped, length-capped) in: announcePending, load-failed, shadowed notices, manifest-plugin notices (hooks.ts ~890-897), the `plugins trust <dir>` approval file list (plugins_cli.ts ~75), `plugins list`, doctor evidence and action text. One shared helper; tests with names containing `\\nnexus: APPROVED ALL`, `\\x1b[5A\\x1b[2K`, bidi overrides: output contains no raw control characters (assert on the exact bytes written to the stream).\n3. Tree walk DoS (`treeFiles`, workspace_plugins.ts:54): cap directories (e.g. 256), depth (e.g. 8), total bytes (e.g. 8 MiB) in addition to 64 files; over any cap = invalid with the reason; and cache the digest per plugin by a stat stamp (dev, ino, size, mtimeNs, ctimeNs of every file + directory listing signature) so repeated reads within one tool call and across calls do not re-hash unchanged trees: the cache must never serve stale content (any stamp change re-hashes; test by changing a byte with mtime preserved via utimes and same size: ctime changes: still detected). Tests: 50,000 empty directories refused fast (<200 ms), 60x1 MiB refused or cached, a hot path benchmark that 100 repeated inspections of an unchanged 64-file tree stays well under 100 ms total.\n4. Protect `.nexus/plugins/**` for the AGENT'S file tools? Decide: workspace plugins' trees live in the workspace and the repo/agent can edit them (change = inactive + notice, same as project hooks). Keep as is, but make the notice for a plugin made inactive by a change louder (once per session, names the changed file) and document the \"agent can neutralise a repo guard by editing it\" limit in docs/PLUGINS.md and HOOKS.md. No protected path for them.\n5. `noteExtensionLoad` must take the same lock/atomic-rename discipline as `plugins trust` for the trust store (a lock file with O_EXCL + pid/start-time staleness like the other stores, or write-temp + rename with a read-modify-write under a lock): test two concurrent writers (child processes) never lose an entry or corrupt the file.\nThen re-run, one at a time: plugin_loader_hardening, plugin_migration, workspace_manifest_plugin, plugin_trust, plugins_dirs, workspace_trust, every hook test (`ls cli/test | grep -iE 'hook'`), content_trust, strict_json, doctor_hooks, doctor (build cli/dist first), request_shape, skills*, managed_policy_allowlists, managed_policy_enforcement, security, security_gates, leak_guard, check_requirements; tsc; the complexity gate (exit code); check_invariants; check_doc_versions; the schema --check generators. Changed/new test files three times. Commit `fix(plugins): <what>` + `Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>`; push. Report under 250 words with the commit hash."}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011ChNmDURN6rKLpG4umLjeK","requestRef":"e20bccf0-3908-46bc-86d1-3853c5a76dd2","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"b8d7ab2c-58af-49f3-8f81-031f818ac23b","timestamp":"2026-11-25T01:17:05.419Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"v1/bg3-trust-abuse-model","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
