{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","hash":"625767c6296eba4786a6fb3c6726678f930c2fd237beb7022327693afa683a7e","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UMojTjPDtaiZ5wsp45AE6b","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-code && cat > /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/rev808.md <<'EOF'\n**Independent hostile review at `622c07fba25807b03cba4e976aae4724f8c1f90a` — REQUEST CHANGES (one blocker). The head has since moved to `d3f8ef038`, a merge commit; the plugin files and `hooks.ts` are unchanged, but `security.ts` gained 36 lines from a merge of other work that this review did not cover, and nothing was re-run at the new head. I am fixing the findings on this branch.**\n\n**Blocking (run) — `cli/src/plugins.ts:62-76` (`pluginDirSources`):** with the workspace equal to HOME, `~/.nexus/plugins/x.mjs` and `~/.config/nexus/plugins/` load as `global` with no approval, and `SecurityManager.isPathProtected` returns `false` for both. A `write_file` of an agent-written `x.mjs` loaded on the next start and executed its code (it created `$HOME/PWNED`): an agent-written file loads as operator code. HK-1 refuses the equivalent hooks file (`operatorFileInWorkspace`) and protects `nexus/hooks.json` (`security.ts:173`); plugin directories got neither. Fix: when an operator plugin directory lies inside the workspace, skip it with a notice (as HK-1 does) and/or protect both directories. `docs/PLUGINS.md` says the operator's directories \"cannot be changed by the repository\", which is false in this case.\n\n**Non-blocking (run):** (2) terminal-escape injection: plugin file names with ESC, newline or bidi characters reach stderr unsanitised in the pending-plugins notice (`plugins.ts` `announcePending`), the load-failed and shadowed notices and the manifest-plugin notices (`hooks.ts` ~890-897): a name containing `\\nnexus: APPROVED ALL` forges a notice line; the `plugins trust <dir>` file list prints `file.path` raw (`plugins_cli.ts` ~75): a skill file named `z\\x1b[5A\\x1b[2K…` reached the approval prompt with its ESC intact, so a repository can overwrite the hook lines the operator is shown; doctor evidence and action text carry the same raw names. Fix: `printableRefusal` or the existing strip from `loadFailureText` on every printed name. (3) `treeFiles` (`workspace_plugins.ts:54`) caps files at 64 but not directories, depth or total bytes, and the tree is re-read and re-hashed several times per tool call, even for unapproved or invalid plugins: 50,000 empty directories cost 3.4 s per inspect; 60 files of 1 MiB cost 545 ms per inspect (32 such plugins ≈ 17 s of hashing per call). Fix: cap directories, depth and total bytes, and cache by stat stamp within a call. (4) Any write to a plugin's tree makes the plugin inactive, so an agent can neutralise a repository guard with one `write_file` (same as HK-1 project hooks; the notice is told once): consider protecting `.nexus/plugins/**`. `noteExtensionLoad` rewrites the trust store without a lock, so it can race with `plugins trust` in another process. A malformed `loadFailed` value drops the whole trust store (fails closed; the store is a protected path).\n\n**Earlier findings:** workspace = HOME blocker above; `/ws` vs `/ws2` and symlinked plugin directories classify correctly; a workspace directory that resolves to an operator directory is deduplicated to global. A failing approved plugin gives a `load-failed` record (reason redacted and capped at 300 characters; a secret-shaped string became `[REDACTED:…]`; ESC and newline stripped), shown in `plugins list` and doctor; a forged or cleared `loadFailed` only causes a retry, never an unapproved load. Hardened read (1 MiB cap, symlink, hard link, FIFO, invalid UTF-8) and the injected-answer re-hash tests passed. The earlier race blockers stay closed (400 verified-copy runs against a concurrent writer: 99 copies, all bytes matching the approved hash, 301 refused). **Manifest plugins:** `./guard.sh` and `bash guard.sh` accepted; `node --run`, `npm run`, `env`, `sh -c`, an absolute `/usr/bin/true`, a script outside the plugin directory, a string command and a script symlinked into the workspace refused; a changed byte → `changed`; an unlisted file, a symlink, a FIFO, a directory swapped for a script, a renamed script → `invalid`; a BOM, duplicate keys, an oversize or deep file, an unknown key, `..` or absolute hook paths refused; hook ordering, deny-only (`ignored_allow`), policy above approval, read-only and untrusted gates, and \"skills add nothing to a request\" are covered by tests. **Tests at that head, 0 failures:** `plugin_loader_hardening` 6, `plugin_migration` 5, `workspace_manifest_plugin` 9, `plugin_trust` 6, `hooks_gate_bypass` 11, `managed_policy_enforcement` 113, `check_requirements` 28 and the rest of the list; `doctor` 60/60 with `dist` built; `tsc`, the complexity gate, invariants, doc versions and the hooks schema `--check` exit 0. **Mutations killed:** digest comparison, unlisted file, `planProjectCommand` skipped (9 failures; a narrower version 1), workspace path instead of the verified copy, terminal check, policy above approval, `load-failed` write; the `sha256` half of the digest comparison alone survived (redundant with the per-file comparison). Not checked: the new head, Node 22, a live end-to-end CLI run, case-variant names, hard-link swap to a file outside the tree, concurrent trust-store writes.\nEOF\ngh pr comment 808 --body-file /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/rev808.md | tail -1; echo \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ) REVIEW (claude-invariants-audit): #808 HK-3 completion REQUEST CHANGES at 622c07fb: with workspace=HOME an agent-written ~/.nexus/plugins/x.mjs loads as operator code (executed in a probe); escape injection in notices/approval list; tree-walk caps. Fixing on v1/hk3-followups. DO NOT MERGE #808.\" >> \"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log\"","description":"Post the HK-3 completion review and log it"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NAZABESR1qMcBa1AkLduN8","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"a317b41792fa50650","summary":"Fix HK-3 completion review findings","message":"Review of #808 (your branch v1/hk3-followups, worktree /home/mike/nexus-wt/hk3f, head was 622c07fb, now d3f8ef038 after someone merged release into it) is REQUEST CHANGES: read the PR comment `gh pr view 808 --comments` (last). `git fetch origin && git status`, merge origin/release/v1.3.0 and origin/v1/hk3-followups (never rebase), plain push at the end, never force. Fix, each with a test that fails without it (mutate a copy, restore from it):\n1. BLOCKING (reproduced: an agent-written ~/.nexus/plugins/x.mjs executed with workspace = HOME): operator plugin dirs (`~/.nexus/plugins`, `~/.config/nexus/plugins`) inside the workspace must NOT load as operator code. Follow what HK-1 does for the hooks file (`operatorFileInWorkspace`): when an operator plugin directory lies inside the workspace (realpath containment, correct `..`/prefix handling, symlinks), SKIP it with a clear one-time notice (\"start Nexus in a project directory; operator plugins in the workspace are not loaded\"), and ALSO add absolute protected-path patterns for both operator plugin dirs (real config/state dir resolution as `security.ts` does for hooks.json/extension_trust.json) so the file tools refuse them in any workspace. Fix the false sentence in docs/PLUGINS.md (\"cannot be changed by the repository\") to state exactly what holds incl. the unsandboxed limit. Tests: workspace = HOME with agent-written plugin in both dirs (not loaded, no PWNED marker), workspace elsewhere (loads), protected-path tests (write/edit/delete refused), `/ws` vs `/ws2`.\n2. Escape injection: every printed plugin/file/skill name must be sanitised (control chars, ESC, newline, bidi controls, DEL escaped to \\uXXXX or stripped, length-capped) in: announcePending, load-failed, shadowed notices, manifest-plugin notices (hooks.ts ~890-897), the `plugins trust <dir>` approval file list (plugins_cli.ts ~75), `plugins list`, doctor evidence and action text. One shared helper; tests with names containing `\\nnexus: APPROVED ALL`, `\\x1b[5A\\x1b[2K`, bidi overrides: output contains no raw control characters (assert on the exact bytes written to the stream).\n3. Tree walk DoS (`treeFiles`, workspace_plugins.ts:54): cap directories (e.g. 256), depth (e.g. 8), total bytes (e.g. 8 MiB) in addition to 64 files; over any cap = invalid with the reason; and cache the digest per plugin by a stat stamp (dev, ino, size, mtimeNs, ctimeNs of every file + directory listing signature) so repeated reads within one tool call and across calls do not re-hash unchanged trees: the cache must never serve stale content (any stamp change re-hashes; test by changing a byte with mtime preserved via utimes and same size: ctime changes: still detected). Tests: 50,000 empty directories refused fast (<200 ms), 60x1 MiB refused or cached, a hot path benchmark that 100 repeated inspections of an unchanged 64-file tree stays well under 100 ms total.\n4. Protect `.nexus/plugins/**` for the AGENT'S file tools? Decide: workspace plugins' trees live in the workspace and the repo/agent can edit them (change = inactive + notice, same as project hooks). Keep as is, but make the notice for a plugin made inactive by a change louder (once per session, names the changed file) and document the \"agent can neutralise a repo guard by editing it\" limit in docs/PLUGINS.md and HOOKS.md. No protected path for them.\n5. `noteExtensionLoad` must take the same lock/atomic-rename discipline as `plugins trust` for the trust store (a lock file with O_EXCL + pid/start-time staleness like the other stores, or write-temp + rename with a read-modify-write under a lock): test two concurrent writers (child processes) never lose an entry or corrupt the file.\nThen re-run, one at a time: plugin_loader_hardening, plugin_migration, workspace_manifest_plugin, plugin_trust, plugins_dirs, workspace_trust, every hook test (`ls cli/test | grep -iE 'hook'`), content_trust, strict_json, doctor_hooks, doctor (build cli/dist first), request_shape, skills*, managed_policy_allowlists, managed_policy_enforcement, security, security_gates, leak_guard, check_requirements; tsc; the complexity gate (exit code); check_invariants; check_doc_versions; the schema --check generators. Changed/new test files three times. Commit `fix(plugins): <what>` + `Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>`; push. Report under 250 words with the commit hash."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
