{"parentUuid":"2bda7573-f2ed-44a8-af39-e600671d8a89","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNmFZrMLUHgGUF4ummhi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The hostile review of the HK-3 completion (#808) came back request changes with one blocker. The review is posted on the PR and the fixes are being made on the branch. #808 stays unmerged.\n\n**The blocker (reproduced):** with the workspace set to the home directory, an agent-written plugin file in `~/.nexus/plugins` or `~/.config/nexus/plugins` loads as operator code with no approval. The probe plugin executed on the next start. The hooks code refuses the equivalent case, but plugin directories got neither that refusal nor protected-path coverage. I sent the HK-1 builder these fixes:\n- Skip operator plugin directories that lie inside the workspace, with a clear notice.\n- Add both directories as protected paths.\n- Correct the docs sentence that says the repository cannot change them.\n\n**Also sent, none blocking:**\n- Plugin and file names with escape or control characters reach terminal output unsanitised. One name forged a notice line, and one overwrote the hook lines shown in the approval prompt. All printed names get sanitised.\n- The manifest-plugin tree walk caps files but not directories, depth or bytes. 50,000 empty directories cost 3.4 seconds per inspect, and large trees would add seconds of hashing per tool call. The builder adds caps and a content-safe cache.\n- The notice for a plugin made inactive by an edit gets louder, with the limit documented.\n- The trust store gets a lock for concurrent writers.\n\nThe review's other checks passed: the earlier race fix, the load-failed record with redaction, the hardened read, and the manifest allowlist rules. All the mutations it tried were caught, except one redundant half of a comparison.\n\nThe branch head moved after the review (someone merged release into it), so the reviewer didn't re-run anything at the new head.\n\nStill running: the BG-3 firer builder, in mutation checks, and the PA-3 fixes for #806. v1.3.0 is not landed. The merge to `main` and the release haven't started."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4507,"cache_read_input_tokens":482476,"output_tokens":657,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4507,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":657,"cache_read_input_tokens":482476,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4507,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4507},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011ChNmFZfSJShGjAghpkMpu","requestRef":"2c6cf38d-4927-4ed9-8965-e66fd00b2b88","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"a5c7172b-9e28-469b-8716-5c87a4b0274c","timestamp":"2026-11-25T01:17:12.417Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"v1/bg3-trust-abuse-model","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
