{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-11-25T01:27:21.601Z","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a6379c334af41ccf9</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_018ttZkAaT5yVe3x5B3mYMMs</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666/tasks/a6379c334af41ccf9.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Complete PA-3 goal semantics\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>All six review findings (B1 and S1 to S6) are fixed, each with a test that fails without it, and the follow-up commits are pushed. PR #806 was already merged into `release/v1.3.0` at `6598f1f69`, before these commits. So the fixes need a new PR into `release/v1.3.0`, and I did not open one. I did edit the #806 body for S5.\n\nThe push created `origin/v1/pa3-completion` as a new branch. Its head is `823a5e12b`. The fix commit is `4cd35eb92`, plus a docs commit and the merge of `origin/release/v1.3.0`.\n\nSomeone else's merge commit (`cd96a94d9`) landed on my branch while I worked. It reset my uncommitted edits to `security.ts`, `sandbox.ts` and the sandbox test. I re-applied them and committed straight away.\n\n- **B1:** `sandbox.ts` now masks the real task-state directory (`NEXUS_STATE_DIR` honoured), in both bwrap branches and for the worker. The tests cover a workspace equal to `$HOME` and one elsewhere, and a sandboxed command can neither read nor write the directory.\n- **S1:** `watch` and `status --replay` use the derived-pause view. Test: `nexus operation watch`, `status --replay --json`, `--dag` and plain `status` all read PAUSED for a killed driver.\n- **S2:** `processStartTicks` and the lock's `processAlive` treat Z and X as gone. The test uses a real zombie.\n- **S3:** `driveOperation` refuses a record whose driver is another live pid, even with no lock file, and the error names the pid.\n- **S4:** I did both parts. Protected paths include `realpathSync(defaultTaskStateDir())`, and the shared check refuses a hard link to a state file by comparing device and inode, but only when the file has other links. It scans just the state directory and does not touch the other protected paths.\n- **S5:** the PR body now says the advisory command check does not cover the state directory. The docs and CHANGELOG say the same.\n- **S6:** I documented rather than changed behaviour. The job_worker and loop comments state that `prepare` overrides the stale pause for jobs and loops, which are not goals; `/goal resume` is the only goal path and stays explicit. Issue #807 describes this.\n\nThe listed tests and gates all pass except two. `runner_examples` and `schedule_examples` fail with \"Cannot find package 'tsx'\" from a temp dir. That is a host-environment failure; I did not confirm it also fails on a clean branch, and I did not look into why. Not run on Node 22.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>284240</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>62</tool_uses><duration_ms>2106958</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
