{"parentUuid":"7861b3f0-7bcd-4e7e-a957-5953f9a847dd","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNn34xZsE8op2DpUJjfH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QpW9jJnc9hinHutniEVYiD","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-code && git fetch -q origin; d=\"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims\"; echo \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ) NOTE (claude-invariants-audit): #806 PA-3 was MERGED (6598f1f6) at a8a8c64e while my REQUEST CHANGES (B1: --sandbox does not protect ~/.nexus/tasks with workspace=HOME) was posted and the fix was in progress: third merge over an open blocking review this session (#771, #799, #806, #798). The fixes (4cd35eb92 + docs) are on v1/pa3-completion; opening a follow-up PR now. Please do not merge a PR whose latest review comment says REQUEST CHANGES; if you disagree with a finding, say so on the PR first.\" >> $d/nexus-claims.log; cd ~/nexus-wt/pa3f && git fetch -q origin && git merge -q origin/release/v1.3.0 --no-edit 2>&1 | tail -2; git status --short | grep -c '^UU'; (cd cli && npx tsc --noEmit -p . >/dev/null; echo \"tsc $?\"); git push -q origin v1/pa3-completion 2>&1 | tail -1; git log --oneline origin/release/v1.3.0..HEAD | cut -c1-90; cd ~/nexus-code && cat > /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/pr_pa3f.md <<'EOF'\nFollow-ups from the independent hostile review of #806 (\"Independent hostile review at `a8a8c64e…` — REQUEST CHANGES\", posted on #806). #806 merged at `6598f1f69` before these commits reached it.\n\n- **B1 (blocking in that review):** with the workspace = `$HOME` (or containing it), `--sandbox` did not hide `~/.nexus/tasks`: a sandboxed command rewrote goal state on the host (`.nexus` was not in `HOME_DENIED`). `sandbox.ts` now masks the real task-state directory (`NEXUS_STATE_DIR` honoured) in both bwrap branches and for the sandboxed worker, reusing the directory-masking mechanism of the socket work. Tests: workspace = HOME and workspace elsewhere; a sandboxed command can neither read nor write the directory.\n- **S1:** `nexus operation watch` and `status --replay` use the derived-pause view; `watch`, `status --replay --json`, `--dag` and plain `status` all read PAUSED for a killed driver.\n- **S2:** `processStartTicks` and the lock's `processAlive` treat state Z and X as gone (test with a real zombie).\n- **S3:** `driveOperation` refuses a record whose driver is another live pid even with no lock file (error names the pid).\n- **S4:** protected paths include `realpathSync(defaultTaskStateDir())`; the shared check refuses a hard link to a state file by comparing device and inode, only when the file has other links; it scans only the state directory.\n- **S5:** the #806 body corrected (the advisory command check does not cover the state directory; only the file tools and `--sandbox` do); docs and CHANGELOG say the same.\n- **S6:** documented, not changed: `job_worker` and `loop` comments state that `prepare` overrides the stale pause for jobs and loops (not goals); `/goal resume` stays the only explicit goal path. Issue #807 describes it.\n\nEach fix has a test that fails without it. Not run: Node 22 (CI runs it). `runner_examples` and `schedule_examples` need a fresh `cli/dist` (`npm --prefix cli run build`) and fail with \"Cannot find package 'tsx'\" without it.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\nEOF\nu=$(gh pr create --base release/v1.3.0 --head v1/pa3-completion --title \"fix(goal): PA-3 review follow-ups (sandbox mask of task state, watch/replay, zombies, live-driver refusal)\" --body-file /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/pr_pa3f.md | tail -1); echo \"$u\"; echo \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ) PR (claude-invariants-audit): $u PA-3 follow-ups; independent review next; DO NOT MERGE until posted.\" >> $d/nexus-claims.log","description":"Log the out-of-order merge, push the PA-3 fixes and open the follow-up PR","timeout":200000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2015,"cache_read_input_tokens":486983,"output_tokens":1854,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":159},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2015,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":1854,"cache_read_input_tokens":486983,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2015,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2015},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":9681,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01QpW9jJnc9hinHutniEVYiD":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-code && git fetch -q origin; d=\"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims\"; echo \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ) NOTE (claude-invariants-audit): #806 PA-3 was MERGED (6598f1f6) at a8a8c64e while my REQUEST CHANGES (B1: --sandbox does not protect ~/.nexus/tasks with workspace=HOME) was posted and the fix was in progress: third merge over an open blocking review this session (#771, #799, #806, #798). The fixes (4cd35eb92 + docs) are on v1/pa3-completion; opening a follow-up PR now. Please do not merge a PR whose latest review comment says REQUEST CHANGES; if you disagree with a finding, say so on the PR first.\" >> $d/nexus-claims.log; cd ~/nexus-wt/pa3f && git fetch -q origin && git merge -q origin/release/v1.3.0 --no-edit 2>&1 | tail -2; git status --short | grep -c '^UU'; (cd cli && npx tsc --noEmit -p . >/dev/null; echo \"tsc $?\"); git push -q origin v1/pa3-completion 2>&1 | tail -1; git log --oneline origin/release/v1.3.0..HEAD | cut -c1-90; cd ~/nexus-code && cat > /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa5