{"parentUuid":"5a5c42a1-b718-4bc9-a5d5-cf628661c3d8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNn4vVNkqdjabw5pCpob","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Bhe6gFYgZNMm39P1h5kF16","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Delta review PA-3 fixes 4cd35eb92","subagent_type":"reviewer","prompt":"Short, time-boxed (about 25 minutes) independent delta review in ~/nexus-code of the PA-3 follow-up fixes that are ALREADY on `origin/release/v1.3.0` (commit `4cd35eb92`, merged with PR #806 at `6598f1f69`) plus the docs-only PR #809 (`gh pr diff 809`). The hostile review of #806 (PR comment \"Independent hostile review at `a8a8c64e…` — REQUEST CHANGES\", `gh pr view 806 --comments`) found: B1 (blocking) with workspace = `$HOME` or containing it, `--sandbox` (bwrap) did not hide `~/.nexus/tasks`, so a sandboxed command rewrote goal state on the host; S1 `nexus operation watch` and `status --replay` showed RUNNING for a killed driver; S2 a zombie driver read ALIVE; S3 a state naming a live pid with no lock ran the plan under a second driver; S4 protected-path gaps (symlinked HOME real path; hard link); S5 wrong PR-body claim; S6 unattended `prepare` overrides the stale pause for jobs/loops (documented, issue #807). Fix commit `4cd35eb92` claims: `sandbox.ts` masks the real task-state directory (`NEXUS_STATE_DIR` honoured) in both bwrap branches and for the sandboxed worker (reusing `hideDirectoryFromSandbox`/`hideDirectories`); watch/replay use the derived-pause view; Z and X states read as gone; `driveOperation` refuses a record whose driver is another live pid even with no lock; protected paths include `realpathSync(defaultTaskStateDir())` and the shared check refuses a hard link to a state file by dev+ino comparison (only when nlink > 1; scans only the state dir).\nVerify each by RUNNING (throwaway HOME, temp workspaces, no network, no inference; real bwrap if `bwrap --version` works): B1 attack: workspace = HOME, workspace = parent of HOME, workspace elsewhere, `NEXUS_STATE_DIR` set to a path under HOME/under /var/tmp/relative/symlinked: a sandboxed command can neither list, read, write nor delete `tasks/*.json` in both bwrap profiles (general and read-only) and via the sandboxed worker; also the docker sandbox mode if it exists (state what it mounts); the mask applies when the directory does not exist yet at wrap time (created later by a drive): can a sandboxed command create it first? S1: `watch`, `status --replay --json`, `--dag`, `status`, `/goal status` agree for a killed driver. S2: real zombie (child of a non-reaping parent) reads gone in BOTH `processStartTicks` and `processAlive`; a process in state D or T is still alive. S3: recorded driver alive and not this process → refuse, error names the pid, no unit executes, even with the lock file removed; a driver that is THIS process re-entering is allowed; pid recycled still pauses rather than refuses? (document what happens). S4: the symlinked-HOME real-path spelling is refused by the file tools; hard-link case: create a hard link to a state file inside a workspace and try write/edit/delete through the file tools: refused; a legitimate file with nlink > 1 elsewhere (not in the state dir) is unaffected; cost of the scan (a state dir with 5,000 files: file-tool latency?) and a TOCTOU (link created after the check). Docs claims in `PA3_GOAL_LIFECYCLE.md`, the manual and CHANGELOG (and #809's changes) vs code: list any false sentence.\nRun, one at a time, at the tip: `goal_driver_identity`, `goal_pa3_completion`, `goal_lifecycle`, `goal_ledger_propagation`, the new/changed tests in `4cd35eb92` (`git show --stat 4cd35eb92`), `sandbox_confine`, `sandbox_profiles`, `sandbox_cancel`, every `operation_*` test, `durable_continuity`, `security`, `leak_guard`, `check_requirements`, plus `runner_examples`/`schedule_examples` after `npm --prefix cli run build` in the review worktree; `cd cli && npx tsc --noEmit -p .`; the complexity gate (check the exit code); `node scripts/check_invariants.mjs`; `node scripts/check_doc_versions.mjs`. Mutations (copy aside, restore from the copy, never `git checkout`): drop the general-branch mask; drop the read-only-branch mask; drop the realpath protected entry; drop the dev+ino check; drop the Z/X handling; drop the live-driver refusal: each must fail a test.\nRules: do NOT edit ~/nexus-code or existing worktrees. `git -C ~/nexus-code fetch origin && git -C ~/nexus-code worktree add --detach ~/nexus-wt/rev809 origin/release/v1.3.0`; `cp -a ~/nexus-code/cli/node_modules ~/nexus-wt/rev809/cli/`; `mkdir -p ~/nexus-wt/rev809/core/target/release && cp ~/nexus-wt/ls1b/core/target/release/{harness-core,nexus-tui} ~/nexus-wt/rev809/core/target/release/`. Tests: `cd ~/nexus-wt/rev809/cli && TMPDIR=/dev/shm HOME=$(mktemp -d) node --import tsx --test test/<name>.test.ts 2>&1 | tail -20`. Never touch the real ~/.nexus, ~/.config/nexus, /etc/nexus. Stop processes by their own pid; never `pkill -f`; never delete anything outside your own temp dirs (no glob deletes in /dev/shm). No commits, pushes or GitHub comments. Remove probes and the worktree at the end. Shell is zsh (`bash -c` for loops); prefix `rtk proxy` if output looks filtered; a safety check blocks scripts containing `rm`.\nReport under 400 words: verdict (ACCEPT / ACCEPT WITH FOLLOW-UPS / REQUEST CHANGES) on the code at the release tip; B1 and S1-S4 each closed or not with the attack run; new findings with file:line, run-or-read, blocking or not (a sandboxed command reading or writing goal state, a goal executing a unit under an unproven or second driver, a state file writable through the file tools by any spelling, are blocking; the documented unsandboxed-shell limit is not); test counts; mutation results; false doc sentences; what you did not check."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creatio