{"parentUuid":"747bfa63-b776-4115-b69a-b7404e8e04fe","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNn6NDENtoyLuB3KcJmV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"#806 (PA-3) was merged by another session at `6598f1f69`, while my request-changes verdict on it (B1, the sandbox hole) was still open and the fixes were in progress. That is the fourth merge over an open blocking review this session, after #771, #799 and #798. I logged it and asked in the claims log that nobody merge a PR whose latest review says request changes.\n\nThe builder's fix commit (`4cd35eb92`) had already been pushed to that PR branch before it merged, so the substantive fixes are on the release branch now:\n- `--sandbox` masks the real goal-state directory.\n- `nexus operation watch` and `status --replay` show PAUSED for a killed driver.\n- A zombie driver reads as gone.\n- The drive path refuses a record whose driver is another live process, even with no lock.\n- The protected path covers the real path, plus hard links to state files.\n\nThe follow-up PR (#809) therefore only adds docs, 12 lines. The builder reports each fix has a test that fails without it. I haven't re-run those tests myself.\n\nNobody independently reviewed those fixes before they landed, so a short delta review of them is running. It will:\n- re-run the sandbox attack across workspace choices, state-directory settings and both bwrap profiles;\n- test the zombie and live-driver cases;\n- try the hard-link case through the file tools.\n\nI'll merge #809 after the review is posted.\n\nStill running: the HK-3 fixes for #808 and the BG-3 firer builder. v1.3.0 is not landed. The merge to `main` and the release haven't started."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3015,"cache_read_input_tokens":491692,"output_tokens":517,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"serv