{"parentUuid":"4c6ac35e-cc66-4c48-909d-d43b3176b5db","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNo1zSnum4esTQRY9iBH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The HK-3 builder pushed its review fixes to #808 (`f375865ed`), and a re-review is running against that head. #808 stays unmerged until it reports.\n\nWhat the builder reports fixed:\n- Operator plugin directories that lie inside the workspace are skipped with a one-time notice. The agent's file tools can no longer write them, so the home-directory case (where an agent-written plugin ran as operator code) is closed.\n- All printed plugin names now go through one escaping helper, covering the loader, `plugins trust`, `plugins list` and doctor.\n- The manifest tree walk is capped at 64 files, 256 directories, 8 levels and 8 MiB, with a content-safe cache. 50,000 empty directories are refused in under 200 ms.\n- A plugin made inactive by an edit gets a louder once-per-session notice.\n- The trust store is written under a lock. Four concurrent writer processes lost no entry.\n\nThe builder reports 22 mutations, all caught. One target was missed: a benchmark of 100 inspections takes 100–130 ms on this host, not \"well under 100\". I haven't re-run any of this.\n\nOne question I asked the reviewer to judge: with the workspace set to home, a hand-installed operator plugin now needs per-file approval, so it could silently stop loading for people who start Nexus there. The review should say whether the notice makes that clear enough.\n\nStill running: the delta review of the PA-3 fixes (the docs follow-up #809 waits on it) and the BG-3 firer builder. v1.3.0 is not landed. The merge to `main` and the release haven't started."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3494,"cache_read_input_tokens":496473,"output_tokens":527,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3494,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":527,"cache_read_input_tokens":496473,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3494,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3494},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011ChNo1zG8S4kJKfhdZRMkD","requestRef":"10055ce8-dd1d-411a-9d5b-db7b6a0c4aef","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"68c24617-c13e-4b2b-bdf3-b2b54c94db89","timestamp":"2026-11-25T01:40:20.455Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"v1/bg3-trust-abuse-model","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
