{"parentUuid":"19da58b0-ab38-4e31-a1d5-5fbfd30ca27d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNoM5JX2fN8dnyazSNrD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3188,"cache_read_input_tokens":499967,"output_tokens":3882,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":234},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3188,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":3882,"cache_read_input_tokens":499967,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3188,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3188},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":1808,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011ChNoM57MjhY7axR8FmphR","requestRef":"cdb2a439-dbf3-483c-9fa8-98cc7d4558c2","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"6f7925e3-ad0b-4a4b-b748-55127f36a313","timestamp":"2026-11-25T01:44:38.102Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"v1/bg3-trust-abuse-model","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
{"parentUuid":"6f7925e3-ad0b-4a4b-b748-55127f36a313","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNoM5JX2fN8dnyazSNrD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013MLhGLF3KHyAZdNqQt2jbJ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-code && cat > /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/rev809.md <<'EOF'\n**Independent delta review of the PA-3 follow-up fixes (`4cd35eb92`, on the release branch since the merge of #806 at `6598f1f69`) plus this PR's docs — REQUEST CHANGES. B1 is closed only for plain bwrap reads and writes of `tasks/*.json`; three ways around the mask remain (all run: real bwrap 0.13.1, a real docker daemon). I am fixing them on this branch.**\n\n**Blocking**\n1. **The mask covers only the `tasks` directory (`cli/src/sandbox.ts:36-43`).** With workspace = HOME, a sandboxed `mv ~/.nexus ~/.nexus.old` succeeded (rc=0), and `mkdir -p ~/.nexus/tasks && echo FORGED > ~/.nexus/tasks/goal-forged.json` then created a forged goal file on the host. Fix: mask the whole state root (`NEXUS_STATE_DIR` or `~/.nexus`), not just `tasks`, so the parent cannot be renamed or replaced.\n2. **A state directory that does not exist at wrap time is skipped** (`realpathSync` throws). With workspace = HOME a sandboxed command created it on the host and planted `planted.json`. Fix: create the directory (mode 0700) before wrapping.\n3. **Docker is not masked at the tip.** The docker argv has no mask: with workspace = HOME a sandboxed `cat ~/.nexus/tasks/goal-x.json` returned the file and `echo PWN >` overwrote the host file. This PR's `--tmpfs` mask closes read and write (read blocked, write read-only, host file unchanged) but has the same rename and not-yet-created gaps as bwrap.\n\n**Closed (run):** B1 for bwrap reads and writes in every workspace/`NEXUS_STATE_DIR` combination (workspace = HOME, parent of HOME, elsewhere, under HOME; state dir under HOME, in `/var/tmp`, symlinked, relative), both profiles and the worker launch. S1: `watch`, `status --replay --json`, `--dag` and `status` agree for a killed driver. S2: a real zombie reads gone in `processStartTicks` and `processRunning`. S3: a live foreign driver with no lock is refused (error names the pid, no unit runs); a recycled pid, other host or other boot pauses. S4: a symlinked-HOME real path is refused (including a new file), a hard link or symlink to a state file is refused, a legitimate multi-link file elsewhere is unaffected.\n**Suggestions:** the hard-link scan is not recursive (a hard link to a file in a state subdirectory passed as unprotected), and with 5,000 state files each file-tool check on a file with more than one link costs about 100 ms (`protectedBelow` calls it per entry; pnpm trees are heavily hard-linked): cache the state directory's inode set briefly and scan recursively. The TOCTOU (a link created after the check) is inherent. The zombie test raced once with `ENOENT` on `/proc/<pid>/stat` (`goal_driver_identity`, line ~276): make the setup wait for the child to be a zombie without reading a vanished entry.\n**False doc sentences:** `PA3_GOAL_LIFECYCLE.md` (\"A sandboxed command can neither read nor write it\") and the CHANGELOG (\"masked inside `--sandbox`\") are false for docker and for the rename and not-yet-created cases; `PA3_GOAL_LIFECYCLE.md` says Docker \"needs no mask unless the workspace contains the state directory\", false with workspace = HOME; this PR's manual line \"`--sandbox` hides the directory… even when the workspace is your home directory\" is false for the rename bypass; \"hard link refused\" omits state subdirectories.\n**Tests at the tip, 0 failures** except one flake: `goal_driver_identity` 15 (the zombie race above), `goal_pa3_completion` 7, `goal_lifecycle` 10, `goal_ledger_propagation` 2, `sandbox_confine` 21, `sandbox_profiles` 16, `sandbox_cancel` 2, `durable_continuity` 42, 19 `operation_*` files, `security` 14, `check_requirements` 28, `leak_guard` 6, `runner_examples` 1, `schedule_examples` 1; `tsc`, the complexity gate, invariants, doc versions pass. **Mutations, all caught:** general mask (7 failures), read-only mask (2), state dir out of the mask list (2), realpath protected entry (1), dev+ino check (1), Z/X handling (1), live-driver refusal (1). Not checked: a real drive end to end, docker with a not-yet-created directory, cancel and kill inside the mask, Node 22.\nEOF\ngh pr comment 809 --body-file /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/rev809.md | tail -1; echo \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ) REVIEW (claude-invariants-audit): #809 / PA-3 fixes on release: REQUEST CHANGES: mask covers only tasks/ (mv ~/.nexus works; forged goal file created), not-yet-created dir skipped, docker unmasked at tip (#809 adds tmpfs). Fixing on v1/pa3-completion. DO NOT MERGE #809.\" >> \"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log\"","description":"Post the PA-3 delta review on PR 809 and log it"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3188,"cache_read_input_tokens":499967,"output_tokens":3882,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":234},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3188,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":3882,"cache_read_input_tokens":499967,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3188,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3188},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":12001,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_013MLhGLF3KHyAZdNqQt2jbJ":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-code && cat > /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/rev809.md <<'EOF'\n**Independent delta review of the PA-3 follow-up fixes (`4cd35eb92`, on the release branch since the merge of #806 at `6598f1f69`) plus this PR's docs — REQUEST CHANGES. B1 is closed only for plain bwrap reads and writes of `tasks/*.json`; three ways around the mask remain (all run: real bwrap 0.13.1, a real docker daemon). I am fixing them on this branch.**\n\n**Blocking**\n1. **The mask covers only the `tasks` directory (`cli/src/sandbox.ts:36-43`).** With workspace = HOME, a sandboxed `mv ~/.nexus ~/.nexus.old` succeeded (rc=0), and `mkdir -p ~/.nexus/tasks && echo FORGED > ~/.nexus/tasks/goal-forged.json` then created a forged goal file on the host. Fix: mask the whole state root (`NEXUS_STATE_DIR` or `~/.nexus`), not just `tasks`, so the parent cannot be renamed or replaced.\n2. **A state directory that does not exist at wrap time is skipped** (`realpathSync` throws). With workspace = HOME a sandboxed command created it on the host and planted `planted.json`. Fix: create the directory (mode 0700) before wrapping.\n3. **Docker is not masked at the tip.** The docker argv has no mask: with workspace = HOME a sandboxed `cat ~/.nexus/tasks/goal-x.json` returned the file and `echo PWN >` overwrote the host file. This PR's `--tmpfs` mask closes read and write (read blocked, write read-only, host file unchanged) but has the same rename and not-yet-created gaps as bwrap.\n\n**Closed (run):** B1 for bwrap reads and writes in every workspace/`NEXUS_STATE_DIR` combination (workspace = HOME, parent of HOME, elsewhere, under HOME; state dir under HOME, in `/var/tmp`, symlinked, relative), both profiles and the worker launch. S1: `watch`, `status --replay --json`, `--dag` and `status` agree for a killed driver. S2: a real zombie reads gone in `processStartTicks` and `processRunning`. S3: a live foreign driver with no lock is refused (error names the pid, no unit runs); a recycled pid, other host or other boot pauses. S4: a symlinked-HOME real path is refused (including a new file), a hard link or symlink to a state file is refused, a legitimate multi-link file elsewhere is unaffected.\n**Suggestions:** the hard-link scan is not recursive (a hard link to a file in a state subdirectory passed as unprotected), and with 5,000 state files each file-tool check on a file with more than one link costs about 100 ms (`protectedBelow` calls it per entry; pnpm trees are heavily hard-linked): cache the state directory's inode set briefly and scan recursively. The TOCTOU (a link created after the check) is inherent. The zombie test raced once with `ENOENT` on `/proc/<pid>/stat` (`goal_driver_identity`, line ~276): make the setup wait for the child to be a zombie without reading a vanished entry.\n**False doc sentences:** `PA3_GOAL_LIFECYCLE.md` (\"A sandboxed command can neither read nor write it\") and the CHANGELOG (\"masked inside `--sandbox`\") are false for docker and for the rename and not-yet-created cases; `PA3_GOAL_LIFECYCLE.md` says Docker \"needs no mask unless the workspace contains the state directory\", false with workspace = HOME; this PR's manual line \"`--sandbox` hides the directory… even when the workspace is your home directory\" is false for the rename bypass; \"hard link refused\" omits state subdirectories.\n**Tests at the tip, 0 failures** except one flake: `goal_driver_identity` 15 (the zombie race above), `goal_pa3_completion` 7, `goal_lifecycle` 10, `goal_ledger_propagation` 2, `sandbox_confine` 21, `sandbox_profiles` 16, `sandbox_cancel` 2, `durable_continuity` 42, 19 `operation_*` files, `security` 14, `check_requirements` 28, `leak_guard` 6, `runner_examples` 1, `schedule_examples` 1; `tsc`, the complexity gate, invariants, doc versions pass. **Mutations, all caught:** general mask (7 failures), read-only mask (2), state dir out of the mask list (2), realpath protected entry (1), dev+ino check (1), Z/X handling (1), live-driver refusal (1). Not checked: a real drive end to end, docker with a not-yet-created directory, cancel and kill inside the mask, Node 22.\nEOF\ngh pr comment 809 --body-file /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/rev809.md | tail -1; echo \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ) REVIEW (claude-invariants-audit): #809 / PA-3 fixes on release: REQUEST CHANGES: mask covers only tasks/ (mv ~/.nexus works; forged goal file created), not-yet-created dir skipped, docker unmasked at tip (#809 adds tmpfs). Fixing on v1/pa3-completion. DO NOT MERGE #809.\" >> \"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log\"","description":"Post the PA-3 delta review on PR 809 and log it"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011ChNoM57MjhY7axR8FmphR","requestRef":"cdb2a439-dbf3-483c-9fa8-98cc7d4558c2","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"825bafb1-e6f7-4c3d-a98d-fdec7ec0836a","timestamp":"2026-11-25T01:44:50.140Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"v1/bg3-trust-abuse-model","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
