{"parentUuid":"cdff27ce-449f-4158-af55-804b4b052c9e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNoM5JX2fN8dnyazSNrD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Tdoj7RDb52dj1tMncHdXZa","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"a6379c334af41ccf9","summary":"Close remaining PA-3 sandbox mask gaps","message":"Delta review of the PA-3 fixes: REQUEST CHANGES, comment on PR #809 (`gh pr view 809 --comments`, last). Your branch v1/pa3-completion (worktree /home/mike/nexus-wt/pa3f; PR #809 is open from it; release has your 4cd35eb92). `git fetch origin && git status`, merge origin/release/v1.3.0 (never rebase), plain `git push origin v1/pa3-completion` at the end (never force). Fix, each with a test that fails without it (mutate a copy, restore from it):\n1. Mask the whole STATE ROOT (`NEXUS_STATE_DIR` or `~/.nexus`, realpath'd), not just `tasks`: with workspace = HOME a sandboxed `mv ~/.nexus ~/.nexus.old` succeeded and a forged `tasks/goal-forged.json` was then created on the host. A tmpfs mount on the state root makes rename/replace fail (EBUSY); the root's other contents (logs, backups, flight records, `~/.nexus/backups`) become invisible in the sandbox: acceptable and intended; check nothing the sandboxed tools legitimately need lives there (run the sandbox_* tests and the examples). Do it in BOTH bwrap profiles, the sandboxed worker launch AND Docker (`--tmpfs` for the state root in the docker argv: #809 added a tasks mask for docker: extend it to the root).\n2. A state dir that does not exist at wrap time: create it (mode 0700, owner-only, recursive for the root) BEFORE wrapping so the mask always applies (today `realpathSync` throws and the mask is skipped, then a sandboxed command creates it on the host). Tests: workspace = HOME with an absent state dir: after the sandboxed command (`mkdir -p ~/.nexus/tasks && echo X > ...`) the HOST has no planted file; the directory is 0700.\n3. Tests for rename (`mv ~/.nexus ~/.nexus.old` fails inside the sandbox, host intact) and the not-yet-created case in the real-bwrap tests (skip as the existing sandbox_confine tests do when bwrap is unavailable); a docker argv test asserting the root mask (and, if a docker daemon is available as the reviewer's was, one real run behind the same skip logic the docker tests use).\n4. Hard-link scan: make it recursive over the state dir with a short-lived cache of the state dir's (dev,ino) set (e.g. 1-2 s TTL, invalidated by a stat stamp of the dir tree top-level mtimes is NOT sufficient: use TTL only and say so); the per-check cost with 5,000 state files and a multi-link file must be well under 10 ms amortised; the TOCTOU stays documented. Tests: hard link to a file in a state SUBDIRECTORY is refused; benchmark bound.\n5. `goal_driver_identity` zombie test races with ENOENT on /proc/<pid>/stat (line ~276): make the setup robust (poll for state Z with ENOENT tolerated, bounded timeout) and run it 20 times in a row.\n6. Docs: make every sentence true: `PA3_GOAL_LIFECYCLE.md` (what the sandbox hides: the state root in bwrap AND docker, created before wrapping; what it does not: an unsandboxed command, same-uid processes outside), CHANGELOG, the manual line, \"hard link refused\" (incl. subdirectories). Remove the false \"Docker needs no mask unless…\" sentence.\nRe-run: goal_driver_identity (20x for the zombie), goal_pa3_completion, goal_lifecycle, goal_ledger_propagation, sandbox_confine, sandbox_profiles, sandbox_cancel, sandbox_docker, sandbox_denial_events, every operation_* test, durable_continuity, runner_examples and schedule_examples (after `npm --prefix cli run build`), security, leak_guard, check_requirements; tsc; the complexity gate (exit code); check_invariants; check_doc_versions. Changed/new test files three times. Commit `fix(goal): <what>` + `Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>`; push. Report under 200 words with the commit hash.","type":"message","recipient":"a6379c334af41ccf9","recipient_kind":"agent","content":"Delta review of the PA-3 fixes: REQUEST CHANGES, …"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3188,"cache_read_input_tokens":499967,"output_tokens":3882,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":234},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3188,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":3882,"cache_read_input_tokens":499967,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3188,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3188},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":9676,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Tdoj7RDb52dj1tMncHdXZa":{"to":"a6379c334af41ccf9","summary":"Close remaining PA-3 sandbox mask gaps","message":"Delta review of the PA-3 fixes: REQUEST CHANGES, comment on PR #809 (`gh pr view 809 --comments`, last). Your branch v1/pa3-completion (worktree /home/mike/nexus-wt/pa3f; PR #809 is open from it; release has your 4cd35eb92). `git fetch origin && git status`, merge origin/release/v1.3.0 (never rebase), plain `git push origin v1/pa3-completion` at the end (never force). Fix, each with a test that fails without it (mutate a copy, restore from it):\n1. Mask the whole STATE ROOT (`NEXUS_STATE_DIR` or `~/.nexus`, realpath'd), not just `tasks`: with workspace = HOME a sandboxed `mv ~/.nexus ~/.nexus.old` succeeded and a forged `tasks/goal-forged.json` was then created on the host. A tmpfs mount on the state root makes rename/replace fail (EBUSY); the root's other contents (logs, backups, flight records, `~/.nexus/backups`) become invisible in the sandbox: acceptable and intended; check nothing the sandboxed