{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","hash":"258ffddfd680d987bd76a39d04ceffff1ce3ed4c5999af5e7a9f86036dcf854b","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013MLhGLF3KHyAZdNqQt2jbJ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-code && cat > /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/rev809.md <<'EOF'\n**Independent delta review of the PA-3 follow-up fixes (`4cd35eb92`, on the release branch since the merge of #806 at `6598f1f69`) plus this PR's docs — REQUEST CHANGES. B1 is closed only for plain bwrap reads and writes of `tasks/*.json`; three ways around the mask remain (all run: real bwrap 0.13.1, a real docker daemon). I am fixing them on this branch.**\n\n**Blocking**\n1. **The mask covers only the `tasks` directory (`cli/src/sandbox.ts:36-43`).** With workspace = HOME, a sandboxed `mv ~/.nexus ~/.nexus.old` succeeded (rc=0), and `mkdir -p ~/.nexus/tasks && echo FORGED > ~/.nexus/tasks/goal-forged.json` then created a forged goal file on the host. Fix: mask the whole state root (`NEXUS_STATE_DIR` or `~/.nexus`), not just `tasks`, so the parent cannot be renamed or replaced.\n2. **A state directory that does not exist at wrap time is skipped** (`realpathSync` throws). With workspace = HOME a sandboxed command created it on the host and planted `planted.json`. Fix: create the directory (mode 0700) before wrapping.\n3. **Docker is not masked at the tip.** The docker argv has no mask: with workspace = HOME a sandboxed `cat ~/.nexus/tasks/goal-x.json` returned the file and `echo PWN >` overwrote the host file. This PR's `--tmpfs` mask closes read and write (read blocked, write read-only, host file unchanged) but has the same rename and not-yet-created gaps as bwrap.\n\n**Closed (run):** B1 for bwrap reads and writes in every workspace/`NEXUS_STATE_DIR` combination (workspace = HOME, parent of HOME, elsewhere, under HOME; state dir under HOME, in `/var/tmp`, symlinked, relative), both profiles and the worker launch. S1: `watch`, `status --replay --json`, `--dag` and `status` agree for a killed driver. S2: a real zombie reads gone in `processStartTicks` and `processRunning`. S3: a live foreign driver with no lock is refused (error names the pid, no unit runs); a recycled pid, other host or other boot pauses. S4: a symlinked-HOME real path is refused (including a new file), a hard link or symlink to a state file is refused, a legitimate multi-link file elsewhere is unaffected.\n**Suggestions:** the hard-link scan is not recursive (a hard link to a file in a state subdirectory passed as unprotected), and with 5,000 state files each file-tool check on a file with more than one link costs about 100 ms (`protectedBelow` calls it per entry; pnpm trees are heavily hard-linked): cache the state directory's inode set briefly and scan recursively. The TOCTOU (a link created after the check) is inherent. The zombie test raced once with `ENOENT` on `/proc/<pid>/stat` (`goal_driver_identity`, line ~276): make the setup wait for the child to be a zombie without reading a vanished entry.\n**False doc sentences:** `PA3_GOAL_LIFECYCLE.md` (\"A sandboxed command can neither read nor write it\") and the CHANGELOG (\"masked inside `--sandbox`\") are false for docker and for the rename and not-yet-created cases; `PA3_GOAL_LIFECYCLE.md` says Docker \"needs no mask unless the workspace contains the state directory\", false with workspace = HOME; this PR's manual line \"`--sandbox` hides the directory… even when the workspace is your home directory\" is false for the rename bypass; \"hard link refused\" omits state subdirectories.\n**Tests at the tip, 0 failures** except one flake: `goal_driver_identity` 15 (the zombie race above), `goal_pa3_completion` 7, `goal_lifecycle` 10, `goal_ledger_propagation` 2, `sandbox_confine` 21, `sandbox_profiles` 16, `sandbox_cancel` 2, `durable_continuity` 42, 19 `operation_*` files, `security` 14, `check_requirements` 28, `leak_guard` 6, `runner_examples` 1, `schedule_examples` 1; `tsc`, the complexity gate, invariants, doc versions pass. **Mutations, all caught:** general mask (7 failures), read-only mask (2), state dir out of the mask list (2), realpath protected entry (1), dev+ino check (1), Z/X handling (1), live-driver refusal (1). Not checked: a real drive end to end, docker with a not-yet-created directory, cancel and kill inside the mask, Node 22.\nEOF\ngh pr comment 809 --body-file /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/rev809.md | tail -1; echo \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ) REVIEW (claude-invariants-audit): #809 / PA-3 fixes on release: REQUEST CHANGES: mask covers only tasks/ (mv ~/.nexus works; forged goal file created), not-yet-created dir skipped, docker unmasked at tip (#809 adds tmpfs). Fixing on v1/pa3-completion. DO NOT MERGE #809.\" >> \"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log\"","description":"Post the PA-3 delta review on PR 809 and log it"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Tdoj7RDb52dj1tMncHdXZa","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"a6379c334af41ccf9","summary":"Close remaining PA-3 sandbox mask gaps","message":"Delta review of the PA-3 fixes: REQUEST CHANGES, comment on PR #809 (`gh pr view 809 --comments`, last). Your branch v1/pa3-completion (worktree /home/mike/nexus-wt/pa3f; PR #809 is open from it; release has your 4cd35eb92). `git fetch origin && git status`, merge origin/release/v1.3.0 (never rebase), plain `git push origin v1/pa3-completion` at the end (never force). Fix, each with a test that fails without it (mutate a copy, restore from it):\n1. Mask the whole STATE ROOT (`NEXUS_STATE_DIR` or `~/.nexus`, realpath'd), not just `tasks`: with workspace = HOME a sandboxed `mv ~/.nexus ~/.nexus.old` succeeded and a forged `tasks/goal-forged.json` was then created on the host. A tmpfs mount on the state root makes rename/replace fail (EBUSY); the root's other contents (logs, backups, flight records, `~/.nexus/backups`) become invisible in the sandbox: acceptable and intended; check nothing the sandboxed tools legitimately need lives there (run the sandbox_* tests and the examples). Do it in BOTH bwrap profiles, the sandboxed worker launch AND Docker (`--tmpfs` for the state root in the docker argv: #809 added a tasks mask for docker: extend it to the root).\n2. A state dir that does not exist at wrap time: create it (mode 0700, owner-only, recursive for the root) BEFORE wrapping so the mask always applies (today `realpathSync` throws and the mask is skipped, then a sandboxed command creates it on the host). Tests: workspace = HOME with an absent state dir: after the sandboxed command (`mkdir -p ~/.nexus/tasks && echo X > ...`) the HOST has no planted file; the directory is 0700.\n3. Tests for rename (`mv ~/.nexus ~/.nexus.old` fails inside the sandbox, host intact) and the not-yet-created case in the real-bwrap tests (skip as the existing sandbox_confine tests do when bwrap is unavailable); a docker argv test asserting the root mask (and, if a docker daemon is available as the reviewer's was, one real run behind the same skip logic the docker tests use).\n4. Hard-link scan: make it recursive over the state dir with a short-lived cache of the state dir's (dev,ino) set (e.g. 1-2 s TTL, invalidated by a stat stamp of the dir tree top-level mtimes is NOT sufficient: use TTL only and say so); the per-check cost with 5,000 state files and a multi-link file must be well under 10 ms amortised; the TOCTOU stays documented. Tests: hard link to a file in a state SUBDIRECTORY is refused; benchmark bound.\n5. `goal_driver_identity` zombie test races with ENOENT on /proc/<pid>/stat (line ~276): make the setup robust (poll for state Z with ENOENT tolerated, bounded timeout) and run it 20 times in a row.\n6. Docs: make every sentence true: `PA3_GOAL_LIFECYCLE.md` (what the sandbox hides: the state root in bwrap AND docker, created before wrapping; what it does not: an unsandboxed command, same-uid processes outside), CHANGELOG, the manual line, \"hard link refused\" (incl. subdirectories). Remove the false \"Docker needs no mask unless…\" sentence.\nRe-run: goal_driver_identity (20x for the zombie), goal_pa3_completion, goal_lifecycle, goal_ledger_propagation, sandbox_confine, sandbox_profiles, sandbox_cancel, sandbox_docker, sandbox_denial_events, every operation_* test, durable_continuity, runner_examples and schedule_examples (after `npm --prefix cli run build`), security, leak_guard, check_requirements; tsc; the complexity gate (exit code); check_invariants; check_doc_versions. Changed/new test files three times. Commit `fix(goal): <what>` + `Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>`; push. Report under 200 words with the commit hash."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
