{"parentUuid":"5099d318-6ffe-4445-8ccd-e4aa7b5269f8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNoNzB1R9WScG6dUq1pp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The delta review of the PA-3 fixes came back request changes. The review is posted on #809 and the PA-3 builder is closing the gaps. #809 stays unmerged. v1.3.0 is not landed. The merge to `main` and the release haven't started.\n\n**Closed, by running attacks with real bwrap and Docker:**\n- Plain reads and writes of the goal-state files under `--sandbox` in every workspace and state-directory combination, both bwrap profiles and the worker launch.\n- `watch` and `--replay` now show PAUSED for a killed driver.\n- A zombie driver reads as gone.\n- A live driver with no lock file is refused.\n- Hard links and a symlinked home are refused by the file tools.\n\n**Still open on the sandbox hole (three, all reproduced):**\n- The mask covers only the `tasks` subdirectory. With the workspace set to home, a sandboxed command renamed `~/.nexus` away and created a forged goal file on the host. The fix is to mask the whole state root, so it can't be renamed or replaced.\n- If the state directory doesn't exist when the sandbox starts, the mask is skipped and a sandboxed command creates it on the host. The fix is to create it first, with mode 0700.\n- Docker has no mask at all on the release branch. Docker read and wrote the host file. #809 adds a mask that blocks that, but it has the same rename and not-yet-created gaps, so the fix covers Docker too.\n\n**Also sent:**\n- The hard-link scan misses state subdirectories and costs about 100 ms per check with 5,000 state files, so it needs a recursive scan plus a short cache.\n- One zombie test flaked once and is being made robust, then run 20 times.\n- Several docs sentences are false (for example \"a sandboxed command can neither read nor write it\"), and the builder rewrites them to what holds.\n\nAll seven mutations the reviewer tried were caught.\n\nStill running: the re-review of the HK-3 fixes (#808) and the BG-3 firer builder. After those: the BG-3 firer review and merge, the readiness re-measure, version bump and changelog, release notes, and the real-server smoke runs on the final tip."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4064,"cache_read_input_tokens":503155,"output_tokens":718,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4064,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":718,"cache_read_input_tokens":503155,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4064,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4064},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011ChNoNyoSUBBy1dgnVaDxH","requestRef":"d6454163-67a8-4691-8774-0c00b3b88922","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"ceb79616-47ad-4d1a-89df-083d73e72327","timestamp":"2026-11-25T01:45:06.593Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"v1/bg3-trust-abuse-model","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
