{"parentUuid":"e72af80a-045e-4b3e-b5c5-55a9ca7e9908","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNpnkprhU3Ba4YpfKQGN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NGM4nNVjfYfeuBEeojrMPQ","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Delta re-review PR #809 sandbox root mask","subagent_type":"reviewer","prompt":"Short, time-boxed (about 25 minutes) independent delta re-review of GitHub PR #809 (PA-3 sandbox follow-ups) in ~/nexus-code, base `release/v1.3.0`. Take the full head SHA from `gh pr view 809 --json headRefOid` (expected to start `d2f3e4bb`), review exactly that, and say whether it moved or merged. My previous review is the PR comment \"Independent delta review of the PA-3 follow-up fixes … REQUEST CHANGES\" (`gh pr view 809 --comments`): the mask covered only the `tasks` dir (workspace = HOME: a sandboxed `mv ~/.nexus ~/.nexus.old` worked and a forged `tasks/goal-forged.json` was created on the host); a state dir not existing at wrap time was skipped (then created on the host by a sandboxed command); Docker had no mask; the hard-link scan was non-recursive and slow (100 ms per check with 5,000 files); a zombie-test flake; false docs. Fix commit `d2f3e4bb3` (`git show --stat`, diff) claims: the real state root (`NEXUS_STATE_DIR`, else `~/.nexus`, realpath'd) is masked in both bwrap profiles, the sandboxed worker launch and Docker; the root is created 0700 before wrapping; the hard-link check walks the state dir recursively against a 1.5 s (dev,ino) snapshot cache; the zombie test polls robustly; docs corrected.\nRe-run the ORIGINAL attacks by RUNNING (throwaway HOME, temp workspaces, no network, no inference; real bwrap if `bwrap --version` works; real docker only if a daemon is available and the existing docker tests use it): workspace = HOME, parent of HOME, elsewhere, workspace inside the state root; `NEXUS_STATE_DIR` unset/under HOME/`/var/tmp`/symlink/relative/with spaces and quotes/`..`-named; a sandboxed command tries: `mv ~/.nexus ~/.nexus.old`, `ln -s`, `mkdir`, `rmdir`, `rm -rf`, `touch`, write/read/list under `tasks/`, `backups/`, flight records, any file in the root, rename of the PARENT of the root, `mount --bind`/`umount` attempts (is `CAP_SYS_ADMIN` dropped?), `/proc/self/root`/`/proc/1/root` escapes to the host path, and creating the state dir first when absent: the host stays unchanged in every case and the root is 0700. What now becomes invisible inside the sandbox (logs, backups, flight records, task stores): does anything a sandboxed tool legitimately needs live under the state root (the verify service, the sandboxed worker's own state, `run_tests`, `nexus verify --sandbox`, `nexus job` unattended jobs which run workers in sandboxes, the TUI bridge, bwrap read-only profile, LSP servers, MCP stdio servers launched inside the sandbox)? Run the sandbox-using tests and examples to catch regressions (`sandbox_*`, `verify_sandbox`, `verify_command`, `mcp_verify`, `runner_examples`/`schedule_examples` after `npm --prefix cli run build`, `lsp*`, any test that sets `NEXUS_STATE_DIR` and sandboxes). Mask-when-the-root-is-the-workspace and mask-when-workspace-is-under-the-root cases: does the sandboxed command still see the workspace (it must! a workspace under `~/.nexus/worktrees` for unattended jobs is a REAL case: operations isolate under `<repo>/.nexus/worktrees` and the runner may keep job worktrees under the state root: check where BG-1 jobs' fresh worktrees live; if they live under the state root the mask would hide the job's own workspace: test an unattended job end to end with the sandbox on). Docker: argv has the root mask; `--tmpfs` semantics with the workspace bind. The hard-link check: recursive walk, snapshot TTL 1.5 s, cost with 5,000 state files, a hard link created inside the TTL window (documented gap), symlinked state dir, the cache not shared across different state roots (two roots in one process: tests with NEXUS_STATE_DIR changes). Docs: every sentence in `PA3_GOAL_LIFECYCLE.md`, the manual, the CHANGELOG about the sandbox and hard links vs code.\nRun at head, one at a time: `goal_driver_identity` (the zombie test 10 times in a row), `goal_pa3_completion`, `goal_lifecycle`, `goal_ledger_propagation`, `sandbox_confine`, `sandbox_profiles`, `sandbox_cancel`, `sandbox_docker`, `sandbox_denial_events` (use `TMPDIR=/dev/shm`; a stray `/tmp/.git` makes it fail with the default TMPDIR: known host state), `verify_sandbox`, every `operation_*` test, `durable_continuity`, `security`, `leak_guard`, `check_requirements`, `runner_examples`, `schedule_examples`; `cd cli && npx tsc --noEmit -p .`; the complexity gate (exit code); `node scripts/check_invariants.mjs`; `node scripts/check_doc_versions.mjs`. Mutations (copy aside, restore from the copy, never `git checkout`): mask only `tasks`; skip the pre-create; drop the docker mask; make the walk non-recursive; each must fail a test.\nRules: do NOT edit ~/nexus-code or existing worktrees. `git -C ~/nexus-code fetch origin && git -C ~/nexus-code worktree add --detach ~/nexus-wt/rev809b <full sha>`; `cp -a ~/nexus-code/cli/node_modules ~/nexus-wt/rev809b/cli/`; `mkdir -p ~/nexus-wt/rev809b/core/target/release && cp ~/nexus-wt/ls1b/core/target/release/{harness-core,nexus-tui} ~/nexus-wt/rev809b/core/target/release/`. Tests: `cd ~/nexus-wt/rev809b/cli && TMPDIR=/dev/shm HOME=$(mktemp -d) node --import tsx --test test/<name>.test.ts 2>&1 | tail -20`. Never touch the real ~/.nexus, ~/.config/nexus, /etc/nexus. Stop processes by their own pid; never `pkill -f`; never delete anything outside your own temp dirs (no glob deletes). No commits, pushes or GitHub comments. Remove probes and the worktree at the end. Shell is zsh (`bash -c` for loops); prefix `rtk proxy` if output looks filtered; a safety check blocks scripts containing `rm`.\nReport under 400 words: verdict (ACCEPT / ACCEPT WITH FOLLOW-UPS / REQUEST CHANGES) at the exact SHA; each earlier blocker closed or not with the attack run; regressions found for sandboxed tools/jobs that legitimately use the state root (blocking if a normal sandboxed workflow breaks); new findings with file:line, blocking or not (a sandboxed command reading, writing, renaming or creating goal state on the host is blocking); test counts; mutation results; what you did not check."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1948,"cache_read_input_tokens":507219,"output_tokens":2697,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":50},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1948,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":2697,"cache_read_input_tokens":507219,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1948,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1948},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":16097,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01NGM4nNVjfYfeuBEeojrMPQ":{"description":"Delta re-review PR #809 sandbox root mask","subagent_type":"reviewer","prompt":"Short, time-boxed (about 25 minutes) independent delta re-review of GitHub PR #809 (PA-3 sandbox follow-ups) in ~/nexus-code, base `release/v1.3.0`. Take the full head SHA from `gh pr view 809 --json headRefOid` (expected to start `d2f3e4bb`), review exactly that, and say whether it moved or merged. My previous review is the PR comment \"Independent delta review of the PA-3 follow-up fixes … REQUEST CHANGES\" (`gh pr view 809 --comments`): the mask covered only the `tasks` dir (workspace = HOME: a sandboxed `mv ~/.nexus ~/.nexus.old` worked and a forged `tasks/goal-forged.json` was created on the host); a state dir not existing at wrap time was skippe