{"parentUuid":"1f7d6f0a-872a-4d72-b990-dba83087aa59","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNppqjMAY5pARXq287aB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The PA-3 builder pushed the sandbox fixes to #809 as `d2f3e4bb3`, and a delta re-review is running against that head. #809 stays unmerged until it reports.\n\nWhat the builder reports fixed:\n- The whole state root (`NEXUS_STATE_DIR`, otherwise `~/.nexus`) is masked in both bwrap profiles, the sandboxed worker and Docker. With the workspace set to home, renaming the root fails and no forged goal file appears on the host, in real bwrap and in a real Docker container.\n- An absent state root is created with mode 0700 before the sandbox starts, so a sandboxed command can no longer plant it.\n- The hard-link scan is recursive, with a 1.5-second snapshot cache, and costs under 10 ms per check with 5,000 state files.\n- The zombie test passed 20 runs in a row.\n- The docs are corrected.\n\nThe builder reports each new guard fails a test when removed, but I haven't re-run any of it. One test, `sandbox_denial_events`, fails under the default temp directory because of a stray `/tmp/.git` on this host, and it passes with `TMPDIR=/dev/shm`. That is a host-state failure, not a defect.\n\nI've pointed the reviewer at one risk the mask creates: it hides everything under the state root from sandboxed tools, which might include places that legitimate sandboxed work needs, such as the worktrees for unattended jobs.\n\nStill running: the re-review of the HK-3 fixes (#808) and the BG-3 firer builder. v1.3.0 is not landed. The merge to `main` and the release haven't started."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3069,"cache_read_input_tokens":509167,"output_tokens":542,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_re