{"parentUuid":"8ff03120-5d15-4000-afae-b82f0e930b78","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNqWnorPVhUTw7DFbDto","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NvzSmpNJGdvFAXzfJXy6nC","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-code && git fetch -q origin; d=\"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims\"; echo \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ) NOTE (claude-invariants-audit): #808 HK-3 was MERGED (39d796fa, 01:29Z) BEFORE its review fixes 7ca90de26/f375865e (committed 01:31-01:32) reached it: fifth PR merged ahead of an announced fix this session. The reviewer's verdict on the fixed head is ACCEPT WITH FOLLOW-UPS; I am opening the PR for the fix branch v1/hk3-followups now (the workspace=HOME agent-written operator plugin blocker is STILL OPEN on release until it merges). Merging order request: for PRs whose latest comment announces a fix in progress, please wait for the fix push.\" >> $d/nexus-claims.log; git diff --stat origin/release/v1.3.0...origin/v1/hk3-followups | tail -3; cat > /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/pr_hk3g.md <<'EOF'\nReview fixes for #808 (HK-3 completion), which merged at `39d796fad` before these commits reached it. Hostile review of #808 at `622c07fb` (REQUEST CHANGES, one blocker) and the re-review of this fix at `f375865e` (ACCEPT WITH FOLLOW-UPS) are on #808.\n\n- **Blocker closed:** with the workspace = HOME (or containing the operator dirs), an agent-written `~/.nexus/plugins/x.mjs` or `~/.config/nexus/plugins/x.mjs` loaded as operator code with no approval. Operator plugin directories inside the workspace are now skipped by real-path containment (`operatorDirInWorkspace`, `plugins.ts`) with a one-time notice, and both are absolute protected paths for the file tools (`security.ts`); the false sentence in `docs/PLUGINS.md` is corrected.\n- **Escape injection:** one helper (`core/printable.ts`) escapes control, bidi and formatting characters and caps length; applied in loader and registry notices, `plugins trust`, `plugins list` and the doctor finding.\n- **Tree walk:** manifest plugin trees capped at 64 files, 256 directories, 8 levels, 8 MiB, with a stat-stamp cache (50,000 empty directories refused in ~35 ms; 100 cached inspections ~47 ms).\n- **Louder notice** when a hook or manifest plugin is made inactive by an edit (limit documented); the trust store is written under an `O_EXCL` lock naming pid and start time (four concurrent writers lose nothing).\n\nOpen follow-ups from the re-review (non-blocking, tracked for the next commit): `doctor.ts` `plugins.config`, `index.ts:1168` (`plugins revoke`) and the HK-2 install/verify/list-installed output print names unescaped; `printableRefusal` handles C0/C1 but not bidi, `printable` omits U+FFF9–FFFB and the U+E0000 tags; a symlinked HOME with absent dirs lets the real-path spelling be written (the loader still skips them); a changed JS plugin file gets only the generic pending notice; `plugins list`/doctor do not mention skipped operator dirs; the lock's stale takeover is not atomic.\n\nTests: `plugin_review_fixes` 7 (22 mutations killed); 34 files, 452 tests pass in the re-review; `tsc`, the complexity gate, invariants, doc versions and the schema `--check` generators pass.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\nEOF\nu=$(gh pr create --base release/v1.3.0 --head v1/hk3-followups --title \"fix(plugins): HK-3 review fixes: operator plugin dirs in the workspace, escaping, tree caps, store lock\" --body-file /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/pr_hk3g.md | tail -1); echo \"$u\"; echo \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ) PR (claude-invariants-audit): $u HK-3 review fixes (reviewed ACCEPT WITH FOLLOW-UPS at f375865e); merging after checks.\" >> $d/nexus-claims.log","description":"Log the out-of-order HK-3 merge and open a PR for the fix branch"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container"