{"parentUuid":"1f4a0b97-437f-408c-9dcb-2f8776764142","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNqZcnv2F7vpxEgsuSZ7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The HK-3 review fixes are merged into `release/v1.3.0` as `17b891b6`, through #810. That PR was already open from the same branch, so I didn't create another. Required checks were green at the exact head, release CI was green at the tip first, and I read the merged state back. The re-review accepted these fixes (`f375865e`) with follow-ups.\n\nThis closes the open blocker: with the workspace set to home, an agent-written operator plugin could load as operator code with no approval. #808 had merged at 01:29 before these fixes reached it, which is the fifth time this session a PR merged ahead of an announced fix. I logged that and asked other agents to wait when a PR's latest comment says a fix is coming. Release CI on the new merge is not yet confirmed.\n\n**Follow-ups from the re-review, to go in the next commit:**\n- A few print sites still output plugin names unescaped: the doctor plugin check, `plugins revoke`, and the HK-2 install and verify output.\n- The escape helper misses bidi override characters and a few other format characters.\n- A symlinked home with the plugin directories absent lets the real-path spelling be written; the loader still skips them.\n- A changed JS plugin file gets only the generic pending notice, without the louder one.\n- `plugins list` and doctor don't mention skipped operator directories.\n- The lock's stale-takeover isn't atomic. This did not reproduce in 12 rounds of 8 writers.\n\nThree mutations survived the review: the unescaped `plugins list` call, the unescaped project-hooks notice and the root-directory-only ctime stamp.\n\n**Still running:** the re-review of the PA-3 sandbox fixes (#809) and the BG-3 firer builder. v1.3.0 is not landed. The merge to `main` and the release haven't started."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":908,"cache_read_input_tokens":517341,"output_tokens":593,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":908,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":593,"cache_read_input_tokens":517341,"cache_creation_input_tokens":908,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":908},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011ChNqZccWj9zkW4eRraABw","requestRef":"6822177a-f50b-44d0-b891-82e11fb828ef","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"a6581dcb-1d1c-45f1-ba9e-d5cdbeea75c4","timestamp":"2026-11-25T02:13:43.589Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"v1/bg3-trust-abuse-model","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
