{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-11-25T02:24:30.685Z","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>ac985d7a18cac0481</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01NGM4nNVjfYfeuBEeojrMPQ</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666/tasks/ac985d7a18cac0481.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Delta re-review PR #809 sandbox root mask\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>### Verdict: REQUEST CHANGES\n\n**The head moved and merged, and the fix was not in the merge.** `gh pr view 809` shows head `7e81557ba` (not `d2f3e4bb3`), state MERGED at 01:46Z, merge commit `7fc645899`. `7e81557ba` was committed at 01:35Z. `d2f3e4bb3` was committed at 01:49Z, three minutes after the merge. It is on `origin/v1/pa3-completion` only and is not an ancestor of `release/v1.3.0`.\n\n`release/v1.3.0` therefore still has `directoriesToHide` masking only `defaultTaskStateDir()`. That is my original blocker 1, plus the non-recursive hard-link scan. I did not re-run the attacks on `7e81557ba`. I reviewed the unmerged `d2f3e4bb3` (worktree `~/nexus-wt/rev809b`, now removed). It needs a new PR to `release/v1.3.0`.\n\n**Earlier blockers at `d2f3e4bb3` (bwrap; the Docker tests ran, but I ran no Docker attack):**\n- **Closed:**\n  - `mv ~/.nexus ~/.nexus.old` fails with \"busy\" when the workspace is HOME.\n  - A forged `goal-forged.json` lands in the tmpfs, and the host is unchanged.\n  - An absent root is created 0700 before wrapping.\n  - Workspace elsewhere with the root unset, under HOME, in `/var/tmp`, with spaces and quotes, or `..`-named: host unchanged.\n  - `rm`, `rmdir`, `touch`, writes, `mount --bind` and `umount`, and `/proc/self/root` and `/proc/1/root`: host unchanged. (My tmpfs-scoped `ln -s` rc=0 never reached the host.)\n- **Not closed, new blockers (a sandboxed command forges host goal state):**\n  1. **Parent rename.** Workspace = parent of HOME: `mv ~ ~-x &amp;&amp; mkdir -p ~/.nexus/tasks &amp;&amp; echo FORGED &gt; ~/.nexus/tasks/goal-forged.json` succeeds, and the forged file is on the host. Workspace = HOME with `NEXUS_STATE_DIR=$HOME/a/st`: `mv ~/a ~/a.old` followed by the same forge also succeeds. Fix: mask or bind-protect every ancestor of the root that lies inside the workspace, or refuse to wrap when the root has a renamable ancestor.\n  2. **Symlinked root.** `NEXUS_STATE_DIR=$HOME/lnk -&gt; $HOME/real` masks only `real`. `mv lnk lnk.old` and `rm -rf lnk` change the host. `sandbox.ts:39-47` masks the realpath, not the configured name. Fix: also mask or lock the unresolved name.\n- **Inside the root (`NEXUS_STATE_DIR` or `~/.nexus`):** a workspace there makes bwrap fail with \"Can't chdir ... No such file\", because the mask hides the workspace. This is fail-closed, not a leak. BG-1 worktrees live at `&lt;repo&gt;/.nexus/worktrees` (`worktree.ts:119`), so the case arises only when the repo is `$HOME`. I did not run an unattended job end to end.\n- **Hard-link scan:** recursion is covered by a test, and the code is simple, but I did not time it with 5,000 files. The 1.5 s snapshot is cached per directory, so a second root rebuilds it. The doc discloses the time-of-check gap.\n\n**Regressions for legitimate sandboxed tools:** none found. The `lsp_*` tests (except `lsp_real_servers`), `verify_sandbox`, `verify_command`, `mcp_verify`, `runner_examples` and `schedule_examples` all pass.\n\n**Tests:** all passed.\n- `goal_*`: 8, 10 and 2 in `goal_pa3_completion`, `goal_lifecycle` and `goal_ledger_propagation`. `goal_driver_identity`: 15.\n- `sandbox_confine`: 22. `sandbox_profiles`: 16. `sandbox_cancel`: 2. `sandbox_docker`: 14. `sandbox_denial_events`: 6. `verify_sandbox`: 10.\n- `durable_continuity`: 42. `security`: 14. `leak_guard`: 6. `check_requirements`: 28.\n- Every `operation_*` test: no failures.\n- `tsc`, the complexity gate, `check_invariants` and `check_doc_versions` all exited 0.\n- The zombie test (run alone with `--test-name-pattern`, 10 times): I counted only 8 pass lines in the captured output, with no failures.\n\n**Mutations (all caught):**\n- Mask only `tasks`: 2 `sandbox_confine` and 2 `sandbox_docker` tests fail.\n- Skip the pre-create: 1 `sandbox_confine` and 1 `sandbox_docker` test fail.\n- Non-recursive walk: 1 `goal_pa3_completion` test fails.\n- Drop the Docker mask: 6 Docker tests fail. This sed also removed the overlay `--tmpfs`, so it was broader than the intended mutation.\n\n**Docs:** `PA3_GOAL_LIFECYCLE.md`, the manual and the CHANGELOG say a sandboxed command cannot rename the root \"even when the workspace is $HOME\". That is false for parent-of-HOME and nested or symlinked roots. The earlier docs on `7e81557ba` say Docker needs no mask.\n\n**Not checked:**\n- A real-Docker attack run.\n- The unattended-job end-to-end run.\n- The hard-link timing.\n- The sandboxed worker's own state, and the TUI bridge.\n- `lsp_real_servers`.\n\nI left throwaway `/dev/shm` temp dirs (`h.*`, `th.*`) because I was told not to glob-delete.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>60210</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>28</tool_uses><duration_ms>1232666</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
