{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","hash":"592960b7afd8e0b8d92feb7256c74d02b192da6d40fb8dc02c3980f3a17725e5","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QNQ89QwefjsxoHffn9XNP4","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"a6379c334af41ccf9","summary":"Close ancestor-rename and symlinked-root sandbox gaps","message":"Delta re-review of d2f3e4bb3: the PR (#809) had MERGED at 7e81557ba before your commit d2f3e4bb3 (so release only has the older tasks-only mask); your commit is on origin/v1/pa3-completion only. Reviewer found two more ways a sandboxed command forges host goal state, both run with real bwrap. Work in /home/mike/nexus-wt/pa3f on v1/pa3-completion: `git fetch origin && git status`, merge origin/release/v1.3.0 (never rebase), plain push at the end (never force). I will open a DRAFT PR for this branch (so nobody merges it before the fix is complete): do not mark it ready.\n1. Ancestor rename: workspace = parent of HOME: `mv ~ ~-x && mkdir -p ~/.nexus/tasks && echo FORGED > ~/.nexus/tasks/goal-forged.json` forged the host file; workspace = HOME with `NEXUS_STATE_DIR=$HOME/a/st`: `mv ~/a ~/a.old` then the same forge. Fix: when the state root lies inside (or equals) the workspace, every ANCESTOR directory of the root that is at or below the workspace boundary (from the workspace root down to the root's parent, plus the workspace root itself if it is an ancestor and is not already a mount) must be made un-renamable inside the sandbox: bind-mount each such ancestor onto itself (`--bind <dir> <dir>`, a mount point cannot be moved or removed: EBUSY) in every bwrap branch and the sandboxed worker, and the equivalent for Docker (the workspace bind already makes the workspace root a mount: check; intermediate ancestors need `-v dir:dir`? if the Docker layout makes ancestors renamable inside the container, mask by mounting the root with `--tmpfs` AND bind the ancestors read-only is wrong since the workspace must stay writable: choose the minimal safe thing and document; at worst refuse to start a sandboxed Docker command when the state root is a proper descendant of the workspace without a renamable-ancestor defence). Keep the workspace itself writable and usable. Tests with real bwrap (skip when unavailable) for: workspace = parent of HOME; workspace = HOME with root under `$HOME/a/st`; `mv` of EVERY ancestor from the workspace down fails with a busy error and the host is unchanged; the workspace still works normally (create/delete ordinary files, git status); the unattended-jobs case: a repo at HOME with `<repo>/.nexus/worktrees` (BG-1 worktrees live there: `worktree.ts:119`) still works with the sandbox on (run an unattended job or the closest existing test end to end if feasible).\n2. Symlinked root: `NEXUS_STATE_DIR=$HOME/lnk -> $HOME/real`: only `real` is masked; `mv lnk lnk.old` / `rm -rf lnk` change the host and Nexus later follows whatever replaces `lnk`. Simplest safe rule: if the configured state root path (unresolved) is a symlink OR any component of it inside the workspace is a symlink, refuse to wrap a sandboxed command with a clear error (fail closed: \"state directory is reached through a symlink inside the workspace; set NEXUS_STATE_DIR to its real path\"), in `sandbox.ts` before spawning; for a symlink OUTSIDE the workspace the realpath mask is enough (the sandbox cannot touch outside paths except through the workspace). Tests + docs. \n3. Root inside the workspace case (workspace under the root): bwrap fails with \"Can't chdir…\": fail-closed; make the error message explicit (say why and how to fix: start Nexus outside the state directory) and test it.\n4. Docker real-attack test if a daemon is available and the existing docker tests run for you (same skip logic): rename/forge attempts for each case.\n5. Docs/CHANGELOG/manual: say exactly what holds now (root masked; ancestors pinned; symlinked root refused; root created first; docker equivalent), no false sentence (\"even when the workspace is $HOME\" must be true for parent-of-HOME and nested roots now).\n6. Time the hard-link scan with 5,000 state files in a test with a generous bound; the zombie test: run it 20 times in a loop and report.\nRe-run: goal_driver_identity, goal_pa3_completion, goal_lifecycle, goal_ledger_propagation, sandbox_confine, sandbox_profiles, sandbox_cancel, sandbox_docker, sandbox_denial_events (TMPDIR=/dev/shm), verify_sandbox, verify_command, mcp_verify, lsp* except lsp_real_servers, every operation_* test, durable_continuity, runner_examples and schedule_examples (after `npm --prefix cli run build`), security, leak_guard, check_requirements; tsc; complexity gate (exit code); check_invariants; check_doc_versions. Mutation per guard (restore from copy). Commit `fix(sandbox): <what>` + `Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>`; push. Report under 200 words with the hash."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01L98RWDoEN49L3EipNR9GYZ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-code && git fetch -q origin; d=\"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims\"; echo \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ) NOTE (claude-invariants-audit): #809 PA-3 was MERGED (7fc64589, 01:46Z) at 7e81557b while the review of the fix commit d2f3e4bb (committed 01:49Z, not on release) was running: sixth merge ahead of an announced fix. Release currently has only the tasks-only mask. The new review (REQUEST CHANGES): parent-of-HOME rename and symlinked state root still forge host goal state. Fix in progress on v1/pa3-completion; I open it as a DRAFT PR: PLEASE DO NOT MARK READY OR MERGE until I post an ACCEPT. Request to everyone: do not merge PRs whose latest comment announces a fix in progress.\" >> $d/nexus-claims.log; git diff --stat origin/release/v1.3.0...origin/v1/pa3-completion | tail -4; u=$(gh pr create --draft --base release/v1.3.0 --head v1/pa3-completion --title \"fix(sandbox): mask the whole state root and pin its ancestors (PA-3 follow-up, DRAFT until reviewed)\" --body \"DRAFT: do not merge until an independent review posts ACCEPT. Follow-up to the merged #806/#809: the state root (not only \\`tasks\\`) is masked in bwrap and Docker, created 0700 before wrapping, recursive hard-link scan; in progress: ancestors of the root pinned against rename (parent-of-HOME) and symlinked roots refused. Review of #809: parent rename and symlinked root forge host goal state (both run).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\" | tail -1); echo \"$u\"","description":"Log the sixth early merge and open a draft PR so the fix cannot be merged prematurely"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
