{"parentUuid":"44d45705-de18-4095-ac52-baa63cf142fd","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNrSE9pDzuA6KgWio5L8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The PA-3 sandbox fix was merged ahead of its follow-up again. #809 merged as `7fc645899` three minutes before the builder's fix commit (`d2f3e4bb3`) landed. That is the sixth time this session a PR merged ahead of an announced fix. `release/v1.3.0` currently has only the older mask that covers the `tasks` subdirectory.\n\nThe independent re-review of the unmerged fix found it closes most of the original attack: renaming `~/.nexus`, a forged goal file, the absent-root plant, the whole-root mask in bwrap and Docker, and the hard-link scan. It also found two ways a sandboxed command still forges host goal state:\n- **Ancestor rename:** with the workspace set to the parent of home, `mv ~ ~-x` followed by `mkdir -p ~/.nexus/tasks` and a write plants a forged goal file on the host. The same works for a state root nested under the workspace.\n- **Symlinked root:** with `NEXUS_STATE_DIR` pointing through a symlink, only the real target is masked. `mv` or `rm -rf` of the symlink changes the host.\n\nI sent the builder fixes for both, plus:\n- Pinning every ancestor of the root inside the workspace (bind-mounted so it can't be moved).\n- Refusing a symlinked root inside the workspace.\n- A clearer error when the workspace sits under the root.\n- A real Docker attack run, if a daemon is available.\n- Docs and a 20-run zombie-test loop.\n\nThe reviewer found no regressions for legitimate sandboxed tools such as LSP, verify and the runner examples.\n\nTo stop another premature merge I opened this fix as a draft PR (#811) and logged that nobody should mark it ready or merge it until I post an accept. I used a draft because other sessions keep merging PRs as soon as checks go green.\n\nStill running: the BG-3 firer builder and the sandbox fix. v1.3.0 is not landed. The merge to `main` and the release haven't started."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3968,"cache_read_input_tokens":521414,"output_tokens":671,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3968,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":671,"cache_read_input_tokens":521414,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3968,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3968},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011ChNrSDwutPpn88VQcNVs7","requestRef":"19ca2094-a359-4e44-9415-0773e87e7798","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"19b4d6a3-4efb-4da5-a196-598cd14f8ef8","timestamp":"2026-11-25T02:25:10.978Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"v1/bg3-trust-abuse-model","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
