{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-11-25T02:45:19.246Z","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a6379c334af41ccf9</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01QNQ89QwefjsxoHffn9XNP4</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666/tasks/a6379c334af41ccf9.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Complete PA-3 goal semantics\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>All six points are done and pushed as `cf696b5ca` on `v1/pa3-completion`. I did not touch the draft PR or mark anything ready.\n\n- **Ancestors (item 1):** when the state root lies inside the workspace, every directory between them is bound onto itself (`--bind` in bwrap, a nested `-v` in Docker), so none can be renamed away. Real-bwrap and real-Docker tests cover root = `$HOME/a/b/st`: all three `mv` calls fail with a busy error, the host is unchanged, and ordinary file work and `git status` still work. My parent-of-HOME test also passes without the pins, so it does not by itself show the pin matters. I did not reproduce the reviewer's rename of HOME in that case.\n- **Symlinks (item 2):** a state path through a symlink inside the workspace is refused with \"set NEXUS_STATE_DIR to its real path\". A symlink outside the workspace is covered by the realpath mask (tested).\n- **Workspace inside the root (item 3):** a workspace that is the state root, or inside `tasks/`, is refused with an explicit message. I deliberately did not refuse a workspace elsewhere under the root. That is the BG-1 case (repo at `$HOME`, job worktree at `&lt;repo&gt;/.nexus/worktrees/&lt;job&gt;`). It now works under the sandbox, and a test shows `tasks/` is unreachable and the root cannot be renamed. I ran no end-to-end unattended job for it.\n- **Docker (item 4):** real-container tests for parent-of-HOME, nested ancestors and the symlink refusal pass.\n- **Docs (item 5):** `PA3_GOAL_LIFECYCLE.md`, the manual and the CHANGELOG say what holds.\n- **Item 6:** the hard-link timing test is unchanged and passes. The zombie test passed 20 of 20 runs.\n\nRemoving each guard failed a test: bwrap pins, Docker pins, symlink refusal, and workspace-in-tasks refusal.\n\nAll the suites you listed pass. `tsc`, the complexity gate (exit 0), `check_invariants` and `check_doc_versions` are clean. The changed test files passed three times. `sandbox_denial_events` passes only under `TMPDIR=/dev/shm`, because of the stray `/tmp/.git` on this host.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>346663</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>23</tool_uses><duration_ms>1223485</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
