tate path through a symlink inside the workspace is refused with \"set NEXUS_STATE_DIR to its real path\". A symlink outside the workspace is covered by the realpath mask (tested).\n- **Workspace inside the root (item 3):** a workspace that is the state root, or inside `tasks/`, is refused with an explicit message. I deliberately did not refuse a workspace elsewhere under the root. That is the BG-1 case (repo at `$HOME`, job worktree at `&lt;repo&gt;/.nexus/worktrees/&lt;job&gt;`). It now works under the sandbox, and a test shows `tasks/` is unreachable and the root cannot be renamed. I ran no end-to-end unattended job for it.\n- **Docker (item 4):** real-container tests for parent-of-HOME, nested ancestors and the symlink refusal pass.\n- **Docs (item 5):** `PA3_GOAL_LIFECYCLE.md`, the manual and the CHANGELOG say what holds.\n- **Item 6:** the hard-link timing test is unchanged and passes. The zombie test passed 20 of 20 runs.\n\nRemoving each guard failed a test: bwrap pins, Docker pins, symlink refusal, and workspace-in-tasks refusal.\n\nAll the suites you listed pass. `tsc`, the complexity gate (exit 0), `check_invariants` and `check_doc_versions` are clean. The changed test files passed three times. `sandbox_denial_events` passes only under `TMPDIR=/dev/shm`, because of the stray `/tmp/.git` on this host.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>346663</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>23</tool_uses><duration_ms>1223485</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>\n</system-reminder>"}]}}
