{"parentUuid":"f8c8ec54-b4e1-4d9c-bba6-1eacde243c08","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNszXzNa9ay6kfxn5rHU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014EqgCooKN2k7yNvucHjvTP","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Re-review PR #811 sandbox ancestors","subagent_type":"reviewer","prompt":"Short, time-boxed (about 25 minutes) independent re-review of GitHub PR #811 (DRAFT; PA-3 sandbox follow-up) in ~/nexus-code, base `release/v1.3.0`. Take the full head SHA from `gh pr view 811 --json headRefOid` (expected to start `cf696b5c`), review exactly that, and say whether it moved. The previous review of the same work is on #809 (`gh pr view 809 --comments`, \"Independent delta re-review … REQUEST CHANGES\"): real-bwrap attacks that still forged host goal state: (1) workspace = PARENT OF HOME: `mv ~ ~-x && mkdir -p ~/.nexus/tasks && echo FORGED > ~/.nexus/tasks/goal-forged.json` succeeded and the forged file landed on the host; (2) workspace = HOME with `NEXUS_STATE_DIR=$HOME/a/st`: `mv ~/a ~/a.old` then the same forge; (3) `NEXUS_STATE_DIR=$HOME/lnk -> $HOME/real`: only `real` was masked, `mv lnk lnk.old` / `rm -rf lnk` changed the host. The builder's fix commit `cf696b5ca` (diff against `7fc645899` = current release tip: `git diff 7fc645899 cf696b5ca`; `git show --stat`) claims: when the state root lies inside the workspace every directory between them is bound onto itself (`--bind` in bwrap, nested `-v` in Docker) so it cannot be renamed; a state path through a symlink inside the workspace is refused (\"set NEXUS_STATE_DIR to its real path\"); a workspace that is the state root or inside `tasks/` is refused with an explicit message; a workspace elsewhere under the root (BG-1 case: repo at `$HOME`, job worktrees at `<repo>/.nexus/worktrees/<job>`) still works. IMPORTANT: the builder says its parent-of-HOME test passes even WITHOUT the pins and that it did not reproduce your rename of HOME in that case. Reproduce case (1) EXACTLY as above first on release tip `7fc645899` (it must forge) and then on `cf696b5ca` (it must NOT: the host file must not exist, `mv ~ ~-x` must fail): if HOME itself (an ancestor ABOVE the root, inside the workspace = its parent, and not a mount point) can still be renamed, that is BLOCKING: the fix must also pin the workspace-root-to-root chain INCLUDING directories between the workspace root and the state root's parent where the workspace root is a proper ancestor of HOME (e.g. `/home`), i.e. every ancestor of the state root that lies at or below the workspace root. Check each ancestor really is a mount point inside the sandbox (`findmnt`/`/proc/self/mountinfo`), and that renames of EVERY ancestor and of the root fail with EBUSY. Also try: workspace = `/` subtree oddities, workspace = HOME with the default root `~/.nexus`; `NEXUS_STATE_DIR` relative, with `..`, with trailing slashes, with a symlinked ANCESTOR (not the leaf) inside the workspace, a symlink OUTSIDE the workspace, a root that does not exist yet (created 0700 first), bind-mount count limits (deep roots, 20 ancestors), the read-only bwrap profile, the sandboxed worker launch, and Docker (run for real if a daemon is available and the existing docker tests run: same cases). Verify the ordinary sandboxed workflow still works in each configuration (create/delete/rename ordinary files in the workspace, `git status`, `git commit`, `npm`-like writes, running `nexus verify --sandbox` or `verify_sandbox` tests) and that the unattended BG-1 case works (a repo at HOME with `<repo>/.nexus/worktrees/<job>`: run an unattended job end to end with the scripted gateway and the sandbox on if feasible, otherwise the closest existing test). Check the docs (`PA3_GOAL_LIFECYCLE.md`, manual, CHANGELOG) against the behaviour: every sentence true.\nRun, one at a time, at the head: `sandbox_confine`, `sandbox_profiles`, `sandbox_cancel`, `sandbox_docker`, `sandbox_denial_events` (use `TMPDIR=/dev/shm`), `verify_sandbox`, `verify_command`, `mcp_verify`, `goal_driver_identity`, `goal_pa3_completion`, `goal_lifecycle`, `goal_ledger_propagation`, every `operation_*` test, `durable_continuity`, `runner_examples`, `schedule_examples` (after `npm --prefix cli run build` in the review worktree), `security`, `leak_guard`, `check_requirements`; `cd cli && npx tsc --noEmit -p .`; the complexity gate (check the exit code); `node scripts/check_invariants.mjs`; `node scripts/check_doc_versions.mjs`. Mutations (copy aside, restore from the copy, never `git checkout`): drop the ancestor pins in bwrap; drop them in Docker; drop the symlink refusal; drop the workspace-in-tasks refusal: each must fail a test; and a test that shows the pin MATTERS (fails without pins) for the parent-of-HOME case: if none exists, say so.\nRules: do NOT edit ~/nexus-code or existing worktrees. `git -C ~/nexus-code fetch origin && git -C ~/nexus-code worktree add --detach ~/nexus-wt/rev811 <full sha>`; `cp -a ~/nexus-code/cli/node_modules ~/nexus-wt/rev811/cli/`; `mkdir -p ~/nexus-wt/rev811/core/target/release && cp ~/nexus-wt/ls1b/core/target/release/{harness-core,nexus-tui} ~/nexus-wt/rev811/core/target/release/`. Tests: `cd ~/nexus-wt/rev811/cli && TMPDIR=/dev/shm HOME=$(mktemp -d) node --import tsx --test test/<name>.test.ts 2>&1 | tail -20`. Use a throwaway HOME for every probe; never touch the real ~/.nexus, ~/.config/nexus, /etc/nexus; probes that rename \"HOME\" must rename a THROWAWAY home inside a temp dir, never your real home. Stop processes by their own pid; never `pkill -f`; never delete anything outside your own temp dirs (no glob deletes). No commits, pushes or GitHub comments. Remove probes and the worktree at the end. Shell is zsh (`bash -c` for loops); prefix `rtk proxy` if output looks filtered; a safety check blocks scripts containing `rm`.\nReport under 400 words: verdict (ACCEPT / ACCEPT WITH FOLLOW-UPS / REQUEST CHANGES) at the exact SHA; attacks (1), (2), (3) each reproduced on the release tip and closed or not on the head; whether the tests prove the pins matter; regressions for legitimate sandboxed workflows and the unattended BG-1 case; new findings with file:line, blocking or not (a sandboxed command renaming/replacing/creating goal state on the host is blocking; a normal sandboxed workflow breaking is blocking); test counts; mutation results; what you did not check."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1386,"cache_read_input_tokens":529095,"output_tokens":2794,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":120},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1386,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":2794,"cache_read_input_tokens":529095,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1386,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1386},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":15510,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_014EqgCooKN2k7yNvucHjvTP":{"description":"Re-review PR #811 sandbox ancestors","subagent_type":"reviewer","prompt":"Short, time-boxed (about 25 minutes) independent re-review of GitHub PR #811 (DRAFT; PA-3 sandbox follow-up) in ~/nexus-code, base `release/v1.3.0`. Take the full head SHA from `gh pr view 811 --json headRefOid` (expected to start `cf696b5c`), review exactly that, and say whether it moved. The previous review of the same work is on #809 (`gh pr view 809 --comments`, \"Independent delta re-review … REQUEST CHANGES\"): real-bwrap attacks that still forged host goal state: (1) workspace = PARENT OF HOME: `mv ~ ~-x && mkdir -p ~/.nexus/tasks && echo FORGED > ~/.nexus/tasks/goal-forged.json` succeeded and the 