{"parentUuid":"7bdcb19c-8dd5-4b14-ba51-27036fd444b0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNt22HWJz8NKznUxXY9P","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The PA-3 builder pushed the ancestor-pinning fix to the draft PR (#811) as `cf696b5ca`, and a re-review is running against that head. #811 stays a draft and unmerged until that review posts an accept.\n\nThe builder reports:\n- **Ancestors:** every directory between the workspace and the state root is bound onto itself in bwrap and nested in Docker, and renaming any of them fails with a busy error in real bwrap and real Docker.\n- **Symlinks:** a state path through a symlink inside the workspace is refused.\n- **Workspaces:** a workspace that is the state root, or is inside `tasks/`, is refused with an explicit message. The BG-1 job-worktree case still works, though the builder did not run an end-to-end unattended job for it.\n- **Tests:** removing each guard fails a test, and the zombie test passed 20 of 20 runs.\n\nOne thing the builder said gives me pause: its parent-of-home test passes even without the new pins, and it did not reproduce the reviewer's rename of home in that case. So I told the reviewer to reproduce that exact attack first on the release tip, where it must forge a file, and then on this head, where it must fail. If home itself can still be renamed, the reviewer treats it as blocking. I also asked the reviewer to check the unattended job case, ordinary sandboxed workflows such as `git commit`, and whether any test proves the pins matter.\n\nThe BG-3 firer builder is still running its tests. v1.3.0 is not landed. The merge to `main` and the release haven't started."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3166,"cache_read_input_tokens":530481,"output_tokens":511,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_sear