her cases, all closed on the head:**\n  - relative path, `..`, trailing slashes\n  - root absent\n  - 20-deep ancestors (bind-count limit not hit)\n  - symlink outside the workspace pointing into it\n  - workspace that is the root or inside `tasks/`\n  - Docker, run for real: cases 1, 2, absent, default root and the symlink refusal behave the same as bwrap\n- **Sandboxed worker launch:** it goes through the same wrapper, so it inherits the plan. Not run live.\n\n**Do the tests prove the pins matter?** Only partly. Dropping the bwrap pins fails one test (the `$HOME/a/b/st` case). The \"parent of HOME\" test still passes without pins, as the builder said.\n\n**Mutations** (restored by `cmp`)\n- Drop bwrap pins: fails 1 of 28.\n- Drop Docker pins: fails 2 of 17.\n- Drop the symlink refusal: fails.\n- Drop the workspace-in-`tasks/` refusal: fails the bwrap suite. The Docker suite stays green (17/17), so the Docker side of that refusal is untested.\n\n**Suites:** every listed suite exits 0, including all `operation_*`, `runner_examples` and `schedule_examples` after the build. `sandbox_confine` is 28/28 and `sandbox_docker` 17/17. `unattended_worktree`, `unattended_gate` and `schedule_unattended` also pass. `tsc`, the complexity gate (exit 0), `check_invariants` and `check_doc_versions` pass.\n\n**New findings (none blocking, since no sandboxed command changed host goal state)**\n1. `cli/src/sandbox.ts` (the early `if (inside(root)) return { pins: [] }` in `stateRootPlan`): when the workspace is below a root that lies outside HOME (`NEXUS_STATE_DIR=/x/st`, workspace `/x/st/worktrees/j`), `tasks/g.json` is readable inside the sandbox. `7fc645899` masked it. Writes fail with EROFS. The doc sentence \"the sandbox cannot reach `tasks/`\" (`PA3_GOAL_LIFECYCLE.md`) is false in that configuration. Fix: also tmpfs-mask `&lt;root&gt;/tasks` when the workspace is inside the root but not inside `tasks`, or narrow the doc to \"root under HOME\".\n2. Read-only bwrap profile with workspace = HOME fails closed: `bwrap: Can't create file …/.nexus`. `7fc645899` worked while `~/.nexus` was absent and failed once it existed; the head always creates it, so it now fails every time. The existing read-only assertion only checks for \"no SENTINEL\", so a bwrap error passes it. Fix: assert the read-only command runs, and handle the mask mount in that branch.\n3. `stateRootPlan` creates the root on the host at every wrap, including when the engine later fails or is refused. This is minor and documented.\n\n**Regressions:** none for ordinary sandboxed work. Create/delete/rename, `git init` and `git status`, and `echo &gt; f` all work with pins, including 20 deep. BG-1 (repo at HOME, worktree `~/.nexus/worktrees/job`) works in a direct probe: HOME is masked, the worktree is writable, `git status` runs, and `mv ~/.nexus` fails. I did not run a full unattended job with the scripted gateway.\n\n**Docs:** the sentences I checked are true except the one in finding 1.\n\n**Not checked:**\n- A full unattended end-to-end job.\n- The sandboxed worker run live.\n- The real `/home` layout with HOME=/home/mike.\n- Whether the `7fc645899` HOME rename depends on the host kernel.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>88497</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>39</tool_uses><duration_ms>1102213</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"},"uuid":"22ec8c46-24da-4e17-9c90-5471f9549d34","timestamp":"2026-11-25T03:04:12.464Z","permissionMode":"bypassPermissions","origin":{"kind":"task-notification","producer":"session-task","runId":"0mwviug7l-7b060c69"},"promptSource":"system","turnOrigin":"task_notification","turnPromptId":"8b26bbf0-94e6-4341-a73b-a3f91796450c","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":46,"turnIndex":326},"queueSkipAttachments":true,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"v1/bg3-trust-abuse-model","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
