{"parentUuid":"1f7ace2b-7d5d-48b8-ba39-75e084499452","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNuRQfuE9tBmZcdRkk41","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TfW2x2jMAh6NBywtRQi8zQ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-code && cat > /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/rev811.md <<'EOF'\n**Independent re-review at `cf696b5ca1787bf81b675d4c4505724a2b9f624e` — ACCEPT WITH FOLLOW-UPS on the security result; two follow-ups are being fixed before this draft is marked ready.** All probes used throwaway homes under `/var/tmp` with real bwrap; Docker ran for real.\n\n**Attacks.** (1) Workspace = parent of HOME: the reviewer could not reproduce the HOME rename on the release tip (`mv` returns EBUSY there: the host `home` dentry carries a covered tmpfs mount), so the builder was right on that point. What did forge on the release tip is a root that does not exist yet (`mkdir -p ~/.nexus/tasks && echo FORGED > …` landed on the host): closed on the head (root created 0700 first, then masked). With `/`, `/var` or a grandparent as the workspace, the release tip let `mv home home-x` succeed or forged state; on the head every ancestor and the root return EBUSY. (2) Workspace = HOME, `NEXUS_STATE_DIR=$HOME/a/st`: forged on the release tip, closed on the head (`mv a a.old` is EBUSY). (3) Symlinked root: forged on the release tip; the head refuses with the explicit message, a symlinked ancestor is refused too. Also closed on the head: relative path, `..`, trailing slashes, an absent root, 20-deep ancestors, a symlink outside the workspace pointing in, a workspace that is the root or inside `tasks/`; Docker (real run) cases 1, 2, absent, default root and the symlink refusal behave like bwrap. The sandboxed worker goes through the same wrapper (not run live).\n**Do the tests prove the pins matter?** Only partly: dropping the bwrap pins fails 1 of 28 (the `$HOME/a/b/st` case); the parent-of-HOME test passes without pins. Mutations: drop bwrap pins (1 failure), drop Docker pins (2 of 17), drop the symlink refusal (fails), drop the workspace-in-`tasks/` refusal (fails the bwrap suite; the Docker suite stays green, so that refusal is untested for Docker).\n\n**Follow-ups:** (1) `cli/src/sandbox.ts`, `stateRootPlan` early `if (inside(root)) return { pins: [] }`: with a workspace below a root outside HOME (`NEXUS_STATE_DIR=/x/st`, workspace `/x/st/worktrees/j`) `tasks/g.json` is readable inside the sandbox (the release tip masked it; writes fail with EROFS), and the doc sentence \"cannot reach `tasks/`\" is false there: also tmpfs-mask `<root>/tasks` when the workspace is inside the root but not inside `tasks`, or narrow the doc. (2) **Regression:** the read-only bwrap profile with workspace = HOME now fails closed every time with `bwrap: Can't create file …/.nexus` (the release tip worked while `~/.nexus` was absent and failed once it existed; the head always creates it); the existing read-only assertion only checks for \"no SENTINEL\", so a bwrap error passes it: assert the command runs, and handle the mask mount in that branch. (3) Minor: `stateRootPlan` creates the root on the host at every wrap, even if the engine later fails or is refused (documented).\n**Regressions:** none for ordinary sandboxed work (create/delete/rename, `git init`/`status`, `echo > f` work with pins, 20 deep); BG-1 (repo at HOME, worktree `~/.nexus/worktrees/job`) works in a direct probe (HOME masked, worktree writable, `git status` runs, `mv ~/.nexus` fails); a full unattended job with the scripted gateway was not run. **Suites:** all exit 0 (`sandbox_confine` 28, `sandbox_docker` 17, `unattended_worktree`, `unattended_gate`, `schedule_unattended`, all `operation_*`, `runner_examples`, `schedule_examples` after the build); `tsc`, the complexity gate, invariants, doc versions pass. Not checked: a full unattended end to end, the worker live, the real `/home` layout, whether the release-tip HOME rename depends on the kernel.\nEOF\ngh pr comment 811 --body-file /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/rev811.md | tail -1","description":"Post the #811 re-review verdict"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2834,"cache_read_input_tokens":533647,"output_tokens":2916,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":203},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2834,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":2916,"cache_read_input_tokens":533647,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2834,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2834},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":9431,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01TfW2x2jMAh6NBywtRQi8zQ":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-code && cat > /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/rev811.md <<'EOF'\n**Independent re-review at `cf696b5ca1787bf81b675d4c4505724a2b9f624e` — ACCEPT WITH FOLLOW-UPS on the security result; two follow-ups are being fixed before this draft is marked ready.** All probes used throwaway homes under `/var/tmp` with real bwrap; Docker ran for real.\n\n**Attacks.** (1) Workspace = parent of HOME: the reviewer could not reproduce the HOME rename on the release tip (`mv` returns EBUSY there: the host `home` dentry carries a covered tmpfs mount), so the builder was right on that point. What did forge on the release tip is a root that does not exist yet (`mkdir -p ~/.nexus/tasks && echo FORGED > …` landed on the host): closed on the head (root created 0700 first, then masked). With `/`, `/var` or a grandparent as the workspace, the release tip let `mv home home-x` succeed or forged state; on the head every ancestor and the root return EBUSY. (2) Workspace = HOME, `NEXUS_STATE_DIR=$HOME/a/st`: forged on the release tip, closed on the head (`mv a a.old` is EBUSY). (3) Symlinked root: forged on the release tip; the head refuses with the explicit message, a symlinked ancestor is refused too. Also closed on the head: relative path, `..`, trailing slashes, an absent root, 20-deep ancestors, a symlink outside the workspace pointing in, a workspace that is the root or inside `tasks/`; Docker (real run) cases 1, 2, absent, default root and the symlink refusal behave like bwrap. The sandboxed worker goes through the same wrapper (not run live).\n**Do the tests prove the pins matter?** Only partly: dropping the bwrap pins fails 1 of 28 (the `$HOME/a/b/st` case); the parent-of-HOME test passes without pins. Mutations: drop bwrap pins (1 failure), drop Docker pins (2 of 17), drop the symlink refusal (fails), drop the workspace-in-`tasks/` refusal (fails the bwrap suite; the Docker suite stays green, so that refusal is untested for Docker).\n\n**Follow-ups:** (1) `cli/src/sandbox.ts`, `stateRootPlan` early `if (inside(root)) return { pins: [] }`: with a workspace below a root outside HOME (`NEXUS_STATE_DIR=/x/st`, workspace `/x/st/worktrees/j`) `tasks/g.json` is readable inside the sandbox (the release tip masked it; writes fail with EROFS), and the doc sentence \"cannot reach `tasks/`\" is false there: also tmpfs-mask `<root>/tasks` when the workspace is inside the root but not inside `tasks`, or narrow the doc. (2) **Regression:** the read-only bwrap profile with workspace = HOME now fails closed every time with `bwrap: Can't create file …/.nexus` (the release tip worked while `~/.nexus` was absent and failed once it existed; the head always creates it); the existing read-only assertion only checks for \"no SENTINEL\", so a bwrap error passes it: assert the command runs, and handle the mask mount in that branch. (3) Minor: `stateRootPlan` creates the root on the host at every wrap, even if the engine later fails or is refused (documented).\n**Regressions:** none for ordinary sandboxed work (create/delete/rename, `git init`/`status`, `echo > f` work with pins, 20 deep); BG-1 (repo at HOME, worktree `~/.nexus/worktrees/job`) works in a direct probe (HOME masked, worktree writable, `git status` runs, `mv ~/.nexus` fails); a full unattended job with the scripted gateway was not run. **Suites:** all exit 0 (`sandbox_confine` 28, `sandbox_docker` 17, `unattended_worktree`, `unattended_gate`, `schedule_unattended`, all `operation_*`, `runner_examples`, `schedule_examples` after the build); `tsc`, the complexity gate, invariants, doc versions pass. Not checked: a full unattended end to end, the worker live, the real `/home` layout, whether the release-tip HOME rename depends on the kernel.\nEOF\ngh pr comment 811 --body-file /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/rev811.md | tail -1","description":"Post the #811 re-review verdict"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011ChNuRQSWbsQ4muUcd4oso","requestRef":"58adbcf9-3262-4e08-a199-16be7dd2e6b5","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"8b4a10e1-d9cc-4bb3-9b56-2baba9e5bb06","timestamp":"2026-11-25T03:04:27.098Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"v1/bg3-trust-abuse-model","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
