{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-11-25T03:18:12.602Z","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a6379c334af41ccf9</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_014dtAmYDD3FtYS1kTXdj7tK</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666/tasks/a6379c334af41ccf9.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Complete PA-3 goal semantics\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Both follow-ups are fixed and pushed as `110b08fb2`; the PR stays a draft.\n\n- **Item 1:** when the workspace is inside the root (external `NEXUS_STATE_DIR` or `&lt;repo&gt;/.nexus/worktrees`), `&lt;root&gt;/tasks` is now tmpfs-masked. bwrap tests show read, write and rename all fail while the workspace works. Docker mounts only the workspace, so `tasks/` is not in the container; its test passes even without the mask and so does not discriminate. I added the Docker test for the workspace-in-`tasks/` refusal.\n- **Item 2:** I could not reproduce a read-only-profile regression with a real fd 3. The failure came from the test helper, which never passed fd 3 to bwrap, so the old assertion passed on a bwrap error. A new helper passes fd 3. The tests assert the marker printed, the root lists empty, the workspace is read-only and the host file is untouched, and an absent root works too.\n- **Pins and refusals:** the grandparent-of-HOME test fails without the pins. A refused wrap (symlinked root) creates nothing, and a test covers it.\n- **Edits not mine:** I found uncommitted changes in the worktree that I did not make: refusing a workspace below an external root, a `worker_isolation` test edit and doc lines. I replaced the refusal with the tasks mask and committed the rest.\n\nRemoving the pins or the bwrap tasks mask each failed a test. `tsc`, the complexity gate (exit 0), `check_invariants`, `check_doc_versions` and all listed suites pass. The sandbox tests passed three times each.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>371941</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>15</tool_uses><duration_ms>819441</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
