{"parentUuid":"1d517eb3-2752-4c59-a01c-3b098bc7bf61","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNwN7ZfC3YBRBgemHajc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LZ5oq1acDYwUrbHYMBnQ5r","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-wt/pa3f && git fetch -q origin && git merge -q origin/release/v1.3.0 --no-edit 2>&1 | tail -2; (cd cli && TMPDIR=/dev/shm HOME=$(mktemp -d) node --import tsx --test test/sandbox_custom_state_root.test.ts 2>&1 | grep -E \"^ℹ (pass|fail) \" | tr '\\n' ' '; npx tsc --noEmit -p . >/dev/null; echo \"tsc $?\"); git add cli/test/sandbox_custom_state_root.test.ts && git commit -q -m \"test(sandbox): align the custom state root tests with the tasks mask\n\nThe committed tests still expected the earlier refusal of a workspace nested under an external state root; the code now masks <root>/tasks instead (110b08fb2), so CI shard 3 failed on two of them. The tests now assert the mask, a writable workspace and an unreachable tasks directory.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>\" && git push -q origin v1/pa3-completion 2>&1 | tail -1; echo \"head $(git rev-parse --short=8 HEAD) remote $(git ls-remote origin refs/heads/v1/pa3-completion | cut -c1-8)\"","description":"Commit and push the corrected custom-state-root tests after re-running them","timeout":200000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1928,"cache_read_input_tokens":549605,"output_tokens":774,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":208},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1928,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":774,"cache_read_input_tokens":549605,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1928,"cache_creation":{"epheme