{"parentUuid":"04d6e6a3-7cd2-426c-a819-30ad5a45ff7f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNxGDgx5qykXm26NmAv7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The PA-3 sandbox follow-up is merged into `release/v1.3.0` as `09eb0b12` (#811). Required checks were green at the exact head, release CI was green at the tip first, and I read the merged state back. Release CI on the new merge is not yet confirmed.\n\nThe first attempt failed CI. Shard 3 on Node 24 had two failing tests in `sandbox_custom_state_root`. Another agent had committed a test file that still expected the earlier \"refuse a workspace nested under an external state root\" behaviour, while the code now masks the task directory instead. The corrected test was sitting uncommitted in the worktree and passed locally (3 of 3). I committed and pushed it, and the checks went green.\n\nThe mask is on the release branch. The final commit (tasks mask when the workspace is inside the state root, the test helper that passes the descriptor, and a refusal of sandbox home mounts that overlap the state root) was read by me against the diff and tests but not by a second reviewer. The earlier security result stands as reviewed: ancestors pinned, symlinked roots refused, root created first. The PA-3 acceptance is therefore closed, with the sandbox protection reviewed in rounds and the last commit self-checked.\n\nStill running: the BG-3 firer builder. The HK-3 print-site follow-ups (a few unescaped names and one missing notice) are not yet assigned. v1.3.0 is not landed. The merge to `main` and the release haven't started."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":341,"cache_read_input_tokens":552882,"output_tokens":483,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_c