{"parentUuid":"87794914-3555-4881-b940-ffec256345f8","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"8f0ae47f-b64a-4081-839c-605d4a5cb6e2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BYBSsrvGc3MM4ppMGnX3F2","type":"tool_result","content":"ok fetched\n164d0e511 Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/release/v1.3.0' into v1/bg3-firer\n791bec9ae test(triggers): mutation-driven tests (watch closes, bound address, bl\n17b891b69 Merge pull request #810 from mikeholownych/v1/hk3-followups\n0\n# v1.3.0 readiness inventory\n\nMeasured against `origin/release/v1.3.0` tip **`2a28fca89`** (2026-11-24, includes #787 PA-1 and #789 PA-3 fingerprint stalls). Version strings are st\n  \"version\": \"1.2.2\",\nv1.2.1-rc.2.md  1.5K\nv1.2.1.md  6.1K\nv1.2.2-rc.1.md  1.1K\nv1.2.2.md  8.3K\nv1.3.0-READINESS.md  5.5K\n# Release process\n\nBuilding, packaging and tagging are described in [Development and release](DEVELOPMENT.md#release-package). This page covers the documentation steps that follow a stable tag.\n\n## After the stable tag\n\nThe release workflow does not touch the README, the CHANGELOG or `docs/releases/LATEST`. Once the stable tag is published, make a manual follow-up commit (a normal PR) that:\n\n1. Sets `docs/releases/LATEST` to the new stable tag (one line, `vX.Y.Z`).\n2. Updates the README status line (\"the latest stable release is ...\") and the README and `quickstart.md` install pins to that tag, and removes any \"in development\" wording for it.\n3. Replaces `Unreleased` in the CHANGELOG heading of the new version with the tag date.\n\n`node scripts/check_doc_versions.mjs` (run in CI) fails when any of these disagree with `LATEST`, so the follow-up PR is the one that turns it green again. The stable-promotion commit itself passes be","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"dc35531e-99da-4d68-a67f-8a090c45f66e","timestamp":"2026-11-25T03:42:14.358Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"ok fetched\n164d0e511 Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/release/v1.3.0' into v1/bg3-firer\n791bec9ae test(triggers): mutation-driven tests (watch closes, bound address, bl\n17b891b69 Merge pull request #810 from mikeholownych/v1/hk3-followups\n0\n# v1.3.0 readiness inventory\n\nMeasured against `origin/release/v1.3.0` tip **`2a28fca89`** (2026-11-24, includes #787 PA-1 and #789 PA-3 fingerprint stalls). Version strings are st\n  \"version\": \"1.2.2\",\nv1.2.1-rc.2.md  1.5K\nv1.2.1.md  6.1K\nv1.2.2-rc.1.md  1.1K\nv1.2.2.md  8.3K\nv1.3.0-READINESS.md  5.5K\n# Release process\n\nBuilding, packaging and tagging are described in [Development and release](DEVELOPMENT.md#release-package). This page covers the documentation steps that follow a stable tag.\n\n## After the stable tag\n\nThe release workflow does not touch the README, the CHANGELOG or `docs/releases/LATEST`. Once the stable tag is published, make a manual follow-up commit (a normal PR) that:\n\n1. Sets `docs/releases/LATEST` to the new stable tag (one line, `vX.Y.Z`).\n2. Updates the README status line (\"the latest stable release is ...\") and the README and `quickstart.md` install pins to that tag, and removes any \"in development\" wording for it.\n3. Replaces `Unreleased` in the CHANGELOG heading of the new version with the tag date.\n\n`node scripts/check_doc_versions.mjs` (run in CI) fails when any of these disagree with `LATEST`, so the follow-up PR is the one that turns it green again. The stable-promotion commit itself passes be","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"87794914-3555-4881-b940-ffec256345f8","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"v1/bg3-trust-abuse-model","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","hash":"21004ad5ec6a7f1d0ee2f04a43687fea7bf8f4f7e67f67b81e1e49254a488ea6","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019FWEJ857GKv6un6hvPo1i9","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"a317b41792fa50650","summary":"HK-3 print-site and notice follow-ups","message":"HK-3 fixes merged (#810, 17b891b6). Remaining non-blocking follow-ups from the re-review of #808/f375865e (comment on #808): do them on a NEW branch `v1/hk3-printsites` from origin/release/v1.3.0 in worktree /home/mike/nexus-wt/hk3g (`git -C ~/nexus-code worktree add -b v1/hk3-printsites ~/nexus-wt/hk3g origin/release/v1.3.0`, symlink cli/node_modules from ~/nexus-code/cli, copy core/target/release binaries from ~/nexus-wt/ls1b/core/target/release). Each with a test that fails without it (mutate a copy, restore from it): (1) unescaped print sites: `doctor.ts` `plugins.config` (~1243-1262) raw plugin file paths; `index.ts:~1168` (`plugins revoke`); the HK-2 install/verify/list-installed output in `plugins_cli.ts` (~153-220); the project-hooks notice; apply the shared `core/printable.ts` helper everywhere a name/path/error from a plugin or repo is printed (grep every `console.`/`stderr.write`/doctor evidence in plugin/hook/doctor code and list sites you checked); (2) `printableRefusal` handles C0/C1 but not bidi, and `printable` omits U+FFF9–FFFB and the U+E0000 tag block: make ONE helper escape C0, DEL, C1, bidi (U+061C, U+200E/F, U+202A-E, U+2066-9), zero-width/format (U+200B-D, U+2060, U+FEFF, U+00AD), interlinear annotation U+FFF9-FB, tags U+E0000-E007F, line/paragraph separators U+2028/9, and lone surrogates; tests on exact bytes; (3) symlinked HOME with absent operator plugin dirs: the real-path spelling of `~/.nexus/plugins` / `~/.config/nexus/plugins` must be a protected path too (realpath the parent that exists + append), tests incl. symlinked HOME; (4) a changed JS plugin file must get the same louder \"NO LONGER IN FORCE: <file> changed\" notice (once per session) as hooks/manifest plugins, not only the generic pending notice; (5) `nexus plugins list` and doctor must mention skipped operator plugin directories (workspace = HOME) with the fix; (6) trust-store lock stale takeover must be atomic: take over via rename of the stale lock file to a unique name then O_EXCL create, so two takers cannot both win; test with 8 concurrent processes over 50 rounds; if `/proc` is unavailable the pid check must not read \"always stale\": fall back to treating a lock younger than 30 s as live. Run the plugin/hook/doctor/trust tests (`ls cli/test | grep -iE 'plugin|hook|trust|doctor|printable'`), security, leak_guard, check_requirements, tsc, the complexity gate (exit code), check_invariants, check_doc_versions; new/changed tests three times. Commit `fix(plugins): <what>` + `Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>`; push with a plain `git push -u origin v1/hk3-printsites` (never force); report under 200 words with the hash. I open a draft PR, review, then merge."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BYBSsrvGc3MM4ppMGnX3F2","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-code && git fetch -q origin; git ls-remote origin refs/heads/v1/bg3-firer | cut -c1-8; cd ~/nexus-wt/bg3 && git log --oneline -3 | cut -c1-80; git status --short | wc -l; ps -eo etime,args | grep -E \"[n]ode --import tsx --test\" | head -3 | cut -c1-100; cd ~/nexus-code; git show origin/release/v1.3.0:docs/releases/v1.3.0-READINESS.md | head -3 | cut -c1-150; git show origin/release/v1.3.0:cli/package.json | grep '\"version\"'; ls docs/releases | tail -5; sed -n 1,40p docs/RELEASE_PROCESS.md | cut -c1-200","description":"Check the BG-3 firer's progress and the release-process inputs: readiness doc, version, release docs"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
