{"parentUuid":"8deebe30-e636-4a51-a8fb-65fd0c371499","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNxKu1Ax2K4dnZzmyRrw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GHhKGKCbqn36JSELv5z977","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Refresh v1.3.0 readiness and draft notes","subagent_type":"general-purpose","prompt":"Prepare the v1.3.0 release documentation on a branch, WITHOUT bumping any version and WITHOUT tagging or pushing tags. Worktree: `git -C ~/nexus-code fetch origin && git -C ~/nexus-code worktree add -b v1/v130-release-docs ~/nexus-wt/reldocs origin/release/v1.3.0`; `ln -s ~/nexus-code/cli/node_modules ~/nexus-wt/reldocs/cli/node_modules`; `mkdir -p ~/nexus-wt/reldocs/core/target/release && cp ~/nexus-wt/ls1b/core/target/release/{harness-core,nexus-tui} ~/nexus-wt/reldocs/core/target/release/`. Read first: `/home/mike/nexus-wt/reldocs/AGENTS.md` (release rules: report gates \"as measured\", e.g. \"ledger closed, qualification pending\"; make no frontier-grade claim without external qualification), `docs/RELEASE_PROCESS.md`, `docs/DEVELOPMENT.md` release section, `docs/v1.3.0/PLAN.md` (units, gates G-1..G-7 at ~lines 125-135, decisions), `docs/releases/v1.3.0-READINESS.md` (stale: measured at 2a28fca89), previous notes `docs/releases/v1.2.2.md` and `v1.2.2-rc.1.md` for format, `CHANGELOG.md` Unreleased section, `docs/v1.3.0/*.md`. The owner has put all units in scope (PF-1..4, AC-1/2, VR-1..3, GV-1..5, LS-1/2, HK-1..3, BG-1..3, PA-1..4, SB-1, MT-1/2, CI speedup); BG-3 firer, MT-2 slices 3-4 and SB-1 slices 2-3 are still being finished by other agents: record their CURRENT state truthfully from the repository (PR numbers via `gh pr list --state all --search`, `git log origin/release/v1.3.0`, claims in `$(git -C ~/nexus-code rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/`) and mark them \"in flight\" where they are.\nDeliver (documentation only, no code): (1) refresh `docs/releases/v1.3.0-READINESS.md`: tip SHA measured; the unit table with status per unit and the merged PR numbers as evidence, verified by grepping the code/docs for each acceptance (e.g. file exists, command registered: `nexus schedule`, `nexus triggers`, `nexus plugins`, `nexus hooks`, `nexus runner`, `nexus job`, `nexus verify`, `nexus policy`, `nexus audit`, `nexus operation budget`; use `node cli/dist/index.js --help` after `npm --prefix cli run build` with a throwaway HOME to list real commands); the independent-review record per security-relevant unit (PR comments exist: list the PR numbers whose reviews found defects and the follow-ups still open, from `gh pr view <n> --comments`: be accurate, do not invent); known open items: issues (`gh issue list --state open`), including #800 (`startsWith(\"..\")` containment sites) and #807 (unattended `prepare` overrides a stale goal pause for jobs/loops); the documented limits (unsandboxed command with faked terminal can approve hooks/plugins/triggers; same-uid processes; no signature on goal state; kernel/bwrap/Docker coverage); the gates G-1..G-7 each measured or \"not yet measured\" with the exact command that would measure it (do NOT claim a gate you did not run; you may run cheap ones: `node scripts/check_*.mjs`, `npx tsc --noEmit -p .`, the complexity gate, `check_doc_versions`; do not run the full suite: CI is the arbiter) and framed per G-7. (2) a draft `docs/releases/v1.3.0-rc.1.md` in the style of `v1.2.2-rc.1.md`/`v1.2.2.md`: what is new per track, behaviour changes that need a migration note (list them all from the CHANGELOG, PR bodies and docs: e.g. workspace JS plugins need per-file approval (`nexus plugins trust`), project hooks accept only an allowlisted command shape and run from verified copies, `mcp.allow` name entries do not admit workspace-defined servers, `nexus policy`, unattended jobs' verifier, `--listen` socket, schedules' UTC cron and 5-minute floor, goal pause semantics, `/team` no longer experimental, BG-3 triggers when they land), security notes and limits, qualification pending wording. Mark every claim with its PR or file as evidence in the doc's own evidence section. (3) CHANGELOG: do NOT replace `Unreleased` (that is done at the RC commit) but check that every merged unit has an entry (list missing ones in your report, add them under Unreleased if clearly missing, following the file's style). No version strings changed anywhere. Run `node scripts/check_doc_versions.mjs` and `npx tsc --noEmit -p .` (in cli/) at the end; commit locally in 2-3 commits `docs(release): …` + `Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>`; push with a plain `git push -u origin v1/v130-release-docs` (never force); do not open a PR (I do). Rules: never touch the real ~/.nexus, ~/.config/nexus, /etc/nexus (throwaway HOME for any command run); no network except `gh` reads; no deletes of anything outside your own temp dirs; shell is zsh (`bash -c` for loops); prefix `rtk proxy` if output looks filtered. Report under 350 words: what you verified vs could not verify, discrepancies you found between the old readiness doc and the repository (units claimed done that are not, or the reverse), missing CHANGELOG entries, and the list of open items an RC needs closed."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":540,"cache_read_input_tokens":556476,"output_tokens":2540,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":384},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":540,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2540,"cache_read_input_tokens":556476,"cache_creation_input_tokens":540,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":540},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":15133,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01GHhKGKCbqn36JSELv5z977":{"description":"Refresh v1.3.0 readiness and draft notes","subagent_type":"general-purpose","prompt":"Prepare the v1.3.0 release documentation on a branch, WITHOUT bumping any version and WITHOUT tagging or pushing tags. Worktree: `git -C ~/nexus-code fetch origin && git -C ~/nexus-code worktree add -b v1/v130-release-docs ~/nexus-wt/reldocs origin/release/v1.3.0`; `ln -s ~/nexus-code/cli/node_modules ~/nexus-wt/reldocs/cli/node_modules`; `mkdir -p ~/nexus-wt/reldocs/core/target/release && cp ~/nexus-wt/ls1b/core/target/release/{harness-core,nexus-tui} ~/nexus-wt/reldocs/core/target/release/`. Read first: `/home/mike/nexus-wt/reldocs/AGENTS.md` (release rules: report gates \"as measured\", e.g. \"ledger closed, qualification pending\"; make no frontier-grade claim without external qualification), `docs/RELEASE_PROCESS.md`, `docs/DEVELOPMENT.md` release section, `docs/v1.3.0/PLAN.md` (units, gates G-1..G-7 at ~lines 125-135, decisions), `docs/releases/v1.3.0-READINESS.md` (stale: measured at 2a28fca89), previous notes `docs/releases/v1.2.2.md` and `v1.2.2-rc.1.md` for format, `CHANGELOG.md` Unreleased section, `docs/v1.3.0/*.md`. The owner has put all units in scope (PF-1..4, AC-1/2, VR-1..3, GV-1..5, LS-1/2, HK-1..3, BG-1..3, PA-1..4, SB-1, MT-1/2, CI speedup); BG-3 firer, MT-2 slices 3-4 and SB-1 slices 2-3 are still being finished by other agents: record their CURRENT state truthfully from the repository (PR numbers via `gh pr list --state all --search`, `git log origin/release/v1.3.0`, claims in `$(git -C ~/nexus-code rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/`) and mark them \"in flight\" where they are.\nDeliver (documentation only, no code): (1) refresh `docs/releases/v1.3.0-READINESS.md`: tip SHA measured; the unit table with status per unit and the merged PR numbers as evidence, verified by grepping the code/docs for each acceptance (e.g. file exists, command registered: `nexus schedule`, `nexus triggers`, `nexus plugins`, `nexus hooks`, `nexus runner`, `nexus job`, `nexus verify`, `nexus policy`, `nexus audit`, `nexus operation budget`; use `node cli/dist/index.js --help` after `npm --prefix cli run build` with a throwaway HOME to list real commands); the independent-review record per security-relevant unit (PR comments exist: list the PR numbers whose reviews found defects and the follow-ups still open, from `gh pr view <n> --comments`: be accurate, do not invent); known open items: issues (`gh issue list --state open`), including #800 (`startsWith(\"..\")` containment sites) and #807 (unattended `prepare` overrides a stale goal pause for jobs/loops); the documented limits (unsandboxed command with faked terminal can approve hooks/plugins/triggers; same-uid processes; no signature on goal state; kernel/bwrap/Docker coverage); the gates G-1..G-7 each measured or \"not yet measured\" with the exact command that would measure it (do NOT claim a gate you did not run; you may run cheap ones: `node scripts/check_*.mjs`, `npx tsc --noEmit -p .`, the complexity gate, `check_doc_versions`; do not run the full suite: CI is the arbiter) and framed per G-7. (2) a draft `docs/releases/v1.3.0-rc.1.md` in the style of `v1.2.2-rc.1.md`/`v1.2.2.md`: what is new per track, behaviour changes that need a migration note (list them all from the CHANGELOG, PR bodies and docs: e.g. workspace JS plugins need per-file approval (`nexus plugins trust`), project hooks accept only an allowlisted command shape and run from verified copies, `mcp.allow` name entries do not admit workspace-defined servers, `nexus policy`, unattended jobs' verifier, `--listen` socket, schedules' UTC cron and 5-minute floor, goal pause semantics, `/team` no longer experimental, BG-3 triggers when they land), security notes and limits, qualification pending wording. Mark every claim with its PR or file as evidence in the doc's own evidence section. (3) CHANGELOG: do NOT replace `Unreleased` (that is done at the RC commit) but check that every merged unit has an entry (list missing ones in your report, add them under Unreleased if clearly missing, following the file's style). No version strings changed anywhere. Run `node scripts/check_doc_versions.mjs` and `npx tsc --noEmit -p .` (in cli/) at the end; commit locally in 2-3 commits `docs(release): …` + `Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>`; push with a plain `git push -u origin v1/v130-release-docs` (never force); do not open a PR (I do). Rules: never touch the real ~/.nexus, ~/.config/nexus, /etc/nexus (throwaway HOME for any command run); no network except `gh` reads; no deletes of anything outside your own temp dirs; shell is zsh (`bash -c` for loops); prefix `rtk proxy` if output looks filtered. Report under 350 words: what you verified vs could not verify, discrepancies you found between the old readiness doc and the repository (units claimed done that are not, or the reverse), missing CHANGELOG entries, and the list of open items an RC needs closed."}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011ChNxKtp1pSazdMbYNy1m1","requestRef":"8411ef14-916d-4883-9718-d104aedb6835","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"8a4cd7d1-4862-4c21-ad23-a335ce4ccce2","timestamp":"2026-11-25T03:42:39.913Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"v1/bg3-trust-abuse-model","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
