{"parentUuid":"90e0f0df-af2a-41a1-976b-14b5057b85df","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNxMcmuvm75w9tCjMnuq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Three pieces of work are in motion toward the release candidate, and nothing new is merged yet.\n\n- **BG-3 firer:** the builder had three local firer commits and a clean tree with nothing running. I woke it to confirm the final gates on the merged state, push the branch, and report. I'll open a draft PR and send it for an independent hostile review.\n- **HK-3 print-site follow-ups:** now assigned to the HK-1/HK-3 builder, on a new branch off the release tip. They cover:\n  - unescaped plugin names in doctor, `plugins revoke` and the HK-2 output;\n  - a bidi-aware escape helper;\n  - the protected real-path spelling under a symlinked home;\n  - the louder notice for a changed JS plugin;\n  - a mention of skipped operator directories in `plugins list` and doctor;\n  - an atomic stale-lock takeover.\n- **Release documentation:** a builder is refreshing the stale readiness inventory (still measured at `2a28fca89`) and drafting `docs/releases/v1.3.0-rc.1.md`. It will not bump any version or tag, and it will not claim a gate it did not run. It will list:\n  - the units, with PR evidence;\n  - the defects the independent reviews found;\n  - open issues #800 and #807;\n  - the documented limits;\n  - every behaviour change that needs a migration note.\n\n**Not done:**\n- MT-2 slices 3–4, the dispatch split and the complexity-baseline move, which needs your acknowledgement.\n- SB-1 slices 2–3, with Codex.\n- The RC itself: version bump, changelog, the merge to `main`, the stable tag, and the real-server smoke runs on the final tip.\n\nv1.3.0 is not landed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2904,"cache_read_input_tokens":557016,"output_tokens":582,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2904,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":582,"cache_read_input_tokens":557016,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2904,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2904},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011ChNxMcazYxpWYF7Es54B2","requestRef":"230036af-8b5a-4efc-9324-834645d357e3","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"93222333-4d99-440c-a0b6-07b81eb87061","timestamp":"2026-11-25T03:42:48.537Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"v1/bg3-trust-abuse-model","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
