{"parentUuid":"38ab520f-a6b1-4729-bc30-978f99210143","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNxRV9e43uKt6WRUbzgn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018ypGiLaqpoPCEPNPiWhqUY","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-wt/bg3 && git fetch -q origin && git status --short | wc -l && git merge -q origin/release/v1.3.0 --no-edit 2>&1 | tail -2; git status --short | grep -c '^UU'; (cd cli && npx tsc --noEmit -p . >/dev/null; echo \"tsc $?\"); git push -q origin v1/bg3-firer 2>&1 | tail -1; echo \"head $(git rev-parse --short=8 HEAD) remote $(git ls-remote origin refs/heads/v1/bg3-firer | cut -c1-8)\"; git diff --stat origin/release/v1.3.0...HEAD | tail -2; cd ~/nexus-code && cat > /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/pr_bg3.md <<'EOF'\nDRAFT: do not merge until an independent hostile review posts ACCEPT.\n\nBG-3 event triggers (the owner put BG-3 back in scope for v1.3.0): the firer on top of the merged trust model (#803).\n\n## What it adds\n- **Where it runs:** a loop inside `nexus runner serve`, next to the schedule engine. It submits through `buildJobSubmission` and the runner's own acceptance (no second execution path): read-only by default, a fresh worktree, no auto, no allow-always, receipts carry `trigger_id`/`trigger_event` (job `origin` gains a `trigger` variant; `job-v1`, `runner-files-v1`, `job-receipt-v1`, `job-status-v1` change additively, ledger entries added). Flags: `--webhook-port`, `--webhook-host`, `--webhook-allow-remote`, `--no-triggers`. A runner with no approved trigger opens no watcher, socket or state; no worker inherits the webhook secret variable.\n- **At every fire:** the approval and the spec file are re-read and re-hashed once; it fires only from that parse. Order: repeated event id and overlapping job dropped first, then approval and trust, then the limiter, then submit.\n- **File-change watcher:** loop guard (`.git`, `.nexus`, `nexus-triggers` paths never count; events dropped and counted while the trigger's previous job runs); limits: 256 directories per trigger, 1,024 in total, 1,000 pending paths, 2-second window; a symlink out of the workspace is dropped and counted.\n- **Webhook listener:** loopback by default (remote only with `--webhook-allow-remote`); 64 KiB body, 8 KiB headers, 10 s request timeout, 32 connections, 1 request per socket; HMAC-SHA256 over `timestamp.delivery.body` with a 5-minute skew; every pre-auth refusal is an identical 401; the limiter runs only after authentication; in-memory replay cache (4,096 entries, 10 minutes, fails closed when full); a timestamp earlier than the listener's start is refused (restart replays) plus an existing-job check on the event id.\n- **Limiter state** private (0600 in a 0700 dir) at `runner/nexus-triggers/state.json`, restored with the validating `restore`; a refused state denies all firings until `nexus triggers release --limiter`. `nexus triggers status|release|fire-test`.\n- The #803 re-review follow-ups (literal `yes`, quarantine cap in `recordFailure`, LRU not resetting a live window, `limiterKey` realpath, EOF handling, escaped path line, worktree-write docs), docs (`docs/TRIGGERS.md`), `examples/triggers`.\n\n## Limits stated in the docs\nA faked terminal can approve or release; a process under your account can read the secret from `/proc`, rewrite state and send signed deliveries; event text can still steer the model (the job's read-only, no-approval rules are the limit); events are not durable (dropped by rate, overlap or quarantine are never replayed); the webhook is plain HTTP; a clock set back reopens a rate window.\n\n## Open items\n`consecutiveFailures` resets on every admission, so job failures reported through `recordFailure` never reach 3 in a row (only rate denials quarantine; documented, `trigger_rate_limit.ts` left alone); `bounds.maxRounds` maps to `maxTotalSteps` (default 5 is tight; docs say 10 or more); `nexus-trigger-state` has no published schema; the example tests need a fresh `npm run build`.\n\n## Tests\n8 new files, 78 tests (`trigger_followups` 7, `trigger_status_cli` 5, …), about 60 mutations each fail their guard when removed (four equivalent mutants listed in the builder's report). `tsc`, the complexity gate, invariants, doc versions and the schema `--check` generators pass locally on Node 24 (not Node 22; not `--sandbox` reachability).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\nEOF\nu=$(gh pr create --draft --base release/v1.3.0 --head v1/bg3-firer --title \"feat(triggers): BG-3 trigger firer: file watcher and signed webhooks through the unattended runner\" --body-file /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/pr_bg3.md | tail -1); echo \"$u\"; echo \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ) PR (claude-invariants-audit): $u BG-3 firer as a DRAFT: do not mark ready or merge until an independent hostile review posts ACCEPT.\" >> \"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log\"","description":"Merge release into the firer branch, push it, and open a draft PR with the body","timeout":200000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3000,"cache_read_input_tokens":559920,"output_tokens":2132,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":45},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3000,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":2132,"cache_read_input_tokens":559920,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3000,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3000},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":n