{"parentUuid":"5135b5aa-cec7-4121-9774-d9c5899c9738","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNxVaPWo9fS95GwAuKF5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The BG-3 trigger firer is now open as draft PR #812, and an independent hostile security review is running against it. #812 stays a draft and unmerged until the review posts an accept. I haven't re-run the firer's own tests myself.\n\n**What the firer does:**\n- It runs as a loop inside `nexus runner serve`, next to the schedule engine, and submits through the same unattended path as `nexus job`.\n- File changes and signed webhooks both start jobs. Webhooks bind loopback by default.\n- The approved spec is re-read and re-hashed at every fire.\n- The builder reports about 60 mutations, each failing its guard when removed, and 78 new tests.\n\n**Open items the builder reported, which the reviewer is judging:**\n- Job failures can never reach the three-in-a-row quarantine, because a counter resets on every admission. Only rate denials quarantine.\n- Events dropped by rate, overlap or quarantine are never replayed.\n- The webhook is plain HTTP.\n- A process under your account can read the webhook secret from `/proc`.\n- The default round limit of 5 is tight; the docs recommend 10 or more.\n\n**What I asked the reviewer to test specifically:**\n- Webhook forging, replay, request smuggling and timing differences between unknown and known triggers.\n- Whether two triggers can set each other off in a cycle, since the loop guard is per trigger.\n- The cost per request of an authenticated flood.\n- A runner with no approved trigger opening no socket, watcher or state.\n\nStill running: the HK-3 print-site follow-ups, the release documentation refresh and the independent review of the firer. Not started: MT-2 slices 3–4 (the baseline move needs your acknowledgement) and SB-1 slices 2–3 with Codex. After those: the release candidate, the merge to `main` and the stable tag. v1.3.0 is not landed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4294,"cache_read_input_tokens":565313,"output_tokens":620,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4294,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":620,"cache_read_input_tokens":565313,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4294,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4294},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011ChNxVaD6mVxSqn9aJwpGR","requestRef":"58239191-b24e-4447-b089-cbf24535bb47","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"eb156aa0-87f0-42bf-944d-4768e03ef7be","timestamp":"2026-11-25T03:44:36.607Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"v1/bg3-trust-abuse-model","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
